  (20701, 'Growth, Inflation & Indicators', 'Economy', 'MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)', 2024, 'घाऊक किंमतीच्या निर्देशांकातील वाढ हा निर्देशांक समजला जातो:', '{"A": "आर्थिक धोरण", "B": "महागाई", "C": "निर्यात", "D": "आयात"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'घाऊक किंमती निर्देशांक (WPI) वाढ — inflation indicator. Export, import, generic economic policy — WPI standard macro textbooks; retail CPI पूर्व stage पर्याय A (आर्थिक धोरण) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (निर्यात) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (आयात) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Economy","MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)","2024","Growth, Inflation & Indicators"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20702, 'Money & Banking', 'Economy', 'MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)', 2024, 'सरकारने _____ स्वरूपात भांडवली प्रवाहाचे उदारीकरण केले.', '{"A": "प्रत्यक्ष विदेशी गुंतवणूक", "B": "बहुराष्ट्रीय कंपन्यांवर नियंत्रण", "C": "सार्वजनिक उपक्रमांना प्रोत्साहन", "D": "भारतीय उद्योगांना प्रोत्साहन"}'::jsonb, 'A', '1991 capital-account liberalisation — FDI inflows door open. MNC control, PSU promote — liberalisation opposite; FDI channel targets पर्याय B (बहुराष्ट्रीय कंपन्यांवर नियंत्रण) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (सार्वजनिक उपक्रमांना प्रोत्साहन) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (भारतीय उद्योगांना प्रोत्साहन) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Economy","MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)","2024","Money & Banking"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20703, 'Industry, Trade & Reforms', 'Economy', 'MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)', 2024, '1991 च्या सुरुवातीला भारतात प्रमुख आर्थिक संकट अनुभवास आले. या संकटातून उद्भवलेल्या समस्या सोडविण्यासाठी सरकारने पुढील कार्यक्रम सुरू केला: (a) समग्र आर्थिक स्थिरीकरण (b) संरचनात्मक सुधारणा (c) राष्ट्रीय शिक्षण धोरण खालीलपैकी कोणते बरोबर आहे?', '{"A": "फक्त (a)", "B": "फक्त (b)", "C": "दोन्ही (a) आणि (b)", "D": "फक्त (c)"}'::jsonb, 'C', '1991 crisis: macroeconomic stabilisation (a) + structural reforms/LPG (b)। National Education Policy — balance-of-payments emergency unrelated पर्याय A (फक्त (a)) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय B (फक्त (b)) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय D (फक्त (c)) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात।', '{"Economy","MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)","2024","Industry, Trade & Reforms"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20704, 'Panchayati Raj', 'Polity', 'MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)', 2024, 'भारतीय राज्यघटनेतील पंचायत राज्य व्यवस्थेशी संबंधित कलम 243-A यामध्ये खालीलपैकी कोणती तरतूद आहे?', '{"A": "राखीव जागा", "B": "ग्राम सभा", "C": "पंचायतींची निवडणूक", "D": "पंचायतींचे लेखापरिक्षण"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Article 243-A explicitly Gram Sabha — registered voters village assembly. Reservation 243-D; elections 243-K; audit elsewhere — 243-A Gram Sabha anchor पर्याय A (राखीव जागा) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (पंचायतींची निवडणूक) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (पंचायतींचे लेखापरिक्षण) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Polity","MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)","2024","Panchayati Raj"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20705, 'Industry, Trade & Reforms', 'Economy', 'MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)', 2024, 'आंतरराष्ट्रीय नाणेनिधी (IMF) ने 1991 मध्ये भारताला मदत देण्यासाठी खालीलपैकी कोणती अट ठेवली होती?', '{"A": "आयात शुल्कात वाढ", "B": "निर्यातीत वाढ", "C": "भारतीय रूपयाचे अवमूल्यन", "D": "आंतरराष्ट्रीय व्यापार कमी करणे"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'IMF 1991 conditionality — rupee devaluation export competitiveness. Import duty increase, cut international trade — adjustment programme opposite पर्याय A (आयात शुल्कात वाढ) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B (निर्यातीत वाढ) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (आंतरराष्ट्रीय व्यापार कमी करणे) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Economy","MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)","2024","Industry, Trade & Reforms"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20706, 'Industry, Trade & Reforms', 'Economy', 'MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)', 2024, 'खालीलपैकी कोणत्या राज्यात पहिल्या निर्यात प्रक्रिया क्षेत्राची स्थापना झाली?', '{"A": "महाराष्ट्र", "B": "गुजरात", "C": "राजस्थान", "D": "दिल्ली"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'India first Export Processing Zone Kandla, Gujarat (1965)। Maharashtra, Rajasthan, Delhi — later zones; Gujarat first EPZ economic geography MCQ पर्याय A (महाराष्ट्र) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (राजस्थान) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (दिल्ली) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Economy","MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)","2024","Industry, Trade & Reforms"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20707, 'Panchayati Raj', 'Polity', 'MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)', 2024, 'भारतीय राज्यघटनेतील खालीलपैकी कोणते कलम ग्रामसभेशी संबंधित आहे?', '{"A": "कलम 244 C", "B": "कलम 243 D", "C": "कलम 243 A", "D": "कलम 241 A"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Gram Sabha constitutionally Article 243-A (Part IX)। 244-C Scheduled Areas variant; 243-D reservation; fictive 241-A — 243-A direct provision पर्याय A (कलम 244 C) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B (कलम 243 D) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (कलम 241 A) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Polity","MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)","2024","Panchayati Raj"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20708, 'Revolutionary Movement', 'History', 'MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)', 2024, 'आर्य बांधव समाज ही गुप्त संघटना उभी करण्यात खालीलपैकी कोणाची महत्वाची भूमिका होती?', '{"A": "शामराव देशपांडे", "B": "श्रीधर हरी खेर", "C": "व्यंकटेश खानखोजे", "D": "सिद्धनाथ कृष्ण काणे"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पर्याय C (व्यंकटेश खानखोजे) — आर्य बांधव समाज ही गुप्त क्रांतिकारी संघटना उभी करण्यात त्यांची महत्त्वाची भूमिका होती. शामराव देशपांडे, श्रीधर खेर आणि सिद्धनाथ काणे इतर सामाजिक किंवा राजकीय संदर्भात ओळखले जातात, पण या गुप्त संघटनेचे नेतृत्व खानखोजे यांच्याशी जोडले जाते।', '{"History","MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)","2024","Revolutionary Movement"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20709, 'Panchayati Raj', 'Polity', 'MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)', 2024, 'लॉर्ड रिपनचा ठराव, ज्याला भारताच्या स्थानिक स्वराज्य संस्थांचा ''मॅग्ना कार्टा'' असे म्हणतात, कोणत्या वर्षी संमत झाला?', '{"A": "1726", "B": "1935", "C": "1882", "D": "1687"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Lord Ripon 1882 local self-government resolution — India local bodies Magna Carta। 1726/1687 Company-era; 1935 provincial autonomy — Ripon local-government charter पर्याय A (1726) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर C (1882) आहे; पर्याय B (1935) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर C (1882) आहे; पर्याय D (1687) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर C (1882) आहे।', '{"Polity","MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)","2024","Panchayati Raj"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20710, 'Panchayati Raj', 'Polity', 'MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)', 2024, 'महाराष्ट्रातील जिल्हा परिषदा आणि पंचायत समित्या यांच्या स्थापनेशी संबंधित असणारा अधिनियम कोणता आहे?', '{"A": "अधिनियम 1958", "B": "अधिनियम 1961", "C": "अधिनियम 1988", "D": "अधिनियम 1948"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Maharashtra Zilla Parishads, Panchayat Samitis Act 1961 — three-tier framework। 1958, 1988, 1948 — other legislative dates; 1961 post-Balwantrai Mehta पर्याय A (अधिनियम 1958) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (अधिनियम 1988) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (अधिनियम 1948) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Polity","MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)","2024","Panchayati Raj"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20711, 'Industry, Trade & Reforms', 'Economy', 'MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)', 2024, 'जुलै 1991 पासून सरकारने व्यापार क्षेत्रात सुधारणांची मालिका सुरू केली असून त्यांचा हेतू भारतीय अर्थव्यवस्था उर्वरित जगाशी उत्तम जोडणे हा आहे. (a) रुपयाचे अवमूल्यन (b) रुपयाची परिवर्तनीयता प्रथम व्यापार आणि नंतर चालू खात्यावर (c) आयात शिथिलीकरण आणि व्यापाराचे बिगर सरकारीकरण (d) निर्यात वृद्धी उपाय खालीलपैकी कोणते बरोबर आहे?', '{"A": "फक्त (a) आणि (b)", "B": "फक्त (c) आणि (d)", "C": "फक्त (a), (b) आणि (c)", "D": "सर्व (a), (b), (c) आणि (d)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'जुलै १९९१ पासील व्यापार सुधारणांमध्ये रुपयाचे अवमूल्यन (a), परिवर्तनीयता (b), आयात शिथिलीकरण (c) व निर्यात वाढ (d) — चारही सत्य. आर्थिक संकटात सर्वसमावेशक पॅकेज होते. फक्त (a)-(b) किंवा (c)-(d) घेणे अपुरे; म्हणून पर्याय D (सर्व) बरोबर, A, B, C अपूर्ण।', '{"Economy","MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)","2024","Industry, Trade & Reforms"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20712, 'Panchayati Raj', 'Polity', 'MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)', 2024, 'जिल्हा परिषदेच्या स्थायी समितीबाबत पुढील विधाने विचारात घ्या. (a) स्थायी समितीसाठी स्वतंत्र सभापतीची तरतूद आहे. (b) जिल्हा परिषदेचे अध्यक्ष हे स्थायी समितीचे अध्यक्ष असतात. (c) जि.प. चे मुख्य कार्यकारी अधिकारी हे स्थायी समितीचे सचिव असतात. (d) जि.प. चे उपमुख्य कार्यकारी अधिकारी हे स्थायी समितीचे सचिव म्हणून काम पाहतात. वरीलपैकी योग्य विधाने निवडा.', '{"A": "(a), (b), (c) बरोबर", "B": "(b), (c) बरोबर", "C": "(b), (d) बरोबर", "D": "यापैकी नाही"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Zilla Parishad Chairperson Standing Committee chair (b); Deputy CEO secretary (d)। Independent chair (a), CEO as secretary (c) — Maharashtra Panchayat law wrong पर्याय A ((a), (b), (c) बरोबर) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B ((b), (c) बरोबर) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (यापैकी नाही) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Polity","MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)","2024","Panchayati Raj"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20713, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)', 2024, 'डॉ. बाबासाहेब आंबेडकर यांनी कोलंबिया विद्यापीठातील एम.ए.च्या पदवीसाठी कोणता प्रबंध लिहीला?', '{"A": "प्राचीन भारतातील व्यापार", "B": "भारताच्या राष्ट्रीय नफ्याचा वाटा", "C": "रूपयाचा प्रश्न", "D": "बुद्ध आणि त्याचा धम्म"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Ambedkar Columbia M.A. thesis Ancient Indian Commerce. National Dividend, Problem of Rupee, Buddha and his Dhamma — later London/LSE phases पर्याय B (भारताच्या राष्ट्रीय नफ्याचा वाटा) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (रूपयाचा प्रश्न) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (बुद्ध आणि त्याचा धम्म) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"History","MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)","2024","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20714, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)', 2024, 'इ.स. 1920 मध्ये माणगांव येथील दक्षिण महाराष्ट्र बहिष्कृत वर्गाच्या परिषदेच्या आयोजनाशी खालीलपैकी कोणत्या व्यक्ती संबंधित होत्या? (a) आप्पासाहेब दादागौंडा पाटील (b) दत्तोबा पवार (c) तुकाराम गणेशाचार्य (d) गंगाराम कांबळे', '{"A": "(a) आणि (b) फक्त", "B": "(b) आणि (c) फक्त", "C": "(c) आणि (d) फक्त", "D": "वरील सर्व बरोबर"}'::jsonb, 'D', '1920 Mangaon Dakshin Maharashtra Bahishkrut Parishad — Appasaheb Patil, Dattoba Pawar, Tukaram Ganeshacharya, Gangaram Kamble. Partial (a)(b) only under-count collective leadership पर्याय A ((a) आणि (b) फक्त) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय B ((b) आणि (c) फक्त) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय C ((c) आणि (d) फक्त) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात।', '{"History","MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)","2024","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20715, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)', 2024, 'खालीलपैकी योग्य विधान ओळखा. (a) श्रीमती विल्सन मुलींसाठी मुंबईत तीन शाळा चालवित होत्या. (b) स्कॉटिश मिशनने पुण्यात पहिली इंग्रजी शाळा सुरू केली. (c) मुलींच्या शिक्षणाचा प्रारंभ मुंबईत अमेरिकन मराठी मिशनने केला.', '{"A": "(a), (b), (c)", "B": "(b), (c)", "C": "केवळ (b)", "D": "केवळ (a)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Mrs Wilson Bombay girls schools; Scottish Mission Pune first English school; American Marathi Mission Mumbai girls education — colonial Maharashtra missionary triad all hold पर्याय B ((b), (c)) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (केवळ (b)) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय D (केवळ (a)) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात।', '{"History","MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)","2024","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20716, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)', 2024, 'विष्णुबुवा ब्रह्मचारी यांनी खालीलपैकी कोणत्या वृत्तपत्राद्वारे वैदीक धर्मावरील टीकेला चोख प्रत्युत्तर दिले होते?', '{"A": "वर्तमान दीपिका", "B": "ज्ञानोदय", "C": "ज्ञान प्रकाश", "D": "संस्कृत चंद्रीका"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Vishnubuwa Brahmachari Vartaman Deepika — Vedic religion polemic defend. Dnyanoday, Dnyan Prakash, Sanskrit Chandrika — other periodicals, different editors पर्याय B (ज्ञानोदय) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (ज्ञान प्रकाश) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (संस्कृत चंद्रीका) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"History","MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)","2024","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20717, 'International Affairs & Summits', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)', 2024, 'खालीलपैकी अयोग्य विधान/ने कोणते/ती? (a) नीमरान संवाद हा भारत-चीन संबंधाविषयी आहे. (b) ओटावा संवाद हा भारत-पाकिस्तान संबंधाविषयी आहे. (c) शांग्री-ला संवाद हा भारत-सिंगापुर संबंधाविषयी आहे. (d) रायसीना संवाद हा भारताच्या भूराजकीय आणि भूआर्थिक गोष्टीसंबंधीची शिखर परिषद आहे. योग्य पर्याय निवडा:', '{"A": "(a), (b), (c)", "B": "(b), (c), (d)", "C": "(a), (c)", "D": "(c), (d)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Neemrana dialogue India–China track-II; Shangri-La Asia-wide security not India–Singapore bilateral. Raisina (d) correct geo-politics summit; Ottawa Pakistan (b) wrong label पर्याय A ((a), (b), (c)) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B ((b), (c), (d)) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D ((c), (d)) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)","2024","International Affairs & Summits"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20718, 'International Affairs & Summits', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)', 2024, '''टू स्टेट सोल्युशन'' हा शब्द काहीवेळा बातम्यांमध्ये कोणत्या देशाच्या घडामोडींच्या संदर्भात उल्लेखला जातो?', '{"A": "चीन", "B": "उत्तर कोरिया", "C": "इराक", "D": "इस्राईल"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Two-state solution news — Israel–Palestine sovereign states side by side. China/Taiwan, Korea reunification, Iraq — different diplomatic vocabularies; Middle-East peace shorthand पर्याय A (चीन) या वाक्यातील व्याकरण/अर्थाशी शब्दयोगी अव्ययाच्या निकषाशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B (उत्तर कोरिया) या वाक्यातील व्याकरण/अर्थाशी शब्दयोगी अव्ययाच्या निकषाशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (इराक) या वाक्यातील व्याकरण/अर्थाशी शब्दयोगी अव्ययाच्या निकषाशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)","2024","International Affairs & Summits"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20719, 'National Appointments & Reports', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)', 2024, 'भारत सरकारद्वारे नेमण्यात आलेल न्या. जी. रोहिणी यांच्या नेतृत्वाखालील आयोग चर्चेत आहे. या आयोगाचा उद्देश काय आहे?', '{"A": "कुस्तीपटूंवर होणारा अन्याय दूर करणे.", "B": "प्रबळ ओबीसी जाती-गटांमधील आरक्षण आणि फायदे यांचे केंद्रीकरण तपासणे.", "C": "संरक्षण क्षेत्रातील आधुनिकीकरणासाठी सुधारणा सुचवणे.", "D": "भ्रष्टाचार आणि काळा पैसा यावर नियंत्रण ठेवणे."}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Rohini Commission — OBC reservations sub-categorisation; dominant OBC castes corner benefits examine. Wrestlers, defence modernisation, black money — unrelated 2020s commission headlines पर्याय A (कुस्तीपटूंवर होणारा अन्याय दूर करणे.) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (संरक्षण क्षेत्रातील आधुनिकीकरणासाठी सुध…) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (भ्रष्टाचार आणि काळा पैसा यावर नियंत्रण …) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)","2024","National Appointments & Reports"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20720, 'Awards & Honours', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)', 2024, '2023 मधील शांततेसाठीचा नोबेल पुरस्कार कोणाला देण्यात आला आहे?', '{"A": "नर्गिस मोहम्मदी", "B": "पियरे ऑगस्टिनी", "C": "जॉन फॉस्से", "D": "क्लॉडीया गोल्डीन"}'::jsonb, 'A', '2023 Nobel Peace Prize — Narges Mohammadi Iran human-rights. Pierre Agostini, Jon Fosse, Claudia Goldin — Physics, Literature, Economics separate categories पर्याय B (पियरे ऑगस्टिनी) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (जॉन फॉस्से) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (क्लॉडीया गोल्डीन) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)","2024","Awards & Honours"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20721, 'International Affairs & Summits', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)', 2024, 'दक्षिणपूर्व आशियाई देशांबरोबरचे संबंध दृढ करण्यासाठी भारताने राबविलेल्या परराष्ट्र धोरणाला सध्या काय नाव दिले आहे?', '{"A": "मस्ट ईस्ट", "B": "ॲक्ट ईस्ट", "C": "फास्ट ईस्ट", "D": "जस्ट ईस्ट"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'India Act East policy — Southeast Asia deeper trade, connectivity, strategic ties (Look East successor)। Must/Fast/Just East — MEA branding invented distractors पर्याय A (मस्ट ईस्ट) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (फास्ट ईस्ट) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (जस्ट ईस्ट) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)","2024","International Affairs & Summits"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20722, 'International Affairs & Summits', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)', 2024, '1960 मध्ये भारत आणि पाकिस्तान यांच्यातील सिंधू जल करारानुसार भारत आणि पाकिस्तानला कोणत्या नद्या देण्यात आल्या?', '{"A": "रावी, सतलज आणि बियास भारताला आणि सिंधू, चिनाब आणि झेलम पाकिस्तानला", "B": "रावी, सतलज आणि बियास पाकिस्तानला आणि सिंधू, चिनाब आणि झेलम भारताला", "C": "मेघना, पद्मा आणि सोमेश्वरी भारताला आणि सिंधू, महानंदा आणि कोसी पाकिस्तानला", "D": "यापैकी नाही"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Indus Waters Treaty 1960: Ravi, Sutlej, Beas India; Indus, Chenab, Jhelum Pakistan — western/eastern river split. Reverse allocation, Bangladesh rivers — Punjab–Sindh basin confuse पर्याय B (रावी, सतलज आणि बियास पाकिस्तानला आणि सि…) प्रश्नातील तथ्ये/गणना/व्याख्येशी विरोधाभासी आहे; पर्याय C (मेघना, पद्मा आणि सोमेश्वरी भारताला आणि …) प्रश्नातील तथ्ये/गणना/व्याख्येशी विरोधाभासी आहे; पर्याय D (यापैकी नाही) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)","2024","International Affairs & Summits"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20723, 'Other', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)', 2024, 'ग्राहक संरक्षण कायदा 2019 हा कोणत्या हेतूसाठी लागू करण्यात आला? (a) 1986 च्या ग्राहक संरक्षण कायद्याची जागा घेणे. (b) ग्राहक संरक्षणाच्या तरतूदी अधिक बळकट करणे. (c) ऑनलाईन व्यवहारात ग्राहकाल संरक्षण देणे. (d) जागतिकीकरणाच्या काळात ग्राहकाचे रक्षण करणे.', '{"A": "फक्त (a)", "B": "फक्त (a) आणि (d)", "C": "फक्त (b), (c) आणि (d)", "D": "(a), (b), (c) आणि (d)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'पर्याय D ((a), (b), (c) आणि (d)) — 2019 चा कायदा 1986 च्या कायद्याची जागा घेतो, ग्राहक संरक्षणाच्या तरतुदी मजबूत करतो, ऑनलाइन व्यवहार समाविष्ट करतो आणि जागतिक बाजारपेठेच्या संदर्भात उपाय देतो — चारही अधिकृत हेतू. फक्त (a) किंवा अर्धवट संयोजन कायद्याच्या सर्वसमावेशक सुधारणेचे अपूर्ण वाचन आहे।', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)","2024","Other"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20724, 'International Affairs & Summits', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)', 2024, 'खालीलपैकी कोणता देश दक्षिण आशियाई मुक्त व्यापार क्षेत्र (SAFTA) चा सभासद नाही?', '{"A": "अफगाणिस्तान", "B": "भूतान", "C": "मालदिव", "D": "म्यानमार"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'SAFTA/SAARC South Asian FTA — Myanmar ASEAN member, not SAFTA. Afghanistan, Bhutan, Maldives — SAFTA members; Myanmar include trap पर्याय A (अफगाणिस्तान) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B (भूतान) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (मालदिव) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)","2024","International Affairs & Summits"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20725, 'Trade Union & Labour Movement', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'In 1918 A.D., who advised to the Mumbai workers to establish the organization ''People''s Union''?', '{"A": "Rajashree Shahu Maharaj", "B": "Dr. Babasaheb Ambedkar", "C": "Narayan Meghaji Lokhande", "D": "Bhai Madhavrao Bagal"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The answer is option A: Rajashree Shahu Maharaj advised Mumbai workers in 1918 to form the ''People''s Union'' as part of his broader labour-welfare and anti-Brahmin reform agenda in Kolhapur and Bombay Presidency circles. Ambedkar''s mass union work came later; Lokhande led the Mill Hands'' Association; Bagal belongs to other cooperative strands—not this 1918 People''s Union prompt. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Trade Union & Labour Movement"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20726, 'International Affairs & Summits', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)', 2024, 'G-20 मध्ये पुढील देशांचा समावेश होत नाही? (a) अर्जेंटिना (b) इटली (c) इंडोनेशिया (d) पाकिस्तान (e) ताजिकिस्तान', '{"A": "(a), (d)", "B": "(a), (c), (e)", "C": "(d), (e)", "D": "(c), (e)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पर्याय C ((d), (e)) — G-20 मध्ये पाकिस्तान आणि ताजिकिस्तान सदस्य नाहीत; अर्जेंटिना, इटली आणि इंडोनेशिया सदस्य आहेत. पर्याय A, B आणि D मध्ये सदस्य देश नासदस्य म्हणून घेतले आहेत किंवा विरुद्ध — MPSC करंटमध्ये G-20 सदस्यत्वाची यादी लक्षात ठेवा।', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)","2024","International Affairs & Summits"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20727, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Pandita Ramabai with the permission of the Ramabai Association, appointed an advisory board to advise her, who among the following was included in this advisory board? i. Justice M. G. Ranade ii. Dr. R. G. Bhandarkar iii. Justice K. T. Telang iv. Bapu Hari Shinde', '{"A": "i and ii only", "B": "ii and iii only", "C": "i and iv only", "D": "i, ii and iii only"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D is correct because Pandita Ramabai''s advisory board under the Ramabai Association included Justice M. G. Ranade, Dr. R. G. Bhandarkar, and Justice K. T. Telang—leading reformers who backed her widows'' home and education work. Bapu Hari Shinde was a Dalit activist but not on this specific board;', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20728, 'Ancient India', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'On which of the following matrimonial relationship between two Royal families, the ancient drama ''Malavikagnimitra'' throws light?', '{"A": "Shunga and Vidarbha (Yadnyasen) family", "B": "Gupta and Vakataka family", "C": "Shakas and Satavahana family", "D": "Chalukya and Vardhana family"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Choose option A: Kalidasa''s Malavikagnimitra dramatises the marriage alliance between Pushyamitra Shunga''s son Agnimitra and the Vidarbha (Yajnaseni) princess Malavika. Gupta–Vakataka, Shaka–Satavahana, and Chalukya–Vardhana pairings belong to other dynastic phases—assigning the play to the wrong royal houses breaks standard ancient-India literature–polity links. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Ancient India"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20729, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Who defended Chiplunkar''s attack on Mahatma Jyotirao Phule through his newspaper, considered as the beginning of non Brahmin journalism?', '{"A": "Narayan Meghaji Lokhande", "B": "Bhau Daji Lad", "C": "Tukaram Tatya Padval", "D": "Krushnaji Bhalekar"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D matches the question because Krushnaji Bhalekar defended Chiplunkar''s newspaper attack on Jyotirao Phule—widely treated in Maharashtra history as an early spark of non-Brahmin journalism. Lokhande focused on mill labour; Bhau Daji Lad on Sanskrit-Orientalist scholarship; Padval on other reform channels—confusing them erases the Phule–Chiplunkar–Bhalekar press triangle examiners test. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20730, 'Other', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)', 2024, 'जागतिक पर्यटन दिन 2023 ची थीम काय आहे?', '{"A": "''पर्यटन आणि सांस्कृतिक विविधता''", "B": "''उत्तम उद्यासाठी शाश्वत पर्यटन''", "C": "''पर्यटन आणि हरित गुंतवणूक''", "D": "''पर्यटनातील नवीन क्षितीजे शोधणे''"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'UNWTO World Tourism Day 2023 theme — sustainable tourism green investment. Other phrases plausible past themes; 2023 specifically tourism+green investment पर्याय A (''पर्यटन आणि सांस्कृतिक विविधता'') या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B (''उत्तम उद्यासाठी शाश्वत पर्यटन'') या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (''पर्यटनातील नवीन क्षितीजे शोधणे'') या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Police Sub-Inspector (PSI)","2024","Other"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20731, 'Medieval India', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'According to Setu Madhavrao Pagadi, who of the following saint renamed himself as ''Shaha Ramjan'' and got converted to Islam by a Sufi Saint Nizamuddin. It is a mystery of cultural history of Maharashtra.', '{"A": "Gorakhnath", "B": "Gahininath", "C": "Jalandharnath", "D": "Kanifnath"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Setu Madhavrao Pagadi''s cultural-history note identifies Kanifnath of the Nath tradition as the saint who took the name ''Shaha Ramjan'' and accepted conversion through the Sufi Nizamuddin line—a debated Maharashtra mystic episode. Gorakhnath, Gahininath, and Jalandharnath belong to the wider Nath pantheon but not this specific Pagadi attribution.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Medieval India"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20732, 'Ancient India', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'What was the medium of trade exchange during vedic period? i. Nishka ii. Krusnal iii. Shatman iv. Gan v. Shreni', '{"A": "i, ii and iii", "B": "ii, iii and iv", "C": "i, ii, iv and v", "D": "i, iii and v"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A works here because Option A locks the Vedic exchange media: Nishka (gold ornament-coin), Krishnal/Krishnala (weight unit), and Shatamana (hundred-fold measure) functioned as recognised media of value. Gan and Shreni relate to guilds and collective enterprise rather than the metallic/token exchange triad the paper keys; bundling iv–v with i–iii overcounts non-currency terms. You can eliminate B (ii, iii and iv), C (i, ii, iv and v), D (i, iii and v) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Ancient India"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20733, 'Gandhian Mass Movements', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Arrange the following events in the correct order. i. White paper ii. Poona pact iii. Nehru report iv. Dharasna Satyagraha', '{"A": "iv, ii, iii, i", "B": "iv, i, ii, iii", "C": "iii, iv, ii, i", "D": "ii, iii, iv, i"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C works here because Chronology runs Nehru Report (1928), Dharasana Satyagraha (1930), Poona Pact (1932), and the White Paper on constitutional reform (1933). Sequences placing the White Paper before the Poona Pact or Dharasana before the Nehru Report invert the Gandhi–Ambedkar–Round Table timeline students drill for late-colonial constitutional politics. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Gandhian Mass Movements"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20734, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'The following statements are written about ______ a. He played an important role in the field of education in Maharashtra. b. He prepared textbooks on various subjects. c. He wrote a book ''Shunyalabdhi'' on Mathematics and Science in Marathi. d. Keshavrao Bhavalkar has written his biography.', '{"A": "Dadoba Pandurang Tarkhadkar", "B": "Atmaram Pandurang Tarkhadkar", "C": "Balshastri Jambhekar", "D": "Gopal Hari Deshmukh"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C is correct because Balshastri Jambhekar pioneered Marathi education, prepared textbooks, wrote ''Shunyalabdhi'' on mathematics and science, and drew a biography by Keshavrao Bhavalkar. Dadoba and Atmaram Tarkhadkar were Prarthana Samaj reformers; Lokhitwadi Deshmukh wrote ''Shatapatre''—swap any of them and the Shunyalabdhi clue no longer fits. You can eliminate A (Dadoba Pandurang Tarkhadkar), B (Atmaram Pandurang Tarkhadkar), D (Gopal Hari Deshmukh) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option C. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20735, 'British Expansion & Governors-General', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'About whom of the following statements are related? i. Religion was separated from politics. ii. Adopted a policy of seclusion towards brave women who followed Sati. iii. To stop child marriage and widow marriage was encouraged. iv. Claimed that the final decision regarding the social law will be his.', '{"A": "Babur", "B": "Humayun", "C": "Akbar", "D": "Aurangzeb"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Akbar separated religion from statecraft in policy, discouraged sati among Rajput women he sought to conciliate, encouraged widow remarriage, and reserved final say on social legislation—matching all four stem clauses. Babur and Humayun belong to earlier Mughal phases; Aurangzeb reversed many of Akbar''s eclectic policies—making him the wrong fit for this reformist profile.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","British Expansion & Governors-General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20736, 'Revolt of 1857', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Bhills in Khandesh protested against British rule because i. The Bhills of the Satpura division got inspiration from the event of the uprising in North India. ii. Taking advantage of the revolt of 1857 Bhagoji Naik and Kazising Naik joined the revolt. iii. Kazising and his associates burnt government treasuries and post offices.', '{"A": "i and ii", "B": "ii and iii", "C": "i and iii", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D works here because all three clauses stand for the 1857-linked Bhil upsurge in Khandesh: inspiration from the northern revolt, Bhagoji Naik and Kazising joining, and attacks on treasuries and post offices. Picking only two limbs overlooks how Satpura Bhil leaders connected local grievances with the wider rebellion—examiners expect the composite ''all of the above''. You can eliminate A (i and ii), B (ii and iii), C (i and iii) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option D. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Revolt of 1857"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20737, 'Rise of Nationalism & INC', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Arrange the following political organizations chronologically. a. Pune Sarvajanik Sabha b. Bombay Presidency Association c. Madras Mahajan Sabha d. Indian Association', '{"A": "b a d c", "B": "a d c b", "C": "c d b a", "D": "d b a c"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The answer is option B: Pune Sarvajanik Sabha (1870) precedes the Indian Association of Calcutta (1876), Madras Mahajan Sabha (1884), and Bombay Presidency Association (1885). Options starting with the Bombay Presidency Association or Madras Sabha place later regional congresses before the Pune Sabha''s documented founding—breaking the moderate-nationalist organisational chronology. Distractors A (b a d c), C (c d b a), D (d b a c) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Rise of Nationalism & INC"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20738, 'Gandhian Mass Movements', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Which of the following decision was taken by Sabarmati treaty?', '{"A": "A competitive co-operative party should be established.", "B": "Students should not be involved in politics.", "C": "There should be no discrimination among lower caste workers and a team of 50 volunteers should be formed and Hindu Muslim unity should be maintained.", "D": "A committee of Motilal Nehru and Jayakar to determine the members of the Central Legislature."}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D is the right choice since Option D reflects the Sabarmati ''treaty'' decision: a committee of Motilal Nehru and M. R. Jayakar would determine Central Legislature membership after the 1922 Bardoli–Sabarmati settlement context. Competitive co-operative party formation, student politics bans, and volunteer corps rules belong to other Gandhi-era resolutions—not this Nehru–Jayakar panel the official answer marks. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Gandhian Mass Movements"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20739, 'Tribal & Peasant Uprisings', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'In 1934 A.D., which of the following region witnessed the establishment of ''Karshak Sangham'' as a peasant organisation?', '{"A": "Andhra Pradesh", "B": "Tamil Nadu", "C": "Kerala", "D": "Bengal"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Kerala saw the formation of Karshak Sangham as a peasant organisation in 1934 within the broader agrarian mobilisation of the Malabar–Travancore belt. Andhra, Tamil Nadu, and Bengal had their own kisan fronts in different years—assigning Karshak Sangham outside Kerala scrambles regional peasant-union geography.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Tribal & Peasant Uprisings"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20740, 'Gandhian Mass Movements', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Who remarked about the ''Dandi Yatra'' as, Rama''s Historical March to Lanka?', '{"A": "Pandit Motilal Nehru and D. J. Tendulkar", "B": "P. C. Ray and D. P. Mishra", "C": "Shankarrao Dev and G. V. Ketkar", "D": "Appasaheb Patwardhan and Suhasini Nambiyar"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A is the right choice since Pandit Motilal Nehru and D. J. Tendulkar likened Gandhi''s Dandi March to ''Rama''s historical march to Lanka'' in contemporary commentary—mythic framing of the salt satyagraha. Shankarrao Dev, Ketkar, Patwardhan, and Nambiyar were active in other nationalist or constructive-work circles without this specific Dandi metaphor attribution. Distractors B (P. C. Ray and D. P. Mishra), C (Shankarrao Dev and G. V. Ketkar), D (Appasaheb Patwardhan and Suhasini Nambi…) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Gandhian Mass Movements"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20741, 'Biodiversity & Conservation', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Observe the following statements: A. There is loss of bio-diversity due to dumping of toxic waste into soil. B. Deforestation is responsible for frequent floods in river. C. Fransisco Mendez was known as ''Amazon Gandhi'' due to his work in energy field.', '{"A": "Only statement C is correct", "B": "Only statement A is correct", "C": "Only statement A and B are correct", "D": "Statement A, B and C are correct"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Toxic dumping destroys soil biodiversity and deforestation worsens flood peaks—statements A and B are sound environmental science. Francisco Mendez is mislabelled: Chico Mendes of the Amazon rubber-tappers'' movement is the ''Amazon Gandhi'' for forest protection, not an ''energy field'' figure—statement C alone is false.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Biodiversity & Conservation"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20742, 'Pollution', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Nitrogen fertilizers in soils releases ______ when broken down by bacteria.', '{"A": "Nitrogen dioxide (NO₂)", "B": "Nitrous oxide (N₂O)", "C": "Nitrogen trioxide (NO₃)", "D": "Nitrogen (N₂)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C matches the question because per the official key. Microbial breakdown of nitrogen fertilisers in soil can release nitrogen oxides; textbooks often cite nitrous oxide (N₂O) from denitrification, but Set A marks nitrogen trioxide (NO₃) here—defer to the official answer rather than debating nomenclature. N₂ is largely inert in this context; NO₂ is a pollutant gas but not the correct limb. You can eliminate A (Nitrogen dioxide (NO₂)), B (Nitrous oxide (N₂O)), D (Nitrogen (N₂)) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option C. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Pollution"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20743, 'Ecology & Ecosystems', 'General Studies', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Some species if eliminated seriously affect the ecosystem. These are called ______', '{"A": "Blue stone", "B": "Red stone", "C": "Yellow stone", "D": "Keystone"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D is correct because Option D names keystone species—organisms whose removal disproportionately collapses community structure (classic sea-otter–kelp examples). ''Blue/red/yellow stone'' labels are distractors with no standing in ecology textbooks; if a species is pivotal to ecosystem integrity, keystone is the precise term examiners want. You can eliminate A (Blue stone), B (Red stone), C (Yellow stone) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option D. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"General Studies","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Ecology & Ecosystems"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20744, 'Climate Change & Global Warming', 'General Studies', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'In relation to Ozone which statements are true? A. Ozone is called protection shield of the Earth. B. In 1985 it was clear that Ozone layer has holes. C. 16th September is celebrated as World Ozone Day. D. In 1989 chemicals responsible for Ozone depletion are banned to utilize.', '{"A": "Only A, B and C", "B": "Only B, C and D", "C": "Only A, C and D", "D": "All the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Choose option D: Ozone shields Earth from UV (A), the 1985 ozone-hole discovery over Antarctica is landmark (B), 16 September is World Ozone Day (C), and the 1987 Montreal Protocol (not 1989 ban wording in the stem) phased out ozone-depleting chemicals (D)—the paper treats all four as jointly true. Partial combinations undercount the Montreal–Vienna ozone-protection narrative. Distractors A (Only A, B and C), B (Only B, C and D), C (Only A, C and D) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"General Studies","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Climate Change & Global Warming"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20745, 'Home Rule Movement', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'In which of the following newspapers did Annie-Besant present her thoughts about Home Rule Movement? a. New India b. Common Weal c. Bombay Gazette d. Telegraph', '{"A": "a and b only", "B": "b and c only", "C": "a and d only", "D": "a, b and c only"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A matches the question because Option A is correct. Annie Besant propagated Home Rule ideas through her papers New India and Common Weal—not Bombay Gazette or Telegraph, which were establishment or Anglo-Indian dailies. Distractors B (b and c only), C (a and d only), D (a, b and c only) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Home Rule Movement"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20746, 'Other', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Observe the following diagram and state which of the following alphabets indicate the gibbous phase of the moon?', '{"A": "B and H", "B": "C and G", "C": "D and F", "D": "E and A"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'In a standard eight-phase moon wheel, gibbous phases (more than half but not full illumination) fall on the letter pairs the diagram marks as D and F—between quarter and full on both waxing and waning sides. Pairs at new crescent or exact quarter positions show crescent or quarter discs, not gibbous bulges.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Other"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20747, 'Other', 'General Studies', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, '"Environment means the sum total of all conditions agencies and influences which affect the development, growth, life and death of an organism, species or race." Who created this definition of environment?', '{"A": "Universal Encyclopedia", "B": "Britanica Encyclopedia", "C": "A. C. Tansley", "D": "Jackie Smith"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The quoted comprehensive definition of environment—as the sum of conditions and influences on an organism''s life—is attributed in the paper to the Universal Encyclopedia. Britannica and Tansley (ecosystem coinage) offer related but distinct formulations; Jackie Smith is an outlier name without this definitional citation.', '{"General Studies","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Other"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20748, 'Minerals & Industries', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'In the western part of Rajasthan minerals like limestone, gypsum and mineral salts reserves are distributed. Which of the following reasons are responsible for this occurrence? a. Western part of Rajasthan was submerged under sea water during permocarboniferous period. b. Western part of Rajasthan receives low rainfall. c. Western part of Rajasthan has hot and dry climate. d. In the western part of Rajasthan the area under vegetation is very low.', '{"A": "only a is correct", "B": "only a and b are correct", "C": "a, b and c are correct", "D": "only d is correct"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The answer is option A: Limestone, gypsum, and evaporite salt deposits in western Rajasthan largely owe to Permo-Carboniferous marine submergence and subsequent evaporation basins—not merely low rainfall or sparse vegetation today. Climate and vegetation (b–d) affect present weathering but do not explain the primary geological origin the question targets. You can eliminate B (only a and b are correct), C (a, b and c are correct), D (only d is correct) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Minerals & Industries"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20749, 'Agriculture & Soils', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Which of the following soil contain the maximum proportion of iron and bauxite minerals?', '{"A": "Red soil", "B": "Regur soil", "C": "Laterite soil", "D": "Alluvial soil"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C matches the question because Laterite soils, formed under intense tropical weathering, accumulate iron and aluminium (bauxite) oxides and appear brick-red. Red soil is iron-rich but not the maximum bauxite host; black regur is basalt-derived cotton soil; alluvial deposits are young and fertile—none match laterite''s ferralitic–bauxitic signature. Distractors A (Red soil), B (Regur soil), D (Alluvial soil) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Agriculture & Soils"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20750, 'Ecology & Ecosystems', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Which of the following is not the type of Ecological pyramid?', '{"A": "Pyramid of number", "B": "Pyramid of biomass", "C": "Pyramid of food web", "D": "Pyramid of energy"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C is the right choice since Ecological pyramids are built on numbers, biomass, or energy—not ''food webs,'' which are network diagrams of feeding links. Options listing number, biomass, or energy pyramids describe standard Elton–Lindeman constructs; choosing any of those as ''not a type'' would contradict basic ecosystem ecology. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Ecology & Ecosystems"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (20751, 'Maharashtra Physical Geography', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'In the physical map of India, Maharashtra plateau is shown by which of the following colours?', '{"A": "Dark green", "B": "Green", "C": "Yellow", "D": "Brown"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'On standard Survey of India physical maps the Maharashtra (Deccan) plateau is shown in yellow—distinct from green coastal strips and brown Himalayan/highland tones. Dark green and green typically mark lower plains or forested tracts; brown marks mountains—mixing colours scrambles the NCERT atlas convention.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Maharashtra Physical Geography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20752, 'Minerals & Industries', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Given below are two statements one labeled as Assertion (A) and other labeled as Reason (R). (A) Cotton is not a weight lossing pure raw material, besides is light in weight and durable. (R) The localization of the cotton textile is found either in cotton producing region or near market.', '{"A": "Both (A) and (R) are true and (R) is the correct explanation of (A)", "B": "Both (A) and (R) are true but (R) is not the correct explanation of (A)", "C": "(A) is true but (R) is false", "D": "(A) is false but (R) is true"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The correct answer is option B — Option B fits the assertion–reason pair: cotton is lightweight and not a pure weight-losing raw material (A true), and mills locate near cotton fields or markets (R true)—but market/cotton proximity rather than weight-loss logic directly explains localization, so R is not the correct explanation of A. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Minerals & Industries"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20753, 'Climatology', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Winter rainfall received by the Mediterranean region is the result of', '{"A": "Shifting of pressure belts", "B": "Low pressure belt occurs over the Mediterranean region during the winter season due to shifting of pressure belts", "C": "Winds blow from the Mediterranean sea towards land", "D": "Orographic rain developed on the windward slope of the Alps"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Mediterranean winter rains occur when the subtropical high-pressure belt shifts southward, allowing cyclonic westerlies and a low-pressure environment over the sea in winter. Shifting belts alone (A) is vague; onshore winds (C) describe a mechanism but not the pressure-belt cause; Alpine orographic rain (D) is local—not the basin-wide winter pattern.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Climatology"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20754, 'Climatology', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'The climatic phenomena retreating monsoon is the result of which of the following atmospheric condition in India?', '{"A": "After reaching to the Himalayan ranges the south-west monsoons retreats", "B": "The apparent movement of the Sun", "C": "The expansion of the high pressure belt from north-western part to south-eastern part of India", "D": "The occurrence of variability in the atmospheric pressure developed over the Indian sub-continent"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Choose option C: Option C captures retreating-monsoon dynamics in India: expansion of the north-west high-pressure belt south-eastward as the ITCZ withdraws, cutting off monsoon flow. Distractors A (After reaching to the Himalayan ranges …), B (The apparent movement of the Sun), D (The occurrence of variability in the at…) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Climatology"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20755, 'Maharashtra Physical Geography', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Which of the following is/are correct statements? In Maharashtra, in order from north, the major hill ranges on the plateau and the river basins to their south are as follows: a. Tapi Purna basin to the south of the Satpura mountain range. b. Godavari river valley to the south of Satmala Ajintha hills. c. Harishchandra Balaghat hill and Bhima river basin to its south. d. Shambhu Mahadeva hills and Krishna river basin to its south.', '{"A": "Only a", "B": "All are correct", "C": "Only a and b", "D": "Only a and c"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The correct answer is All are correct. The Godavari, the longest river of the Deccan (~1,465 km, ~668 km in Maharashtra), rises at Brahmagiri near Trimbakeshwar (Nashik) and drains eastward into the Bay of Bengal. The Krishna river rises at Mahabaleshwar in the Sahyadri and flows east across Maharashtra, Karnataka, Telangana and Andhra Pradesh before draining into the Bay of Bengal. The three incorrect options are close-sounding distractors; anchoring on the exact keyword in the stem eliminates them in seconds.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Maharashtra Physical Geography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20756, 'Maharashtra Physical Geography', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'The Sahyadri range is not straight but at many places it is curved, because', '{"A": "The Sahyadri range is curved at many places because of the headward erosion of the Konkan rivers originating in Sahyadri", "B": "The Sahyadri range is curved at many places because of the lateral erosion of the Konkan rivers originating in Sahyadri", "C": "The Sahyadri range is curved at many places because of the downward erosion of the Konkan rivers originating in Sahyadri", "D": "Due to heavy rainfall the Sahyadri range is heavily eroded and hence it is curved"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Choose option A: Konkan rivers erode headward into the Sahyadri scarp, cutting embayments that make the range appear sinuous rather than straight. Lateral or downward erosion alone misstates the dominant headward retreat process; attributing curvature merely to ''heavy rainfall'' without river mechanics is too vague for the correct explanation. You can eliminate B (The Sahyadri range is curved at many pl…), C (The Sahyadri range is curved at many pl…), D (Due to heavy rainfall the Sahyadri rang…) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Maharashtra Physical Geography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20757, 'Oceanography', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Trenches are found mainly along the coast of the western Pacific Ocean because', '{"A": "The western margin of the Pacific Ocean is the sub-duction zone", "B": "Along the western border of the Pacific Ocean parallel mountain ranges are aligned", "C": "The continental slope of the western part of the Pacific Ocean is steep", "D": "The western part of the Pacific Ocean is characterised by a large number of trenches"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A is correct because the western Pacific margin is a classic convergent/subduction boundary where oceanic lithosphere plunges beneath continental plates, creating deep ocean trenches. Parallel ranges (B) and steep slopes (C) are associated features but not the fundamental reason; counting trenches (D) describes distribution without explaining tectonic cause. You can eliminate B (Along the western border of the Pacific…), C (The continental slope of the western pa…), D (The western part of the Pacific Ocean i…) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Oceanography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20758, 'Indian Rivers & Drainage', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'As compared to the Godavari and Krishna rivers, the course of the Kaveri river receives large volume of water during winter, because', '{"A": "The course of the river Kaveri receives heavy rainfall from the south-west monsoons", "B": "The course of the river Kaveri receives heavy rainfall from the north-east monsoons", "C": "The course of the river Kaveri receives rainfall from both south-west and north-east monsoons", "D": "The tributaries of the Kaveri provide large volume of water to the course of the Kaveri"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Working through the options, The course of the river Kaveri receives heavy rainfall from the north-east monsoons is the correct one. The Godavari, the longest river of the Deccan (~1,465 km, ~668 km in Maharashtra), rises at Brahmagiri near Trimbakeshwar (Nashik) and drains eastward into the Bay of Bengal. The Krishna river rises at Mahabaleshwar in the Sahyadri and flows east across Maharashtra, Karnataka, Telangana and Andhra Pradesh before draining into the Bay of Bengal. Add this correct option to your active-recall flashcard deck; MPSC repeats the underlying fact in some form every two to three prelim cycles.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Indian Rivers & Drainage"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20759, 'Climatology', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'On which of the following day does the summer solstice occurs in the southern hemisphere?', '{"A": "21 March", "B": "21 June", "C": "23 September", "D": "22 December"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The correct answer is option D — Summer solstice in the Southern Hemisphere falls around 22 December, when the Sun is overhead at the Tropic of Capricorn. 21 June is the Northern Hemisphere summer solstice; March and September mark equinoxes—choosing June applies northern-season logic to the wrong hemisphere. Distractors A (21 March), B (21 June), C (23 September) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Climatology"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20760, 'Minerals & Industries', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'In his theory of industrial location Alfred Weber tried to establish the pivotal role of which of the following factors?', '{"A": "Labour cost plays a pivotal role in the selection of industrial location", "B": "Cost of raw material plays a pivotal role in the selection of industrial location", "C": "Market accessibility plays a pivotal role in the selection of industrial location", "D": "Transport cost plays a pivotal role in the selection of industrial location"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Alfred Weber''s industrial-location theory centres transport costs—weight loss en route and distance to markets— as the pivotal locational force in his triangle/least-cost framework. Labour, raw-material, or market accessibility matter as secondary agglomerative factors in extensions, but Weber''s core is transport minimisation.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Minerals & Industries"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20761, 'Other', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Consider the following statements and select the correct answer using the code given below. 1. A compact settlement is most probably surrounded by hamlets. 2. Compact settlements are not found in the Himalayan region.', '{"A": "Only 1 is correct", "B": "Only 2 is correct", "C": "Both 1 and 2 are correct", "D": "Neither 1 nor 2 is correct"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The answer is option B: Option B is correct. Compact settlements are dense nucleated villages—not typically surrounded by hamlets (statement 1 false); and they are largely absent in rugged Himalayan terrain where dispersed/linear patterns dominate (statement 2 true). Accepting both statements (C) or statement 1 alone (A) contradicts standard settlement-geography classification. You can eliminate A (Only 1 is correct), C (Both 1 and 2 are correct), D (Neither 1 nor 2 is correct) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option B. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Other"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20762, 'Electricity & Magnetism', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, '______ are materials whose resistivities become zero below a critical temperature.', '{"A": "Conductors", "B": "Insulators", "C": "Super conductors", "D": "None of these"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Superconductors exhibit zero electrical resistivity below a critical temperature—distinct from ordinary conductors, insulators, or generic ''none''. Options naming normal conductors or insulators miss the phase-transition phenomenon discovered in mercury and cuprate materials.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Electricity & Magnetism"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20763, 'Optics & Sound', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'If an object is placed symmetrically between two plane mirrors inclined at an angle of 36°, then how many images will be formed?', '{"A": "8", "B": "9", "C": "10", "D": "11"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'For mirrors inclined at θ, number of images = (360/θ) − 1; at 36° that gives 10 − 1 = 9. Answers 8, 10, or 11 apply wrong formulas or forget the subtract-one rule for symmetric placement between two plane mirrors.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Optics & Sound"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20764, 'Modern & Nuclear Physics', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'When α-particle emits from a radioactive element then', '{"A": "atomic number decreases by 2 and mass number decreases by 4", "B": "atomic number decreases by 1 and mass number decreases by 2", "C": "atomic number increases by 1", "D": "atomic number and mass number remains same"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Choose option A: alpha emission ejects a helium nucleus (²He⁴), reducing atomic number by 2 and mass number by 4. Beta emission shifts atomic number by 1 without the −4 mass change; ''no change'' describes gamma decay—mixing these transformation rules is a common radioactivity trap. Distractors B (atomic number decreases by 1 and mass n…), C (atomic number increases by 1), D (atomic number and mass number remains s…) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Modern & Nuclear Physics"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20765, 'Mechanics & Motion', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'P/ρ + hg + ½v² = constant is the mathematical statement of ______ [CANCELLED]', '{"A": "Equation of continuity", "B": "Bernoulli''s equation", "C": "Pascal''s law", "D": "Euler''s equation"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A is the right choice since MPSC cancelled this question—no official key applies in scored papers. The equation P/ρ + gh + ½v² = constant is Bernoulli''s principle (option B in content), while the correct option A (continuity equation) conflicts with standard fluid mechanics—likely why the item was withdrawn. Treat it as non-examinable rather than forcing a live answer. You can eliminate B (Bernoulli''s equation), C (Pascal''s law), D (Euler''s equation) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Mechanics & Motion"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20766, 'Nutrition', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Match the following – Vitamins and respective deficiency diseases: a. Vit. A b. Vit. D c. Vit. C d. Vit. B₁₂ i. Rickets ii. Scurvy iii. Anaemia iv. Night blindness', '{"A": "iii, ii, iv, i", "B": "iv, i, ii, iii", "C": "i, iv, iii, ii", "D": "ii, iii, iv, i"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B works here because Match vitamins to deficiencies: A → night blindness (iv), D → rickets (i), C → scurvy (ii), B₁₂ → anaemia (iii)—grid B. Swapping rickets with scurvy or B₁₂ with A misaligns well-memorised nutrition pairs tested in every biology paper. Distractors A (iii, ii, iv, i), C (i, iv, iii, ii), D (ii, iii, iv, i) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Nutrition"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20767, 'Heat & Thermodynamics', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'The fever of a child is 104°F. What is this temperature in degree Celsius?', '{"A": "35°C", "B": "37°C", "C": "39°C", "D": "40°C"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Convert Fahrenheit to Celsius: (104 − 32) × 5/9 = 40°C. Values near normal body temperature (37°C) or 35°C ignore the high fever reading; 39°C is closer but still below the exact conversion the calculation demands.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Heat & Thermodynamics"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20768, 'Other', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Which of the following statement is correct?', '{"A": "The speed of Planet is faster when they are nearer to the sun and slower when they are farther away from the sun.", "B": "The speed of Planet is faster when they are farther from the sun and slower when they are nearer to the sun.", "C": "The speed of Planet is same when they are nearer to the sun or farther away from the sun.", "D": "The speed of Planet is faster when they are nearer to the sun or farther away from the sun."}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A states Kepler''s second-law logic: planets move faster at perihelion (near the Sun) and slower at aphelion—conservation of areal velocity. Reversed speed-distance relations (B) or constant speed (C) contradict orbital mechanics; the ''both faster'' option (D) is nonsensical.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Other"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20769, 'Zoology (Animal Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Conchology is the study of what?', '{"A": "Coelenterates", "B": "Mollusca", "C": "Shells of Mollusca", "D": "Mantle of Mollusca"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The answer is option C: Conchology is the branch devoted to mollusc shells—their structure, taxonomy, and collection. General Mollusca study is malacology; coelenterates and mantle alone are narrower or wrong phylum targets—''shells of Mollusca'' is the precise definition. You can eliminate A (Coelenterates), B (Mollusca), D (Mantle of Mollusca) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option C. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Zoology (Animal Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20770, 'Zoology (Animal Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Phyllum Mollusca contains soft bodied animals characterized of: a. They are second largest phyllum in animal kingdom b. They are generally bilaterally symmetrical c. They are only Terrestrial animals d. They are having muscular foot Which of the statements given above is/are correct?', '{"A": "only a", "B": "a, b and d", "C": "a, b and c", "D": "only a and b"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B matches the question because Mollusca is the second-largest phylum, generally bilaterally symmetrical, and possesses a muscular foot—statements a, b, and d. Claiming they are only terrestrial (c) is incorrect because most molluscs are marine or freshwater; options keeping (c) overcount a false restriction. Distractors A (only a), C (a, b and c), D (only a and b) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Zoology (Animal Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20771, 'Botany (Plant Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Anguina tritici is the parasitic nematode found on ______ plant.', '{"A": "Wheat", "B": "Rice", "C": "Jowar", "D": "Bajra"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Anguina tritici (wheat seed gall nematode) parasitises wheat—not rice, jowar, or bajra. It is a classic crop-pathology example in Maharashtra agricultural science syllabi; assigning it to other cereals breaks the anguina–tritici (Triticum) name clue.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Botany (Plant Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20772, 'Government Schemes & Yojanas', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Who are the beneficiaries of Annapurna Yojana?', '{"A": "School girls", "B": "Casual labours", "C": "Senior citizens who are not under National Old Age Pension Scheme", "D": "Retired soldiers"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C is the right choice since annapurna Yojana supplies free food grains to indigent senior citizens not covered under the National Old Age Pension Scheme. School girls, casual labourers, and retired soldiers fall under other nutrition or pension programmes—not Annapurna''s targeted elderly food-security niche. You can eliminate A (School girls), B (Casual labours), D (Retired soldiers) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option C. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Government Schemes & Yojanas"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20773, 'Agriculture Economy', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Which of the following major policy interventions are the part of the land reforms in India? a. Abolition of intermediaries b. Tenancy reforms c. Fixing ceilings on land holdings d. Consolidation of land holdings', '{"A": "a, b and c", "B": "b, c and d", "C": "a, b and d", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D lists all four pillars of Indian land reform: abolition of intermediaries, tenancy reform, ceiling on holdings, and consolidation. Omitting any one—intermediaries, tenancy, or consolidation—understates the integrated post-Independence agrarian policy bundle the planning era implemented.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Agriculture Economy"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20774, 'Growth, Inflation & Indicators', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Balanced growth rate aims at', '{"A": "equality between growth rate of income, growth rate of output and growth rate of natural resources", "B": "equality between growth rate of income and growth rate of population", "C": "equality between growth rate of natural resources and growth rate of income", "D": "equality between growth rate of natural resources and growth rate of population"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The correct answer is option A — ''Balanced growth rate'' in development literature seeks alignment between growth of national income, output, and natural-resource use—sustainable macro balance. Pairing income only with population (B) or resources with population (D) describes different Harrod–Domar or demographic-equilibrium ideas, not the three-way balance correct here. Distractors B (equality between growth rate of income …), C (equality between growth rate of natural…), D (equality between growth rate of natural…) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Growth, Inflation & Indicators"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20775, 'Population & Demography', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Urbanization means a. Centralization of population in the cities b. Decentralization of population in the cities c. Centralization of population in villages d. Increase in density of population', '{"A": "Only a", "B": "Only a and b", "C": "Only a and d", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Urbanisation means concentration of population in cities (a)—not decentralisation within cities (b), village centralisation (c), or density alone without urban shift (d). Options bundling decentralisation or village trends describe counter-urbanisation or rural dynamics, not urbanisation proper.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Population & Demography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20776, 'Government Schemes & Yojanas', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Which of the following statements about Atal Mission for Rejuvenation and Urban Transformation (AMRUT) is not correct?', '{"A": "AMRUT is flagship mission of Government of India", "B": "It was launched by Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs", "C": "It addresses the challenges of water supply in cities across the country", "D": "It was launched on 25th June, 2015 in 500 cities in the country"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C is correct because the statement marked incorrect is (C)—the paper keys that AMRUT''s description as stated is incorrect its official framing (Set A). Flagship status (A), MoHUA launch (B), and the June 2015 rollout in selected cities (D) align with government releases; accept the correct ''not correct'' limb even if wording feels debatable. You can eliminate A (AMRUT is flagship mission of Government…), B (It was launched by Ministry of Housing …), D (It was launched on 25th June, 2015 in 5…) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option C. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Government Schemes & Yojanas"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20777, 'Poverty & Unemployment', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'If deprivation score of a household is ______ percent or greater, then that household is called multidimensionally poor.', '{"A": "20.33", "B": "50.33", "C": "40.33", "D": "33.3"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D gives the global MPI cutoff: a household is multidimensionally poor when its weighted deprivation score reaches at least 33.3%. Figures like 20.33%, 40.33%, or 50.33% are distractors near but not equal to the one-third threshold UNDP–OPHI methodology uses.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Poverty & Unemployment"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20778, 'Growth, Inflation & Indicators', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'According to Schumpeter, a. Development is a discontinuous and spontaneous change in the stationary state. b. While growth is a gradual and steady change in the long run which, comes about by a gradual increase in the rate of savings and population. Which of the statement above is/are correct?', '{"A": "a only", "B": "b only", "C": "a and b", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C is correct because Schumpeter distinguished discontinuous innovative ''development'' from gradual long-run ''growth'' driven by savings and population—both statements (a) and (b) capture his definitions. Choosing only one limb or ''none'' splits a paired conceptual distinction examiners treat as jointly valid. Distractors A (a only), B (b only), D (None of the above) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Growth, Inflation & Indicators"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20779, 'Growth, Inflation & Indicators', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Balanced growth theory requires balance between a. Consumer goods and industrial goods b. Capital goods and industrial goods c. Agricultural sector and industrial sector d. All sectors in the economy', '{"A": "Only a", "B": "Only c", "C": "Only d", "D": "Only a and b"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C is correct. Rosenstein-Rodan''s balanced-growth theory stresses simultaneous development across all sectors of the economy—not only consumer–industrial goods (a) or agriculture–industry (b) dyads. Narrow two-sector picks miss the big-push, economy-wide coordination the theory advocates.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Growth, Inflation & Indicators"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20780, 'Industry, Trade & Reforms', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Since July 1991, comprehensive liberalization measures have been undertaken to improve the supply side of the economy. Among these the more important are: a. Trade and capital flows reforms b. Industrial deregulation c. Disinvestment and Public Enterprises Reforms d. Financial sector reforms', '{"A": "a and b", "B": "c and d", "C": "a, b and c", "D": "a, b, c and d"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Post-July 1991 liberalisation bundled trade and capital-flow reforms, industrial deregulation, PSU disinvestment, and financial-sector reforms—all supply-side measures. Picking only trade–industry pairs (a–b) or only PSU–finance pairs (c–d) undercounts the comprehensive reform package.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Industry, Trade & Reforms"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20781, 'Economic Planning & Five Year Plans', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'The formulation and success of a plan require the following: a. Planning Commission, Statistical data, Objectives b. Fixation of Targets and Priorities, Mobilisation of Resources c. Incorrupt and Efficient Administration, Proper Development Policy d. Economy in Administration, Education base', '{"A": "a only", "B": "a and b", "C": "a, b and c", "D": "a, b, c and d"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D is the right choice since Successful planning needs institutions and data (a), target-setting and resource mobilisation (b), honest administration and policy (c), plus administrative economy and an education base (d)—all listed as requirements. Truncating to only (a) or (a)+(b) ignores implementation and human-capital prerequisites. Distractors A (a only), B (a and b), C (a, b and c) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Economic Planning & Five Year Plans"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20782, 'Poverty & Unemployment', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, '''A country is poor, because it is poor'' this statement is of ______', '{"A": "G. Myrdal", "B": "Ragnar Nurks", "C": "Robbins", "D": "Marshall"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Ragnar Nurkse''s vicious-circle thesis—''a country is poor because it is poor''—describes low saving, low investment, and poverty reinforcing each other. Myrdal''s cumulative causation, Robbins'' scarcity definition, and Marshallian partial equilibrium are different economic ideas.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Poverty & Unemployment"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20783, 'Economic Planning & Five Year Plans', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'The long-term objectives of economic planning, as spelt out in various plan documents have been as follows: a. Economic growth, self-reliance b. Removal of unemployment, reduction in income inequalities c. Elimination of poverty, modernization d. Inclusiveness and sustainability of growth', '{"A": "a only", "B": "b only", "C": "c only", "D": "a, b, c and d"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Choose option D: Long-term planning objectives span growth and self-reliance (a), unemployment and inequality reduction (b), poverty elimination and modernisation (c), and inclusive sustainable growth (d)—collectively in plan documents. Single-objective choices (a, b, or c alone) fragment the multi-goal planning charter. You can eliminate A (a only), B (b only), C (c only) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option D. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Economic Planning & Five Year Plans"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20784, 'Money & Banking', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'In 2014, the Government implemented which of the following Scheme for financial inclusion?', '{"A": "Demonetization Scheme", "B": "Property Disclosure Scheme", "C": "Pradhan Mantri Jan Dhan Yojana", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C matches the question because Pradhan Mantri Jan Dhan Yojana (2014) was the flagship financial-inclusion drive—no-frills accounts, RuPay cards, and insurance linkages. Demonetisation (2016) and income-disclosure schemes belong to other years and purposes—not the 2014 inclusion push the question names. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Money & Banking"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20785, 'Poverty & Unemployment', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Rangarajan Committee, 2014 defined poverty line for 2011-12 at Rs. ______ per capita per day consumption expenditure for urban areas and Rs. ______ per capita per day for rural areas.', '{"A": "Rs. 50 and Rs. 35", "B": "Rs. 47 and Rs. 32", "C": "Rs. 55 and Rs. 40", "D": "Rs. 60 and Rs. 45"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Rangarajan Committee (2014) set the 2011–12 poverty line at about ₹47 per capita per day (urban) and ₹32 (rural). Higher pairs like ₹50/₹35 or ₹55/₹40 misquote the committee''s published consumption-expenditure thresholds.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Poverty & Unemployment"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20786, 'Acids, Bases & Salts', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'How is 1.0N H₂SO₄ solution is prepared from 10 dm³ of 1.5M H₂SO₄ solution?', '{"A": "By adding 5 dm³ of water to it", "B": "By adding 294 g of H₂SO₄ to it", "C": "By adding 20 dm³ of water to it", "D": "By adding 174 g of H₂SO₄ to it"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The correct answer is option C — To dilute 10 dm³ of 1.5 M H₂SO₄ to 1.0 N (0.5 M for diprotic acid), total volume should reach 30 dm³—add 20 dm³ water. Adding 5 dm³ or mass of acid without proper volumetric dilution miscalculates normality from molarity for H₂SO₄. You can eliminate A (By adding 5 dm³ of water to it), B (By adding 294 g of H₂SO₄ to it), D (By adding 174 g of H₂SO₄ to it) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option C. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Acids, Bases & Salts"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20787, 'Acids, Bases & Salts', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Which of the following mathematical relationships should be used to calculate the pH of a 0.10M aqueous HCl solution?', '{"A": "pH = log₁₀(1.0 × 10⁻¹)", "B": "pH = log₁₀(1.0 × 10¹)", "C": "pH = -log₁₀(1.0 × 10⁻¹)", "D": "pH = -log₁₀(0.10 × 10¹)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C applies for strong acid: pH = −log₁₀[H⁺]; for 0.10 M HCl, [H⁺] = 0.10 = 1.0 × 10⁻¹, so pH = −log(10⁻¹) = 1. Positive-log or wrong concentration forms (A, B, D) yield incorrect pH values.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Acids, Bases & Salts"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20788, 'Chemical Bonding & Reactions', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Which of the following is correct for the shapes of NH₃ and BF₃?', '{"A": "NH₃ – Pyramidal and BF₃ – Pyramidal", "B": "NH₃ – Planar and BF₃ – Planar", "C": "NH₃ – Planar and BF₃ – Pyramidal", "D": "NH₃ – Pyramidal and BF₃ – Planar"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D works here because VSEPR gives NH₃ a pyramidal shape (lone pair on N) and BF₃ a trigonal planar shape (no lone pair on B). Pairing both as pyramidal or both as planar ignores the lone-pair repulsion difference central to undergraduate chemistry. Distractors A (NH₃ – Pyramidal and BF₃ – Pyramidal), B (NH₃ – Planar and BF₃ – Planar), C (NH₃ – Planar and BF₃ – Pyramidal) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Chemical Bonding & Reactions"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20789, 'Organic Chemistry', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Which of the following hydrocarbon has 80% carbon? (H = 1, C = 12)', '{"A": "Benzene", "B": "Methane", "C": "Ethane", "D": "Cyclohexane"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Ethane (C₂H₆) has mass 30 with 24 from carbon—80% carbon by mass. Methane is 75%, benzene and cyclohexane have higher carbon fractions but the correct 80% figure matches ethane''s 24/30 ratio with H=1, C=12.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Organic Chemistry"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20790, 'Public Finance & Budget', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'What is meant by Gender Budget?', '{"A": "Separate budget for men", "B": "Separate budget for women", "C": "Independent provisions for men in the general budget", "D": "Independent provisions for women in the general budget"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Choose option D: Gender budgeting tracks independent provisions for women within the general budget—not separate male/female budgets (A–B) nor vague ''provisions for men'' (C). It mainstreams gender impact across ministries while keeping accounts inside the unified budget framework. Distractors A (Separate budget for men), B (Separate budget for women), C (Independent provisions for men in the g…) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Public Finance & Budget"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20791, 'Organic Chemistry', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, '180 g of acetic acid (CH₃COOH) is mixed with 180 g of water (H₂O). The mole fraction of acetic acid in the resultant solution is [H = 1, C = 12, O = 16]', '{"A": "0.23", "B": "1.0", "C": "0.5", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The answer is option A: Moles: acetic acid 180 g ÷ 60 = 3 mol; water 180 g ÷ 18 = 10 mol; mole fraction of acid = 3/(3+10) ≈ 0.23. Answers 0.5 or 1.0 treat equal masses as equal moles—ignoring the 60 vs 18 g mol⁻¹ difference. You can eliminate B (1.0), C (0.5), D (None of the above) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Organic Chemistry"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20792, 'Cell Biology & Genetics', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, '______ are precursors of enzymes. a. Zymogens b. Ribosomes c. RNA d. Protein Which of the option given above is/are correct?', '{"A": "only a", "B": "only b and c", "C": "only a and c", "D": "only d"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The correct answer is option A — Zymogens are inactive enzyme precursors activated by cleavage (e.g., pepsinogen → pepsin). Ribosomes and RNA are not enzyme precursors; generic protein (d) is too broad—only zymogens carry the precise biochemistry label. Distractors B (only b and c), C (only a and c), D (only d) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Cell Biology & Genetics"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20793, 'Chemical Bonding & Reactions', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'If one mole of an ideal gas occupies 22.4 Lit at Standard Temperature and Pressure, then the value of the universal gas constant R is', '{"A": "0.0821 atm Lit mol⁻¹ K⁻¹", "B": "8.314 × 10⁷ Joules K⁻¹ mol⁻¹", "C": "82.1 atm Lit mol⁻¹ K⁻¹", "D": "8.314 erg K⁻¹ mol⁻¹"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A states R = 0.0821 L atm mol⁻¹ K⁻¹ from PV = nRT at STP (1 atm, 273 K, 22.4 L). The joule and erg forms in other options use wrong unit conversions or magnitudes—only 0.0821 matches the standard chemistry constant.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Chemical Bonding & Reactions"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20794, 'Chemical Bonding & Reactions', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Find the wrong pair.', '{"A": "Labiatae – Lamiaceae", "B": "Palmae – Arecaceae", "C": "Compositae – Clusiaceae", "D": "Umbelliferae – Apiaceae"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Compositae is the old name for Asteraceae (sunflower family)—not Clusiaceae (mangosteen family). Labiatae–Lamiaceae, Palmae–Arecaceae, and Umbelliferae–Apiaceae are valid synonym pairs; the Compositae–Clusiaceae link is the mismatched pair.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Chemical Bonding & Reactions"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20795, 'State Government', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Which of the following statement is not included in Article 164?', '{"A": "The Chief Minister shall be appointed by the Governor", "B": "The Council of Ministers shall not be collectively responsible to the State Legislature", "C": "The other Minister shall be appointed by the Governor on the advice of the Chief Minister", "D": "A Minister who for any period of six consecutive months is not a member of the Legislature of the State shall at the expiration of that period cease to be a minister"}'::jsonb, 'B', '"The Council of Ministers shall not be collectively responsible to the State Legislature" is the option marked correct in the official key. Article 16 guarantees equality of opportunity in matters of public employment. Article 164 states that the Chief Minister is appointed by the Governor and other ministers on the CM''s advice. This kind of item rewards steady factual reading over aggressive shortcut techniques — the marks come from having read the source once, not from clever elimination.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","State Government"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20796, 'Constitutional Framework & Preamble', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Indian citizenship of a person can be terminated if A. A person voluntary acquire the citizenship of some other country. B. A person who has become a citizen through registration is sentenced to imprisonment for 18 months within five years of his registration. C. The government of India is satisfied that citizenship was obtained by fraud. D. A person has shown disloyalty to the Constitution of India.', '{"A": "A, B and C", "B": "A, C and D", "C": "B and C", "D": "A, B, C and D"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The answer is option B: Citizenship terminates on voluntary foreign naturalisation (A), fraud (C), and disloyalty to the Constitution (D)—but not merely because a registered citizen received an 18-month sentence within five years (B), which is not a standard termination ground in the Citizenship Act list correct here. Distractors A (A, B and C), C (B and C), D (A, B, C and D) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Constitutional Framework & Preamble"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20797, 'Cell Biology & Genetics', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Which of the following statement/s is/are correct? a. Enzymes are organic catalyst that accelerate biochemical reaction. b. Enzymes are made up from proteins. c. Enzyme activity is not depends upon temperature. d. Amylase is an enzyme that act on starch.', '{"A": "a and b", "B": "a, c and d", "C": "a, b and d", "D": "all the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C works here because Enzymes are protein catalysts (a, b) and amylase digests starch (d); statement (c) is false because enzyme activity is strongly temperature-dependent with an optimum and denaturation at high heat. Options including (c) as true contradict basic enzymology lab observations. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Cell Biology & Genetics"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20798, 'Constitutional Framework & Preamble', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Which of the following is/are correct pair/s with regard to acceptance in the Indian Constitution? A. America – Post of Vice President B. Canada – The concept of ''Union'' for the Central Government C. South Africa – Election method of Rajya Sabha D. Ireland – Nomination method of the members of the Rajya Sabha by the President who have done special work in specific area', '{"A": "Only A", "B": "A and C", "C": "A, B and D", "D": "A, B, C and D"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'India borrowed the Vice-Presidency from the U.S. (A), ''Union'' strong-centre model from Canada (B), Rajya Sabha election method from South Africa (C), and Rajya Sabha nomination from Ireland (D)—all accepted pairs. Partial lists drop valid borrowings tested in polity comparison tables.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Constitutional Framework & Preamble"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20799, 'Constitutional & Statutory Bodies', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Which of the following is/are the main objective/s of Committee of Parliament on Official language? A. To review the progress made in the use of Hindi for official purposes of the Union and to make recommendations to increase the use of Hindi. B. Looking into the linguistic demands for new States and make suggestions in that regard. C. Identify the endangered language and make recommendations to protect and preserve them. D. Examine the vernacular education and make recommendations for effective implementation of the three languages formula.', '{"A": "A only", "B": "B, C and D", "C": "A and D", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Choose option A: the Committee of Parliament on Official Language reviews Hindi use in Union administration and recommends expansion—its core mandate (A). State reorganisation on language (B), endangered-language preservation (C), and three-language formula implementation (D) belong to other commissions—not this committee''s primary charter. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Constitutional & Statutory Bodies"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20800, 'Botany (Plant Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'What is the principal function of the light-dependent reactions of photosynthesis?', '{"A": "To transfer the NADH₂ and ATP", "B": "To utilize the NADPH and ATP", "C": "To generate the NADPH and ATP", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C is the right choice since Light-dependent reactions in the thylakoid generate ATP and NADPH used later in the Calvin cycle—they do not primarily ''utilise'' those products (B) or merely transfer NADH₂ (A). Option D over-bundles stages that belong to different photosynthetic phases. You can eliminate A (To transfer the NADH₂ and ATP), B (To utilize the NADPH and ATP), D (All of the above) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option C. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Botany (Plant Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (20801, 'Panchayati Raj', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Consider the following statement/s with reference to the President of Zilla Parishad. [CANCELLED] A. If 1/5th of the total number of members of the Zilla Parishad moves a motion of no confidence and passes it, the President has to resign from office. B. Sudhakarrao Naik''s cabinet took the decision to give ministerial status to the President of Zilla Parishad. C. Vasantrao Naik''s cabinet took the decision to give ministerial status to the President of Zilla Parishad. D. Vasantdada Patil''s cabinet took the decision to give ministerial status to the President of Zilla Parishad. Select the incorrect statements from the above.', '{"A": "A and C", "B": "B and D", "C": "A and B", "D": "C and D"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A works here because MPSC cancelled this question—no official key applies in scored papers. Statements on Zilla Parishad president no-confidence thresholds and which Maharashtra cabinet granted ministerial status to the president drew factual dispute. Treat as withdrawn; the correct option A is for reference only in self-study. Distractors B (B and D), C (A and B), D (C and D) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Panchayati Raj"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20802, 'Constitutional & Statutory Bodies', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Which of the following is/are non-constitutional body/bodies? I. NITI Aayog II. State Finance Commission III. National Commission for Backward Classes IV. Central Information Commission', '{"A": "Only I is correct", "B": "Only III and IV are correct", "C": "Only I, III and IV are correct", "D": "Only I and IV are correct"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Only I and IV are correct matches the question. The Finance Commission (Article 280) is constituted every five years by the President to recommend distribution of tax revenues between the Union and States and grants-in-aid. NITI Aayog (National Institution for Transforming India) replaced the Planning Commission on 1 January 2015; the PM is its ex-officio Chairperson. For MPSC prelims, one line of revision is enough to lock this fact into memory — add it to your one-page factual notebook.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Constitutional & Statutory Bodies"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20803, 'Constitutional & Statutory Bodies', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Key Provisions of Lokpal and Lokayukta (Amendment) Act, 2016: A. It amended the Lokpal and Lokayukta Act, 2013 (which came into force on 16 January 2014). B. It also amended Section 44 of the 2013 Act that deals with the Provision of furnishing details of assets and liabilities of Public Servants. C. Made it compulsory that all States should set up the office of the Lokayukta within one year. D. The Amendment has removed the period of 30 days for furnishing details of assets and liabilities of Public Servants. Which of the statements given above are correct?', '{"A": "A, B and C", "B": "A, B and D", "C": "A, C and D", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The answer is option B: Option B lists correct Lokpal Amendment Act 2016 points: it amended the 2013 Act and Section 44 on asset declarations, and removed the 30-day filing window (D)—while (C) wrongly claims compulsory Lokayukta in all states within one year, which the amendment did not impose. Bundling (C) with true limbs is incorrect the correct combination. You can eliminate A (A, B and C), C (A, C and D), D (All of the above) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option B. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Constitutional & Statutory Bodies"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20804, 'Elections & Representation', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Match the pairs correctly. A. Part – I → i. Fundamental Rights B. Part – III → ii. Panchayat Raj C. Part – IX → iii. Citizenship D. Part – II → iv. The Union and its territory', '{"A": "iv, ii, iii, i", "B": "iii, i, ii, iv", "C": "ii, iii, i, iv", "D": "iv, i, ii, iii"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D matches the question because Constitution parts map: Part I → Union and territory (iv), Part II → Citizenship (iii), Part III → Fundamental Rights (i), Part IX → Panchayats (ii). Any grid swapping FR with citizenship or Panchayats with territory breaks the Part-number memory table. You can eliminate A (iv, ii, iii, i), B (iii, i, ii, iv), C (ii, iii, i, iv) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option D. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Elections & Representation"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20805, 'Constitutional & Statutory Bodies', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Which of the following pair is incorrect? National Party of India – Year of establishment', '{"A": "Communist Party of India (Marxist) CPI-M – 1964", "B": "Communist Party of India (CPI) – 1926", "C": "Bahujan Samaj Party (B.S.P.) – 1984", "D": "All India Trinamool Congress (AITC) – 1998"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'CPI was founded in 1925 (Kanpur conference), not 1926—making the CPI–1926 pair wrong. CPI(M)–1964, BSP–1984, and AITC–1998 align with recognised national-party chronology; only the CPI date is off by one year in the correct trap.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Constitutional & Statutory Bodies"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20806, 'Constitutional Framework & Preamble', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Provisions of the Constitution relating to the administration of Scheduled Areas and Scheduled Tribes in Schedule – V', '{"A": "may be altered by the Governor", "B": "may be altered by the President", "C": "may be altered by the Parliament by Constitutional Amendment requiring special majority", "D": "may be altered by the Parliament by ordinary legislation"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Fifth Schedule provisions on Scheduled Areas and Tribes may be altered by Parliament through ordinary legislation—Governor and President have roles in regulation but not unilateral ''alteration'' of Schedule V framework as the correct answer stresses. Special-majority amendment (C) overstates the required procedure for these provisions.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Constitutional Framework & Preamble"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20807, 'Constitutional & Statutory Bodies', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Which of the following is/are a duties of National Commission for Backward Classes?', '{"A": "To enquire into specific complaints with respect to the deprivation of rights and safeguards of the socially and educationally backward classes", "B": "To participate and advise on the socio-economic development of the socially and educationally backward classes", "C": "To discharge other functions in relation to the protection, welfare, development and advancement of socially and educationally backward classes", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D is correct because NCBC enquires into deprivation complaints (A), advises on socio-economic development (B), and performs protection/welfare functions (C)—all statutory duties post-102nd Amendment. Single-clause picks overlook the commission''s comprehensive backward-classes mandate. Distractors A (To enquire into specific complaints wit…), B (To participate and advise on the socio-…), C (To discharge other functions in relatio…) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Constitutional & Statutory Bodies"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20808, 'Government Schemes & Yojanas', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Consider the following statements regarding ''Zero Hour'' of Lok Sabha: A. The time immediately following the question hour and laying of papers and before any listed business is taken up in the house has come to be known as the zero hour. B. For raising matters during the zero hour members has to give notice between 8.00 a.m. to 9.30 a.m. everyday to the Speaker. C. At present, thirty matters per day as per their priority are allowed to be raised during zero hour. D. There is no maximum limit on the number of matters that can be raised on any given day as there is no provision in rules about Zero Hour. Which of the statements given above are correct?', '{"A": "A and B", "B": "A, B and D", "C": "B, C and D", "D": "A and D"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The correct answer is option D — Zero Hour sits after Question Hour without formal rule limits (A, D)—members need not give 8–9.30 a.m. notice daily (B false), and the ''30 matters per day'' cap (C) is not a fixed rule. Pairing B with true limbs or accepting C contradicts Lok Sabha practice notes. You can eliminate A (A and B), B (A, B and D), C (B, C and D) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option D. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Government Schemes & Yojanas"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20809, 'Government Schemes & Yojanas', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Which of the following are the objectives of the ''SVAMITVA'' Scheme? A. Ensure financial stability to villagers by letting them use their property to take loans. B. Create precise land records for urban planning and implementation. C. Lessen property related disputes. D. Determine property tax.', '{"A": "Only A", "B": "B, C and D", "C": "A, C and D", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C captures SVAMITVA objectives correct here: property-backed financial access (A), dispute reduction (C), and property-tax determination (D)—while (B) on ''urban planning'' misstates a rural drone-survey and gram panchayat property-record scheme. All-four options (D) wrongly include the urban-planning limb.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Government Schemes & Yojanas"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20810, 'Centre-State Relations', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'After the extensive discussion in the Constituent Assembly, the following provisions was/were included. Which Article does not include? I. Fundamental duties under Art. 51A II. Constitutional Amendment under Art. 368 III. National emergency under Art. 352 IV. Ordinance under Art. 123', '{"A": "Only I correct", "B": "Only II correct", "C": "All of the above are correct", "D": "None of the above are correct"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through the options, Only I correct is the correct one. The Constituent Assembly first met on 9 December 1946; it adopted the Constitution on 26 November 1949 (Constitution Day) and it came into force on 26 January 1950. Fundamental Duties (Article 51A, Part IV-A) were added by the 42nd Amendment (1976) on the recommendation of the Swaran Singh Committee; the 86th Amendment (2002) took the count from ten to eleven. This kind of item rewards steady factual reading over aggressive shortcut techniques — the marks come from having read the source once, not from clever elimination.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Centre-State Relations"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20811, 'Constitutional Framework & Preamble', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'In which State was the 10th International Tourism Mart organized in November 2022?', '{"A": "Maharashtra", "B": "Uttar Pradesh", "C": "Mizoram", "D": "Assam"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The 10th International Tourism Mart (November 2022) was held in Mizoram—showcasing North-East tourism products. Maharashtra, Uttar Pradesh, and Assam hosted other events but not this ITM edition flagged in 2022–23 current-affairs capsules.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Constitutional Framework & Preamble"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20812, 'Other', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Choose the correct option considering the following statements. a. Ramesh Bais is appointed as the Governor of Maharashtra. b. Earlier he was the Governor of Tripura State. c. He belongs to Chhattisgarh State.', '{"A": "Only a is correct", "B": "a and b both are correct", "C": "a and c both are correct", "D": "a, b and c are correct"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D is the right choice since Option D is correct for Ramesh Bais: appointed Maharashtra Governor, earlier Tripura Governor, and hails from Chhattisgarh—all three statements stand. Single-statement picks (only a, or a+b without c) undercount the composite biographical facts the paper treats as jointly true. Distractors A (Only a is correct), B (a and b both are correct), C (a and c both are correct) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Other"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20813, 'Parliament', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Which of the following statements are correct regarding the legal relationship between the Central and State Government in India? A. The subject of transfer of property other than agricultural land is included in the Concurrent List. B. The subject of wealth tax on property other than agricultural land is included in the Union List. C. The subject of entertainment tax is included in the Concurrent List. D. The subject of ''Antiquities Museum'' is included in the State List.', '{"A": "A, B and C", "B": "B, C and D", "C": "A, B and D", "D": "A, C and D"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C works here because Transfer of property (non-agricultural) is Concurrent (A); wealth tax on non-agricultural property was Union List (B); antiquities and museums are State List (D)—all correct. Entertainment tax is State List, not Concurrent—so (C) is the false statement among the four. Distractors A (A, B and C), B (B, C and D), D (A, C and D) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Parliament"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20814, 'National Appointments & Reports', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Examine the following statements regarding the ''Nutrition Promotion Campaign'' of the United Nations. A. Afshan Khan was nominated as the co-ordinator of this Campaign. B. Antony Blinken was nominated as the co-ordinator of this Campaign. C. To eradicate malnutrition by 2030 is the objective of this Campaign. D. This campaign is implemented in countries suffering with malnutrition in the world. Identify the correct statements from the above.', '{"A": "A and B are correct", "B": "C and D are correct", "C": "A, C and D are correct", "D": "A, B and D are correct"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Choose option C: UN Nutrition Promotion Campaign: Afshan Khan as coordinator (A), 2030 malnutrition eradication goal (C), focus on malnutrition-affected countries (D)—not U.S. Secretary Blinken (B). Pairing Blinken with UN nutrition leadership confuses American diplomacy with UN agency appointment. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","National Appointments & Reports"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20815, 'Government Schemes & Yojanas', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Which of the following city was the host of ''5th ASEAN-India Business Summit'' in 2023?', '{"A": "New Delhi", "B": "Dhaka", "C": "Kuala Lumpur", "D": "Singapore city"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The correct answer is option C — the 5th ASEAN–India Business Summit 2023 was hosted in Kuala Lumpur—Malaysia''s capital as ASEAN chair context. New Delhi, Dhaka, and Singapore hosted other summits or regional forums but not this 2023 business summit edition. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Government Schemes & Yojanas"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20816, 'International Affairs & Summits', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'The Shrine of Sammed Shikharji has been in news for the past few days. Identify the correct statements about this pilgrimage site. A. It is the pilgrimage site of Jain community. B. This pilgrimage site is at Girdhi in the Jharkhand State. C. This pilgrimage site is at Aravali Mountain in Rajasthan. D. It is the pilgrimage site of Hindu community.', '{"A": "Only A and C are correct", "B": "Only A and B are correct", "C": "Only B and C are correct", "D": "Only C is correct"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Sammed Shikharji (Shikharji/Parasnath) is a major Jain pilgrimage site on Parasnath Hill in Giridih district, Jharkhand—statements A and B. Aravali/Rajasthan (C) and Hindu-community claims (D) are wrong; only the Jain–Jharkhand pairing survives.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","International Affairs & Summits"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20817, 'Other', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'In the Budget 2023 of Maharashtra State, which Corporations was announced to be established? A. Raje Umaji Naik Economic Development Corporation. B. Marathwada Milk Development Corporation. C. Jagadjyoti Mahatma Basaveshwar Economic Development Corporation. D. Saint Kashiba Gurav Youth Economic Development Corporation.', '{"A": "Only A and D", "B": "Only A, C and D", "C": "Only B, C and D", "D": "Only B and C"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B is the right choice since Maharashtra Budget 2023 announced Raje Umaji Naik Economic Development Corporation, Jagadjyoti Basaveshwar Economic Development Corporation, and Saint Kashiba Gurav Youth Economic Development Corporation (A, C, D)—not the Marathwada Milk Development Corporation alone. Partial lists drop valid corporations the budget speech named. You can eliminate A (Only A and D), C (Only B, C and D), D (Only B and C) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option B. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Other"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20818, 'International Affairs & Summits', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Who among the following inaugurated IBA Women''s World Boxing Championship, 2023 in New Delhi?', '{"A": "Shri Anurag Singh Thakur", "B": "Shri Narendra Modi", "C": "Shri Amit Shah", "D": "Smt. Jayashree Banerjee"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Union Minister Anurag Singh Thakur inaugurated the IBA Women''s World Boxing Championship 2023 in New Delhi. PM Modi, Amit Shah, and Banerjee did not serve as the inaugurating minister for this specific championship event in the correct current-affairs note.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","International Affairs & Summits"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20819, 'Other', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Which Mission did India conduct to aid earthquake affected in ''Turkey''?', '{"A": "Operation Rahat", "B": "Operation Hamdard", "C": "Operation Dost", "D": "Operation Sakha"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C matches the question because Option C names Operation Dost—India''s humanitarian relief mission after the February 2023 Turkey–Syria earthquakes. Operation Rahat (Yemen evacuation), Hamdard, and Sakha belong to other disaster or military operations—mixing them erases the Turkey earthquake headline. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Other"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20820, 'Defence & Security', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Identify the correct statement/s from the following in relation to ''UN COP 15'' A. The Global Biodiversity Agreement was approved by this Council. B. The Global Biodiversity Agreement was done under the Presidency of America. C. China presided ''UN COP 15''. D. There is a need to make efforts to reduce the consequences of climate change and the conservation of threatened species in the agreement.', '{"A": "A and B are correct", "B": "B and D are correct", "C": "B and C are correct", "D": "A, C and D are correct"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The answer is option D: UN COP15 (Montreal 2022, China presidency) adopted the Kunming–Montreal Global Biodiversity Framework (A), under Chinese presidency (C), targeting species and climate-linked conservation (D)—not American presidency (B). Pairing the U.S. as COP15 president is the clear distractor. Distractors A (A and B are correct), B (B and D are correct), C (B and C are correct) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Defence & Security"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20821, 'Sports', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Match the following. Winner of Arjun Award 2022 – Sports a. Bhakti Kulkarni → i. Badminton b. Sakshi Kumari → ii. Kabaddi c. Lakshya Sen → iii. Chess', '{"A": "i, iii, ii", "B": "ii, i, iii", "C": "iii, ii, i", "D": "i, ii, iii"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Choose option C: arjuna Award 2022 mapping: Bhakti Kulkarni → chess (iii), Sakshi Kumari → kabaddi (ii), Lakshya Sen → badminton (i)—order iii, ii, i. Swapping Sen with Kulkarni or Kumari breaks sport–recipient pairs from the 2022 honours list. You can eliminate A (i, iii, ii), B (ii, i, iii), D (i, ii, iii) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option C. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Sports"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20822, 'National Appointments & Reports', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Where was the 25th National E-Governance Conference, 2022 held?', '{"A": "Kollam – Kerala", "B": "Mumbai – Maharashtra", "C": "Ahmedabad – Gujarat", "D": "Katra – Jammu Kashmir"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D is correct because Option D locates the 25th National E-Governance Conference 2022 at Katra, Jammu & Kashmir—linking e-governance outreach with the Vaishno Devi pilgrimage hub. Kollam, Mumbai, and Ahmedabad hosted other e-gov or tech events but not this 25th edition. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","National Appointments & Reports"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20823, 'International Affairs & Summits', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Which country has removed the mention of the British Monarchy from its currency notes in 2023?', '{"A": "Australia", "B": "New Zealand", "C": "Switzerland", "D": "Canada"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A is correct because australia announced removing the British monarch from its $5 banknote in 2023—keeping King Charles off the new design while retaining Parliament-approved imagery. New Zealand, Switzerland, and Canada did not make this specific 2023 currency redesign announcement. Distractors B (New Zealand), C (Switzerland), D (Canada) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","International Affairs & Summits"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20824, 'Awards & Honours', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Who has been appointed as the Chairman of Pension Fund Regulatory and Development Authority (PFRDA) by Government in March 2023?', '{"A": "Amitava Mukharjee", "B": "Deepak Mohanty", "C": "Rajesh Malhotra", "D": "Supratim Bandopadhyay"}'::jsonb, 'B', '"Deepak Mohanty" is the fact the question is pointing at. The year 2023 anchors this question — the correct option is the fact that dates to that year. The examiner rewards precision on this item — every option is engineered to feel plausible, but only the marked one matches the exact wording of the source document.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Awards & Honours"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20825, 'Other', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'UNESCO has dedicated International Education Day of 2023 to which country''s girls and women?', '{"A": "Iran", "B": "Afghanistan", "C": "Israel", "D": "Vietnam"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B works here because UNESCO dedicated International Education Day 2023 to Afghan girls and women denied schooling under Taliban restrictions—a global solidarity theme. Iran, Israel, and Vietnam were not the focus of that year''s UNESCO dedication. You can eliminate A (Iran), C (Israel), D (Vietnam) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option B. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Other"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20826, 'Awards & Honours', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'Match the pairs about ''Padma Shri'' Award, 2023. Person – Field a. Ramesh Patange → i. Science and Engineering b. Dr. Mahendra Pal → ii. Literature and Education c. Uma Shankar Pande → iii. Art d. Parshuram Khune → iv. Social Work', '{"A": "ii, iii, i, iv", "B": "iii, ii, iv, i", "C": "i, iv, iii, ii", "D": "ii, i, iv, iii"}'::jsonb, 'D', '"ii, i, iv, iii" is the option marked correct in the official key. The year 2023 anchors this question — the correct option is the fact that dates to that year. The correct pairing above matches every column-A entry with its column-B partner as marked in the official key. The MPSC pattern for questions of this type is to plant one exact fact and three plausible-looking alternatives; the fact-based option is always the answer.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Awards & Honours"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20827, 'Trade Union & Labour Movement', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'इ. स. 1918, साली मुंबईतील कामगारांना ''पिपल्स युनियन'' ही संघटना स्थापना करण्याचा उपदेश कोणी केला होता?', '{"A": "राजश्री शाहू महाराज", "B": "डॉ. बाबासाहेब आंबेडकर", "C": "नारायण मेघाजी लोखंडे", "D": "भाई माधवराव बागल"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'थेट उत्तर — पर्याय A। राजश्री शाहू महाराजांनी १९१८ मध्ये मुंबईतील कामगारांना ''पिपल्स युनियन'' स्थापन करण्याचा सल्ला दिला — कोल्हापूर आणि बॉम्बे प्रेस मधील कामगार कल्याण व ब्राह्मणेतर सुधारणा कार्यक्रमाचा भाग. आंबेडकरांचे संघटन कार्य नंतर; लोखंडे Mill Hands'' Association; बागल सहकारी प्रवाह — १९१८ च्या People''s Union प्रश्नाशी जुळत नाहीत।', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Trade Union & Labour Movement"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20828, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'पंडिता रमाबाईनी रमाबाई असोसिएशनच्या अनुमतीने आपल्याला सल्ला देण्यासाठी एक सल्लागार मंडळ नेमले. त्यात खालीलपैकी कोणाचा समावेश होता? i. न्यायमूर्ती म. गो. रानडे ii. डॉ. आर. जी. भांडारकर iii. न्यायमूर्ती के. टी. तेलंग iv. बापू हरी शिंदे', '{"A": "केवळ i व ii", "B": "केवळ ii व iii", "C": "केवळ i व iv", "D": "केवळ i, ii व iii"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय D येतो. पंडिता रमाबाई यांच्या रमाबाई असोसिएशनच्या सल्लागार मंडळावर न्यायमूर्ती म. गो. रानडे, डॉ. आर. जी. भांडारकर आणि न्यायमूर्ती के. टी. तेलंग होते — विधवा गृह आणि शिक्षण कार्यासाठी अग्रगण्य सुधारक. बापू हरी शिंदे दलित कार्यकर्ते होते, पण या विशिष्ट मंडळावर नव्हते; रानडे किंवा तेलंग वगळणारे पर्याय महाराष्ट्रातील सामाजिक सुधारणा जाळ्याचे चुकीची जोडणी।', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20829, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'ब्राह्मणेतर पत्रकारितेची मुहूर्तमेढ रोवून चिपळूणकरांच्या महात्मा ज्योतिराव फुलेंवरील हल्ल्याचा बचाव आपल्या वृत्तपत्राद्वारे कोणी केला?', '{"A": "नारायण मेघाजी लोखंडे", "B": "भाऊ दाजी लाड", "C": "तुकाराम तात्या पडवळ", "D": "कृष्णाजी भालेकर"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'योग्य निवड पर्याय D। कृष्णाजी भालेकर यांनी चिपळूणकरांच्या वृत्तपत्रातील ज्योतिराव फुलेंवरील हल्ल्याचा बचाव केला — महाराष्ट्र इतिहासात ब्राह्मणेतर पत्रकारितेची सुरुवात म्हणून ओळखले जाते. लोखंडे गिरणी कामगार; भाऊ दाजी लाड संस्कृत-ओरिय; पडवळ इतर सुधारणा मार्ग — Phule–Chiplunkar–Bhalekar त चuकीचे।', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20830, 'Ancient India', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, '''मालविकाग्निमित्र'' या प्राचीन नाटकान कोणत्या दोन राजघराण्याच्या वैवाहिक संबंधावर प्रकाश पडतो?', '{"A": "शुंग आणि विदर्भ (यज्ञसेन) घराणे", "B": "गुप्त आणि वाकाटक घराणे", "C": "शक आणि सातवाहन घराणे", "D": "चालुक्य आणि वर्धन घराणे"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'या विषयात पर्याय A अचूक उत्तर मानले जाते। Kalidasa चे चा पुत्र Agnimitra आणि Vidarbha (Yajnaseni) राजकुमारी Malavika यांच्या वैवाहिक संबंध नाट्य रूपात सादर विषय-पॅकमध्ये हा बिंदू पुन्हा विचारला जाऊ शकतो, म्हणून मुख्य तथ्य एकत्र लक्षात ठेवा.।', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Ancient India"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20831, 'Medieval India', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'सेतू माधवराव पगडी यांच्या मते, जाथ पंथातील कोणत्या संताने ''शहा रमजान'' हे नाव धारण करून सुफी संत निजामुद्दिन यांच्या कडून इस्लाम धर्माची दिक्षा घेतली. हे महाराष्ट्राच्या सांस्कृतिक इतिहासातील एक गूढ आहे.', '{"A": "गोरखनाथ", "B": "गहिनीनाथ", "C": "जालन्धरनाथ", "D": "कानिफनाथ"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'परीक्षा कीनुसार पर्याय D। सेतू माधवराव पगडी यांच्या सांस्कृतिक इतिहास नोंदीनुसार नाथ परंपरेतील कानिफनाथ ''शहा रमजान'' नाव घेत सुफी निजामुद्दीन परंपरेत दीक्षा घेत — महाराष्ट्रातील वादग्रस्त रहस्यवादी प्रसंग. गोरखनाथ, गहिनीनाथ, जालन्धरनाथ व्यापक नाथ परंपरा, पण ही विशिष्ट Pagadi attribution नाही।', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Medieval India"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20832, 'Gandhian Mass Movements', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'खालील घटनांची योग्य क्रमाने मांडणी करा. i. श्वेत पत्रिका ii. पुणे करार iii. नेहरू अहवाल iv. धारसना सत्याग्रह', '{"A": "iv, ii, iii, i", "B": "iv, i, ii, iii", "C": "iii, iv, ii, i", "D": "ii, iii, iv, i"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेप्रमाणे उत्तर iii, iv, ii, i. जवाहरलाल नेहरू (1889–1964) हे भारताचे पहिले पंतप्रधान (1947–1964) होते; ते नियोजित अर्थव्यवस्था व अलिप्ततावादी परराष्ट्र धोरणाचे शिल्पकार मानले जातात. बरोबर पर्याय आपल्या active-recall flashcard सेटमध्ये जोडा; MPSC मूळ तथ्य दर दोन-तीन पूर्व परीक्षा चक्रात परत विचारते.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Gandhian Mass Movements"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20833, 'Ancient India', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'वैदिक काळात व्यापारात विनिमयाचे माध्यम काय होते? i. निष्क ii. कृष्णल iii. शतमान iv. गण v. श्रेणी', '{"A": "i, ii व iii", "B": "ii, iii व iv", "C": "i, ii, iv व v", "D": "i, iii व v"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'पुष्टी केलेला उत्तर पर्याय A। वैदिक काळात विनिमयाचे माध्यम: निष्क (सोन्याचे दागिने-नाणे), कृष्णल/कृष्णला (वजन एकक), शतमान (शंभर पट माप) — हे तीन मान्य मूल्य माध्यम. गण आणि श्रेणी ग/सामूहिक उपक्रम; iv–v i–iii सोबत जोडल्यास चलन नसलेले शब्द अधिक मोजले जातात।', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Ancient India"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20834, 'Rise of Nationalism & INC', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'पुढील राजकीय संघटनांचा कालानुक्रमे योग्य क्रम लावा. अ. पुणे सार्वजनिक सभा ब. बॉम्बे प्रेसिडेन्सी असोसिएशन क. मद्रास महाजन सभा ड. इंडियन असोसिएशन', '{"A": "ब अ ड क", "B": "अ ड क ब", "C": "क ड ब अ", "D": "ड ब अ क"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'योग्य निवड पर्याय B। पुणे sarvajanik Sabha (१८७०) (१८७६), (१८८४), (१८८५) पूर्वी। Bombay Presidency किंवा — मध्यमवादी-राष्ट्रवादी organisational chronology तुटते।', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Rise of Nationalism & INC"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20835, 'Gandhian Mass Movements', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'खालीलपैकी कोणता निर्णय साबरमती करारने घेण्यात आला?', '{"A": "प्रतियोगी सहकारिता पक्षाची स्थापना करावी.", "B": "विद्यार्थ्यांनी राजकारणात मध्यभागी करून घेऊ नये.", "C": "कनिष्ठ जातीय कामगारामध्ये भेदभाव करू नये, तसेच 50 स्वयंसेवकांचे पथक उभारावे व हिंदू मुस्लिम ऐक्य राखावे.", "D": "मोतीलाल नेहरू आणि जयकर यांच्या समितीने मध्यवर्ती विधिमंडळाचे सदस्य निश्चित करावे."}'::jsonb, 'D', 'पर्याय D (मोतीलाल नेहरू आणि जयकर यांच्या समितीने …) — Sabarmati ''treaty'' decision: Motilal Nehru आणि M. Jayakar समिती Central Legislature membership 1922 Bardoli–Sabarmati settlement नंतर determine. Competitive co-operative party, student politics bans, volunteer corps — other Gandhi-era resolutions; Nehru–Jayakar panel key marks पर्याय A (प्रतियोगी सहकारिता पक्षाची स्थापना कराव…) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B (विद्यार्थ्यांनी राजकारणात मध्यभागी करून…) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (कनिष्ठ जातीय कामगारामध्ये भेदभाव करू नय…) प्रश्नातील तथ्ये/गणना/व्याख्येशी विरोधाभासी आहे।', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Gandhian Mass Movements"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20836, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'पुढील वाक्ये ______ यांच्या विषयी आहेत. अ. महाराष्ट्राच्या शिक्षण क्षेत्रात त्यांनी महत्त्वाची भूमिका बजावली. ब. त्यांनी वेगवेगळ्या विषयांवर पाठ्यपुस्तके तयार केली. क. गणित आणि शास्त्रावर त्यांनी ''शून्यलब्धी'' हे पुस्तक मराठीतून लिहीले. ड. केशवराव भवाळकरांनी त्यांचे चरित्र लिहीले आहे.', '{"A": "दादोबा पांडुरंग तरखडकर", "B": "आत्माराम पांडुरंग तरखडकर", "C": "बाळशास्त्री जांभेकर", "D": "गोपाळ हरी देशमुख"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'थेट उत्तर — पर्याय C। बाळशास्त्री जांभेकर Marathi शिक्षणाचे अग्रदूत, पाठ्यपुस्तके, ''श'' गणित-विज्ञान, केशवराव भावळकर चरित्र. दादोबा/आत्म Tarkhadkar प्रार्थना समाज; ल ''शत'' — अद केल्यास Shunyalabdhi clue बसत नाही।', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20837, 'Tribal & Peasant Uprisings', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'इ. स. 1934 मध्ये ''कर्षक संघम'' एक शेतकरी संघटना म्हणून खालीलपैकी कोणत्या प्रांतात स्थापन करण्यात आली?', '{"A": "आंध्रप्रदेश", "B": "तामिळनाडू", "C": "केरळ", "D": "बंगाल"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'इतिहासात हे लक्षात ठेवा — पर्याय C (केरळ) बरोबर आहे. १९३४ मध्ये ''कर्षक संघम'' ही शेतकरी संघटना केरळात (मलबार–त्रावणकोर भागात) स्थापन करण्यात आली, जी शेतकरी-आंदोलनाच्या इतिहासात महत्त्वाची आहे. आंध्रप्रदेश, तामिळनाडू आणि बंगाल येथेही शेतकरी संघटना होत्या, पण ''कर्षक संघम'' (१९३४) विशेषतः केरळाशी जोडले जाते. पर्याय A, B आणि D इतर प्रांतांशी जुळतात।', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Tribal & Peasant Uprisings"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20838, 'Gandhian Mass Movements', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'दांडीयात्रेच्या उल्लेख ''रामाचा लंकेपर्यंत ऐतिहासिक मार्च'' असे कोणी केला?', '{"A": "पंडित मोतीलाल नेहरू आणि डी. जी. तेंडुलकर", "B": "पी. सी. रे आणि डी. पी. मिश्रा", "C": "शंकरराव देव आणि ग. वि. केतकर", "D": "अप्पासाहेब पटवर्धन आणि सुहासिनी नंबियार"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'तेंडुलकर (पर्याय A) आहे. चुकीचे पर्याय B (पी. मिश्रा), C (शंकरराव देव आणि ग. केतकर), D (अप्पासाहेब पटवर्धन आणि सुहासिनी नंब…) पर्याय B (पी. मिश्रा) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (शंकरराव देव आणि ग. केतकर) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (अप्पासाहेब पटवर्धन आणि सुहासिनी नंबियार) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Gandhian Mass Movements"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20839, 'Revolt of 1857', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'खानदेशातील भिल्लांनी ब्रिटिश राजवटीस विरोध केला होता कारण i. उत्तर भारतातील उठावाच्या घटनापासून सातपुडा विभागातील भिल्लांना प्रेरणा मिळाली. ii. 1857 च्या उठावाचा फायदा घेऊन भागोजी नाईक व काझिसिंग नाईक उठावात सामिल झाले. iii. काझिसिंग व त्यांच्या सहकाऱ्यांनी सरकारी खजिना व पोस्ट जाळले.', '{"A": "i व ii", "B": "ii व iii", "C": "i व iii", "D": "वरीलपैकी सर्व"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'या प्रश्नाचे बरोबर उत्तर पर्याय D (वरीलपैकी सर्व) आहे. १८५७ च्या उठावाच्या पार्श्वभूमीवर खानदेशातील भिलांनी ब्रिटिश राजवटीस विरोध केला — उत्तर भारतातील उठावाची प्रेरणा (i), भागोजी नाईक व काझिसिंग नाईक यांचा सहभाग (ii), आणि सरकारी खजिना व पोस्ट जाळणे (iii) — तिन्ही कारणे योग्य आहेत. पर्याय A (i व ii), B (ii व iii) आणि C (i व iii) यांत एक कारण वगळले आहे, म्हणून अपूर्ण आहेत।', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Revolt of 1857"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20840, 'British Expansion & Governors-General', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'खालील विधाने कोणासंदर्भात आहेत? i. धर्माची राजकारणामून फाळणी घेतली. ii. सती जाणाऱ्या शूर स्त्रियांवरील अलिप्ततेचे धोरण स्वीकारले. iii. बालविवाह थांबविणे व विधवा विवाहाला उत्तेजन दिले. iv. सामाजिक कायद्याबाबत अंतिम निर्णय आपला असल्याचा दावा केला.', '{"A": "बाबर", "B": "हुमायुन", "C": "अकबर", "D": "औरंगजेब"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'प्रश्नातील विधाने तपासल्यास पर्याय C बरोबर आहे। Babur/; — सुधारणावादी चरित्र योग्य नाही MPSC प्रश्नपत्रिकेत अशा तपशीलांची पुनरावृत्ती होते, म्हणून मुख्य संकल्पना लक्षात ठेवा.।', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","British Expansion & Governors-General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20841, 'Biodiversity & Conservation', 'General Studies', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'खालील विधाने पहा: अ. घातक कचरा मृदेमध्ये टाकल्यामुळे जैवविविधता कमी होते. ब. नद्यामध्ये वारंवार पूर येण्यामानी वृक्षतोड कारणीभूत आहे. क. फ्रान्सिस्को मेंडझ यांच्या उर्जा क्षेत्रातील कार्यामुळे त्यांना ''अमेझॉन गांधी'' म्हणून संबोधतात.', '{"A": "फक्त विधान क बरोबर आहे", "B": "फक्त विधान अ बरोबर आहे", "C": "फक्त विधान अ आणि ब बरोबर आहेत", "D": "विधान अ, ब आणि क बरोबर आहेत"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पर्याय C (फक्त विधान अ आणि ब बरोबर आहेत) — पर्याय A (फक्त विधान क बरोबर आहे) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B (फक्त विधान अ बरोबर आहे) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (विधान अ, ब आणि क बरोबर आहेत) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"General Studies","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Biodiversity & Conservation"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20842, 'Home Rule Movement', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'खालीलपैकी कोणत्या वृत्तपत्रातून अॅनी-बेझंट यांनी होमरूल चळवळी बद्दलचे विचार मांडले? अ. न्यू इंडिया ब. कॉमन वील क. बॉम्बे गॅझेट ड. टेलीग्राफ', '{"A": "अ आणि ब फक्त", "B": "ब आणि क फक्त", "C": "अ आणि ड फक्त", "D": "अ, ब आणि क फक्त"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'गणितात हे सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय A येतो। New India आणि — Bombay Gazette/Telegraph स्थापना दैनिके। Bombay Gazette add moderate प्रेस पत्रकारिता गोंधळ उत्तर निश्चित करताना प्रश्नातील मुख्य संकल्पना आणि वर्ष लक्षात ठेवा.।', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Home Rule Movement"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20843, 'Pollution', 'General Studies', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'मातीतील नायट्रोजन खत जिवाणूद्वारे तोडल्यास ______ मुक्त होते.', '{"A": "नायट्रोजन डायऑक्साइड (NO₂)", "B": "नायट्रस ऑक्साइड (N₂O)", "C": "नायट्रोजन ट्रायऑक्साइड (NO₃)", "D": "नायट्रोजन (N₂)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'विश्लेषण केल्यास पर्याय C योग्य ठरतो. मातीतील नायट्रोजन खत जीवाणू breakdown दरम्यान nitrous oxide (N₂O) विनाइट्र textbooks cite, पण Set A nitrogen trioxide (NO₃) mark करते — ऐवजी key follow करा। N₂ largely inert; NO₂ pollutant gas पण योग्य limb नाही।', '{"General Studies","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Pollution"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20844, 'Climate Change & Global Warming', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'ओझोन संदर्भात खालील कोणती विधाने बरोबर आहेत? अ. ओझोनला पृथ्वीचे रक्षण कवच म्हणतात. ब. 1985 मध्ये ओझोन थराला छिद्र पडल्याचे स्पष्ट झाले. क. 16 सप्टेंबर हा जागतिक ओझोन दिवस म्हणून साजरा केला जातो. ड. 1989 मध्ये ओझोन क्षयास कारणीभूत रसायन वापरावर बंदी घालण्यात आली.', '{"A": "फक्त अ, ब आणि क", "B": "फक्त ब, क आणि ड", "C": "फक्त अ, क आणि ड", "D": "वरील सर्व"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'पर्याय D (वरील सर्व) — अर्धवट combinations Montreal–Vienna ozone-protection कथा अपूर्ण. पर्याय A (फक्त अ, ब आणि क) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय B (फक्त ब, क आणि ड) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय C (फक्त अ, क आणि ड) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात।', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Climate Change & Global Warming"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20845, 'Ecology & Ecosystems', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'काही प्रजाती नष्ट झाल्या तर पर्यावरणावर गंभीर परिणाम करतात त्यांना ______ म्हणतात.', '{"A": "निळा दगड", "B": "लाल दगड", "C": "पिवळा दगड", "D": "किस्टोन"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'पर्यावरणशास्त्रात हे लक्षात ठेवा — ज्या प्रजातीचा नाश झाल्यास संपूर्ण पर्यास्थितिक तंत्राची रचना असमान प्रमाणात कोसळते, त्यांना किस्टोन प्रजाती म्हणतात; समुद्र ओटर–केल्प हे उदाहरण प्रसिद्ध आहे. निळा, लाल किंवा पिवळा दगड हे फक्त दगडांचे रंग आहेत, पर्यावरणीय संकल्पना नाहीत — म्हणून पर्याय D। पर्याय A (निळा दगड) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B (लाल दगड) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (पिवळा दगड) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Ecology & Ecosystems"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20846, 'Other', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, '"पर्यावरण म्हणजे सजीवांच्या किंवा जीवसमूहांच्या जीवन, वाढ, विकास व मृत्यूवर परिणाम करणारी सर्व परिस्थिती, तिची कारके व त्यांचा प्रभाव होय." पर्यावरणाची ही व्याख्या कोणी केली?', '{"A": "विश्वकोष", "B": "ब्रिटानिका विश्वकोष", "C": "ए. सी. टान्सले", "D": "जॅकी स्मिथ"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'भूगोलात हे स्थिर — पर्याय A बरोबर आहे। Environment सर्वसमावेशक व्याख्या — जीवांच्या जीवन अटी/influences sum — । Britannica/Tansley (ecosystem) related distinct; Jackie Smith वेगळा घटक व citation नाही।', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Other"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20847, 'Minerals & Industries', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'पश्चिम राजस्थानाच्या प्रदेशात चुनखडक, जिप्सम आणि खनिज मीठाचे साठे विनंतीत झालेले आहेत. खालीलपैकी कोणती कारणे या खनिजांच्या साठ्यांच्या वितरणास कारणीभूत आहेत? a. पर्मोकार्बोनिफेरस युगात पश्चिम राजस्थानाचा भाग समुद्राच्या पाण्याखाली होता. b. पश्चिम राजस्थानाच्या प्रदेशात पर्जन्याचे प्रमाण कमी आहे. c. पश्चिम राजस्थानाच्या प्रदेशात हवामान उष्ण व कोरडे आहे. d. पश्चिम राजस्थानाच्या प्रदेशात वनस्पतीदना खालील क्षेत्र अत्यल्प आहे.', '{"A": "फक्त a बरोबर आहे", "B": "फक्त a आणि b बरोबर आहेत", "C": "a, b आणि c बरोबर आहेत", "D": "फक्त d बरोबर आहे"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'भूगोलात हे स्थिर — पर्याय A बरोबर आहे। , gypsum, -Carboniferous समुद्राचे बुडवण/evaporation basins — present low rainfall/ नाहीत। Climate/vegetation (b–d) present weathering; ।', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Minerals & Industries"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20848, 'Agriculture & Soils', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'खालीलपैकी कोणत्या मृदेत लोह व बॉक्साइट खनिजाचे प्रमाण अधिक असते?', '{"A": "तांबडी मृदा", "B": "रेगूर मृदा", "C": "जांभी मृदा", "D": "गाळाची मृदा"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'योग्य उत्तर पर्याय C आहे। Red soil iron-rich पण max bauxite host नाही; ; विषय-पॅकमध्ये हा बिंदू पुन्हा विचारला जाऊ शकतो, म्हणून मुख्य तथ्य एकत्र लक्षात ठेवा। MPSC प्रश्नपत्रिकेत अशा तपशीलांची पुनरावृत्ती होते, म्हणून मुख्य संकल्पना लक्षात ठेवा.।', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Agriculture & Soils"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20849, 'Other', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'खालील आकृतीचे निरीक्षण करून खालीलपैकी कोणत्या मूळाक्षरांनी चंद्राचा तीन चतुर्थांश भाग प्रकाशित दर्शविला आहे हे नमूद करा?', '{"A": "B आणि H", "B": "C आणि G", "C": "D आणि F", "D": "E आणि A"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पर्याय C (D आणि F) — आठ-टप्प्यांच्या चंद्र चक्रात गिबस (अर्ध्यापेक्षा जAst पण पूर्ण नाही) टप्पे D आणि F वर दर्शविले जातात। B–H किंवा E–A नवचंद्र/अर्धचंद्र किंवा पूर्णचंद्राशी जुळतात; फक्त D–F जोडी तीन-चतुर्थांश प्रकाश दर्शवते।', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Other"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (20850, 'Ecology & Ecosystems', 'General Studies', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2023, 'खालीलपैकी कोणता परिस्थितिकी मनोऱ्याचा प्रकार नाही?', '{"A": "संख्येचा मनोरा", "B": "वैवविक वस्तुमानाचा मनोरा", "C": "अन्नजाळी मनोरा", "D": "उर्जेचा मनोरा"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'या प्रश्नाचे बरोबर उत्तर पर्याय C आहे. पारिस्थितिक pyramids numbers, biomass, ऊर्जा — ''food webs'' जाळे diagrams feeding जोडते, pyramid type नाही उत्तर निश्चित करताना प्रश्नातील मुख्य संकल्पना आणि वर्ष लक्षात ठेवा.।', '{"General Studies","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2023","Ecology & Ecosystems"}'::text[], 'Medium')
