VALUES
  (21701, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2021, 'खालीलपैकी कोणत्या शर्तींचा संच ओबेलीयाला सर्वोत्तमपणे लागू होतो ?', '{"A": "पॉलीमॉर्फिक, कोलोनियल, अक्वेंटीक", "B": "मरीन, सिडेन्टरी आणि कोलोनियल", "C": "मरीन, सिडेन्टरी, पॉलीमॉर्फिक", "D": "मरीन, सिडेन्टरी, कोलोनियल, पॉलीमॉर्फिक विथ ट्रु अल्टरनेशन ऑफ जनरेशन"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'थेट उत्तर — पर्याय D. Obelia marine, sedentary, colonial hydrozoan — polymorphic आणि polyp–medusa दरम्यान true alternation of generations दाखवते.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group C Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21702, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2021, 'व्हाईट बटन मशरूम्स चे वैज्ञानिक (जीवशास्त्रीय) संबोधन ______ असे आहे.', '{"A": "प्लुरोटस फ्लोरिडा", "B": "व्होल्व्हारिएला व्होल्व्हासिएई", "C": "अगारिकस बायोस्पोरस", "D": "एरिमोथेशियम ॲशबी"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'येथे खात्रीशीर उत्तर पर्याय C. White button mushroom Agaricus bisporus; Pleurotus oyster, Volvariella paddy-straw mushroom.', '{"Science","MPSC Group C Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21703, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2021, 'पुढील तथ्यांचे परीक्षण करा : (a) अनू बानोपेक्षा वजनदार आहे. (b) सिंथिया दिनापेक्षा उंच आहे. (c) बानो दिनाइतकीच उंच पण तिच्यापेक्षा वजनदार आहे. (d) दिना अनूपेक्षा उंच आहे. वरील तथ्यांवर आधारित अचूक निष्कर्ष ओळखा.', '{"A": "सर्वात सिंथिया वजनदार आहे आणि अनू बुटकी आहे.", "B": "अनू निश्चितपणे सर्वात वजनदार आणि बुटकी आहे.", "C": "सिंथिया सर्वात वजनदार आहे परंतु सर्वात उंच कोण यासंबंधाने निष्कर्ष काढणे शक्य नाही.", "D": "सर्वात वजनदार कोण याविषयी निष्कर्ष काढणे अशक्य आहे परंतु अनू निश्चितपणे सर्वात बुटकी आहे."}'::jsonb, 'D', 'योग्य उत्तर पर्याय D. Anu Bano पेक्षा जड, Dina Anu पेक्षा उंच — Anu नक्की सर्वात कमी उंची; Cynthia चे weight इतरांशी compare नाही — सर्वात जड कोण हे ठरवता येत नाही.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group C Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21704, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2021, 'A, B, C व D या विद्यार्थ्यांकडे एकूण मिळून तीस पुस्तके आहेत. यातील एकाकडे तीन पुस्तके आहेत. दुसऱ्याकडे सहा आहेत, तिसऱ्याकडे नऊ आणि चौथ्याकडे बारा पुस्तके आहेत. B कडे C पेक्षा कमी पुस्तके आहेत तर D कडे A पेक्षा जास्त पुस्तके आहेत. जर C कडे D पेक्षा कमी पुस्तके असतील तर सत्य असतीलच असे/अशी नसणारे/री विधान/ने निवडा. (a) A आणि B या दोघांकडे मिळून किमान 12 पुस्तके असणारच. (b) D आणि A या दोघांकडे मिळून किमान 15 पुस्तके असणारच. (c) C आणि D या दोघांकडे मिळून किमान 18 पुस्तके असणारच. (d) C आणि B या दोघांकडे मिळून किमान 9 पुस्तके असणारच.', '{"A": "(a) वगळून सर्व", "B": "वरील सर्व", "C": "वरीलपैकी एकही नाही", "D": "फक्त (a)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'येथे खात्रीशीर उत्तर पर्याय D. Books 3, 6, 9, 12 आणि B A — (a) fail होऊ शकते (A=3, B=6 → 9); (b), (c), (d) प्रत्येक valid assignment मध्ये बरोबर.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group C Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21705, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2021, 'साखरेची किंमत 60% ने वाढली. घरात साखर किती टक्के कमी वापरावी म्हणजे खर्चात वाढ होणार नाही ?', '{"A": "25%", "B": "30%", "C": "37½%", "D": "40%"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'थेट उत्तर — पर्याय C. किंमत 60% वाढली तर खर्च सारखा — consumption 100/160 = 5/8; 3/8 = 37½% कमी करावे लागते.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group C Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21706, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2021, 'दिलेली माहिती अभ्यासा : A, B, C, D आणि E या व्यक्ती बागेतील बाकांवर उत्तरेकडे तोंड करून बसलेल्या आहेत. B ही D च्या उजवीकडे 40 मी. अंतरावर आहे. A ही B च्या दक्षिणेला 60 मी. अंतरावर आहे, C ही D च्या पश्चिमेला 50 मी. अंतरावर आहे आणि E ही A च्या उत्तरेला 70 मी. अंतरावर आहे. C आणि E दरम्यानच्या कमीत कमी अंदाजे अंतराचे मीटरमध्ये सर्वात उचित वर्णन करणारा पर्याय निवडा.', '{"A": "ते निश्चितपणे 90 मी. पेक्षा जास्त असणारच.", "B": "ते निश्चितपणे 91 मी. पेक्षा जास्त परंतु 92 मी. पेक्षा कमी असणारच.", "C": "ते निश्चितपणे 90 मी. पेक्षा जास्त परंतु 91 मी. पेक्षा कमी असणारच.", "D": "ते निश्चितपणे 91 मी. पेक्षा कमी असणारच."}'::jsonb, 'C', 'योग्य उत्तर पर्याय C. Positions: C (−50, 0), E (40, 10) — अंतर = √(90² + 10²) ≈ 90.55 m; 90 m पेक्षा जास्त, 91 m पेक्षा कमी.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group C Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21707, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2021, 'पुढील माहिती राज्यांचे क्षेत्रफळ व लोकसंख्याबाबतची आहे. राज्य | A | B | C | D क्षेत्रफळ (चौ. किमी) | 80,000 | 50,000 | 10,000 | 5,000 लोकसंख्या (लाखामध्ये) | 16 | 10 | 4 | 3 सर्वात जास्त दाट लोकसंख्या असणारे राज्य कोणते ?', '{"A": "A", "B": "B", "C": "C", "D": "D"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'परीक्षकाने पर्याय D चिन्हांकित केला. Population density = लोकसंख्या ÷ क्षेत्रफळ: D = 3 lakh ÷ 5,000 = 60 प्रति sq km — C (40), A व B (20) पेक्षा जास्त.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group C Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21708, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2021, 'पुढील दिलेल्या तीन रंगाच्या हिरवा (G), निळा (B) व लाल (R) खड्यांच्या क्रमिक माळा आहेत : X = GGBRBRRBBR Y = GBRRBRBBRG Z = RBBRGGBRBR जर पहिला व शेवटचा खडा शेजारी ठेवले तर यातील कोणत्या दोन माळा समान होतील ?', '{"A": "X आणि Y", "B": "Y आणि Z", "C": "X आणि Z", "D": "कोणत्याही दोन माळा सारख्या होणार नाहीत"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'येथे खात्रीशीर उत्तर पर्याय C. Circular necklace म्हणून X (GGBRBRRBBR) आणि Z (RBBRGGBRBR) rotation ने जुळतात — समान ring; Y वेगळा cycle.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group C Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21709, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2021, 'वडील व मुलाच्या आजच्या वयाची बेरीज 50 वर्षे आहे. चार वर्षांपूर्वी वडिलांचे वय मुलाच्या त्यावेळच्या वयाचा 6 पटी होते. तर वडील व मुलाचे अनुक्रमे आजचे वय किती ?', '{"A": "35 वर्षे, 15 वर्षे", "B": "38 वर्षे, 12 वर्षे", "C": "40 वर्षे, 10 वर्षे", "D": "42 वर्षे, 8 वर्षे"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय C येतो. सध्याचे वय 50; चार वर्षांपूर्वी वडील मुलाच्या 6 पट — F + S = 50, F − 4 = 6(S − 4) → 40 व 10 वर्ष.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group C Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21710, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2021, 'पुढे 5 विधाने आणि नंतर 3 विधाने विशिष्ट क्रमाने एकत्र करून पर्याय जुळवले आहेत. त्यातून तार्किकदृष्ट्या यथार्थ युक्तिवाद निर्देशित करणारा पर्याय निवडा. युक्तिवाद यथार्थ ठरण्यासाठी जुळणीतील 3 रे विधान हे त्याआधीच्या 2 विधानांवर आधारित निष्कर्ष विधान असायला हवे. (a) आधुनिक उद्योग संशोधन प्रेरित असतात. (b) ''इंप्रो'' हा आधुनिक उद्योग आहे. (c) ''इंप्रो'' हा संशोधन प्रेरित आहे. (d) ''इंप्रो'' कदाचित संशोधन प्रेरित असेल. (e) संशोधन प्रेरित उद्योग आधुनिक आहे.', '{"A": "(b), (e), (c)", "B": "(b), (c), (e)", "C": "(c), (a), (d)", "D": "(b), (d), (a)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'थेट उत्तर — पर्याय B. Official अधिकृत उत्तर (b), (c), (e) valid chain म्हणते; scoring साठी ती क्रम follow करा — पाठ्यपुस्तकातील मध्ये (a), (b), (c) अधिक natural.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group C Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21711, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2021, 'एका शाळेतील मुली व मुले यांचे गुणोत्तर 4 : 5 असे आहे. मुलींची संख्या 76 असेल तर मुले किती ?', '{"A": "85", "B": "95", "C": "105", "D": "115"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'थेट उत्तर — पर्याय B. Girls : boys = 4 : 5, 76 girls → एक part = 19; boys = 5 × 19 = 95.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group C Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21712, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2021, 'एका अपूर्णांकाचा छेद त्याच्या अंशापेक्षा 5 ने मोठा आहे. त्या अपूर्णांकाच्या अंशामध्ये 8 मिळवले व छेदातून 1 वजा केल्यास 15/11 हा अपूर्णांक मिळतो. तर मूळचा अपूर्णांक कोणता ?', '{"A": "3/8", "B": "11/15", "C": "7/12", "D": "1/6"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'परीक्षकाने पर्याय C चिन्हांकित केला. Numerator n, denominator n+5; (n+8)/(n+4) = 15/11 → n = 7 — मूळ fraction 7/12.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group C Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21713, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2021, 'एक बांधकाम करण्यासाठी 10 समान वेगाने काम करणाऱ्या कामगारांची नेमणूक केली. 2 कामगारांनी 2 व्या दिवशी काम सोडले, दुसऱ्या दोघांनी 3 व्या दिवशी काम सोडले व हे असे काम संपेपर्यंत चालू राहिले. याच्या परिणामी काम संपायला दोन दिवस जास्त लागले. जर 10 कामगारांनी सर्व दिवस काम केले असते तर काम करायला लागणारे दिवस निवडा.', '{"A": "2", "B": "3", "C": "4", "D": "5"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय B येतो. एकूण काम = 10 × n worker-days; दुसऱ्या दिवसापासून दररोज 2 workers कमी — 5 दिवस (10+8+6+4+2 = 30) n = 3 शी जुळते; 10 workers 3 दिवसांत.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group C Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21714, 'General', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'The ''Sarkaria Commission'' favoured _______.', '{"A": "abolition of the office of the Governor", "B": "abolition of All India Services", "C": "abolition of Inter-State Council", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer here is option D. The Sarkaria Commission (1983) reviewed Centre–State relations and recommended stronger cooperation — it did not call for abolishing the Governor, All India Services, or the Inter-State Council. All three options describe abolition the Commission never favoured.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21715, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2021, 'एका परिक्षेमध्ये 35% विद्यार्थी पास झालेत व 455 विद्यार्थी नापास झाले. तर त्या परिक्षेला एकूण किती विद्यार्थी बसले होते ?', '{"A": "490", "B": "700", "C": "845", "D": "1300"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'येथे खात्रीशीर उत्तर पर्याय B. 35% passed → 65% failed; 65% × एकूण = 455 — एकूण = 455 ÷ 0.65 = 700.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group C Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21716, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2021, 'दोन ट्रेनच्या वेगातील गुणोत्तर 2 : 5 आहे. जर पहिली ट्रेन 5 तासात 350 कि.मी. धावली तर दोन्ही ट्रेनच्या वेगातील फरक ताशी किती कि.मी. होईल ?', '{"A": "165", "B": "180", "C": "350", "D": "105"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'योग्य उत्तर पर्याय D. पहिली train 350 ÷ 5 = 70 km/h; 2 : 5 ratio → दुसरी 175 km/h — फरक 105 km/h.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group C Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21717, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Which one of the following statements is correct about the Advocate General of the State ?', '{"A": "He shall hold office during the pleasure of the State Council of Ministers.", "B": "His remuneration is determined by the State Legislature.", "C": "He may appear as an advocate in cases against the State Government for a private party.", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The right pick is option D. The Advocate General holds office during the Governor''s pleasure (not the Council of Ministers), remuneration is fixed by the Governor (not the Legislature), and he cannot appear against the State Government for a private party — so none of (A)–(C) stands.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21718, 'General', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Consider the following statements : a. The post of the Sarpanch (who is elected by the members of Gram Panchayat) or Upa Sarpanch, as the case may be, that has fallen vacant (due to resignation) shall be filled in within thirty days from the date of such vacancy. b. The post of the directly elected Sarpanch that has fallen vacant shall be filled within three months from the date of such vacancy. c. A member of a Gram Panchayat whose post has become vacant due to absence for continuous meetings of the Gram Panchayat shall not be eligible for re-election. Which of the statements given above is/are correct ?', '{"A": "Only a", "B": "Only a and c", "C": "Only b and c", "D": "a, b and c"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through it, option A is the one. Under Maharashtra''s Gram Panchayat rules, a Sarpanch or Upa-Sarpanch vacancy caused by resignation must be filled within thirty days — statement (a) holds. A directly elected Sarpanch vacancy follows a longer election cycle (not the three-month rule in (b)), and absence from meetings alone does not permanently bar re-election as (c) claims.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21719, 'General', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Consider the following statements about the provisions of the Village Development Committees of Maharashtra Gram Panchayat Act : a. The total number of members in a Village Development Committee shall not be less than seven and not more than seventeen. b. Not less than one-third of its members shall be from amongst the members of the Gram Panchayat. c. Not less than one-half of the members shall be women. d. The Deputy Sarpanch shall be its ex-officio chairman. e. Gram Sevak shall be its ex-officio member-secretary. Which of the statements given above are correct ?', '{"A": "Only a, b, c and d", "B": "Only b, c and e", "C": "Only a, b, c and e", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Straight to the answer — option B. A Village Development Committee must have at least one-third members from the Gram Panchayat, at least half women, and the Gram Sevak as ex-officio member-secretary — (b), (c), and (e). The member ceiling in (a) and making the Deputy Sarpanch ex-officio chairman in (d) do not match the Act.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21720, 'General', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Assertion (A) : Legislative control over administration in a Parliamentary system is different from that of Presidential system. Reason (B) : An important feature of democratic government is the legislative control over administration.', '{"A": "Both ''A'' and ''B'' are true and ''B'' is the correct explanation of ''A''.", "B": "Both ''A'' and ''B'' are true, but ''B'' is not the correct explanation of ''A''.", "C": "''A'' is true, but ''B'' is false.", "D": "''A'' is false, but ''B'' is true."}'::jsonb, 'B', 'On this one, option B. Both assertions are true: parliamentary and presidential systems exercise legislative control over the executive differently, and democratic government does involve such control. But (B) states a general democratic fact — it does not explain why the two systems differ, so it is not the correct explanation of (A).', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21721, 'General', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Which of the following statements related to ''Money Bill'' is/are correct ? a. It can be introduced either by a minister or by a private member. b. It cannot be introduced except on the recommendation of the Governor. c. If any question arises whether the bill is a money bill or not, the decision of the Governor is final. d. In case of a deadlock over a money bill, the Governor can summon a joint sitting of Legislative Assembly and Legislative Council. Answer Options :', '{"A": "Only a and b", "B": "Only b", "C": "Only a, b and c", "D": "Only a, c and d"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Go with option B. At the state level a Money Bill can be introduced only on the Governor''s recommendation — that is (b) alone. Private members cannot introduce it ((a) wrong), the Speaker (not the Governor) decides money-bill disputes ((c) wrong), and there is no joint sitting route for a state money-bill deadlock ((d) wrong).', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21722, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Narayan Meghaji Lokhande presented the questions of workers in which of the following newspapers ?', '{"A": "Samachar Chandrika", "B": "Prabhakar", "C": "Deenbandhu", "D": "Dnyanprakash"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right pick is option C. Narayan Meghaji Lokhande — Maharashtra''s pioneer trade-union organiser — raised mill-workers'' demands through the newspaper Deenbandhu from the 1880s. Samachar Chandrika, Prabhakar, and Dnyanprakash were other periodicals, not his labour platform.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21723, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Match the pairs : A B a. Balshastri Jambhekar I. Establishment of Widow Home b. Gopal Hari Deshmukh II. First supporter of female education c. Mahatma Jyotiba Phule III. Congregation for remarriage d. Maharshi Dhondo Keshav Karve IV. Orphanage Answer Options :', '{"A": "a-III, b-IV, c-II, d-I", "B": "a-II, b-III, c-IV, d-I", "C": "a-II, b-III, c-I, d-IV", "D": "a-III, b-II, c-IV, d-I"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Straight to the answer — option B. Balshastri Jambhekar backed early female education (a–II); Lokhitwadi Gopal Hari Deshmukh worked for widow remarriage (b–III); Jyotiba Phule ran orphanage and social institutions (c–IV); Maharshi Karve founded the Widow Home (d–I). That full set is option B.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21724, 'General', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'The Parliament of India acquires the power to legislate on any subject on the State List in national interest if a resolution to that effect is passed by the', '{"A": "Lok Sabha by a majority of its total membership.", "B": "Lok Sabha by a majority of not less than two-thirds of its total membership.", "C": "Rajya Sabha by a majority of its total membership.", "D": "Rajya Sabha by a majority of not less than two-thirds of its members present and voting."}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Pick option D. Article 249 empowers Parliament to legislate on a State List subject when the Rajya Sabha passes a resolution by not less than two-thirds of the members present and voting — not a simple Lok Sabha majority, and not two-thirds of the Rajya Sabha''s total strength.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21725, 'General', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Generally, the High Court of a State consists of a Chief Justice and _______.', '{"A": "nine other Judges", "B": "such other Judges as may be determined by the Governor", "C": "such other Judges as may be determined by the Parliament", "D": "such other Judges as may be determined by the President"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D. Article 216 says every High Court consists of a Chief Justice and such other Judges as the President may from time to time deem necessary — not a fixed bench of nine, nor a number fixed by the Governor or Parliament alone.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21726, 'General', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'The Constituent Assembly appointed a number of committees to deal with different tasks and works of Constitution-making. Who was the Chairman of the Rules of Procedure Committee ?', '{"A": "Dr. B.R. Ambedkar", "B": "Alladi Krishnaswami Ayyar", "C": "Dr. Rajendra Prasad", "D": "Dr. K.M. Munshi"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Working through it, option C is the one. Dr Rajendra Prasad chaired the Constituent Assembly''s Rules of Procedure Committee. Ambedkar headed the Drafting Committee; Alladi Krishnaswami Ayyar and K.M. Munshi were on drafting work but not this particular chairmanship.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21727, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Match the following : A B a. Pandita Ramabai I. ''Stree-Purush Tulana'' Book b. Ramabai Ranade II. Establishment of Nirashrit Seva Sadan c. Tarabai Shinde III. Establishment of Sharada Sadan d. Janakka Shinde IV. Establishment of ''Hindu Ladies Social Club'' Answer Options :', '{"A": "a-II, b-III, c-IV, d-I", "B": "a-I, b-IV, c-III, d-II", "C": "a-III, b-IV, c-I, d-II", "D": "a-IV, b-II, c-III, d-I"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C. Pandita Ramabai opened Sharada Sadan (a–III); Ramabai Ranade helped start the Hindu Ladies Social Club (b–IV); Tarabai Shinde authored Stree-Purush Tulana (c–I); Janakka Shinde was linked to Nirashrit Seva Sadan (d–II).', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21728, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Paramhans Sabha was established at Mumbai in 1849 and gave the emphasis on the following reforms : a. Widow Remarriage b. Women''s Education c. Break the Caste Barrier d. Acceptance of Idol Worship Which of the statements given above is/are correct ?', '{"A": "Only a and b", "B": "Only b and c", "C": "Only c", "D": "Only a, c and d"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'On this one, option C. Paramhans Sabha (1849, Mumbai), founded by Dadoba Pandurang, stressed breaking caste barriers and rejected idol worship. Widow remarriage, women''s education, and accepting idol worship were not its programme — only (c) fits.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21729, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'According to Dadabhai Naoroji, ''What was being drained out was _______, that could generate more economic development if invested in India.'' Fill in the blanks with the given right option.', '{"A": "Handicraft production", "B": "Indian currency", "C": "Entire cotton production", "D": "Potential surplus"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D. Dadabhai Naoroji''s ''drain of wealth'' thesis held that what Britain extracted was India''s potential surplus — income that, if invested at home, could have fuelled further development. Handicrafts, currency alone, or cotton output alone miss his core economic argument.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21730, 'General', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Match the following regarding and emergence of Indian workers and Labour movement : A B a. Narayan Meghaji Lokhande I. First President of All India Trade Union Congress b. Mahatma Gandhi II. Establishment of Madras Labour Union c. B.P. Wadia III. Establishment of Ahmedabad Textile Labour Association d. Lala Lajpat Rai IV. Placed the problems of labour through Deenbandhu newspaper Answer Options :', '{"A": "a-IV, b-III, c-II, d-I", "B": "a-III, b-IV, c-I, d-II", "C": "a-II, b-I, c-IV, d-III", "D": "a-IV, b-I, c-II, d-III"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Go with option A. Lokhande publicised labour issues in Deenbandhu (a–IV); Gandhi built the Ahmedabad Textile Labour Association (b–III); B.P. Wadia helped form the Madras Labour Union (c–II); Lala Lajpat Rai became the first president of the All India Trade Union Congress (d–I).', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21731, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Who made the following thoughts/statements regarding the effects of colonialism on Indians ? a. Indian economy ran overseas. b. Due to economic abstraction, world known enriched India became poverty stricken. c. An exploitation of Indian economy is like Ransom. d. By taking sword in hand it is time to manage our business. Answer Options :', '{"A": "a-Ramesh Chandra Dutt, b-Justice Ranade, c-Sir George Oxenden, d-Lokhitwadi Gopal Hari Deshmukh", "B": "a-Justice Ranade, b-Sir George Oxenden, c-Ramesh Chandra Dutt, d-Lokhitwadi Gopal Hari Deshmukh", "C": "a-Lokhitwadi Gopal Hari Deshmukh, b-Ramesh Chandra Dutt, c-Justice Ranade, d-Sir George Oxenden", "D": "a-Justice Ranade, b-Lokhitwadi Gopal Hari Deshmukh, c-Sir George Oxenden, d-Ramesh Chandra Dutt"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Pick option C. Lokhitwadi Gopal Hari Deshmukh argued the Indian economy was run for overseas benefit (a); R.C. Dutt showed how a once-rich India was reduced to poverty through economic drain (b); Justice Ranade compared colonial exploitation to ransom (c); Sir George Oxenden''s line about taking the sword to manage our own business closes the set (d).', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21732, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Which of the following crops production increased due to commercialization of agriculture during British Period ? a. Tea, Wheat b. Sugarcane, Cotton c. Jute, Indigo d. Tobacco, Opium Which of the statements given above are correct ?', '{"A": "Only a and b", "B": "Only a, c and d", "C": "Only b, c and d", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Working through it, option C is the one. Under commercial agriculture the British pushed export-oriented crops — sugarcane and cotton, jute and indigo, tobacco and opium ((b), (c), (d)). Tea expansion and wheat as a paired commercialisation claim in (a) is the weak link here.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21733, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Which award was given to Pandita Ramabai by the British Government ?', '{"A": "Kaisar-e-Hind", "B": "Kaisar-e-Hindu", "C": "Kaisar-e-Lady", "D": "Indian Super Lady"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer — option A. The British Government honoured Pandita Ramabai with the Kaisar-i-Hind medal for her social and humanitarian work. The other option spellings are not the actual imperial award title.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21734, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Who was the first leader of the revolution of native for farmers ? a. Baba Bhand b. Bijania c. Kajara Singh d. Tantya Bhilla Which of the statements given above is/are correct ?', '{"A": "Only a and b", "B": "Only c and d", "C": "Only b", "D": "Only d"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The right pick is option D. Tantya Bhilla (Tantia Bhil) led one of the earliest armed peasant/tribal revolts against oppressive land revenue — treated in Maharashtra history as the first major leader of the native farmers'' rebellion. Baba Bhand, Bijania, and Kajara Singh do not carry that ''first leader'' tag in standard texts.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21735, 'General', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Which of the following statements are true regarding the Revolt of 1857 ? a. With treacherous attitude Pant Sachiv of Bhor Chimnaji Raghunath (first) tendered Rango Bapuji Gupte to Britishers. b. Rani Bakabai of Nagpur Bhosale Dynasty supported the revolters. c. Chimasaheb of Kolhapur Chhatrapati Dynasty participated in revolt. d. Son of Rango Bapuji Gupte Sitarampant and Ramji Shirsal of Sawantwadi also participated in the Revolt. Answer Options :', '{"A": "Only a and c", "B": "Only b, c and d", "C": "Only a, c and d", "D": "Only c and d"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'On this one, option C. In Maharashtra''s 1857 story, Pant Sachiv Chimnaji Raghunath of Bhor betrayed Rango Bapuji Gupte (a); Kolhapur''s Chhatrapati Chimasaheb joined the revolt (c); Sitarampant (Rango''s son) and Ramji Shirsal of Sawantwadi took part (d). Rani Bakabai of Nagpur did not support the rebels — so (b) is excluded.', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21736, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'The longest National Highway in India is _______.', '{"A": "NH 44", "B": "NH 01", "C": "NH 48", "D": "NH 06"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through it, option A is the one. NH 44 — earlier numbered NH 7 — runs Srinagar to Kanyakumari and is India''s longest highway at roughly 4,000 km. NH 1, NH 48, and NH 6 are major corridors but shorter than this north–south trunk route.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21737, 'General', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Match the Industrial Regions and Industrial Areas : District Irrigation Scheme a. Nashik I. Butibori b. Kolhapur II. Shendra c. Nagpur III. Vinchur d. Aurangabad IV. Hupari Answer Options :', '{"A": "a-IV, b-III, c-II, d-I", "B": "a-III, b-I, c-II, d-IV", "C": "a-III, b-I, c-IV, d-II", "D": "a-III, b-IV, c-I, d-II"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Straight to the answer — option D. Nashik pairs with Vinchur (III), Kolhapur with Hupari (IV), Nagpur with Butibori (I), and Aurangabad with Shendra (II) — each district mapped to its recognised MIDC/industrial node. Ignore the misprinted ''Irrigation Scheme'' header; match the industrial-area names the list gives.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21738, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'The Civil Rebellion began from which of the following regions ?', '{"A": "Punjab and Sindh", "B": "Maharashtra and Karnataka", "C": "Andhra Pradesh and Orissa", "D": "Bengal and Bihar"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer here is option D. The Civil Rebellion phase of 1857 spread earliest and most intensely from Bengal and Bihar — the sepoy mutiny at Meerut linked with civilian uprisings across the Gangetic heartland before rippling elsewhere.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21739, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Which State of India accounted for the second rank in National Highway length as per report of Basic Road Statistics of India, 2017 ?', '{"A": "Maharashtra", "B": "Rajasthan", "C": "Madhya Pradesh", "D": "Uttar Pradesh"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'On this one, option D. Basic Road Statistics of India (2017) placed Uttar Pradesh second among states in National Highway length — Maharashtra often leads the table, but UP held the second slot in that report year.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21740, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'The salient features of Aurangabad Industrial City : a. Well-planned and greenfield smart city. b. The abbreviation is AURIC. c. The total investment will be ₹ 1,000 crs. d. It is a part of Delhi-Mumbai industrial corridor. Choose the correct option :', '{"A": "Only a", "B": "Only a and b", "C": "Only a, b and c", "D": "Only a, b and d"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer here is option D. AURIC is a DMIC-linked greenfield smart city and its name stands for Aurangabad Industrial City — (a), (b), and (d) hold. Statement (c) fixing total investment at exactly ₹1,000 crore understates the phased project outlay in official briefs.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21741, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'India''s population growth and temporal changes during 1981 to 2011 indicates the population transition stage of', '{"A": "Period of High growth with declining trend", "B": "Period of Rapid growth", "C": "Period of Steady growth", "D": "Period of Stagnant growth"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The examiner has marked option A. Between 1981 and 2011 India''s population kept growing in absolute terms but the growth rate was slowing — fertility fell and the curve shows high growth with a declining trend, not rapid acceleration or stagnation.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21742, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'The State which produces natural gas and mineral oil in India is _______.', '{"A": "Kerala", "B": "Himachal Pradesh", "C": "Goa", "D": "Assam"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The right pick is option D. Assam — Digboi and the broader Brahmaputra valley — produces both mineral oil and natural gas among the states listed. Kerala, Himachal Pradesh, and Goa lack comparable hydrocarbon production profiles in Indian energy geography.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21743, 'General', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'On the basis of soil formation, the first detailed and scientific soil classification of Maharashtra was done in 1938 by :', '{"A": "Dr. D. Smith", "B": "Dr. Kellogg and Dr. Thorp", "C": "Dr. Dokuchaev", "D": "Dr. Basu and Dr. Shirur"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Working through it, option D is the one. Dr Basu and Dr Shirur carried out the first detailed scientific soil classification of Maharashtra in 1938. Smith, Kellogg–Thorp, and Dokuchaev belong to global or foreign classification traditions, not this state-specific survey.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21744, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Which creeks are included in the ''Central Konkan'' of Maharashtra''s Konkan Regional Division ?', '{"A": "Deogarh, Achara and Karli creeks", "B": "Rajapuri, Bankot and Kelshi creeks", "C": "Dharamtar, Kalawal and Terekhol creeks", "D": "Dahanu, Vasai and Datiware creeks"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Straight to the answer — option B. Central Konkan in Maharashtra''s regional division covers Rajapuri, Bankot, and Kelshi creeks — mid-coast estuaries between the southern and northern Konkan blocks. Deogarh–Karli, Dharamtar–Terekhol, and Dahanu–Vasai sets belong to other subdivisions.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21745, 'General', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Which one of the following regions indicates the example of high intensity zone of earthquake in India ?', '{"A": "The Zone of Peninsula", "B": "Himalayan Belt from Kashmir to Assam", "C": "Central Zone", "D": "Ganga Plain"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Go with option B. The Himalayan belt from Kashmir to Assam sits in India''s highest seismic-intensity zone — young collision tectonics and repeated great earthquakes. The Peninsula, central block, and Ganga plain are comparatively lower-intensity on standard zoning maps.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21746, 'General', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Match the correct pairs of Irrigation Schemes and Districts in Maharashtra : District Irrigation Scheme a. Satara I. Mukane b. Nashik II. Vishnupuri c. Nanded III. Kanher d. Yavatmal IV. Bembala Answer Options :', '{"A": "a-II, b-III, c-IV, d-I", "B": "a-III, b-I, c-II, d-IV", "C": "a-III, b-IV, c-I, d-II", "D": "a-IV, b-II, c-III, d-I"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Pick option B. Kanher belongs to Satara (III), Mukane to Nashik (I), Vishnupuri to Nanded (II), and Bembala to Yavatmal (IV) — option B gives a–III, b–I, c–II, d–IV. Swapping Mukane to Satara or Kanher to Nashik breaks the standard Maharashtra irrigation map.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21747, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'The Laccadive islands and Minicoy islands are separated by', '{"A": "Eight Degree Channel", "B": "Nine Degree Channel", "C": "Ten Degree Channel", "D": "Zero Degree Channel"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B. The Nine Degree Channel separates the Laccadive island group from Minicoy in the Lakshadweep archipelago. Eight Degree Channel lies further north; Ten Degree separates Andaman from Nicobar.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21748, 'General', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'As per G.T. Trewartha''s climate classification, Western Coastal Plain and Tripura State exhibit which of the following types of climate ?', '{"A": "Humid Mountain Climate", "B": "Tropical Arid Climate", "C": "Tropical Monsoon Climate", "D": "Humid Sub-tropical Climate"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The examiner has marked option C. In G T Trewartha''s scheme the western coastal plain and Tripura fall under tropical monsoon (Am) climate — heavy seasonal rain in humid tropics. Humid mountain, tropical arid, and humid sub-tropical codes fit Himalayan, desert, or interior settings, not this pairing.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21749, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, '_______ is the apex organisation to provide credit for the promotion of agriculture and allied activities in rural areas.', '{"A": "Reserve Bank", "B": "State Bank of India", "C": "NABARD", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right pick is option C. NABARD is the apex body for promoting agricultural and allied rural credit through cooperatives and regional rural banks. RBI regulates; SBI is a commercial bank — neither carries NABARD''s distinct apex refinance mandate.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21750, 'General', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'According to the 2011 Census, the density of population in the country is _______.', '{"A": "117 per sq. km.", "B": "157 per sq. km.", "C": "282 per sq. km.", "D": "382 per sq. km."}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Straight to the answer — option D. Census 2011 put India''s population density at 382 persons per square kilometre — up from 325 in 2001. The 117, 157, and 282 figures belong to earlier decades or misquoted averages, not the all-India 2011 headline.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (21751, 'General', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Which of the following percentage indicates the proportion of rain received in Maharashtra from North-Western monsoon ?', '{"A": "58%", "B": "65%", "C": "85%", "D": "95%"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'On this one, option C. According to the answer key, about 85% of Maharashtra''s annual rainfall comes from the southwest monsoon current — the bulk of the state''s precipitation budget in standard geography texts. The stem says ''North-Western monsoon''; if your textbook wording differs, defer to the key figure of 85%.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21752, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, '_______ was introduced in 1995 for inexpensive and speedy settlement of bank customer disputes.', '{"A": "Prudential Norms", "B": "Customer Service Committee", "C": "Banking Ombudsman Scheme", "D": "International Accounting Practices"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Go with option C. The Banking Ombudsman Scheme, introduced in 1995, gives bank customers an inexpensive and speedy forum for dispute redress — RBI''s dedicated grievance layer. Prudential norms, customer-service committees, and accounting standards serve different regulatory functions.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21753, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Consider the following statements : a. After Independence, the Government of India appointed the National Income Committee in August, 1948. b. The committee consisted of Prof. P.C. Mahalanobis, Prof. D.R. Gadgil and Prof. V.K.R.V. Rao. c. The first report of the National Income Committee appeared in 1951 and the final report in 1954. Which of the statements given above is/are incorrect ? Answer Options :', '{"A": "Only a", "B": "Only a and b", "C": "Only a and c", "D": "Only b and c"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Pick option A. The National Income Committee did include Mahalanobis, Gadgil, and V K R V Rao and its reports came in 1951 and 1954 — (b) and (c) stand. Statement (a) alone is keyed incorrect, likely over the August 1948 appointment date versus the accepted 1949 chronology in standard accounts.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21754, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'What is the biggest source of income for the Central Government in the Union Budget 2021 – 22 ?', '{"A": "GST", "B": "Borrowing and other liabilities", "C": "Income Tax", "D": "Corporate Tax"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Working through it, option B is the one. In Union Budget 2021–22, borrowing and other liabilities formed the largest single receipt head — ahead of GST, income tax, or corporate tax individually — reflecting pandemic-year deficit financing through market borrowings.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21755, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Which of the following market segments is growth and profit oriented in the Indian Commercial Banking System ?', '{"A": "Mutual Funds", "B": "Mobile Banking", "C": "Retail Banking", "D": "Internet Banking"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C. Indian commercial banks treat retail banking — personal accounts, loans, cards, and cross-sell — as the high-growth, profit-oriented segment. Mutual funds, mobile, and internet channels support delivery but retail drives the margin story the syllabus highlights.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21756, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Productivity in Indian agriculture is mainly dependent on two sets of factors. Those are : a. Technological Factors b. Human Resource c. Institutional Factors d. Irrigation Facilities Answer Options :', '{"A": "Only a and c", "B": "Only a and d", "C": "Only a and b", "D": "Only c and d"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The examiner has marked option A. Agricultural productivity in India is mainly explained by technological inputs — seeds, mechanisation, plant protection — and institutional factors such as land tenure, credit, extension, and marketing. Human-resource or irrigation-only pairings capture partial drivers, not the keyed dual set.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21757, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Which of the following is not an important objective of Special Economic Zones in India ?', '{"A": "Generation of additional economic activity", "B": "Promotion of export", "C": "Development of agriculture", "D": "Creation of employment"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Go with option C. SEZ policy aims at extra economic activity, exports, and employment through industrial and tax incentives — not primary-sector agriculture development. Agriculture sits outside the export-processing and manufacturing logic SEZ notifications emphasise.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21758, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'The infant mortality rate is the number of deaths of children under _______ of age in a given geographical area during a given year, per 1000 live births.', '{"A": "One year", "B": "One month", "C": "One week", "D": "One day"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through it, option A is the one. Infant mortality rate counts deaths of children under one year of age per 1,000 live births in a given area and year — not one month, week, or day.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21759, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Which of the following is/are the objectives of Fiscal Responsibility and Budget Management Act, 2003 ? a. To set limits on government borrowings under a time-bound programme. b. To achieve zero revenue deficit and bring down fiscal deficits. c. To make the government responsible for ensuring long term macroeconomic stability. d. Improving transparency in the fiscal operations of the government. Answer Options :', '{"A": "None of the above", "B": "All of the above", "C": "Only a and b", "D": "Only c and d"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'On this one, option B. The FRBM Act 2003 sets borrowing limits on a time-bound path, targets zero revenue deficit and lower fiscal deficit, secures long-term macro stability, and improves fiscal transparency — all four objectives appear in the statute, so ''all of the above'' is the match.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21760, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'According to Chief Economic Advisor Krishnamurthy Subramaniam (Economic Survey 2020-21), what may be the shape of Economic recovery ?', '{"A": "U-shape", "B": "S-shape", "C": "V-shape", "D": "Z-shape"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Straight to the answer — option C. Chief Economic Adviser Krishnamurthy Subramanian, in the Economic Survey 2020-21, argued India''s rebound after the COVID shock could follow a V-shaped recovery — a sharp fall followed by a relatively quick upturn.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21761, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Consider the following statements : a. International trade is based on differences in prices of goods and services from country to country. b. The terms of trade refer to the exchange ratio of export and import goods or their price ratio. c. The Balance of Payments record in International Trade is maintained in a standard double entry book-keeping method. Which of the statements given above are correct ? Answer Options :', '{"A": "All of the above", "B": "Only a", "C": "Only c", "D": "Only a and b"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The examiner has marked option A. International trade rests on cross-country price differences (a); terms of trade measure export–import price ratios (b); and the balance of payments is kept in standard double-entry form (c) — all three statements stand.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21762, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'What is the range of tax rates for taxable income as per the Union Budget, 2020 of India ?', '{"A": "5% to 25%", "B": "5% to 35%", "C": "5% to 30%", "D": "5% to 20%"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right pick is option C. Union Budget 2020 retained the new personal income-tax slabs with rates from 5% up to 30% on taxable income — not 25%, 35%, or a 20% ceiling.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21763, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Which of the following statements are correct ? a. The price of electricity for Indian households is lowest in the world. b. The price of electricity for Indian industries is highest in the world. c. Cost recovery in distribution of power is satisfactory in India. Answer Options :', '{"A": "Only a and b", "B": "Only b and c", "C": "Only a and c", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer here is option D. Economic Survey data do not support any of the three claims: household power is not the world''s cheapest, industrial tariffs are not the world''s highest, and cost recovery in distribution remains weak — so none of a, b, or c holds.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21764, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'A neutron having energy of 0.025 eV is a/an _______.', '{"A": "Thermal neutron", "B": "Epithermal neutron", "C": "Fast neutron", "D": "Slow neutron"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'On this one, option A. A neutron with about 0.025 eV energy is at room-temperature thermal energy — the slow neutrons used in thermal reactors — not epithermal, fast, or merely ''slow'' in the loose sense.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21765, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Transfer of heat from a body at low temperature to a body at higher temperature is', '{"A": "impossible", "B": "possible by keeping both the bodies in contact", "C": "possible by doing some external work", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Go with option C. Heat will not flow spontaneously from a colder to a hotter body, but a refrigerator or heat pump can move it that way by doing external work — exactly what the Second Law allows.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21766, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Choose the correct pair/pairs of the animal/animals and their scientific name/names ? a. Asiatic lion — Panthera leo persica b. Royal Bengal Tiger — Panthera tigris c. Indian Rhinoceros — Rhinoceros unicornis d. Thamin Deer — Cervus eldi Answer Options :', '{"A": "Only b and c", "B": "Only c and d", "C": "Only a and c", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D. All four pairings check out: Asiatic lion — Panthera leo persica; Royal Bengal Tiger — Panthera tigris; Indian Rhinoceros — Rhinoceros unicornis; Thamin Deer — Cervus eldi.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21767, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'The high strength-to-weight ratio of _______ alloy mainly recommends their use in aircraft and automobile industries.', '{"A": "light steel", "B": "light titanium", "C": "light copper", "D": "light aluminium"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Straight to the answer — option D. Light aluminium alloys give high strength for low weight, which is why aircraft and automobile bodies rely on them more than on light steel, titanium, or copper.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21768, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'The minimum audible frequency of sound means', '{"A": "threshold intensity of audibility", "B": "lower pitch limit of audibility", "C": "upper pitch limit of audibility", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Pick option B. The minimum audible frequency is the lower pitch limit of human hearing — roughly 20 Hz — not threshold intensity (loudness) or the upper pitch cut-off.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21769, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'In lower atmosphere, smog is formed by the reaction between hydrocarbon and nitrogen oxide. This interaction produces _______ as secondary pollutants.', '{"A": "only ozone and aldehydes", "B": "only aldehydes and ketones", "C": "only aldehydes, ketones, peroxyacyl nitrate", "D": "ozone, aldehydes, ketones, peroxyacyl nitrate"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The right pick is option D. Photochemical smog from hydrocarbons and nitrogen oxides yields a full basket of secondary pollutants — ozone, aldehydes, ketones, and peroxyacyl nitrates (PAN) — not just one or two classes.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21770, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Diamond is a _______.', '{"A": "Metallic Crystal", "B": "Covalent Crystal", "C": "Ionic Crystal", "D": "Molecular Crystal"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Working through it, option B is the one. Diamond is a covalent network crystal — each carbon bonded tetrahedrally in a giant lattice — not metallic, ionic, or a simple molecular crystal.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21771, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Amoeba is a protozoan animal because a. it is a cellular animal without tissues and organs. b. it is the simplest and most primitive of all animals. c. pseudopodia is present for locomotion. d. it is a pore-bearing animal. Which of the statement/s given above is/are correct ?', '{"A": "Only a", "B": "Only a and c", "C": "Only a, b and c", "D": "Only c and d"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C. Amoeba is a single-celled protozoan without tissues or organs (a), among the simplest animals (b), and moves by pseudopodia (c) — pore-bearing (d) describes sponges, not amoeba.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21772, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Which of the following animal group/groups was/were the first vertebrate to become adapted to life on land ?', '{"A": "Only c and d (Mammals and Aves)", "B": "Only b and d (Amphibians and Aves)", "C": "Only a (Reptilians)", "D": "Only b (Amphibians)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'On this one, option D. Amphibians were the first vertebrates to colonise land, bridging aquatic and terrestrial life — reptiles, birds, and mammals adapted later.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21773, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Which of the following is the causal organism of Wheat Rust disease ?', '{"A": "Puccinia graminis tritici", "B": "Xanthomonas citri", "C": "Puccinia purpurea", "D": "Plasmopora viticola"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Pick option A. Wheat rust is caused by the fungus *Puccinia graminis* tritici — the classic black/stem rust pathogen — not citrus, sorghum, or grape downy-mildew organisms.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21774, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'In Agriculture, groundwater is tapped by _______.', '{"A": "canals", "B": "sinking wells", "C": "ponds", "D": "tanks"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Working through it, option B is the one. Farmers reach groundwater by sinking tubewells or bore wells into the aquifer — canals, ponds, and tanks store or convey surface water instead.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21775, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'When kidney tubular reabsorption fails, copious urination follows. What is this disease (metabolic disorder) called ?', '{"A": "Diabetes mellitus", "B": "Diabetes insipidus", "C": "Juvenile onset diabetes", "D": "Non-insulin dependent diabetes mellitus"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B. When kidney tubules fail to reabsorb water, the patient passes huge volumes of dilute urine — diabetes insipidus — not the sugar-driven polyuria of diabetes mellitus.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21776, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Which of the following vaccine is administered by oral route ?', '{"A": "Bacillus Calmette-Guerin", "B": "Sabin", "C": "Salk", "D": "Mumps, Measles, Rubella"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B. Sabin polio vaccine is given orally (OPV); BCG, Salk polio, and MMR are injected routes.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21777, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Srikant stands facing north on the ground. He turns right and travels 30 km. Then he turns left and travels 20 km. Again he turns right and travels 40 km. Again he turns right and travels 35 km. Which direction is he facing now ?', '{"A": "East", "B": "North-East", "C": "South-West", "D": "South"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'On this one, option D. From North: right to East (30 km), left to North (20 km), right to East (40 km), right to South (35 km) — he ends facing South.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21778, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Which of the following cholesterol is considered as good cholesterol ?', '{"A": "LDL cholesterol", "B": "VLDL cholesterol", "C": "LDL and VLDL cholesterol", "D": "HDL cholesterol"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Straight to the answer — option D. HDL cholesterol carries excess cholesterol back to the liver for disposal — the ''good'' fraction — whereas LDL and VLDL raise arterial risk.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21779, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'A devotee, while going to pray in the temple, put flowers on each step that indicated its number. When he offered 9 flowers to God, he had 17 flowers in balance. If the temple had 24 steps, then how many flowers did the devotee have ?', '{"A": "415", "B": "362", "C": "346", "D": "326"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D. Flowers on steps 1 through 24 total 1+2+…+24 = 300; after offering 9 to God and keeping 17, the devotee started with 300+9+17 = 326 flowers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21780, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'In a class of 100 students, 40 students passed in Mathematics and 60 passed in English. 8 students failed in both Mathematics and English. How many students passed in both the subjects ?', '{"A": "5", "B": "15", "C": "8", "D": "16"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Go with option C. Eight failed both, so 92 passed at least one subject; both-pass = Maths + English − at least one = 40+60−92 = 8.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21781, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Niraj''s watch is fast by 5½ minutes in a day. Piyush''s watch lags behind by 35 seconds per hour. If their watches indicated the same time at 8 o''clock in the morning, then by how many minutes would Neeraj''s watch be ahead of Piyush''s watch that night at 12 o''clock ?', '{"A": "10 minutes", "B": "13 minutes", "C": "9 minutes", "D": "14 minutes"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B. From 8 a.m. to midnight is 16 hours: Niraj''s watch gains 5½ × (16/24) = 11/3 minutes, and Piyush''s loses 35 × 16 ÷ 60 = 28/3 minutes — together 13 minutes ahead.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21782, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'There are 8 points in a plane, no three of which are collinear. If lines are drawn by joining two points, how many such lines would be drawn ?', '{"A": "25", "B": "29", "C": "27", "D": "28"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Pick option D. With 8 points and no three collinear, every line joins two points — number of lines = ⁸C₂ = 8×7/2 = 28.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21783, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Who discovered the natural classification system of plants ?', '{"A": "Theophrastus", "B": "Bentham and Hooker", "C": "Carl Linnaeus", "D": "G.M. Smith"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Go with option B. Bentham and Hooker''s *Genera Plantarum* laid out a natural classification of flowering plants by affinity — Theophrastus and Linnaeus came earlier; G.M. Smith worked on algae.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21784, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Neha can do a work in 6 days and Rekha can do it in 18 days. How many days would it take them to do the same work if they worked together ?', '{"A": "4.5", "B": "4", "C": "5", "D": "3.5"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer — option A. Combined rate 1/6 + 1/18 = 2/9 per day, so Neha and Rekha finish together in 9/2 = 4.5 days.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21785, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'In the following question, events I and II are given. You have to read both carefully and decide their nature of relationship. You have to assume that the given information in I and II are true and decide the correct answer. Events : I. Mr. Hari was killed in a fire. II. A fire broke out in the company. Answer Options :', '{"A": "I is the effect and II is its principal cause.", "B": "II is the effect and I is its principal cause.", "C": "II is the effect, but I is not its principal cause.", "D": "None of the above is correct."}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The right pick is option D. A company fire and Mr Hari''s death in some fire are separate facts — without proof they are the same incident, no option correctly fixes cause and effect.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21786, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'By which Venn-diagram can the given sets of words be shown ? Teachers, Writers, Married persons.', '{"A": "Three overlapping circles (all intersecting)", "B": "Two separate circles", "C": "Two overlapping circles with one separate", "D": "Three concentric circles"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer — option A. Some teachers are writers, some writers are married, and each set can overlap the others — three mutually intersecting circles capture all three possibilities.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21787, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'If A = 1, B = 2, C = 3, ....., Z = 26, then how will you write the word ''GODFATHER'' ?', '{"A": "7-15-6-4-20-12-8-5-18", "B": "7-15-4-6-20-8-5-18-18", "C": "7-15-4-6-2-10-8-5-18", "D": "7-15-4-6-1-20-8-5-18"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Working through it, option D is the one. Letter values G-O-D-F-A-T-H-E-R give 7-15-4-6-1-20-8-5-18 — match each alphabet position to its number in order.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21788, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Find the odd man out from the following numbers : 343, 324, 3375, 10648, 64', '{"A": "64", "B": "3375", "C": "324", "D": "10648"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The examiner has marked option C. 343, 3375, 10648 and 64 are perfect cubes (7³, 15³, 22³, 4³); 324 = 18² is a square, not a cube — the odd one out.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21789, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Niraj covered the first 20 km distance, out of a total of 60 km, at a speed of 10 km/hr, the next 20 km distance at 12 km/hr and the remaining 20 km distance at 15 km/hr. What is the average speed of Niraj to cover the 60 km distance ?', '{"A": "12 km/hr", "B": "13 km/hr", "C": "14 km/hr", "D": "11 km/hr"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The verified answer here is option A. Time for three equal 20 km legs: 20/10 + 20/12 + 20/15 = 5 hours total; average speed = 60 ÷ 5 = 12 km/hr.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21790, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Which of the following is in descending order ?', '{"A": "5/8, 9/13, 11/17", "B": "5/8, 11/17, 9/13", "C": "9/13, 11/17, 5/8", "D": "11/17, 9/13, 5/8"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right pick is option C. As decimals: 9/13 ≈ 0.692, 11/17 ≈ 0.647, 5/8 = 0.625 — descending order is 9/13, then 11/17, then 5/8.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21791, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'The simple interest and compound interest for 2 years of a sum is ₹ 1,800 and ₹ 1,890 respectively. What is the rate of interest per cent per annum ?', '{"A": "10", "B": "9", "C": "12", "D": "15"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through it, option A is the one. CI minus SI for 2 years equals P(r/100)²; with SI = 1800 giving Pr/50 = 1800, the extra ₹90 fixes r at 10% per annum.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21792, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'On reducing the entry fee by 35% in a park, the number of visitors increased by 40%. Then the percent increase or decrease in the income from the entry fee is', '{"A": "7% decrease", "B": "9% increase", "C": "9% decrease", "D": "5% decrease"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The examiner has marked option C. New revenue = 0.65 × 1.40 = 0.91 of the original — a 9% decrease, not a simple 5% net change.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21793, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'According to the report of the National Crime Registration Department, the information related to Child Crime is as follows : a. In the year 2018, 109 children were sexually abused every day. b. 39827 such incidents were reported in 2018. c. In 2018, there were 21401 incidents of rape of girls. d. The highest 2832 incidents of rape on children occurred in Maharashtra (2018). Which of the above statements are correct ?', '{"A": "Only a, b and c", "B": "Only b, c and d", "C": "Only a, c and d", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer here is option D. All four statements match the NCRB 2018 child-crime figures cited in that year''s report — daily abuse count, total incidents, girl rape cases and Maharashtra''s top rank.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21794, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'The schools, colleges, universities, educational as well as private institutions may witness historical places. Keeping this aim in view, which is the first State in India that decided to set up ''Jail Tourism'' ?', '{"A": "Rajasthan", "B": "Uttar Pradesh", "C": "Maharashtra", "D": "Bihar"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Working through it, option C is the one. Maharashtra was the first State to launch ''Jail Tourism'', opening historic prisons for students and visitors to learn from the freedom struggle.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21795, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Department of AIDS control has been merged with _______ and now it is known as National AIDS Control Organisation (NACO).', '{"A": "Family Planning Association of India", "B": "Department of Health and Family Welfare", "C": "National Leprosy Eradication Programme", "D": "National TB Control Programme"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Straight to the answer — option B. The erstwhile Department of AIDS Control was merged into the Department of Health and Family Welfare and now functions as NACO under that ministry.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21796, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Following is the work of Dinabandhu Sahu, honoured by NIRI : a. A book of ''Farming the Ocean'' on sea algae. b. Production of short film ''Biodiversity of Life'' based on Mary Kom. c. Fellowship and Research in International Society for Energy Environment and Sustainability. d. Sea farm training based on Project Chilika. Which of the above sentences is/are incorrect ?', '{"A": "Only a and c", "B": "Only b", "C": "Only a, c and d", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B. Dinabandhu Sahu''s sea-algae book, ISEES fellowship and Chilika sea-farm training are credited to him; the Mary Kom biodiversity short film is not — only statement (b) is wrong.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21797, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Which of the following novels written by Sonali Navangul has won the ''Marathi Sahitya Akademi Award'' in 2021 ?', '{"A": "Swachhand", "B": "Dream Runner", "C": "Prakashvata", "D": "Madhyaratrinantarche Taas"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer here is option D. Sonali Navangul''s novel ''Madhyaratrinantarche Taas'' won the Marathi Sahitya Akademi Award in 2021.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21798, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Winner of the Nobel Prize for Economics (2019), Abhijeet Banerjee''s life journey till date is given in points below. Reorder them and choose the correct option. a. Contributed in preparation of Scheme Nyuntam Aay Yojana (NYAY) for poverty eradication in India. b. Written a book titled ''Poor Economics''. c. Received the Infosys Prize. d. Studied economics at Presidency College, Kolkata. Answer Options :', '{"A": "c, b, d, a", "B": "d, b, a, c", "C": "d, c, b, a", "D": "c, b, a, d"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Straight to the answer — option C. Chronology: economics at Presidency College, Kolkata (d) → Infosys Prize (c) → ''Poor Economics'' (b) → NYAY scheme work (a).', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21799, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Which of the following are characteristics of GSAT-30 ? a. Weight – 3357 kg b. Provides high quality Television, Telecommunication and Broadcast services c. Equipped with 12C, 12Ku Band Transponder d. High quality communication satellite Answer Options :', '{"A": "Only a and c", "B": "Only b and d", "C": "Only a, c and d", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D. GSAT-30 weighed about 3357 kg, carried 12 C and 12 Ku-band transponders, and served TV, telecom and broadcast needs as a high-quality communication satellite — all four points hold.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21800, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Lionel Messi was selected for which of the following awards in 2021 for the seventh time ?', '{"A": "European Golden Shoe", "B": "World Player of the Year", "C": "World Soccer Player of the Year", "D": "Ballon d''Or"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Working through it, option D is the one. Lionel Messi won the Ballon d''Or in 2021 — his record seventh time — not the Golden Shoe or FIFA''s differently named player awards.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (21801, 'General', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'On the eve of 75th Independence day, who was honoured with the peacetime Gallantry Award — ''Ashoka Chakra'' ? a. ASI Babu Ram b. Police Constable Altaf Hussain c. Lt. Governor Girish Chandra Murmu d. Governor of Mizoram, P.S. Shreedharan Pillai Answer Options :', '{"A": "Only a and b", "B": "Only c and d", "C": "Only b", "D": "Only a"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The right pick is option D. On the 75th Independence Day peacetime gallantry list, ASI Babu Ram alone received the Ashoka Chakra among the names given — not the other three.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21802, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Consider the following statements : a. Kiwi is India''s first certified organic fruit. b. Arunachal Pradesh is the first State in the country to obtain an organic certification for its Kiwis. Which of the statements given above is/are correct ?', '{"A": "Only a", "B": "Only b", "C": "Both a and b", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The examiner has marked option C. Kiwi is India''s first certified organic fruit, and Arunachal Pradesh was the first State to obtain organic certification for its kiwi crop — both statements stand.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21803, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'In which year did Avani Chaturvedi, Bhawana Kanth and Mohana Singh create history by becoming the first women pilots to be commissioned into the fighter stream of Indian Air Force ?', '{"A": "2015", "B": "2016", "C": "2017", "D": "2018"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Straight to the answer — option B. Avani Chaturvedi, Bhawana Kanth and Mohana Singh were commissioned as the IAF''s first women fighter pilots in 2016.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21804, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Which Space agency has launched the first all-electric experimental aircraft ''X-57 Maxwell'' ?', '{"A": "LAPAN", "B": "ISRO", "C": "CNES", "D": "NASA"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Working through it, option D is the one. NASA developed and tested the all-electric experimental aircraft X-57 Maxwell — not ISRO, LAPAN or CNES.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21805, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Which artificial satellite was launched by India on 11th December, 2019 through PSLV – C48 launcher ?', '{"A": "RISAT – 2BR1", "B": "EMISAT", "C": "CARTOSAT – 2B", "D": "GSAT – 31"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A. PSLV-C48 on 11 December 2019 placed RISAT-2BR1 into orbit along with nine customer satellites.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21806, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Under Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana (Urban) (PMAY-U), as on 18th January, 2021 _______ houses have been sanctioned.', '{"A": "68.1 Lakhs", "B": "128.8 Lakhs", "C": "165.8 Lakhs", "D": "109.2 Lakhs"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer here is option D. PMAY-U data as on 18 January 2021 put total sanctioned houses at about 109.2 lakh — the figure the answer key selects.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21807, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'Select the right option regarding the Chairperson of 93rd Akhil Bhartiya Marathi Sahitya Sammelan, Senior Literary Author and Thinker, Father Francis Dibrito''s life happenings till date. a. National Award for translation of ''Subodh Bible – Nava Karar'' book by Sahitya Academy. b. Chairperson of 15th Marathi Christi Sahitya Sammelan in Pune. c. The ordination as a Catholic priest. d. Chief Editor of newsletter ''Suvarta''. Answer Options :', '{"A": "c, d, b and a", "B": "d, c, a and b", "C": "c, b, a and d", "D": "d, a, b and c"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The examiner has marked option A. Father Francis Dibrito''s timeline runs: ordination as priest (c) → chief editor of ''Suvarta'' (d) → chair of the 15th Marathi Christi Sahitya Sammelan, Pune (b) → Sahitya Akademi translation award for ''Subodh Bible – Nava Karar'' (a).', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21808, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'खालील विधाने विचारात घ्या : अ. सरपंचावे (ज्याची निवड ग्राम पंचायतीच्या सभासदांकडून झालेली आहे) अथवा उपसरपंचावे, रिक्त (राजीनामामुळे) झालेले पद ते रिक्त झाल्याच्या दिनांका पासून तीस दिवसांच्या आत भरले पाहिजे. ब. थेट जनतेमार्फत निवडलेल्या सरपंचावे रिक्त झालेले पद ते रिक्त झाल्याच्या दिनांका पासून तीन महिन्यांच्या आत भरले पाहिजे. क. ग्राम पंचायतीच्या ज्या सदस्याचे पद सतत ग्राम पंचायतीच्या सभेला गैरहजर राहण्याच्या कारणास्तव रिकामे झाले असेल तर तो लगेच पुन्हा निवडून येण्यास पात्र नसतो. वरीलपैकी कोणते विधान/ने बरोबर आहे/आहेत ?', '{"A": "फक्त अ", "B": "फक्त अ आणि क", "C": "फक्त ब आणि क", "D": "अ, ब आणि क"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय A येतो. Maharashtra Gram Panchayat नियमांनुसार resignation मुळे Sarpanch किंवा Upa-Sarpanch पद रिक्त झाल्यास ते तीस दिवसांत भरावे लागते — विधान (a) बरोबर. थेट निवडलेल्या Sarpanch च्या रिक्त जागेस (b) मधील तीन महिन्यांचा नियम लागत नाही, आणि सलग सभा गैरहजरी (c) प्रमाणे re-election अपात्रता निर्माण करत नाही.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21809, 'General', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, '''सरकारिया आयोग'' _________ यासाठी अनुकूल होते.', '{"A": "राज्यपाल पद रद्द करावे", "B": "अखिल भारतीय सेवा रद्द करावी", "C": "आंतर-राज्य परिषद रद्द करावी", "D": "वरीलपैकी एकही नाही"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'येथे खात्रीशीर उत्तर पर्याय D. Sarkaria Commission (1983) ने Centre–State relations पाहिले आणि सहकार्य मजबूत करण्याची शिफारस केली — Governor, All India Services किंवा Inter-State Council रद्द करण्याचे ते समर्थन करत नव्हते. तीनही पर्याय अशी रद्दीची मागणी सांगतात जी Commission ने केली नाही.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21810, 'General', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'सर्वसाधारणपणे, राज्याच्या उच्च न्यायालयामध्ये मुख्य न्यायाधीश आणि _________ समावेश असतो.', '{"A": "इतर नऊ न्यायाधीशांचा", "B": "राज्यपाल ठरविल इतके इतर न्यायाधीशांचा", "C": "संसद ठरविल इतके इतर न्यायाधीशांचा", "D": "राष्ट्रपती ठरविल इतके इतर न्यायाधीशांचा"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'परीक्षकाने पर्याय D चिन्हांकित केला. Article 216 नुसार प्रत्येक High Court मध्ये Chief Justice आणि President वेळोवेळी आवश्यक समजेल तितके इतर न्यायाधीश — नऊ जणांची निश्चित bench नाही, Governor किंवा Parliament एकट्याने ठरवत नाहीत.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21811, 'General', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'विधान (अ) : संसदीय पद्धतीमध्ये प्रशासनावरील कायदेमंडळाचे नियंत्रण अध्यक्षीय पद्धतीपेक्षा भिन्न असते. कारण (ब) : प्रशासनावर कायदेमंडळाचे नियंत्रण हे लोकसत्ताक शासनाचे महत्त्वाचे वैशिष्ट्य आहे.', '{"A": "''अ'' आणि ''ब'' दोन्हीही बरोबर आणि ''ब'' हे ''अ'' चे योग्य स्पष्टीकरण आहे.", "B": "''अ'' आणि ''ब'' दोन्हीही बरोबर, परंतु ''ब'' हे ''अ'' चे योग्य स्पष्टीकरण नाही.", "C": "''अ'' हे बरोबर आहे, परंतु ''ब'' हे चुकीचे आहे.", "D": "''अ'' हे चुकीचे आहे, परंतु ''ब'' हे बरोबर आहे."}'::jsonb, 'B', 'या प्रश्नात पर्याय B. दोन्ही विधाने खरे: parliamentary व presidential प्रणाली executive वर legislative control वेगळ्या पद्धतीने करतात, आणि लोकशाहीत असे नियंत्रण असते. पण (B) सामान्य लोकशाही तथ्य सांगते — दोन प्रणाली का वेगळ्या आहेत हे स्पष्ट करत नाही, म्हणून (A) चे योग्य स्पष्टीकरण नाही.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21812, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'राज्याच्या महाधिवक्त्यासंबंधी खालीलपैकी कोणते विधान बरोबर आहे ?', '{"A": "तो राज्याच्या मंत्री परिषदेची इच्छा असेपर्यंत आपल्या पदावर राहू शकतो.", "B": "त्याचे मानधन राज्य विधिमंडळाद्वारे निश्चित केले जाते.", "C": "तो राज्यशासना विरुद्ध असलेल्या खटल्यात खाजगी पक्षकारासाठी वकील म्हणून उभा राहू शकतो.", "D": "वरीलपैकी एकही नाही"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'योग्य उत्तर पर्याय D. Advocate General Governor च्या pleasure वर पद धरतो (Council of Ministers वर नाही), वेतन Governor ठरवतो (Legislature नाही), आणि तो private party साठी State Government विरुद्ध वकिली करू शकत नाही — म्हणून (A)–(C) पैकी काहीही उभे राहत नाही.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21813, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'महाराष्ट्र ग्राम पंचायत अधिनियमातील ''ग्राम विकास समित्या'' संबंधीच्या तरतुदी बाबत खालील विधाने विचारात घ्या : अ. ग्राम विकास समितीतील सदस्यांची एकूण संख्या सातपेक्षा कमी नसेल आणि सतरा पेक्षा जास्त नसेल. ब. ग्राम विकास समितीतील सदस्यांपैकी एकूतीयांशापेक्षा कमी नसतील इतके सदस्य ग्राम पंचायतीच्या सदस्यांमधील असतील. क. तिच्या सदस्यांपैकी एक द्वितीयांशापेक्षा कमी नसतील इतके सदस्य महिला असतील. ड. उप सरपंच हा तिचा पदसिद्ध अध्यक्ष असेल. ई. ग्रामसेवक हा तिचा पदसिद्ध सदस्य-सचिव असेल. वरीलपैकी कोणती विधाने योग्य आहेत ?', '{"A": "फक्त अ, ब, क आणि ड", "B": "फक्त ब, क आणि ई", "C": "फक्त अ, ब, क आणि ई", "D": "वरील सर्व"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'थेट उत्तर — पर्याय B. Village Development Committee मध्ये किमान एक-third सदस्य Gram Panchayat मधून, अर्धे महिला, आणि Gram Sevak ex-officio member-secretary — (b), (c), (e). (a) मधील सदस्य संख्येची मर्यादा आणि (d) मध्ये Deputy Sarpanch ला ex-officio chairman करणे कायद्याशी जुळत नाही.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21814, 'General', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, '''अर्थ विधेयका'' बाबतीत खालीलपैकी कोणते विधान/ने बरोबर आहे/आहेत ? अ. ते मंत्री किंवा खाजगी सदस्य मांडू शकतो. ब. ते राज्यपालांच्या शिफारशी शिवाय मांडता येत नाही. क. एखादे विधेयक अर्थ विधेयक आहे किंवा नाही असा प्रश्न उपस्थित झाल्यास राज्यपालांचा अंतिम निर्णय असतो. ड. जर दोन्ही सभागृहांमध्ये अर्थ विधेयका बाबत पेच निर्माण झाल्यास राज्यपाल विधानसभा आणि विधान परिषदेची संयुक्त बैठक बोलावू शकतात. पर्यायी उत्तरे :', '{"A": "फक्त अ आणि ब", "B": "फक्त ब", "C": "फक्त अ, ब आणि क", "D": "फक्त अ, क आणि ड"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'पर्याय B निवडा. राज्यस्तरावर Money Bill फक्त Governor च्या recommendation वरच सादर होऊ शकते — फक्त (b). Private member सादर करू शकत नाही ((a) चुकीचे), money-bill वाद Speaker ठरवतो Governor नाही ((c) चुकीचे), आणि state money-bill deadlock साठी joint sitting मार्ग नाही ((d) चुकीचे).', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21815, 'General', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'भारतीय संसदेला राज्यसूचीतील कोणत्याही विषयाबाबत राष्ट्रीय हितासाठी कायदा करण्याचा अधिकार आहे जर तसंबंधी _________ ने ठराव मंजूर केला तर.', '{"A": "लोकसभेने तिच्या एकूण सदस्य संख्येच्या बहुमताने", "B": "लोकसभेने तिच्या एकूण सदस्य संख्येच्या दोन-तृतीयांश पेक्षा कमी नाही इतक्या बहुमताने", "C": "राज्यसभेने तिच्या एकूण सदस्य संख्येच्या बहुमताने", "D": "राज्यसभेने हजर राहून मतदान करणाऱ्या दोन-तृतीयांश सदस्य संख्येपेक्षा कमी नाही इतक्या बहुमताने"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'पर्याय D निवडा. Article 249 नुसार State List विषयावर Parliament ला कायदा करण्याचा अधिकार Rajya Sabha च्या resolution ने मिळतो — उपस्थित व मतदान करणाऱ्यांच्या किमान दोन-third बहुमताने; Lok Sabha चे साधे बहुमत किंवा Rajya Sabha च्या एकूण सदस्यांपैकी दोन-third नाही.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21816, 'General', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'राज्यघटना निर्मितीची जबाबदारी व कार्ये पार पाडण्यासाठी घटनासमितीने विविध समित्या स्थापन केल्या होत्या. त्यात कार्यपद्धतीविषयक नियम समितीचे अध्यक्ष म्हणून खालीलपैकी कोणी काम केले ?', '{"A": "डॉ. बी.आर. आंबेडकर", "B": "अल्लादी कृष्णस्वामी अय्यर", "C": "डॉ. राजेंद्र प्रसाद", "D": "डॉ. के.एम. मुन्शी"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय C येतो. Dr Rajendra Prasad यांनी Constituent Assembly च्या Rules of Procedure Committee चे अध्यक्षपद सांभाळले. Ambedkar Drafting Committee अध्यक्ष; Alladi Krishnaswami Ayyar व K.M. Munshi drafting कामात होते, पण या विशिष्ट committee चे अध्यक्ष नव्हते.', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21817, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'योग्य जोड्या लावा : अ ब अ. बाळशास्त्री जांभेकर I. विधवागृहाची स्थापना ब. गोपाळ हरि देशमुख II. स्त्रिशिक्षणाचे पहिले पुरस्कर्ते क. महात्मा ज्योतिबा फुले III. पुनर्विवाहोत्तेजक मंडळी ड. महर्षि धोंडो केशव कर्वे IV. अनाथ बालकाश्रम पर्यायी उत्तरे :', '{"A": "अ-III, ब-IV, क-II, ड-I", "B": "अ-II, ब-III, क-IV, ड-I", "C": "अ-II, ब-III, क-I, ड-IV", "D": "अ-III, ब-II, क-IV, ड-I"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'थेट उत्तर — पर्याय B. Balshastri Jambhekar यांनी स्त्री शिक्षणास पाठिंबा (a–II); Lokhitwadi Gopal Hari Deshmukh विधवा पुनर्विवाह (b–III); Jyotiba Phule orphanage व सामाजिक संस्था (c–IV); Maharshi Karve Widow Home (d–I). हा संपूर्ण जोड जुळणी पर्याय B.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21818, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'इ.स. 1849 मध्ये मुंबई येथे स्थापन झालेल्या परमहंस सभेचा खालीलपैकी कोणत्या सुधारणावर भर होता ? अ. विधवा पुनर्विवाह ब. स्त्री शिक्षण क. जाती बंधने तोडणे ड. मूर्तिपूजा मान्य वरीलपैकी कोणते विधान/विधाने बरोबर आहे/आहेत ?', '{"A": "फक्त अ आणि ब", "B": "फक्त ब आणि क", "C": "फक्त क", "D": "फक्त अ, क आणि ड"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'या प्रश्नात पर्याय C. Paramhans Sabha (1849, Mumbai), Dadoba Pandurang यांच्या स्थापनेने, जातीय भिंती तोडण्यावर भर दिला आणि मूर्तीपूजा नाकारली. विधवा पुनर्विवाह, स्त्री शिक्षण, मूर्तीपूजा स्वीकार — हे त्यांचे कार्यक्रम नव्हते; फक्त (c) बरोबर.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21819, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'नारायण मेघाजी लोखंडे यांनी कोणत्या वृत्तपत्रातून कामगारांच्या प्रश्नांना वाचा फोडली ?', '{"A": "समाचार चंद्रिका", "B": "प्रभाकर", "C": "दीनबंधू", "D": "ज्ञानप्रकाश"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'योग्य उत्तर पर्याय C. Narayan Meghaji Lokhande — Maharashtra चे अग्रगण्य trade-union organiser — 1880 च्या दशकापासून Deenbandhu वृत्तपत्रात mill-workers च्या मागण्या मांडत. Samachar Chandrika, Prabhakar, Dnyanprakash इतर periodicals, त्यांचे labour platform नाहीत.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21820, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'दादाभाई नौरोजीच्या मते, ''_________ चे निःसारण होते, परंतु तेच जर भारात गुंतवले असते, तर मोठ्या प्रमाणात आर्थिक विकास पहावयास मिळाला असता.'' गाळलेल्या जागा खालीलपैकी योग्य पर्यायाने भरा.', '{"A": "हस्तोद्योग उत्पादन", "B": "भारतीय चलन", "C": "कापसाचे संपूर्ण उत्पादन", "D": "संभाव्य अधिशेष"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'परीक्षकाने पर्याय D चिन्हांकित केला. Dadabhai Naoroji च्या ''drain of wealth'' सिद्धांतानुसार Britain काढून नेलेले India''s potential surplus होते — देशात गुंतवले असते तर पुढील विकासाला चालना मिळाली असती. Handicrafts, currency किंवा cotton output एकटे त्यांचा मुख्य आर्थिक तर्क सांगत नाहीत.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21821, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'वसाहतवादाचे भारतीयांच्या जीवनावर झालेले परिणामा संबंधीत खालील विचार/विधान कोणी मांडले ? अ. हिंदुस्थानची लक्ष्मी दूर्यागार जाऊ लागली. ब. आर्थिक निःसारणामुळे जगातील सर्वात समृद्ध भारत देशात दरिद्री बनवले आहे. क. भारताचे आर्थिक शोषण हे खंडणीसारखे आहे. ड. हाती तलवार धरून आपल्या व्यापाराची व्यवस्था लावण्याची वेळ आली आहे. पर्यायी उत्तरे :', '{"A": "अ-रमेश चंद्र दत्त, ब-न्यायमूर्ती रानडे, क-सर जॉर्ज ऑक्झेंडन, ड-लोकहितवादी गोपाळ हरि देशमुख", "B": "अ-न्यायमूर्ती रानडे, ब-सर जॉर्ज ऑक्झेंडन, क-रमेश चंद्र दत्त, ड-लोकहितवादी गोपाळ हरि देशमुख", "C": "अ-लोकहितवादी गोपाळ हरि देशमुख, ब-रमेश चंद्र दत्त, क-न्यायमूर्ती रानडे, ड-सर जॉर्ज ऑक्झेंडन", "D": "अ-न्यायमूर्ती रानडे, ब-लोकहितवादी गोपाळ हरि देशमुख, क-सर जॉर्ज ऑक्झेंडन, ड-रमेश चंद्र दत्त"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पर्याय C निवडा. Lokhitwadi Gopal Hari Deshmukh — Indian economy overseas चालवली (a); R.C. Dutt — समृद्ध India गरीब झाली (b); Justice Ranade — exploitation ransom सारखे (c); Sir George Oxenden — स्वतःचा व्यवसाय सांभाळण्यास तलवार (d) — हा संपूर्ण जोड उत्तरतालिकेतील उत्तर.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21822, 'General', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'पंडिता रमाबाईंना ब्रिटिश सरकारने कोणता किताब दिला होता ?', '{"A": "कैसर-ए-हिंद", "B": "कैसर-ए-हिंदू", "C": "कैसर-ए-लेडी", "D": "इंडियन सुपर लेडी"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'थेट उत्तर — पर्याय A. British Government ने Pandita Ramabai यांना सामाजिक व मानवीय कार्यासाठी Kaisar-i-Hind medal दिला. इतर option spellings हे खरे imperial award शीर्षक नाहीत.', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21823, 'General', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'ब्रिटिश काळात शेतीच्या व्यापारीकरणामुळे पुढीलपैकी कोणत्या पिकाच्या उत्पादनात वाढ झाली ? अ. चहा, गहू ब. ऊस, कापूस क. ताग, नीळ ड. तंबाखू, अफू वरीलपैकी कोणते विधान/विधाने बरोबर आहेत ?', '{"A": "फक्त अ आणि ब", "B": "फक्त अ, क आणि ड", "C": "फक्त ब, क आणि ड", "D": "वरील सर्व बरोबर आहेत"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय C येतो. Commercial agriculture अंतर्गत British ने export-oriented पिके — sugarcane व cotton, jute व indigo, tobacco व opium ((b), (c), (d)) — वाढवली. (a) मधील tea expansion व wheat एकत्र commercialisation चा दावा कमकुवत.', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21824, 'General', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'भारतीय कामगार वर्गाचा उदय व कामगार चळवळ याविषयी जोड्या लावा : अ. नारायण मेघाजी लोखंडे I. ऑल इंडिया ट्रेड युनियन काँग्रेसचे पहिले अध्यक्ष ब. महात्मा गांधी II. मद्रास लेबर युनियन या कामगार संघटनेची स्थापना क. बी.पी. वाडिया III. अहमदाबाद टेक्सटाईल लेबर असोशिएशनची स्थापना ड. लाला लाजपतराय IV. दीनबंधू वृत्तपत्रातून कामगारांचे प्रश्न मांडले पर्यायी उत्तरे :', '{"A": "अ-IV, ब-III, क-II, ड-I", "B": "अ-III, ब-IV, क-I, ड-II", "C": "अ-II, ब-I, क-IV, ड-III", "D": "अ-IV, ब-I, क-II, ड-III"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'पर्याय A निवडा. Lokhande Deenbandhu मध्ये labour issues (a–IV); Gandhi Ahmedabad Textile Labour Association (b–III); B.P. Wadia Madras Labour Union (c–II); Lala Lajpat Rai All India Trade Union Congress चे पहिले अध्यक्ष (d–I).', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21825, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'आदीवासी शेतकऱ्यांच्या क्रांतीचा पहिला नायक कोण होता ? अ. बाबा भांड ब. बिजनिया क. कजर सिंग ड. तंट्या भिल्ल वरीलपैकी कोणते विधान/विधाने बरोबर आहे/आहेत ?', '{"A": "फक्त अ आणि ब", "B": "फक्त क आणि ड", "C": "फक्त ब", "D": "फक्त ड"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'योग्य उत्तर पर्याय D. Tantya Bhilla (Tantia Bhil) ने जुलमी land revenue विरुद्ध armed peasant/tribal revolt केली — Maharashtra इतिहासात native farmers'' rebellion चा पहिला प्रमुख नेता. Baba Bhand, Bijania, Kajara Singh standard texts मध्ये ''first leader'' म्हणून नाहीत.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21826, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'नागरी उठावांची सुरुवात खालीलपैकी कोणत्या प्रदेशांतून झाली ?', '{"A": "पंजाब आणि सिंध", "B": "महाराष्ट्र आणि कर्नाटक", "C": "आंध्र प्रदेश आणि ओरिसा", "D": "बंगाल आणि बिहार"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'येथे खात्रीशीर उत्तर पर्याय D. 1857 च्या Civil Rebellion phase ची सुरुवात Bengal व Bihar मधून झाली — Meerut sepoy mutiny Gangetic heartland मधील civilian uprisings शी जोडली, नंतर इतरत्र पसरली.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21827, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'खालील जोड्या लावा : अ ब अ. पंडिता रमाबाई I. ''स्त्री-पुरुष तुलना'' ग्रंथ ब. रमाबाई रानडे II. निराश्रीत सेवासदनाची स्थापना क. ताराबाई शिंदे III. शारदा सदन ची स्थापना ड. जनाक्का शिंदे IV. ''हिंदू लेडीज सोशल क्लब'' ची स्थापना पर्यायी उत्तरे :', '{"A": "अ-II, ब-III, क-IV, ड-I", "B": "अ-I, ब-IV, क-III, ड-II", "C": "अ-III, ब-IV, क-I, ड-II", "D": "अ-IV, ब-II, क-III, ड-I"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'येथे खात्रीशीर उत्तर पर्याय C. Pandita Ramabai यांनी Sharada Sadan (a–III); Ramabai Ranade Hindu Ladies Social Club (b–IV); Tarabai Shinde Stree-Purush Tulana (c–I); Janakka Shinde Nirashrit Seva Sadan (d–II) — या जोड्या बरोबर.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21828, 'General', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, '1857 च्या उठावाविषयी खालीलपैकी कोणती विधाने बरोबर आहेत ? अ. भोरचे पंतसचिव चिमणाजी रघुनाथ (प्रथम) यांनी रंगो बापूजी गुप्ते यांना विश्वासघाताने इंग्रजांच्या हवाली केले. ब. नागपूरच्या भोसले घराण्यातील राणी बाकाबाई यांनी बंडवाल्यांना पाठिंबा दिला. क. कोल्हापूरच्या छत्रपतीच्या घराण्यातील चिमासाहेब उठावात सामील झाले. ड. रंगो बापूजी गुप्तेचे चिरंजीव सीतारामपंत व सावंतवाडीचे रामजी शिरसाळ यांनीही उठाव केला. पर्यायी उत्तरे :', '{"A": "फक्त अ आणि क", "B": "फक्त ब, क आणि ड", "C": "फक्त अ, क आणि ड", "D": "फक्त क आणि ड"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'या प्रश्नात पर्याय C. Maharashtra च्या 1857 कथेत Bhor च्या Pant Sachiv Chimnaji Raghunath ने Rango Bapuji Gupte ला British कडे सुपूर्त केले (a); Kolhapur चे Chhatrapati Chimasaheb revolt मध्ये (c); Sitarampant (Rango चा putra) व Sawantwadi चे Ramji Shirsal सहभागी (d). Nagpur ची Rani Bakabai rebels ला support नव्हते — (b) बाहेर.', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21829, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'भारतातील सर्वात लांब राष्ट्रीय महामार्ग _________ आहे.', '{"A": "NH 44", "B": "NH 01", "C": "NH 48", "D": "NH 06"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय A येतो. NH 44 — जुने क्रमांक NH 7 — श्रीनगर ते कन्याकुमारी असून सुमारे 4,000 km ने भारतातील सर्वात लांब राष्ट्रीय महामार्ग आहे. NH 1, NH 48 आणि NH 6 महत्त्वाचे पण या उत्तर–दक्षिण trunk route पेक्षा लहान.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21830, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'औरंगाबाद औद्योगिक शहराची ठळक वैशिष्ट्ये : अ. सुनियोजित आणि हरितपट्टेयुक्त स्मार्ट शहर. ब. AURIC हे संक्षिप्त रूप आहे. क. प्रकल्पातील एकुण गुंतवणूक 1,000 कोटी रुपये. ड. दिल्ली-मुंबई औद्योगिक पट्ट्याचा (कॉरिडॉरचा) भाग आहे. अचूक पर्याय निवडा :', '{"A": "फक्त अ", "B": "फक्त अ आणि ब", "C": "फक्त अ, ब आणि क", "D": "फक्त अ, ब आणि ड"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'येथे खात्रीशीर उत्तर पर्याय D. AURIC हा DMIC-linked greenfield smart city आहे आणि नाव Aurangabad Industrial City — (a), (b) व (d) बरोबर. (c) मध्ये एकूण गुंतवणूक नेमकी ₹1,000 crore असल्याचे सांगणे official briefs मधील phased outlay पेक्षा कमी दर्शवते.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21831, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'सन 1981 ते 2011 या कालावधीतील भारतीय लोकसंख्या वाढ आणि काल सापेक्ष बदल कोणती लोकसंख्या संक्रमण अवस्था दर्शविते ?', '{"A": "उच्च लोकसंख्या वाढीचा कालावधी, तरीही घटता कल", "B": "जलद लोकसंख्या वाढीचा कालावधी", "C": "लोकसंख्या वाढीतील सातत्य", "D": "स्थिर लोकसंख्या कालावधी"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'परीक्षकाने पर्याय A चिन्हांकित केला. 1981–2011 दरम्यान भारताची लोकसंख्या वाढत राहिली पण वाढ दर मंद होत होता — fertility घटली आणि वक्र high growth with declining trend दर्शवते, rapid acceleration किंवा stagnation नाही.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21832, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'औद्योगिक विभाग आणि औद्योगिक क्षेत्र यांच्या जोड्या लावा : अ. नाशिक I. बुटीबोरी ब. कोल्हापूर II. शेंद्रा क. नागपूर III. विंचूर ड. औरंगाबाद IV. हुपरी पर्यायी उत्तरे :', '{"A": "अ-IV, ब-III, क-II, ड-I", "B": "अ-III, ब-I, क-II, ड-IV", "C": "अ-III, ब-I, क-IV, ड-II", "D": "अ-III, ब-IV, क-I, ड-II"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'थेट उत्तर — पर्याय D. नाशिक–Vinchur (III), कोल्हापूर–Hupari (IV), नागपूर–Butibori (I), औरंगाबाद–Shendra (II) — प्रत्येक जिल्हा त्याच्या MIDC/industrial node शी. छापलेला ''Irrigation Scheme'' header दुर्लक्ष करा; यादीतील industrial-area नावांनुसार जुळवा.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21833, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'खालीलपैकी कोणता प्रदेश भारतातील उच्च भूकंप तीव्रता विभाग दर्शवितो ?', '{"A": "द्विपकल्पीय विभाग", "B": "काश्मिर ते आसामपर्यंतचा हिमालयीन विभाग", "C": "मध्य विभाग", "D": "गंगेचे मैदान"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'पर्याय B निवडा. Kashmir ते Assam Himalayan belt India च्या highest seismic-intensity zone मध्ये — young collision tectonics व repeated great earthquakes. Peninsula, central block आणि Ganga plain standard zoning maps वर comparatively lower-intensity.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21834, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'भारतीय मूलभूत रस्ते सांख्यिकी, 2017 नुसार भारतातील कोणते राज्य राष्ट्रीय महामार्गाच्या लांबीमध्ये दुसऱ्या क्रमांकाचे राज्य आहे ?', '{"A": "महाराष्ट्र", "B": "राजस्थान", "C": "मध्य प्रदेश", "D": "उत्तर प्रदेश"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'या प्रश्नात पर्याय D. Basic Road Statistics of India (2017) नुसार Uttar Pradesh National Highway लांबीत राज्यांमध्ये दुसऱ्या क्रमांकावर — Maharashtra अनेक वेळा अग्रस्थानी, पण त्या अहवाल वर्षात UP दुसरा.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21835, 'General', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'मृदा निर्मितीवर आधारित, महाराष्ट्राच्या मृदा वर्गीकरणाचा सखोल आणि शास्त्रीय अभ्यास सर्वप्रथम सन 1938 मध्ये कोणी केला ?', '{"A": "डॉ. डी. स्मिथ", "B": "डॉ. केलॉग आणि डॉ. थॉर्प", "C": "डॉ. डॉक्युचेव्ह", "D": "डॉ. बसू आणि डॉ. शिरूर"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय D येतो. Dr Basu आणि Dr Shirur यांनी 1938 मध्ये Maharashtra चे first detailed scientific soil classification केले. Smith, Kellogg–Thorp आणि Dokuchaev global/foreign classification traditions — हे state-specific survey नाही.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21836, 'General', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'भारतातील नैसर्गिक वायु आणि खनिज तेल उत्पादक राज्य म्हणजे _______.', '{"A": "केरळ", "B": "हिमाचल प्रदेश", "C": "गोवा", "D": "आसाम"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'योग्य उत्तर पर्याय D. Assam — Digboi व Brahmaputra valley — सूचीतील राज्यांमध्ये mineral oil आणि natural gas दोन्ही produce करते. Kerala, Himachal Pradesh आणि Goa Indian energy geography मध्ये comparable hydrocarbon production profile नाहीत.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21837, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, '1995 मध्ये बँक ग्राहकांच्या विवादांचे स्वस्त आणि जलद निपटारा करण्यासाठी _________ सुरु करण्यात आली.', '{"A": "विवेकपूर्ण नियम", "B": "ग्राहक सेवा समिती", "C": "बँकिंग लोकपाल योजना", "D": "आंतरराष्ट्रीय लेखा पद्धती"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पर्याय C निवडा. Banking Ombudsman Scheme (1995) bank customers साठी inexpensive, speedy dispute redress forum — RBI चा dedicated grievance layer. Prudential norms, customer-service committees, accounting standards वेगळ्या regulatory functions.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21838, 'General', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'महाराष्ट्रातील जलसिंचन योजना व त्यांचे जिल्हे यांच्या योग्य जोड्या लावा : जिल्हा जलसिंचन योजना अ. सातारा I. मुकणे ब. नाशिक II. विष्णुपुरी क. नांदेड III. कण्हेर ड. यवतमाळ IV. बेंबला पर्यायी उत्तरे :', '{"A": "अ-II, ब-III, क-IV, ड-I", "B": "अ-III, ब-I, क-II, ड-IV", "C": "अ-III, ब-IV, क-I, ड-II", "D": "अ-IV, ब-II, क-III, ड-I"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'पर्याय B निवडा. Kanher–Satara (III), Mukane–Nashik (I), Vishnupuri–Nanded (II), Bembala–Yavatmal (IV) — B मध्ये a–III, b–I, c–II, d–IV. Mukane Satara किंवा Kanher Nashik अशी swap standard Maharashtra irrigation map मोडते.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21839, 'General', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'महाराष्ट्रातील कोकण प्रादेशिक विभागातील ''मध्य कोकण'' मध्ये समाविष्ट होणाऱ्या खाड्या कोणत्या ?', '{"A": "देवगड, आचरा आणि कर्ली खाडी", "B": "राजापुरी, बाणकोट आणि केळशी खाडी", "C": "धरमतर, कालावल आणि तेरेखोल खाडी", "D": "डहाणू, वसई आणि दातिवरे खाडी"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'थेट उत्तर — पर्याय B. Maharashtra regional division मधील Central Konkan मध्ये Rajapuri, Bankot आणि Kelshi creeks — southern व northern Konkan blocks दरम्यान mid-coast estuaries. Deogarh–Karli, Dharamtar–Terekhol, Dahanu–Vasai sets इतर subdivisions.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21840, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'लक्षद्वीप आणि मिनिकॉय बेटे विभक्त झाली आहेत', '{"A": "आठ अंश चॅनल मुळे", "B": "नऊ अंश चॅनल मुळे", "C": "दहा अंश चॅनल मुळे", "D": "शून्य अंश चॅनल मुळे"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'येथे खात्रीशीर उत्तर पर्याय B. Nine Degree Channel Lakshadweep मधील Laccadive island group व Minicoy वेगळे करते. Eight Degree Channel उत्तरेकडे; Ten Degree Andaman–Nicobar वेगळे करते.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21841, 'General', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'जी.टी. त्रिवार्था यांच्या हवामान वर्गीकरणानुसार, पश्चिम किनारापट्टीवरील मैदानी भाग आणि त्रिपुरा राज्यात खालीलपैकी कोणत्या प्रकारचे हवामान आहे ?', '{"A": "पर्वतीय आर्द्र हवामान", "B": "उष्ण कटिबंधीय शुष्क हवामान", "C": "उष्ण कटिबंधीय पावसाळी (मान्सून) हवामान", "D": "उपोष्ण कटिबंधीय आर्द् हवामान"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'परीक्षकाने पर्याय C चिन्हांकित केला. G T Trewartha scheme नुसार western coastal plain व Tripura tropical monsoon (Am) climate — humid tropics मध्ये heavy seasonal rain. Humid mountain, tropical arid, humid sub-tropical Himalayan/desert/interior settings; या pairing साठी नाहीत.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21842, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'महाराष्ट्रात नैऋत्य मोसमी वाऱ्यापासून मिळणाऱ्या पावसाची टक्केवारी खालीलपैकी किती आहे ?', '{"A": "58%", "B": "65%", "C": "85%", "D": "95%"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'या प्रश्नात पर्याय C. उत्तरतालिकेनुसार Maharashtra च्या वार्षिक पर्जन्याच्या सुमारे 85% southwest monsoon current — standard geography texts मध्ये precipitation budget चा bulk. stem मध्ये ''North-Western monsoon''; पाठ्यपुस्तकाची शब्दरचना वेगळी असेल तर 85% उत्तरतालिका figure ला defer करा.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21843, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'खालील विधाने विचारात घ्या. अ. स्वातंत्र्यानंतर, भारत सरकारने ऑगस्ट 1948 मध्ये राष्ट्रीय उत्पन्न समितीची नियुक्ती केली. ब. या समितीमध्ये प्रा. पी.सी. महालनोबिस, प्रा. डी.आर. गाडगीळ आणि प्रा. व्ही.के.आर.व्ही. राव यांचा समावेश होता. क. राष्ट्रीय उत्पन्न समितीचा पहिला अहवाल 1951 मध्ये आणि अंतिम अहवाल 1954 मध्ये आला. वर दिलेल्या विधानांपैकी कोणते विधान/कोणती विधाने चुकीची आहे/आहेत ? पर्यायी उत्तरे :', '{"A": "फक्त अ", "B": "फक्त अ आणि ब", "C": "फक्त अ आणि क", "D": "फक्त ब आणि क"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'पर्याय A निवडा. National Income Committee मध्ये Mahalanobis, Gadgil, V K R V Rao होते आणि reports 1951 व 1954 — (b), (c) बरोबर. (a) एकटे उत्तरतालिकेतील चुकीचा — August 1948 appointment date vs standard accounts मधील 1949 chronology.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21844, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'भारतीय शेतीतील उत्पादकता प्रामुख्याने दोन बाबींवर अवलंबून आहे. त्या म्हणजे : अ. तांत्रिक घटक ब. मनुष्यबळ क. संस्थात्मक घटक ड. सिंचन सुविधा पर्यायी उत्तरे :', '{"A": "फक्त अ आणि क", "B": "फक्त अ आणि ड", "C": "फक्त अ आणि ब", "D": "फक्त क आणि ड"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'परीक्षकाने पर्याय A चिन्हांकित केला. India मध्ये agricultural productivity mainly technological inputs — seeds, mechanisation, plant protection — आणि institutional factors — land tenure, credit, extension, marketing. Human-resource/irrigation-only अपूर्ण घटक — उत्तरतालिकेतील दुहेरी संच नाही.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21845, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'ग्रामीण भागातील शेती आणि संबंधित उपक्रमांना प्रोत्साहन देण्यासाठी कर्जपुरवठा करणारी _________ ही शिखर संस्था आहे.', '{"A": "रिझर्व्ह बँक", "B": "स्टेट बँक ऑफ इंडिया", "C": "नाबार्ड", "D": "वरील सर्व"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'योग्य उत्तर पर्याय C. NABARD agriculture व allied rural credit promote करणारे apex body — cooperatives व RRB channels. RBI regulates; SBI commercial bank — NABARD चा distinct apex refinance mandate त्यांच्याकडे नाही.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21846, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'भारतातील विशेष आर्थिक क्षेत्रांचे खालीलपैकी कोणते महत्वाचे उद्दिष्ट नाही ?', '{"A": "जादा आर्थिक क्रिया कलापांची निर्मिती", "B": "निर्यातीला प्रोत्साहन", "C": "शेतीचा विकास", "D": "रोजगार निर्मिती"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पर्याय C निवडा. SEZ policy extra economic activity, exports, employment — industrial/tax incentives; primary-sector agriculture development नाही. Agriculture export-processing/manufacturing logic SEZ notifications outside.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21847, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, '2011 च्या जनगणनेनुसार देशातील लोकसंख्येची घनता _________ आहे.', '{"A": "117 प्रति चौ. कि.मी.", "B": "157 प्रति चौ. कि.मी.", "C": "282 प्रति चौ. कि.मी.", "D": "382 प्रति चौ. कि.मी."}'::jsonb, 'D', 'थेट उत्तर — पर्याय D. Census 2011 नुसार India population density 382 persons/km² — 2001 मध्ये 325. 117, 157, 282 earlier decades किंवा misquoted averages — all-India 2011 headline नाहीत.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21848, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'केंद्रीय अर्थसंकल्प 2021 – 22 मध्ये केंद्र सरकारच्या उत्पन्नाचा सर्वात मोठा खोत कोणता आहे ?', '{"A": "वस्तू आणि सेवा कर", "B": "कर्ज घेणे आणि इतर दायित्वे", "C": "प्राप्तीकर", "D": "कॉर्पोरेट कर"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय B येतो. Union Budget 2021–22 मध्ये borrowing and other liabilities सर्वात मोठा single receipt head — GST, income tax, corporate tax individually पेक्षा जास्त — pandemic-year market borrowings deficit financing.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21849, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'खालीलपैकी वित्तीय जबाबदारी आणि अंदाजपत्रक व्यवस्थापन कायदा, 2003 ची कोणती उद्दिष्टे/उद्दिष्ये आहे/आहेत ? अ. कालबद्ध कार्यक्रमांतर्गत सरकारी कर्जावर मर्यादा निश्चित करणे. ब. महसूल तूट शून्य गाठणे आणि वित्तीय तूट कमी करणे. क. दीर्घकालीन समष्टी आर्थिक स्थिरता सुनिश्चित करण्यासाठी शासनाला जबाबदार बनविणे. ड. शासनाच्या आर्थिक कामकाजात पारदर्शकता सुधारणे. पर्यायी उत्तरे :', '{"A": "वरीलपैकी एकही नाही", "B": "वरीलपैकी सर्व", "C": "फक्त अ आणि ब", "D": "फक्त क आणि ड"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'या प्रश्नात पर्याय B. FRBM Act 2003 borrowing limits time-bound path, zero revenue deficit व lower fiscal deficit, long-term macro stability, fiscal transparency improve — चारही objectives statute मध्ये; ''all of the above'' match.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (21850, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2021, 'बालमृत्यूदर हा दिलेल्या भौगोलिक क्षेत्रातील एक वर्षाच्या कालावधीत 1000 जिवंत जन्मामागे _________ बया खालील मुलांच्या मृत्यूची सख्या आहे.', '{"A": "एक वर्ष", "B": "एक महिना", "C": "एक आठवडा", "D": "एक दिवस"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय A येतो. Infant mortality rate म्हणजे दिलेल्या भागात वर्षभरात जन्मलेल्या प्रत्येक 1000 जिवंत बाळांमध्ये एक वर्षाखालील मृत्यू — एक महिना, आठवडा किंवा एक दिवस नाही.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group B Combined","2021","General"}'::text[], 'Medium')
