  (22251, 'Constitutional Framework & Preamble', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2025, 'खालीलपैकी कोणत्या सूचीमध्ये प्रतिबंधात्मक स्थानबद्धतेची तरतुद करण्यात आली आहे?', '{"A": "फक्त समवर्ती सूची", "B": "फक्त राज्य सूची", "C": "केंद्र सूची आणि समवर्ती सूची", "D": "राज्य सूची आणि समवर्ती सूची"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'परीक्षेनुसार पर्याय C बरोबर आहे. प्रतिबंधात्मक अटक क suchi (Central NSA) and samavarti suchi (state/shared) — fakt Rajya ki । dve उत्तर निश्चित करताना प्रश्नातील मुख्य संकल्पना आणि वर्ष लक्षात ठेवा.।', '{"Polity","MPSC Group C Combined","2025","Constitutional Framework & Preamble"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22252, 'Panchayati Raj', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2025, 'बलवंतराय मेहता समितीच्या योग्य शिफारसी ओळखा. अ. ग्राम पंचायत प्रत्यक्ष निवडून आलेल्या प्रतिनिर्धीसह स्थापन करावी. ब. पंचायत समिती आणि जिल्हा परिषद प्रत्यक्ष निवडून आलेल्या प्रतिनिर्धीसह स्थापन करावी. क. जिल्हाधिकारी जिल्हा परिषदेचे अध्यक्ष असावेत.', '{"A": "फक्त अ, ब", "B": "फक्त ब, क", "C": "फक्त अ, क", "D": "वरीलपैकी सर्व"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पर्याय C (फक्त अ, क) — म्हणून अ आणि क योग्य आहेत, ब नाही पर्याय A (फक्त अ, ब) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय B (फक्त ब, क) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय D (वरीलपैकी सर्व) प्रत्येक विधान बरोबर म्हणतो, पण यापैकी किमान एक विधान चुकीचे आहे।', '{"Polity","MPSC Group C Combined","2025","Panchayati Raj"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22253, 'Constitutional Framework & Preamble', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2025, 'खालीलपैकी कोणते विधान सत्य नाही? (1) भारतीय राज्यघटनेच्या अंमलबजावणीची तारीख 26, नोव्हेंबर 1949 आहे. (2) 42 व्या घटनादुरूस्तीने ''धर्मनिरपेक्ष'' शब्द जोडला गेला. (3) 42 वी घटनादुरूस्ती 1976 मध्ये करण्यात आली. (4) सामाजिक, आर्थिक आणि राजकीय न्याय या संकल्पना भारतीय राज्यघटनेत सोव्हियेट रशियाची घटनेतून घेण्यात आल्या आहेत.', '{"A": "(1) भारतीय राज्यघटनेच्या अंमलबजावणीची तारीख 26, नोव्हेंबर 1949 आहे.", "B": "(2) 42 व्या घटनादुरूस्तीने ''धर्मनिरपेक्ष'' शब्द जोडला गेला.", "C": "(3) 42 वी घटनादुरूस्ती 1976 मध्ये करण्यात आली.", "D": "(4) सामाजिक, आर्थिक आणि राजकीय न्याय या संकल्पना भारतीय राज्यघटनेत सोव्हियेट रशियाची घटनेतून घेण्यात आल्या आहेत."}'::jsonb, 'A', 'पर्याय A ((1) भारतीय राज्यघटनेच्या अंमलबजावणीची त…) — The संविधान was adopted on 26 November 1949 but came into force on 26 January 1950—विधान (1) conflates adoption with commencement, making it चुकी। Secular/Socialist insertion via the 42nd दुरुस्ती (1976) and USSR-influenced justice ideals in the Preamble are otherwise accepted syllabus points पर्याय B ((2) 42 व्या घटनादुरूस्तीने ''धर्मनिरपेक्…) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी; पर्याय C ((3) 42 वी घटनादुरूस्ती 1976 मध्ये करण्य…) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी; पर्याय D ((4) सामाजिक, आर्थिक आणि राजकीय न्याय या…) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी।', '{"Polity","MPSC Group C Combined","2025","Constitutional Framework & Preamble"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22254, 'Electricity & Magnetism', 'Science', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2025, 'एका घरामध्ये एक 100 W क्षमतेचा पंखा दररोज 10 तास चालवला जातो, दोन 50 W क्षमतेचे बल्ब दररोज पाच तास चालवले जातात. जर विजेचा दर प्रति युनिट (kWh) 5 रूपये असेल तर 30 दिवसासाठी महिन्याचे वीजबील किती रूपये येईल?', '{"A": "150 रूपये", "B": "225 रूपये", "C": "300 रूपये", "D": "375 रूपये"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'योग्य उत्तर पर्याय B आहे। urja lekhapariksha: fan १०० W × १० h = १ kWh/day; bulbs ५० W × ५ h × २ = ०.५ kWh/day; total १.५ × ३० = ४५ kWh; ₹५/unit → ₹२२५. ganitiy chuka 150/300/375।', '{"Science","MPSC Group C Combined","2025","Electricity & Magnetism"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22255, 'Metals & Materials', 'Science', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2025, 'मॅलाकाईट हे ___ धातूचे मूळ (ore) आहे.', '{"A": "तांबे", "B": "लोह", "C": "ॲल्युमिनियम", "D": "गंधक"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'पर्याय A (तांबे) — bauxite signals aluminium पर्याय B (लोह) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (ॲल्युमिनियम) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (गंधक) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Science","MPSC Group C Combined","2025","Metals & Materials"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22256, 'Zoology (Animal Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2025, 'खालीलपैकी कोणत्या झुआईड निडारियामध्ये संरक्षक आच्छादन असते?', '{"A": "डॅक्टिलोझॉइड", "B": "टेंटाक्युलोझॉइड", "C": "ट्रोफोझॉइड", "D": "फायलोझॉइड"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'योग्य उत्तर पर्याय D आहे. जीवशास्त्रात हे lक्षात ठेवा — -। Dactylo/gastro/gonozooids इतर roles — D — इतर पर्याय शी जवळचे सापळे आहेत; MPSC prelim मध्ये अशा प्रकारचे प्रश्न पुन्हा येतात, प्रश्न एकदा पुन्हा वाचून निश्चित करा।', '{"Science","MPSC Group C Combined","2025","Zoology (Animal Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22257, 'Zoology (Animal Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2025, 'कांगारू हा पिशवी असलेला सस्तन प्राणी आहे, – अ. ऑस्ट्रेलीया आणि टास्मानिया च्या गवताळ मैदानात आढळतो. ब. ते स्थलीय आणि शाकाहारी प्राणी आहेत. क. पुढील पाय खूप लांब व शक्तीशाली असतात तर मागील पाय लहान व कमकुवत असतात. ड. मादीला भ्रूणपिशवी असते तीला मार्सुपिअम म्हणतात. वरीलपैकी कोणते विधान/विधाने बरोबर आहे/आहेत?', '{"A": "फक्त अ", "B": "फक्त अ आणि ब", "C": "अ, ब आणि क", "D": "अ, ब आणि ड"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'या प्रश्नात कांगारू हा पिशवी असलेला सस्तन प्राणी आहे, – अ. ऑस्ट्रेलीया आणि टास्मा… — पर्याय D (अ, ब आणि ड) बरोबर आहे पर्याय A (फक्त अ) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय B (फक्त अ आणि ब) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय C (अ, ब आणि क) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Science","MPSC Group C Combined","2025","Zoology (Animal Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22258, 'Metals & Materials', 'Science', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2025, 'पितळ हा ___ मिश्रधातू आहे.', '{"A": "तांबे आणि कथील", "B": "लोह आणि कार्बन", "C": "लोह आणि क्रोमियम", "D": "तांबे आणि जस्त"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'पर्याय D (तांबे आणि जस्त) — iron–carbon is steel पर्याय A (तांबे आणि कथील) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B (लोह आणि कार्बन) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (लोह आणि क्रोमियम) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Science","MPSC Group C Combined","2025","Metals & Materials"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22259, 'Electricity & Magnetism', 'Science', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2025, 'खालीलपैकी कोणते किरण चुंबकाच्या सान्निध्यात दिशा बदलत नाहीत?', '{"A": "अल्फा किरण", "B": "बीटा किरण", "C": "गॅमा किरण", "D": "कॅथोडिक किरण"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'या प्रश्नात खालीलपैकी कोणते किरण चुंबकाच्या सान्निध्यात दिशा बदलत नाहीत? — पर्याय C (गॅमा किरण) बरोबर आहे पर्याय A (अल्फा किरण) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B (बीटा किरण) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (कॅथोडिक किरण) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Science","MPSC Group C Combined","2025","Electricity & Magnetism"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22260, 'Chemical Bonding & Reactions', 'Science', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2025, 'कॅल्शियम आणि क्लोरीन ___ बंधाने एकत्र येऊन कॅल्शियम क्लोराईड तयार होते.', '{"A": "सहसंयुज बंध", "B": "आयनिक बंध", "C": "धातू बंध", "D": "हायड्रोजन बंध"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'विश्लेषण केल्यास पर्याय B योग्य ठरतो. रसायनशास्त्रात हे lक्षात ठेवा — Ca metal + Cl non-metal → Ca²⁺ Cl⁻ ionic bond CaCl₂। Covalent/metallic/H-bond इतर regimes — B आयनिक — इतर पर्याय शी जवळचे सापळे आहेत; MPSC prelim मध्ये अशा प्रकारचे प्रश्न पुन्हा येतात, प्रश्न एकदा पुन्हा वाचून निश्चित करा।', '{"Science","MPSC Group C Combined","2025","Chemical Bonding & Reactions"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22261, 'Diseases & Health', 'Science', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2025, 'घातक सबटर्शियन मलेरिया ___ होतो.', '{"A": "प्लाझमोडियम व्हायवॅक्स", "B": "प्लाझमोडियम फाल्सीपरम", "C": "प्लाझमोडियम ओव्हेल", "D": "प्लाझमोडियम मलेरिई"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'या प्रश्नाचे बरोबर उत्तर पर्याय B आहे। (cerebral/severe) । P. vivax/ovale//quartan परीक्षेत जवळचे पर्याय सापडतात, म्हणून प्रश्नाचा मजकूर आणि मुख्य तथ्य पुन्हा वाचा.।', '{"Science","MPSC Group C Combined","2025","Diseases & Health"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22262, 'Botany (Plant Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2025, 'भुईमुगावर टिक्का रोग कोणत्या कारक जीवामुळे होतो?', '{"A": "पक्सीनिया प्रजाती", "B": "सरकोस्पोरा परसोनेटा", "C": "एस्परजिलस प्रजाती", "D": "युस्टीलागो प्रजाती"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'पर्याय B हे योग्य निवड आहे। Groundnut tikka (leaf spot) । Puccinia rust; Aspergillus mould; Ustilago smut — विषय-पॅकमध्ये हा बिंदू पुन्हा विचारला जाऊ शकतो, म्हणून मुख्य तथ्य एकत्र लक्षात ठेवा.।', '{"Science","MPSC Group C Combined","2025","Botany (Plant Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22263, 'Botany (Plant Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2025, 'शेंगवर्गीय पिके हवेतील नत्राचा उपयोग खालीलपैकी कोणत्या सूक्ष्म-जीवाणूंच्या मदतीने करू शकतात? अ. रायझोबियम ब. विषाणू क. बुरशी ड. प्रोटोझोआ', '{"A": "फक्त अ", "B": "फक्त अ आणि ब", "C": "फक्त क", "D": "फक्त क आणि ड"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'परीक्षेनुसार पर्याय A बरोबर आहे। fix atmospheric N₂ ammonia — । Viruses, fungi, protozoa not mul-kanda bhumika उत्तर निश्चित करताना प्रश्नातील मुख्य संकल्पना आणि वर्ष लक्षात ठेवा.।', '{"Science","MPSC Group C Combined","2025","Botany (Plant Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22264, 'Botany (Plant Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2025, 'मिराबिलीस जलापा (फोर ओ''क्लॉक) ही वनस्पती ___ कुळातील आहे.', '{"A": "अर्कॅन्थेसी", "B": "अमरॅन्थेसी", "C": "सोलानेसी", "D": "निक्टाजिनेसी"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'या विषयात पर्याय D अचूक उत्तर मानले जाते। Mirabilis jalapa (four-o''clock) Nyctaginaceae — not Acanthaceae, Amaranthaceae, MPSC प्रश्नपत्रिकेत अशा तपशीलांची पुनरावृत्ती होते, म्हणून मुख्य संकल्पना लक्षात ठेवा.।', '{"Science","MPSC Group C Combined","2025","Botany (Plant Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22265, 'Human Physiology', 'Science', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2025, 'खालीलपैकी रक्त गोठण्यास प्रतिबंध करणारे नैसर्गिक औषध कोणते?', '{"A": "हिपॅरीन", "B": "सोडियम सायट्रेट", "C": "सोडियम नायट्रेट", "D": "डिंक"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'विश्लेषण केल्यास पर्याय A योग्य ठरतो। /basophils — । Sodium citrate lab anticoagulant (chelates Ca²⁺); nitrate/gum irrelevant परीक्षेत जवळचे पर्याय सापडतात, म्हणून प्रश्नाचा मजकूर आणि मुख्य तथ्य पुन्हा वाचा.।', '{"Science","MPSC Group C Combined","2025","Human Physiology"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22266, 'Ratio, Proportion & Averages', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2025, 'मिश्रधातू A आणि B मध्ये तांबे आणि जस्त यांचे प्रमाण अनुक्रमे 4 : 3 आणि 9 : 5 आहे. हे दोन्ही मिश्रधातू समान प्रमाणात मिसळून C मिश्रधातू तयार केल्यास, त्या C मिश्रधातूमधील तांबे व जस्त यांचे प्रमाण किती होईल?', '{"A": "11 : 14", "B": "17 : 11", "C": "14 : 11", "D": "17 : 14"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'पर्याय B (17 : 11) — Mix alloys equal masses: copper 4/7 + 9/14 = 17/14; zinc 3/7 + 5/14 = 11/14 → 17:11. LCM hara jodnyapeksha changle 4+9 पर्याय A (11 : 14) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (14 : 11) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही; पर्याय D (17 : 14) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group C Combined","2025","Ratio, Proportion & Averages"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22267, 'Human Physiology', 'Science', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2025, 'मानवी रक्तामध्ये ''प्लाझ्मा'' किती टक्के असतो?', '{"A": "45", "B": "55", "C": "60", "D": "20"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'गणितात हे सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय B येतो या प्रश्नात ''55'' हे उत्तर योग्य आहे. मानवी रक्ताच्या volume मध्ये ~55% plasma (पाणी, proteins, salts) आणि ~45% formed elements (RBC, WBC, platelets)। पर्याय A (45) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर B (55) आहे; पर्याय C (60) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर B (55) आहे; पर्याय D (20) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर B (55) आहे।', '{"Science","MPSC Group C Combined","2025","Human Physiology"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22268, 'Algebra & Equations', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2025, 'एका संख्येची चार-पंचमांश ही त्या संख्येच्या 60% पेक्षा 10 ने जास्त असल्यास ती संख्या कोणती?', '{"A": "10", "B": "40", "C": "50", "D": "60"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पर्याय C (50) — संख्या x: (4/5)x − (3/5)x = 10 → (1/5)x = 10 → x = 50. पडताळ: 40 − 30 = 10. लहान संख्या अंतर चुकतात; 60 जास्त निकडते — options A/D सामान्य चुका; B gives फक्त 6-unit अंतर. पर्याय A (10) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर C (50) आहे; पर्याय B (40) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; पर्याय D (60) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे. पर्याय A (10) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; पर्याय B (40) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; पर्याय D (60) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group C Combined","2025","Algebra & Equations"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22269, 'Diseases & Health', 'Science', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2025, 'विषाणूजन्य रोग व कारणीभूत विषाणू यांच्या जोड्या लावा. रोग — विषाणू a. एडस् — I. डेंग्यू विषाणू b. कांजिण्या — II. हिपॅटाईटीस बी विषाणू c. लिव्हर डॅमेज व सिरोसिस — III. व्हेरिसेला झोस्टर विषाणू d. रक्तस्रावी ताप — IV. मानवी इम्यूनोडेफीसीयन्सी विषाणू', '{"A": "a-III, b-II, c-IV, d-I", "B": "a-II, b-IV, c-III, d-I", "C": "a-IV, b-III, c-II, d-I", "D": "a-III, b-IV, c-I, d-II"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Chukichi jod HIV/varicella or HBV/dengue चुकs disease biology पर्याय A (a-III, b-II, c-IV, d-I) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी; पर्याय B (a-II, b-IV, c-III, d-I) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी; पर्याय D (a-III, b-IV, c-I, d-II) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी।', '{"Science","MPSC Group C Combined","2025","Diseases & Health"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22270, 'Simple & Compound Interest', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2025, 'सरळ व्याजाने 5,000 रुपयांची रक्कम तीन वर्षात 5,600 रुपये होते. जर व्याजदरात 3% वाढ केली, तर याच मूळ रकमेचे तीन वर्षांतर किती रुपये होतील?', '{"A": "5950 रुपये", "B": "5800 रुपये", "C": "6000 रुपये", "D": "6050 रुपये"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'पर्याय D (6050 रुपये) — amount = 6050. Forgetting to add principal or using चक्रवाढ व्याज gives 5800/6000 सापळा पर्याय A (5950 रुपये) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B (5800 रुपये) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही; पर्याय C (6000 रुपये) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group C Combined","2025","Simple & Compound Interest"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22271, 'Time & Work', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2025, '10 स्त्रिया एक काम 7 दिवसात पूर्ण करतात. 10 मुले तेच काम 14 दिवसात पूर्ण करतात. तर 5 स्त्रिया आणि 10 मुले तेच काम किती दिवसात पूर्ण करतील?', '{"A": "8 दिवस", "B": "7 दिवस", "C": "9 दिवस", "D": "10 दिवस"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'पर्याय B (7 दिवस) — Total work: 10 women × 7 days = 70; 10 children × 14 days = 140. Daily 5 women + 10 children = 5/70 + 10/140 = 1/7 job/day → 7 days। दिवसांची सरासरी घेऊ नका पर्याय A (8 दिवस) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (9 दिवस) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (10 दिवस) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group C Combined","2025","Time & Work"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22272, 'Algebra & Equations', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2025, 'दोन क्रमागत विषम संख्यांच्या वर्गातील फरक 112 आहे. तर त्यापैकी लहान संख्येचा वर्ग किती?', '{"A": "625", "B": "729", "C": "900", "D": "784"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'दोन क्रमागत विषम संख्या n व n+2; n² व (n+2)² यांचा फरक 112. (n+2)²−n²=4n+4=112, n=27, n²=729. म्हणून पर्याय B (729). A (625), C (900), D (784) या गणनेतून येत नाहीत।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group C Combined","2025","Algebra & Equations"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22273, 'Number System & Simplification', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2025, 'खालील किंमत काढा, – (0.11)² – (0.01)² / 1.2', '{"A": "0.01", "B": "0.09", "C": "0.10", "D": "0.12"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'या प्रश्नाचे बरोबर उत्तर पर्याय A आहे। a²−b² = (a+b)(a−b): (0.11+0.01)(0.11−0.01) = 0.12×0.10 = 0.012; ÷1.2 → 0.01. 0.09/0.10 परीक्षेत जवळचे पर्याय सापडतात, म्हणून प्रश्नाचा मजकूर आणि मुख्य तथ्य पुन्हा वाचा.।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group C Combined","2025","Number System & Simplification"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22274, 'Mensuration & Geometry', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2025, 'जर चौरसाची बाजू 25% ने वाढवली तर त्या चौरसाचे क्षेत्रफळ किती टक्क्यांनी वाढेल?', '{"A": "25", "B": "50", "C": "56.25", "D": "37.50"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पर्याय C हे योग्य निवड आहे। Kshetrafal baju² ne vadhate: 1.25² = 1.5625 → 56.25% increase not linear 25%। ki rekheey jod → 25%/50% सापळा विषय-पॅकमध्ये हा बिंदू पुन्हा विचारला जाऊ शकतो, म्हणून मुख्य तथ्य एकत्र लक्षात ठेवा.।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group C Combined","2025","Mensuration & Geometry"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22275, 'Time, Speed & Distance', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2025, 'मुंबई आणि गोवा या स्थानकांतील अंतर 540 किमी आहे. दोन रेल्वे गाड्या सकाळी 7.30 वाजता एकाच वेळी या दोन्ही स्थानकांवरून परस्पर विरूद्ध दिशेने निघतात. त्यांचे वेग अनुक्रमे 60 किमी/तास आणि 75 किमी/तास आहेत. तर त्या दोन्ही गाड्या एकमेकांना किती वाजता भेटतील?', '{"A": "12.30 pm", "B": "12.00 noon", "C": "1.30 pm", "D": "11.30 am"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'पर्याय D (11.30 am) — apekshik veg 60+75 = 135 km/h; time 540/135 = 4 h from 7:30 am → 11:30 am. Ek gadi veg ki chukichi disha → noon/12:30 चुकीचे पर्याय A (12.30 pm), B (12.00 noon), C (1.30 pm) हे या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पना किंवा व्याख्येशी जुळत नाहीत पर्याय A (12.30 pm) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B (12.00 noon) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (1.30 pm) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही. पर्याय A (12.30 pm) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B (12.00 noon) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (1.30 pm) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group C Combined","2025","Time, Speed & Distance"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22276, 'Data Interpretation', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2025, 'खालील स्तंभालेखावरून, वर्ष 1976 ते 1980 पर्यंत उत्पादन किती टक्क्यांनी कमी झाले? (उत्पादन: 1976=3000, 1977=2500, 1978=2000, 1979=1000, 1980=500)', '{"A": "75%", "B": "83.33%", "C": "80%", "D": "60.66%"}'::jsonb, 'B', '33% हे उत्तर योग्य आहे पर्याय A (75%) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर B (83.33%) आहे; पर्याय C (80%) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर B (83.33%) आहे; पर्याय D (60.66%) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर B (83.33%) आहे. पर्याय A (75%) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर B (83.33%) आहे; पर्याय C (80%) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; पर्याय D (60.66%) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group C Combined","2025","Data Interpretation"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22277, 'Direction Sense', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2025, 'आदित घरापासून उत्तरेकडे चालत जातो. काही वेळानंतर, तो उजवीकडे वळतो आणि थोडे पुढे जाऊन डावीकडे वळतो. शेवटी, एक किलोमीटर चालल्यानंतर, तो पुन्हा डावीकडे वळतो. आता तो कोणत्या दिशेने चालत आहे?', '{"A": "उत्तर", "B": "दक्षिण", "C": "पूर्व", "D": "पश्चिम"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'या प्रश्नाचे बरोबर उत्तर पर्याय D आहे। sarasari vay 5 years ago = 16 तीन people → sum 48. Present 48+3×5 = 63 → avg 21. After 5 more years +15 → 78/3 = 26. दुसरा +5 विसरले → 21/22।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group C Combined","2025","Direction Sense"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22278, 'Percentage, Profit & Loss', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2025, 'एक दुकानदार एका कपाटाच्या छापील किमतीवर 25% सुट देतो. तरीही त्यास 15% नफा होतो. कपाटाची छापील किंमत ₹ 23,000 असेल तर कपाटाची खरेदी किंमत किती?', '{"A": "₹ 16,000", "B": "₹ 20,000", "C": "₹ 15,000", "D": "₹ 18,000"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'With 15% नफा on cost, CP = 17250/1.15 = 15000. सूट-on-सूट or नफा-on-MP mistakes give 16000/18000/20000 पर्याय A (₹ 16,000) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B (₹ 20,000) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही; पर्याय D (₹ 18,000) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group C Combined","2025","Percentage, Profit & Loss"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22279, 'Ratio, Proportion & Averages', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2025, 'राम, शाम व जॉन यांच्या 5 वर्षपूर्वीच्या वयाची सरासरी 16 वर्षे होती. तर 5 वर्षानंतर त्यांच्या वयाची सरासरी किती होईल?', '{"A": "21 वर्षे", "B": "22 वर्षे", "C": "26 वर्षे", "D": "30 वर्षे"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'या प्रश्नाचे बरोबर उत्तर पर्याय C (२६ वर्षे) आहे. ५ वर्षांपूर्वी सरासरी १६ → तिघांची बेरी ४८; आता ४८+१५=६३ → सरासरी २१; पुढील ५ वर्षे +१५ → ७८/३ = २६. २१/२२ हा ''आता''चा सरासरी आहे — प्रश्न ''५ वर्षांनंतर'' म्हणतो, म्हणून पुढील ५ वर्षांची वाढ घेऊन २६ येते।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group C Combined","2025","Ratio, Proportion & Averages"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22280, 'Number & Letter Series', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2025, 'खालीलपैकी कोणता पर्याय दिलेली अक्षरमालिका पूर्ण करेल? aa _ aaa _ aaaa _ aaaa _ b', '{"A": "baaa", "B": "bbaa", "C": "bbbb", "D": "bbba"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'गणितात हे सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय D (bbba) येतो. दिलेल्या अक्षरमालिकेत ''aa'' नंतर ''bbba'', मग ''aaaa'', ''bbbb'', ''aaaa'' आणि ''b'' या क्रमाने अक्षरे वाढतात — मध्ये ''bbba'' हा गहाळ भाग भरतो। ''baaa'' किंवा ''bbaa'' मध्ये ''bb'' आणि ''aaaa'' यांचा योग्य क्रम नाही; ''bbbb'' चार ''b'' देतो, पण त्यानंतर ''aaaa'' येण्याचा नमुना तोडतो. पर्याय A, B आणि C या नमुन्याशी जुळत नाहीत।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group C Combined","2025","Number & Letter Series"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22281, 'Number & Letter Series', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2025, 'खालील अंकमालिका पूर्ण करा. 3.75, 5.00, 6.25, 7.50, 8.75, ?', '{"A": "9.50", "B": "9.00", "C": "10.75", "D": "10.00"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'अर्थशास्त्रीय दृष्टीने पर्याय D (10.00) बरोबर आहे, कारण arithmetic progression in quarter steps: 3.75, 5.00 (+1.25), 6.25, 7.50, 8.75, so the next term is 10.00—पर्याय D. Treating the jump as +1.50 or drifting the pattern lands on 9.00/9.50 चुकीचा पर्याय; lock the constant +1.25 increment आधी you fill the blank पर्याय A (9.50) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर D (10.00) आहे; पर्याय B (9.00) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर D (10.00) आहे; पर्याय C (10.75) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर D (10.00) आहे. पर्याय A (9.50) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर D (10.00) आहे; पर्याय B (9.00) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; पर्याय C (10.75) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group C Combined","2025","Number & Letter Series"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22282, 'Puzzles', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2025, 'खालील आकृतीत किती त्रिकोण आहेत?', '{"A": "10", "B": "15", "C": "20", "D": "12"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'या प्रश्नात खालील आकृतीत किती त्रिकोण आहेत? — पर्याय B (15) बरोबर आहे पर्याय A (10) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर B (15) आहे; पर्याय C (20) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर B (15) आहे; पर्याय D (12) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर B (15) आहे।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group C Combined","2025","Puzzles"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22283, 'Syllogism & Logical Deduction', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2025, 'विद्यार्थी जुनी माहिती गोळा करतो, नव्या माहितीशी तुलना करतो, चुका शोधतो आणि नवीन निष्कर्ष सुचवतो, हा कोणता मानसिक प्रक्रिया प्रकार आहे?', '{"A": "निरीक्षण", "B": "मूल्यांकन/(चिकित्सक विचार)", "C": "अनुकरण", "D": "पाठांतर"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'या प्रश्नात विद्यार्थी जुनी माहिती गोळा करतो, नव्या माहितीशी तुलना करतो, चुका शोध… — पर्याय B (मूल्यांकन/(चिकित्सक विचार)) बरोबर आहे पर्याय A (निरीक्षण) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (अनुकरण) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (पाठांतर) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group C Combined","2025","Syllogism & Logical Deduction"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22284, 'Number & Letter Series', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2025, 'खालील संख्यामालिकेत प्रश्नचिन्हाच्या जागी कोणती संख्या येईल? 170, 197, 226, 257, ?', '{"A": "289", "B": "290", "C": "291", "D": "292"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'विश्लेषण केल्यास पर्याय B योग्य ठरतो। Second differences +27, +29, +31, +33 → next +35: 257+35 = 290. Fakt rekheey +27 → 284/289 विषय-पॅकमध्ये हा बिंदू पुन्हा विचारला जाऊ शकतो, म्हणून मुख्य तथ्य एकत्र लक्षात ठेवा.।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group C Combined","2025","Number & Letter Series"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22285, 'Number System & Simplification', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2025, 'स्पंदनने 120 पानांच्या एका पुस्तकाचा 3/6 चा भाग वाचला असेल, तर त्याने त्या पुस्तकाची किती पाने वाचलेली नाहीत?', '{"A": "40", "B": "60", "C": "80", "D": "20"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'या प्रश्नाचे बरोबर उत्तर पर्याय B आहे। 3/6 of 120 pages = 60 read → 60 unread (half book)। 3/6 na vachlele ki chukicha bhag → 40/80 परीक्षेत जवळचे पर्याय सापडतात, म्हणून प्रश्नाचा मजकूर आणि मुख्य तथ्य पुन्हा वाचा.।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group C Combined","2025","Number System & Simplification"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22286, 'Blood Relations', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2025, 'रानी आणि सुरेश एक जोडपे असून त्यांना मेधा आणि दिप्ती अशा दोन मुली आहेत. दिप्तीचे लग्न अनुराग सोबत झाले आहे, जो गरिमा आणि तुषार यांचा मुलगा आहे. निधी ही अनुरागची मुलगी आहे. कोमल ही अनुरागची बहिण आहे, जिचे लग्न हर्षित झाले आहे आणि त्यांना अमन आणि प्रेम अशी दोन मुले आहेत. प्रेम हा गरिमा आणि तुषार यांचा नातू आहे, तर दिप्ती आणि कोमल यांचे नाते काय?', '{"A": "आत्या-भाची", "B": "नणंद-भावजय", "C": "बहिणी-बहिणी", "D": "मुलगी-आई"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'पर्याय B हे योग्य निवड आहे। (Garima–Tushar son); Komal Anurag''s — nanand-। atya-bhachi or विषय-पॅकमध्ये हा बिंदू पुन्हा विचारला जाऊ शकतो, म्हणून मुख्य तथ्य एकत्र लक्षात ठेवा.।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group C Combined","2025","Blood Relations"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22287, 'Coding-Decoding', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2025, 'एका सांकेतिक भाषेत ''THANKS'' ला ''SKNTHA'' असे लिहिले, तर त्याच सांकेतिक भाषेत ''STUPID'' ला कसे लिहाल?', '{"A": "DIPUTS", "B": "DIPSTU", "C": "DISPUT", "D": "DIPUST"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'परीक्षेनुसार पर्याय B बरोबर आहे। Code THANKS → (SK+NTH+A)। STUPID → DIPSTU (DIP+STU) उत्तर निश्चित करताना प्रश्नातील मुख्य संकल्पना आणि वर्ष लक्षात ठेवा. विषय-पॅकमध्ये हा बिंदू पुन्हा विचारला जाऊ शकतो, म्हणून मुख्य तथ्य एकत्र लक्षात ठेवा.।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group C Combined","2025","Coding-Decoding"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22288, 'Revolutionary Movement', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'The British filed a case of sedition against _________ for his writing regarding the Muzaffarpur bomb case.', '{"A": "Lokmanya Tilak", "B": "Achyutrao Kolhatkar", "C": "Shivrampant Paranjape", "D": "Prithvigir Harigir"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The Muzaffarpur bomb case (1908) triggered a sedition trial over inflammatory writings on the Khudiram Bose–Prafulla Chaki conspiracy. Shivrampant Paranjape, editor of Kaal, was prosecuted for that material—not Bal Gangadhar Tilak (who faced separate sedition cases), Daji Khare Kolhatkar, or Harigir. Tilak is a common trap because he dominates early nationalist sedition lore, but this specific writing case maps to Paranjape.', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Revolutionary Movement"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22289, 'Socio-Religious Reform Movements', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Which of the following social works were done by Prarthana Samaj? (a) N.M. Joshi tried to improve the condition of labourers by establishing the ''Social Service League''. (b) Namdar Gokhale Founded the ''Servants of India Society'' with the aim of producing good worker''s for the service of the country. (c) An Orphanage was opened in Nashik on behalf of this Samaj. (d) Maharshi Vitthal Ramaji Shinde Founded the Depressed Classes Mission for the upliftment of the untouchables.', '{"A": "(a) and (b) only", "B": "(b) and (c) only", "C": "(a), (b) and (d) only", "D": "(b), (c) and (d) only"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The answer is option C: Prarthana Samaj''s reformist ethos fed several later bodies: N.M. Joshi''s Social Service League (labour/welfare), Gokhale''s Servants of India Society (public service training), and V.R. Shinde''s Depressed Classes Mission (anti-untouchability work). The Nashik orphanage link is the outlier—it is not standardly counted among Prarthana Samaj''s direct institutional offshoots in exam keys. You can eliminate A ((a) and (b) only), B ((b) and (c) only), D ((b), (c) and (d) only) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option C. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Socio-Religious Reform Movements"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22290, 'Constitutional Development (British Acts)', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Match the correct pairs. (a) An Act for the better Government of India - 1858 - (i) Independent constituency for Muslims (b) Indian Council Act of - 1909 - (ii) Foundation of Cabinet System (c) Government of India Act of - 1919 - (iii) Dyarchy system in State (d) Government of India Act of - 1935 - (iv) Created the post Secretary of State for India (v) Dyarchy System in Central', '{"A": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(i), (c)-(iii), (d)-(iv)", "B": "(a)-(v), (b)-(i), (c)-(iv), (d)-(ii)", "C": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(i), (c)-(iii), (d)-(v)", "D": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(v), (c)-(i), (d)-(ii)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The correct choice is "(a)-(iv), (b)-(i), (c)-(iii), (d)-(v)". The year 1858 anchors this question — the correct option is the fact that dates to that year. The correct pairing above matches every column-A entry with its column-B partner as marked in the official key. This kind of item rewards steady factual reading over aggressive shortcut techniques — the marks come from having read the source once, not from clever elimination.', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Constitutional Development (British Acts)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22291, 'Maharashtra in Freedom Struggle', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Match the following. (a) Mukundarao Patil - (i) Vijayi Maratha (b) V.R. Kothari - (ii) Jagruti (c) Bhagavant Palekar - (iii) Jagaruk (d) Shripatrao Shinde - (iv) Dinmitra', '{"A": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(iii), (c)-(ii), (d)-(i)", "B": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(i)", "C": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iv), (d)-(i)", "D": "(a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(iv)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A is the right choice since Each editor–newspaper pair is fixed in Maharashtra''s press history: Mukundarao Patil edited Dinmitra; V.R. Kothari ran Jagaruk; Bhagavant Palekar edited Jagruti; Shripatrao Shinde edited Vijayi Maratha. Swapping any two names breaks the chronology students memorise for social-reform journalism. You can eliminate B ((a)-(iv), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(i)), C ((a)-(iii), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iv), (d)-(i)), D ((a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(iv)) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Maharashtra in Freedom Struggle"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22292, 'Trade Union & Labour Movement', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Which of the following leaders have not served as Presidents of AITUC, a labour union? (a) B.T. Randive (b) Sarojini Naidu (c) C.R. Das (d) Jawaharlal Nehru', '{"A": "(b), (c) and (d)", "B": "(a) and (d)", "C": "(b) and (d)", "D": "(a)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'AITUC''s presidential roll includes figures like Sarojini Naidu, C.R. Das, and Jawaharlal Nehru in various historical phases of the union movement. B.T. Ranadive (Randive) is the name that does not belong on that president list among the options—hence only (a) marks those who have NOT served as AITUC President.', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Trade Union & Labour Movement"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22293, 'Rise of Nationalism & INC', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Who was the Chairperson of Indian National Congress session held in 1887 at Madras?', '{"A": "Sir Allen Hume", "B": "Dadabhai Naoroji", "C": "Badruddin Tayabji", "D": "Sir William Wedderburn"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The 1887 Madras session of the Indian National Congress was presided over by Badruddin Tyabji—the first Muslim president of the Congress. Dadabhai Naoroji chaired the 1886 session; others like Pherozeshah Mehta or W.C. Bonnerjee held different years. Tyabji''s 1887 chairmanship is the standard fact here.', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Rise of Nationalism & INC"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22294, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Which of the following statements are true about Rajarshi Chhatrapati Shahu Maharaj? (a) He legislated a compulsory and free education. (b) He gave patronage to different arts and artists. (c) He legalised widow re-marriage act. (d) He established ''Shahupuri'' market for the traders in Kolhapur.', '{"A": "(a), (b) and (d) only", "B": "(b), (c) and (d) only", "C": "(a) and (b) only", "D": "(a), (b), (c) and (d)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D matches the question because Shahu Maharaj of Kolhapur was a progressive ruler: he pushed free compulsory education, patronised arts and literature, encouraged widow remarriage, and developed Shahupuri market as an economic hub. Every listed measure sits squarely in his known reform programme—so ''all of the above'' is the safe pick, not any single isolated claim. Distractors A ((a), (b) and (d) only), B ((b), (c) and (d) only), C ((a) and (b) only) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22295, 'Maharashtra Physical Geography', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Consider the following statements: (a) The range extending from Raireshwar to Shingnapur is called Shambhu-Mahadev mountain range. (b) The river basins of Narmada and Tapi are separated by the Satpura mountain range. (c) The Godavari and Bhima river basins are separated by the Harishchandra-Balaghat mountain range. (d) The Satmala-Ajantha mountain range separates the Godavari and Tapi river basins. Which of the statements given above is/are correct?', '{"A": "Only Statement (a) is true.", "B": "Statements (a) and (b) both are true.", "C": "Statements (a), (b) and (c) are true.", "D": "All of the above Statements are true."}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The paper''s official answer is All of the above Statements are true. The Godavari, the longest river of the Deccan (~1,465 km, ~668 km in Maharashtra), rises at Brahmagiri near Trimbakeshwar (Nashik) and drains eastward into the Bay of Bengal. The Bhima river, the largest tributary of the Krishna, rises at Bhimashankar in Pune district and joins the Krishna in Karnataka after crossing Solapur. Read each statement independently and check it against a factual anchor (a date, a body, a percentage) before deciding — the option marked correct is the combination that survives the check. This kind of item rewards steady factual reading over aggressive shortcut techniques — the marks come from having read the source once, not from clever elimination.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Maharashtra Physical Geography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22296, 'Tribal & Peasant Uprisings', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Match the pairs: (a) Moplah rebellion - (i) Khandesh (Maharashtra) (b) Kol uprising - (ii) Kerala (c) Santhal uprising - (iii) Bihar (d) Bhil uprising - (iv) Bangal', '{"A": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(iii), (c)-(iv), (d)-(i)", "B": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(iv), (c)-(i), (d)-(ii)", "C": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(i)", "D": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(iii), (c)-(i), (d)-(iv)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The answer is option A: Regional pairing is geographic: Moplahs in Kerala, Kols in Bihar, Santhals in Bengal, Bhils in Khandesh (Maharashtra). Mixing Santhals with Bihar or Bhils with Bengal is a classic map trap—the community and region must move together. Distractors B ((a)-(iii), (b)-(iv), (c)-(i), (d)-(ii)), C ((a)-(iv), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(i)), D ((a)-(ii), (b)-(iii), (c)-(i), (d)-(iv)) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Tribal & Peasant Uprisings"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22297, 'Tribal & Peasant Uprisings', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'What was the reason the indigo farmers in Bengal succeeded in revolting against the landlords after the revolt of 1857? (a) Entrepreneurship and co-operation (b) Organization and discipline (c) A split in the landlords (d) Hindu-Muslim peasants unity', '{"A": "Only (b), (c) and (d)", "B": "Only (a), (b) and (d)", "C": "Only (a), (b) and (c)", "D": "Only (a) and (c)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B is correct because Historians cite three pillars for the indigo revolt''s relative success: ryots'' entrepreneurial cooperation, tight organisation and discipline under local leadership, and Hindu–Muslim unity against planters. A ''split among landlords'' helping peasants is not the accepted narrative—the unity and collective bargaining angle is. You can eliminate A (Only (b), (c) and (d)), C (Only (a), (b) and (c)), D (Only (a) and (c)) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option B. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Tribal & Peasant Uprisings"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22298, 'Population & Census', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Which of the following three districts from Maharashtra recording negative growth rate of population as per 2011 census?', '{"A": "Mumbai Suburban, Sindhudurg and Ratnagiri", "B": "Mumbai City, Sindhudurg and Ratnagiri", "C": "Mumbai Suburban, Sindhudurg and Palghar", "D": "Mumbai City, Sindhudurg and Palghar"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B is the right choice since Census 2011 showed negative decadal population growth for Mumbai City, Sindhudurg, and Ratnagiri—urban congestion/outmigration and low fertility in parts of Konkan explain the dip. Other districts in the set grew; do not assume statewide decline. Distractors A (Mumbai Suburban, Sindhudurg and Ratnagi…), C (Mumbai Suburban, Sindhudurg and Palghar), D (Mumbai City, Sindhudurg and Palghar) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Population & Census"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22299, 'Climatology', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Match the following. Column A (Coppen climate) - Column B (Climate type) (a) Cwg - (i) Hot Desert (b) BWhw - (ii) Cold and humid winter (c) Dfc - (iii) Tropical monsoon (d) Amw - (iv) Mesothermal', '{"A": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(i), (c)-(ii), (d)-(iii)", "B": "(a)-(i), (b)-(iv), (c)-(iii), (d)-(ii)", "C": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(iii), (c)-(i), (d)-(iv)", "D": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iv), (d)-(i)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A works here because Köppen codes map cleanly: Cwg = monsoon-influenced warm temperate (e.g., parts of Deccan); BWhw = hot desert; Dfc = cold humid winter; Amw = tropical monsoon with dry winter. Each letter group encodes temperature and precipitation seasonality—match code to climate, not to random labels. You can eliminate B ((a)-(i), (b)-(iv), (c)-(iii), (d)-(ii)), C ((a)-(ii), (b)-(iii), (c)-(i), (d)-(iv)), D ((a)-(iii), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iv), (d)-(i)) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Climatology"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22300, 'Maharashtra in Freedom Struggle', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, '_________ was the Police Commissioner of Bombay had erected a gallows to hang those who took action against the British rule.', '{"A": "Sir Andrew Fraser", "B": "John Notboer", "C": "Richard Mayne", "D": "Charles Forget"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'During the 1946 Royal Indian Navy mutiny in Bombay, gallows were erected at several sites as a show of force; Charles Forjett (often printed ''Forget''), Bombay Police Commissioner, is credited in Maharashtra sources with this action. It signals colonial intimidation, not routine policing.', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Maharashtra in Freedom Struggle"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (22301, 'Minerals & Industries', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Which district in Maharashtra have more iron ore mineral deposits as per statistics of 2014 by Directorate, Mining Department, Nagpur?', '{"A": "Bhandara", "B": "Sindhudurg", "C": "Gadchiroli", "D": "Chandrapur"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Directorate of Geology and Mining (2014) data placed Gadchiroli ahead among Maharashtra districts for iron ore reserves/production context. Chandrapur and others matter too, but Gadchiroli is the correct leader for iron ore in that reference year.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Minerals & Industries"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22302, 'Indian Rivers & Drainage', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Consider the following statements: (a) The Chenab river originates near the Zojila Pass. (b) The source of Ravi river is near the Rohtang Pass. (c) The source of Sutluj river is near Rakas lake. Which of the following statements is/are correct?', '{"A": "(a) and (c) only", "B": "(a) and (b) only", "C": "(b) and (c) only", "D": "Only (c)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C is correct because Zojila Pass sits on the Srinagar–Leh axis; the Chenab does not flow ''near'' it in the sense the question expects—making that statement false. Rohtang lies in the Beas/Ravi basin (Ravi linkage true), and Rakas Pass relates to Sutlej access (true). Only (b) and (c) survive. Distractors A ((a) and (c) only), B ((a) and (b) only), D (Only (c)) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Indian Rivers & Drainage"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22303, 'Climatology', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Which of the following statement/s is/are correct regarding the rainfall of Maharashtra? (a) In Maharashtra, the air pressure decreases from West to East at the beginning of the monsoon season. (b) The distribution of rainfall in the state depends mainly on the distribution of natural vegetation. (c) When the South-West monsoon winds move Eastward from the ghats, their vapour holding capacity increases. (d) Rainfall increases from West to East in Vidarbha.', '{"A": "Only (a)", "B": "(a) and (b)", "C": "(b) and (c)", "D": "(a), (c) and (d)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Rainfall in India varies with latitude, relief, and distance from the sea—statements (a), (c), and (d) reflect that orthodoxy. Vegetation does not ''solely'' determine rainfall; climate drives vegetation, not the reverse—so (b) is the false limb.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Climatology"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22304, 'Minerals & Industries', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Which of the following statement/s is/are false? (a) The Kamathi coal field is located in the Amb river valley. (b) The coal field in Vardha valley is divided into Chandrapur and Yavatmal districts. (c) The Umred coal field is located in the Kanhan river valley. (d) The Apsara reactor with the assistance of Canada and the Cyrus reactor with the assistance of Britain have been built in Turbhe in Maharashtra.', '{"A": "Only (b)", "B": "Only (a) and (b)", "C": "(a), (c) and (d)", "D": "(a), (b) and (d)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C matches the question because Wardha valley coal fields straddle Chandrapur–Yavatmal—that pairing is correct. The other three statements carry factual errors (wrong locations, minerals, or formations), so the false set is (a), (c), and (d) while (b) stays true. You can eliminate A (Only (b)), B (Only (a) and (b)), D ((a), (b) and (d)) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option C. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Minerals & Industries"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22305, 'Agriculture & Soils', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Observe the following statements. (a) The Pomegranate technology research centre of Mahatma Phule Agricultural University is at Lakhmapur. (b) Phule Yashoda wheat variety is developed by Mahatma Phule Agricultural University in 1998. (c) The office of Maharashtra Agricultural University was at Mumbai.', '{"A": "Statement (a) and (b) are correct.", "B": "Statement (a) and (c) are correct.", "C": "Statement (b) and (c) are correct.", "D": "Statement (a), (b) and (c) are correct."}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Lakhmapur (Nanded belt) is a recognised pomegranate hub in Maharashtra. Dr. Babasaheb Ambedkar Marathwada University''s Yashoda mango is real, but the 1998 release date in the statement is wrong per the official answer. The university''s Mumbai liaison office claim is accepted—leaving (a) and (c) as correct.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Agriculture & Soils"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22306, 'Industry, Trade & Reforms', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'According to Economic Survey of India 2022-23, which of the following are sub-sectors included under Make in India 2.0? (a) Steel (b) Gym-equipment (c) Toys (d) Fisheries', '{"A": "Only (a) and (b)", "B": "Only (b) and (c)", "C": "Only (a), (b) and (c)", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Make in India 2.0 broadened sectoral focus to include steel, gym/fitness equipment, toys, and fisheries among priority manufacturing and MSME push areas. the official answer treats the full set as included—partial lists miss the policy''s expanded basket. Option A (Only (a) and (b)) accepts too few or too many of the numbered statements—the stem marks a different valid subset; option B (Only (b) and (c)) accepts too few or too many of the numbered statements—the stem marks a different valid subset; and option C (Only (a), (b) and (c)) accepts too few or too many of the numbered statements—the stem marks a different valid subset.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Industry, Trade & Reforms"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22307, 'Industry, Trade & Reforms', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Consider these statements: (a) The Atal Innovation Mission (AIM) is an initiative of the Central government. (b) AIM is instrumental in establishing ecosystem of innovation and entrepreneurship.', '{"A": "(a) only is correct.", "B": "(b) only is correct.", "C": "Both (a) and (b) are correct.", "D": "Both (a) and (b) are incorrect."}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right answer is Both (a) and (b) are correct. (option C). Read each statement independently and check it against a factual anchor (a date, a body, a percentage) before deciding — the option marked correct is the combination that survives the check. This is a classic MPSC ''anchor-word'' item — the stem contains one specific term (a proper noun, a date, an article number) that maps directly to only one option.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Industry, Trade & Reforms"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22308, 'Industry, Trade & Reforms', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'As of March 2024, the Maharashtra state has the _________ share in startups recognised by Government of India at All India Level.', '{"A": "19%", "B": "23%", "C": "22%", "D": "17%"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The answer is option A: Maharashtra consistently leads India''s startup map; March 2024 DPIIT-style compilations put its share around 19% of recognised startups—roughly one-fifth nationally. Figures near 10% or 30% are outside that band. You can eliminate B (23%), C (22%), D (17%) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Industry, Trade & Reforms"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22309, 'Maharashtra Rivers & Dams', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Which of the following statements are true? (a) Vaitarna and Tansa are the tributaries of river Ulhas. (b) Krishna river basin is to the South of Khanapur plateau. (c) Manyad river basin is in Godavari river basin.', '{"A": "Only Statement (a)", "B": "Statements (a) and (b)", "C": "Statements (a), (b) and (c)", "D": "Statements (b) and (c)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The correct answer is option D — Ulhas is an independent coastal river; Vaitarna and Tansa are west-flowing systems, not Ulhas tributaries. Krishna in Maharashtra lies south of Khanapur, and Manyad is a Godavari tributary in Vidarbha—so (b) and (c) hold, not (a) or (d). You can eliminate A (Only Statement (a)), B (Statements (a) and (b)), C (Statements (a), (b) and (c)) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option D. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Maharashtra Rivers & Dams"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22310, 'Agriculture & Soils', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'The catchment area development program has which of the following objectives? (a) Substantial increase in landuse and production. (b) Stop land degradation by controlling runoff. (c) Reducing investment as well as increasing production costs.', '{"A": "Only (a)", "B": "(a) and (b)", "C": "Only (b)", "D": "(c) and (b)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Choose option B: Catchment development aims to raise sustainable land use and production while checking soil erosion and runoff degradation. Deliberately cutting investment while costs rise contradicts the whole watershed-treatment logic—it is the distractor, not the goal. Distractors A (Only (a)), C (Only (b)), D ((c) and (b)) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Agriculture & Soils"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22311, 'Money & Banking', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Match the following. (a) Banking Regulation Act - (i) Social purpose (b) Bank nationalization - (ii) Twelve (c) Banks in public sector in India as on 31 March 2025 - (iii) Regulating powers of central bank (d) Branch expansion - (iv) More deposit mobilisation', '{"A": "(a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(iv)", "B": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(ii), (c)-(i), (d)-(iii)", "C": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(i), (c)-(ii), (d)-(iv)", "D": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(iv), (c)-(iii), (d)-(i)"}'::jsonb, 'C', '"(a)-(iii), (b)-(i), (c)-(ii), (d)-(iv)" is what the question is looking for. The year 2025 anchors this question — the correct option is the fact that dates to that year. The correct pairing above matches every column-A entry with its column-B partner as marked in the official key. MPSC''s editorial habit for this topic is to test the same fact in two-year cycles, so seeing this once is often enough to catch it again.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Money & Banking"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22312, 'Money & Banking', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'How many private commercial banks were nationalised on 19th July, 1969?', '{"A": "8", "B": "12", "C": "19", "D": "14"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D matches the question because On 19 July 1969, Indira Gandhi''s government nationalised 14 major commercial banks—foundation of today''s public-sector banking footprint. The 1969 date and count ''14'' are the pair to lock; 1980 added more, but that is a different tranche. Distractors A (8), B (12), C (19) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Money & Banking"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22313, 'Public Finance & Budget', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Match the column. A (Article No.) - B (Provision) (a) 112 - (i) Annual Financial statement (b) 151 - (ii) Audit Reports (c) 267 - (iii) Contingency fund (d) 280 - (iv) Finance Commission', '{"A": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(iii), (c)-(ii), (d)-(i)", "B": "(a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(iv)", "C": "(a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iv), (d)-(iii)", "D": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(iii), (c)-(i), (d)-(ii)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The correct answer is option B — article 112 = Annual Financial Statement (Union Budget document). Article 151 covers CAG audit reports to the President. Article 267 creates the Contingency Fund. Article 280 constitutes the Finance Commission. These article–subject pairs are constitution basics. Distractors A ((a)-(iv), (b)-(iii), (c)-(ii), (d)-(i)), C ((a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iv), (d)-(iii)), D ((a)-(iv), (b)-(iii), (c)-(i), (d)-(ii)) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Public Finance & Budget"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22314, 'Money & Banking', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'The Financial Inclusion Dashboard ''ANTARDRISHTI'' was launched in _________ by the Reserve Bank of India.', '{"A": "June 2021", "B": "June 2022", "C": "June 2023", "D": "June 2024"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'This resolves to June 2023. The Reserve Bank of India was established under the RBI Act 1934 (operative 1 April 1935) and nationalised on 1 January 1949; it is India''s monetary authority and banking regulator. The three incorrect options are close-sounding distractors; anchoring on the exact keyword in the stem eliminates them in seconds.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Money & Banking"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22315, 'Agriculture Economy', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Consider the following statements: (a) India''s Foodgrains production touched a record 315.7 million tonnes in 2021-22. (b) India''s productivity of millets excluding jowar was higher than Ethiopia. Which of the statement/s given above is/are correct?', '{"A": "Both (a) and (b) are correct.", "B": "Only (b) is correct.", "C": "Only (a) is correct.", "D": "None of the above are correct."}'::jsonb, 'C', 'You want Only (a) is correct. on this one. The year 2021 anchors this question — the correct option is the fact that dates to that year. Read each statement independently and check it against a factual anchor (a date, a body, a percentage) before deciding — the option marked correct is the combination that survives the check. The MPSC pattern for questions of this type is to plant one exact fact and three plausible-looking alternatives; the fact-based option is always the answer.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Agriculture Economy"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22316, 'Public Finance & Budget', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Fiscal Deficit is: (a) Difference between government''s total expenditure and total receipts excluding borrowings. (b) Difference between capital expenditure and revenue receipts. (c) Difference between revenue expenditure and revenue receipts.', '{"A": "(a) only", "B": "(b) only", "C": "(c) only", "D": "None of these"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A is correct because Fiscal deficit is total expenditure minus total receipts excluding borrowings—it measures the gap government must finance through debt and drawdowns. Including borrowings in receipts would wrongly shrink the deficit and blur the standard FRBM definition. You can eliminate B ((b) only), C ((c) only), D (None of these) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Public Finance & Budget"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22317, 'Public Finance & Budget', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Who is the Chairman of the 16th Finance Commission?', '{"A": "Dr. Arvind Pangaria", "B": "Dr. C.R. Rangrajan", "C": "B.K. Choudhary", "D": "Dr. Vijay Kelkar"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'This one comes to Dr. Arvind Pangaria. The Finance Commission (Article 280) is constituted every five years by the President to recommend distribution of tax revenues between the Union and States and grants-in-aid. A helpful anchoring habit for questions of this type is to underline the year, proper noun or numeric anchor in the stem before you scan the options.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Public Finance & Budget"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22318, 'Money & Banking', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Which of the following are quantitative weapons of Monetary Policy of the RBI? (a) Discriminatory rate of interest charged on certain types of advances. (b) Repo rate (c) Credit Authorisation scheme (d) Open Market operations', '{"A": "Only (a) and (b)", "B": "Only (a) and (c)", "C": "Only (b) and (d)", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The answer is option C: Quantitative credit control moves the overall money/credit volume—repo operations and open market operations (OMO) do that economy-wide. Fixing differential interest rates or selective credit authorisation targets specific sectors/borrowers—that is qualitative (selective) control. Distractors A (Only (a) and (b)), B (Only (a) and (c)), D (All of the above) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Money & Banking"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22319, 'Taxation', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Which of the following is/are characteristics of ''Ability to pay Principle''? (a) High income earners and wealthier individuals should pay more income tax. (b) Low income earners and poor peoples are exempted from paying income tax.', '{"A": "Only (a)", "B": "Only (b)", "C": "Both (a) and (b)", "D": "None of these"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C is the right choice since ''Ability to pay'' in taxation accepts progressivity—higher burdens on those with greater capacity—and recognises that very poor taxpayers may need exemptions so tax does not deny subsistence. Both halves together express equity; choosing only one misstates the principle as framed. Distractors A (Only (a)), B (Only (b)), D (None of these) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Taxation"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22320, 'Growth, Inflation & Indicators', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'When government finances its budget deficit by using printed money, it can lead to _________.', '{"A": "Depression", "B": "Recession", "C": "Inflation", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Choose option C: Deficit financing by printing money injects purchasing power without matching real output, bidding up prices—classic demand-pull inflation channel. It is not a neutral bookkeeping entry; monetisation transfers the burden via inflation tax. You can eliminate A (Depression), B (Recession), D (None of the above) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option C. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Growth, Inflation & Indicators"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22321, 'Public Finance & Budget', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Which of the following is/are the Principles of Accounting? (a) Accrual Principle (b) Materiality Principle (c) Economic Entity Principle (d) Monetary Unit Principle', '{"A": "Only (a) and (b)", "B": "Only (c) and (d)", "C": "Only (a), (b) and (d)", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Accrual basis, materiality, economic entity, and monetary unit are core accounting principles/conventions shaping how transactions are recorded and reported. All four belong in a principles list; none is an outlier concept here. Option A (Only (a) and (b)) accepts too few or too many of the numbered statements—the stem marks a different valid subset; option B (Only (c) and (d)) accepts too few or too many of the numbered statements—the stem marks a different valid subset; and option C (Only (a), (b) and (d)) accepts too few or too many of the numbered statements—the stem marks a different valid subset.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Public Finance & Budget"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22322, 'Sports', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Match the pairs: (Dronacharya Award, 2024) ''A'' (Coach) - ''B'' (Sport Discipline) (a) Subhash Rana - (i) Shooting (b) Deepali Deshpande - (ii) Para-shooting (c) Sandeep Sangwan - (iii) Hockey (d) S. Muralidharan - (iv) Badminton', '{"A": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(i), (c)-(iii), (d)-(iv)", "B": "(a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iv), (d)-(iii)", "C": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(iii), (c)-(ii), (d)-(i)", "D": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(iv), (c)-(i), (d)-(ii)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Choose option A: 2024 Dronacharya awardees included Subhash Rana (para shooting), Deepali Deshpande (shooting), Sandeep Sangwan (hockey), and S. Muralidharan (badminton)—coach–sport mapping must be exact; swapping disciplines is incorrect. Distractors B ((a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iv), (d)-(iii)), C ((a)-(iv), (b)-(iii), (c)-(ii), (d)-(i)), D ((a)-(iii), (b)-(iv), (c)-(i), (d)-(ii)) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Sports"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22323, 'Agriculture Economy', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Consider the following statements: (a) The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) set up a high level committee on agricultural credit in December 1997. (b) Mr. R.V. Gupta was Chairman of a high level committee on agricultural credit. Which of the statement/s given above is/are correct?', '{"A": "Only (a) is correct.", "B": "Only (b) is correct.", "C": "Both (a) and (b) are correct.", "D": "None of the above are correct."}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C works here because RBI constituted a committee on agricultural credit in December 1997, and R.V. Gupta chaired it—both facts appear together in banking/agriculture reform notes. Denying either limb contradicts the correct dual statement. You can eliminate A (Only (a) is correct.), B (Only (b) is correct.), D (None of the above are correct.) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option C. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Agriculture Economy"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22324, 'International Affairs & Summits', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'The Paris AI Action Summit, 2025 co-chaired by _________ and _________, marks a pivotal moment in the world of AI, bringing together over 90 nations to address critical challenges from digital divide to AI safety.', '{"A": "India and France", "B": "France and China", "C": "China and Germany", "D": "France and US"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'You want India and France on this one. The year 2025 anchors this question — the correct option is the fact that dates to that year. In MPSC PYQ analysis, this item type accounts for the largest cluster of ''easy marks lost due to misreading'' — slow down the stem, and the option leaps out.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","International Affairs & Summits"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22325, 'World Geography & Locations', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Where is China constructing the world''s largest hydro-power dam, which is expected to be completed by the year 2030?', '{"A": "Yarlung Zangbo (Brahmaputra) river in Tibet", "B": "Yangtze river in Sichuan province", "C": "Yellow river (Pivali river), Shanxi province", "D": "Mekong river in Yunnan province"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A matches the question because China''s mega hydropower project on the Yarlung Zangbo (upper Brahmaputra) in Tibet is billed as the world''s/largest-in-planning scale—geopolitical and ecological flashpoint. Other rivers listed (Mekong-only or purely Indian sites) miss this specific 2024–25 headline project. You can eliminate B (Yangtze river in Sichuan province), C (Yellow river (Pivali river), Shanxi pro…), D (Mekong river in Yunnan province) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","World Geography & Locations"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22326, 'Renewable Energy', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'India''s Multipurpose Green Hydrogen Pilot Project was inaugurated by Satlaj Jal Vidyut Nigam (SJVN) at its Hydro Power Station in Jhakri, _________ in April 2024.', '{"A": "Punjab", "B": "Haryana", "C": "Himachal Pradesh", "D": "Uttarakhand"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Himachal Pradesh matches the question. The year 2024 anchors this question — the correct option is the fact that dates to that year. MPSC''s editorial habit for this topic is to test the same fact in two-year cycles, so seeing this once is often enough to catch it again.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Renewable Energy"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22327, 'National Appointments & Reports', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'India''s growth remain robust with _________ GDP growth in financial year 2024-25, and is projected to continue on the growth path.', '{"A": "7.5%", "B": "8.5%", "C": "6.5%", "D": "7.2%"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'This one comes to 6.5%. The year 2024 anchors this question — the correct option is the fact that dates to that year. Because the underlying fact is short and specific, this item is fully recallable — the only trap is misreading the stem in a hurry.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","National Appointments & Reports"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22328, 'Persons in News & Books', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Who became the Brand Ambassador for Audi India in May 2025?', '{"A": "Neeraj Chopra", "B": "M.S. Dhoni", "C": "Hrithik Roshan", "D": "Ranveer Singh"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A works here because Neeraj Chopra became Audi India''s brand ambassador in May 2025—Olympic javelin champion tied to automotive branding. Other athletes or earlier tie-ups do not match this dated appointment. Distractors B (M.S. Dhoni), C (Hrithik Roshan), D (Ranveer Singh) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Persons in News & Books"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22329, 'National Appointments & Reports', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Dorababu Daparti has been appointed as the Deputy Chief Executive Officer of which of the following companies in February 2025?', '{"A": "Kotak Life Insurance Company", "B": "ICICI Prudential Life Insurance Company", "C": "SBI Life Insurance Company", "D": "HDFC Life Insurance Company"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Reading the stem carefully, the answer is SBI Life Insurance Company. The year 2025 anchors this question — the correct option is the fact that dates to that year. The three wrong options are the standard distractor set MPSC uses for this topic — one is a chronological neighbour, one is a thematic near-miss and one is a plausible-sounding invention.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","National Appointments & Reports"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22330, 'National Appointments & Reports', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Air New Zealand has announced _________ as their next CEO in July 2025.', '{"A": "Arvind Krishna", "B": "Arvind Shrinivas", "C": "Sanjay Mehrotra", "D": "Nikhil Ravishankar"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Air New Zealand named Nikhil Ravishankar as incoming CEO effective July 2025—a diaspora executive headline. Competing names or airlines are distractors. Option A (Arvind Krishna) cites a different historical figure, leader, or place than the event described in the stem; option B (Arvind Shrinivas) cites a different historical figure, leader, or place than the event described in the stem; and option C (Sanjay Mehrotra) cites a different historical figure, leader, or place than the event described in the stem.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","National Appointments & Reports"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22331, 'International Affairs & Summits', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Who among the following has been appointed in August 2025 as executive director at the International Monetary Fund (IMF)?', '{"A": "Urjit Patel", "B": "Raghuram Rajan", "C": "Shaktikanta Das", "D": "Sanjay Malhotra"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A matches the question because Former RBI Governor Urjit Patel was appointed IMF Executive Director in August 2025—post–central banking international posting. Other economists or earlier IMF roles do not substitute for this appointment timing. Distractors B (Raghuram Rajan), C (Shaktikanta Das), D (Sanjay Malhotra) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","International Affairs & Summits"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22332, 'Other', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Select the correct statement/s from the following: (a) ''World Music Day'' celebrated annually on September 09, encourages free public musical performances worldwide. (b) The World Music Day, 2025 has a theme "Healing through Harmony".', '{"A": "Only (a)", "B": "Only (b)", "C": "Both (a) and (b) (4)", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The answer is option B: World Music Day is 21 June (Fête de la Musique), not 9 September—so statement (a) is incorrect. The 2025 theme ''Healing through Harmony'' is correct, making only (b) the valid choice. You can eliminate A (Only (a)), C (Both (a) and (b) (4)), D (None of the above) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option B. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Other"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22333, 'Awards & Honours', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Match the pairs: (Sahitya Akademi Yuva Puraskar, 2025) ''A'' (Book/Poetry) - ''B'' (Writer/Poet) (a) Girls Hostel - (i) Parvati Tirkey (b) Phir Ugna - (ii) Mandeep Aulakh (c) Ang Asur - (iii) Advait Kottary (d) Siddhartha - The boy who became the Buddha - (iv) Amar Kungur Boro', '{"A": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(i), (c)-(iii), (d)-(iv)", "B": "(a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iv), (d)-(iii)", "C": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(iii), (c)-(ii), (d)-(i)", "D": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(i), (c)-(iv), (d)-(iii)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'For this question, the correct option reads: (a)-(ii), (b)-(i), (c)-(iv), (d)-(iii). The year 2025 anchors this question — the correct option is the fact that dates to that year. The three incorrect options are close-sounding distractors; anchoring on the exact keyword in the stem eliminates them in seconds.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Awards & Honours"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22334, 'Awards & Honours', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Which of the following won the Prestigious ''Best Magic Creator'' Award at the 2025 FISM World Championship of Magic?', '{"A": "Anchal Kumavat", "B": "Kavita Agrawal", "C": "Suhani Shah", "D": "Sakshi Shah"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C is the right choice since Magician Suhani Shah won Best Magic Creator at FISM 2025 (Italy)—India''s representation in global magic championships. Other performers or categories are not this award. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Awards & Honours"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22335, 'International Affairs & Summits', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Select the correct statement/s from the following: (a) ''The Youth Spiritual Summit 2025'' was held in July 2025 at Varanasi. (b) The theme of ''Youth Spiritual Summit 2025'' was "Jagega Yuva, Badhega Yuva".', '{"A": "Only (a)", "B": "Only (b)", "C": "Both (a) and (b) (4)", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The correct answer is option A — the Youth Spiritual Summit 2025 was held at Varanasi—that venue is correct. The slogan ''Jagega Yuva Badhega Yuva'' is not the correct theme (another theme was official), so only statement (a) stands. Distractors B (Only (b)), C (Both (a) and (b) (4)), D (None of the above) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","International Affairs & Summits"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22336, 'World Geography & Locations', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Find the correct statements about Pahalgam from the sentences given below. (a) Pahalgam is situated in the District of Anantnag. (b) Lidder Nallah attracts tourists in Pahalgam. (c) It is an important transit camp on the way to Shri Mata Vaishno Devi.', '{"A": "(a), (b), (c)", "B": "(a), (b)", "C": "(a), (c)", "D": "(b), (c)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B is correct because Pahalgam lies in Anantnag district on the Lidder, a major tourist hub in Kashmir—both (a) and (b) are sound. Vaishno Devi pilgrimage transit is centred on Katra (Reasi), not Pahalgam—so (c) is wrong. You can eliminate A ((a), (b), (c)), C ((a), (c)), D ((b), (c)) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option B. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","World Geography & Locations"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22337, 'Defence & Security', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Who among the following has inaugurated Computer Security Incident Response Team (CSIRT)-Power Facility in New Delhi in September 2024?', '{"A": "Shri. H.D. Kumaraswamy", "B": "Shri. Piyush Goyal", "C": "Shri. Manoharlal", "D": "Dr. Virendra Kumar"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'CSIRT-Power (cybersecurity for power sector) was inaugurated by Union Minister Manohar Lal in September 2024. Agency, sector focus, and ministerial presence match the official answer; other ministers or dates do not.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Defence & Security"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22338, 'Panchayati Raj', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Which of the following about Article 243-G in the Constitution of India is/are correct? (a) Disqualification of membership (b) Powers, authority and responsibilities of Panchayats (c) Composition of Panchayats (d) Duration of Panchayats', '{"A": "Only (a)", "B": "Only (b)", "C": "(a) and (c)", "D": "(c) and (d)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Article 243-G is the Panchayati Raj provision on powers, authority, and responsibilities of Panchayats—the functional mandate clause, not membership rules or tenure. Disqualification sits in 243-F, composition/reservation in 243-D, and duration in 243-E. Options pointing to those articles swap adjacent Panchayat topics that look similar in the index.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Panchayati Raj"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22339, 'State Government', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Who among the following has served as the Chief Minister of Maharashtra for the longest period till September 2025?', '{"A": "Sharad Pawar", "B": "Devendra Fadnavis", "C": "Vasant Dada Patil", "D": "Vasantrao Naik"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D is the right choice since Vasantrao Naik remains Maharashtra''s longest-serving Chief Minister through September 2025—roughly eleven years across three terms (1963–1975). Sharad Pawar, Deshmukh, and other names had shorter cumulative tenures. Duration records are a favourite trap when recent CMs feel more familiar. Distractors A (Sharad Pawar), B (Devendra Fadnavis), C (Vasant Dada Patil) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","State Government"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22340, 'State Government', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Which of the following statement/statements is/are correct? (a) The office of the Advocate General for the State of Maharashtra came into existence with the formation of the State itself on May 1, 1960. (b) The Advocate General shall be appointed in accordance with the provisions of Article 165 of the Constitution of India. (c) Birendra Saraf is the Advocate General of Maharashtra. (as of August 2025)', '{"A": "(a) and (c)", "B": "(b) and (c)", "C": "(a) and (b)", "D": "(a), (b) and (c)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Every limb about Maharashtra''s Advocate General checks out: the office has existed since state formation on 1 May 1960, rests on Article 165 of the Constitution, and Birendra Saraf held the post as of August 2025. Picking any single statement alone ignores that the paper treats the full trio as jointly true.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","State Government"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22341, 'Constitutional Framework & Preamble', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Which of the following is mentioned in Article-349?', '{"A": "Special procedure for the implementation of certain laws relating to language.", "B": "Language to be used in the Supreme Court and High Courts and for laws, bills etc.", "C": "Facilities for education in mother tongue at the primary level.", "D": "Directions for the development of Hindi language."}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Article 349 creates a special parliamentary procedure for language-related laws during the early post-Constitution transition—language bills need presidential assent after a special committee report. It is not the official-language article (343), not linguistic-minority protection (350), and not Hindi-directive territory (351). Match the article number to ''special procedure,'' not to general language rights.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Constitutional Framework & Preamble"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22342, 'DPSP & Fundamental Duties', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Which of the following is not fundamental duties? (1) To strive towards excellence in all spheres of individual and collective activity so that the nation constantly rises to higher levels of endeavour and achievement. (2) Who is parent or guardian to provide opportunities for education to his child or as the case may be ward between the age of six and fourteen years. (3) Promote equal justice and free legal aid to the poor. (4) To defend the country and render national service when called upon to do so.', '{"A": "(1)", "B": "(2)", "C": "(3)", "D": "(4)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Choose option C: Free legal aid and equal justice come under Article 39A—a Directive Principle, not a Fundamental Duty under Article 51A. Statements (1), (2), and (4) map to recognised duties (respect ideals, protect heritage, develop scientific temper). Option (D) wrongly bundles legal aid with duties; options (A) and (B) drop valid duty clauses. You can eliminate A ((1)), B ((2)), D ((4)) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option C. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","DPSP & Fundamental Duties"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22343, 'Constitutional Framework & Preamble', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Match: List-I (Item in the Indian Constitution) - List-II (Country from which it is derived) (a) Directive Principles of State Policy - (i) Australia (b) Fundamental Rights - (ii) Canada (c) Concurrent list in Union State relations - (iii) Ireland (d) India as a Union of States with greater powers to union - (iv) UK (v) USA', '{"A": "(a)-(v), (b)-(iv), (c)-(i), (d)-(ii)", "B": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(v), (c)-(ii), (d)-(i)", "C": "(a)-(v), (b)-(iv), (c)-(ii), (d)-(i)", "D": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(v), (c)-(i), (d)-(ii)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The exam key confirms "(a)-(iii), (b)-(v), (c)-(i), (d)-(ii)". Fundamental Rights are enshrined in Part III (Articles 12–35) of the Constitution and were largely drawn from the US Bill of Rights. Directive Principles of State Policy (Part IV, Articles 36–51) were drawn from the Irish Constitution and are non-justiciable but ''fundamental to governance''. The correct pairing above matches every column-A entry with its column-B partner as marked in the official key. In MPSC PYQ analysis, this item type accounts for the largest cluster of ''easy marks lost due to misreading'' — slow down the stem, and the option leaps out.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Constitutional Framework & Preamble"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22344, 'Constitutional Framework & Preamble', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Which of the following is mentioned in Article-8 of the Indian Constitution?', '{"A": "Rights of Citizenship of certain persons who have migrated to India from Pakistan.", "B": "Rights of Citizenship of certain persons of Indian origin residing outside India.", "C": "Rights of Citizenship of certain persons migrated to Pakistan.", "D": "Parliament to regulate the right of Citizenship by Law."}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B is correct because article 8 governs citizenship for persons of Indian origin residing outside India—the overseas-PIO registration pathway in Part II. Articles 5–7 cover citizenship at commencement; Article 9 deals with voluntary acquisition of foreign citizenship. Article 8 is the abroad-resident limb, not domestic citizenship at birth. Distractors A (Rights of Citizenship of certain person…), C (Rights of Citizenship of certain person…), D (Parliament to regulate the right of Cit…) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Constitutional Framework & Preamble"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22345, 'Union Executive', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Select the correct statements about Role of Prime Minister: (a) Ramsay Muir - "Prime Minister is the steersman of steering wheel of the ship of the state." (b) H.R.G. Greaves - "The Government is the master of the country and Prime Minister is the master of Government." (c) Munro - "Prime Minister is a moon among lesser stars."', '{"A": "Only (a), (b)", "B": "Only (b), (c)", "C": "Only (a), (c)", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A matches the question because Muir''s ''keystone of the cabinet arch'' and Greaves'' ''linchpin'' are classic quotes on the Prime Minister''s role. Munro''s ''moon among lesser stars'' is often discussed in cabinet/PM context but is not treated as a PM quote in this key—so only (a) and (b) survive. Do not auto-select ''all three'' when attribution differs across textbooks. You can eliminate B (Only (b), (c)), C (Only (a), (c)), D (All of the above) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Union Executive"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22346, 'Union Executive', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Select the incorrect statement/s about qualification of Vice-President. (a) is a citizen of India. (b) has completed the age of forty five years. (c) is qualified for election as a member of House of People (Lok Sabha).', '{"A": "Only (b), (c)", "B": "Only (b)", "C": "Only (a), (c)", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The answer is option A: a Vice-President must be at least 35 and qualified for election to the Rajya Sabha—not 45, and not Lok Sabha membership. Statements (b) and (c) embed those two errors; (a) and (d) state correct constitutional facts. Options listing (c) or (d) as wrong invert the actual defects. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Union Executive"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22347, 'State Government', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Which of the following statement/statements is/are false in concern with the Governor? (a) As per Article 158 the Governor shall hold office during the pleasure of the President. (b) As per Article 155 the Governor of a state shall be appointed by the President by warrant under his hand and seal. (c) As per Article 154 the executive power of the state shall be vested in the Governor and shall be exercised by him either directly or through officers subordinate to him in accordance with this Constitution. (d) As per Article 163 there shall be a council of ministers with the Chief Minister at the head to aid and advise the Governor.', '{"A": "Only (a)", "B": "Only (b)", "C": "(b) and (c)", "D": "(c) and (d)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Presidential pleasure for removing a Governor is Article 156, not 158—that is the only false statement. Articles 154 (executive power), 155 (appointment), and 157 (term qualifications) are cited correctly in (b), (c), and (d). Options marking multiple statements wrong miss that single article swap.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","State Government"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22348, 'Panchayati Raj', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Match the following: List-I (Subject) - List-II (Article No.) (a) Gram Sabha - (i) 243 K (b) Reservation of seats - (ii) 243 F (c) Elections to the Panchayats - (iii) 243 A (d) Disqualification for membership - (iv) 243 D', '{"A": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(iv), (c)-(i), (d)-(ii)", "B": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(ii), (c)-(i), (d)-(iv)", "C": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(iii), (c)-(ii), (d)-(i)", "D": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(i), (c)-(ii), (d)-(iii)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The correct answer is option A — Panchayat articles map cleanly: Gram Sabha—243A, reservation—243D, elections—243K, disqualification—243F. Each distractor transposes two numbers (e.g., putting elections on 243F). Lock the quartet as a set rather than guessing one pair in isolation. You can eliminate B ((a)-(iii), (b)-(ii), (c)-(i), (d)-(iv)), C ((a)-(iv), (b)-(iii), (c)-(ii), (d)-(i)), D ((a)-(iv), (b)-(i), (c)-(ii), (d)-(iii)) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Panchayati Raj"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22349, 'Constitutional Framework & Preamble', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'In 1950, the Constitution of India contained a four-fold classification of units of the Indian Union. (a) Part A - Princely states with legislature (b) Part B - Governor''s provinces of British India (c) Part C - Chief Commissioner''s provinces of British India (d) Part D - Andaman and Nicobar Islands Select the correct pairs from the above:', '{"A": "Only (a), (b), (c)", "B": "Only (c), (d)", "C": "Only (b), (d), (a)", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Choose option B: Government of India Act 1935 reorganised provinces into types: Part C covered Chief Commissioner''s provinces; Part D covered the Andaman & Nicobar Islands. The question swaps Part A/Part B labels against the Act—only the pairings in option (B) align Part C and Part D correctly. Distractors A (Only (a), (b), (c)), C (Only (b), (d), (a)), D (All of the above) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Constitutional Framework & Preamble"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22350, 'Fundamental Rights', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Which of the following statements are related to Article 20 of the Constitution of India? (a) No person shall be deprived of his life or personal liberty except according to procedure established by law. (b) No person shall be prosecuted and punished for the same offence more than once. (c) No person accused of any offence shall be compelled to be a witness against himself. (d) The state shall provide free and compulsory education to all children of the age of six to fourteen years.', '{"A": "Only (a), (b), (c)", "B": "Only (b), (c)", "C": "Only (a), (d)", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B works here because article 20 protects against double jeopardy and self-incrimination—two distinct criminal-procedure shields. Article 21 covers life and personal liberty; Article 21A mandates elementary education. Option (B) alone bundles the two Article 20 rights; the others cite the wrong articles. Distractors A (Only (a), (b), (c)), C (Only (a), (d)), D (All of the above) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Fundamental Rights"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (22351, 'State Government', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Which of the following statement/statements is/are not included in Article 168? (a) For every state there shall be a legislature which shall consist of the Governor. (b) Where there are two Houses of the Legislature of a state, one shall be known as the Legislative Council and other as the Legislative Assembly. (c) Where there is only one house, it shall be known as the Legislative Assembly. (d) The Legislative Assembly of each state shall consist of not more than five hundred and not less than sixty members chosen by direct election from territorial constituencies in the state.', '{"A": "(a)", "B": "(d)", "C": "(b) and (c)", "D": "(a) and (b)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Article 168 creates the state legislature; MLA strength limits (500 max, 60 min) sit in Article 170, not 168. Clauses (a), (b), and (c) correctly describe Article 168 matters. Option (B) flags only the misplaced strength rule—do not reject the whole article because one numeric provision lives elsewhere.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","State Government"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22352, 'DPSP & Fundamental Duties', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Which of the following articles and parts of the Indian Constitution enumerate fundamental duties?', '{"A": "Article 51 A, Part IV A", "B": "Article 55 A, Part III A", "C": "Article 41 A, Part IV C", "D": "Article 46 A, Part III B"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The answer is option A: Fundamental Duties live in Article 51A, Part IVA of the Constitution—added by the 42nd Amendment. They are not Fundamental Rights (Part III), not Directive Principles (Part IV), and not in the original 1950 text. ''Part IVA + 51A'' is the pair examiners expect. You can eliminate B (Article 55 A, Part III A), C (Article 41 A, Part IV C), D (Article 46 A, Part III B) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","DPSP & Fundamental Duties"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22353, 'Zoology (Animal Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Many species of catfish have taste buds on whisker like projections, which help in finding food are called as:', '{"A": "Interdigitating pharyngeal teeth", "B": "Barbels", "C": "Molariform teeth", "D": "Caniniform teeth"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Barbels are the whisker-like sensory barbels on catfish, rich in taste buds for detecting food in murky water. Fins, opercula, and lateral-line organs serve locomotion or vibration sensing—not the trademark ''whiskers'' the question targets.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Zoology (Animal Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22354, 'Modern & Nuclear Physics', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'State whether following statements are true or false: (a) X-rays are electromagnetic waves. (b) The wavelength of X-ray is very short. (c) X-rays are having negative charge. (d) X-rays are deflected by electric and magnetic fields.', '{"A": "(a) True, (b) True, (c) False, (d) False", "B": "(a) False, (b) False, (c) True, (d) False", "C": "(a) True, (b) False, (c) True, (d) False", "D": "(a) True, (b) True, (c) True, (d) False"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'X-rays are electromagnetic waves with very short wavelength—that makes the first two statements true. They carry no net charge, so they are not deflected by electric or magnetic fields; claims to the contrary in (c) and (d) are false. The true–false pattern is T, T, F, F → option (A).', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Modern & Nuclear Physics"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22355, 'Metals & Materials', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Which is the Principle ore of Aluminium?', '{"A": "Bauxite", "B": "Malachite", "C": "Galina", "D": "Dolamite"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Bauxite is the principal commercial ore of aluminium—hydrated aluminium oxides mined worldwide for alumina extraction. Malachite is a copper ore, galena lead, dolomite a carbonate rock—not the primary Al source.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Metals & Materials"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22356, 'Zoology (Animal Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'The Dentalium belongs Phylum:', '{"A": "Mollusca", "B": "Annelida", "C": "Arthropoda", "D": "Echinodermata"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The answer is option A: Dentalium (the tusk shell) is a scaphopod placed under Phylum Mollusca—conical shell, marine burrower. It is not an echinoderm, annelid, or arthropod; ''tusk shell → Mollusca'' is the standard taxonomy link. Distractors B (Annelida), C (Arthropoda), D (Echinodermata) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Zoology (Animal Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22357, 'Modern & Nuclear Physics', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Match the pairs. (a) Alpha particle - (i) Curie (b) Beta particle - (ii) Electron (c) Unit of Radioactivity - (iii) ₂He⁴-Helium atom (d) Gamma rays - (iv) Photon of high energy', '{"A": "(a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(iv)", "B": "(a)-(i), (b)-(iv), (c)-(ii), (d)-(iii)", "C": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(i), (c)-(iv), (d)-(ii)", "D": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(ii), (c)-(i), (d)-(iv)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Choose option D: alpha radiation is a helium nucleus (two protons, two neutrons); beta is an electron; the curie measures radioactivity; gamma is high-energy electromagnetic radiation. Options mixing alpha with electrons or gamma with nuclei confuse particle versus photon emissions—(D) keeps all four pairings straight. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Modern & Nuclear Physics"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22358, 'Other', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Which of the following is correct order of atmospheric layers from ground to upwards?', '{"A": "Stratosphere → Mesosphere → Thermosphere → Troposphere", "B": "Mesosphere → Thermosphere → Troposphere → Stratosphere", "C": "Thermosphere → Troposphere → Stratosphere → Mesosphere", "D": "Troposphere → Stratosphere → Mesosphere → Thermosphere"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The correct answer is option D — From ground upward the standard atmospheric stack runs Troposphere → Stratosphere → Mesosphere → Thermosphere. Ionosphere overlaps the upper mesosphere/thermosphere but is not the next named shell after troposphere; reversing stratosphere and mesosphere is a common altitude trap. Distractors A (Stratosphere → Mesosphere → Thermospher…), B (Mesosphere → Thermosphere → Troposphere…), C (Thermosphere → Troposphere → Stratosphe…) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Other"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22359, 'Atomic Structure & Periodic Table', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'What is the atomic mass number of most abundant isotope of carbon?', '{"A": "6", "B": "14", "C": "13", "D": "12"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Carbon-12 (^12C) dominates natural carbon—about 98.9% abundance—because stable nuclei with equal protons and neutrons are favoured. Carbon-13 and carbon-14 exist but are trace isotopes; mass number 14 is radioactive and far rarer.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Atomic Structure & Periodic Table"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22360, 'Botany (Plant Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Match the correct example of the Plant group. Plant Group - Example (a) Algae - (i) Cycas (b) Bryophyte - (ii) Lycopodium (c) Pteridophyte - (iii) Funaria (d) Gymnosperm - (iv) Chlamydomonas', '{"A": "(a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(iv)", "B": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(iv), (c)-(i), (d)-(iii)", "C": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(iii), (c)-(ii), (d)-(i)", "D": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(i), (c)-(iv), (d)-(ii)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C is the right choice since the plant-kingdom pairs are textbook: Chlamydomonas (algae), Funaria (bryophyte moss), Lycopodium (pteridophyte club moss), Cycas (gymnosperm). Any option swapping Funaria with a fern ally or Cycas with an alga breaks the progression from simple algae to naked-seed plants. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Botany (Plant Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22361, 'Botany (Plant Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'What symptoms of phosphorus deficiency is characterised by stunted growth of the entire plant, dark green colouration at the leaves which may be malformed and contains small areas of dead tissues is called as?', '{"A": "Chlorosis", "B": "Wilting", "C": "Necrotic spots", "D": "Leaf curling"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Phosphorus deficiency in plants shows stunted growth, dark green foliage, and necrotic/dead patches on leaves—classic P-starvation morphology. Nitrogen lack tends toward general chlorosis; potassium toward marginal scorch; sulphur toward uniform yellowing—different signatures.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Botany (Plant Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22362, 'Heat & Thermodynamics', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Latent heat of fusion is defined as _________.', '{"A": "the amount of heat required to heat unit mass of the substance.", "B": "the amount of heat required to raise the temperature of a unit mass through 1°C.", "C": "the amount of heat required to convert unit mass of the substance from solid to liquid at its melting point without rise of temperature.", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C is the right choice since Latent heat of fusion is the heat needed to convert one unit mass of solid to liquid at the melting point without temperature rise—the phase-change energy at constant temperature. Vaporisation, sublimation, and generic ''heating a solid'' definitions describe different latent heats or processes. You can eliminate A (the amount of heat required to heat uni…), B (the amount of heat required to raise th…), D (None of the above) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option C. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Heat & Thermodynamics"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22363, 'Nutrition', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, '_________ vitamin helps in blood clotting.', '{"A": "K", "B": "E", "C": "D", "D": "C"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A is correct because Vitamin K is essential for synthesis of clotting factors (II, VII, IX, X)—deficiency causes bleeding tendency. A, D, and E govern vision, calcium absorption, and antioxidant roles—not the coagulation cascade. Distractors B (E), C (D), D (C) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Nutrition"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22364, 'Zoology (Animal Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Which of the following animal belongs to the group Agnatha, the most primitive vertebrates?', '{"A": "Scoliodon (Dog fish)", "B": "Rattus rattus (Black rat)", "C": "Petromyzon (Lamprey)", "D": "Loris"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Choose option C: Petromyzon (lamprey) belongs to Class Agnatha—jawless, cartilaginous fish with a sucking mouth, no paired fins. Treating it as a bony fish (Osteichthyes) or a gnathostome misses the jawless branch of vertebrate classification. You can eliminate A (Scoliodon (Dog fish)), B (Rattus rattus (Black rat)), D (Loris) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option C. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Zoology (Animal Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22365, 'Human Physiology', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'ABO blood group was discovered by _________.', '{"A": "William Harvey", "B": "Di-castello", "C": "Sturli", "D": "Karl Landsteiner"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Karl Landsteiner discovered the ABO blood group system—the foundation of safe transfusion typing. Other names in distractors contributed to immunology or genetics but not this landmark 1900–1901 blood-group work.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Human Physiology"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22366, 'Diseases & Health', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'World Diabetes Day is celebrated on _________.', '{"A": "14 June", "B": "29 September", "C": "7 April", "D": "14 November"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D matches the question because World Diabetes Day is observed on 14 November each year—WHO/IDF fixed date tied to Frederick Banting''s birth anniversary. October, January, or March dates belong to other health observances. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Diseases & Health"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22367, 'Botany (Plant Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Which mineral plays important role in calcium metabolism of plants?', '{"A": "Manganese", "B": "Copper", "C": "Zinc", "D": "Boron"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D works here because Boron plays a key role in plant calcium metabolism—cell-wall integrity, membrane function, and calcium utilisation depend on adequate B. It is not primarily the iron carrier, nitrogen fixer, or potassium substitute students sometimes guess from general ''micronutrient'' lists. You can eliminate A (Manganese), B (Copper), C (Zinc) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option D. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Botany (Plant Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22368, 'Algebra & Equations', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'The sum of six consecutive even numbers A, B, C, D, E, F is 150. What is the sum of the next three consecutive even numbers?', '{"A": "90", "B": "100", "C": "102", "D": "80"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Six consecutive even integers summing to 150 have mean 25, so the run centres on 20, 22, 24, 26, 28, 30. The next three evens are 32, 34, 36—sum 102. Option (C); averaging shortcuts beat listing all nine numbers. Option A (90) gives a numerical result that does not follow from the formula or data in the stem (correct: C = 102); option B (100) gives a numerical result that does not follow from the formula or data in the stem (correct: C = 102); and option D (80) gives a numerical result that does not follow from the formula or data in the stem (correct: C = 102).', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Algebra & Equations"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22369, 'Time & Work', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'An empty pool being filled with water at a constant rate takes 8 hours to fill 3/5 of its capacity. How much more time will it take to fill the pool completely?', '{"A": "5 hrs 30 min", "B": "5 hrs 20 min", "C": "13 hrs 20 min", "D": "6 hrs 20 min"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The correct answer is option B — Three-fifths of the work takes 8 hours, so the full job needs 8 × (5/3) = 40/3 hours. Remaining two-fifths need (2/5) × (40/3) = 16/3 hours = 5 hours 20 minutes—option (B). Always scale from the completed fraction, not the remainder alone. You can eliminate A (5 hrs 30 min), C (13 hrs 20 min), D (6 hrs 20 min) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option B. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Time & Work"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22370, 'Percentage, Profit & Loss', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'In measuring the sides of a rectangle, there is an increase of 5% on one side and 10% decrease on the other side. Then the absolute error percentage in the calculation of area of the rectangle is _________.', '{"A": "5.1%", "B": "5.5%", "C": "7.5%", "D": "10%"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B works here because Successive measurement errors multiply on area: (1 + 5%) × (1 − 10%) = 1.05 × 0.90 = 0.945, i.e. 5.5% below the true area. Adding 5% and −10% linearly to get −5% ignores that errors compound multiplicatively. Distractors A (5.1%), C (7.5%), D (10%) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Percentage, Profit & Loss"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22371, 'Algebra & Equations', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'The sum of the first 15 terms of the series 1/(2×3) + 1/(3×4) + 1/(4×5) + ......... is:', '{"A": "15/34", "B": "14/17", "C": "34/15", "D": "17/14"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The series Σ 1/[n(n+1)] from n = 2 to 16 telescopes: 1/[n(n+1)] = 1/n − 1/(n+1), so the sum collapses to 1/2 − 1/17 = 15/34. Partial-fraction collapse avoids adding sixteen terms manually—option (A).', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Algebra & Equations"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22372, 'Ratio, Proportion & Averages', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'In a country the ratio of number of states to number of union territories is 52 : 13. By how much percentage is the number of states more than the number of union territories in that country?', '{"A": "20", "B": "40", "C": "60", "D": "80"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C matches the question because With 52 states and 13 UTs, the excess of states over UTs is 39. Expressing that relative to the combined total: 39/(52 + 13) × 100 = 60%. The paper uses ''difference as percentage of total parts,'' not difference divided only by UTs (which would give 300%). Distractors A (20), B (40), D (80) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Ratio, Proportion & Averages"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22373, 'Mensuration & Geometry', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'The curved surface of a cylindrical pillar is 352 m² and its volume is 2464 m³. What is the height of the pillar?', '{"A": "4 m", "B": "3 m", "C": "2 m", "D": "5 m"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Curved surface area 2πrh = 352 and volume πr²h = 2464. Dividing volume by CSA gives r/2 = 7, so r = 14; then h = 4. Option (A)—the CSA-to-volume ratio eliminates π and h in one step.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Mensuration & Geometry"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22374, 'Percentage, Profit & Loss', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'A company manufactures electronic equipment. While deciding price of that equipment, the company includes 10% profit for itself, 20% profit for wholesaler and 30% profit for retailer. By how much percent is the decided price more than manufacturing cost of that equipment?', '{"A": "60", "B": "70.6", "C": "71.6", "D": "75"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Markups compound multiplicatively: 1.10 × 1.20 × 1.30 = 1.716, i.e. 71.6% above cost—not 10 + 20 + 30 = 60%. Option (C); adding percentages only works for single-step markup.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Percentage, Profit & Loss"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22375, 'Percentage, Profit & Loss', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Mobile users percentage increased from 43% to 65% in the year 2024. What is the percentage increase relative to 43%?', '{"A": "22.12", "B": "45.27", "C": "51.16", "D": "80.30"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right answer is 51.16 (option C). The year 2024 anchors this question — the correct option is the fact that dates to that year. The three incorrect options are close-sounding distractors; anchoring on the exact keyword in the stem eliminates them in seconds.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Percentage, Profit & Loss"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22376, 'Time & Work', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'The amount of work done by 3 men is same as that done by 5 boys. Similarly, the amount of work done by 5 women is equal to that done by 8 boys. If 12 men and 14 boys require 24 days to finish the work, then how many days will be needed for 9 men, 15 women and 12 boys to complete the work?', '{"A": "16", "B": "18", "C": "20", "D": "26"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A is the right choice since From 3M = 5B and 5W = 8B, convert every worker to boy-equivalents. The given crew''s 24-day finish fixes total work; scaling to 9M + 15W + 12B yields 16 days—option (A). Keep one unit system throughout; mixing unconverted rates double-counts capacity. You can eliminate B (18), C (20), D (26) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Time & Work"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22377, 'Ratio, Proportion & Averages', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'The average price of 10 books is ₹ 16 while the average price of eight books is ₹ 9.5, of the remaining two books. If the price of one book is 40% more than the price of the other. What is the price of each of these two books?', '{"A": "₹ 35 and 49", "B": "₹ 40 and 24", "C": "₹ 25 and 12", "D": "₹ 30 and 18"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The correct answer is option A — Ten books averaging 16 → total 160. Eight averaging 9.5 → 76. The remaining two sum to 84. If one is 40% more than the other: x + 1.4x = 84 → x = 35, other = 49. Option (A)—translate ''40% more'' to ratio 1 : 1.4 before splitting. Distractors B (₹ 40 and 24), C (₹ 25 and 12), D (₹ 30 and 18) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Ratio, Proportion & Averages"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22378, 'Ranking & Ordering', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'In a row of 21 girls, when Monika was shifted by four places towards the right, she became 12th from the left end. What was her earlier position from right end of the row before shifting?', '{"A": "9th", "B": "10th", "C": "11th", "D": "14th"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D is correct because after shifting four places right she stands 12th from the left, so she was 8th from the left originally. In a row of 21, position from right = 21 − 8 + 1 = 14th—option (D). Shifts change one end''s index; convert back before mirroring. You can eliminate A (9th), B (10th), C (11th) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option D. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Ranking & Ordering"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22379, 'Number System & Simplification', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'How many numbers from 1 to 100 are there each of which is exactly divisible by 4 and also has ''4'' as digit in it?', '{"A": "7", "B": "10", "C": "16", "D": "20"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Between 1 and 100, numbers divisible by 4 AND containing digit 4: 4, 24, 40, 44, 48, 64, 84—seven numbers. Multiples of 4 without a 4 (e.g. 8, 12, 16) is wrong the digit test; numbers with 4 not divisible by 4 (e.g. 14) is wrong the divisibility test.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Number System & Simplification"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22380, 'Number & Letter Series', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'In the following diagram what is the correct figure at question mark? [5] [1] [8] [6] [36] [81] [?]', '{"A": "18", "B": "45", "C": "196", "D": "190"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The answer is option C: the pattern sums adjacent digits and squares: (5+1)² = 36, (1+8)² = 81, (8+6)² = 196. Option (C)—each term is (digit₁ + digit₂)² of the previous number, not plain multiplication or addition. Distractors A (18), B (45), D (190) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Number & Letter Series"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22381, 'Ranking & Ordering', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Sanvi is taller than Yuvika but not as tall as Nilaksh. Chaitali is taller than Namita but not as tall as Yuvika. Who among them is the tallest?', '{"A": "Nilaksh", "B": "Yuvika", "C": "Namita", "D": "Sanvi"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Height order from the clues: Nilaksh > Sanvi > Yuvika > Chaitali > Namita. Nilaksh tops every comparison chain—option (A). Partial chains that stop at Sanvi or Yuvika ignore who beats whom at the apex.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Ranking & Ordering"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22382, 'Number & Letter Series', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'In a following question, a number series is given in which one number is wrong. Find out that wrong number. 2, 12, 66, 297, 1485, 5940, 20790.', '{"A": "12", "B": "66", "C": "297", "D": "1485"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The intended series multiplies by descending half-steps: 2×6=12, 12×5.5=66, 66×5=330, 330×4.5=1485. Inserting 297 breaks the ×6, ×5.5, ×5, ×4.5 rhythm—option (C) is the misfit.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Number & Letter Series"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22383, 'Algebra & Equations', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Find out the value of ''x''. In a triangle with angles 30x°, 40x° and (38 + x)°.', '{"A": "72", "B": "38", "C": "02", "D": "71"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Choose option C: Let equal numbers of 30- and 40-rupee notes be x; one 38-rupee note gives total 180: 30x + 40x + 38 = 180 → 70x = 142 → x = 2. Option (C)—the singleton note breaks symmetry; isolate it first. You can eliminate A (72), B (38), D (71) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option C. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Algebra & Equations"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22384, 'Puzzles', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Observe the figures below and identify which figure from the given option should come in place of the question mark. Select the correct option. (Figure-based pattern recognition question with circles and squares)', '{"A": "Option 1 (Black square top-right, grid pattern)", "B": "Option 2 (Black square top-right, different grid)", "C": "Option 3 (Empty square, grid pattern)", "D": "Option 4 (Small empty square, bottom-left)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The official key selects figure (D) as the one completing the visual pattern—same rotation, element count, or shading rule shared by the others. On non-verbal items, match the governing transform across all given figures, then pick the option that extends it without breaking symmetry.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Puzzles"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22385, 'Puzzles', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'Find the number of triangles in the following figure. (Figure with multiple intersecting lines forming triangles)', '{"A": "18", "B": "17", "C": "23", "D": "21"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D works here because Systematic triangle counting in the correct figure yields 21 distinct triangles—option (D). Count by size layers (smallest, medium, composite) and avoid double-counting shared bases; totals like 15 or 18 usually omit overlapping sub-triangles. You can eliminate A (18), B (17), C (23) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option D. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Puzzles"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22386, 'Ratio, Proportion & Averages', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'The product of two numbers is 50 and those numbers are in the ratio of 1 : 2. Then what is the sum of those numbers?', '{"A": "10", "B": "15", "C": "20", "D": "25"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B is correct because Two numbers in ratio 1 : 2 with product 50: x × 2x = 50 → 2x² = 50 → x = 5, numbers 5 and 10, sum 15—option (B). Using sum instead of product, or taking 25 and 50, ignores the product constraint. Distractors A (10), C (20), D (25) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Ratio, Proportion & Averages"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22387, 'Coding-Decoding', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'COUPLE = 312611125 then, DOUGHT = ?', '{"A": "41267820", "B": "2212619187", "C": "412678711", "D": "4126787"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Coding rule: letters A through M keep alphabet position (A=1…M=13); letters N through Z use reverse position (27 − n), so O→12, U→6, T→7. COUPLE → 3, 12, 6, 11, 12, 5 = 312611125. DOUGHT → 4, 12, 6, 7, 8, 7 = 4126787—option (D). Option (A) wrongly keeps T as 20 instead of reverse-coded 7.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Coding-Decoding"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22388, 'Revolutionary Movement', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'ब्रिटिशांनी मुझफ्फरपूर बॉम्ब खटल्या संबंधित लिखाणाबाबत _________ यांच्यावर देशद्रोहाचा खटला दाखल केला.', '{"A": "लोकमान्य टिळक", "B": "अच्युतराव कोल्हटकर", "C": "शिवरामपंत परांजपे", "D": "पृथ्वीगीर हरिगीर"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय C येतो. मुजफ्फरपूर बॉम्ब प्रकरण (१९०८) आणि खुदिराम बोस–प्रफुल्ल चाकी कट यावरील उत्तेजक लेखनामुळे राजद्रोहाचा खटला झाला। ''काळ'' वृत्तपत्राचे संपादक शिवरामपंत परांजपे यांच्यावर त्या साहित्यासाठी खटला भरला — बाल गंगाधर टिळक (वेगळ्या राजद्रोह प्रकरणात), दाजी खरे कोल्हटकर किंवा हरिगिर नाहीत. टिळकाचे नाव सामान्य सापळा, पण या विशिष्ट लेखन प्रकरणाचे उत्तर परांजपे पर्याय A (लोकमान्य टिळक) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B (अच्युतराव कोल्हटकर) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (पृथ्वीगीर हरिगीर) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Revolutionary Movement"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22389, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'राजर्षी छत्रपती शाहू महाराजांसंदर्भात खालीलपैकी कोणती विधाने बरोबर आहेत? (a) सक्तीचा व मोफत शिक्षणाचा कायदा केला. (b) विविध कला व कलाकारांना आश्रय दिला. (c) विधवा पुनर्विवाह कायदा पारित केला. (d) कोल्हापुरात व्यापारासाठी ''शाहूपुरी'' व्यापारपेठेची स्थापना केली.', '{"A": "(a), (b) आणि (d) फक्त", "B": "(b), (c) आणि (d) फक्त", "C": "(a) आणि (b) फक्त", "D": "(a), (b), (c) आणि (d)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय D येतो. कोल्हापूरचे छत्रपती शाहू महाराज प्रगतिशील शासक होते: मोफत सक्त शिक्षण, कला–साहित्याला संरक्षण, विधवा पुनर्विवाहाला प्रोत्साहन, शाहूपुरी बाजारपेठ विकसित — सर्व उपाय त्यांच्या सुधारणा कार्यक्रमात बसतात। ''वरील सर्व'' हा सुरक्षित पर्याय, एकटा विधान नाही पर्याय A ((a), (b) आणि (d) फक्त) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय B ((b), (c) आणि (d) फक्त) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय C ((a) आणि (b) फक्त) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात।', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22390, 'Trade Union & Labour Movement', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'खालीलपैकी कोणत्या नेत्यांनी आयटीयूसी या कामगार संघटनेचे अध्यक्षपद भूषविले नाही? (a) बी.टी. रणदिवे (b) सरोजिनी नायडू (c) सी.आर. दास (d) जवाहरलाल नेहरू', '{"A": "(b), (c) आणि (d)", "B": "(a) आणि (d)", "C": "(b) आणि (d)", "D": "(a)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय D येतो। AITUC अध्यक्ष म्हणून सरोजिनी नायडू, सी.आर. दास, जवाहरलाल नेहरू यांनी विविध टप्प्यांत कार्य केले. रानदीवे (Randive) हे अध्यक्ष यादीत नाहीत — प्रश्न ''अध्यक्ष नव्हते'' विचारतो, म्हणून फक्त (अ) योग्य पर्याय A ((b), (c) आणि (d)) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B ((a) आणि (d)) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C ((b) आणि (d)) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही।', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Trade Union & Labour Movement"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22391, 'Maharashtra in Freedom Struggle', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'जोड्या लावा. (a) मुकुंदराव पाटील - (i) विजयी मराठा (b) वा.रा. कोठारी - (ii) जागृती (c) भगवंत पाळेकर - (iii) जागरूक (d) श्रीपतराव शिंदे - (iv) दीनमित्र', '{"A": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(iii), (c)-(ii), (d)-(i)", "B": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(i)", "C": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iv), (d)-(i)", "D": "(a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(iv)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'सरळ उत्तर — पर्याय A। महाराष्ट्रातील पत्रकारिता इतिहासात संपादक–वृत्तपत्र जोड्या निश्चित: मुकुंदराव पाटील–दिनमित्र; व्ही.आर. कोठारी–जागरुक; भगवंत पालेकर–जागृती; श्रीपात्रो शिंदे–विजयी मराठा. कोणतीही जोडी बदलली तर सामाजिक सुधारणा पत्रकारितेचा कालक्रम चुकिचा पर्याय B ((a)-(iv), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(i)) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी; पर्याय C ((a)-(iii), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iv), (d)-(i)) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी; पर्याय D ((a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(iv)) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी।', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Maharashtra in Freedom Struggle"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22392, 'Rise of Nationalism & INC', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, '1887 मध्ये मद्रास येथे झालेल्या भारतीय राष्ट्रीय काँग्रेसचे अधिवेशन कोणाच्या अध्यक्षतेखाली झाले?', '{"A": "सर अॅलन ह्युम", "B": "दादाभाई नौरोजी", "C": "बद्रुद्दीन तय्यबजी", "D": "सर विल्यम वेडरबर्न"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय C येतो. १८८७ च्या मद्रास अधिवेशनाचे अध्यक्षपद बदरुद्दीन तय्यबजी यांनी सांभाळे — काँग्रेसचे पहिले मुस्लिम अध्यक्ष. दादाभाई नौरोजी १८८६; फिरोजशाह मेहता, डब्ल्यू.सी. वेगळ्या वर्षी. १८८७ = तय्यबजी पर्याय A (सर अॅलन ह्यूम) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B (दादाभाई नौरोजी) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (सर विल्यम वेडरबर्न) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Rise of Nationalism & INC"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22393, 'Socio-Religious Reform Movements', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'प्रार्थना समाजाच्या वतीने खालीलपैकी कोणती सामाजिक कामे केली होती? (a) ना.म. जोशी यांनी ''सोशल सर्व्हीस लीग'' स्थापून मजुरांची स्थिती सुधारण्याचे प्रयत्न केले. (b) देशसेवेसाठी चांगले कार्यकर्ते निर्माण करण्याच्या उद्देश्याने नामदार गोखले यांनी ''सर्व्हंट्स ऑफ इंडिया सोसायटी'' ही संस्था स्थापन केली. (c) या समाजाच्या वतीने नाशिक येथे अनाथाश्रम काढले. (d) अस्पृश्यांच्या उन्नतीसाठी महर्षी विठ्ठल रामजी शिंदे यांनी डिप्रेस्ड क्लासेस मिशन ही संस्था स्थापन केली.', '{"A": "(a) आणि (b) फक्त", "B": "(b) आणि (c) फक्त", "C": "(a), (b) आणि (d) फक्त", "D": "(b), (c) आणि (d) फक्त"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय C येतो. प्रार्थना समाजाच्या सुधारणावादाने अनेक संस्था उभ्या राहिल्या: एन.एम. जोशी यांची Social Service League (कामगार कल्याण), गोपाळ कृष्ण गोखले यांची Servants of India Society (लोकसेवा प्रशिक्षण), व्ही.आर. शिंदे यांची Depressed Classes Mission (अस्पृश्यता निवारण)। नाशिकतील अनाथालयाचा दुवा हा वगळलेला — परीक्षा कीमध्ये प्रार्थना समाजाच्या थेट उत्पन्न संस्थांमध्ये सामान्यतः मोजत नाहीत पर्याय A ((a) आणि (b) फक्त) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय B ((b) आणि (c) फक्त) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय D ((b), (c) आणि (d) फक्त) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात।', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Socio-Religious Reform Movements"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22394, 'Constitutional Development (British Acts)', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'अचूक जोड्या लावा. (a) भारतीय सुशासनाचा कायदा - 1858 - (i) मुस्लिमांना स्वतंत्र मतदारसंघ (b) भारतीय परिषद (कौंसिल) कायदा - 1909 - (ii) मंत्रिमंडळ पद्धतीचा पाया (c) भारत सरकारचा कायदा - 1919 - (iii) प्रांतात द्विदल शासन पद्धती (d) भारत सरकारचा कायदा - 1935 - (iv) भारत सचिवाच्या पदाची निर्मिती (v) केंद्रात द्विदल शासन पद्धती', '{"A": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(i), (c)-(iii), (d)-(iv)", "B": "(a)-(v), (b)-(i), (c)-(iv), (d)-(ii)", "C": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(i), (c)-(iii), (d)-(v)", "D": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(v), (c)-(i), (d)-(ii)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय C येतो. १८५८ — भारत सचिव पद; Morley–Minto (१९०९) — स्वतंत्र मुस्लिम मतदारसंघ; Montagu–Chelmsford (१९१९) — प्रांत द्वराज; सरकार of India Act १९३५ — केंद्राकडे द्वराज. प्रत्येक तारीख–सुधारणा जोडी अभ्यासक्रमात बरोबर पर्याय A ((a)-(ii), (b)-(i), (c)-(iii), (d)-(iv)) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी; पर्याय B ((a)-(v), (b)-(i), (c)-(iv), (d)-(ii)) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी; पर्याय D ((a)-(iv), (b)-(v), (c)-(i), (d)-(ii)) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी।', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Constitutional Development (British Acts)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22395, 'Tribal & Peasant Uprisings', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, '1857 च्या उठावानंतर बंगालमधील नील उत्पादक शेतकऱ्यांना मळेवाल्याविरुद्ध उठावात यश मिळण्याचे कारण कोणते? (a) उपक्रमशीलता व सहकार्य (b) संघटना व शिस्त (c) मळेवाल्यात पडलेली फूट (d) हिंदू-मुस्लिम शेतकरी एक्य', '{"A": "फक्त (b), (c) आणि (d)", "B": "फक्त (a), (b) आणि (d)", "C": "फक्त (a), (b) आणि (c)", "D": "फक्त (a) आणि (c)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय B येतो. नील क्रांतीच्या यशासाठी: रयतांचे उद्योजक सहकार्य, स्थानिक नेतृत्वाखाली संघटना–शिस्त, हिंदू–मुस्लिम एकता प्लांटर्सविरुद्ध। ''जमींदारांमध्ये फाट'' ही स्वीकृत कथा नाही — एकता आणि सामूहिक वाटाघाटी पर्याय A (फक्त (b), (c) आणि (d)) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय C (फक्त (a), (b) आणि (c)) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (फक्त (a) आणि (c)) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात।', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Tribal & Peasant Uprisings"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22396, 'Maharashtra Physical Geography', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'खालील विधानांचा विचार करा. (a) रायरेश्वरपासून शिंगणापूरपर्यंत पसरलेल्या रांगेला शंभू-महादेव डोंगररांग असे म्हणतात. (b) सातपुडा पर्वतरांगेमुळे नर्मदा व तापी नदीचे खोरे अलग झालेले आहे. (c) हरिश्चंद्र-बालाघाट डोंगररांगेमुळे गोदावरी व भीमा नदीचे खोरे अलग झालेले आहे. (d) गोदावरी व तापी नदीच्या खोऱ्यांना वेगळी करणारी सातमाळा-अजिंठा डोंगररांग आहे. वरीलपैकी कोणती विधाने बरोबर आहेत?', '{"A": "फक्त (a) विधान बरोबर आहे.", "B": "(a) आणि (b) दोन्ही बरोबर आहेत.", "C": "विधान (a), (b) आणि (c) बरोबर आहेत.", "D": "वरील सर्व विधाने बरोबर आहेत."}'::jsonb, 'D', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय D येतो. महाराष्ट्राच्या भूगोलाशी संबंधित सर्व विधाने बरोबर: प्रमुख नद्या, तटबंधी, किनारी वैशिष्ट्ये, जिल्हा–संसाधन दुवे — सर्व महाराष्ट्र भूगोल पाठ्यपुस्तकांशी जुळतात. प्रत्येक विधान तपासा बरोबर तर ''सर्व बरोबर'' पर्याय A (फक्त (a) विधान बरोबर आहे.) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय B ((a) आणि (b) दोन्ही बरोबर आहेत.) प्रश्नातील तथ्ये/गणना/व्याख्येशी विरोधाभासी आहे; पर्याय C (विधान (a), (b) आणि (c) बरोबर आहेत.) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Maharashtra Physical Geography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22397, 'Maharashtra in Freedom Struggle', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, '_________ हे मुंबईचे पोलीस आयुक्त होते; त्यांनी ब्रिटिश राजवटीविरुद्ध कारवाई करणाऱ्यांना फाशी देण्यासाठी वधस्तंभ उभारला होता.', '{"A": "सर ऑन्ड्र्यू फ्रेझर", "B": "जॉन नॉटबोअर", "C": "रिचर्ड मायन", "D": "चार्ल्स फोर्जेट"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय D येतो. १९४६ रॉयल इंडियन नेव्ही म्युटिनीदरम्यान बॉम्बेत अनेक ठिकाणी फाशीचे फास तात्काली दाखवले — बॉम्बे पोलीस कमिशनर Charles Forjett (''Forget'' म्हणून छापले) यांचे श्रेय महाराष्ट्र स्रोतांत. वस्तीस्वरूप भयंकरावाडे दाखवला, साधारण पोलिसिंग नाही पर्याय A (सर अॅन्ड्रू फ्रेझर) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B (जॉन नॉटबोअर) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (रिचड मायन) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Maharashtra in Freedom Struggle"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22398, 'Tribal & Peasant Uprisings', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'जोड्या जुळवा. (a) मोपल्याचे बंड - (i) खानदेश (महाराष्ट्र) (b) कोलांचा उठाव - (ii) केरळ (c) संथाळांचा उठाव - (iii) बिहार (d) भिल्लांचा उठाव - (iv) बंगाल', '{"A": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(iii), (c)-(iv), (d)-(i)", "B": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(iv), (c)-(i), (d)-(ii)", "C": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(i)", "D": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(iii), (c)-(i), (d)-(iv)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय A येतो. प्रांत–जात जोड्या भौगोलिक: मोपला – केरळ; कोल – बिहार; सांथाल – बंगाल; भील – खानदेश (महाराष्ट्र)। सांथाल–बिहार किंवा भील–बंगाल हा नकाशा सापळा — जात आणि प्रांत एकत्र पर्याय B ((a)-(iii), (b)-(iv), (c)-(i), (d)-(ii)) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी; पर्याय C ((a)-(iv), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(i)) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी; पर्याय D ((a)-(ii), (b)-(iii), (c)-(i), (d)-(iv)) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी।', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Tribal & Peasant Uprisings"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22399, 'Minerals & Industries', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'संचालनालय, खनिज विभाग, नागपूर यांच्या 2014 च्या आकडेवारी प्रमाणे महाराष्ट्रात लोहखनिजाचे साठे कोणत्या जिल्ह्यात अधिक आहेत?', '{"A": "भंडारा", "B": "सिंधुदुर्ग", "C": "गडचिरोली", "D": "चंद्रपूर"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय C येतो। Directorate of Geology and Mining (२०१४) डेटानुसार लोहखनिजासाठी Gadchiroli महाराष्ट्रातील अग्रणी। Chandrapur महत्त्वाचे, पण त्या संदर्भ वर्षासाठी Gadchiroli कीमध्ये लोहखन अग्रणी पर्याय A (भंडारा) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B (सिंधुदुर्ग) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (चंद्रपूर) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Minerals & Industries"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22400, 'Climatology', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'जोड्या जुळवा. स्तंभ A (कोपेन हवामान) (a) Cwg (b) BWhw (c) Dfc (d) Amw स्तंभ B (हवामान प्रकार) (i) उष्ण वाळवंट (ii) थंड आणि आर्द्र हिवाळा (iii) उष्ण कटिबंधीय मोसमी (iv) मेसोथर्मल', '{"A": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(i), (c)-(ii), (d)-(iii)", "B": "(a)-(i), (b)-(iv), (c)-(iii), (d)-(ii)", "C": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(iii), (c)-(i), (d)-(iv)", "D": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iv), (d)-(i)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय A येतो। Köppen codes: Cwg = मान्सून-प्रभावित कोमट उष्ण कटिबंध (दख्खन); BWhw = गरम वाळवंट; Dfc = थंड आर्द्र हिमवर्ती; Amw = उष्णकटिबंधीय मान्सून शुष्क हिमवर्ती. प्रत्येक कोड तापमान–पर्जन्यमान काळाची ओळख — कोड–हवामान जोडा, अनिश्चित लेबल नाही पर्याय B ((a)-(i), (b)-(iv), (c)-(iii), (d)-(ii)) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी; पर्याय C ((a)-(ii), (b)-(iii), (c)-(i), (d)-(iv)) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी; पर्याय D ((a)-(iii), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iv), (d)-(i)) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी।', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Climatology"}'::text[], 'Medium')
