VALUES
  (22451, 'State Government', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'खालीलपैकी कोणते विधान/विधाने कलम 168 मध्ये समाविष्ट नाही/नाहीत? (a) प्रत्येक राज्यासाठी एक कायदेमंडळ असेल ज्यामध्ये राज्यपाल असतील. (b) जिथे राज्याच्या कायदेमंडळाची दोन सभागृहे असतील, तिथे एक विधान परिषद आणि दुसरे विधानसभा म्हणून ओळखले जाईल. (c) जिथे फक्त एकच सभागृह असेल, तेथे ते विधानसभा म्हणून ओळखले जाईल. (d) प्रत्येक राज्याच्या विधानसभेत राज्यातील प्रादेशिक मतदारसंघांमधून थेट निवडणुकीद्वारे निवडलेले पाचशेपेक्षा जास्त आणि साठपेक्षा कमी नसलेले सदस्य असतील.', '{"A": "(a)", "B": "(d)", "C": "(b) आणि (c)", "D": "(a) आणि (b)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय B येतो. कलम १६८ राज्य विधानमंडळ स्थापन करते; MLA संख्या मर्यादा (कमाल ५००, किमान ६०) कलम १७० मध्ये, १६८ मध्ये नाही। (a)(b)(c) १६८ बाबत बरोबर; पर्याय (B) फक्त चुकीची संख्या-तरतूद दर्शवतो पर्याय A ((a)) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C ((b) and (c)) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D ((a) and (b)) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","State Government"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22452, 'DPSP & Fundamental Duties', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'भारतीय संविधानाच्या खालीलपैकी कोणत्या कलमात आणि भागात मूलभूत कर्तव्ये समाविष्ट आहेत?', '{"A": "कलम 51 A, भाग IV A", "B": "कलम 55 A, भाग III A", "C": "कलम 41 A, भाग IV C", "D": "कलम 46 A, भाग III B"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'सरळ उत्तर — पर्याय A। मूलभूत कर्तव्ये कलम ५१अ, भाग IVA — ४२ वी दुरुस्ती. मूलभूत हक्क (III), मार्गदर्शक तत्त्वे (IV) नाहीत; १९५० मूळ मजकुरात नव्हते। ''भाग IVA + ५१अ'' ही परीक्षेत अपेक्षित जोडी पर्याय B (Article 55 A, Part III A) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (Article 41 A, Part IV C) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (Article 46 A, Part III B) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","DPSP & Fundamental Duties"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22453, 'Modern & Nuclear Physics', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'खालील विधाने बरोबर की चूक ते सांगा. (a) क्ष-किरण या विद्युत चुंबकीय लहरी आहेत. (b) क्ष-किरणांची तरंगलांबी खूप कमी असते. (c) क्ष-किरणांवर ऋण भार असतो. (d) क्ष-किरण विद्युत आणि चुंबकीय क्षेत्रामुळे विचलित होतात.', '{"A": "(a) बरोबर, (b) बरोबर, (c) चूक, (d) चूक", "B": "(a) चूक, (b) चूक, (c) बरोबर, (d) चूक", "C": "(a) बरोबर, (b) चूक, (c) बरोबर, (d) चूक", "D": "(a) बरोबर, (b) बरोबर, (c) बरोबर, (d) चूक"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'विज्ञानात हे स्थिर — X-किरणे विद्युतचुंबकीय तरंग, अतिशय लहान तरंगलांबी — (a)(b) खरे. निव्वळ विद्युभार नसल्याने विद्युत/चुंबकीय क्षेत्रात वाकत नाहीत — (c)(d) खोटे। T,T,F,F → पर्याय (A) पर्याय B ((a) False, (b) False, (c) True, (d) Fal…) प्रश्नातील तथ्ये/गणना/व्याख्येशी विरोधाभासी आहे; पर्याय C ((a) True, (b) False, (c) True, (d) False) प्रश्नातील तथ्ये/गणना/व्याख्येशी विरोधाभासी आहे; पर्याय D ((a) True, (b) True, (c) True, (d) False) प्रश्नातील तथ्ये/गणना/व्याख्येशी विरोधाभासी आहे।', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Modern & Nuclear Physics"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22454, 'Heat & Thermodynamics', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'अप्रकट विलयन उष्मा म्हणजे _________.', '{"A": "पदार्थाच्या एकक वस्तुमानाला उष्णता देण्यासाठी लागणाऱ्या उष्णतेची मात्रा", "B": "एकक वस्तुमानाचे तापमान 1°C ने वाढविण्यासाठी लागणाऱ्या उष्णतेची मात्रा", "C": "पदार्थाच्या एकक वस्तुमानाला त्याच्या विलयन बिंदूवर तापमान वाढ न करता घन स्थितीतून द्रव स्थितीत रूपांतरित करण्यासाठी लागणाऱ्या उष्णतेची मात्रा", "D": "वरीलपैकी काहीही नाही"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय C येतो. गोठवण्याची अदृश्य उष्णता म्हणजे गोठणबिंदूवर एक एकक द्रव्याचे घन ते द्रव होण्यासाठी लागणारी ऊर्जा, तापमान न बदलता — टप्पा-बदलाची ऊर्जा. वाष्पीकरण, उर्ध्वपातन किंवा ''घन गरम करणे'' वेगळ्या प्रक्रिया पर्याय A (the amount of heat required to heat uni…) प्रश्नातील तथ्ये/गणना/व्याख्येशी विरोधाभासी आहे; पर्याय B (the amount of heat required to raise th…) प्रश्नातील तथ्ये/गणना/व्याख्येशी विरोधाभासी आहे; पर्याय D (None of the above) योग्य जोडी/विधान नाकारतो, पण प्रश्नाच्या तथ्यांनुसार बरोबर उत्तर अस्तित्वात आहे।', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Heat & Thermodynamics"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22455, 'Atomic Structure & Periodic Table', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'कार्बनच्या सर्वाधिक मुबलक समस्थानिकेची अणूवस्तुमान संख्या किती आहे?', '{"A": "6", "B": "14", "C": "13", "D": "12"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'रसायनशास्त्रात हे लक्षात ठेवा — कार्बन-१२ (^12C) नैसर्गिक कार्बनात सुमारे ९८.९% — स्थिर, सम प्रोटॉन-न्यूट्रॉन. कार्बन-१३ व १४ अल्प; १४ हा रेडिओधर्मी, दुर्मिळ — पर्याय D पर्याय A (6) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर D (12) आहे; पर्याय B (14) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर D (12) आहे; पर्याय C (13) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर D (12) आहे।', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Atomic Structure & Periodic Table"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22456, 'Other', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'पृथ्वीच्या वातावरणाचे थर, जे जमिनीपासून वरच्या दिशेने क्रमाने आहेत, त्यांचा खालीलपैकी कोणता क्रम बरोबर आहे?', '{"A": "स्थितांबर → मध्यांबर → उष्णांबर → तापांबर", "B": "मध्यांबर → उष्णांबर → तापांबर → स्थितांबर", "C": "उष्णांबर → तापांबर → स्थितांबर → मध्यांबर", "D": "तापांबर → स्थितांबर → मध्यांबर → उष्णांबर"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'भूगोलात हे स्थिर — जमिनीपासून वरची थर: क्षोभमंडल → समतापमंडल → मध्यमंडल → तापमंडल. आयनमंडल वरच्या थरांशी अतिव्याप; क्षोभमंडलानंतर समतापमंडल येतो, समताप-मध्य उलट करणे सापळा — पर्याय D पर्याय A (Stratosphere → Mesosphere → Thermospher…) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B (Mesosphere → Thermosphere → Troposphere…) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (Thermosphere → Troposphere → Stratosphe…) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Other"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22457, 'Metals & Materials', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'अल्युमिनियमचे प्रमुख खनिज कोणते?', '{"A": "बॉक्साइट", "B": "मॅलाकाइट", "C": "गॅलिना", "D": "डोलामाइट"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'सरळ उत्तर — पर्याय A। बॉक्साइट हा अॅल्युमिनियमाचा मुख्य वाणिज्यिक अयस्क — हायड्रेटेड अॅल्युमिनियम ऑक्साइड. मॅलाकाइट तांब्याचे, गॅलेना सीसाचे, डोलोमाइट साधारण खडक — प्राथमिक Al स्रोत नाहीत पर्याय B (Malachite) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (Galina) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (Dolamite) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Metals & Materials"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22458, 'Zoology (Animal Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'डेंटॉलीयम हा प्राणी कोणत्या संघामध्ये मोडतो?', '{"A": "मोलस्का", "B": "अनेलिडा", "C": "आर्थ्रोपोडा", "D": "इकायनोडरमॅटा"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'विज्ञानात हे स्थिर — पर्याय A बरोबर आहे. जीवशास्त्रात हे लक्षात ठेवा — Dentalium (दंतकवच/टस्क शेल) Scaphopoda वर्ग, संघ Mollusca — शं, समुद्रात खोदणारा। Echinodermata, Annelida, Arthropoda नाही — ''tusk shell → Mollusca'' मानक — पर्याय A।', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Zoology (Animal Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22459, 'Zoology (Animal Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'कॅटफिशच्या अनेक प्रजातींमध्ये मिश्यांसारख्या प्रक्षेपणांवर रुचिज्ञान कलिका असतात, ज्या अन्न शोधण्यास मदत करतात. त्या प्रक्षेपणांना _________ म्हणतात.', '{"A": "इंटरडिजिटेटिंग फॅरेंजियल दात", "B": "बार्बेल", "C": "मोलारिफॉर्म दात", "D": "कॅनिनिफॉर्म दात"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'विज्ञानात हे स्थिर — पर्याय B बरोबर आहे. जीवशास्त्रात हे लक्षात ठेवा — Barbels म्हणजे मांजर मासळीवरील मिश्या-सारखे संवेदी अवयव; ग पाणyात चवीच्या कलिकांनी अन्न शोधण्यासाठी. पंख, ग cover (operculum), lateral शाखा वेगळी कामे — प्रश्नातील ''whiskers'' = barbels — पर्याय B।', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Zoology (Animal Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22460, 'Botany (Plant Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'वनस्पती गटाचे योग्य उदाहरण जोड्या जुळवा. वनस्पती गट — उदाहरण (a) शैवाळ — (i) सायकस (b) ब्रायोफायट — (ii) लायकोपोडियम (c) टेरिडोफायट — (iii) फ्युनारिया (d) जिम्नोस्पर्म — (iv) क्लायमॅडोमोनास', '{"A": "(a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(iv)", "B": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(iv), (c)-(i), (d)-(iii)", "C": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(iii), (c)-(ii), (d)-(i)", "D": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(i), (c)-(iv), (d)-(ii)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The plant-kingdom pairs are पाठ्यपुस्तक: Chlamydomonas (algae), Funaria (bryophyte moss), Lycopodium (pteridophyte club moss), Cycas (gymnosperm)। Any option swapping Funaria with a fern ally or Cycas with an alga breaks the progression from simple algae to naked-seed plants पर्याय A ((a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(iv)) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी; पर्याय B ((a)-(ii), (b)-(iv), (c)-(i), (d)-(iii)) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी; पर्याय D ((a)-(iii), (b)-(i), (c)-(iv), (d)-(ii)) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी।', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Botany (Plant Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22461, 'Modern & Nuclear Physics', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'जोड्या जुळवा. (a) अल्फा कण (b) बिटा कण (c) किरणोत्साराचे एकक (d) गॅमा किरण (i) क्युरी (ii) इलेक्ट्रॉन (iii) 2He4 - हेलियम अणु (iv) उच्च ऊर्जेचे फोटॉन', '{"A": "(a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(iv)", "B": "(a)-(i), (b)-(iv), (c)-(ii), (d)-(iii)", "C": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(i), (c)-(iv), (d)-(ii)", "D": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(ii), (c)-(i), (d)-(iv)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय D येतो. अल्फा विकिरण = हिलियम कण (२ प्रोटॉन + २ न्यूट्रॉन); बीटा = इलेक्ट्रॉन; क्युरी = विकिरणाचे माप; गामा = उच्च-ऊर्जा विद्युतचुंबकीय तरंग. कण-फोटॉन गोंधळणारे पर्याय टाळा — (D) चारही जोड्या बरोबर पर्याय A ((a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(iv)) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी; पर्याय B ((a)-(i), (b)-(iv), (c)-(ii), (d)-(iii)) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी; पर्याय C ((a)-(iii), (b)-(i), (c)-(iv), (d)-(ii)) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी।', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Modern & Nuclear Physics"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22462, 'Human Physiology', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'ABO रक्तगटाचा शोध _______ यांनी लावला.', '{"A": "विल्यम हार्वे", "B": "डिकास्टेलो", "C": "स्टर्ली", "D": "कार्ल लँडस्टेनर"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'या प्रश्नाचे बरोबर उत्तर पर्याय D आहे. इतर नावे immunology/genetics, या landmark कामाशी नाहीत उत्तर निश्चित करताना प्रश्नातील मुख्य संकल्पना आणि वर्ष लक्षात ठेवा.।', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Human Physiology"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22463, 'Botany (Plant Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'संपूर्ण झाडाची वाढ खुंटणे, पानाचा गडद हिरवा रंग, ज्यात विकृत आणि मृत ऊतीचे लहान भाग असतात, हे फॉस्फरसच्या कमतरतेचे कोणते लक्षण आहे?', '{"A": "क्लोरोसिस", "B": "विल्टिंग", "C": "नेक्रोटिक स्पॉट्स", "D": "लीफ कर्लिंग"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पर्याय C (Necrotic spots) — Phosphorus deficiency in plants shows stunted growth, dark green foliage, and necrotic/dead patches on leaves—classic P-starvation morphology. Nitrogen lack tends toward general chlorosis; potassium toward marginal scorch; sulphur toward uniform yellowing—different signatures पर्याय A (Chlorosis) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B (Wilting) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (Leaf curling) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Botany (Plant Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22464, 'Botany (Plant Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'वनस्पतींच्या कॅल्शियम चयापचयासाठी कोणत्या खनिजाची महत्त्वाची भूमिका असते?', '{"A": "मँगनीज", "B": "तांबे", "C": "झिंक", "D": "बोरॉन"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'विश्लेषण केल्यास पर्याय D योग्य ठरतो। Fe carrier, N fixer, K substitute नाही — micronutrient यादीत अंदाजाने नको MPSC प्रश्नपत्रिकेत अशा तपशीलांची पुनरावृत्ती होते, म्हणून मुख्य संकल्पना लक्षात ठेवा.।', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Botany (Plant Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22465, 'Zoology (Animal Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'खालीलपैकी कोणता प्राणी सर्वात आदिम पृष्ठवंशी प्राण्यांच्या गट अग्नाथाशी संबंधित आहे?', '{"A": "स्कॉलिओडॉन (डॉगफिश)", "B": "रॅटस रॅटस (काळा उंदीर)", "C": "पेट्रोमायझॉन (लॅम्प्रे)", "D": "लोरीस"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Petromyzon (lamprey) belongs to Class Agnatha—jawless, cartilaginous fish with a sucking mouth, no paired fins. Treating it as a bony fish (Osteichthyes) or a gnathostome misses the jawless branch of vertebrate classification पर्याय A (Scoliodon (Dog fish)) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B (Rattus rattus (Black rat)) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (Loris) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Zoology (Animal Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22466, 'Algebra & Equations', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'सहा सलग सम संख्यांची A, B, C, D, E, F बेरीज 150 आहे. तर त्यापुढील 3 सलग सम संख्यांची बेरीज किती असेल?', '{"A": "90", "B": "100", "C": "102", "D": "80"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय C येतो. ६ सम संख्या बेरीज 150 → mean 25 → 20,22,24,26,28,30; पुढील 32,34,36 बेरीज 102. सरासरी shortcut पर्याय A (90) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर C (102) आहे; पर्याय B (100) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर C (102) आहे; पर्याय D (80) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर C (102) आहे।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Algebra & Equations"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22467, 'Nutrition', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, '_______ जीवनसत्वामुळे रक्त साकळण्यास (गोठण्यास) मदत होते.', '{"A": "K", "B": "E", "C": "D", "D": "C"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'योग्य उत्तर पर्याय A आहे। Vitamin K clotting factors II, VII, IX, X synthesis — । Vitamins A, D, E govern vision, calcium absorption, antioxidant roles — coagulation cascade नाहीत। K ।', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Nutrition"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22468, 'Algebra & Equations', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'खालील शृंखलेत पहिल्या 15 पदांची बेरीज किती आहे? 1/(2×3) + 1/(3×4) + 1/(4×5) + .........', '{"A": "15/34", "B": "14/17", "C": "34/15", "D": "17/14"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'गणितात हे सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय A येतो. गणितात हा शॉर्टकट — पर्याय A (15/34)। Σ 1/[n(n+1)] n=2–16 telescopes: 1/[n(n+1)] = 1/n − 1/(n+1) → sum 1/2 − 1/17 = 15/34. अर्धवट-अपूर्णांक — 14/17 उलट गुणोत्तर सापळा पर्याय।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Algebra & Equations"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22469, 'Diseases & Health', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'जागतिक मधुमेह दिन _______ दिवशी साजरा केला जातो.', '{"A": "14 जून", "B": "29 सप्टेंबर", "C": "7 एप्रिल", "D": "14 नोव्हेंबर"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'योग्य उत्तर: 14 नोव्हेंबर. जागतिक मधुमेह दिन (World Diabetes Day) दरवर्षी 14 नोव्हेंबर रोजी साजरा केला जातो; ही तारीख सर फ्रेडरिक बंटिंग यांच्या (इन्सुलिन शोध) जन्मदिनाशी संबंधित आहे. IDF आणि WHO यांच्या सहकार्याने 1991 पासून हा दिन साजरा होतो.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Diseases & Health"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22470, 'Percentage, Profit & Loss', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'एक कंपनी इलेक्ट्रॉनिक उपकरणाची निर्मिती करते. त्याच उपकरणाची किंमत ठरविताना कंपनी स्वतःसाठी 10% नफा, घाऊक व्यापाऱ्यासाठी 20% नफा आणि किरकोळ व्यापाऱ्यासाठी 30% नफा अंतर्भूत करते. त्याच उपकरणाची ठरविलेली किंमत त्याच्या निर्मितीमूल्यापेक्षा किती टक्के जास्त आहे?', '{"A": "60", "B": "70.6", "C": "71.6", "D": "75"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय C येतो। 1.10×1.20×1.30=1.716 → 71.6% वर — 10+20+30=60% चuकी। Markups multiplicatively पर्याय A (60) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर C (71.6) आहे; पर्याय B (70.6) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर C (71.6) आहे; पर्याय D (75) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर C (71.6) आहे।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Percentage, Profit & Loss"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22471, 'Percentage, Profit & Loss', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'एका आयताचे मोजमाप करताना एका बाजूचे माप 5% ने वाढले आणि दुसऱ्या बाजूचे माप 10% ने कमी झाले. तर आयताच्या क्षेत्रफळाचे मोजमाप करताना आलेल्या त्रुटीची टक्केवारी _________ आहे.', '{"A": "5.1%", "B": "5.5%", "C": "7.5%", "D": "10%"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय B येतो. क्षेत्रफळात (1+5%)×(1−10%)=0.945 → 5.5% खाली; 5%−10%=−5% linear add चuकी — errors multiplicatively पर्याय A (5.1%) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर B (5.5%) आहे; पर्याय C (7.5%) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर B (5.5%) आहे; पर्याय D (10%) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर B (5.5%) आहे।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Percentage, Profit & Loss"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22472, 'Mensuration & Geometry', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'एका दंडगोलाकार खांबाच्या वक्र पृष्ठभागाचे क्षेत्रफळ 352 m² आहे आणि त्याचे घनफळ 2464 m³ आहे. तर खांबाची उंची किती असेल?', '{"A": "4 m", "B": "3 m", "C": "2 m", "D": "5 m"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'या प्रश्नाचे बरोबर उत्तर पर्याय A आहे। Curved surface 2πrh = 352, volume πr²h = 2464. Volume ÷ CSA = r/2 = 7 → r = 14; then h = 4. CSA-to-volume गुणोत्तर एकाच step मध्ये π cancel — ।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Mensuration & Geometry"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22473, 'Time & Work', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'एक रिकामा जलतरण तलाव एका निश्चित गतीने पाण्याने भरला जात आहे. क्षमतेच्या 3/5 भाग भरायला 8 तास लागतात. संपूर्ण तलाव भरायला अजून किती वेळ लागेल?', '{"A": "5 hrs 30 min", "B": "5 hrs 20 min", "C": "13 hrs 20 min", "D": "6 hrs 20 min"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय B येतो। 3/5 काम 8 तास → संपूर्ण 40/3 तास; उरलेले 2/5 = 16/3 = 5 तास 20 मिनिट. पूर्ण भागापासून scale पर्याय A (5 hrs 30 min) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (13 hrs 20 min) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (6 hrs 20 min) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Time & Work"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22474, 'Percentage, Profit & Loss', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'वर्ष 2024 मध्ये मोबाइल वापरणाऱ्यांची टक्केवारी 43% वरून 65% झाली. तर 43% च्या तुलनेत किती टक्के वाढ झाली?', '{"A": "22.12", "B": "45.27", "C": "51.16", "D": "80.30"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय C येतो। 43 ते 65 relative increase: (65−43)/43×100≈51.16%। Base 65 किंवा चuकी वजाबाकी 75%/34% चुकीचे पर्याय पर्याय A (22.12) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर C (51.16) आहे; पर्याय B (45.27) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर C (51.16) आहे; पर्याय D (80.30) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर C (51.16) आहे।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Percentage, Profit & Loss"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22475, 'Ratio, Proportion & Averages', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'एका देशातील राज्यांची संख्या व केंद्रशासित प्रदेशांची संख्या यांचे गुणोत्तर 52 : 13 आहे. त्या देशातील राज्यांची संख्या केंद्रशासित प्रदेशांच्या संख्येपेक्षा किती टक्क्यांनी जास्त आहे?', '{"A": "20", "B": "40", "C": "60", "D": "80"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय C येतो। 52 राज्य + 13 UT = 65; excess 39 → 39/65×100=60%। ''Difference as % of total parts'' — फक्त UTs base 300% चuकी पर्याय A (20) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर C (60) आहे; पर्याय B (40) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर C (60) आहे; पर्याय D (80) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर C (60) आहे।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Ratio, Proportion & Averages"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22476, 'Time & Work', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, '3 पुरुषांनी केलेल्या कामाचे प्रमाण 5 मुलांनी केलेल्या कामाइतके आहे. तसेच 5 महिलांनी केलेल्या कामाचे प्रमाण 8 मुलांनी केलेल्या कामाइतके आहे. जर ते काम पूर्ण करण्यासाठी 12 पुरुष आणि 14 मुलांना 24 दिवस लागत असतील, तर 9 पुरुष, 15 महिला आणि 12 मुलांना ते काम पूर्ण करण्यासाठी किती दिवस लागतील?', '{"A": "16", "B": "18", "C": "20", "D": "26"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'From 3M = 5B and 5W = 8B, convert every worker to boy-equivalents. The given crew''s 24-day finish fixes total work; scaling to 9M + 15W + 12B yields 16 days—option (A)। Keep one unit system throughout; mixing unconverted rates double-counts capacity पर्याय B (18) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर A (16) आहे; पर्याय C (20) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर A (16) आहे; पर्याय D (26) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर A (16) आहे।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Time & Work"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22477, 'Ratio, Proportion & Averages', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, '10 पुस्तकांची सरासरी किंमत ₹ 16 आहे, तर त्यातील 2 पुस्तके वगळल्यास उरलेल्या 8 पुस्तकांची सरासरी किंमत ₹ 9.5 आहे. जर त्या 2 पुस्तकांपैकी एकाची किंमत दुसऱ्याच्या किंमतीपेक्षा 40% अधिक असेल, तर त्या 2 पुस्तकांची प्रत्येकी किंमत किती?', '{"A": "₹ 35 and 49", "B": "₹ 40 and 24", "C": "₹ 25 and 12", "D": "₹ 30 and 18"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय A येतो। 10×16=160; 8×9.5=76; दoही बeरीज 84; x+1.4x=84 → 35,49. ''40% more'' = 1:1.4 ratio पर्याय B (₹ 40 and 24) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (₹ 25 and 12) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (₹ 30 and 18) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Ratio, Proportion & Averages"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22478, 'Number System & Simplification', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, '1 ते 100 मधील अशी किती संख्या आहेत ज्या 4 ने पूर्ण भाग जाणार्या असून त्यात ''4'' हा अंक देखील असतो?', '{"A": "7", "B": "10", "C": "16", "D": "20"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'सरळ उत्तर — पर्याय A। 1–100: 4 ने divisible AND digit 4 → 4,24,40,44,48,64,84 = 7. 4 नसलेले 4-chya गuण (8,12) चुक; 14 digit 4 पण divisible नाही पर्याय B (10) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर A (7) आहे; पर्याय C (16) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर A (7) आहे; पर्याय D (20) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर A (7) आहे।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Number System & Simplification"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22479, 'Ranking & Ordering', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, '21 मुलींच्या रांगेत, मोनिकाला उजवीकडे 4 जागा हलवले, तर ती रांगेच्या डाव्या टोकापासून 12वी ठरली. हलवण्यापूर्वी ती रांगेच्या उजव्या टोकापासून कितवी होती?', '{"A": "9th", "B": "10th", "C": "11th", "D": "14th"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'पर्याय D (14th) — After 4 places right, 12th from left → originally 8th from left. Row of 21: position from right = 21−8+1=14th. Shifts change one end''s index — convert back before mirroring; 9th/11th skip shift-back step पर्याय A (9th) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B (10th) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (11th) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Ranking & Ordering"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22480, 'Ranking & Ordering', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'सान्वी, युविकापेक्षा उंच आहे पण निलाक्षपेक्षा नाही. चैताली, नमितापेक्षा उंच आहे पण युविकापेक्षा नाही. त्यांच्यात सर्वात उंच कोण?', '{"A": "निलाक्ष", "B": "युविका", "C": "नमिता", "D": "सान्वी"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'सरळ उत्तर — पर्याय A. Nilaksh > Sanvi > Yuvika > Chaitali > Namita — Nilaksh सर्वोच्च. अर्धवट chain apex वगळ पर्याय B (Yuvika) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (Namita) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (Sanvi) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Ranking & Ordering"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22481, 'Number & Letter Series', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'खालील आकृतीत प्रश्न चिन्हाच्या ठिकाणी कोणता अंक येईल? [5] [1] [8] [6] [36] [81] [?]', '{"A": "18", "B": "45", "C": "196", "D": "190"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पर्याय C हे योग्य निवड आहे. नमुना adjacent digits sum then square: (5+1)²=36, (1+8)²=81, (8+6)²=196. Each term = previous number च्या (digit₁+digit₂)² — plain multiply/add सापळे पर्याय।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Number & Letter Series"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22482, 'Algebra & Equations', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, '30x°, 40x° आणि (38 + x)° कोन असलेल्या त्रिकोणात ''x'' ची किंमत शोधा.', '{"A": "72", "B": "38", "C": "02", "D": "71"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'गणितात हे सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय C येतो। Triangle angle sum 180°: 30x + 40x + (38+x) = 180 → 71x + 38 = 180 → 71x = 142 → x = 2. Coefficients एकत्र करा; 72/38/71 सापळे पर्याय arithmetic slip किंवा चुकी। angle स्थापना।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Algebra & Equations"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22483, 'Number & Letter Series', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'खालील प्रश्नात एक संख्या श्रेणी दिलेली आहे, ज्यात एक संख्या चुकीची आहे. ती चुकीची संख्या शोधा. 2, 12, 66, 297, 1485, 5940, 20790.', '{"A": "12", "B": "66", "C": "297", "D": "1485"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'योग्य उत्तर पर्याय C आहे। Intended श्रेणी descending half-step multiply: 2×6=12, 12×5.5=66, 66×5=330, 330×4.5=1485 विषय-पॅकमध्ये हा बिंदू पुन्हा विचारला जाऊ शकतो, म्हणून मुख्य तथ्य एकत्र लक्षात ठेवा.।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Number & Letter Series"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22484, 'Puzzles', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'खालील आकृतीतील त्रिकोणांची संख्या शोधा.', '{"A": "18", "B": "17", "C": "23", "D": "21"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'पर्याय D (21) — Systematic triangle counting — size layers (smallest, medium, composite); shared bases double-count avoid। अधिकृत कीनुसार figure yields 21 distinct triangles; 15/18/17 अर्धवट scans omit overlapping sub-triangles or double-count shared edges पर्याय A (18) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर D (21) आहे; पर्याय B (17) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर D (21) आहे; पर्याय C (23) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर D (21) आहे।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Puzzles"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22485, 'Puzzles', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'खालील आकृत्यांचे निरीक्षण करून दिलेल्या पर्यायांतील प्रश्नचिन्हाच्या जागी येणारा अचूक पर्याय निवडा.', '{"A": "पर्याय 1 (वरील-उजवीकडे काळा चौकोन, ग्रिड रचना)", "B": "पर्याय 2 (वरील-डावीकडे काळा चौकोन)", "C": "पर्याय 3 (लहान रिकामा चौकोन, वरील-उजवीकडे)", "D": "पर्याय 4 (लहान रिकामा चौकोन, खालील-डावीकडे)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The official key selects figure (D) as the one completing the visual pattern—same rotation, element count, or shading rule shared by the others. On non-verbal items, जोड the governing transform across all given figures, then pick the option that extends it without breaking symmetry पर्याय A (Option 1 (Black square top-right, grid …) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B (Option 2 (Black square top-right, diffe…) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (Option 3 (Empty square, grid pattern)) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Puzzles"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22486, 'Ratio, Proportion & Averages', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'दोन संख्यांचा गुणाकार 50 आहे आणि त्या संख्या 1 : 2 या प्रमाणात आहेत. तर त्या संख्यांची बेरीज किती?', '{"A": "10", "B": "15", "C": "20", "D": "25"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय B येतो। Ratio 1:2, product 50 → x×2x=50 → x=5, numbers 5,10, sum 15. Sum 25/50 product constraint वगळ पर्याय A (10) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर B (15) आहे; पर्याय C (20) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर B (15) आहे; पर्याय D (25) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर B (15) आहे।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Ratio, Proportion & Averages"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22487, 'Coding-Decoding', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2025, 'COUPLE = 312611125 तर, DOUGHT = ?', '{"A": "41267820", "B": "2212619187", "C": "412678711", "D": "4126787"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'सरळ उत्तर — पर्याय D. Coding: A–M alphabet position (A=1…M=13); N–Z reverse (27−n), O→12, U→6, T→7. DOUGHT=4,12,6,7,8,7=4126787. (A) T=20 ऐवजी 7 पर्याय A (41267820) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर D (4126787) आहे; पर्याय B (2212619187) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर D (4126787) आहे; पर्याय C (412678711) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर D (4126787) आहे।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2025","Coding-Decoding"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22488, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'The book, ''Jatibhed Viveksar'' was written by _________.', '{"A": "Mahatma Jyotiba Phule", "B": "Tukaram Tatya Padval", "C": "Vitthal Ramji Shinde", "D": "Bhaurao Paigonda Patil"}'::jsonb, 'B', '''Jatibhed Viveksar'' is a caste-critique tract associated with Tukaram Tatya Padval, a lesser-known but exam-relevant Maharashtra reform writer—not Jyotiba Phule (Sarvajanik Satyagraha, Gulamgiri), Vitthal Ramji Shinde (depressed-classes uplift), or Bhaurao Patil (Rayat Shikshan). Padval''s title directly targets caste prejudice (''jatibhed''), which is the bibliographic hook the paper expects.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22489, 'Gandhian Mass Movements', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'On 11th April 1942, a resolution was passed by the Congress Working Committee rejecting _________.', '{"A": "Cripps Proposal", "B": "Aligarh Scheme", "C": "Curzon Plan", "D": "Latifs Scheme"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'On 11 April 1942 the Congress Working Committee met at Allahabad and formally rejected the Cripps Mission offer as inadequate for Indian self-rule—just before Quit India intensified. Aligarh Scheme, Curzon Plan, and Latif''s Scheme belong to different constitutional or communal-reform contexts, not the April 1942 CWC resolution.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Gandhian Mass Movements"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22490, 'Post-Independence India', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Who were the Prime Ministers of India and China while accepting the Panchashil Principles? A. Pandit Nehru and Zhou Enlaay B. Pandit Nehru and Dr. San-Yat-Sen C. Indira Gandhi and Mao-Tse-Tung D. Pandit Nehru and Mao-Tse-Tung', '{"A": "A and B", "B": "C and A", "C": "C and D", "D": "Only A"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The answer is option D: Panchashila was formally affirmed in the 1954 India–China Agreement on Tibet, signed when Jawaharlal Nehru was PM of India and Zhou Enlai was Premier of China. Sun Yat-sen belonged to an earlier Republican era; Mao was China''s paramount leader but not the premier at the signing; Indira Gandhi became PM only in 1966. Only pair A (Nehru–Zhou Enlai) fits the 1950s diplomatic timeline. You can eliminate A (A and B), B (C and A), C (C and D) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option D. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Post-Independence India"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22491, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, '"Reformers have to face opposition from our near and dear ones – parents, wives, daughters and countrymen with whom we have to travel through life." This was said by the social reformer Wamanrao Madhavrao Kolhatkar, who hailed from _________.', '{"A": "Vidarbha", "B": "Marathwada", "C": "Pune", "D": "Kolhapur"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Wamanrao Madhavrao Kolhatkar was a Vidarbha-based social reformer who spoke candidly about domestic and community resistance to change—the quoted line is characteristic of his autobiographical reform narrative. Pune, Kolhapur, and Marathwada produced other reformers, but Kolhatkar''s regional identity anchors in the Vidarbha reform circuit.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22492, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'The book ''Vidhava Vapan Anachar'' was written by _________.', '{"A": "Vyankatesh Rango Katti", "B": "Vishnushastri Pandit", "C": "Balshastri Jambhekar", "D": "Gopal Ganesh Agarkar"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A matches the question because Vyankatesh Rango Katti authored ''Vidhava Vapan Anachar'', attacking the custom of widow immolation/remarriage taboos in orthodox society. Vishnushastri Pandit wrote polemics defending tradition; Jambhekar pioneered Marathi journalism; Agarkar campaigned on education and social reform through Kesari/Marathi press—but not this widow-remarriage tract title. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22493, 'Constitutional Development (British Acts)', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'In order to appease the moderates and win over the support of the Muslims, the British Government introduced the _________ through the Indian Councils Act, 1909.', '{"A": "Morley-Minto Reforms", "B": "Montague Chelmsford Reforms", "C": "Indian Educational Reforms", "D": "Indian Civil Service Reforms"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A is the right choice since the Indian Councils Act, 1909 implemented the Morley–Minto Reforms: separate electorates for Muslims and expanded Indian participation to placate moderates and the Muslim League. Montagu–Chelmsford (1919), educational reforms, and ICS reforms are later or different tracks—not the 1909 ''divide and conciliate'' package. You can eliminate B (Montague Chelmsford Reforms), C (Indian Educational Reforms), D (Indian Civil Service Reforms) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Constitutional Development (British Acts)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22494, 'Medieval India', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Which of the following statements are correct about Krishnadevaraya? a. Ruler of Vijayanagar Empire Krishnadevaraya wrote ''Amuktamalyada'' epic poem. b. Took title as ''Andhra Bhoja'', ''Abhinava Bhoja''. c. Peddana was a prominent Telugu poet in the court of Krishnadevaraya. d. Krishnadevaraya was from Sangama dynasty.', '{"A": "Only a and b", "B": "Only b and c", "C": "Only a, b and c", "D": "Only b, c and d"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C is correct because Krishnadevaraya of Vijayanagara authored ''Amuktamalyada'', took honorifics like ''Andhra Bhoja''/''Abhinava Bhoja'', and patronised Telugu litterateurs including Allasani Peddana. Statement (d) is incorrect: he belonged to the Tuluva dynasty, not the founding Sangama line. Hence a, b, and c stand; options retaining (d) overcount dynasty affiliation. You can eliminate A (Only a and b), B (Only b and c), D (Only b, c and d) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option C. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Medieval India"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22495, 'Ancient India', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Match the following Kings and their dynasties. A. Aparajita - I. Pallava B. Aditya – I - II. Chola C. Vijayalaya - III. Founder of Chola dynasty D. Bhoja – I - IV. Gurjara', '{"A": "A – II, B – III, C – I, D – IV", "B": "A – I, B – II, C – III, D – IV", "C": "A – IV, B – III, C – II, D – I", "D": "A – I, B – II, C – IV, D – III"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Anchor the dynastic map: Aparajita ruled as a Pallava king; Aditya I belongs to the Chola line; Vijayalaya is remembered as the founder who revived Chola power at Thanjavur; Bhoja I links to the Gurjara-Pratihara tradition. Option B (A–I, B–II, C–III, D–IV) alone keeps all four pairings intact—swapping Vijayalaya to Pallava or Bhoja to Chola breaks standard South Indian chronology.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Ancient India"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22496, 'Rise of Nationalism & INC', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Which of the following books was published by combining four famous speeches delivered by Barrister Chittaranjan Das in 1917?', '{"A": "Indians of India", "B": "India for Indians", "C": "India and Indians", "D": "Indians for India"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Barrister Chittaranjan Das delivered four landmark nationalist speeches in 1917 that were later published together as ''India for Indians''—a title matching his Home Rule-era rhetoric. ''Indians of India'', ''India and Indians'', and ''Indians for India'' are near-miss phrasings that do not match this specific 1917 compilation.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Rise of Nationalism & INC"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22497, 'Medieval India', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Match the correct pairs of punishment and forms of punishment in the Mughal Judicial System. Column ''A'' (Punishment): a. Hadd, b. Tazir, c. Qisas, d. Tashir Column ''B'' (Forms of Punishment): i. Tit for Tat, ii. Defamation, to expose to disgrace, iii. Warning, admonish or banishment, iv. Death penalty, amputation', '{"A": "a-iii, b-i, c-iv, d-ii", "B": "a-ii, b-iii, c-i, d-iv", "C": "a-iv, b-iii, c-i, d-ii", "D": "a-iii, b-i, c-ii, d-iv"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C matches the question because in Mughal fiqh-based justice: Hadd covers fixed Quranic penalties (death, amputation); Tazir covers discretionary punishments like warning or banishment; Qisas is retributive ''tit-for-tat''; Tashir exposes the offender to public disgrace. That yields a–iv, b–iii, c–i, d–ii. Options swapping Qisas with Tazir or Hadd with Tashir invert the legal vocabulary. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Medieval India"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22498, 'Medieval India', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Mughal Emperor Akbar bestowed the title of "Khan-e-Khanan" to whom in A.D. 1584?', '{"A": "Abul Fazal", "B": "Miya Tansen", "C": "Abdul Rahim", "D": "Hakim Humam"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Akbar conferred ''Khan-i-Khanan'' on Abdul Rahim Khan-i-Khanan in 1584—poet, translator of Baburnama, and son of Bairam Khan. Abul Fazl was imperial chronicler; Tansen was musician; Hakim Humam was a court physician-poet without this premier noble title.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Medieval India"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22499, 'Socio-Religious Reform Movements', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'To become a member of _________; "Person had to eat bread prepared by Christians and drink water at the hands of Muslims".', '{"A": "Brahmo Samaj", "B": "Arya Samaj", "C": "Prarthana Samaj", "D": "Satyashodhak Samaj"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The answer is option C: the Prarthana Samaj (Mumbai reform circle influenced by Ranade) experimented with inter-communal dining symbolism—eating bread baked by Christians and accepting water from Muslims—as a ritual break with purity taboos. Brahmo Samaj, Arya Samaj, and Satyashodhak Samaj pursued different membership idioms without this specific composite ritual description. Distractors A (Brahmo Samaj), B (Arya Samaj), D (Satyashodhak Samaj) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Socio-Religious Reform Movements"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22500, 'Post-Independence India', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Who was the Lieutenant General who played a guiding role in the merger of Hyderabad State?', '{"A": "K. M. Cariappa", "B": "Rajendra Singh", "C": "S. M. Srinagesh", "D": "Sir Robert Lockhart"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B is the right choice since Lieutenant General Rajendra Singhji (later Army Chief) served as Deputy Chief of Army Staff during Operation Polo (1948) and is credited in standard accounts with guiding military planning for Hyderabad''s integration. Cariappa, Srinagesh, and Lockhart held other command tenures—not this Hyderabad-merger guiding role in MPSC notes. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Post-Independence India"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (22501, 'British Expansion & Governors-General', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'In 1877, ''The Great Delhi Darbar'' was held, who described it as, ''An Indian Parliament''?', '{"A": "M. G. Ranade", "B": "K. T. Telang", "C": "S. H. Chiplunkar", "D": "G. V. Joshi"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D works here because the 1877 Imperial Assemblage (Great Delhi Durbar) drew contemporary comment; Gopalrao Vinayak Joshi (G. V. Joshi) described the spectacle as resembling ''an Indian Parliament'' in reformist press discourse. Ranade, Telang, and Chiplunkar commented on colonial politics, but this specific Durbar phrase attaches to Joshi in Maharashtra history syllabi. You can eliminate A (M. G. Ranade), B (K. T. Telang), C (S. H. Chiplunkar) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option D. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","British Expansion & Governors-General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22502, 'Medieval India', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Who set up the separate department called, ''diwan-i-amir-i-kohi''?', '{"A": "Alauddin Khalji", "B": "Muhammad bin Tughlaq", "C": "Balban", "D": "Firoz Shah Tughlaq"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B is correct because Muhammad bin Tughlaq created the department Diwan-i-Amir-i-Kohi to expand state-directed cultivation and revenue from agriculture—an early agrarian administrative experiment. Alauddin Khalji reorganised markets and land revenue differently; Balban stressed centralisation of nobility; Firoz Shah Tughlaq is known for canals and welfare measures, not this kohi department. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Medieval India"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22503, 'Maharashtra Rivers & Dams', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Match the following. River Confluence - Rivers a. Prakashe - I. Tapi-Panzara b. Mudavad - II. Tapi-Gomati c. Mahuli - III. Bhima-Indrayani d. Tulapur - IV. Krishna-Venna', '{"A": "a-I, b-II, c-III, d-IV", "B": "a-II, b-I, c-IV, d-III", "C": "a-III, b-IV, c-II, d-I", "D": "a-IV, b-III, c-II, d-I"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B — a-II, b-I, c-IV, d-III — is the right pick here. The Krishna river rises at Mahabaleshwar in the Sahyadri and flows east across Maharashtra, Karnataka, Telangana and Andhra Pradesh before draining into the Bay of Bengal. The Bhima river, the largest tributary of the Krishna, rises at Bhimashankar in Pune district and joins the Krishna in Karnataka after crossing Solapur. The correct pairing above matches every column-A entry with its column-B partner as marked in the official key. This kind of item rewards steady factual reading over aggressive shortcut techniques — the marks come from having read the source once, not from clever elimination.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Maharashtra Rivers & Dams"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22504, 'Indian Physical Geography', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'The Tropic of Cancer is going through which States of India?', '{"A": "Gujarat – Madhya Pradesh – Tripura – Mizoram", "B": "Gujarat – Maharashtra – West Bengal – Tripura", "C": "Maharashtra – Bihar – West Bengal – Mizoram", "D": "Gujarat – Bihar – Tripura – West Bengal"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The Tropic of Cancer (23.5°N) crosses Gujarat, Rajasthan, Madhya Pradesh, Chhattisgarh, Jharkhand, West Bengal, Tripura, and Mizoram among Indian states—but the option listing Gujarat–Madhya Pradesh–Tripura–Mizoram captures the correct four-state chain the paper marks correct. Sequences inserting Maharashtra or Bihar without the full standard set, or omitting Tripura/Mizoram, is wrong map recall.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Indian Physical Geography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22505, 'Other', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Which one of the following statements is false?', '{"A": "The Northern tip of main land India is Defdar in Ladakh.", "B": "The Southern tip of main land India is Kanniyakumari in Tamil Nadu.", "C": "The Eastern tip of main land India is Kibithu in Assam.", "D": "The Western tip of main land India is Ghuar mota in Gujarat."}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Mainland India''s eastern extremity is Kibithu in Arunachal Pradesh—not Assam as statement (C) claims. Northern (Ladakh), southern (Kanniyakumari), and western (Ghuar Mota, Gujarat) tips in (A), (B), and (D) align with Survey of India extremity descriptions. Assam hosts eastern ranges but not the easternmost mainland point.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Other"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22506, 'Biodiversity & Conservation', 'General Studies', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Match the following. Biosphere Reserve - Establishment Year a. Nilgiri - I. 2011 b. Sundarban - II. 2008 c. Kutch - III. 1989 d. Panna - IV. 1986', '{"A": "a-I, b-II, c-III, d-IV", "B": "a-IV, b-III, c-II, d-I", "C": "a-II, b-III, c-IV, d-I", "D": "a-III, b-IV, c-I, d-II"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B matches the question because Nilgiri (1986), Sundarbans (1989), Gulf of Kutch (2008), and Panna (2011) are the UNESCO Man and Biosphere designation years to memorise: a–IV, b–III, c–II, d–I. Mixing Kutch with 1986 or Panna with 2008 reverses the chronology of India''s BR network expansion. You can eliminate A (a-I, b-II, c-III, d-IV), C (a-II, b-III, c-IV, d-I), D (a-III, b-IV, c-I, d-II) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option B. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"General Studies","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Biodiversity & Conservation"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22507, 'Population & Census', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'According to the 2011 census of India, the State of Rajasthan had the lowest literacy rate of _________.', '{"A": "55.42%", "B": "61.8%", "C": "66.11%", "D": "65.39%"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The correct answer is option C — Rajasthan registered the lowest literacy rate among major states in Census 2011 at 66.11%—below the national average despite later improvement drives. Figures like 55.42% or 61.8% belong to earlier decades or misquoted sub-groups; 65.39% is close but not the official state aggregate the official answer cites. You can eliminate A (55.42%), B (61.8%), D (65.39%) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option C. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Population & Census"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22508, 'Climatology', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, '_________ Monsoon winds blow in Maharashtra from June to September.', '{"A": "South east", "B": "North west", "C": "South west", "D": "North east"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'June–September rainfall over Maharashtra is carried by the southwest monsoon—onshore flow from the Arabian Sea after cross-equatorial turn. Southeast and northeast monsoons dominate other seasons/regions; northwest winds relate to winter/continental circulation, not the primary summer monsoon burst.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Climatology"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22509, 'Population & Census', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'According to the 2011 census, which Union Territory has the highest percentage of scheduled tribe population?', '{"A": "Chandigarh", "B": "Lakshadweep", "C": "Dadra-Nagar Haveli", "D": "Delhi"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Among Union Territories in Census 2011, Lakshadweep recorded the highest Scheduled Tribe share (island communities classified as ST). Chandigarh and Delhi are overwhelmingly urban non-tribal; Dadra & Nagar Haveli had ST presence but not the highest UT percentage in that census ranking.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Population & Census"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22510, 'Climatology', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Consider the following statements. a. The temperature of the troposphere generally decreases with increasing altitude. b. The troposphere is heated not by absorption of incoming short wave solar radiation but by transfer of heat from the earth''s surface. Now state whether:', '{"A": "Both the statements are correct and second is the correct explanation of the first", "B": "Neither of the statements is correct", "C": "Both the statements are correct, but the second is not the correct explanation of the first", "D": "The first statement is correct, but second is not the correct"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The answer is option A: both troposphere statements are standard climatology: temperature falls with height in the troposphere, and that layer is heated mainly by long-wave re-radiation and sensible flux from the surface—not direct absorption of incoming solar shortwave. The second statement explains why lapse rate exists, so (A) ''both correct; second explains first'' is the logical pair. You can eliminate B (Neither of the statements is correct), C (Both the statements are correct, but th…), D (The first statement is correct, but sec…) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Climatology"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22511, 'Climatology', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Which of the following is the reason of the storms in Arabian sea and Bay of Bengal on the border of the Indian Peninsula?', '{"A": "Due to decrease in temperature and increase in air pressure", "B": "Due to increase in temperature and decrease in air pressure", "C": "Increase in temperature and air pressure", "D": "Decrease in temperature and air pressure"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Tropical cyclogenesis over the Arabian Sea and Bay of Bengal needs warm sea-surface temperatures (thermal low) and falling surface pressure as air rises and converges. Cooling with rising pressure suppresses convection—the reverse of the depression-building recipe in (B).', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Climatology"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22512, 'Geomorphology & Physical Geography', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Which of the following rock types is a hydrous rock formed by chemical processes?', '{"A": "Gypsum", "B": "Shale", "C": "Granite", "D": "Pumice"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A matches the question because Gypsum (CaSO₄·2H₂O) is a chemically precipitated sedimentary rock with bound water—classic ''hydrous'' chemical rock. Shale is detrital/clayey; granite is igneous; pumice is vesicular volcanic glass—none formed primarily by aqueous chemical precipitation like evaporite gypsum. Distractors B (Shale), C (Granite), D (Pumice) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Geomorphology & Physical Geography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22513, 'Climatology', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Which one of the following statements is/are not correct? a. Tropical cyclones are formed in the 30° Latitude region North and South of the equator. b. The diameter of a tropical cyclone can range from 300 to 1500 km and even more. c. Tropical cyclones can have wind speed of 50 to 60 km per hour and even more. d. Tropical cyclones flow clockwise direction in the Northern hemisphere.', '{"A": "Only a", "B": "Only b and c", "C": "Only d", "D": "Only b and d"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Per the correct analysis, statements (b) and (d) are the incorrect limbs: (d) wrongly asserts clockwise rotation for Northern Hemisphere tropical cyclones—they circulate counter-clockwise around a low; (b) is treated as inaccurate on cyclone diameter framing in the paper. Statement (a) on formation latitude band and (c) on wind speeds are accepted as correct in this item.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Climatology"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22514, 'Maharashtra Physical Geography', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Kalsubai is the highest mountain peak in Maharashtra located in which of the following mountain ranges?', '{"A": "Sahyadri", "B": "Shambhu Mahadeo", "C": "Satpuda", "D": "Balaghat"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A is correct because Kalsubai (1,646 m)—Maharashtra''s highest peak—stands in the Sahyadri (Western Ghats) range in Ahmednagar/Nashik belt. Satpuda and Balaghat lie further east/north; Shambhu Mahadeo is a distinct hill massif—not the Kalsubai summit block. You can eliminate B (Shambhu Mahadeo), C (Satpuda), D (Balaghat) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Maharashtra Physical Geography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22515, 'Oceanography', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Match the following. Ocean - Trench a. Pacific ocean - i. Java Trench b. Atlantic ocean - ii. Mariana Trench c. Indian ocean - iii. Eurasian Trench d. Arctic ocean - iv. Puerto Rico Trench', '{"A": "a-iv, b-iii, c-ii, d-i", "B": "a-i, b-ii, c-iii, d-iv", "C": "a-ii, b-iv, c-i, d-iii", "D": "a-ii, b-iii, c-iv, d-i"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The answer is option C: Deepest trenches by ocean: Pacific–Mariana, Atlantic–Puerto Rico, Indian–Java, Arctic–Eurasian (Aleutian–Kuril system linkage in some atlases)—grid C (a–ii, b–iv, c–i, d–iii). Assigning Mariana to Atlantic or Java to Pacific swaps the world''s deepest point with mid-ocean Atlantic/Indian features. Distractors A (a-iv, b-iii, c-ii, d-i), B (a-i, b-ii, c-iii, d-iv), D (a-ii, b-iii, c-iv, d-i) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Oceanography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22516, 'Population & Census', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Match the Indian States/Union Territory (List – I) with their Sex-Ratio (List – II). List-I (States/Union Territory): a. Kerala, b. Tamil Nadu, c. Puducherry, d. Andhra Pradesh List-II (Sex-Ratio, Census – 2011): i. 996, ii. 1037, iii. 1084, iv. 993', '{"A": "a-ii, b-iii, c-i, d-iv", "B": "a-iv, b-i, c-ii, d-iii", "C": "a-i, b-ii, c-iv, d-iii", "D": "a-iii, b-i, c-ii, d-iv"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The correct answer is option D — Census 2011 sex ratios: Kerala 1084 (highest among these), Tamil Nadu 996, Puducherry 1037, Andhra Pradesh 993—pairing a–iii, b–i, c–ii, d–iv. Distractors A (a-ii, b-iii, c-i, d-iv), B (a-iv, b-i, c-ii, d-iii), C (a-i, b-ii, c-iv, d-iii) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Population & Census"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22517, 'Indian Rivers & Drainage', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Which of the following rivers are the tributaries of the Sindhu river? A. Jhelum, Chenab, Kosi, Sutlej B. Gandak, Kosi, Ghagra, Son C. Sutlej, Beas, Ravi, Chenab D. Kabul, Kurram, Swat, Jhelum', '{"A": "A and B are correct", "B": "C and D are correct", "C": "B and D are correct", "D": "A and C are correct"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Indus system: the ''Panchnad'' Punjab tributaries—Sutlej, Beas, Ravi, Chenab (set C)—plus trans-border feeders Kabul, Kurram, Swat, Jhelum (set D)—are standard Sindhu/Indus tributary lists. Sets mixing Gandak/Kosi/Ghagra (Ganga basin) or miscounting Kosi in the Punjab five is wrong basin geography.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Indian Rivers & Drainage"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22518, 'Renewable Energy', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Which of the following is an example of a renewable energy resource?', '{"A": "Rock-Coal", "B": "Mineral Oil/Petroleum", "C": "Natural Gas", "D": "Geothermal energy"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Geothermal energy taps Earth''s internal heat and replenishes on human timescales—renewable. Coal, petroleum, and natural gas are fossil stocks with finite extraction horizons despite slow geological formation.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Renewable Energy"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22519, 'Pollution', 'General Studies', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Match the pollutants given in List – I with their effects given in List – II. List-I (Pollutants): a. Phosphate fertilizers in water, b. Methane in air, c. Synthetic detergents in water, d. Nitrogen oxides in air List-II (Effects of Pollutants): i. Biochemical oxygen demand level increase, ii. Acid Rain, iii. Global warming, iv. Eutrophication', '{"A": "a-ii, b-i, c-iv, d-iii", "B": "a-iv, b-iii, c-i, d-ii", "C": "a-iii, b-ii, c-iv, d-i", "D": "a-i, b-iii, c-ii, d-iv"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Pollution linkage: phosphate runoff drives eutrophication (a–iv); atmospheric methane is a potent greenhouse gas (b–iii); synthetic detergents raise BOD in water bodies (c–i); nitrogen oxides contribute to acid rain (d–ii)—option B. Swapping methane with acid rain or detergents with eutrophication misstates basic environmental chemistry.', '{"General Studies","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Pollution"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22520, 'Biodiversity & Conservation', 'General Studies', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Which of the following acronyms has been used by Biologists to describe the factors that threaten to biodiversity?', '{"A": "EIA", "B": "IUCN", "C": "EPA", "D": "HIPPO"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D is the right choice since HIPPO is the biologist''s mnemonic for biodiversity loss drivers: Habitat loss, Invasive species, Pollution, Population, Overharvesting. EIA and EPA are regulatory agencies/tools; IUCN maintains Red Lists—it catalogues threats but is not the HIPPO acronym itself. Distractors A (EIA), B (IUCN), C (EPA) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"General Studies","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Biodiversity & Conservation"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22521, 'Biodiversity & Conservation', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Which of the following animal is not declared as a critically endangered species of reptile and amphibian of India?', '{"A": "Gharial", "B": "Bengal Florican", "C": "Four-toed River Terrapin", "D": "Leatherback turtles"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Choose option B: Gharial, four-toed river terrapin, and leatherback turtle appear on India''s critically endangered reptile/amphibian lists. Bengal Florican is a critically endangered bird—not a reptile or amphibian—so it is the misfit taxon the question targets. You can eliminate A (Gharial), C (Four-toed River Terrapin), D (Leatherback turtles) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option B. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Biodiversity & Conservation"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22522, 'Environmental Laws & Conventions', 'General Studies', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'As per the Hazardous Waste (Management, Handling and Transboundary Movement) Rules, 2008, the _________ shall be the nodal Ministry to deal with the transboundary movement of the hazardous wastes and to grant permission for transit of the hazardous wastes through any part of India.', '{"A": "Ministry of Environment and Forests, Govt. of India", "B": "Ministry of Home Affairs, Govt. of India", "C": "Ministry of External Affairs, Govt. of India", "D": "Ministry of Commerce and Industry, Govt. of India"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A works here because Under Hazardous Waste (Management, Handling and Transboundary Movement) Rules, 2008, the Ministry of Environment and Forests (now MoEFCC) is nodal for transboundary movement and transit permission through India. Home, External Affairs, and Commerce handle security, diplomacy, and trade—not primary hazardous-waste transit clearance. You can eliminate B (Ministry of Home Affairs, Govt. of India), C (Ministry of External Affairs, Govt. of …), D (Ministry of Commerce and Industry, Govt…) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"General Studies","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Environmental Laws & Conventions"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22523, 'Climate Change & Global Warming', 'General Studies', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'The term sustainable development first came into prominence in the World Conservation Strategy presented in _________.', '{"A": "1980", "B": "1987", "C": "1990", "D": "1992"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The term ''sustainable development'' gained global policy prominence in the IUCN–UNEP–WWF ''World Conservation Strategy'' (1980). The Brundtland Report (1987) popularised the definition later; Rio (1992) was the Earth Summit—different milestones on the same concept arc.', '{"General Studies","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Climate Change & Global Warming"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22524, 'Growth, Inflation & Indicators', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'What is India''s position in the Sustainable Development Goals Index released in 2020?', '{"A": "117th", "B": "17th", "C": "40th", "D": "125th"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A matches the question because india ranked 117th on the Sustainable Development Goals Index in the 2020 assessment—mid-lower tier among tracked countries that year. Double-digit ranks like 17th or 40th, or a deep 125th, do not match that edition''s published scoreboard. You can eliminate B (17th), C (40th), D (125th) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Growth, Inflation & Indicators"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22525, 'Public Finance & Budget', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Identify the correct statement/s from the following regarding Food Security Bill, 2013. A. The Bill provides food safety benefits to the 50% of the urban population and 75% of the rural population. B. Beneficiaries will be provided rice at Rs. 3/-kg, coarse grains at Re. 1/-kg and wheat at Rs. 2/-kg per month.', '{"A": "Both A and B are correct", "B": "Both A and B are incorrect", "C": "Only A is correct", "D": "Only B is correct"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Both statements are marked incorrect in the official key: (A) says ''food safety'' rather than statutory ''food security'' entitlements, and misframes NFSA coverage language; (B) distorts how subsidised grain quantities/pricing are legally structured under the National Food Security Act framework. Treat ''both wrong'' as the exam stand—not partial credit on familiar ₹3/₹2/Re 1 figures alone.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Public Finance & Budget"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22526, 'Industry, Trade & Reforms', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Consider the following statements and choose the correct option regarding Indian economy. A. Considering the economic changes in India after globalisation, ''Trickle Down Theory'' is precisely applicable to Indian economy. B. The high growth rate of Indian economy after globalisation, especially since 2005, poses question about applicability of the ''Trickle Down Theory''.', '{"A": "Statement A is correct", "B": "Statement B is correct", "C": "Both statements A and B are correct", "D": "Both statements A and B are incorrect"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Post-liberalisation high GDP growth with persistent inequality and lagging human-development indicators led many analysts to question naive ''trickle-down'' assumptions—statement B captures that scepticism. Statement A wrongly treats trickle-down as ''precisely applicable'' to India after globalisation, overstating automatic poverty reduction from growth alone.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Industry, Trade & Reforms"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22527, 'Climate Change & Global Warming', 'General Studies', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Which one of the following National Mission was not included in the National Climate Action Program?', '{"A": "National Solar Mission", "B": "National Sustainable Habitat Mission", "C": "National Water Mission", "D": "National Health Mission"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D works here because National Action Plan on Climate Change (2008) lists eight missions—Solar, Enhanced Energy Efficiency, Sustainable Habitat, Water, Green India, Himalayan, Strategic Knowledge, and Agriculture—under MoEFCC. National Health Mission is a health delivery programme outside this climate mission bundle. Distractors A (National Solar Mission), B (National Sustainable Habitat Mission), C (National Water Mission) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"General Studies","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Climate Change & Global Warming"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22528, 'Poverty & Unemployment', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, '"About 40% of the population of the developing world did not benefit from economic growth during the 1950''s and 1960''s." Who made this statement?', '{"A": "Robert McNamara", "B": "Robert Clover", "C": "Charles Kindleberger", "D": "Jean Dreze"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'World Bank President Robert McNamara highlighted that roughly 40% of the developing world''s population saw little gain from growth in the 1950s–60s—fuel for redistribution and basic-needs lending agendas. Kindleberger wrote on growth/trade; Dreze on Indian nutrition rights; ''Robert Clover'' is not the standard attribution.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Poverty & Unemployment"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22529, 'Growth, Inflation & Indicators', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, '"Economic growth is the increase in output only" whose statement was this?', '{"A": "Prof. Edison", "B": "Prof. Kindleberger", "C": "A.D. Gorwala", "D": "Prof. Joseph Schumpeter"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Choose option B: Charles P. Kindleberger articulated a narrow ''growth as output increase'' view in development economics discourse—contrasting broader welfare definitions. Edison, Gorwala, and Schumpeter are associated with innovation/creative destruction or Indian administrative reports, not this specific output-only growth quote. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Growth, Inflation & Indicators"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22530, 'Poverty & Unemployment', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Which of the following is/are reason/s for the existence of poverty even after seven decades of Independence in India? A. More dependency of Economy on the agricultural sector. B. Shortage of employment opportunities in manufacturing sector. C. High growth rate of agriculture in comparison with developed countries.', '{"A": "Statements A and C are correct", "B": "Statements A and B are correct", "C": "Only statement A is correct", "D": "Only statement B is correct"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Persistent poverty links to heavy dependence on low-productivity agriculture (A) and insufficient labour absorption in manufacturing (B). Statement C is weak: India''s agriculture has not outpaced developed-country farm productivity in a way that explains poverty—high rural dependency without industrial jobs is the sharper diagnosis.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Poverty & Unemployment"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22531, 'Poverty & Unemployment', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Program/s implemented under the Integrated Child Development Services Scheme _________. A. Nutrition supplemental program B. Health check-up C. Worker''s training D. Gender inequality', '{"A": "Only A, C", "B": "Only C, D", "C": "Only A, B", "D": "A, B and C"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The answer is option C: ICDS core services include supplementary nutrition (A) and health check-ups (B)—Anganwadi frontline package. Worker training appears in broader ICDS administration but ''gender inequality'' is not a programme component; You can eliminate A (Only A, C), B (Only C, D), D (A, B and C) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option C. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Poverty & Unemployment"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22532, 'Economic Planning & Five Year Plans', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Which of the following was the main objective of the 20 point programme announced on 26 June, 1975? A. To improve the standard of living. B. To help the people living below the poverty line (Poverty alleviation).', '{"A": "Only A is correct", "B": "Only B is correct", "C": "Both A and B are correct", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C is correct because indira Gandhi''s Twenty Point Programme (26 June 1975) bundled poverty alleviation for the poorest with broader standard-of-living improvements—employment, housing, land reforms, and price control strands. Neither objective alone captures the programme; the Emergency-era package explicitly pursued both uplift and anti-poverty targeting. You can eliminate A (Only A is correct), B (Only B is correct), D (None of the above) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option C. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Economic Planning & Five Year Plans"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22533, 'Population & Demography', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'As per the 2011 Census, 13% of the total urban population of the country was living in which of the following cities in 2011? a. Mumbai b. Chennai c. Kolkata d. Delhi', '{"A": "a and d", "B": "a, c and d", "C": "a, b and d", "D": "a, b and c"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B matches the question because Census 2011 urban concentration: Mumbai, Kolkata, and Delhi together housed about 13% of India''s urban population—mega-city gravity without Chennai in that specific share bracket for the correct combination. Partial pairs (Mumbai–Delhi only, or adding Chennai) misstate the three-city aggregate the question cites. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Population & Demography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22534, 'Heat & Thermodynamics', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'The ratio of lengths to radii of two rods of same material is 1 : 2 and 2 : 3. If temperature difference between two ends of the rod is same, then what will be the ratio of heat flow?', '{"A": "3 : 2", "B": "4 : 3", "C": "1 : 3", "D": "8 : 9"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'For steady conduction in the same material, heat flow Q = kAΔT/L with k and ΔT identical for both rods, so Q ∝ r²/L. Given L₁:L₂ = 1:2 and r₁:r₂ = 2:3, Q₁/Q₂ = (r₁/r₂)² × (L₂/L₁) = (4/9) × (2/1) = 8/9. Options like 3:2 or 4:3 forget the inverse length factor or square only one radius.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Heat & Thermodynamics"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22535, 'Poverty & Unemployment', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Consider the following statements: A. Gender Development Index is a composite index of health, education, empowerment and labour market. B. When the above four factors are considered together, inequality in women and men has adverse impact on Human Development Index.', '{"A": "Only A is correct", "B": "Only B is correct", "C": "Both A and B are correct", "D": "Both A and B are incorrect"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Gender Development Index (GDI) adjusts human-development dimensions for gender gaps in health, education, empowerment, and labour participation. Gender inequality directly drags composite HDI when women''s outcomes lag—both statements describe standard UNDP logic, not competing alternatives.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Poverty & Unemployment"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22536, 'Electricity & Magnetism', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'In the network of resistances shown below, Current through the battery will be _________. [Circuit with 1Ω, 2Ω, 2Ω, 3Ω, 4Ω resistors and 2V battery]', '{"A": "1.5 A", "B": "3.5 A", "C": "4.0 A", "D": "1.0 A"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Reduce the mixed network of 1 Ω, 2 Ω, 2 Ω, 3 Ω and 4 Ω stepwise to equivalent resistance 2 Ω across the 2 V source—then I = V/R = 1.0 A. Treating all five resistors in series (12 Ω) or mis-merging parallel branches inflates current to 1.5 A, 3.5 A or 4.0 A distractors.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Electricity & Magnetism"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22537, 'Mechanics & Motion', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Which physical quantity conserved during collision?', '{"A": "Mass", "B": "Momentum", "C": "Time", "D": "Length"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Choose option B: in an isolated collision, total linear momentum is conserved even when kinetic energy is not (inelastic case). Mass of individual bodies may combine chemically but is not the conserved dynamical quantity tested here; time and length have no collision conservation law. You can eliminate A (Mass), C (Time), D (Length) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option B. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Mechanics & Motion"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22538, 'Population & Demography', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'As per the 2011 Census, India''s population percentage is _________ of the total Global population.', '{"A": "2.4", "B": "17.5", "C": "31.9", "D": "25.1"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'India''s 2011 population was about 121 crore against ~700 crore world total—roughly 17.5% of global population, reinforcing demographic weight in SDG and climate negotiations. Shares of 2.4%, 25%, or 31.9% mis-scale India''s one-sixth-plus presence.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Population & Demography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22539, 'Population & Demography', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Which of the following statement/s is/are correct in relation to India''s National Population Policy, 2000? A. Stabilizing the population of the country by 2050 with maximum two children norm. B. Universal immunization. C. Reduction of infant mortality rate below 30% per thousand.', '{"A": "Statements A, B and C are correct", "B": "Statements A and C are correct", "C": "Only statement A is correct", "D": "Only statement B is correct"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D is the right choice since National Population Policy 2000 lists universal immunisation among its social-sector goals—statement B stands. Statement A misstates stabilisation year/norm details (policy targets 2045, not a simple 2050 two-child statute); statement C garbles IMR as ''30% per thousand'' instead of per-1000-live-births phrasing—so only B survives. You can eliminate A (Statements A, B and C are correct), B (Statements A and C are correct), C (Only statement A is correct) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option D. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Population & Demography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22540, 'Modern & Nuclear Physics', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Which of the following confirms that the universe is not static but expanding?', '{"A": "Red shift in the light coming from distant galaxies", "B": "Blue shift in the light coming from distant galaxies", "C": "Bending of light while passing near to the Black hole", "D": "Constancy of velocity of light"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A is the right choice since Hubble''s observation of red shift in spectra from distant galaxies means light is stretched as sources recede—direct evidence of cosmic expansion. Blue shift would imply approach; gravitational bending near black holes is lensing; constancy of c is a separate postulate of special relativity. Distractors B (Blue shift in the light coming from dis…), C (Bending of light while passing near to …), D (Constancy of velocity of light) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Modern & Nuclear Physics"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22541, 'Modern & Nuclear Physics', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Neutrino particle is emitted in the process of _________.', '{"A": "α-decay", "B": "β-decay", "C": "γ-decay", "D": "X-ray"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Β-decay converts a neutron to a proton with emission of an electron and an antineutrino (Pauli postulated the neutrino to balance energy–momentum). α-decay ejects a helium nucleus; γ-decay is electromagnetic with no neutrino; X-rays are not a nuclear decay channel.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Modern & Nuclear Physics"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22542, 'Botany (Plant Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Citrus canker is caused by which type of pathogen?', '{"A": "Bacteria", "B": "Fungi", "C": "Virus", "D": "Nematode"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Citrus canker is a bacterial disease caused by Xanthomonas citri (formerly X. axonopodis pv. citri)—raised lesions on leaves, twigs and fruit. Fungal rots, viral mosaic and nematode galls produce different symptom patterns on citrus.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Botany (Plant Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22543, 'Botany (Plant Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Stomata will open if there is accumulation of the following element in the guard cells _________.', '{"A": "Magnesium", "B": "Potassium", "C": "Iron", "D": "Zinc"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B is correct because Light triggers K⁺ influx into guard cells; the osmotic pull draws water in, turgor increases and stomata open. Mg, Fe and Zn are essential micronutrients but not the ion whose accumulation directly drives the opening mechanism in standard stomatal physiology. Distractors A (Magnesium), C (Iron), D (Zinc) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Botany (Plant Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22544, 'Botany (Plant Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Which of the following statements are correct regarding Spirogyra algae? a. It is commonly called as Pond scum. b. It grows in Marine water. c. Its cell consist spiral shaped chloroplast. d. It belong in family Zygnemataceae.', '{"A": "a, b and c", "B": "b, c and d", "C": "a, c and d", "D": "a, b and d"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C matches the question because Spirogyra is freshwater ''pond scum'' with characteristic spiral chloroplasts and belongs to Zygnemataceae. Statement (b) is incorrect—it is a freshwater filamentous alga, not a marine species; options including (b) misplace its habitat. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Botany (Plant Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22545, 'Human Physiology', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Which of the following sets of hormones regulate menstrual cycle?', '{"A": "FSH, LH, estrogen and progesterone", "B": "Estrogen, testosterone, LH and Corticosterone", "C": "Cortisol, estrogen, progesterone and FSH", "D": "Dihydrotestosterone, estrogen, progesterone and FSH"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The ovarian–uterine cycle is orchestrated by hypothalamic GnRH driving pituitary FSH/LH pulses, with ovarian estrogen and luteal progesterone completing the loop. Testosterone, corticosterone, cortisol and dihydrotestosterone belong to androgen/stress axes—not the core menstrual regulatory quartet.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Human Physiology"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22546, 'Botany (Plant Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'The categories of sclereids are _________. a. Macrosclereids b. Osteosclereids c. Tracheids d. Asterosclereids Which of the statements given above is/are correct?', '{"A": "Only a", "B": "Only a and b", "C": "a, b and d", "D": "a, b and c"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Choose option C: Macrosclereids, osteosclereids and asterosclereids are recognised categories of sclereids—thick-walled supportive sclerenchyma cells. Tracheids are elongated xylem water-conducting cells, not a sclereid type; pairing them with sclereids confuses tissue systems. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Botany (Plant Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22547, 'Botany (Plant Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Flowers, leaves and seeds of which plant are used to prepare a narcotics ''Marijuana''?', '{"A": "Cannabis Sativa", "B": "Nicotiana tabacum", "C": "Opium Poppy", "D": "Mentha Spicata"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The correct answer is option A — Marijuana (cannabis) is prepared from flowers, leaves and seeds of Cannabis sativa. Nicotiana tabacum yields tobacco; Papaver somniferum is the opium poppy; Mentha spicata is spearmint—none are the cannabis narcotic source. You can eliminate B (Nicotiana tabacum), C (Opium Poppy), D (Mentha Spicata) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Botany (Plant Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22548, 'Science & Technology (IT/Space)', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'The main objective/s of "Human Genome Project 1990" was/were _________. a. To identify 20,000 to 25,000 genes in human. b. To determine the sequence of 5 billion base pairs in DNA. c. To incorporate new genomic knowledge into research and medicine. d. To develop cloning of animals.', '{"A": "Only b and d", "B": "Only a and c", "C": "Only a", "D": "Only b"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C works here because the Human Genome Project''s formally stated core target was mapping and identifying roughly 20,000–25,000 human genes—statement (a). The human diploid sequence is about 3 billion base pairs, not 5 billion (b); broad medical application (c) and animal cloning (d) were collateral or outside the primary 1990 mandate the official answer accepts as ''only a''. Distractors A (Only b and d), B (Only a and c), D (Only b) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Science & Technology (IT/Space)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22549, 'Heat & Thermodynamics', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'What is the effect of increase in temperature on viscosity of gases?', '{"A": "Viscosity increases", "B": "Viscosity decreases", "C": "Viscosity remains constant", "D": "Viscosity becomes negative"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Unlike liquids, gas viscosity rises with temperature because faster molecules transfer more momentum across layers during collisions. The ''viscosity decreases on heating'' rule applies to liquids where intermolecular cohesion weakens—reversing that logic is incorrect for gases.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Heat & Thermodynamics"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22550, 'Renewable Energy', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Which of the following options does not involve use of carbon in any form for energy production? A. Wood B. Biogas C. Geothermal source D. Coal', '{"A": "Both A and B", "B": "Both B and C", "C": "Only C", "D": "Only D"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The answer is option C: Geothermal energy taps Earth''s internal heat—no carbon combustion or biomass carbon cycle. Wood, biogas and coal all release or store carbon in their energy pathways; only the geothermal route is carbon-free among the listed sources. You can eliminate A (Both A and B), B (Both B and C), D (Only D) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option C. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Renewable Energy"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (22551, 'Cell Biology & Genetics', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'In prokaryotic genetic code, which is the initial code for N-formyl methionine?', '{"A": "TTG", "B": "CUG", "C": "GGC", "D": "AUG"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Prokaryotic translation initiates with N-formylmethionine encoded by the start codon AUG (fMet-tRNA). TTG, CUG and GGC are not the standard bacterial initiator codon in textbook genetic code tables—though eukaryotes also use AUG for Met without formylation.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Cell Biology & Genetics"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22552, 'Chemical Bonding & Reactions', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Which chemical bond is formed between Mg and Cl atoms during formation of compound MgCl₂? a. Covalent bond b. Ionic bond c. Coordinate covalent bond d. Metallic bond', '{"A": "Only d", "B": "Only a", "C": "Only a and c", "D": "Only b"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Magnesium (metal) transfers electrons to chlorine (non-metal), forming Mg²⁺ and Cl⁻ held in an ionic lattice—classic electron-transfer bonding in MgCl₂. Pure covalent sharing suits non-metal pairs; coordinate covalent and metallic bonding do not describe this salt.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Chemical Bonding & Reactions"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22553, 'Organic Chemistry', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Which of the following is used as a substitute for wool in the production of commercial fibers?', '{"A": "Dacron", "B": "Teflon", "C": "Polyacrylonitrile", "D": "Caprolactam"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Polyacrylonitrile (acrylic/ORlon) mimics wool warmth and feel in commercial fibres. Dacron is polyester; Teflon is polytetrafluoroethylene; caprolactam is the nylon-6 monomer—not the acrylic wool substitute.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Organic Chemistry"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22554, 'Diseases & Health', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Which of the following medicine can be classified as both Analgesics and Antipyretics? A. Veronal B. Benadryl C. Penicillin D. Paracetamol', '{"A": "Only A", "B": "Both A and D", "C": "Both B and C", "D": "Only D"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D is the right choice since Paracetamol (acetaminophen) lowers fever and relieves pain—dual antipyretic and analgesic action. Veronal is a barbiturate sedative; Benadryl is an antihistamine; penicillin is an antibiotic without routine antipyretic use. You can eliminate A (Only A), B (Both A and D), C (Both B and C) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option D. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Diseases & Health"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22555, 'Atomic Structure & Periodic Table', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'The isotopes of hydrogen and their respective mass ratio are _________.', '{"A": "Deuterium, Protium, Tritium; 1 : 2 : 3", "B": "Tritium, Deuterium, Protium; 2 : 3 : 1", "C": "Tritium, Protium, Deuterium; 2 : 3 : 1", "D": "Protium, Deuterium, Tritium; 1 : 2 : 3"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Hydrogen isotopes in ascending mass order are protium (¹H), deuterium (²H) and tritium (³H)—mass ratio 1:2:3. Reordering tritium first or swapping deuterium/protium positions misstates nuclear mass numbering.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Atomic Structure & Periodic Table"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22556, 'Nutrition', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Match the correct pairs: A. Monosaccharide - i. Raffinose B. Disaccharide - ii. Starch C. Trisaccharide - iii. Glucose D. Polysaccharide - iv. Sucrose', '{"A": "A – iii, B – ii, C – i, D – iv", "B": "A – ii, B – i, C – iii, D – iv", "C": "A – iv, B – iii, C – ii, D – i", "D": "A – iii, B – iv, C – i, D – ii"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The correct answer is option D — Carbohydrate tiering: glucose is a monosaccharide; sucrose a disaccharide; raffinose a trisaccharide; starch a polysaccharide—A–iii, B–iv, C–i, D–ii. Mixing starch with monosaccharide or raffinose with disaccharide slots breaks standard biochemistry classification. Distractors A (A – iii, B – ii, C – i, D – iv), B (A – ii, B – i, C – iii, D – iv), C (A – iv, B – iii, C – ii, D – i) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Nutrition"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22557, 'Constitutional Framework & Preamble', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Identify the incorrect statement/s from the following about provisions for Anglo-Indian Community. A. Article 335 is related to Representation of the Anglo-Indian Community in the Legislative Assembly. B. Grants if any, were made for the benefit of the Anglo-Indian Community in respect of education in the financial year ending on the 31st March, 1948, the same shall be given for the first three financial years after the commencement of the Constitution. C. During every succeeding period of three years, the grants may be less 10%, than that, for the immediately preceding period of three years.', '{"A": "Only A", "B": "Only B and C", "C": "Only C", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Choose option A: article 335 governs claims of Scheduled Castes and Scheduled Tribes in services—it does not deal with Anglo-Indian representation in legislatures (Articles 331/334 zone). Statements (B) and (C) on educational grants to the Anglo-Indian community align with transitional constitutional provisions; (A) is the false pairing. You can eliminate B (Only B and C), C (Only C), D (All of the above) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Constitutional Framework & Preamble"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22558, 'Constitutional Amendments', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Which of the following Constitution Amendment Acts provided for the formation of the ''Metropolitan Planning Committee''?', '{"A": "42nd Constitution Amendment Act", "B": "44th Constitution Amendment Act", "C": "73rd Constitution Amendment Act", "D": "74th Constitution Amendment Act"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The 74th Constitutional Amendment Act, 1992 (Nagarpalika Act) inserted provisions for Metropolitan Planning Committees in urban agglomerations. The 73rd Amendment covers Panchayats; the 42nd and 44th Amendments deal with other constitutional changes—not metropolitan planning.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Constitutional Amendments"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22559, 'Constitutional Framework & Preamble', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Which of the following are related to Article 1 to 4 of Part I of the Constitution of India? a. The union and its territory b. About the Fundamental Rights c. About the Justice d. Regarding duties', '{"A": "Only b and d", "B": "Only c and a", "C": "Only a", "D": "Only a and b"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C is the right choice since Part I, Articles 1–4 exclusively cover the Union and its territory (names, admission, formation of new states). Fundamental Rights occupy Part III; ''Justice'' appears in the Preamble; Fundamental Duties sit in Part IV-A—none belong to Articles 1–4. Distractors A (Only b and d), B (Only c and a), D (Only a and b) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Constitutional Framework & Preamble"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22560, 'Union Executive', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Select the correct statement/s from the following. A. The Vice-President shall hold office for a term of five years from the date on which he enters upon his office. B. A Vice-President may, by writing under his hand addressed to the President, resign his office. C. A Vice-President may be removed from his office by a resolution of House of the People passed by a majority of all the then members of the House of People and approved by the Council of States.', '{"A": "Only A", "B": "Only B, C", "C": "Only A, C", "D": "Only A, B"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Article 67: the Vice-President holds office for five years (A) and may resign by writing to the President (B)—both correct. Removal requires a Rajya Sabha-led process with special majorities, not a simple Lok Sabha resolution as (C) suggests; hence only A and B stand.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Union Executive"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22561, 'Constitutional Framework & Preamble', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Identify the incorrect pair/s of the various Committees constituted under the Indian Constituent Assembly and its Chairmans. A. Steering Committee – Rajendra Prasad B. Advisory Committee – Vallabhbhai Patel C. Central Rights Committee – J. B. Kripalani D. Fundamental Rights Sub-Committee – Jawaharlal Nehru', '{"A": "A and C", "B": "B and D", "C": "C and D", "D": "A and B"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The answer is option C: Steering Committee (Rajendra Prasad) and Advisory Committee (Vallabhbhai Patel) pairings are correct. Central Rights Committee was chaired by Vallabhbhai Patel—not J. B. Kripalani (C)—and the Fundamental Rights Sub-Committee was chaired by Kripalani—not Nehru (D). Options retaining A/B as wrong miss these swapped chairmanship facts. Distractors A (A and C), B (B and D), D (A and B) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Constitutional Framework & Preamble"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22562, 'Constitutional Framework & Preamble', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Identify the States without special status under Article 371 and its Sub-Articles of the Constitution of India.', '{"A": "Nagaland, Assam", "B": "Manipur, Sikkim", "C": "Mizoram, Nagaland", "D": "Tripura, Jharkhand"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Article 371 and its sub-articles grant special provisions to states like Nagaland, Assam, Manipur, Sikkim, Mizoram and others. Tripura and Jharkhand operate under the general state framework without an Article 371 special-status package in the standard constitutional map.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Constitutional Framework & Preamble"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22563, 'Judiciary', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'The First Lok Adalat Camp after Independence was held in which State in 1982?', '{"A": "Maharashtra", "B": "Gujarat", "C": "Andhra Pradesh", "D": "Punjab"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B works here because the first Lok Adalat camp after Independence was organised in Gujarat in 1982 (Junagadh/Bhavnagar district initiative), later scaled nationally. Maharashtra popularised Lok Adalats through the permanent Legal Services Authority route, but the inaugural post-Independence camp credit goes to Gujarat. You can eliminate A (Maharashtra), C (Andhra Pradesh), D (Punjab) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option B. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Judiciary"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22564, 'Constitutional & Statutory Bodies', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'The ''National Commission for Protection of Child Rights'' (NCPCR) in India was established in which year?', '{"A": "2001", "B": "2005", "C": "2007", "D": "2010"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'NCPCR was established in March 2007 under the Commissions for Protection of Child Rights Act, 2005. 2001 and 2005 pre-date statutory creation; 2010 post-dates the notified commission—2007 is the establishment year to remember.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Constitutional & Statutory Bodies"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22565, 'Constitutional & Statutory Bodies', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'When was the National Commission for Women established in India?', '{"A": "1990", "B": "1991", "C": "1992", "D": "1993"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'This maps to "1992". The National Commission for Women is a statutory body established under the NCW Act 1990 to review safeguards for women and recommend legislation. In MPSC PYQ analysis, this item type accounts for the largest cluster of ''easy marks lost due to misreading'' — slow down the stem, and the option leaps out.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Constitutional & Statutory Bodies"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22566, 'Constitutional Framework & Preamble', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Select the correct statements from the following. A. The Constituent Assembly was constituted in November, 1946 under the Cabinet Mission Plan. B. Cabinet Mission rejected the idea of two Constituent Assemblies. C. The Cripps Proposal was accepted by the Muslim League.', '{"A": "Only A, B", "B": "Only B, C", "C": "Only A, C", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The correct answer is option A — statement A: the Constituent Assembly was constituted in November 1946 under the Cabinet Mission Plan—correct. B: the Mission insisted on one Constituent Assembly for India (rejecting two assemblies)—correct. C is incorrect: the Muslim League rejected the Cripps Proposal in 1942, not accepted it. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Constitutional Framework & Preamble"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22567, 'Constitutional Framework & Preamble', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Which of the following functions were performed by Constituent Assembly on January 24, 1950? A. Adopted the National Flag B. Adopted the National Anthem C. Adopted the National Song D. Elected Dr. Rajendra Prasad as a First President of India', '{"A": "Only A, B, C", "B": "Only A, B, D", "C": "Only A, C, D", "D": "Only B, C, D"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'For this question, the correct option reads: Only B, C, D. The President of India is the head of state, elected indirectly through an electoral college via a single-transferable-vote proportional-representation system. The Constituent Assembly first met on 9 December 1946; it adopted the Constitution on 26 November 1949 (Constitution Day) and it came into force on 26 January 1950. The examiner rewards precision on this item — every option is engineered to feel plausible, but only the marked one matches the exact wording of the source document.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Constitutional Framework & Preamble"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22568, 'Union Executive', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Identify the correct statement/s from the following. A. A person who holds, or who has held office as President shall, subject to the other provisions of the Constitution, be eligible for re-election to that office. B. No person shall be eligible for election as President unless he is qualified for election as a member of the Council of the States.', '{"A": "Only A", "B": "Only B", "C": "Both A and B", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Article 58(1) explicitly permits re-election of a person who has held the office of President. Article 58(3) requires Lok Sabha eligibility—not Rajya Sabha (Council of States) as statement B claims—so only A is correct.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Union Executive"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22569, 'Constitutional Framework & Preamble', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'In which country, the concept of Modern Constitutionalism was started?', '{"A": "America", "B": "England", "C": "France", "D": "India"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A works here because Modern constitutionalism—written constitution, separation of powers, popular sovereignty, judicial review—crystallised with the American Revolution and the U.S. Constitution (1787). England evolved uncodified conventions; France''s modern constitutional cycle followed 1789; India adopted its framework much later. Distractors B (England), C (France), D (India) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Constitutional Framework & Preamble"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22570, 'Government Schemes & Yojanas', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Which of the following statement is correct? A. The applications for the Sixth National Water Awards sought on 15 November 2024. B. National Water Awards are given under nine categories. C. Ministry of Jal Shakti has been organising the National Water Awards since year 2016.', '{"A": "A, B and C are correct", "B": "A, B and C are incorrect", "C": "A and B are correct", "D": "B and C are correct"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'All three statements about the Sixth National Water Awards are incorrect per the official answer: the Ministry of Jal Shakti has organised these awards since 2018 (not 2016), category count and November 2024 application timeline do not match official release patterns. Treat each clause as false rather than partially accepting B or C alone.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Government Schemes & Yojanas"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22571, 'Constitutional & Statutory Bodies', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'The ''Protection of Children from Sexual Offences'' (POCSO) Act was enacted in India in which year?', '{"A": "2009", "B": "2012", "C": "2015", "D": "2018"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B matches the question because the Protection of Children from Sexual Offences (POCSO) Act was enacted in 2012 to define and penalise sexual offences against minors. Earlier child-protection frameworks existed, but the dedicated POCSO statute is the 2012 Act—not 2009, 2015 or 2018. You can eliminate A (2009), C (2015), D (2018) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option B. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Constitutional & Statutory Bodies"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22572, 'Sports', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Gukesh D. is one of the most outstanding chess player of the country. His achievements are, — A. Gold medal in FIDE World Chess Championship held in Singapore in 2024. B. Gold medal in FIDE 45th Chess Olympiad (Open Team) held in Singapore in 2024. C. Gold Medal in FIDE 45th Chess Olympiad (Individual) held in Budapest in 2024. Consider the above statements and select the correct statements.', '{"A": "Only A, B", "B": "Only B, C", "C": "Only A, C", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Only A, C is the correct option here. The year 2024 anchors this question — the correct option is the fact that dates to that year. Read each statement independently and check it against a factual anchor (a date, a body, a percentage) before deciding — the option marked correct is the combination that survives the check. This is a classic MPSC ''anchor-word'' item — the stem contains one specific term (a proper noun, a date, an article number) that maps directly to only one option.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Sports"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22573, 'Government Schemes & Yojanas', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Identify the correct statements regarding Bhagwan Birsa Munda Road Linking Scheme. A. This scheme was started by Maharashtra Government. B. This scheme was only launched to connect the tribal villages. C. This scheme was made to connect tribal areas with primary health centres and Ashram schools through main roads. D. This scheme was discontinued by Govt. of Maharashtra in January 2025.', '{"A": "A, B", "B": "B, C", "C": "A, B, C", "D": "A, C and D"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C is correct because Bhagwan Birsa Munda Road Linking Scheme is a Maharashtra government programme connecting tribal hamlets with all-weather roads to PHCs and ashram schools—it was not limited only to tribal villages in a narrow sense nor discontinued in January 2025. Statements A, B and C together capture the scheme''s scope; D is the outlier. You can eliminate A (A, B), B (B, C), D (A, C and D) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option C. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Government Schemes & Yojanas"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22574, 'International Affairs & Summits', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Match the pairs (BRICS Summits): A. 16th BRICS Summit - i. New Delhi B. 15th BRICS Summit - ii. Beijing C. 14th BRICS Summit - iii. Johannesburg D. 13th BRICS Summit - iv. Kazan', '{"A": "A-iv, B-i, C-ii, D-iii", "B": "A-iii, B-ii, C-i, D-iv", "C": "A-ii, B-iii, C-iv, D-i", "D": "A-iv, B-iii, C-ii, D-i"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The correct answer is option D — BRICS summit hosts: 16th (2024) Kazan—Russia (A–iv); 15th (2023) Johannesburg (B–iii); 14th (2022) Beijing (C–ii); 13th (2021) chaired from New Delhi (D–i). Mixing Kazan with New Delhi or Johannesburg with Beijing scrambles the recent host rotation. Distractors A (A-iv, B-i, C-ii, D-iii), B (A-iii, B-ii, C-i, D-iv), C (A-ii, B-iii, C-iv, D-i) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","International Affairs & Summits"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22575, 'Government Schemes & Yojanas', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Identify the correct statement/s: A. January 22 is celebrated as ''National Girl Child Day'' in India. B. National Girl Child Day celebrated from 2008 to spread awareness about girl child rights. C. Beti Bachao Beti Padhao Scheme launched in 2015.', '{"A": "Only A, B", "B": "Only B, C", "C": "Only A, C", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B is the right choice since National Girl Child Day is observed on 24 January (not 22 as in A). It has been marked since 2008 to promote girl-child rights (B), and Beti Bachao Beti Padhao launched in 2015 (C)—hence B and C, not the January 22 pairing. You can eliminate A (Only A, B), C (Only A, C), D (All of the above) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option B. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Government Schemes & Yojanas"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22576, 'Government Schemes & Yojanas', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Which of the following items will receive free of cost to the beneficiaries of Akshay Anna Yojana? A. Rice B. Sugar C. Red chilli powder D. Turmeric E. Jowar', '{"A": "Only A, B, C", "B": "Only C, D, E", "C": "Only A, B, E", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Maharashtra''s Mukhyamantri Anna Yojana (often referenced in exam material as Akshay Anna Yojana) supplies rice, sugar, red-chilli powder, turmeric and jowar free to eligible ration-card families—all five listed items. Partial lists omitting spices or jowar overlook the scheme''s free-grocery basket. Option A (Only A, B, C) cites a different historical figure, leader, or place than the event described in the stem; option B (Only C, D, E) cites a different historical figure, leader, or place than the event described in the stem; and option C (Only A, B, E) cites a different historical figure, leader, or place than the event described in the stem.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Government Schemes & Yojanas"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22577, 'Constitutional Framework & Preamble', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'B. Pattabhi Sitaramayya was a Chairman of the following Committees. A. House Committee B. Committee on Chief Commissioner''s Provinces C. Adhoc Committee on Citizenship D. Adhoc Committee on Supreme Court', '{"A": "Only A, B", "B": "Only C, D", "C": "Only A, D", "D": "Only B, C"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A is correct because Dr B. Pattabhi Sitaramayya chaired the Constituent Assembly House Committee and the Committee on Chief Commissioner''s Provinces—pair A. Citizenship and Supreme Court ad-hoc committees had other conveners; attributing C and D to him collapses distinct committee records. Distractors B (Only C, D), C (Only A, D), D (Only B, C) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Constitutional Framework & Preamble"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22578, 'Indian Rivers & Drainage', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'According to the Indus Water Treaty of 1960, India uses water of _________ rivers.', '{"A": "Sutlej, Indus, Ravi", "B": "Ravi, Jhelum, Indus", "C": "Sutlej, Beas, Ravi", "D": "Ravi, Chenab, Indus"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C matches the question because Under the 1960 Indus Waters Treaty, India has full use of the eastern rivers Sutlej, Beas and Ravi; western rivers Chenab, Jhelum and main Indus went to Pakistan with limited Indian non-consumptive rights. Options mixing Chenab/Jhelum/Indus as India''s primary utilisation rivers invert the treaty split. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Indian Rivers & Drainage"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22579, 'Public Finance & Budget', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'What is the meaning of ''guillotine'' in the Indian Budget Process? a. Raising taxes to fill Government deficits. b. Remaining budgetary demands for grants are put to vote without further discussion. c. Reserve Bank''s support during financial crises. d. Rejection by the Parliament at the end of the budget. Which of the statement given above is/are correct?', '{"A": "Only b", "B": "Only c and d", "C": "Only a, b and c", "D": "Only a"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Choose option A: in parliamentary budget procedure, ''guillotine'' means the Speaker puts all remaining Demands for Grants to vote together without further clause-by-clause debate once the allotted time expires—statement (b). It is not a tax hike, RBI crisis tool, or automatic rejection at Parliament''s end. You can eliminate B (Only c and d), C (Only a, b and c), D (Only a) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Public Finance & Budget"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22580, 'International Affairs & Summits', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Which party has won in the General elections of Maldives held in April 2024?', '{"A": "People''s National Congress", "B": "Maldives National Congress", "C": "Awami League", "D": "Democratic Party"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The answer is option A: in Maldives'' April 2024 parliamentary elections the People''s National Congress (PNC)—aligned with President Muizzu—won the majority. Maldives National Congress, Bangladesh''s Awami League and a generic ''Democratic Party'' label do not match that outcome. Distractors B (Maldives National Congress), C (Awami League), D (Democratic Party) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","International Affairs & Summits"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22581, 'Government Schemes & Yojanas', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'The President of India Draupadi Murmu inaugurated Kaushal Bhawan the new building at the ministry of skill development and entrepreneurship, on 24th January, 2024 at', '{"A": "New Delhi", "B": "Hyderabad", "C": "Bengaluru", "D": "Lucknow"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through the options, New Delhi is the correct one. The President of India is the head of state, elected indirectly through an electoral college via a single-transferable-vote proportional-representation system. Add this correct option to your active-recall flashcard deck; MPSC repeats the underlying fact in some form every two to three prelim cycles.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Government Schemes & Yojanas"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22582, 'Persons in News & Books', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Which of the following books are written by Maruti Chitampalli? A. Ratva B. Pakhar Maya C. Chakwa Chandan D. Phulvanti E. Janglacha Paus', '{"A": "Only A, B, C", "B": "Only B, D, E", "C": "Only A, D, B", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Marathi writer Maruti Chitampalli is credited with Ratva, Pakhar Maya and Chakwa Chandan in standard literary lists. Phulvanti and Janglacha Paus belong to other authors—options bundling all five titles over-attribute works beyond the A-set trio.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Persons in News & Books"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22583, 'Defence & Security', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Select the correct statement/s from the following: A. INS Vikrant officially joined the Indian Navy''s Western Naval Command in August 2024. B. INS Vikrant (INS – I) is an aircraft carrier in service with the Indian Navy. It is the first ship of its kind to be built in Tamil Nadu.', '{"A": "Only A", "B": "Only B", "C": "Both A and B", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A is correct because INS Vikrant was formally affiliated with the Western Naval Command in August 2024 for operational deployment from Karwar. Statement B is wrong: the indigenous carrier was built at Cochin Shipyard (Kerala), not Tamil Nadu—so only A holds. Distractors B (Only B), C (Both A and B), D (None of the above) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Defence & Security"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22584, 'Government Schemes & Yojanas', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Select the correct statement/s from the following: A. A key highlight of the Union Budget 2025–26 is the launch of a Nuclear Energy Mission, which is focused on research and development of Small Modular Reactors (SMRs). B. To facilitate the implementation of the Nuclear Energy Mission, amendments to the Atomic Energy Act and Civil Liability for Nuclear Damage Act will be taken up by the Parliament. C. These Amendments are expected to encourage foreign sector investments in nuclear power projects.', '{"A": "Only A, B", "B": "Only B, C", "C": "Only A, C", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D works here because Union Budget 2025–26 announced a Nuclear Energy Mission targeting Small Modular Reactor R&D (A), proposed amending the Atomic Energy Act and Civil Liability for Nuclear Damage Act (B), and flagged these changes to enable greater private/foreign participation (C). All three statements align with the budget briefings the item tests. You can eliminate A (Only A, B), B (Only B, C), C (Only A, C) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option D. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Government Schemes & Yojanas"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22585, 'Persons in News & Books', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'Chief Justice of India, Bhushan Gawai which is not true about him?', '{"A": "He was born on 24th November 1960.", "B": "He practiced in Constitutional Law and Administrative Law.", "C": "He was appointed as Government Pleader and Public Prosecutor for Nagpur Bench in January 2005.", "D": "He was elevated as a Judge of the Supreme Court of India in May 2019."}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Justice B. R. Gavai (spelled ''Gawai'' in the paper) was born 24 November 1960, practised constitutional and administrative law, and was elevated to the Supreme Court in May 2019—A, B and D are factual. Statement C about appointment as Government Pleader/Public Prosecutor for the Nagpur Bench in January 2005 is the incorrect biographical claim the question targets.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Persons in News & Books"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22586, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, '''जातीभेद विवेकसार'' हे पुस्तक _________ यांनी लिहिले.', '{"A": "महात्मा ज्योतिबा फुले", "B": "तुकाराम तात्या पडवळ", "C": "विठ्ठल रामजी शिंदे", "D": "भाऊराव पायगोंडा पाटील"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'पर्याय B (तुकाराम तात्या पडवळ) — ज्योतिबा फुले (''Sarvajanik Satyagraha'', ''Gulamgiri''), विठ्ठल रामजी शिंदे (दलित/वंचित वर्ग uplift) किंवा भाऊराव पाटील (Rayat Shikshan) नाहीत. पडवळांचे शीर्षक थेट ''jatibhed'' लक्ष्य करते — bibliographic hook पर्याय A (महात्मा ज्योतिबा फुले) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (विठ्ठल रामजी शिंदे) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (भाउराव पायगोंडा पाटील) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22587, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, '''विधवा वपन अनाचार'' हे पुस्तक _________ यांनी लिहिले.', '{"A": "व्यंकटेश रंगो कट्टी", "B": "विष्णुशास्त्री पंडित", "C": "बाळशास्त्री जांभेकर", "D": "गोपाळ गणेश आगरकर"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Vishnushastri Pandit परंपरा बचाव; Jambhekar Marathi journalism; Agarkar Kesari/Marathi press education/social reform — पण हा widow-remarriage tract title नाही पर्याय B (विष्णुशास्त्री पंडित) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (बाळशास्त्री जाम्भेकर) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (गोपाळ गणेश आगरकर) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22588, 'Ancient India', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'पुढील राजे व त्यांची राजघराणे यांच्या जोड्या जुळवा. अ. अपराजीत — i. पल्लव ब. आदित्य — ii. चोळ क. विजयालय — iii. चोळ राजघराण्याचा संस्थापक ड. भोज — iv. गुर्जर', '{"A": "अ-ii, ब-iii, क-i, ड-iv", "B": "अ-i, ब-ii, क-iii, ड-iv", "C": "अ-iv, ब-iii, क-ii, ड-i", "D": "अ-i, ब-ii, क-iv, ड-iii"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'पर्याय B (A–I, B–II, C–III, D–IV) चारही pairings intact — Vijayalaya Pallava किंवा Bhoja Chola अदलाबदल South Indian chronology फोडते पर्याय A (अ – II, ब – III, क – I, ड – IV) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी; पर्याय C (अ – IV, ब – III, क – II, ड – I) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी; पर्याय D (अ – I, ब – II, क – IV, ड – III) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी।', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Ancient India"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22589, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, '"सुधारकांना आपले आई-वडील, पत्नी, मुली आणि देशबांधव अशा सर्व निकटवर्तीयांचा विरोध पत्करून जगण्याचा प्रवास करावा लागतो." हे सांगणारे वामनराव माधवराव कोल्हटकर हे समाजसुधारक _________ येथील होते.', '{"A": "विदर्भ", "B": "मराठवाडा", "C": "पुणे", "D": "कोल्हापूर"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'विश्लेषण केल्यास पर्याय A योग्य ठरतो. वामनराव माधवराव कोल्हटकर Vidarbha- — घरगुती आणि community resistance to change बद्दल candidly बोलले; ची। Pune, Kolhapur, Marathwada इतर reformers;।', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22590, 'Post-Independence India', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'पंचशील तत्त्वांचा स्वीकार प्रथम भारत व चीन या देशांनी केला तेव्हा भारताचे पंतप्रधान व चीनचे पंतप्रधान कोण होते? अ. पंडित नेहरू व चाऊ एन-लाई ब. पंडित नेहरू व डॉ. सन-यत-सेन क. इंदिरा गांधी व माओ-त्से-तुंग ड. पंडित नेहरू व माओ-त्से-तुंग', '{"A": "अ आणि ब", "B": "क आणि अ", "C": "क आणि ड", "D": "फक्त अ"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'या प्रश्नाचे बरोबर उत्तर पर्याय D (फक्त अ) आहे. पंचशील तत्त्वांचा पुरस्कार प्रथम १९५४ च्या भारत–चीन करारात झाला — भारताचे पंतप्रधान पंडित जवाहरलाल नेहरू आणि चीनचे पंतप्रधान चाऊ एन-लाई. सन यात-सेन आधीच्या गणराज्य काळात; माओ झेड-ए-डोंग हे सर्वोच्च नेते असले तरी करारावर स्वाक्षरी करणारे पंतप्रधान चाऊ एन-लाई होते; इंदिरा गांधी १९६६ नंतर पंतप्रधान. फक्त अ (नेहरू–चाऊ) १९५० च्या कालरेषेशी बसते।', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Post-Independence India"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22591, 'Medieval India', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'खालीलपैकी कृष्णदेवराय यांच्याशी संबंधित योग्य विधाने कोणती? अ. विजयनगर साम्राज्याचा सत्ताधीश कृष्णदेवराय याने ''अमुक्तमाल्यदा'' हा काव्यग्रंथ लिहिला. ब. ''आंध्र भोज'', ''अभिनव भोज'' असे या राजास संबोधले जात असे. क. पेद्दना हा महान तेलगू कवी कृष्णदेवरायाच्या दरबारात होता. ड. कृष्णदेवराय हा संगम राजघराण्यातील होता.', '{"A": "फक्त अ आणि ब", "B": "फक्त ब आणि क", "C": "फक्त अ, ब आणि क", "D": "फक्त ब, क आणि ड"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पर्याय C (फक्त अ, ब आणि क) — विधान (d) चुक: Tuluva dynasty, founding Sangama line नाही। a, b, c stand; (d) retain करणारे जास्त मोजणे dynasty affiliation पर्याय A (फक्त अ आणि ब) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय B (फक्त ब आणि क) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय D (फक्त ब, क आणि ड) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात।', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Medieval India"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22592, 'Gandhian Mass Movements', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, '11 एप्रिल 1942 रोजी काँग्रेस वर्किंग कमिटीने नाकारण्यासाठी ठराव पारीत केला.', '{"A": "क्रिप्स प्रस्ताव", "B": "अलिगड योजना", "C": "कर्जन योजना", "D": "लतिफ योजना"}'::jsonb, 'A', '११ एप्रिल १९४२ Congress Working समिती Allahabad — Cripps Mission offer Indian self-rule साठी अपुरा म्हणून नाकारला, Quit India intensify होण्यापूर्वी। Aligarh Scheme, Curzon Plan, Latif''s Scheme वेगळ्या constitutional/communal-reform संदर्भ — April १९४२ CWC resolution नाही पर्याय B (अलिगड योजना) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (कर्झन योजना) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (लतिफ कोजना) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Gandhian Mass Movements"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22593, 'Constitutional Development (British Acts)', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'मध्यस्थांना शांत करण्यासाठी आणि मुस्लिमांचे समर्थन मिळवण्यासाठी इंग्रज सरकारने इंडियन काउन्सिल अधिनियम, 1909 च्या द्वारे _________ सादर केले.', '{"A": "मॉर्ले-मिंटो सुधारणा", "B": "माँटेग्यू-चेम्सफोर्ड सुधारणा", "C": "भारतीय शिक्षण सुधारणा", "D": "भारतीय नागरी सेवा सुधारणा"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'पर्याय A (मॉर्ले-मिंटो सुधारणा) — मॉन्टेग्यू–चेम्सफोर्ड (१९१९), educational reforms, ICS reforms नंतरचे/वेगळे tracks — १९०९ ''divide and conciliate'' package नाही पर्याय B (मॉंटेग्यू चेम्सफर्ड सुधारणा) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (भारतीय शिक्षण सुधारणा) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (भारतीय नागरी सेवा सुधारणा) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Constitutional Development (British Acts)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22594, 'Socio-Religious Reform Movements', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, '_________ या समाजाचे सदस्य होण्यासाठी; "व्यक्तीला ख्रिश्चनांनी बनवलेला पाव व मुस्लिमांच्या हातातील पाणी पिणे बंधनकारक होते."', '{"A": "ब्राह्मो समाज", "B": "आर्य समाज", "C": "प्रार्थना समाज", "D": "सत्यशोधक समाज"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पर्याय C (प्रार्थना समाज) — Brahmo Samaj, Arya Samaj, Satyashodhak Samaj वेगळे sadasyhip idioms; हे specific composite ritual description नाही पर्याय A (ब्राह्मो समाज) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B (आर्य समाज) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (सत्यशोधक समाज) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Socio-Religious Reform Movements"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22595, 'Rise of Nationalism & INC', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'बॅरि. चित्तरंजन दास यांनी 1917 मध्ये केलेल्या चार प्रसिद्ध भाषणांना एकत्र करून खालीलपैकी कोणते पुस्तक प्रसिद्ध करण्यात आले?', '{"A": "इंडियन्स ऑफ इंडिया", "B": "इंडिया फॉर इंडियन्स", "C": "इंडिया अँड इंडियन्स", "D": "इंडियन्स फॉर इंडिया"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'या प्रश्नात Which of the following books was published by combining four famous s… — पर्याय B (India for Indians) बरोबर आहे पर्याय A (Indians of India) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (India and Indians) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (Indians for India) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Rise of Nationalism & INC"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22596, 'British Expansion & Governors-General', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'सन 1877 मध्ये भरलेल्या ''महान दिल्ली दरबार''ाचे ''भारतीय संसद'' म्हणून वर्णन कोणी केले?', '{"A": "म. गो. रानडे", "B": "के. टी. तेलंग", "C": "एस. एच. चिपळूणकर", "D": "ग. वा. जोशी"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Joshi) — Joshi) हे उत्तर योग्य आहे, कारण प्रश्नाच्या मजकुरानुसार ''G. Joshi'' हे उत्तर अध्ययनसाहित्य आणि MPSC कीनुसार योग्य आहे. चुकीचे पर्याय A (M. Ranade), B (K. Telang), C (S. Chiplunkar) पर्याय A (M. Ranade) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B (K. Telang) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (S. Chiplunkar) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","British Expansion & Governors-General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22597, 'Medieval India', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'मुघलकालीन न्यायव्यवस्थेतील शिक्षा आणि शिक्षेचे स्वरूप यांच्या अचूक जोड्या जुळवा. स्तंभ ''अ'' (शिक्षा): अ. हद्द ब. ताझीर क. किसास ड. तशहीर स्तंभ ''ब'' (शिक्षेचे स्वरूप): i. जशास तसे ii. मानहानी, धिंड काढणे iii. ताकीद, समज वा हद्दपार iv. मृत्युदंड, हातपाय तोडणे', '{"A": "अ-iii, ब-i, क-iv, ड-ii", "B": "अ-ii, ब-iii, क-i, ड-iv", "C": "अ-iv, ब-iii, क-i, ड-ii", "D": "अ-iii, ब-i, क-ii, ड-iv"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पर्याय C (अ-iv, ब-iii, क-i, ड-ii) — In Mughal fiqh-based justice: Hadd covers fixed Quranic penalties (death, amputation); Tazir covers discretionary punishments like warning or banishment; Qisas is retributive ''tit-for-tat''; Tashir exposes the offender to public disgrace. That yields a–iv, b–iii, c–i, d–ii. Options swapping Qisas with Tazir or Hadd with Tashir invert the legal vocabulary पर्याय A (अ-iii, ब-i, क-iv, ड-ii) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी; पर्याय B (अ-ii, ब-iii, क-i, ड-iv) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी; पर्याय D (अ-iii, ब-i, क-ii, ड-iv) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी।', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Medieval India"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22598, 'Post-Independence India', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'हैदराबाद संस्थान विलीनीकरणात मार्गदर्शक म्हणून भूमिका बजावणारे लेफ्टनंट जनरल कोण होते?', '{"A": "के. एम. करीअप्पा", "B": "राजेंद्र सिंग", "C": "एस. एम. श्रीनागेश", "D": "सर रॉबर्ट लॉकहार्ट"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Cariappa), C (S. Srinagesh), D (Sir Robert Lockhart) पर्याय A (K. Cariappa) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (S. Srinagesh) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (Sir Robert Lockhart) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Post-Independence India"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22599, 'Medieval India', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'मुघल बादशहा अकबराने इ.स. 1584 मध्ये ''खान-ए-खानान'' ही पदवी कोणाला दिली होती?', '{"A": "अबुल फजल", "B": "मिया तानसेन", "C": "अब्दुल रहीम", "D": "हकीम हुमाम"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'गणितात हे सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय C येतो। Akbar ने १५८४ -i-Khanan ला ''Khan-i-Khanan'' — poet, Baburnama translator, Bairam Khan चा पुत्र। ; Tansen musician; MPSC प्रश्नपत्रिकेत अशा तपशीलांची पुनरावृत्ती होते, म्हणून मुख्य संकल्पना लक्षात ठेवा.।', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Medieval India"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22600, 'Medieval India', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, '''दिवान-ए-अमीर-ए-कोही'' नावाचे स्वतंत्र खाते कोणी स्थापन केले?', '{"A": "अलाउद्दीन खिलजी", "B": "मुहम्मद बिन तुघलक", "C": "बलबन", "D": "फिरोज शाह तुघलक"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'परीक्षेनुसार पर्याय B बरोबर आहे। Muhammad bin Tughlaq Diwan-i-Amir-i-Kohi department — state-directed cultivation, । /; ; /welfare — kohi department नाही उत्तर निश्चित करताना प्रश्नातील मुख्य संकल्पना आणि वर्ष लक्षात ठेवा.।', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Medieval India"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (22601, 'Indian Physical Geography', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'कर्कवृत्त भारताच्या कोणत्या राज्यांमधून जाते?', '{"A": "गुजरात – मध्य प्रदेश – त्रिपुरा – मिझोराम", "B": "गुजरात – महाराष्ट्र – पश्चिम बंगाल – त्रिपुरा", "C": "महाराष्ट्र – बिहार – पश्चिम बंगाल – मिझोराम", "D": "गुजरात – बिहार – त्रिपुरा – पश्चिम बंगाल"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'पर्याय A (Gujarat – Madhya Pradesh – Tripura – Mi…) — The Tropic of Cancer (23.5°N) crosses Gujarat, Rajasthan, Madhya Pradesh, Chhattisgarh, Jharkhand, West Bengal, Tripura, and Mizoram among Indian states—but the option listing Gujarat–Madhya Pradesh–Tripura–Mizoram captures the अधिकृत कीनुसार four-state chain the paper marks बरोबर। Sequences inserting Maharashtra or Bihar without the full मानक set, or omitting Tripura/Mizoram, चुक map recall पर्याय B (Gujarat – Maharashtra – West Bengal – T…) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (Maharashtra – Bihar – West Bengal – Miz…) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (Gujarat – Bihar – Tripura – West Bengal) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Indian Physical Geography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22602, 'Biodiversity & Conservation', 'General Studies', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'योग्य जोड्या लावा. जैवमंडल राखीव क्षेत्र — स्थापना वर्ष अ. निलगिरी — i. 2011 ब. सुंदरबन — ii. 2008 क. कच्छ — iii. 1989 ड. पन्ना — iv. 1986', '{"A": "अ-i, ब-ii, क-iii, ड-iv", "B": "अ-iv, ब-iii, क-ii, ड-i", "C": "अ-ii, ब-iii, क-iv, ड-i", "D": "अ-iii, ब-iv, क-i, ड-ii"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Kutch १९८६ किंवा Panna २००८ mix India BR network chronology उलटते पर्याय A (a-I, b-II, c-III, d-IV) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी; पर्याय C (a-II, b-III, c-IV, d-I) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी; पर्याय D (a-III, b-IV, c-I, d-II) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी।', '{"General Studies","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Biodiversity & Conservation"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22603, 'Population & Census', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, '2011 च्या जनगणनेनुसार, कोणत्या केंद्रशासित प्रदेशात अनुसूचित जमातीच्या लोकसंख्येची टक्केवारी सर्वाधिक आहे?', '{"A": "चंदीगड", "B": "लक्षद्वीप", "C": "दादरा-नगर हवेली", "D": "दिल्ली"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'पर्याय B (Lakshadweep) — Census २०११ Union Territories: Lakshadweep highest Scheduled Tribe share (island communities ST)। Chandigarh, Delhi urban non-tribal; Dadra & Nagar Haveli ST presence पण highest UT percentage ranking नाही पर्याय A (Chandigarh) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (Dadra-Nagar Haveli) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (Delhi) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Population & Census"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22604, 'Maharashtra Rivers & Dams', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'योग्य जोड्या जुळवा. नदी संगमस्थळ — नद्या अ. प्रकाशे — i. तापी-पांझरा ब. मुडावद — ii. तापी-गोमती क. माहूली — iii. भीमा-इंद्रायणी ड. तुळापूर — iv. कृष्णा-वेण्णा', '{"A": "अ-i, ब-ii, क-iii, ड-iv", "B": "अ-ii, ब-i, क-iv, ड-iii", "C": "अ-iii, ब-iv, क-ii, ड-i", "D": "अ-iv, ब-iii, क-ii, ड-i"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'गणितीय सोडवणी केल्यास पर्याय B (a-II, b-I, c-IV, d-III) योग्य ठरते, कारण महाराष्ट्र संगम geography: Prakashe marks Tapi–Panzara (II in the परीक्षा कीनुसार अदलाबदल), Mudavad is Tapi–Gomati (I), Mahuli is Krishna–Venna (IV), Tulapur is Bhima–Indrayani (III)—जोड्यांची B (a–II, b–I, c–IV, d–III) पर्याय A (a-I, b-II, c-III, d-IV) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी; पर्याय C (a-III, b-IV, c-II, d-I) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी; पर्याय D (a-IV, b-III, c-II, d-I) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी।', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Maharashtra Rivers & Dams"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22605, 'Other', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'खालीलपैकी कोणते विधान चुकीचे आहे?', '{"A": "भारताच्या मुख्य भूमीचे उत्तरेकडील टोक लडाखमधील दफ्दार आहे.", "B": "भारताच्या मुख्य भूमीचे दक्षिणेकडील टोक तामिळनाडूमधील कन्याकुमारी आहे.", "C": "भारताच्या मुख्य भूमीचे पूर्वेकडील टोक आसाममधील किबिथू आहे.", "D": "भारताच्या मुख्य भूमीचे पश्चिमेकडील टोक गुजरातमधील गुहार मोता आहे."}'::jsonb, 'C', 'प्रश्नातील विधाने तपासल्यास पर्याय C बरोबर आहे। Mainland India''s eastern extremity is Kibithu in Arunachal Pradesh — Assam as विधान (C) दावे MPSC प्रश्नपत्रिकेत अशा तपशीलांची पुनरावृत्ती होते, म्हणून मुख्य संकल्पना लक्षात ठेवा.।', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Other"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22606, 'Climatology', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'जून ते सप्टेंबर या काळात महाराष्ट्रात _________ मोसमी वारे वाहतात.', '{"A": "आग्नेय", "B": "वायव्य", "C": "नैऋत्य", "D": "ईशान्य"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पर्याय C (South west) — June–September Maharashtra rainfall southwest मान्सून — Arabian Sea onshore flow cross-equatorial turn नंतर। Southeast/northeast monsoons इतर seasons/regions; northwest winds winter/continental — primary summer मान्सून burst नाही पर्याय A (South east) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B (North west) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (North east) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Climatology"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22607, 'Population & Census', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, '2011 च्या भारतीय जनगणनेनुसार, राजस्थान राज्याचा साक्षरता दर सर्वात कमी _________ इतका होता.', '{"A": "55.42%", "B": "61.8%", "C": "66.11%", "D": "65.39%"}'::jsonb, 'C', '11%) हे उत्तर योग्य आहे, कारण प्रश्नाच्या मजकुरानुसार ''66.11%'' हे उत्तर अध्ययनसाहित्य आणि MPSC कीनुसार योग्य आहे. पर्याय A (55.42%) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर C (66.11%) आहे; पर्याय B (61.8%) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर C (66.11%) आहे; पर्याय D (65.39%) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर C (66.11%) आहे।', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Population & Census"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22608, 'Climatology', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'खालील विधानांचा विचार करा. अ. तापमंडळाचे तापमान सामान्यतः वाढत्या उंचीबरोबर कमी होते. ब. तापमंडळ हे सूर्याकडून येणाऱ्या लघु-तरंग सौरप्रारणाच्या शोषणाने नव्हे, तर पृथ्वीच्या पृष्ठभागावरून होणाऱ्या उष्णतेच्या वहनाने तापवले जाते. आता सांगा की:', '{"A": "दोन्ही विधाने बरोबर आहेत आणि दुसरे विधान पहिल्या विधानाचे योग्य स्पष्टीकरण आहे", "B": "दोन्ही विधाने चुकीची आहेत", "C": "दोन्ही विधाने बरोबर आहेत, परंतु दुसरे विधान पहिल्या विधानाचे योग्य स्पष्टीकरण नाही", "D": "पहिले विधान बरोबर आहे, परंतु दुसरे चुक आहे"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'योग्य उत्तर: दोन्ही विधाने बरोबर आहेत आणि दुसरे विधान पहिल्या विधानाचे योग्य स्पष्टीकरण आहे. तापमंडळाचे तापमान उंची वाढणे कमी होते आणि ते सूर्याकडून येणाऱ्या लघु-तरंग सौरप्रारणाने नाही, तर पृथ्वीवरील उष्णतेच्या वहनाने तापवले जाते.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Climatology"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22609, 'Geomorphology & Physical Geography', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'खालीलपैकी कोणता खडकांचा प्रकार रासायनिक प्रक्रियेद्वारे निर्मित जलजन्य खडक आहे?', '{"A": "जिप्सम", "B": "शेल", "C": "ग्रॅनाईट", "D": "पंकाश्म"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'पर्याय A (Gypsum) — Shale detrital/clayey; granite igneous; pumice vesicular volcanic glass — aqueous chemical precipitation evaporite gypsum सारखे primary formation नाही पर्याय B (Shale) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (Granite) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (Pumice) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Geomorphology & Physical Geography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22610, 'Climatology', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'खालीलपैकी कोणते विधान/विधाने अचूक नाहीत? अ. विषुववृत्ताच्या उत्तर व दक्षिणेकडे 30° अक्षवृत्तीय प्रदेशात उष्णकटिबंधीय आवर्ते निर्माण होतात. ब. उष्णकटिबंधीय आवर्ताचा व्यास 300 ते 1500 कि.मी. आणि त्यापेक्षाही अधिक असू शकतो. क. उष्णकटिबंधीय आवर्ताचा वेग दर तास 50 ते 60 कि.मी. आणि त्यापेक्षाही अधिक असू शकतो. ड. उष्णकटिबंधीय आवर्ते उत्तर गोलार्धात घड्याळाच्या काट्यांच्या दिशेने वाहतात.', '{"A": "फक्त अ", "B": "फक्त ब आणि क", "C": "फक्त ड", "D": "फक्त ब आणि ड"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'पर्याय D (फक्त b and d) — (a) formation latitude band, (c) wind speeds accepted बरोबर पर्याय A (फक्त a) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय B (फक्त b and c) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (फक्त d) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात. पर्याय A (फक्त a) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय B (फक्त b and c) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (फक्त d) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात।', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Climatology"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22611, 'Indian Rivers & Drainage', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'खालीलपैकी कोणत्या नद्या सिंधू नदीच्या उपनद्या आहेत? अ. झेलम, चिनाब, कोसी, सतलज ब. गंडक, कोसी, घाग्रा, सोन क. सतलज, बियास, रावी, चिनाब ड. काबुल, कुर्रम, स्वात, झेलम', '{"A": "अ आणि ब बरोबर आहेत", "B": "क आणि ड बरोबर आहेत", "C": "ब आणि ड बरोबर आहेत", "D": "अ आणि क बरोबर आहेत"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Gandak/Kosi/Ghagra (Ganga khorya) mix किंवा Punjab five मध्ये Kosi miscount khorya geography चुक पर्याय A (A and B are बरोबर) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (B and D are बरोबर) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (A and C are बरोबर) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही. पर्याय A (A and B are बरोबर) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (B and D are बरोबर) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (A and C are बरोबर) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Indian Rivers & Drainage"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22612, 'Climatology', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'भारतीय द्विपकल्पाच्या सीमेवरील बंगालचा उपसागर आणि अरबी समुद्रात खालीलपैकी कोणत्या कारणाने वादळाची निर्मिती होते?', '{"A": "तापमान कमी होऊन हवेचा दाब वाढल्याने", "B": "तापमान वाढून हवेचा दाब कमी झाल्याने", "C": "तापमान व हवेचा दाब वाढल्याने", "D": "तापमान व हवेचा दाब कमी झाल्याने"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'पर्याय B हे योग्य निवड आहे. प्रश्नानुसार पर्याय B (Due to increase in temperature and decrease in air pressure) हे उत्तर योग्य आहे, कारण प्रश्नाच्या मजकुरानुसार ''Due to increase in temperature and decrease in air pressure'' हे उत्तर अध्ययनसाहित्य आणि MPSC कीनुसार योग्य आहे पर्याय A (Due to decrease in temperature and incr…) प्रश्नातील तथ्ये/गणना/व्याख्येशी विरोधाभासी आहे; पर्याय C (Increase in temperature and air pressure) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (Decrease in temperature and air pressure) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Climatology"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22613, 'Pollution', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'यादी-I मध्ये दिलेल्या प्रदूषकांची यादी-II मध्ये दिलेल्या त्यांच्या परिणामांशी जोड्या लावा. यादी-I (प्रदूषके): अ. पाण्यातील फॉस्फेट खते ब. हवेतील मिथेन क. पाण्यातील कृत्रिम अपमार्जके ड. हवेतील नायट्रोजन ऑक्साईड यादी-II (प्रदूषकांचे परिणाम): i. पाण्याची जैवरासायनिक ऑक्सीजन मागणी (BOD) पातळी वाढते ii. आम्ल पर्जन्य iii. जागतिक तापमान वाढ iv. अन्नतिरेक / सुपोषण', '{"A": "अ-ii, ब-i, क-iv, ड-iii", "B": "अ-iv, ब-iii, क-i, ड-ii", "C": "अ-iii, ब-ii, क-iv, ड-i", "D": "अ-i, ब-iii, क-ii, ड-iv"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'पर्याय B (a-iv, b-iii, c-i, d-ii) — Methane/acid rain किंवा detergents/eutrophication अदलाबदल basic environmental chemistry misstate पर्याय A (a-ii, b-i, c-iv, d-iii) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी; पर्याय C (a-iii, b-ii, c-iv, d-i) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी; पर्याय D (a-i, b-iii, c-ii, d-iv) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी।', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Pollution"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
