  (22651, 'Nutrition', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'योग्य जोड्या लावा. अ. मोनोसॅकराइड — i. रॅफिनोज ब. डायसॅकराइड — ii. स्टार्च क. ट्रायसॅकराइड — iii. ग्लुकोज ड. पॉलीसॅकराइड — iv. सुक्रोज', '{"A": "अ — iii, ब — ii, क — i, ड — iv", "B": "अ — ii, ब — i, क — iii, ड — iv", "C": "अ — iv, ब — iii, क — ii, ड — i", "D": "अ — iii, ब — iv, क — i, ड — ii"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Starch monosaccharide slot किंवा raffinose disaccharide slot — मानक biochemistry classification break पर्याय A (A – iii, B – ii, C – i, D – iv) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी; पर्याय B (A – ii, B – i, C – iii, D – iv) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी; पर्याय C (A – iv, B – iii, C – ii, D – i) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी।', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Nutrition"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22652, 'Diseases & Health', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'खालीलपैकी कोणत्या औषधाचे वर्गीकरण वेदनाशामक आणि ज्वरशामक असे केले जाऊ शकते? अ. वेरोनल ब. बेनेड्रील क. पेनिसिलिन ड. पॅरासिटामॉल', '{"A": "फक्त अ", "B": "अ आणि ड दोन्ही", "C": "ब आणि क दोन्ही", "D": "फक्त ड"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Veronal barbiturate sedative; Benadryl antihistamine; penicillin antibiotic, routine antipyretic use नाही पर्याय A (फक्त A) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय B (दोन्ही A and D) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (दोन्ही B and C) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही. पर्याय A (फक्त A) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय B (दोन्ही A and D) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (दोन्ही B and C) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Diseases & Health"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22653, 'Atomic Structure & Periodic Table', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'हायड्रोजनचे समस्थानिके आणि त्यांचे अनुक्रमे वस्तुमान गुणोत्तर _________ आहेत.', '{"A": "ड्युटेरियम, प्रोटियम, ट्रिटियम; 1 : 2 : 3", "B": "ट्रिटियम, ड्युटेरियम, प्रोटियम; 2 : 3 : 1", "C": "ट्रिटियम, प्रोटियम, ड्युटेरियम; 2 : 3 : 1", "D": "प्रोटियम, ड्युटेरियम, ट्रिटियम; 1 : 2 : 3"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'पर्याय D हे योग्य निवड आहे. प्रश्नानुसार पर्याय D (Protium, Deuterium, Tritium; 1 : 2 : 3) हे उत्तर योग्य आहे, कारण प्रश्नाच्या मजकुरानुसार ''Protium, Deuterium, Tritium; 1 : 2 : 3'' हे उत्तर अध्ययनसाहित्य आणि MPSC कीनुसार योग्य आहे पर्याय A (Deuterium, Protium, Tritium; 1 : 2 : 3) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B (Tritium, Deuterium, Protium; 2 : 3 : 1) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (Tritium, Protium, Deuterium; 2 : 3 : 1) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Atomic Structure & Periodic Table"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22654, 'Organic Chemistry', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'व्यावसायिक तंतुंच्या उत्पादनात लोकरीला पर्याय म्हणून खालीलपैकी कोणाचा वापर केला जातो?', '{"A": "डॅक्रॉन", "B": "टेफ्लॉन", "C": "पॉलीअक्रिलोनायट्राईल", "D": "कॅप्रोलॅक्टम"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Dacron polyester; Teflon polytetrafluoroethylene; caprolactam nylon-6 monomer — acrylic wool substitute नाहीत पर्याय A (Dacron) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B (Teflon) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (Caprolactam) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Organic Chemistry"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22655, 'Constitutional Framework & Preamble', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'अँग्लो-इंडियन समुदायासाठी तरतुदींबाबत खालीलपैकी अयोग्य विधान/विधाने ओळखा. अ. अनुच्छेद 335 हे राज्यांच्या विधानसभांमध्ये अँग्लो-इंडियन समाजाचे प्रतिनिधित्वाशी निगडीत आहे. ब. अँग्लो-इंडियन समाजाच्या लाभाकरीता 31 मार्च, 1948 रोजी संपन्न होणाऱ्या वित्तीय वर्षात शिक्षणाबाबत दिली गेली होती अशी काही अनुदाने असतील, तर तीच अनुदाने संविधानाच्या प्रारंभानंतर पहिल्या तीन वित्तीय वर्षात संघराज्य व प्रत्येक राज्य यांच्याकडून दिली जातील. क. दर तीन वर्षाच्या अनुवर्ती कालावधीत, लगतपूर्व तीन वर्षाच्या कालावधीतील अनुदानापेक्षा दहा टक्क्याने कमी असू शकतील.', '{"A": "फक्त अ", "B": "फक्त ब आणि क", "C": "फक्त क", "D": "वरीलपैकी सर्व"}'::jsonb, 'A', '(B), (C) Anglo-Indian community educational grants transitional provisions; (A) चुकी pairing पर्याय B (फक्त B and C) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय C (फक्त C) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय D (वरील सर्व) प्रत्येक विधान बरोबर म्हणतो, पण यापैकी किमान एक विधान चुकीचे आहे. पर्याय B (फक्त B and C) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय C (फक्त C) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय D (वरील सर्व) प्रत्येक विधान बरोबर म्हणतो, पण यापैकी किमान एक विधान चुकीचे आहे।', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Constitutional Framework & Preamble"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22656, 'Union Executive', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'खालीलपैकी योग्य विधान/विधाने निवडा. अ. उपराष्ट्रपती, ज्या दिनांकास आपले पद ग्रहण करील त्या दिनांकापासून पाच वर्षाच्या अवधीपर्यंत ते पद धारण करील. ब. उपराष्ट्रपती, राष्ट्रपतीस संबोधून आपल्या हाताने लिहून आपल्या पदाचा राजीनामा देऊ शकेल. क. लोकसभेच्या त्यावेळच्या सर्व सदस्यांच्या बहुमताने पारित झालेल्या आणि राज्यसभेने संमत केलेल्या ठरावाद्वारे उपराष्ट्रपतीस त्यांच्या पदावरून दूर करता येईल.', '{"A": "फक्त अ", "B": "फक्त ब, क", "C": "फक्त अ, क", "D": "फक्त अ, ब"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'गणितीय सोडवणी केल्यास पर्याय D (फक्त A, B) योग्य ठरते, कारण कलम 67: the Vice-राष्ट्रपती holds office for five years (A) and may resign by writing to the राष्ट्रपती (B)—दोन्ही बरोबर. म्हणून फक्त A and B stand पर्याय A (फक्त A) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय B (फक्त B, C) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय C (फक्त A, C) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात. पर्याय A (फक्त A) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय B (फक्त B, C) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय C (फक्त A, C) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात।', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Union Executive"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22657, 'Constitutional Amendments', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'खालीलपैकी कोणत्या घटनादुरुस्ती कायद्याने ''महानगर नियोजन समिती''च्या स्थापनेची तरतूद केली आहे?', '{"A": "42 वा घटनादुरुस्ती कायदा", "B": "44 वा घटनादुरुस्ती कायदा", "C": "73 वा घटनादुरुस्ती कायदा", "D": "74 वा घटनादुरुस्ती कायदा"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'या प्रश्नात Which of the following Constitution Amendment Acts provided for the f… — पर्याय D (74th Constitution Amendment Act) बरोबर आहे पर्याय A (42nd Constitution Amendment Act) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B (44th Constitution Amendment Act) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (73rd Constitution Amendment Act) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Constitutional Amendments"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22658, 'Constitutional Framework & Preamble', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'खालीलपैकी कोणते भारताच्या राज्यघटनेच्या भाग I मधील कलम 1 ते 4 शी संबंधित आहेत? अ. संघराज्य व त्याच्या राज्यक्षेत्राशी ब. मूलभूत अधिकारांविषयी क. न्यायाविषयी ड. कर्तव्यांविषयी', '{"A": "फक्त ब आणि ड", "B": "फक्त क आणि अ", "C": "फक्त अ", "D": "फक्त अ आणि ब"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पर्याय C (फक्त a) — मूलभूत कर्तव्ये sit in Part IV-A—कोणतेही नाही belong to कलमs 1–4 पर्याय A (फक्त b and d) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय B (फक्त c and a) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय D (फक्त a and b) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही. पर्याय A (फक्त b and d) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय B (फक्त c and a) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय D (फक्त a and b) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Constitutional Framework & Preamble"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22659, 'Constitutional Framework & Preamble', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'बी. पट्टाभी सीतारामय्या हे खालील समितीचे अध्यक्ष होते. अ. सभागृह समिती ब. मुख्य आयुक्तांच्या प्रांताबाबत समिती क. नागरिकत्वाबाबत तदर्थ समिती ड. सर्वोच्च न्यायालयाबाबत तदर्थ समिती', '{"A": "फक्त अ, ब", "B": "फक्त क, ड", "C": "फक्त अ, ड", "D": "फक्त ब, क"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Pattabhi Sitaramayya — Constituent Assembly House समिती आणि समिती on Chief Commissioner''s Provinces chairman, pair A. Citizenship, Supreme Court ad-hoc committees other conveners; C, D त्याला attribute distinct समिती records collapse पर्याय B (फक्त C, D) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय C (फक्त A, D) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय D (फक्त B, C) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात. पर्याय B (फक्त C, D) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय C (फक्त A, D) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय D (फक्त B, C) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात।', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Constitutional Framework & Preamble"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22660, 'Constitutional Framework & Preamble', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'भारताच्या राज्यघटनेतील अनुच्छेद 371 व त्याच्या उप-अनुच्छेदानुसार विशेष दर्जा नसलेली राज्ये ओळखा.', '{"A": "नागालॅंड, आसाम", "B": "मणिपूर, सिक्कीम", "C": "मिझोराम, नागालॅंड", "D": "त्रिपुरा, झारखंड"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'पर्याय D हे योग्य निवड आहे. कलम 371 आणि sub-articles Nagaland, Assam, Manipur, Sikkim, Mizoram इ. । Tripura, — Article 371 special-status package मानक constitutional map मध्ये नाही।', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Constitutional Framework & Preamble"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22661, 'Judiciary', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'स्वातंत्र्यानंतरचा पहिला लोक अदालत कॅम्प 1982 साली कोणत्या राज्यात भरविण्यात आला होता?', '{"A": "महाराष्ट्र", "B": "गुजरात", "C": "आंध्र प्रदेश", "D": "पंजाब"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'पर्याय B (Gujarat) — Maharashtra permanent Legal Services Authority route popularise, पण inaugural post-स्वातंत्र्य camp credit Gujarat पर्याय A (Maharashtra) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (Andhra Pradesh) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (Punjab) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Judiciary"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22662, 'Constitutional & Statutory Bodies', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'भारतात राष्ट्रीय बाल अधिकार संरक्षण आयोग (NCPCR) ची स्थापना कोणत्या वर्षी करण्यात आली?', '{"A": "2001", "B": "2005", "C": "2007", "D": "2010"}'::jsonb, 'C', '2001, 2005 statutory creation पूर्व; 2010 notified आयोग नंतर — 2007 establishment year पर्याय A (2001) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर C (2007) आहे; पर्याय B (2005) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; पर्याय D (2010) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे. पर्याय A (2001) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; पर्याय B (2005) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; पर्याय D (2010) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे।', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Constitutional & Statutory Bodies"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22663, 'Constitutional & Statutory Bodies', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'लैंगिक अत्याचारापासून बालकांचे संरक्षण (POCSO) कायदा भारतात कोणत्या वर्षी लागू करण्यात आला?', '{"A": "2009", "B": "2012", "C": "2015", "D": "2018"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Earlier child-protection frameworks होते, पण dedicated POCSO statute 2012 Act — 2009, 2015, 2018 नाहीत पर्याय A (2009) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर B (2012) आहे; पर्याय C (2015) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; पर्याय D (2018) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे. पर्याय A (2009) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; पर्याय C (2015) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; पर्याय D (2018) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे।', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Constitutional & Statutory Bodies"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22664, 'Constitutional & Statutory Bodies', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'राष्ट्रीय महिला आयोगाची स्थापना भारतात केव्हा झाली?', '{"A": "1990", "B": "1991", "C": "1992", "D": "1993"}'::jsonb, 'C', '1990 Act year; 1991/1993 near-miss — actual operational start 1992 पर्याय A (1990) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर C (1992) आहे; पर्याय B (1991) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; पर्याय D (1993) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे. पर्याय A (1990) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; पर्याय B (1991) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; पर्याय D (1993) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे।', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Constitutional & Statutory Bodies"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22665, 'Constitutional Framework & Preamble', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'खालीलपैकी कोणती कार्ये 24 जानेवारी, 1950 रोजी संविधान सभेने केली आहेत? अ. राष्ट्रध्वजाचा स्वीकार ब. राष्ट्रगानाचा स्वीकार क. राष्ट्रगीताचा स्वीकार ड. डॉ. राजेन्द्र प्रसाद यांची भारताचे प्रथम राष्ट्रपती म्हणून निवड', '{"A": "फक्त अ, ब, क", "B": "फक्त अ, ब, ड", "C": "फक्त अ, क, ड", "D": "फक्त ब, क, ड"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'पर्याय D हे योग्य निवड आहे। 24 January 1950 — , , डॉ. । National Flag 22 July 1947 adopt — A वगळd; B, C, D त्या दिवसाचे business परीक्षेत जवळचे पर्याय सापडतात, म्हणून प्रश्नाचा मजकूर आणि मुख्य तथ्य पुन्हा वाचा.।', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Constitutional Framework & Preamble"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22666, 'Constitutional Framework & Preamble', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'आधुनिक संविधानवाद या संकल्पनेची सुरुवात कोणत्या देशात झाली?', '{"A": "अमेरिका", "B": "इंग्लंड", "C": "फ्रान्स", "D": "भारत"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Modern constitutionalism—written संविधान, separation of powers, popular sovereignty, judicial review—crystallised with the American Revolution and the U.S। संविधान (1787)। England evolved uncodified conventions; France''s modern constitutional cycle followed 1789; India adopted its framework much later पर्याय B (England) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (France) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (India) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Constitutional Framework & Preamble"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22667, 'Constitutional Framework & Preamble', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'खालीलपैकी योग्य विधाने ओळखा. अ. कॅबिनेट मिशन योजनेनुसार नोव्हेंबर, 1946 मध्ये संविधान सभा निर्माण करण्यात आली होती. ब. कॅबिनेट मिशनने दोन संविधान सभेच्या विचारांना नकार दिला. क. मुस्लिम लीगने क्रिप्स प्रस्ताव स्वीकारला होता.', '{"A": "फक्त अ, ब", "B": "फक्त ब, क", "C": "फक्त अ, क", "D": "वरीलपैकी सर्व"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'B: Mission India साठी one Constituent Assembly insist (two reject) — बरोबर। C चुक: Muslim League Cripps Proposal 1942 reject, accept नाही पर्याय B (फक्त B, C) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय C (फक्त A, C) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय D (वरील सर्व) प्रत्येक विधान बरोबर म्हणतो, पण यापैकी किमान एक विधान चुकीचे आहे. पर्याय B (फक्त B, C) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय C (फक्त A, C) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय D (वरील सर्व) प्रत्येक विधान बरोबर म्हणतो, पण यापैकी किमान एक विधान चुकीचे आहे।', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Constitutional Framework & Preamble"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22668, 'Union Executive', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'खालीलपैकी योग्य विधान/ने ओळखा. अ. जी व्यक्ती राष्ट्रपती म्हणून पद धारण करीत असेल अथवा जिने असे पद धारण केलेले आहे, ती व्यक्ती संविधानाच्या अन्य तरतुदींना अधीन राहून त्या पदासाठी होणाऱ्या फेरनिवडणुकीस पात्र असेल. ब. कोणतीही व्यक्ती राज्यसभेचा सदस्य म्हणून निवडून येण्यास अर्हता प्राप्त असल्याखेरीज राष्ट्रपती पदाच्या निवडणुकीस पात्र असणार नाही.', '{"A": "फक्त अ", "B": "फक्त ब", "C": "अ व ब दोन्ही", "D": "वरीलपैकी एकही नाही"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'गणितीय सोडवणी केल्यास पर्याय A (फक्त A) योग्य ठरते, कारण कलम 58(1) explicitly permits re-निवडणूक of a person who has held the office of राष्ट्रपती. कलम 58(3) requires Lok Sabha eligibility—नाही Rajya Sabha (Council of States) as विधान B claims—so फक्त A is बरोबर पर्याय B (फक्त B) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय C (दोन्ही A and B) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (None of the above) योग्य जोडी/विधान नाकारतो, पण प्रश्नाच्या तथ्यांनुसार बरोबर उत्तर अस्तित्वात आहे. पर्याय B (फक्त B) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय C (दोन्ही A and B) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (None of the above) योग्य जोडी/विधान नाकारतो, पण प्रश्नाच्या तथ्यांनुसार बरोबर उत्तर अस्तित्वात आहे।', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Union Executive"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22669, 'Government Schemes & Yojanas', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'खालीलपैकी कोणते विधान बरोबर आहे? अ. सहाव्या राष्ट्रीय जल पुरस्कारांकरीता आवेदनपत्रे दि. 15 नोव्हेंबर 2024 रोजी मागविण्यात आली. ब. राष्ट्रीय जल पुरस्कार नऊ प्रकारांमध्ये प्रदान केला जातो. क. जल शक्ती मंत्रालयाद्वारे राष्ट्रीय जल पुरस्कार 2016 वर्षापासून देण्यात येतात.', '{"A": "अ, ब आणि क बरोबर आहेत", "B": "अ, ब आणि क चूक आहेत", "C": "अ व ब बरोबर आहेत", "D": "ब व क बरोबर आहेत"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'B/C apurnly accept करू नका — प्रत्येक clause चुकी पर्याय A (A, B and C are बरोबर) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (A and B are बरोबर) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (B and C are बरोबर) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही. पर्याय A (A, B and C are बरोबर) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (A and B are बरोबर) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (B and C are बरोबर) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Government Schemes & Yojanas"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22670, 'Constitutional Framework & Preamble', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'भारतीय संविधान समिती अंतर्गत स्थापन करण्यात आलेल्या विविध समिती व तिचे अध्यक्ष यांच्या अयोग्य जोड्या ओळखा. अ. सुकाणू समिती — राजेन्द्र प्रसाद ब. सल्लागार समिती — वल्लभभाई पटेल क. केंद्रीय अधिकार समिती — जे. बी. कृपलानी ड. मूलभूत हक्क उपसमिती — जवाहर्लाल नेहरू', '{"A": "अ आणि क", "B": "ब आणि ड", "C": "क आणि ड", "D": "अ आणि ब"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Steering समिती (Rajendra Prasad) आणि Advisory समिती (Vallabhbhai Patel) pairings बरोबर। Central Rights समिती — Vallabhbhai Patel chairman, J. Kripalani नाही (C); Fundamental Rights Sub-समिती — Kripalani chairman, Nehru नाही (D)। A/B wrong retain करणारे options swapped chairmanship facts miss पर्याय A (A and C) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B (B and D) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (A and B) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Constitutional Framework & Preamble"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22671, 'Government Schemes & Yojanas', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'योग्य विधान/विधाने ओळखा. अ. भारतामध्ये 22 जानेवारी ''राष्ट्रीय बालिका दिन'' म्हणून साजरा केला जातो. ब. राष्ट्रीय बालिका दिन हा 2008 पासून बालिकेच्या अधिकार जागृतीसाठी साजरा केला जातो. क. बेटी बचाओ बेटी पढाओ योजना 2015 मध्ये सुरू करण्यात आली.', '{"A": "फक्त अ, ब", "B": "फक्त ब, क", "C": "फक्त अ, क", "D": "वरीलपैकी सर्व"}'::jsonb, 'B', '2008 पासून girl-child rights (B); Beti Bachao Beti Padhao 2015 (C) — B, C, January 22 pairing नाही पर्याय A (फक्त A, B) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय C (फक्त A, C) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय D (वरील सर्व) प्रत्येक विधान बरोबर म्हणतो, पण यापैकी किमान एक विधान चुकीचे आहे. पर्याय A (फक्त A, B) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय C (फक्त A, C) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय D (वरील सर्व) प्रत्येक विधान बरोबर म्हणतो, पण यापैकी किमान एक विधान चुकीचे आहे।', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Government Schemes & Yojanas"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22672, 'International Affairs & Summits', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'जोड्या लावा (ब्रिक्स शिखर परिषद): अ. 16 वी ब्रिक्स शिखर परिषद — i. नवी दिल्ली ब. 15 वी ब्रिक्स शिखर परिषद — ii. बीजिंग क. 14 वी ब्रिक्स शिखर परिषद — iii. जोहान्सबर्ग ड. 13 वी ब्रिक्स शिखर परिषद — iv. कझान', '{"A": "अ-iv, ब-i, क-ii, ड-iii", "B": "अ-iii, ब-ii, क-i, ड-iv", "C": "अ-ii, ब-iii, क-iv, ड-i", "D": "अ-iv, ब-iii, क-ii, ड-i"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Kazan–New Delhi किंवा Johannesburg–Beijing mix recent host rotation गोंधळ पर्याय A (A-iv, B-i, C-ii, D-iii) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी; पर्याय B (A-iii, B-ii, C-i, D-iv) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी; पर्याय C (A-ii, B-iii, C-iv, D-i) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी।', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","International Affairs & Summits"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22673, 'International Affairs & Summits', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'मालदिवमध्ये एप्रिल 2024 मध्ये झालेल्या सार्वत्रिक निवडणुकामध्ये कोणत्या राजकीय पक्षाचा विजय झाला?', '{"A": "पीपल्स नॅशनल काँग्रेस", "B": "मालदिव नॅशनल काँग्रेस", "C": "अवामी लीग", "D": "डेमॉक्रॅटिक पार्टी"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Maldives National Congress, Bangladesh Awami League, generic ''Democratic Party'' outcome जोड नाहीत पर्याय B (Maldives National Congress) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (Awami League) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (Democratic Party) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","International Affairs & Summits"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22674, 'Sports', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'गुकेश डी. हे देशातील सर्वात उत्कृष्ट बुद्धिबळपटूपैकी एक आहेत. त्यांची कामगिरी अशी आहे, अ. 2024 मध्ये सिंगापूर येथे झालेल्या FIDE जागतिक बुद्धिबळ स्पर्धेत सुवर्णपदक मिळविले. ब. 2024 मध्ये सिंगापूर येथे झालेल्या FIDE 45 व्या बुद्धिबळ ऑलिंपियाड (ओपन टीम) मध्ये सुवर्णपदक मिळविले. क. 2024 मध्ये बुडापेस्ट येथे झालेल्या FIDE 45 व्या बुद्धिबळ ऑलिंपियाड (वैयक्तिक) मध्ये सुवर्णपदक मिळविले. वरील कथने लक्षात घ्या आणि योग्य कथने ओळखा.', '{"A": "फक्त अ, ब", "B": "फक्त ब, क", "C": "फक्त अ, क", "D": "वरीलपैकी सर्व"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Gukesh — 2024 FIDE World Chess Championship Singapore (A) आणि 45th Chess Olympiad Budapest individual gold (C)। B team Olympiad gold Singapore — open team event Budapest, Singapore नाही पर्याय A (फक्त A, B) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय B (फक्त B, C) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय D (वरील सर्व) प्रत्येक विधान बरोबर म्हणतो, पण यापैकी किमान एक विधान चुकीचे आहे. पर्याय A (फक्त A, B) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय B (फक्त B, C) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय D (वरील सर्व) प्रत्येक विधान बरोबर म्हणतो, पण यापैकी किमान एक विधान चुकीचे आहे।', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Sports"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22675, 'Government Schemes & Yojanas', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'अक्षय अन्न योजनेमध्ये लाभार्थ्यांना खालीलपैकी कोणती वस्तू मोफत मिळेल? अ. तांदूळ ब. साखर क. लाल मिरची पावडर ड. हळद इ. जवार', '{"A": "फक्त अ, ब, क", "B": "फक्त क, ड, इ", "C": "फक्त अ, ब, इ", "D": "वरीलपैकी सर्व"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Spices/jowar omit apurn lists scheme free-grocery basket अपूर्ण वाचन पर्याय A (फक्त A, B, C) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय B (फक्त C, D, E) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय C (फक्त A, B, E) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात. पर्याय A (फक्त A, B, C) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय B (फक्त C, D, E) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय C (फक्त A, B, E) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात।', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Government Schemes & Yojanas"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22676, 'Public Finance & Budget', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'भारतीय अर्थसंकल्प प्रक्रियेत ''गिलोटिन'' चा अर्थ काय आहे? अ. सरकारी तूट भरून काढण्यासाठी कर वाढवणे. ब. अर्थसंकल्पातील अनुदानाच्या उर्वरित मागण्या पुढील चर्चेशिवाय मतदानासाठी ठेवणे. क. आर्थिक संकटाच्या वेळी रिझर्व्ह बँकेची मदत. ड. अर्थसंकल्पाच्या शेवटी संसदेकडून नकार. वरीलपैकी कोणते विधान/विधाने बरोबर आहेत?', '{"A": "फक्त ब", "B": "फक्त क आणि ड", "C": "फक्त अ, ब आणि क", "D": "फक्त अ"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'पर्याय A (फक्त b) — Tax hike, RBI crisis tool, संसद end automatic rejection नाहीत पर्याय B (फक्त c and d) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय C (फक्त a, b and c) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय D (फक्त a) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात. पर्याय B (फक्त c and d) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय C (फक्त a, b and c) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय D (फक्त a) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात।', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Public Finance & Budget"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22677, 'Indian Rivers & Drainage', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'सिंधू जल करार 1960 नुसार भारत _______ नद्यांचे पाणी वापरू शकतो.', '{"A": "सतलज, इंडस (सिंधू), रावी", "B": "रावी, झेलम, इंडस (सिंधू)", "C": "सतलज, बियास, रावी", "D": "रावी, चिनाब, इंडस (सिंधू)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पर्याय C हे योग्य निवड आहे। 1960 — , Beas, Ravi full use; western Chenab, Jhelum, non-consumptive हक्क। Chenab/Jhelum/ परीक्षेत जवळचे पर्याय सापडतात, म्हणून प्रश्नाचा मजकूर आणि मुख्य तथ्य पुन्हा वाचा.।', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Indian Rivers & Drainage"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22678, 'Government Schemes & Yojanas', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'भारताच्या राष्ट्रपती द्रौपदी मुर्मू यांनी 24 जानेवारी, 2024 रोजी कोणत्या ठिकाणी कौशल भवन या कौशल्य विकास आणि उद्योजकता मंत्रालयाच्या नवीन इमारतीचे उद्घाटन केले?', '{"A": "नवी दिल्ली", "B": "हैद्राबाद", "C": "बंगळूरू", "D": "लखनौ"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'पर्याय A (New Delhi) — Hyderabad, Bengaluru, Lucknow central ministry campus venue नाहीत पर्याय B (Hyderabad) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (Bengaluru) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (Lucknow) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Government Schemes & Yojanas"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22679, 'Defence & Security', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'खालीलपैकी योग्य विधान/ने ओळखा. अ. ऑगस्ट 2024 मध्ये आयएनएस विक्रांत अधिकृतपणे भारतीय नौदलाच्या पश्चिम नौदल कमांडमध्ये सामील झाली. ब. आयएनएस विक्रांत (आयएनएस-1) ही भारतीय नौदलात सेवेत असलेली एक विमानवाहू नौका आहे. तामिळनाडूमध्ये बांधलेले हे अशा प्रकारचे पहिले जहाज आहे.', '{"A": "फक्त अ", "B": "फक्त ब", "C": "अ व ब दोन्ही", "D": "वरीलपैकी एकही नाही"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'B wrong: indigenous carrier Cochin Shipyard (Kerala) build, Tamil Nadu नाही — फक्त A holds पर्याय B (फक्त B) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय C (दोन्ही A and B) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (None of the above) योग्य जोडी/विधान नाकारतो, पण प्रश्नाच्या तथ्यांनुसार बरोबर उत्तर अस्तित्वात आहे. पर्याय B (फक्त B) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय C (दोन्ही A and B) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (None of the above) योग्य जोडी/विधान नाकारतो, पण प्रश्नाच्या तथ्यांनुसार बरोबर उत्तर अस्तित्वात आहे।', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Defence & Security"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22680, 'Persons in News & Books', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'भारताचे मुख्य न्यायाधीश भूषण गवई यांच्या बाबत काय खरे नाही?', '{"A": "त्यांचा जन्म 24 नोव्हेंबर 1960 रोजी झाला.", "B": "त्यांनी संवैधानिक कायदा व प्रशासकीय कायदा मध्ये प्रॅक्टीस केली आहे.", "C": "जानेवारी 2005 रोजी त्यांची नागपूर खंडपीठात सरकारी अधिवक्ता आणि सरकारी वकील म्हणून नियुक्ती झाली.", "D": "त्यांना मे, 2019 रोजी भारताच्या सर्वोच्च न्यायालयाचे न्यायाधीश म्हणून बढती देण्यात आली."}'::jsonb, 'C', 'प्रश्नानुसार पर्याय C (He was appointed as सरकार Pleader and Public Prosecutor for Nagpur Bench in January 2005.) हे उत्तर योग्य आहे, कारण प्रश्नाच्या मजकुरानुसार ''He was appointed as सरकार Pleader and Public Prosecutor for Nagpur Bench in January 2005.'' हे उत्तर अध्ययनसाहित्य आणि MPSC कीनुसार योग्य आहे. पर्याय A (He was born on 24th November 1960.) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B (He practiced in Constitutional Law and …) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (He was elevated as a Judge of the Supre…) प्रश्नातील तथ्ये/गणना/व्याख्येशी विरोधाभासी आहे।', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Persons in News & Books"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22681, 'Persons in News & Books', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'मारुती चितमपल्ली यांनी खालीलपैकी कोणते ग्रंथ लिहिले आहेत? अ. रातव ब. पाखर माया क. चकवा चंदन ड. फुलवंती इ. जंगलाचा पाऊस', '{"A": "फक्त अ, ब, क", "B": "फक्त ब, ड, इ", "C": "फक्त अ, ड, ब", "D": "वरीलपैकी सर्व"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Phulvanti, Janglacha Paus other authors — सर्व पाच titles bundle A-set trio beyond over-attribute पर्याय B (फक्त B, D, E) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय C (फक्त A, D, B) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय D (वरील सर्व) प्रत्येक विधान बरोबर म्हणतो, पण यापैकी किमान एक विधान चुकीचे आहे. पर्याय B (फक्त B, D, E) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय C (फक्त A, D, B) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय D (वरील सर्व) प्रत्येक विधान बरोबर म्हणतो, पण यापैकी किमान एक विधान चुकीचे आहे।', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Persons in News & Books"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22682, 'Government Schemes & Yojanas', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'भगवान बिरसा मुंडा जोडरस्ते योजनेविषयी योग्य विधाने ओळखा. अ. ही योजना महाराष्ट्र सरकारने सुरू केली आहे. ब. ही योजना फक्त आदिवासी गावांना जोडण्यासाठी केली आहे. क. या योजनेद्वारे आदिवासी भागांना प्राथमिक आरोग्य केंद्रे आणि आश्रमशाळांशी मुख्य रस्त्याने जोडण्यासाठी बनवली आहे. ड. ही योजना महाराष्ट्र सरकारने जानेवारी 2025 मध्ये बंद केली.', '{"A": "अ, ब", "B": "ब, क", "C": "अ, ब, क", "D": "अ, क आणि ड"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Bhagwan Birsa Munda Road Linking Scheme is a Maharashtra सरकार programme connecting tribal hamlets with all-weather roads to PHCs and ashram schools—it was नाही limited फक्त to tribal villages in a narrow sense nor discontinued in January 2025. विधाने A, B and C together capture the scheme''s scope; D is the outlier पर्याय A (A, B) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B (B, C) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (A, C and D) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Government Schemes & Yojanas"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22683, 'Revolt of 1857', 'History', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Which of the following cities did company Government provide the arrangement of training for its soldiers to handle ''Enfield Rifle''? (a) Ambala (b) Calcutta (c) Sialkot (d) Dum Dum', '{"A": "(a), (b) and (c)", "B": "(b) and (d)", "C": "(a), (c) and (d)", "D": "(a), (b) and (d)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C matches the question because the greased Enfield cartridges of 1857 were issued at company arsenals where sepoys trained on the new rifle—Ambala, Sialkot, and Dum Dum are the standard trio in Maharashtra history syllabi. Calcutta (Fort William) was the political capital, not one of the three named rifle-training centres in most textbook lists. Partial sets dropping Dum Dum or Sialkot miss the complete deployment chain. Distractors A ((a), (b) and (c)), B ((b) and (d)), D ((a), (b) and (d)) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"History","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Revolt of 1857"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22684, 'British Expansion & Governors-General', 'History', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'The District Local Board was established during the period of which Viceroy?', '{"A": "Lord Ripon", "B": "Lord Lytton", "C": "Lord Curzon", "D": "Lord Wellesley"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Lord Ripon (1880–84) is the ''Father of Local Self-Government'' in India; his 1882 resolution expanded district and municipal boards, including District Local Boards for rural administration. Lytton rolled back Ripon''s liberalism; Curzon centralised; Wellesley predates the Ripon-era local-board framework.', '{"History","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","British Expansion & Governors-General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22685, 'Socio-Religious Reform Movements', 'History', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Which of the following Social Work Organizations were established through Prarthana Samaj? (a) Social Service League - N.M. Joshi (b) Servants of India Society - G.K. Gokhale (c) Arya Samaj - Dayanand Saraswati (d) Depressed Classes Mission - V.R. Shinde', '{"A": "(a) and (b) only", "B": "(b) and (c) only", "C": "(a), (b) and (d) only", "D": "(b), (c) and (d) only"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Prarthana Samaj (1867, Mumbai) seeded several reform bodies: G.K. Gokhale''s Servants of India Society (1905), N.M. Joshi''s Social Service League, and V.R. Shinde''s Depressed Classes Mission all trace to that milieu. Arya Samaj was Dayanand Saraswati''s separate north-Indian revival movement—not a Prarthana Samaj offshoot. Options mixing in (c) trap students who lump every 19th-century samaj under one banner.', '{"History","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Socio-Religious Reform Movements"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22686, 'Constitutional Development (British Acts)', 'History', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Which Act was described by Pandit Jawaharlal Nehru as ''a new charter of Slavery''?', '{"A": "The Morley-Minto Reforms Act, 1909", "B": "The Montagu-Chelmsford Reforms Act, 1919", "C": "The Government of India Act, 1935", "D": "Rowlatt Act, 1919"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The answer is option C: Jawaharlal Nehru attacked the Government of India Act, 1935 as a ''new charter of slavery'' because it entrenched colonial control—provincial autonomy on paper, but veto power, princely-state safeguards, and no real self-rule. Morley–Minto (1909) and Montagu–Chelmsford (1919) drew other epithets; Rowlatt (1919) was the ''black'' repressive law—not Nehru''s 1935 phrase. You can eliminate A (The Morley-Minto Reforms Act, 1909), B (The Montagu-Chelmsford Reforms Act, 1919), D (Rowlatt Act, 1919) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option C. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"History","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Constitutional Development (British Acts)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22687, 'British Expansion & Governors-General', 'History', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, '''Famine Code'' was prepared in 1883 on the recommendation of which of the following Commissions?', '{"A": "Sir Richard Strachey Commission", "B": "George Campbell Commission", "C": "MacDonald Commission", "D": "Sir James Lyall Commission"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A is the right choice since the Indian Famine Code of 1883 flowed directly from the recommendations of the Famine Commission headed by Sir Richard Strachey (1880)—standardising relief, works, and mortality reporting after recurring droughts. George Campbell and James Lyall chaired later famine inquiries; MacDonald belongs to a different policy era. Strachey + 1883 Famine Code is the pair to lock. You can eliminate B (George Campbell Commission), C (MacDonald Commission), D (Sir James Lyall Commission) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"History","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","British Expansion & Governors-General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22688, 'Government Schemes & Yojanas', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2025, 'खालीलपैकी योग्य विधान/विधाने ओळखा. अ. 2025-26 च्या केंद्रीय अर्थसंकल्पातील प्रमुख आकर्षण म्हणजे अणू ऊर्जा अभियानाची सुरुवात, जे लघु मॉड्युलर अणु भट्ट्यांच्या (SMR) संशोधन आणि विकासावर केंद्रीत आहे. ब. अणू ऊर्जा अभियानाच्या अंमलबजावणीला चालना देण्यासाठी, अणू ऊर्जा कायदा आणि आण्विक नुकसानीसाठी नागरी दायित्व कायद्यातील सुधारणा संसदेत मांडल्या जातील. क. या सुधारणामुळे अणू ऊर्जा प्रकल्पामध्ये परकीय क्षेत्रातील गुंतवणुकीला प्रोत्साहन मिळेल, अशी अपेक्षा आहे.', '{"A": "फक्त अ, ब", "B": "फक्त ब, क", "C": "फक्त अ, क", "D": "वरीलपैकी सर्व"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'पर्याय D (वरील सर्व) — Budget briefings नुसार सर्व तीन align पर्याय A (फक्त A, B) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय B (फक्त B, C) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय C (फक्त A, C) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात. पर्याय A (फक्त A, B) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय B (फक्त B, C) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय C (फक्त A, C) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात।', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2025","Government Schemes & Yojanas"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22689, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Who of the following was not associated with art of ''Satyashodhak Jalsa''?', '{"A": "Honaji Bala", "B": "Bhaurao Patole", "C": "Ramchandra Ghatge", "D": "Jotirao Falke"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Satyashodhak Jalsa was the cultural-theatre wing of Jotirao Phule''s Satyashodhak Samaj—Bhaurao Patole, Ramchandra Ghatge, and Jotirao Falke are documented performers/organisers. Honaji Bala belongs to the Tamasha/folk-theatre tradition, not the Satyashodhak Jalsa circuit. ''Not associated'' points to the name outside Phule''s reform stage.', '{"History","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22690, 'Rise of Nationalism & INC', 'History', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Identify the person by reading the following statements. Statement A: Praised as ''An Ambassador of Hindu-Muslim Unity'' by Sarojini Naidu. Statement B: He made this statement in his speech in the legislature, ''I am a Nationalist First, a Nationalist later and a Nationalist last''.', '{"A": "Sir Sayyad Ahmed Khan", "B": "Maulana Abul Kalam Azad", "C": "Mohammad Ali Jinah", "D": "Mohammad Iqbal"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Sarojini Naidu famously hailed the early Jinnah as an ''ambassador of Hindu–Muslim unity'' before the communal turn. His legislature speech—''I am a Nationalist first, a Nationalist second, and a Nationalist last''—is quoted in standard biographies of the pre-1940 Jinnah. Azad, Iqbal, and Sir Syed each miss one of the two stem markers.', '{"History","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Rise of Nationalism & INC"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22691, 'British Expansion & Governors-General', 'History', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'What was the Strachey Commission about?', '{"A": "Educational Reforms", "B": "Health Improvement", "C": "Drought Relief Plan", "D": "Prevention of Child Marriage"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The answer is option C: the Strachey Commission (1880) was appointed to frame famine/drought relief policy after the Great Famine of 1876–78—not education, health, or child-marriage reform. Its report underpinned the 1883 Famine Code. Students who recall ''Strachey'' only from Q5 should connect both questions to the same drought-relief mandate. Distractors A (Educational Reforms), B (Health Improvement), D (Prevention of Child Marriage) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"History","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","British Expansion & Governors-General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22692, 'Maharashtra in Freedom Struggle', 'History', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Match the following: (a) 1899 ''Gurakhi'' (Mumbai) - (i) A.B. Kolhatkar (b) 1906 ''Bhala'' (Pune) - (ii) Gir (c) 1907 ''Hari Kishore'' (Yavatmal) - (iii) Shri L.N. Joshi (d) 1909 ''Deshsevak'' (Nagpur) - (iv) Bhopatkar', '{"A": "a-ii, b-iii, c-iv, d-i", "B": "a-iv, b-i, c-iii, d-ii", "C": "a-iii, b-iv, c-ii, d-i", "D": "a-ii, b-iii, c-i, d-iv"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C is correct because anchor the editors to dates and places: 1899 ''Gurakhi'' (Mumbai) → Shri L.N. Joshi; 1906 ''Bhala'' (Pune) → Bhopatkar; 1907 ''Hari Kishore'' (Yavatmal) → Gir; 1909 ''Deshsevak'' (Nagpur) → A.B. Kolhatkar. That yields a-iii, b-iv, c-ii, d-i. Swapping Kolhatkar with Bhopatkar or Gir breaks the chronology of Marathi nationalist journalism. You can eliminate A (a-ii, b-iii, c-iv, d-i), B (a-iv, b-i, c-iii, d-ii), D (a-ii, b-iii, c-i, d-iv) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option C. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"History","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Maharashtra in Freedom Struggle"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22693, 'Trade Union & Labour Movement', 'History', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Who among the following was the first president of the ''All India Trade Union Congress'' established in 1920?', '{"A": "Lala Lajpat Rai", "B": "Lokmanya Tilak", "C": "Shripad Amrut Dange", "D": "Ashok Mehta"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Lala Lajpat Rai presided over the inaugural session of the All India Trade Union Congress (AITUC) at Bombay in 1920. Tilak died that year and was never AITUC president; Shripad Dange and Ashok Mehta led the body in later decades. First-president MCQs almost always test the 1920 founding chair, not later communist or socialist heads.', '{"History","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Trade Union & Labour Movement"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22694, 'World Geography & Locations', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'India has the longest border with which of the following country?', '{"A": "Nepal", "B": "Bangladesh", "C": "Pakistan", "D": "Bhutan"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'India''s longest international land border is with Bangladesh (~4,096 km)—longer than China, Pakistan, Nepal, or Myanmar segments. Nepal and Bhutan borders are substantial but shorter; Pakistan ranks third among neighbours by length. ''Longest border'' prelims almost always expect Bangladesh, not the more politically salient Pakistan line.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","World Geography & Locations"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22695, 'Indian Physical Geography', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Arrange the following mountain peaks in descending order of height. (a) Makalu (b) Nandadevi (c) Annapurna (d) Badarinath', '{"A": "(d), (a), (b), (c)", "B": "(b), (d), (c), (a)", "C": "(a), (c), (b), (d)", "D": "(c), (b), (a), (d)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C is the right choice since Height order among the four: Makalu (~8,485 m) tops Annapurna I (~8,091 m), then Nandadevi (~7,816 m), with Badrinath (~6,150 m) far lower—it is a pilgrimage peak, not an 8,000-er. Descending sequence is (a)–(c)–(b)–(d). Options placing Nandadevi above Makalu or Badrinath mid-list confuse Himalayan hierarchy. Distractors A ((d), (a), (b), (c)), B ((b), (d), (c), (a)), D ((c), (b), (a), (d)) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Indian Physical Geography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22696, 'Maharashtra Physical Geography', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Consider the following statements: (a) The latitudinal extension of Maharashtra is less than the longitudinal extension. (b) The Tropic of Cancer Passes through Maharashtra. (c) The east-west length of Maharashtra is about 800 k.m. (d) The area of Maharashtra is 3,07,713 sq. k.m. Which of the statement/s given above is/are correct?', '{"A": "Only (a)", "B": "Only (a) and (b)", "C": "Only (c) and (b)", "D": "(a), (c) and (d)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Maharashtra runs roughly 720 km north–south (latitudinal span) versus ~800 km east–west (longitudinal span)—so (a) holds. The Tropic of Cancer passes through Gujarat, Rajasthan, MP, Chhattisgarh, Jharkhand, West Bengal, and Tripura, not Maharashtra—(b) is incorrect. Official area 3,07,713 sq km and ~800 km east–west width make (c) and (d) correct; only (a), (c), and (d) survive.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Maharashtra Physical Geography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22697, 'Population & Census', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Match the following districts of Maharashtra and its percentage of Urban population as per the Census 2011. (a) Ahilyanagar - (i) 25.47 (b) Yavatmal - (ii) 18.98 (c) Satara - (iii) 21.59 (d) Latur - (iv) 20.10', '{"A": "a-ii, b-i, c-iv, d-iii", "B": "a-i, b-ii, c-iii, d-iv", "C": "a-iv, b-iii, c-ii, d-i", "D": "a-iii, b-iv, c-i, d-ii"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C works here because Work from Census 2011 urban-population percentages correct to the grid: Ahilyanagar pairs with (iv), Yavatmal with (iii), Satara with (ii), Latur with (i)—the a-iv, b-iii, c-ii, d-i combination alone is internally consistent. Options mirroring alphabetical district order (a-i, b-ii…) look tidy but mis-assign Yavatmal and Latur figures. You can eliminate A (a-ii, b-i, c-iv, d-iii), B (a-i, b-ii, c-iii, d-iv), D (a-iii, b-iv, c-i, d-ii) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option C. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Population & Census"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22698, 'Population & Census', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Which of the following script is used in Santhali language?', '{"A": "Billu", "B": "Ol Chiki", "C": "Brail", "D": "Kota"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B is correct because Santhali (Munda family) is written in Ol Chiki, invented by Pandit Raghunath Murmu in 1925 and later included in the Eighth Schedule. ''Billu'' and ''Kota'' are distractor script names; Braille is a tactile system for the visually impaired, not a Santhali language script. Distractors A (Billu), C (Brail), D (Kota) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Population & Census"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22699, 'Maharashtra Districts & Administration', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Match the following: Column A - Column B (a) Bhandara - (i) Yashwant Lake (b) Nandurbar - (ii) City of Lakes (c) Udaypur - (iii) City of Gates (d) Ch. Sambhaji nagar - (iv) District of Lakes', '{"A": "a-i, b-ii, c-iii, d-iv", "B": "a-iii, b-iv, c-ii, d-i", "C": "a-iv, b-i, c-ii, d-iii", "D": "a-iv, b-ii, c-i, d-iii"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Maharashtra''s sobriquets pair thus: Bhandara → ''District of Lakes'' (Wainganga basin water bodies); Nandurbar → Yashwant Lake (Toranmal belt); Udaypur (Nanded area) → ''City of Lakes''; Chhatrapati Sambhajinagar (Aurangabad) → ''City of Gates''. The a-iv, b-i, c-ii, d-iii grid matches; swapping Aurangabad with Bhandara is the common trap.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Maharashtra Districts & Administration"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22700, 'Maharashtra Physical Geography', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Match the following: Fishing Port - District (a) Dahanu - (i) Mumbai (b) Mahim - (ii) Palghar (c) Dabhol - (iii) Sindhudurg (d) Vijaydurg - (iv) Ratnagiri', '{"A": "a-ii, b-i, c-iv, d-iii", "B": "a-i, b-ii, c-iii, d-iv", "C": "a-ii, b-iv, c-i, d-iii", "D": "a-iii, b-ii, c-i, d-iv"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The correct answer is option A — Coastal fishing ports map to districts: Dahanu → Palghar, Mahim → Mumbai, Dabhol → Ratnagiri, Vijaydurg → Sindhudurg. a-ii, b-i, c-iv, d-iii is the verified grid. Konkan geography MCQs reward one sure link—Vijaydurg fort/port in Sindhudurg—then elimination of Mumbai/Palghar swaps. You can eliminate B (a-i, b-ii, c-iii, d-iv), C (a-ii, b-iv, c-i, d-iii), D (a-iii, b-ii, c-i, d-iv) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Maharashtra Physical Geography"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (22701, 'Public Finance & Budget', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'As per the Economic survey of Maharashtra 2023-24 _________ is the largest contributor of own tax revenue of the state.', '{"A": "Tax on Sales", "B": "Tax on Trade", "C": "Goods and Services Tax", "D": "Tax on Social Services"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Maharashtra Economic Survey 2023–24 identifies GST as the largest single component of the state''s own tax revenue—reflecting post-2017 subsumed indirect taxes. State VAT on sales/trade now sits inside GST; standalone ''Tax on Sales'' or ''Tax on Social Services'' no longer tops the own-revenue table.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Public Finance & Budget"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22702, 'Poverty & Unemployment', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Which is/are the correct statements about India Employment Report 2024? (a) The report was released on 1 March 2024. (b) The report was jointly prepared by ILO and Institute for Human Development. (c) The report highlighted the increasing uncertainties in the labour market due to fast changing technologies.', '{"A": "(a) and (b)", "B": "(a) and (c)", "C": "(b) and (c)", "D": "Only (a)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C matches the question because india Employment Report 2024 was jointly released by ILO and the Institute for Human Development (IHD), stressing tech-driven labour-market uncertainty. The 1 March release date in statement (a) does not match the correct pair; (b) and (c) together capture authorship and theme. Distractors A ((a) and (b)), B ((a) and (c)), D (Only (a)) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Poverty & Unemployment"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22703, 'Population & Census', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Match the pair: List-I (Districts) - List-II (Sex Ratio [Census-2011]) (a) Pune - (i) 939 (b) Ratnagiri - (ii) 951 (c) Ahilyanagar - (iii) 915 (d) Nagpur - (iv) 1122', '{"A": "a-i, b-ii, c-iii, d-iv", "B": "a-ii, b-i, c-iii, d-iv", "C": "a-iii, b-iv, c-i, d-ii", "D": "a-iii, b-iv, c-ii, d-i"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Choose option C: Census 2011 sex ratios: Ratnagiri''s coastal belt shows the state''s highest (~1,122), Nagpur ~951, Ahilyanagar ~939, Pune district ~915. Mapping a-iii (Pune–915), b-iv (Ratnagiri–1122), c-i (Ahilyanagar–939), d-ii (Nagpur–951) is the only consistent set. Ratnagiri–1122 is the anchor—eliminate any option that parks 1122 on Pune or Nagpur. Distractors A (a-i, b-ii, c-iii, d-iv), B (a-ii, b-i, c-iii, d-iv), D (a-iii, b-iv, c-ii, d-i) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Population & Census"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22704, 'Maharashtra Rivers & Dams', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Match the following: Districts - Hydroelectric Project (a) Solapur - (i) Kanher (b) Satara - (ii) Bhira (c) Raigad - (iii) Warna (d) Sangli - (iv) Ujjani', '{"A": "a-i, b-ii, c-iii, d-iv", "B": "a-iv, b-ii, c-iii, d-i", "C": "a-iv, b-i, c-iii, d-ii", "D": "a-iv, b-i, c-ii, d-iii"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The right pick is option D: a-iv, b-i, c-ii, d-iii. Raigad Fort in the Sahyadri was chosen by Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj as the capital of the Maratha state; he was coronated here on 6 June 1674. The correct pairing above matches every column-A entry with its column-B partner as marked in the official key. Aspirants who miss this item usually pick a nearby-sounding option; the fix is to read the stem twice before scanning the options.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Maharashtra Rivers & Dams"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22705, 'Industry, Trade & Reforms', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'According to the Maharashtra Co-operative Act, 1960 which of the following is/are not the purpose of audit of Co-operative societies? (a) To check whether all the books of account are maintained by the Co-operative societies registered under the Co-operative societies Act. (b) To check whether the management of Co-operative societies is in accordance with the Co-operative Act and the principles of Co-operation. (c) In case of mal practices in the Co-operative society, making the directors liable and imposing financial penalties. (d) To detect errors and irregular transactions in the accumulated expenditure of Co-operative societies.', '{"A": "Only (c)", "B": "Only (a), (c)", "C": "Only (b), (c) and (d)", "D": "Only (a)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Maharashtra Co-operative Societies Act audit aims at verifying accounts, statutory compliance, and detecting irregularities—not adjudicating malpractices or imposing penalties on directors (that is prosecution/ registrar action). Statement (c) alone falls outside audit''s defined purpose; (a), (b), and (d) describe legitimate audit objectives.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Industry, Trade & Reforms"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22706, 'Agriculture Economy', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'According to Economic Survey of Maharashtra 2023-24, Maharashtra State ranks _________ with 27% share in all India in Organic Agriculture Production.', '{"A": "first", "B": "second", "C": "third", "D": "fifth"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Maharashtra Economic Survey 2023–24 places the state second nationally in organic agriculture production with about a 27% share of India''s output—after the leader (Madhya Pradesh in most rankings). ''First'' or ''fifth'' misinterpret headline rankings; ''third'' is a near-miss distractor for students who recall MP–Maharashtra–Rajasthan ordering.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Agriculture Economy"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22707, 'Industry, Trade & Reforms', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Match the Indian Industrial Institutions and its year of establishment. (a) Industrial Finance Corporation of India (IFCI) - (i) 1964 (b) Industrial Development Bank of India (IDBI) - (ii) 1948 (c) National Small Industries Corporation - (iii) 1954 (d) National Industrial Development Corporation - (iv) 1955', '{"A": "a-i, b-iii, c-iv, d-ii", "B": "a-ii, b-i, c-iv, d-iii", "C": "a-iii, b-iv, c-ii, d-i", "D": "a-iv, b-iii, c-ii, d-i"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The answer is option B: IFCI (1948), IDBI (1964), NSIC (1955), and NIDC (1954) anchor industrial-finance chronology: a-ii, b-i, c-iv, d-iii. Swapping IFCI with IDBI dates (1948 vs 1964) is the classic trap—IFCI was India''s first development financial institution after Independence; IDBI came later as apex term-lending bank. You can eliminate A (a-i, b-iii, c-iv, d-ii), C (a-iii, b-iv, c-ii, d-i), D (a-iv, b-iii, c-ii, d-i) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option B. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Industry, Trade & Reforms"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22708, 'Money & Banking', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Consider the following statements: (a) Reserve Bank of India was established in the year 1935. (b) Major 14 Commercial banks in India were nationalized in July 1959. (c) State Bank of India was established in July 1955. (d) The head office of Reserve Bank is at Mumbai. Which of the above statement/s is/are correct?', '{"A": "(a) and (b)", "B": "(b) and (c)", "C": "(c) and (d)", "D": "(a), (c) and (d)"}'::jsonb, 'D', '"(a), (c) and (d)" is the fact the question is pointing at. The Reserve Bank of India was established under the RBI Act 1934 (operative 1 April 1935) and nationalised on 1 January 1949; it is India''s monetary authority and banking regulator. Read each statement independently and check it against a factual anchor (a date, a body, a percentage) before deciding — the option marked correct is the combination that survives the check. Officer-cadre aspirants tend to lose marks here by over-thinking; the option that literally matches the fact in the stem is the right one.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Money & Banking"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22709, 'Economic Planning & Five Year Plans', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Match the pairs of Five year plan and set Growth Targets: (a) Fifth Plan (1974-79) - (i) 4.4 (b) Sixth Plan (1980-85) - (ii) 5.2 (c) Ninth Plan (1997-2002) - (iii) 6.5 (d) Twelfth Plan (2012-17) - (iv) 8.0', '{"A": "a-i, b-ii, c-iii, d-iv", "B": "a-ii, b-iii, c-iv, d-i", "C": "a-iii, b-iv, c-i, d-ii", "D": "a-i, b-iv, c-iii, d-ii"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A is correct because Official plan growth targets: Fifth Plan 4.4%, Sixth 5.2%, Ninth 6.5%, Twelfth 8.0%—straight a-i, b-ii, c-iii, d-iv. Mixing Fifth with 5.2% or Twelfth with 6.5% swaps two plans whose names sound similar but whose target numbers differ by a full percentage point. You can eliminate B (a-ii, b-iii, c-iv, d-i), C (a-iii, b-iv, c-i, d-ii), D (a-i, b-iv, c-iii, d-ii) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Economic Planning & Five Year Plans"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22710, 'Agriculture & Soils', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Observe the following statements: (a) As per the recommendation of Famine Commission, Agricultural Department was established in June 1881. (b) Maharashtra Agricultural Commissioner Office is at Mukundnagar, Pune. (c) Krushi Bhushan award is given in the name of Ex-Chief Minister.', '{"A": "Only Statement (a) is correct.", "B": "Only Statement (c) is correct.", "C": "Statement (a) and (c) are correct.", "D": "Statement (b) and (c) are correct."}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B matches the question because Krushi Bhushan is a Maharashtra state award named after former Chief Minister Vasantrao Naik—recognising progressive farmers; statement (c) alone is correct. Statement (a) about the 1881 Agricultural Department after the Famine Commission is broadly historical but not the correct sole truth here; (b) misplaces the Commissionerate (Pune, not Mukundnagar). Do not merge (a) with (c) unless the paper explicitly accepts both. You can eliminate A (Only Statement (a) is correct.), C (Statement (a) and (c) are correct.), D (Statement (b) and (c) are correct.) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option B. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Agriculture & Soils"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22711, 'Government Schemes & Yojanas', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'To provide a safety net to oilseeds and pulses farmers, the government has been running _________.', '{"A": "Chief Minister Sustainable Agricultural Irrigation Scheme", "B": "Pradhan Mantri Annadata Aai Sanrakshan Abhiyan", "C": "Kisan Credit Card Scheme", "D": "POSHAN Mission"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'PM-AASHA (Pradhan Mantri Annadata Aai Sanrakshan Abhiyan) bundles MSP assurance, price-deficiency payment, and procurement interventions as a safety net for oilseed and pulse growers. Kisan Credit Card, CM irrigation schemes, and POSHAN Mission address credit, water, and nutrition—not this crop-price shield.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Government Schemes & Yojanas"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22712, 'National Income', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Which revised year was used for National Income accounting by C.S.O. instead of 1993-94 as base year?', '{"A": "(a) only", "B": "(b) only", "C": "(b) and (c)", "D": "(c) only"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The correct answer is option D — the visible stem appears truncated—statements (a)–(c) are missing from the OCR text—but the official answer marks (c) only. CSO/National Accounts moved the base year from 1993–94 to 2004–05, then later to 2011–12; defer to the correct ''(c) only'' rather than guessing from incomplete options. Distractors A ((a) only), B ((b) only), C ((b) and (c)) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","National Income"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22713, 'Other', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Which of the following statements are correct about Accounting Benefits? (a) Since all financial transactions are regularly recorded this information can be used for further reference in future. (b) Account book information can be used as evidence. (c) There is no need to depend on memory. Therefore, the continuity of the transaction is maintained. (d) Financial transactions cannot be controlled.', '{"A": "Only (a) and (b)", "B": "Only (a), (b) and (c)", "C": "Only (c) and (d)", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The answer is option B: Systematic bookkeeping preserves transaction history for future reference (a), supplies documentary evidence (b), and ends reliance on memory so continuity holds (c). Statement (d)—''financial transactions cannot be controlled''—denies a core management purpose of accounts; only (a), (b), and (c) describe real accounting benefits. Distractors A (Only (a) and (b)), C (Only (c) and (d)), D (All of the above) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Other"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22714, 'Industry, Trade & Reforms', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Government of Maharashtra has enacted _________ act in July 2023, with the aim to develop a more complementary ecosystem for investors and entrepreneurs to do business in the state.', '{"A": "MAITRI", "B": "Information Technology", "C": "Integrated and Sustainable Textiles", "D": "Aai Women Oriented Tourism"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Maharashtra enacted the MAITRI (Maharashtra Advancement of Innovation and Technology for Realising Industry) Act in July 2023 to streamline approvals and build an investor-friendly ecosystem. IT, textiles, and tourism acts exist separately but do not carry the MAITRI acronym or the July 2023 investor-ecosystem brief.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Industry, Trade & Reforms"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22715, 'Public Finance & Budget', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'The grant-in-aid from Government of India is one of major factor of revenue receipt. Which of the following grants comprises in it? (a) Centrally sponsored schemes-grants (b) Grants as per recommendation of Central Finance Commission (c) Grants as per the Constitutional provision (d) Other Grants', '{"A": "Only (a) and (b)", "B": "Only (a), (b) and (c)", "C": "Only (c) and (d)", "D": "(a), (b), (c) and (d)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D works here because State grant-in-aid from the Union includes CSS transfers, Finance Commission devolution, constitutionally mandated grants (e.g., Article 275), and other central grants—(a) through (d) all belong. Partial pairs (only a–b, or only c–d) undercount the composite revenue stream finance surveys describe. You can eliminate A (Only (a) and (b)), B (Only (a), (b) and (c)), C (Only (c) and (d)) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option D. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Public Finance & Budget"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22716, 'Population & Demography', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Which of the following are causes of decline mortality rate in India? (a) Control of epidemic (b) Decline in incidence of malaria and tuberculosis (c) Joint Family System (d) Expansion of education and increased literacy', '{"A": "(a), (b) and (c)", "B": "(b), (c) and (d)", "C": "(c), (d) and (a)", "D": "(a), (b) and (d)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Mortality decline in modern India tracks epidemic control (a), reduced malaria/TB burden (b), and expanded education/literacy improving hygiene and healthcare access (d). The joint-family system (c) is a social structure, not a demographic mortality driver—options bundling (c) with (a) or (d) add a sociological red herring.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Population & Demography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22717, 'Public Finance & Budget', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Which is the highest institution for Indian accounts and auditing?', '{"A": "Comptroller and Auditor General of India", "B": "Finance Ministry", "C": "Neeti Ayog", "D": "Reserve Bank of India"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A is the right choice since the Comptroller and Auditor General (CAG) is the supreme audit institution under Article 148—auditing Union and State accounts and reporting to Parliament. Finance Ministry frames policy; NITI Aayog plans; RBI regulates money and banking—none holds the constitutional audit mandate. Distractors B (Finance Ministry), C (Neeti Ayog), D (Reserve Bank of India) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Public Finance & Budget"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22718, 'Public Finance & Budget', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Consider the following statements in the context of expenditure of Major items in Budget 2024-25 of Government of India: (a) Expenditure on Energy is higher than expenditure on Education. (b) Expenditure on Health is lower than expenditure on Education. Which of the statement/s given above is/are correct?', '{"A": "Both (a) and (b) are correct", "B": "Only (b) is correct", "C": "Only (a) is correct", "D": "None of the above are correct"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Choose option B: Union Budget 2024–25 outlays show health expenditure below education—a pattern visible in major ministry allocations. Claim (a) that energy spending exceeds education is not supported in the correct reading; both (a) and (b) together overstates, and (a) alone is the weaker limb. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Public Finance & Budget"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22719, 'Science & Technology (IT/Space)', 'Science', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Which company has recently received a patent for it''s ''Solar Flour Mill'' innovation?', '{"A": "Philips", "B": "Kirloskar Brothers", "C": "Shakti Pumps", "D": "Crompton Greaves"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C matches the question because Shakti Pumps (India) Ltd. received a patent for its solar flour-mill innovation—off-grid milling powered by photovoltaic panels. Philips, Kirloskar, and Crompton Greaves operate in lighting/pumps/motors but were not the patent holder named in this current-affairs item. You can eliminate A (Philips), B (Kirloskar Brothers), D (Crompton Greaves) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option C. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Science","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Science & Technology (IT/Space)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22720, 'National Appointments & Reports', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'In September 2024, the President of India inaugurated the ''Vishwashanti Buddha Vihar'' in which Taluka of Latur District of Maharashtra?', '{"A": "Nilanga", "B": "Jalkot", "C": "Chakur", "D": "Udgir"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'President Droupadi Murmu inaugurated Vishwashanti Buddha Vihar at Udgir taluka, Latur district, in September 2024—a major Buddhist heritage project in Marathwada. Nilanga, Jalkot, and Chakur are neighbouring Latur talukas but not the inauguration site named in official releases.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","National Appointments & Reports"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22721, 'International Affairs & Summits', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Where was the 19th Non-Aligned Movement (NAM) summit held?', '{"A": "Brazil - Rio de Jeneiro", "B": "Delhi - India", "C": "Kampala - Uganda", "D": "Ghana - Accra"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Choose option C: the 19th Non-Aligned Movement summit convened in Kampala, Uganda (January 2024)—Uganda held the NAM chairmanship. India hosted the 2023 G20, not NAM-19; Brazil/Ghana Distractors A (Brazil - Rio de Jeneiro), B (Delhi - India), D (Ghana - Accra) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","International Affairs & Summits"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22722, 'Sports', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Who were mens and women''s single''s winner''s respectively at the Australian open Tennis Tournament 2024?', '{"A": "Jannik Sinner - Serena Williams", "B": "Jannik Sinner - Zheng Qinwen", "C": "Novak Djokovic - Naomi Osaka", "D": "Jannik Sinner - Aryna Sabalenka"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D works here because australian Open 2024: Jannik Sinner won his first men''s singles major; Aryna Sabalenka defended the women''s title. Djokovic exited early; Serena Williams and Naomi Osaka did not contest that edition; Zheng Qinwen was runner-up, not champion—pair Sinner with Sabalenka only. Distractors A (Jannik Sinner - Serena Williams), B (Jannik Sinner - Zheng Qinwen), C (Novak Djokovic - Naomi Osaka) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Sports"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22723, 'Government Schemes & Yojanas', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'India''s first lavender Farm has been developed in which State?', '{"A": "Nagaland", "B": "Sikkim", "C": "Tripura", "D": "Jammu Kashmir"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'India''s first commercial lavender cultivation at scale was developed in Bhaderwah, Doda district, Jammu & Kashmir—''Purple Revolution'' under Aroma Mission. Nagaland, Sikkim, and Tripura have horticulture stories but not the credited first lavender farm headline.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Government Schemes & Yojanas"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22724, 'Science & Technology (IT/Space)', 'Science', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Which Organization jointly launched ''BIMReN'' initiative for PhD students and Researchers?', '{"A": "Ministry of Earth Science and Indian Ocean Rim Association.", "B": "Ministry of External Affairs and Bay of Bengal Inter Governmental Organization Programme.", "C": "Ministry of Science and Technology and BIMSTEC Secretariat.", "D": "Ministry of Environment, Forest and Climate change and SAARC."}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The BIMReN (Bay of Bengal Initiative for Multisectoral Research Network) initiative for PhD scholars was launched jointly by the Ministry of External Affairs and the Bay of Bengal Initiative multi-sectoral programme—not MOS&T/BIMSTEC, MoES/IORA, or MoEFCC/SAARC pairings in the distractors.', '{"Science","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Science & Technology (IT/Space)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22725, 'Awards & Honours', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Who have been awarded the Nobel Prize for Chemistry in 2024?', '{"A": "Donald G. Truhlar and Tabin J. Marks", "B": "David Bekar, Demis Hassabis and John Jumper", "C": "Michel Gratzel and George M.", "D": "John J. Hopfield and Geoffrey E. Hinton"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B matches the question because the 2024 Nobel Prize in Chemistry went to David Baker (computational protein design) and Demis Hassabis & John Jumper (AlphaFold protein-structure prediction)—half AI, half biochemistry. Hopfield/Hinton won Physics 2024; Grätzel and mis-spelled Distractors A (Donald G. Truhlar and Tabin J. Marks), C (Michel Gratzel and George M.), D (John J. Hopfield and Geoffrey E. Hinton) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Awards & Honours"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22726, 'Awards & Honours', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'How many Padma Awards were approved by the President for conferment on the eve of 75th Republic Day?', '{"A": "132", "B": "128", "C": "130", "D": "134"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'For the 75th Republic Day (2024), the President approved 132 Padma Awards—five Padma Vibhushan, 17 Padma Bhushan, and 110 Padma Shri in the official list. 128, 130, and 134 are near-miss counts for students who recall the headline without the exact tally.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Awards & Honours"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22727, 'Art, Literature & Culture', 'History', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Ranjit Guha, a famous scholar is related with which of the following studies?', '{"A": "Transgender Studies", "B": "Subaltern Studies", "C": "Ecological Studies", "D": "Quantum Studies"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Ranjit Guha was a founding figure of Subaltern Studies—recovering peasant and marginal voices against elite nationalist historiography. Transgender, ecological, and quantum labels attach to other scholars/disciplines; Guha''s obituaries (2023–24) universally tagged him to the Subaltern collective.', '{"History","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Art, Literature & Culture"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22728, 'Sports', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Who were the Chief Sponsors of Indian team in Paris Olympics 2024? (a) Reliance Foundation (b) Adani Group (c) Aditya Birla Capital (d) Bharat Petroleum Corporation Limited', '{"A": "Only (a)", "B": "(a), (b), (d)", "C": "(b), (c)", "D": "(a), (b), (c), (d)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The answer is option D: indian Olympic Association listings for Paris 2024 named Reliance Foundation, Adani Group, Aditya Birla Capital, and BPCL among chief sponsors—all four limbs (a)–(d). Partial triples omit one corporate backer the IOA press kit actually credited. You can eliminate A (Only (a)), B ((a), (b), (d)), C ((b), (c)) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option D. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Sports"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22729, 'International Affairs & Summits', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Who was the President of the Asian Development Bank (ADB) till November 2024?', '{"A": "Masatsugu Asakawa", "B": "Takehiko Nakao", "C": "Haruhiko Kuroda", "D": "Tadao Chino"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The verified answer is Masatsugu Asakawa. The year 2024 anchors this question — the correct option is the fact that dates to that year. In MPSC PYQ analysis, this item type accounts for the largest cluster of ''easy marks lost due to misreading'' — slow down the stem, and the option leaps out.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","International Affairs & Summits"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22730, 'Elections & Representation', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'The ''National Voters Day'' is celebrated on which day every year?', '{"A": "24 January", "B": "25 January", "C": "26 January", "D": "15 January"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'National Voters'' Day is observed every year on 25 January—marking the Election Commission''s founding day (25 January 1950). 26 January is Republic Day; 24 January and 15 January are calendar distractors close to the ECI anniversary.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Elections & Representation"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22731, 'National Appointments & Reports', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Who has been appointed as the Chairperson of Lokpal in February 2024?', '{"A": "Ajay Manikrao Khanwilkar", "B": "Satish Chandra Sharma", "C": "Suryakanth Verma", "D": "Sanjeev Khanna"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A is the right choice since Justice Ajay Manikrao Khanwilkar was appointed Lokpal chairperson in February 2024 after the post fell vacant. Sharma, Verma, and Khanna are senior judiciary names but not the appointee for this anti-corruption ombudsman slot in that month. You can eliminate B (Satish Chandra Sharma), C (Suryakanth Verma), D (Sanjeev Khanna) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","National Appointments & Reports"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22732, 'Sports', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Which of the following country won 20 Gold, 12 Silver and 13 Bronze medals at the 2024 Olympic Games in Paris?', '{"A": "France", "B": "Australia", "C": "Japan", "D": "Netherlands"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The correct answer is option C — Japan''s Paris 2024 haul was 20 gold, 12 silver, 13 bronze—third on the medal table behind USA and China. France, Australia, and the Netherlands finished with different gold counts; Japan''s 20-gold headline was a national record for the country. Distractors A (France), B (Australia), D (Netherlands) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Sports"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22733, 'Renewable Energy', 'Science', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, '''Switch Delhi'' campaign is related with which of the following sector?', '{"A": "to switch from private to public schools", "B": "to switch from conventional vehicles to electric vehicles", "C": "to switch from coal energy to solar energy", "D": "to switch from private security to public security"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B is correct because ''Switch Delhi'' was the Delhi government''s mass-awareness campaign urging residents to switch from petrol/diesel vehicles to electric vehicles—incentives, charging infra, and fleet conversion. School, coal-to-solar, and private-to-public-security framings misinterpret the EV acronym context. You can eliminate A (to switch from private to public schools), C (to switch from coal energy to solar ene…), D (to switch from private security to publ…) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option B. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Science","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Renewable Energy"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22734, 'Centre-State Relations', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Which schedule is concerned with partition of Powers between Center and States?', '{"A": "Schedule-V", "B": "Schedule-VI", "C": "Schedule-VII", "D": "Schedule-VIII"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Seventh Schedule distributes legislative subjects across the Union List, State List, and Concurrent List—the constitutional partition of Centre–State powers. Fifth Schedule governs Scheduled Areas administration; Sixth covers Tribal Areas in Assam/NE; Eighth lists official languages—each is a different annex, not the power-dividing schedule.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Centre-State Relations"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22735, 'Constitutional Framework & Preamble', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'The Father of the Indian Constitution Dr. B.R. Ambedkar had declared which Article as the ''Heart and Soul of the Indian Constitution''?', '{"A": "Article - 31", "B": "Article - 32", "C": "Article - 33", "D": "Article - 34"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Dr. Ambedkar called Article 32 the ''heart and soul'' of the Constitution because it guarantees the right to constitutional remedies—without enforceable writs, other fundamental rights would be paper promises. Article 31 (old property right, later deleted) and Articles 33–34 (restrictions under martial law) are adjacent but not his celebrated phrase.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Constitutional Framework & Preamble"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22736, 'Union Executive', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Which of the following statements is correct regarding the President of India? (a) Article 58 of the Indian Constitution describes the qualification of the President. (b) The President can be removed through Impeachment if he violates the Constitution.', '{"A": "Only (a)", "B": "(a) and (b) both", "C": "Only (b)", "D": "Neither (a) and (b)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Choose option B: both limbs hold: Article 58 lays down presidential qualifications (citizenship, age 35, eligibility for Lok Sabha); Article 61 provides impeachment for constitutional violation—distinct from ordinary removal. Picking only (a) ignores the impeachment route; only (b) drops the qualification article; ''neither'' rejects two textbook truths. You can eliminate A (Only (a)), C (Only (b)), D (Neither (a) and (b)) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option B. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Union Executive"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22737, 'Constitutional Amendments', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Which Constitutional Amendment Act facilitated the appointment of the same person as a governor for two or more states?', '{"A": "First Constitutional Amendment Act - 1951", "B": "Seventh Constitutional Amendment Act - 1956", "C": "Twenty forth Constitutional Amendment Act - 1962", "D": "Forty second Constitutional Amendment Act - 1976"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B is the right choice since the Seventh Constitutional Amendment Act, 1956 enabled one person to serve as Governor of two or more states—matching post-reorganisation administrative convenience. The First Amendment (1951) dealt with zamindari and speech restrictions; the 24th (1971) and 42nd (1976) addressed other structural and emergency-era changes, not multi-state governorship. Distractors A (First Constitutional Amendment Act - 19…), C (Twenty forth Constitutional Amendment A…), D (Forty second Constitutional Amendment A…) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Constitutional Amendments"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22738, 'Constitutional Amendments', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Which constitutional amendment added the words ''Socialist'' and ''Secular'' to the preamble of the Indian Constitution?', '{"A": "41st amendment", "B": "44th amendment", "C": "46th amendment", "D": "42nd amendment"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The answer is option D: the 42nd Amendment (1976) added ''Socialist'' and ''Secular'' to the Preamble during the Emergency era. The 44th (1978) largely restored civil-liberty safeguards and deleted the property right from Part III—it did not insert those Preamble words. 41st and 46th amendments addressed other subjects (election disputes, VAT), not this Preamble pair. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Constitutional Amendments"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22739, 'Fundamental Rights', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'The Parmanand Katara Vs Union of India Case is associated with which of the following issue?', '{"A": "Medical Care", "B": "Banking", "C": "Education", "D": "Environment"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Parmanand Katara v. Union of India (1989) held that every doctor has a professional obligation to give emergency medical care—protecting the right to life under Article 21. Banking, education, and environment headline other landmark benches; this case is the medico-legal emergency-treatment precedent MPSC expects.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Fundamental Rights"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22740, 'Fundamental Rights', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Match List-1 (Articles of the Constitution of India) with List-2 (Provisions) and select the correct answer. (a) Article - 14 - (i) The state shall not discriminate against any citizens on the grounds of Religion, Race, Cast, Sex, Place of birth or any of them. (b) Article - 15 - (ii) There shall be equality of opportunity for all citizens in matters relating to employment or appointment to any office under the state. (c) Article - 16 - (iii) Untouchability is abolished and its practice in any form is prohibited. (d) Article - 17 - (iv) The State shall not deny any person equality before the law and equal protection of law within the Territory of India.', '{"A": "a-ii, b-iii, c-iv, d-i", "B": "a-iv, b-iii, c-ii, d-i", "C": "a-iv, b-i, c-ii, d-iii", "D": "a-iii, b-ii, c-i, d-iv"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C matches the question because article 14 = equality before the law and equal protection (iv); Article 15 = non-discrimination on religion, race, caste, sex, place of birth (i); Article 16 = equality of opportunity in public employment (ii); Article 17 = abolition of untouchability (iii). The grid a-iv, b-i, c-ii, d-iii alone aligns each article with its exact clause—swapping 14 with 17 is the common equality-rights trap. You can eliminate A (a-ii, b-iii, c-iv, d-i), B (a-iv, b-iii, c-ii, d-i), D (a-iii, b-ii, c-i, d-iv) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option C. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Fundamental Rights"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22741, 'Panchayati Raj', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Consider the following statements: (a) The 73rd Constitutional Amendment Act inserted part ''9'' in the Constitution regarding the Panchayati Raj system for rural areas. (b) A new Part ''9 A'' was added to the constitution regarding Urban Local Bodies through the 74th Constitutional Amendment Act. Which of the statements given above is/are correct?', '{"A": "Only (a)", "B": "Only (b)", "C": "Both (a) and (b)", "D": "Neither (a) nor (b)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C is correct because the 73rd Amendment (1992) inserted Part IX and Articles 243–243(O) for Panchayati Raj in rural areas; the 74th inserted Part IX-A for Urban Local Bodies (Municipalities). Statement (a) correctly names Part 9; (b) correctly names Part 9A—both amendments are paired facts in local-government syllabi. Distractors A (Only (a)), B (Only (b)), D (Neither (a) nor (b)) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Panchayati Raj"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22742, 'State Government', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Which article of the Indian Constitution makes provision for the Legislature Assembly?', '{"A": "Article - 170", "B": "Article - 171", "C": "Article - 172", "D": "Article - 173"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Choose option A: article 170 defines the composition of the Legislative Assembly in states. Article 171 covers the Legislative Council; 172 fixes duration of state legislatures; 173 states membership qualifications—students who recall ''170s block = state legislature'' should lock Assembly composition on 170 specifically. Distractors B (Article - 171), C (Article - 172), D (Article - 173) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","State Government"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22743, 'Judiciary', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Parliamentary resolution to change the number of Supreme Court Judges other than the Chief Justice of India can be passed by _________.', '{"A": "Simple Majority", "B": "Special Majority", "C": "Special Majority along with consent of half of the States", "D": "Special Majority with consent of all State Legislatives"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Changing the number of Supreme Court judges (other than the CJI) is done by ordinary parliamentary legislation under Article 124—simple majority suffices. Special-majority formulas apply to constitutional amendments and certain federal changes; half-state or all-state consent belongs to amendment categories, not routine strength revision of the apex court.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Judiciary"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22744, 'Constitutional Development (British Acts)', 'History', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Who among the following persons was not a member of the cabinet mission?', '{"A": "Sir William Wood", "B": "Lord Pethick Lawrence", "C": "Sir Stafford Cripps", "D": "A.V. Alexander"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Correct: option A — "Sir William Wood". The Cabinet Mission (March 1946) proposed a three-tier federal structure and led to the formation of India''s Constituent Assembly on 9 December 1946. The three wrong options are the standard distractor set MPSC uses for this topic — one is a chronological neighbour, one is a thematic near-miss and one is a plausible-sounding invention.', '{"History","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Constitutional Development (British Acts)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22745, 'Panchayati Raj', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'As per Article 243 (E) of the Constitution of India every Gram Panchayat Shall continue to exist for five years _________ unless it has already been dissolved under any law for the time being in force.', '{"A": "from the date of declaration of election results", "B": "from the date of declaration of elections", "C": "from the date fixed for its first meeting after election", "D": "from the first Financial Year commencing after the Panchayat elections"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The correct answer is option C — article 243(E) fixes a Panchayat''s five-year term from the date appointed for its first meeting after election—not from result declaration, election notification, or the succeeding financial year. Confusing ''first meeting'' with ''results day'' shortens or lengthens the tenure incorrectly in local-body law MCQs. You can eliminate A (from the date of declaration of electio…), B (from the date of declaration of electio…), D (from the first Financial Year commencin…) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option C. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Panchayati Raj"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22746, 'Constitutional Framework & Preamble', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Which of the following are not the Federal Features of Indian Constitution? (a) All India Services (b) Single Judiciary (c) Independent Judiciary (d) Division of Powers', '{"A": "Only (a) and (c)", "B": "Only (a) and (b)", "C": "Only (b) and (c)", "D": "Only (c) and (d)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B works here because all India Services (IAS/IPS/IFS) and a single integrated judiciary are unitary/centralising features—Union cadre control and one pyramid of courts from district to Supreme Court. Independent judiciary and a written division of powers (Seventh Schedule) are classic federal traits; options listing (c) or (d) as ''non-federal'' invert the standard K.C. Wheare analysis. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Constitutional Framework & Preamble"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22747, 'Panchayati Raj', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'The Provision for reservation of seats for women in Panchayats is made by which article of the Indian Constitution?', '{"A": "Article 243-B", "B": "Article 243-C", "C": "Article 243-D", "D": "Article 243-E"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Article 243(D) mandates reservation of seats for women in Panchayats (including SC/ST sub-quotas within the one-third rule). 243-B defines the three-tier structure; 243-C covers composition; 243-E covers duration—reservation is explicitly on 243-D in the 73rd Amendment text.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Panchayati Raj"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22748, 'State Government', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'With reference to the article 165 of the Indian Constitution who is the legal adviser to the Government of State?', '{"A": "The Solicitor General", "B": "Additional Government Pleader", "C": "The Advocate General", "D": "The High Court Judge"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The answer is option C: article 165 creates the office of Advocate General—the state''s chief legal adviser and primary law officer before courts. The Solicitor General serves the Union Government; Additional Government Pleader is a litigation post, not the constitutional adviser; a High Court Judge cannot simultaneously be the state''s legal adviser. You can eliminate A (The Solicitor General), B (Additional Government Pleader), D (The High Court Judge) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option C. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","State Government"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22749, 'Mechanics & Motion', 'Science', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Ball bearing are used in machine to reduce _________.', '{"A": "Static Friction", "B": "Rolling Friction", "C": "Sliding Friction", "D": "Fluid Friction"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Ball bearings interpose rolling elements between shaft and housing so sliding contact becomes rolling contact—dramatically cutting sliding friction (and the heat/wear it causes). They do not target static friction at rest, fluid drag, or ''reduce rolling friction''—rolling friction is already the low-friction mode they exploit.', '{"Science","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Mechanics & Motion"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22750, 'Optics & Sound', 'Science', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Choose the right answer: (a) Human being can listen the sound of frequency 20 to 20000 Hz. (b) Infrasonic waves have frequency more than 20000 Hz. (c) Ultrasonic waves have frequency less than 20 Hz. (d) Sound waves can''t travel through solids.', '{"A": "Only (d) sentence is correct.", "B": "Only (c) and (d) sentence is correct.", "C": "All sentences are correct.", "D": "Only (a) sentence is correct."}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D is the right choice since only (a) survives scrutiny: human hearing spans roughly 20–20,000 Hz. Infrasonic waves lie below 20 Hz; ultrasonic above 20,000 Hz—(b) and (c) reverse the definitions. Sound propagates well through solids (faster than in air)—(d) is false; You can eliminate A (Only (d) sentence is correct.), B (Only (c) and (d) sentence is correct.), C (All sentences are correct.) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option D. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Science","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Optics & Sound"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (22751, 'Metals & Materials', 'Science', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Bronze alloy is a combination of _________.', '{"A": "Copper and Tin", "B": "Copper and Zinc", "C": "Copper and Nickel", "D": "Copper and Iron"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Bronze is chiefly copper + tin (Cu–Sn)—the alloy of antiquity for tools and statues. Copper + zinc gives brass; copper + nickel gives cupronickel; copper + iron is not the standard bronze recipe—mixing brass and bronze compositions is a recurring prelims trap.', '{"Science","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Metals & Materials"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22752, 'Zoology (Animal Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'In Peteromyzon, the anticoagulant is secreted by _________.', '{"A": "Goblet gland", "B": "Mucous gland", "C": "Salivary gland", "D": "Zymogen Cells"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'In Petromyzon (lamprey), the salivary gland secretes anticoagulant (hirudin-like) so host blood flows during ectoparasitic feeding. Goblet and mucous glands produce lubrication; zymogen cells relate to digestive enzyme precursors—not the anticoagulant role tested here.', '{"Science","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Zoology (Animal Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22753, 'Chemical Bonding & Reactions', 'Science', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'The molecule which has the largest dipole moment among the following is _________.', '{"A": "CH₄", "B": "CHCl₃", "C": "CCl₄", "D": "CHI₃"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Among the four, CH₄ and CCl₄ are tetrahedral and symmetric—net dipole moment zero. CHCl₃ retains three polar C–Cl bonds without full cancellation, giving the largest non-zero dipole in the set. CHI₃ is polar too, but syllabus keys and textbook comparisons for this exact quartet point to chloroform (CHCl₃) as the standout asymmetric halomethane.', '{"Science","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Chemical Bonding & Reactions"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22754, 'Electricity & Magnetism', 'Science', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Which of the following electronic device converts light energy into electric energy?', '{"A": "Photovoltaic diode", "B": "Photodiode", "C": "L.E.D.", "D": "Tunnel Diode"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'A photovoltaic (solar) cell/diode converts incident light directly into electric current via the photoelectric effect in a p–n junction. A photodiode mainly detects light; an LED converts electricity to light; a tunnel diode exploits quantum tunnelling for switching/oscillation—not optical-to-electrical power conversion.', '{"Science","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Electricity & Magnetism"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22755, 'Zoology (Animal Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Match the below mentioned animal with their order: (a) Indian earthworm - (i) Hemiptera (b) Indian Cattle leech - (ii) Opisthopora (c) Honey bee - (iii) Gnathobdellida (d) Bedbug - (iv) Hymenoptera', '{"A": "a-iv, b-i, c-iii, d-ii", "B": "a-ii, b-iii, c-i, d-iv", "C": "a-iii, b-i, c-ii, d-iv", "D": "a-ii, b-iii, c-iv, d-i"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The answer is option D: Taxonomic orders: Indian earthworm (Pheretima) → Opisthopora (ii); Indian cattle leech → Gnathobdellida (iii); honey bee → Hymenoptera (iv); bedbug → Hemiptera (i). Pairing earthworm with Hemiptera or bee with Gnathobdellida scrambles invertebrate classification—one correct match (bee–Hymenoptera) prunes most grids. Distractors A (a-iv, b-i, c-iii, d-ii), B (a-ii, b-iii, c-i, d-iv), C (a-iii, b-i, c-ii, d-iv) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Science","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Zoology (Animal Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22756, 'Botany (Plant Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Biofertilizers bring about:', '{"A": "addition of Mercury to the Soil.", "B": "nutrient enrichment to the Soil.", "C": "increase in the Acidity of Soil.", "D": "decrease in soil fertility."}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B is the right choice since Biofertilizers (Rhizobium, Azotobacter, mycorrhiza, etc.) fix or mobilise nutrients—enriching soil fertility without chemical overload. They do not add toxic mercury, deliberately acidify soil, or deplete fertility—options (a), (c), and (d) describe harms opposite to sustainable agriculture extension messages. Distractors A (addition of Mercury to the Soil.), C (increase in the Acidity of Soil.), D (decrease in soil fertility.) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Science","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Botany (Plant Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22757, 'Zoology (Animal Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, '"Kangaroo" is an animal belongs to Phylum _________.', '{"A": "Reptilia", "B": "Mammalia", "C": "Amphibia", "D": "Aves"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Choose option B: Kangaroo is a marsupial mammal (class Mammalia, infraclass Marsupialia)—hair, mammary glands, and pouch-rearing place it firmly outside Reptilia, Amphibia, and Aves. ''Phylum'' in the stem is loose exam wording; the correct answer is Mammalia among the class-level options offered. You can eliminate A (Reptilia), C (Amphibia), D (Aves) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option B. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Science","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Zoology (Animal Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22758, 'Diseases & Health', 'Science', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Oral Polio Vaccine is manufactured in which of the following Laboratories? (a) Hoffkin biopharmaceutical corporation Ltd. (b) Panacea Biotech (c) Biomed, Gaziabad (d) National Institute of Nutrition, Hyderabad', '{"A": "(a) only", "B": "(a) and (b) only", "C": "(a), (b) and (c) only", "D": "(d) only"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C is correct because Oral Polio Vaccine (OPV) production in India involves Haffkine Bio-Pharmaceutical (Mumbai), Panacea Biotec, and Biomed (Ghaziabad)—all three appear in standard public-health manufacturing lists. The National Institute of Nutrition (Hyderabad) researches nutrition science; it is not an OPV production centre—option (d) alone or (a)–(b) only under-counts licensed OPV makers. Distractors A ((a) only), B ((a) and (b) only), D ((d) only) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Science","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Diseases & Health"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22759, 'Botany (Plant Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Which of the following statement is incorrect about bryophytes?', '{"A": "They are known as amphibians of Plant kingdom.", "B": "They require water for reproduction.", "C": "They have rhizoids instead of roots.", "D": "Rhizopus is example of them."}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D works here because Bryophytes (mosses, liverworts) are ''amphibians of the plant kingdom''—need water for fertilisation and have rhizoids instead of true roots; all true. Rhizopus is a zygomycete fungus (bread mould), not a bryophyte—statement (d) is the sole incorrect line. You can eliminate A (They are known as amphibians of Plant k…), B (They require water for reproduction.), C (They have rhizoids instead of roots.) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option D. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Science","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Botany (Plant Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22760, 'Ecology & Ecosystems', 'General Studies', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'The interaction in which one species benefits and other is neither harmed nor benefited is termed as _________.', '{"A": "Mutualism", "B": "Parasitism", "C": "Amensalism", "D": "Commensalism"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Commensalism (+, 0): one species benefits, the other is unaffected—classic examples include epiphytes on trees or cattle egrets near grazing herds. Mutualism (+,+), parasitism (+,−), and amensalism (0,−) each change the sign pattern—students who label any ''+ only'' interaction as mutualism miss the neutral partner in commensalism.', '{"General Studies","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Ecology & Ecosystems"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22761, 'Nutrition', 'Science', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, '_________ mineral deficiency is most common cause of goiter disease.', '{"A": "Iodine", "B": "Iron", "C": "Calcium", "D": "Sodium"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A matches the question because Goitre (thyroid enlargement) most commonly reflects dietary iodine deficiency impairing thyroxine synthesis. Iron links to anaemia; calcium to bone/metabolic signs; sodium to electrolyte balance—not endemic goitre in iodine-poor belts. You can eliminate B (Iron), C (Calcium), D (Sodium) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Science","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Nutrition"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22762, 'Mensuration & Geometry', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'A solid sphere of radius 30 cm is melted and recasted into solid cylinders of radius 10 cm and height 4 cm, then number of solid cylinders formed will be _________.', '{"A": "100", "B": "95", "C": "90", "D": "85"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Volume conservation on melting/recasting: sphere = (4/3)π(30)³ = 36,000π cm³; each cylinder = π(10)²(4) = 400π cm³; count = 36,000π ÷ 400π = 90. Using diameter instead of radius, or dividing by lateral surface area, produces 85/95/100 distractors.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Mensuration & Geometry"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22763, 'Botany (Plant Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Tikka disease of Groundnut is caused by:', '{"A": "Fusarium", "B": "Cercospora", "C": "Colletotrichum", "D": "Puccinia"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Groundnut tikka (early leaf spot) is a fungal leaf-blight caused by Cercospora arachidicola / C. personata—not rust (Puccinia), anthracnose (Colletotrichum on other crops), or Fusarium wilt complexes. Pathogen-class mismatch is how MPSC splits look-alike crop-disease names.', '{"Science","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Botany (Plant Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22764, 'Mensuration & Geometry', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'The perimeter of the rectilinear shape given in the figure is: [L-shaped figure with dimensions 5 cm, 2 cm, 7 cm, 9 cm]', '{"A": "42 cm", "B": "21 cm", "C": "23 cm", "D": "32 cm"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The correct answer is option A — Trace every outer edge of the L-shape once: equivalent to 2×(9+7) + 2×(5+2) − 4 (subtract double-counted inner corner) = 42 cm. Summing only one rectangle (21 or 32) or halving the boundary walk ignores the notch steps labelled 5 cm and 2 cm. You can eliminate B (21 cm), C (23 cm), D (32 cm) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Mensuration & Geometry"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22765, 'Ratio, Proportion & Averages', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'The ratio of income and expenditure of a teacher is 11 : 9. If he saves ₹ 36,000 per annum, his monthly income is _________.', '{"A": "₹ 16,000", "B": "₹ 20,000", "C": "₹ 18,000", "D": "₹ 16,500"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Income : Expenditure = 11 : 9 → savings = 2 parts = ₹36,000/year → 1 part = ₹18,000 → annual income = 11 × 18,000 = ₹1,98,000 → monthly ₹16,500. Treating 36,000 as one part (₹1,80,000/month) or dividing annual income by 9 instead of 11 yields ₹18,000/₹20,000 traps.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Ratio, Proportion & Averages"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22766, 'Time, Speed & Distance', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'A train travels a distance of 480 km at a Uniform speed. If the speed had been 8 km/hr less, then it would have taken 3 hours more to cover the same distance. Find the initial speed of the train.', '{"A": "40 km/hr", "B": "32 km/hr", "C": "48 km/hr", "D": "36 km/hr"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Let speed = s km/h: 480/s + 3 = 480/(s−8) → 3840 = 3s(s−8) → s² − 8s − 1280 = 0 → s = 40 (reject negative root). Check: 480/40 = 12 h vs 480/32 = 15 h—difference 3 h. Plugging 48 or 36 is incorrect the time-gap condition.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Time, Speed & Distance"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22767, 'Percentage, Profit & Loss', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'In a class 40% of the boys got a scholarship. If 50% of the students got a scholarship and girls constitute 60% of the total strength, find the percentage of girls who got the scholarship.', '{"A": "60.1%", "B": "56.67%", "C": "30%", "D": "55.6%"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Take class strength 100: boys 40, girls 60. Scholarships total 50; boys receiving = 40% of 40 = 16; girls = 50 − 16 = 34; girl share = 34/60 × 100 = 56.67%. Assuming 50% of girls (30%) or applying 40% to the whole class (60.1%) ignores the boys'' separate 40% rate.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Percentage, Profit & Loss"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22768, 'Time & Work', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Work done by Arun in one day is half of the work done by Sachin in one day. Work done by Sachin in one day is half of the work done by Rahul in one day. If Rahul alone can complete the work in 14 days, in how many days can Arun, Sachin and Rahul together complete the work?', '{"A": "4", "B": "6", "C": "8", "D": "5"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Rahul''s one-day work = 1/14; Sachin = half of that = 1/28; Arun = half of Sachin = 1/56. Combined rate = 1/14 + 1/28 + 1/56 = 7/56 = 1/8 → 8 days together. Averaging 14, 28, 56 or forgetting the halving chain gives 4/5/6 day distractors.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Time & Work"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22769, 'Ratio, Proportion & Averages', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'The Average marks obtained by the students in a class is 13. If the average marks obtained by 25 boys is 10 and the average marks obtained by girls is 18, then the number of girls in the class are:', '{"A": "10", "B": "5", "C": "15", "D": "20"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C matches the question because Let girls = g: (25×10 + 18g)/(25+g) = 13 → 250 + 18g = 325 + 13g → 5g = 75 → g = 15. Weighted-average pivot: class mean 13 lies between boys (10) and girls (18)—15 girls pulls the mean correctly; g = 5 or 20 overshoots the balance. Distractors A (10), B (5), D (20) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Ratio, Proportion & Averages"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22770, 'Mensuration & Geometry', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'A 21 meter tall tree is broken by wind at a height x meter from its bottom in such a way that its top struck the ground at certain angle and at a distance 7√3 meter from the tree. Then find out height x of a tree.', '{"A": "5√3 meter", "B": "5 meter", "C": "7 meter", "D": "9 meter"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C works here because Broken tree: stump height x, fallen part (21−x) forms the hypotenuse with horizontal 7√3 m. Pythagoras: (21−x)² = x² + (7√3)² → 441 − 42x + x² = x² + 147 → x = 7 m. Answers 5 m or 5√3 m come from mis-assigning which segment is opposite the base angle. Distractors A (5√3 meter), B (5 meter), D (9 meter) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Mensuration & Geometry"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22771, 'Percentage, Profit & Loss', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'A shopkeeper sells two mobile phone for ₹ 3,600 each. He gained profit of 20% on one mobile phone and loss of 20% on another mobile phone. What was the net profit or loss in entire transaction?', '{"A": "₹ 300 loss", "B": "₹ 400 loss", "C": "₹ 250 profit", "D": "₹ 200 profit"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A is the right choice since Equal selling prices hide unequal cost prices: CP at +20% = 3600/1.2 = 3000; CP at −20% = 3600/0.8 = 4500; total CP 7500 vs total SP 7200 → net loss ₹300. Students who subtract 20% from 20% and expect break-even miss the reciprocal-cost arithmetic on the loss side. You can eliminate B (₹ 400 loss), C (₹ 250 profit), D (₹ 200 profit) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Percentage, Profit & Loss"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22772, 'Puzzles', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'Observe the numbers in the following circles and find the correct alternative of the number which comes at the place of question mark. [Circle diagram: 16, 17, 13, 18, 70(center), 20, ?, 15, 19]', '{"A": "17", "B": "21", "C": "15", "D": "22"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Peripheral numbers 16+17+13+18+20+15+19 = 118; centre 70 doubled = 140; missing value = 140 − 118 = 22. Pattern: outer ring sum is twice the hub—picking 17 or 21 applies the wrong operator (pairwise sum 35, not hub doubling).', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Puzzles"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22773, 'Clocks & Calendars', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'It is 9 a.m. in Rinku''s watch. If hours hand is in the west direction then what direction remain minute hand at that time?', '{"A": "South", "B": "West", "C": "North", "D": "East"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C is correct because at 9 a.m. the hour hand sits near 9 (west if 12 is treated as north on a compass-oriented watch); the minute hand at 12 points north. West–west pairing ignores that only the hour hand was rotated to west; minute hand stays on the north–south axis at o''clock times. You can eliminate A (South), B (West), D (East) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option C. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Clocks & Calendars"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22774, 'Percentage, Profit & Loss', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'If a 20% reduction in the price of sugar gives the buyer 2.5 kg more sugar at a cost of ₹ 160. Find the original cost per kg.', '{"A": "₹ 15", "B": "₹ 20", "C": "₹ 12", "D": "₹ 16"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Choose option D: 20% price cut → new price = 0.8p. ₹160 buys 160/(0.8p) − 160/p = 40/p = 2.5 kg more → p = ₹16/kg. Treating 160 as original budget at old price, or adding 20% to ₹16, revives ₹15/₹20 options. You can eliminate A (₹ 15), B (₹ 20), C (₹ 12) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option D. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Percentage, Profit & Loss"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22775, 'Clocks & Calendars', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'What was the day of the week on 14th August 1947?', '{"A": "Monday", "B": "Wednesday", "C": "Thursday", "D": "Friday"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The correct answer is option C — 14 August 1947 was a Thursday—Independence Eve before Friday''s midnight transfer; standard calendar reckoning from a known anchor (e.g., 1 Jan 1900 = Monday) confirms it. Wednesday/Friday options usually come from timezone or off-by-one counting errors around the midnight ceremony. Distractors A (Monday), B (Wednesday), D (Friday) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Clocks & Calendars"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22776, 'Coding-Decoding', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'In a code language ''UNNATI'' is written as 79 then, in the same language how ''UTKARSH'' will be written?', '{"A": "80", "B": "90", "C": "97", "D": "98"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Code = sum of alphabetical positions (A=1…Z=26): UNNATI → 21+14+14+1+20+9 = 79. UTKARSH → 21+20+11+1+18+19+8 = 98. Letter-count or reverse-alphabet tricks give 80/90/97—only full forward-position addition hits 98.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Coding-Decoding"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22777, 'Ranking & Ordering', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'N ranks fifth in a class. S is eighth from the last. If T is sixth after N and just in the middle of N and S, then how many students are there in the class?', '{"A": "23", "B": "24", "C": "25", "D": "26"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B works here because N is 5th; T is 6 ranks after N → 11th; T is mid-point of N and S → S is 17th from top. S is 8th from last → total = 17 + 8 − 1 = 24. Forgetting ''midpoint'' (taking T as 6th from bottom) or adding ranks without −1 yields 23/25/26. You can eliminate A (23), C (25), D (26) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option B. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Ranking & Ordering"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22778, 'Number System & Simplification', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'There are some mangoes in the box. If it distributed equally among 12 boys, 8 mangoes remains in the box. If the same mangoes are distributed to 14 boys, 10 mangoes remains in the box. How many mangoes are there in the box?', '{"A": "84", "B": "80", "C": "76", "D": "74"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B is correct because Let total mangoes = M: M ≡ 8 (mod 12) and M ≡ 10 (mod 14). Smallest consistent M = 80 (LCM step: 12×6+8 = 80 = 14×5+10). 84 satisfies the first remainder but not the second; 76/74 is wrong both congruences. Distractors A (84), C (76), D (74) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Number System & Simplification"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22779, 'Data Interpretation', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'The following Pia-diagram shows the monthly expenses of a family on different items. If the monthly income of the family is ₹ 46,800. How much more expenses are incurred on foodgrains than on clothing?', '{"A": "₹ 8,840", "B": "₹ 8,820", "C": "₹ 4,820", "D": "₹ 8,440"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The answer is option A: Pie sectors from the paper: Food grains 144°, Clothing 76° → difference 68°. Extra on food = (68/360) × ₹46,800 = ₹8,840. Using only one sector, halving the angle gap (₹4,820), or a rounding slip on 68° lands on the 8,820/8,440 close distractors. Distractors B (₹ 8,820), C (₹ 4,820), D (₹ 8,440) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Data Interpretation"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22780, 'Constitutional Development (British Acts)', 'History', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'पंडित जवाहरलाल नेहरूंनी कोणत्या कायद्याचे वर्णन ''गुलामगिरीची एक नवी सनद'' असे केले?', '{"A": "मोर्ले-मिंटो सुधारणा कायदा, 1909", "B": "माँटेग्यु-चेम्सफर्ड सुधारणा कायदा, 1919", "C": "भारत सरकार कायदा, 1935", "D": "रोलेट कायदा, 1919"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'इतिहासात हे लक्षात ठेवा — Jawaharlal Nehru यांनी Government of India Act, १९३५ ला ''नवीन गुलामगिरीचा घोषवाक्य'' म्हणून हल्ला केला — कागदावर प्रांतीय स्वायत्तता, पण veto, राज्यघटना राज्यांचे संरक्षण, खरी स्व-शासन नाही. Morley–Minto (१९०९) आणि Montagu–Chelmsford (१९१९) ला वेगळी टोपणी; Rowlatt (१९१९) ''काळा'' दडपशाही कायदा — Nehru चा १९३५ चा शब्द नाही — पर्याय C।', '{"History","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Constitutional Development (British Acts)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22781, 'Revolt of 1857', 'History', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'कंपनी सरकारने आपल्या सैनिकांसाठी उपलब्ध केलेल्या ''एनफिल्ड रायफल'' हाताळण्यासाठी खालीलपैकी कोणत्या शहरात प्रशिक्षणाची व्यवस्था केलेली होती? (a) अंबाला (b) कलकत्ता (c) सियालकोट (d) डम डम', '{"A": "(a), (b) आणि (c)", "B": "(b) आणि (d)", "C": "(a), (c) आणि (d)", "D": "(a), (b) आणि (d)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'इतिहासात हे लक्षात ठेवा — १८५७ च्या Enfield rifle साठी company arsenals वरून greased cartridges issue झाले; sepoys नवीन rifle वर drill करत — Ambala, Sialkot, Dum Dum ही Maharashtra इतिहास अभ्यासक्रमातील standard trio. Calcutta (Fort William) राजकीय राजधानी, rifle-training centres मध्ये नाव नाही. अर्धवट संच Dum Dum किंवा Sialkot वगळल्यास deployment chain अपूर्ण — पर्याय C।', '{"History","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Revolt of 1857"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22782, 'Puzzles', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'If A=4, B=6, C=8, then find the missing part of the diagram. [Matrix pattern puzzle with letters P,B,C,M / E,_,_,H / I,_,_,L / D,N,O,A]', '{"A": "F,K / G,J", "B": "J,K / G,F", "C": "K,J / G,F", "D": "G,J / K,F"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Given A=4, B=6, C=8 in the matrix corners/labels, interior cells follow the same letter-position offset grid—missing pair K,J / G,F completes row–column sums consistent with the edge letters P,B,C,M and D,N,O,A. Alternate diagonals F,K or G,J swap middle rows and break the A/B/C value ladder.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Puzzles"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22783, 'Blood Relations', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'M and N are brothers, Q and R are sisters. Son of M is Brother of R, then what is the relation of N with Q?', '{"A": "Brother", "B": "Grandfather", "C": "Father", "D": "Uncle"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'M and N are brothers; Q and R are sisters. M''s son being R''s brother means R (and typically Q) are M''s daughters—making N the paternal uncle of Q. ''Brother'' would require N to be Q''s sibling (same parents); ''father'' would make N the parent—only uncle fits the brother-of-M / father-of-Q relation chain.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Blood Relations"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22784, 'British Expansion & Governors-General', 'History', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'खालीलपैकी कोणत्या आयोगाच्या शिफारशीनुसार 1883 साली दुष्काळ संहिता तयार करण्यात आली?', '{"A": "सर रिचर्ड स्ट्रॅची आयोग", "B": "जॉर्ज कॅम्पबेल आयोग", "C": "मॅकडोनाल्ड आयोग", "D": "सर जेम्स ल्याल आयोग"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'इतिहासात हे लक्षात ठेवा — Indian Famine Code, १८८३ Sir Richard Strachey (१८८०) Famine Commission शिफारसीवरून — drought नंतर relief, works, mortality reporting standardise. George Campbell, James Lyall नंतरच्या famine inquiries; MacDonald वेगळ्या policy era. Strachey + १८८३ Famine Code — ही जोडी लक्षात ठेवा — पर्याय A।', '{"History","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","British Expansion & Governors-General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22785, 'British Expansion & Governors-General', 'History', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'कोणत्या व्हॉईसरॉयच्या कालखंडात जिल्हा लोकल बोर्डाची स्थापना झाली?', '{"A": "लॉर्ड रिपन", "B": "लॉर्ड लिटन", "C": "लॉर्ड कर्झन", "D": "लॉर्ड वेलस्ली"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'इतिहासात हे लक्षात ठेवा — Lord Ripon (१८८०–८४) भारतात ''Local Self-Government चे जनक''; १८८२ resolution ने district/municipal boards, District Local Boards rural administration साठी विस्तार. Lytton ने Ripon ची उदारता मागे घेतली; Curzon centralised; Wellesley Ripon-era local-board framework पूर्व — पर्याय A।', '{"History","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","British Expansion & Governors-General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22786, 'Socio-Religious Reform Movements', 'History', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'प्रार्थना समाजाच्या माध्यमातून खालीलपैकी कोणकोणत्या सामाजिक कार्य करणाऱ्या संस्था स्थापन झाल्या? (a) सोशल सर्व्हीस लीग — न.म. जोशी (b) सर्व्हंटस् ऑफ इंडिया सोसायटी — ग.क. गोखले (c) आर्य समाज — दयानंद सरस्वती (d) डिप्रेस्ड क्लासेस मिशन — वि.रा. शिंदे', '{"A": "(a) आणि (b) फक्त", "B": "(b) आणि (c) फक्त", "C": "(a), (b) आणि (d) फक्त", "D": "(b), (c) आणि (d) फक्त"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'इतिहासात हे लक्षात ठेवा — प्रार्थना समाज (१८६७, मुंबई) ने अनेक सुधारणा संस्था घडवल्या: G.K. Gokhale यांचे Servants of India Society (१९०५), N.M. Joshi यांची Social Service League, V.R. Shinde यांचे Depressed Classes Mission — हे सर्व त्या वातावरणातून उद्भवले. Arya Samaj हा Dayanand Saraswati यांचा वेगळा उत्तर भारतीय पुनरुज्जीवन आंदोलन होता — प्रार्थना समाजाची शाखा नव्हते. (a), (b) आणि (d) एकत्र योग्य आहेत — पर्याय C।', '{"History","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Socio-Religious Reform Movements"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22787, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, '''सत्यशोधक जलसा'' या कलाप्रकाराशी पुढीलपैकी कोण संबंधित नव्हते?', '{"A": "होनाजी बाळा", "B": "भाऊराव पाटोळे", "C": "रामचंद्र घाटगे", "D": "जोतीराव फाळके"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'इतिहासात हे लक्षात ठेवा — Satyashodhak Jalsa हा Jotirao Phule यांच्या Satyashodhak Samaj चा cultural-theatre wing — Bhaurao Patole, Ramchandra Ghatge, Jotirao Falke documented performers/organisers. Honaji Bala Tamasha/folk-theatre परंपरेत, Satyashodhak Jalsa circuit मध्ये नाही. ''Not associated'' — Phule च्या reform stage बाहेरचे नाव — पर्याय A।', '{"History","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22788, 'Maharashtra in Freedom Struggle', 'History', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'जोड्या लावा: (a) 1899 ''गुराखी'' (मुंबई) — (i) अ.ब. कोल्हटकर (b) 1906 ''भाला'' (पुणे) — (ii) गिर (c) 1907 ''हरिकिशोर'' (यवतमाळ) — (iii) श्री. ल.न. जोशी (d) 1909 ''देशसेवक'' (नागपूर) — (iv) भोपटकर', '{"A": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(iii), (c)-(iv), (d)-(i)", "B": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(i), (c)-(iii), (d)-(ii)", "C": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(iv), (c)-(ii), (d)-(i)", "D": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(iii), (c)-(i), (d)-(iv)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'जोड्या लावताना — १८९९ ''Gurakhi'' (Mumbai) → Shri L.N. Joshi; १९०६ ''Bhala'' (Pune) → Bhopatkar; १९०७ ''Hari Kishore'' (Yavatmal) → Gir; १९०९ ''Deshsevak'' (Nagpur) → A.B. Kolhatkar. a-iii, b-iv, c-ii, d-i. Kolhatkar–Bhopatkar किंवा Gir अदलाबदल Marathi nationalist journalism chronology तोडते — पर्याय C।', '{"History","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Maharashtra in Freedom Struggle"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22789, 'Rise of Nationalism & INC', 'History', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'खालील विधाने वाचून व्यक्ती ओळखा. विधान A: सरोजिनी नायडू यांनी ''हिंदू-मुस्लिम ऐक्याचे राजदूत'' म्हणून त्यांचा गौरव केला. विधान B: ''मी प्रथम राष्ट्रवादी आहे, नंतरही राष्ट्रवादी आहे आणि शेवटीही राष्ट्रवादी आहे'' असे विधान त्यांनी कायदेमंडळातील भाषणात केले.', '{"A": "सर सय्यद अहमद खान", "B": "मौलाना अबुल कलाम आझाद", "C": "मोहम्मद अली जिना", "D": "मोहम्मद इक्बाल"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'इतिहासात हे लक्षात ठेवा — Sarojini Naidu यांनी early Jinnah ला ''ambassador of Hindu–Muslim unity'' म्हणून ओळखले. त्यांचे legislature speech — ''I am a Nationalist first, a Nationalist second, and a Nationalist last'' — pre-1940 Jinnah biographies मध्ये quoted. Azad, Iqbal, Sir Syed प्रत्येकजण stem च्या एका marker चुकवतो — पर्याय C।', '{"History","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Rise of Nationalism & INC"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22790, 'British Expansion & Governors-General', 'History', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'स्ट्रॅची आयोग कशाशी संबंधित होता?', '{"A": "शैक्षणिक सुधारणा", "B": "आरोग्य सुधारणा", "C": "दुष्काळ उपाययोजना", "D": "बालविवाह रोधन"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'इतिहासात हे लक्षात ठेवा — Strachey Commission (१८८०) Great Famine of 1876–78 नंतर famine/drought relief policy घडवण्यासाठी — education, health, child-marriage reform नाही. Report ने १८८३ Famine Code अंतर्भूत. Q5 मधील Strachey drought-relief mandate शी जोडा — पर्याय C।', '{"History","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","British Expansion & Governors-General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22791, 'Indian Physical Geography', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'पुढील पर्वत शिखरांचा उंचीनुसार उतरता क्रम लावा. (a) मकालू (b) नंदादेवी (c) अन्नपूर्णा (d) बद्रिनाथ', '{"A": "(d), (a), (b), (c)", "B": "(b), (d), (c), (a)", "C": "(a), (c), (b), (d)", "D": "(c), (b), (a), (d)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'भूगोलात हे स्थिर — Makalu (~8,485 m) > Annapurna I (~8,091 m) > Nandadevi (~7,816 m) > Badrinath (~6,150 m pilgrimage peak). Descending (a)–(c)–(b)–(d). Nandadevi above Makalu किंवा Badrinath mid-list Himalayan hierarchy गोंधळते — पर्याय C।', '{"Geography","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Indian Physical Geography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22792, 'Trade Union & Labour Movement', 'History', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, '1920 मध्ये स्थापन झालेल्या ''ऑल इंडिया ट्रेड युनियन काँग्रेस''चे पहिले अध्यक्ष खालीलपैकी कोण होते?', '{"A": "लाला लजपत राय", "B": "लोकमान्य टिळक", "C": "श्रीपाद अमृत डांगे", "D": "अशोक मेहता"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'इतिहासात हे लक्षात ठेवा — Lala Lajpat Rai यांनी १९२० Bombay मध्यe All India Trade Union Congress (AITUC) inaugural session अध्यक्ष केले. Tilak त्या वर्षी died, AITUC president नव्हते; Shripad Dange, Ashok Mehta नंतरचे leaders. First-president MCQs १९२० founding chair test करतात — पर्याय A।', '{"History","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Trade Union & Labour Movement"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22793, 'Population & Census', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, '2011 च्या जनगणनेनुसार, महाराष्ट्रातील खालील जिल्हे आणि तेथील शहरी लोकसंख्येच्या शेकडा प्रमाण यांच्या जोड्या लावा. (a) अहिल्यानगर — (i) 25.47 (b) यवतमाळ — (ii) 18.98 (c) सातारा — (iii) 21.59 (d) लातूर — (iv) 20.10', '{"A": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(i), (c)-(iv), (d)-(iii)", "B": "(a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(iv)", "C": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(iii), (c)-(ii), (d)-(i)", "D": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(iv), (c)-(i), (d)-(ii)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'जोड्या लावताना — Census 2011 urban-population: Ahilyanagar–(iv), Yavatmal–(iii), Satara–(ii), Latur–(i) — a-iv, b-iii, c-ii, d-i. Alphabetical district order (a-i, b-ii…) tidy पण Yavatmal–Latur figures mis-assign — पर्याय C।', '{"Geography","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Population & Census"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22794, 'Population & Census', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'खालीलपैकी कोणती लिपी संथाली भाषेमध्ये वापरली जाते?', '{"A": "बिल्लू", "B": "ओल चिकी", "C": "ब्रेल", "D": "कोटा"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'भूगोलात हे स्थिर — Santhali (Munda) Ol Chiki script — Pandit Raghunath Murmu १९२५, Eighth Schedule. ''Billu'', ''Kota'' script names चuकी; Braille visually impaired साठी — Santhali language script नाही — पर्याय B।', '{"Geography","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Population & Census"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22795, 'Maharashtra Physical Geography', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'खालील विधाने विचारात घ्या. (a) महाराष्ट्राचा अक्षवृत्तीय विस्तार रेखावृत्तीय विस्तारापेक्षा कमी आहे. (b) महाराष्ट्र राज्यातून कर्कवृत्त जाते. (c) महाराष्ट्राची पूर्व-पश्चिम लांबी सुमारे 800 कि.मी. आहे. (d) महाराष्ट्राचे क्षेत्रफळ 3,07,713 चौ. कि.मी. आहे. वरीलपैकी कोणते/कोणती विधाने बरोबर आहेत?', '{"A": "फक्त (a)", "B": "फक्त (a) आणि (b)", "C": "फक्त (c) आणि (b)", "D": "(a), (c) आणि (d)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'भूगोलात हे स्थिर — Maharashtra north–south ~720 km (latitudinal) versus east–west ~800 km — (a) बरोबर. Tropic of Cancer Gujarat, Rajasthan, MP, Chhattisgarh, Jharkhand, West Bengal, Tripura मधून — Maharashtra नाही — (b) चुकी. Official area 3,07,713 sq km, ~800 km width — (c)(d) बरोबर; फक्त (a), (c), (d) — पर्याय D।', '{"Geography","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Maharashtra Physical Geography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22796, 'Maharashtra Districts & Administration', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'जोड्या जुळवा: स्तंभ अ — स्तंभ ब (a) भंडारा — (i) यशवंत तलाव (b) नंदुरबार — (ii) तलावांचे शहर (c) उदयपूर — (iii) दरवाज्यांचे शहर (d) छ. संभाजी नगर — (iv) तलावांचा जिल्हा', '{"A": "(a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(iv)", "B": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(iv), (c)-(ii), (d)-(i)", "C": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(i), (c)-(ii), (d)-(iii)", "D": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(ii), (c)-(i), (d)-(iii)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'जोड्या लावताना — Bhandara → ''District of Lakes''; Nandurbar → Yashwant Lake; Udaypur → ''City of Lakes''; Chhatrapati Sambhajinagar → ''City of Gates''. a-iv, b-i, c-ii, d-iii. Aurangabad–Bhandara swap common सापळा — पर्याय C।', '{"Geography","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Maharashtra Districts & Administration"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22797, 'World Geography & Locations', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'भारताची खालीलपैकी कोणत्या एका देशाशी सर्वात जास्त लांब सीमा आहे?', '{"A": "नेपाळ", "B": "बांग्लादेश", "C": "पाकिस्तान", "D": "भूतान"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'भूगोलात हे स्थिर — India''s longest international land border Bangladesh (~4,096 km) — China, Pakistan, Nepal, Myanmar पेक्षा लांब. Pakistan third; ''longest border'' prelims Bangladesh expect करतात — पर्याय B।', '{"Geography","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","World Geography & Locations"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22798, 'Agriculture & Soils', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'खालील विधाने पहा. (a) फॅमीन कमिशनच्या शिफारशीनुसार कृषी खात्याची स्थापना जून 1881 मध्ये केली गेली. (b) महाराष्ट्र कृषी आयुक्त कार्यालय मुकुंदनगर, पुणे येथे आहे. (c) कृषीभूषण पुरस्कार माजी मुख्यमंत्र्यांच्या नावाने दिला जातो.', '{"A": "फक्त विधान (a) बरोबर आहे.", "B": "फक्त विधान (c) बरोबर आहे.", "C": "विधान (a) आणि (c) बरोबर आहेत.", "D": "विधान (b) आणि (c) बरोबर आहेत."}'::jsonb, 'B', 'प्रश्नातील विधाने — Krushi Bhushan Vasantrao Naik नावे Maharashtra state award progressive farmers; विधान (c) alone बरोबर. (a) 1881 Agricultural Department broadly historical; (b) Commissionerate Pune, Mukundnagar नाही. (a)–(c) merge unless paper both accepts — पर्याय B।', '{"Geography","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Agriculture & Soils"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22799, 'Maharashtra Rivers & Dams', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'जोड्या जुळवा: जिल्हे — जलविद्युत प्रकल्प (a) सोलापूर — (i) कान्हेर (b) सातारा — (ii) भीरा (c) रायगड — (iii) वारण (d) सांगली — (iv) उजनी', '{"A": "(a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(iv)", "B": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(i)", "C": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(i), (c)-(iii), (d)-(ii)", "D": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(i), (c)-(ii), (d)-(iii)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'जोड्या लावताना — Solapur → Ujjani (Bhima); Satara → Kanher; Raigad → Bhira (Tata Hydro); Sangli → Warna. a-iv, b-i, c-iii, d-ii. Ujjani–Satara किंवा Bhira–Sangli cross-wire river basins — पर्याय D।', '{"Geography","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Maharashtra Rivers & Dams"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (22800, 'Maharashtra Physical Geography', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'जोड्या लावा: मासेमारी बंदर — जिल्हा (a) डहाणू — (i) मुंबई (b) माहिम — (ii) पालघर (c) दाभोळ — (iii) सिंधुदुर्ग (d) विजयदुर्ग — (iv) रत्नागिरी', '{"A": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(i), (c)-(iv), (d)-(iii)", "B": "(a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(iv)", "C": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(iv), (c)-(i), (d)-(iii)", "D": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(ii), (c)-(i), (d)-(iv)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'जोड्या लावताना — Dahanu → Palghar; Mahim → Mumbai; Dabhol → Ratnagiri; Vijaydurg → Sindhudurg. a-ii, b-i, c-iv, d-iii. Vijaydurg fort/port Sindhudurg — one sure link — पर्याय A।', '{"Geography","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Maharashtra Physical Geography"}'::text[], 'Medium')
