  (23011, 'Judiciary', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, '''केशवानंद भारती'' प्रकरणाबाबत खालील विधाने विचारात घ्या: (A) हे प्रकरण भारताचे मुख्य न्यायाधीश A.N. Ray यांच्या अध्यक्षतेखालील 13 न्यायमूर्तींच्या घटनापीठासमोर ऐकले गेले. (B) 7 विरुद्ध 6 अशा बहुमताने घटनापीठाने मूलभूत रचना सिद्धांत मांडला. (C) या प्रकरणाने ''गोलकनाथ'' प्रकरणातील निर्णय बदलला. (D) हे प्रकरण न्यायिक सक्रियतेचे उदाहरण मानले जाते. वरीलपैकी कोणती विधाने बरोबर आहेत?', '{"A": "(A), (B) आणि (C)", "B": "(B), (C) आणि (D)", "C": "फक्त (B)", "D": "(A), (B), (C) आणि (D)"}'::jsonb, 'B', '(A) bench headship err — trio B–C–D accepted पर्याय A ((A), (B) and (C)) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही; पर्याय C ((B) फक्त) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय D ((A), (B), (C) and (D)) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही. पर्याय A ((A), (B) and (C)) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C ((B) फक्त) फक्त) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय D ((A), (B), (C) and (D)) , (B), (C) and (D)) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही. पर्याय A ((A), (B) and (C)) , (B) and (C)) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C ((B) फक्त) फक्त) फक्त) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय D ((A), (B), (C) and (D)) , (B), (C) and (D)) , (B), (C) and (D)) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही।', '{"Polity","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Judiciary"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23012, 'Constitutional & Statutory Bodies', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'केंद्रीय माहिती आयोगामध्ये एक मुख्य माहिती आयुक्त आणि जास्तीत जास्त किती माहिती आयुक्तांचा समावेश असतो?', '{"A": "पाच माहिती आयुक्त", "B": "दहा माहिती आयुक्त", "C": "सहा माहिती आयुक्त", "D": "आठ माहिती आयुक्त"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'योग्य उत्तर पर्याय B आहे। Five, six, eight सापळा पर्याय — ''1 + maximum 10'' परीक्षेत जवळचे पर्याय सापडतात, म्हणून प्रश्नाचा मजकूर आणि मुख्य तथ्य पुन्हा वाचा. उत्तर निश्चित करताना प्रश्नातील मुख्य संकल्पना आणि वर्ष लक्षात ठेवा.।', '{"Polity","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Constitutional & Statutory Bodies"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23013, 'Constitutional Framework & Preamble', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'भारताच्या नागरिकत्वाविषयी खालीलपैकी योग्य विधान/विधाने कोणते? (A) भारतामध्ये एकल नागरिकत्व पद्धती आहे. (B) नागरिकत्व कायदा 1955 साली संमत करण्यात आला. (C) भारतीय राज्यघटनेच्या भाग 4 मध्ये नागरिकत्वाची तरतूद आहे.', '{"A": "फक्त (A) आणि (C) बरोबर", "B": "फक्त (A) बरोबर", "C": "फक्त (A) आणि (B) बरोबर", "D": "वरील सर्व बरोबर आहेत"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'भारतीय नागरिकत्व भाग II (कलम ५–११) मध्ये; भाग IV मार्गदर्शक तत्त्वे, नागरिकत्व नाही — (C) चुकी. (A) एकल नागरिकत्व व (B) १९५५ चा कायदा — दोन्ही बरोबर. म्हणून (A) व (B) = पर्याय C. A, B, D चुकीचे।', '{"Polity","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Constitutional Framework & Preamble"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23014, 'Constitutional Amendments', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'कोणत्या घटनादुरुस्ती कायद्याद्वारे दिल्लीला राष्ट्रीय राजधानी क्षेत्र म्हटले गेले?', '{"A": "63 वी घटनादुरुस्ती कायदा", "B": "69 वी घटनादुरुस्ती कायदा", "C": "91 वी घटनादुरुस्ती कायदा", "D": "93 वी घटनादुरुस्ती कायदा"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'संविधानात हे लक्षात ठेवा — पर्याय B बरोबर आहे। 63rd, 91st, 93rd इतर subjects (Panchayat विस्तार, विरोधी defection, OBC ) — Delhi NCT status नाहीत परीक्षेत जवळचे पर्याय सापडतात, म्हणून प्रश्नाचा मजकूर आणि मुख्य तथ्य पुन्हा वाचा.।', '{"Polity","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Constitutional Amendments"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23015, 'Constitutional & Statutory Bodies', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'भारतातील विविध राष्ट्रीय आयोगांच्या संदर्भात खालील तरतुदी विचारात घ्या. (A) भारतीय राज्यघटनेच्या कलम 339 नुसार अनुसूचित जाती आणि जमातीसाठी राष्ट्रीय आयोगाची स्थापना करण्यात आली. (B) राष्ट्रीय महिला आयोग अधिनियम 1990 नुसार राष्ट्रीय महिला आयोगाची स्थापना करण्यात आली. (C) राष्ट्रीय अल्पसंख्यांक आयोग अधिनियम 1992 नुसार राष्ट्रीय अल्पसंख्यांक आयोगाची स्थापना करण्यात आली. (D) 27 डिसेंबर 1993 रोजी राष्ट्रीय मानवाधिकार आयोग स्थापन करण्यासंदर्भातील अध्यादेश काढण्यात आला. वरीलपैकी बरोबर तरतूद/तरतुदी कोणती/कोणत्या आहे/आहेत?', '{"A": "(A) आणि (C)", "B": "(B) आणि (D)", "C": "(A) आणि (D)", "D": "(B) आणि (C)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'SC/ST national आयोग kalam 338/338A — कलम 339 नाही; NHRC Protection of Human adhikar Act, 1993 — December 1993 ordinance katha jodle statutory tathya thevle नाही पर्याय A ((A) and (C)) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही; पर्याय B ((B) and (D)) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही; पर्याय C ((A) and (D)) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही. पर्याय A ((A) and (C)) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B ((B) and (D)) and (D)) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही; पर्याय C ((A) and (D)) and (D)) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही. पर्याय A ((A) and (C)) and (C)) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B ((B) and (D)) and (D)) and (D)) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही; पर्याय C ((A) and (D)) and (D)) and (D)) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही।', '{"Polity","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Constitutional & Statutory Bodies"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23016, 'Parliament', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'पहिल्या लोकसभेच्या संदर्भात खालील विधाने विचारात घ्या. (A) 25 ऑक्टोबर 1951 ते 21 फेब्रुवारी 1952 या कालावधीत झालेल्या भारताच्या पहिल्या सार्वत्रिक निवडणुकीनंतर 17 एप्रिल 1952 रोजी पहिल्या लोकसभेची स्थापना करण्यात आली. (B) पहिल्या लोकसभेचे पहिले अधिवेशन 13 मे 1952 रोजी सुरू झाले. (C) पहिल्या लोकसभेने आपला कालावधी पूर्ण केला आणि ती 1 एप्रिल 1957 रोजी विसर्जित झाली. (D) श्री. जी.व्ह. मावळणकर हे पहिल्या लोकसभेचे उपसभापती होते. वरीलपैकी कोणते विधान/विधाने बरोबर आहे/आहेत?', '{"A": "केवळ (A)", "B": "(A) आणि (B)", "C": "(B), (C) आणि (D)", "D": "केवळ (D)"}'::jsonb, 'B', '(A) १७ एप्रिल १९५२ निर्वाचन व (B) १३ मे १९५२ पहिले अधिवेशन — बरोबर. (C) पूर्ण कार्यकाळ १ एप्रिल १९५७ — चुकी; (D) मावळणकर उपाध्यक्ष नव्हे, अध्यक्ष. म्हणून (A) व (B) = पर्याय B. A, C, D चुकीचे।', '{"Polity","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Parliament"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23017, 'Constitutional Framework & Preamble', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'भारतीय राज्यघटना धर्मनिरपेक्ष राज्य स्थापित करते म्हणजेच (A) राज्य रोजगाराच्या बाबतीत धर्माच्या आधारावर भेदभाव करते. (B) राज्याने कोणत्याही विशिष्ट धर्माला अग्रक्रमाने वागणूक देण्याचे टाळले आहे. (C) राज्य सर्व धर्मांना समान समजते. (D) सर्व जनतेला श्रद्धा आणि पूजा करण्याचे स्वातंत्र्य आहे. (E) कोणत्याही अपवादाशिवाय, शैक्षणिक संस्था धार्मिक शिक्षण (शिकवण) देण्यास स्वतंत्र आहेत.', '{"A": "(A), (B) आणि (C)", "B": "(B), (C) आणि (D)", "C": "(A), (C), (D) आणि (E)", "D": "(B) आणि (D)"}'::jsonb, 'B', '(A) religious discrimination rojgar endorse secularism ulta; (E) sarva schools religious instruction universalise — minority, कलम 28 limits पर्याय A ((A), (B) and (C)) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही; पर्याय C ((A), (C), (D) and (E)) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही; पर्याय D ((B) and (D)) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही. पर्याय A ((A), (B) and (C)) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C ((A), (C), (D) and (E)) , (C), (D) and (E)) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही; पर्याय D ((B) and (D)) and (D)) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही. पर्याय A ((A), (B) and (C)) , (B) and (C)) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C ((A), (C), (D) and (E)) , (C), (D) and (E)) , (C), (D) and (E)) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही; पर्याय D ((B) and (D)) and (D)) and (D)) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही।', '{"Polity","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Constitutional Framework & Preamble"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23018, 'Persons in News & Books', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'कर्पुरी ठाकूर अलीकडे बातम्यांमध्ये होते. त्यांच्याबाबत खालीलपैकी काय खरे नाही?', '{"A": "त्यांना ''जननायक'' म्हणून ओळखले जाते.", "B": "ते बिहारचे पहिले गैर-कांग्रेसी मुख्यमंत्री होते.", "C": "त्यांचा जन्म 1924 मध्ये, समस्तीपुर जिल्ह्यातील एका गावात झाला.", "D": "त्यांनी 1952 ची राज्य विधानसभा निवडणूक समस्तीपुर मतदारसंघातून जिंकली होती."}'::jsonb, 'D', 'परीक्षेनुसार पर्याय D बरोबर आहे। Karpoori Thakur (''Jan Nayak'') Bihar पहिला non-काँग्रेस CM, 1924 Samastipur जिल्हा born — पण 1952 , Samastipur constituency नाही। A–C biographical staples; (D) 1952 seat detail चुकी।', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Persons in News & Books"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23019, 'Elections & Representation', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'राज्यघटनेतील कोणती कलमे आपल्या देशातील निवडणूक व्यवस्थेसाठी तरतूद करतात?', '{"A": "कलम 124 ते 128", "B": "कलम 324 ते 329", "C": "कलम 256 ते 259", "D": "कलम 274 ते 279"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'संविधानात हे लक्षात ठेवा — पर्याय B बरोबर आहे। Articles 324–329 : निवडणूक आयोग (324), conduct (325–327), disqualifications (329)। 124–128 Supreme Court; 256–259, 274–279 centre–state finance — electoral framework नाहीत।', '{"Polity","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Elections & Representation"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23020, 'National Appointments & Reports', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'जागतिक क्षुधा निर्देशांक 2023 मध्ये भारताचा कितवा क्रमांक लागतो?', '{"A": "100", "B": "111", "C": "101", "D": "123"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'करंट अफेयर्स — पर्याय B बरोबर आहे। Rank 100, 101, 123 adjacent years/misremembered near-चुक सापळे पर्याय उत्तर निश्चित करताना प्रश्नातील मुख्य संकल्पना आणि वर्ष लक्षात ठेवा.।', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","National Appointments & Reports"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23021, 'National Appointments & Reports', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'नव्या संसद भवनाबाबत पुढीलपैकी योग्य विधाने विचारात घ्या. (a) नव्या संसदेतील लोकसभेच्या आंतरिक भागाची रचना राष्ट्रीय प्राणी सिंहाच्या संकल्पनेवर आधारित आहे. (b) राज्यसभेची रचना भारताच्या राष्ट्रीय फुल कमळाच्या संकल्पनेवर आधारित आहे. (c) नव्या संसद भवनाचे उद्घाटन 28 मे 2023 रोजी करण्यात आले. (d) लोकसभा अध्यक्षांच्या बाजूला ऐतिहासिक अशोक चक्राची स्थापना केली आहे.', '{"A": "विधाने (b), (c) योग्य आहेत.", "B": "विधाने (a), (b), (c) योग्य आहेत.", "C": "विधाने (b), (c), (d) योग्य आहेत.", "D": "(a), (b), (c), (d) योग्य आहेत."}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Lok Sabha peacock/national bird motif — lion/national prani नाही; Ashok Chakra Speaker beside verified design claim नाही — (b), (c) fakt hold पर्याय B (विधाने (a), (b), (c) are बरोबर.) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (विधाने (b), (c), (d) are बरोबर.) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D ((a), (b), (c), (d) are बरोबर.) प्रश्नातील तथ्ये/गणना/व्याख्येशी विरोधाभासी आहे. पर्याय B (विधाने (a), (b), (c) are बरोबर.) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (विधाने (b), (c), (d) are बरोबर.) , (c), (d) are बरोबर; पर्याय D ((a), (b), (c), (d) are बरोबर.) , (b), (c), (d) are बरोबर. पर्याय B (विधाने (a), (b), (c) are बरोबर.) , (b), (c) are बरोबर; पर्याय C (विधाने (b), (c), (d) are बरोबर.) , (c), (d) are बरोबर; पर्याय D ((a), (b), (c), (d) are बरोबर.) , (b), (c), (d) are बरोबर।', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","National Appointments & Reports"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23022, 'Sports', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'आशियाई क्रीडा स्पर्धा 2023 विषयी योग्य विधाने ओळखा. (a) या स्पर्धा चीनमधील हांगझोऊ या ठिकाणी भरवण्यात आल्या. (b) उद्घाटन प्रसंगी लवलीना बोर्गोहेन या नेमबाजाने भारताकडून ध्वजधारकाची भूमिका बजावली. (c) या स्पर्धेत 28 सुवर्णपदकांसह भारताने चौथे स्थान पटकावले. (d) या स्पर्धेत एकूण 107 पदके भारताला मिळाली.', '{"A": "(a), (b), (c)", "B": "(a), (b), (d)", "C": "(b), (c), (d)", "D": "(a), (c), (d)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'पर्याय D ((a), (c), (d)) — पर्याय A ((a), (b), (c)) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही; पर्याय B ((a), (b), (d)) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही; पर्याय C ((b), (c), (d)) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही. पर्याय A ((a), (b), (c)) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B ((a), (b), (d)) , (b), (d)) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही; पर्याय C ((b), (c), (d)) , (c), (d)) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही. पर्याय A ((a), (b), (c)) , (b), (c)) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B ((a), (b), (d)) , (b), (d)) , (b), (d)) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही; पर्याय C ((b), (c), (d)) , (c), (d)) , (c), (d)) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही।', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Sports"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23023, 'Science & Technology (IT/Space)', 'Science', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'कोणती अंतराळ संस्था भारताला सौर मिशन आदित्य-एल1 वर लक्ष ठेवण्यास मदत करते?', '{"A": "NASA", "B": "ESA", "C": "JAXA", "D": "रॉसकॉसमॉस"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'गणितात हे सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय B येतो। NASA, JAXA, Roscosmos अधिकृत मोहीम नाहीत उत्तर निश्चित करताना प्रश्नातील मुख्य संकल्पना आणि वर्ष लक्षात ठेवा. विषय-पॅकमध्ये हा बिंदू पुन्हा विचारला जाऊ शकतो, म्हणून मुख्य तथ्य एकत्र लक्षात ठेवा.।', '{"Science","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Science & Technology (IT/Space)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23024, 'Awards & Honours', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'योग्य कथने ओळखा. (a) नर्गिस मोहम्मदी यांना नोबेल शांतता पुरस्कार, 2023 प्रदान करण्यात आला. (b) नर्गिस मोहम्मदी ह्या समता व महिलांच्या हक्कांच्या पुरस्कर्त्या आहेत. (c) नर्गिस मोहम्मदी या शिरिन ईबादी यांनी स्थापन केलेल्या डिफेन्डर्स ऑफ ह्युमन राईट्स सेंटरला 2004 मध्ये सहभागी झाल्या.', '{"A": "फक्त (a), (b)", "B": "फक्त (b), (c)", "C": "फक्त (a), (c)", "D": "वरीलपैकी सर्व"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'पर्याय A (Only (a), (b)) — पर्याय B (फक्त (b), (c)) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय C (फक्त (a), (c)) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (वरील सर्व) प्रत्येक विधान बरोबर म्हणतो, पण यापैकी किमान एक विधान चुकीचे आहे. पर्याय B (फक्त (b), (c)) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय C (फक्त (a), (c)) , (c)) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (वरील सर्व) प्रत्येक विधान बरोबर म्हणतो, पण यापैकी किमान एक विधान चुकीचे आहे. पर्याय B (फक्त (b), (c)) , (c)) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय C (फक्त (a), (c)) , (c)) , (c)) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (वरील सर्व) प्रत्येक विधान बरोबर म्हणतो, पण यापैकी किमान एक विधान चुकीचे आहे।', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Awards & Honours"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23025, 'National Appointments & Reports', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'बार कौन्सिल ऑफ इंडियाच्या ''आंतरराष्ट्रीय वकील परिषद 2023'' चे उद्घाटन कोणत्या शहरात झाले?', '{"A": "नवी दिल्ली", "B": "मुंबई", "C": "कोलकाता", "D": "बेंगळुरु"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'करंट अफेयर्स — पर्याय A बरोबर आहे। Bar Council of India आंतरराष्ट्रीय Lawyers परिषद 2023 New Delhi inaugurate — central legal-संस्था कार्यक्रम। Mumbai, Kolkata, Bengaluru BCI परिषद नाहीत।', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","National Appointments & Reports"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23026, 'Defence & Security', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'परदेशातील भारतीय नागरिकांच्या संरक्षणासाठी राबवलेल्या मोहिमा आणि देश यांच्या योग्य जोड्या लावा. मोहिमा - देश (a) ऑपरेशन अजय - (i) युक्रेन (b) ऑपरेशन गंगा - (ii) इस्राईल (c) ऑपरेशन देवशक्ती - (iii) सुदान (d) ऑपरेशन कावेरी - (iv) अफगाणिस्तान', '{"A": "a-(i), b-(ii), c-(iii), d-(iv)", "B": "a-(ii), b-(iii), c-(iv), d-(i)", "C": "a-(ii), b-(i), c-(iv), d-(iii)", "D": "a-(iv), b-(ii), c-(iii), d-(i)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पर्याय C (a-(ii), b-(i), c-(iv), d-(iii)) — पर्याय A (a-(i), b-(ii), c-(iii), d-(iv)) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी; पर्याय B (a-(ii), b-(iii), c-(iv), d-(i)) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी; पर्याय D (a-(iv), b-(ii), c-(iii), d-(i)) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी. पर्याय A (a-(i), b-(ii), c-(iii), d-(iv)) , b-(ii), c-(iii), d-(iv)) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी; पर्याय B (a-(ii), b-(iii), c-(iv), d-(i)) , b-(iii), c-(iv), d-(i)) , b-(iii), c-(iv), d-(i)) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी; पर्याय D (a-(iv), b-(ii), c-(iii), d-(i)) , b-(ii), c-(iii), d-(i)) , b-(ii), c-(iii), d-(i)) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी।', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Defence & Security"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23027, 'Government Schemes & Yojanas', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'मुख्यमंत्री सौर कृषी वाहिनी योजनेबाबत पुढीलपैकी योग्य विधाने ओळखा. (a) ही योजना जून 2017 मध्ये देवेंद्र फडणवीस मुख्यमंत्री असताना सुरू केली होती. (b) या योजनेचा मुख्य हेतू शेतकऱ्यांना कृषी फीडरच्या माध्यमातून वीज पुरवठा उपलब्ध करून देणे हा आहे. (c) या योजनेअंतर्गत शेतकऱ्यांना प्रति एकर ₹ 50,000 भाडे देण्याचा निर्णय सरकारने घेतला. (d) 33 kV उपकेंद्रापासून 10 कि.मी. पर्यंतच्या सरकारी जमिनीवर सोलार पॅनल उभारले जातात.', '{"A": "(a), (d) योग्य आहेत.", "B": "(a), (b), (c) योग्य आहेत.", "C": "(a), (b) योग्य आहेत.", "D": "(a), (c), (d) योग्य आहेत."}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पर्याय C ((a), (b) are correct) — पर्याय A ((a), (d) are बरोबर) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही; पर्याय B ((a), (b), (c) are बरोबर) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही; पर्याय D ((a), (c), (d) are बरोबर) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही. पर्याय A ((a), (d) are बरोबर) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B ((a), (b), (c) are बरोबर) , (b), (c) are बरोबर) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही; पर्याय D ((a), (c), (d) are बरोबर) , (c), (d) are बरोबर) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही. पर्याय A ((a), (d) are बरोबर) , (d) are बरोबर) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B ((a), (b), (c) are बरोबर) , (b), (c) are बरोबर) , (b), (c) are बरोबर) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही; पर्याय D ((a), (c), (d) are बरोबर) , (c), (d) are बरोबर) , (c), (d) are बरोबर) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही।', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Government Schemes & Yojanas"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23028, 'National Appointments & Reports', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'खालीलपैकी योग्य जोड्या जुळवा. (A) - (B) (a) डॉ. नितीन करमाळकर समिती - (i) महाराष्ट्रात राष्ट्रीय शैक्षणिक धोरण 2020 च्या अंमलबजावणीसाठी (b) नितीन करीर समिती - (ii) महाराष्ट्र भूषण पुरस्कार वितरणावेळी झालेल्या दुर्घटनेच्या चौकशीसाठी (c) सुनिल पवार समिती - (iii) कांद्याचे दर का कोसळतात, याचा अभ्यास करण्यासाठी (d) डॉ. के. कस्तुरीरंगन समिती - (iv) राष्ट्रीय शैक्षणिक धोरण 2020 नुसार पूर्वप्राथमिक ते पदवोपर्यंतचा अभ्यासक्रम तयार करण्यासाठी', '{"A": "a-(i), b-(ii), c-(iii), d-(iv)", "B": "a-(ii), b-(iii), c-(iv), d-(i)", "C": "a-(iii), b-(iv), c-(ii), d-(i)", "D": "a-(iv), b-(ii), c-(i), d-(iii)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'पर्याय A (a-(i), b-(ii), c-(iii), d-(iv)) — Kasturirangan ↔ national NEP syllabus choukhat — a-(i) madhun d-(iv)। Transposed samiti mandates samanya MPSC पर्याय B (a-(ii), b-(iii), c-(iv), d-(i)) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी; पर्याय C (a-(iii), b-(iv), c-(ii), d-(i)) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी; पर्याय D (a-(iv), b-(ii), c-(i), d-(iii)) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी. पर्याय B (a-(ii), b-(iii), c-(iv), d-(i)) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी; पर्याय C (a-(iii), b-(iv), c-(ii), d-(i)) , b-(iv), c-(ii), d-(i)) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी; पर्याय D (a-(iv), b-(ii), c-(i), d-(iii)) , b-(ii), c-(i), d-(iii)) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी. पर्याय B (a-(ii), b-(iii), c-(iv), d-(i)) , b-(iii), c-(iv), d-(i)) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी; पर्याय C (a-(iii), b-(iv), c-(ii), d-(i)) , b-(iv), c-(ii), d-(i)) , b-(iv), c-(ii), d-(i)) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी; पर्याय D (a-(iv), b-(ii), c-(i), d-(iii)) , b-(ii), c-(i), d-(iii)) , b-(ii), c-(i), d-(iii)) मध्ये किमान एक जोडी चुकीच्या क्रमाने मांडली आहे, म्हणून ती वर्गातून वगळावी।', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","National Appointments & Reports"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23029, 'Government Schemes & Yojanas', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'अलीकडेच ओडिशाच्या मुख्यमंत्र्यांनी मुख्यमंत्री संपूर्ण पुष्टी योजना सुरू केली आहे. या योजनेचे/ची प्राथमिक उद्दिष्ट/े कोणते? (a) मुलींच्या उच्च शिक्षणाला चालना देणे. (b) राज्यातील माता आणि बालकांच्या पोषणामध्ये सुधारणा करणे. (c) किशोरवयीन मुलांना रोजगाराच्या संधी उपलब्ध करून देणे. (d) ग्रामीण भागात कृषी उत्पादन वाढवणे.', '{"A": "फक्त (a) बरोबर आहे.", "B": "फक्त (b) बरोबर आहे.", "C": "(a) आणि (d) बरोबर आहेत.", "D": "(c) आणि (d) बरोबर आहेत."}'::jsonb, 'B', 'करंट अफेयर्स — पर्याय B बरोबर आहे। (Odisha) — maternal/। , adolescent employment, योजना objectives उत्तर निश्चित करताना प्रश्नातील मुख्य संकल्पना आणि वर्ष लक्षात ठेवा.।', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Government Schemes & Yojanas"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23030, 'Judiciary', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'कोणते कलम उच्च न्यायालयांना मूलभूत अधिकारांच्या अंमलबजावणीसाठी निर्देश जारी करण्याचा अधिकार देते?', '{"A": "कलम 226", "B": "कलम 135", "C": "कलम 143", "D": "कलम 133"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'कलम 226 empowers High Courts to issue writs for enforcement of Fundamental Rights and for ''any other purpose'' within their territorial jurisdiction—the primary HC writ remedy. Articles 133, 135 and 143 concern appeals, jurisdiction transfer and advisory opinions, not this enforcement power पर्याय B (Article 135) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (Article 143) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (Article 133) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Polity","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Judiciary"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23031, 'Persons in News & Books', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'एम.एस. स्वामीनाथन यांच्याविषयी योग्य विधाने ओळखा. (a) ते तमिळनाडु येथील रहिवासी होते. (b) त्यांचे उच्च शिक्षण ऑक्सफर्ड विद्यापीठात झाले होते. (c) ते कृषी विभागाचे शास्त्रज्ञ होते. (d) ते काही काळ राज्यसभेचे सदस्य होते. (e) त्यांना रॅमन मॅगसेसे पुरस्कार मिळाला होता.', '{"A": "(a), (b), (c), (e)", "B": "(a), (c), (d), (e)", "C": "(b), (c), (d), (e)", "D": "(a), (b), (c), (d)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'पर्याय B ((a), (c), (d), (e)) — S. Swaminathan Tamil Nadu, krushi scientist, Rajya Sabha sadasya, Ramon Magsaysay purak — (a), (c), (d), (e)। Oxford shikshan (b) vegl — IARI/Cambridge advanced prashikshan, Oxford jod key nakar पर्याय A ((a), (b), (c), (e)) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही; पर्याय C ((b), (c), (d), (e)) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही; पर्याय D ((a), (b), (c), (d)) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही. पर्याय A ((a), (b), (c), (e)) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C ((b), (c), (d), (e)) , (c), (d), (e)) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही; पर्याय D ((a), (b), (c), (d)) , (b), (c), (d)) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही. पर्याय A ((a), (b), (c), (e)) , (b), (c), (e)) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C ((b), (c), (d), (e)) , (c), (d), (e)) , (c), (d), (e)) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही; पर्याय D ((a), (b), (c), (d)) , (b), (c), (d)) , (b), (c), (d)) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही।', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Persons in News & Books"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23032, 'National Appointments & Reports', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'महिला आरक्षण विधेयक 2023 संदर्भात खालील विधाने विचारात घ्या. (a) नारीशक्ती वंदन अधिनियम हे अधिकृतपणे घटनात्मक (128 वे घटनादुरुस्ती) विधेयक 2023 म्हणून भारताच्या संसदेत सादर करण्यात आले. (b) महिला आरक्षण विधेयक पंतप्रधान नरेंद्र मोदी यांनी 10 सप्टेंबर 2023 रोजी लोकसभेत सादर केले. (c) या कायद्याद्वारे लोकसभा आणि राज्य विधानसभेच्या 30% जागा महिलांना देण्यात येणार आहेत. (d) नव्या संसद भवनातील हे पहिले विधेयक आहे. वरीलपैकी योग्य विधाने ओळखा.', '{"A": "(a) आणि (d) बरोबर आहेत.", "B": "(a) आणि (b) बरोबर आहेत.", "C": "(a), (b), (c) बरोबर आहेत.", "D": "(a), (b), (c) आणि (d) बरोबर आहेत."}'::jsonb, 'A', 'पर्याय A ((a) and (d) are correct.) — पर्याय B ((a) and (b) are बरोबर.) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही; पर्याय C ((a), (b), (c) are बरोबर.) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही; पर्याय D ((a), (b), (c) and (d) are बरोबर.) प्रश्नातील तथ्ये/गणना/व्याख्येशी विरोधाभासी आहे. पर्याय B ((a) and (b) are बरोबर.) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C ((a), (b), (c) are बरोबर.) , (b), (c) are बरोबर; पर्याय D ((a), (b), (c) and (d) are बरोबर.) , (b), (c) and (d) are बरोबर. पर्याय B ((a) and (b) are बरोबर.) and (b) are बरोबर; पर्याय C ((a), (b), (c) are बरोबर.) , (b), (c) are बरोबर; पर्याय D ((a), (b), (c) and (d) are बरोबर.) , (b), (c) and (d) are बरोबर।', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","National Appointments & Reports"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23033, 'Awards & Honours', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'योग्य कथने ओळखा (पद्म पुरस्कार 2024). (a) त्यामध्ये 30 पुरस्कार प्राप्तकर्त्या महिला आहेत. (b) त्यामध्ये 6 पद्म विभूषण पुरस्कार जाहीर केले गेले. (c) 17 पद्म भूषण आणि 110 पद्मश्री पुरस्कार जाहीर करण्यात आले.', '{"A": "फक्त (a), (b)", "B": "फक्त (b), (c)", "C": "फक्त (a), (c)", "D": "वरीलपैकी सर्व"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पर्याय C (Only (a), (c)) — पर्याय A (फक्त (a), (b)) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B (फक्त (b), (c)) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय D (All of these) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही. पर्याय A (फक्त (a), (b)) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B (फक्त (b), (c)) , (c)) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय D (All of these) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही. पर्याय A (फक्त (a), (b)) , (b)) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B (फक्त (b), (c)) , (c)) , (c)) मध्ये फक्त काही विधाने घेतली आहेत, पण प्रश्नातील सर्व बरोबर विधाने एकत्र येतात; पर्याय D (All of these) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्यक्ती/स्थळ/संस्थेशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","Awards & Honours"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23034, 'International Affairs & Summits', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group C Combined', 2024, 'फाईव्ह आईज्ज युतीमध्ये खालीलपैकी कोणत्या देशांचा समावेश होतो? (a) अमेरिका (b) ब्रिटन (c) न्यूझीलंड (d) ऑस्ट्रेलिया (e) फ्रान्स (f) जर्मनी', '{"A": "(a), (b), (c), (d)", "B": "(a), (b), (c), (e)", "C": "(a), (b), (e), (f)", "D": "(a), (b), (c), (d), (e)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'List America, Britain, New Zealand, Australia sadasya; France, Germany नाही — option (a) char बरोबर navane non-members vina select पर्याय B ((a), (b), (c), (e)) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही; पर्याय C ((a), (b), (e), (f)) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही; पर्याय D ((a), (b), (c), (d), (e)) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही. पर्याय B ((a), (b), (c), (e)) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C ((a), (b), (e), (f)) , (b), (e), (f)) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही; पर्याय D ((a), (b), (c), (d), (e)) , (b), (c), (d), (e)) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही. पर्याय B ((a), (b), (c), (e)) , (b), (c), (e)) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C ((a), (b), (e), (f)) , (b), (e), (f)) , (b), (e), (f)) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही; पर्याय D ((a), (b), (c), (d), (e)) , (b), (c), (d), (e)) , (b), (c), (d), (e)) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही।', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group C Combined","2024","International Affairs & Summits"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23035, 'State Government', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'The term of the member of the Legislative Council is _______ years.', '{"A": "5", "B": "6", "C": "2½", "D": "4½"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Members of the Legislative Council serve six-year terms—with one-third retiring every two years in states that have an upper house. Five, two-and-a-half, and four-and-a-half years confuse Lok Sabha tenure or staggered fractions with the full Council term length. Option A (5) gives a numerical result that does not follow from the formula or data in the stem (correct: B = 6); option C (2½) conflicts with the definition, collocations, or calculation path that supports B (6); and option D (4½) conflicts with the definition, collocations, or calculation path that supports B (6).', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","State Government"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23036, 'Heat & Thermodynamics', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'At what temperature °C and °F both has same value?', '{"A": "4°C", "B": "−4°C", "C": "−40°C", "D": "+40°C"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Celsius and Fahrenheit scales intersect at −40° (−40°C = −40°F)—the lone point where numerical values coincide. +4°C is 39°F; −4°C and +40°C pairs do not satisfy F = (9/5)C + 32 at equal readings.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Heat & Thermodynamics"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23037, 'Organic Chemistry', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'L.P.G. contains the chemical components _______.', '{"A": "Methane and Butane", "B": "Methane and Ethane", "C": "Methane and Ethanol", "D": "Butane and Isobutane"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The correct answer is option D — LPG (liquefied petroleum gas) is mainly a mix of butane and isobutane (propane in winter blends)—stored under pressure as liquid. Methane is pipeline natural gas; ethanol is not a standard LPG component; methane–ethane pairs describe CNG or refinery gas, not domestic LPG cylinders. You can eliminate A (Methane and Butane), B (Methane and Ethane), C (Methane and Ethanol) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option D. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Organic Chemistry"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23038, 'State Government', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'How many members can be nominated by the Governor in Legislative Assembly?', '{"A": "Only one", "B": "One sixth of the total number of members present in the Assembly", "C": "One twelfth of the total number of members present in the Assembly", "D": "Only twelve"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Choose option A: article 171(3) allows the Governor to nominate one member to the Legislative Assembly from the Anglo-Indian community when that community is not adequately represented—''only one'' in the correct formulation. Fractional formulae (one-sixth/twelfth) belong to Legislative Council nominations, not this Assembly provision. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","State Government"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23039, 'Pollution', 'General Studies', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Leakage of poisonous gas Methyl Isocyanide from a factory took lives of thousands at _______.', '{"A": "Bhuj", "B": "Bhopal", "C": "Mumbai", "D": "Bhuvaneshwar"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B works here because the Bhopal gas tragedy (1984) followed methyl isocyanate (MIC) leak from the Union Carbide plant—killing thousands overnight. Bhuj (2001 earthquake), Mumbai, and Bhubaneswar are geographic distractors without this industrial-disaster linkage. Distractors A (Bhuj), C (Mumbai), D (Bhuvaneshwar) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"General Studies","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Pollution"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23040, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Who founded the ''Balhatya Pratibandhak Gruha'' at Pune?', '{"A": "Maharshi Dhondo Keshav Karve", "B": "Ramabai Ranade", "C": "Mahatma Jyotirao Phule", "D": "Ishwarchandra Vidyasagar"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Mahatma Phule founded the Balhatya Pratibandhak Gruha (infanticide prevention home) at Pune to protect widows and unwanted infants—part of his anti-caste social programme. Karve''s Anath Balikashram, Ramabai Ranade''s Seva Sadan, and Vidyasagar''s Calcutta work parallel but distinct institutions.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23041, 'Climatology', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Coastal region of _______ State receives rainfall due to North-East Monsoon winds.', '{"A": "Goa", "B": "Punjab", "C": "Maharashtra", "D": "Tamilnadu"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The answer is option D: Tamil Nadu''s Coromandel coast receives winter rainfall from the retreating north-east monsoon (October–December)—unlike most of peninsular India''s summer south-west monsoon. Goa, Punjab, and Maharashtra''s Konkan get their main rain from south-west monsoon, not NE winter currents. You can eliminate A (Goa), B (Punjab), C (Maharashtra) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option D. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Climatology"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23042, 'Human Physiology', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'The weight of human brain is approximately _______ grams.', '{"A": "800 to 1000", "B": "1300 to 1400", "C": "1500 to 1600", "D": "500 to 600"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B matches the question because an adult human brain weighs roughly 1300–1400 grams—about 2% of body weight but consuming disproportionate energy. 800–1000 g undercounts; 1500–1600 g overstates; 500–600 g is child/brain-atrophy range. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Human Physiology"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23043, 'Gandhian Mass Movements', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Who gave the slogan ''Do or Die''?', '{"A": "Rashbihari Bose", "B": "Motilal Nehru", "C": "Mahatma Gandhi", "D": "Bankimchandra Chatterjee"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C works here because Mahatma Gandhi gave the ''Do or Die'' call during the Quit India Movement (August 1942)—launching mass satyagraha against British rule. Rashbihari Bose, Motilal Nehru, and Bankim Chandra belong to other eras; Gandhi + 1942 is the slogan pairing. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Gandhian Mass Movements"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23044, 'Simple & Compound Interest', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Nilima invested Rs. 60,000 in a nationalised bank for 2 years at the rate of 8.5 p.c. p.a. at compound interest. What amount will Nilima receive from the bank at the end of 2 years?', '{"A": "Rs. 70,433.5", "B": "Rs. 70,200", "C": "Rs. 70,933.5", "D": "Rs. 70,633.5"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Compound interest: 60,000 × (1.085)² = 60,000 × 1.177225 = Rs 70,633.50—option D. Simple-interest or one-year-only calculation gives Rs 70,200 band; wrong power or rate lands on 70,433/70,933 traps.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Simple & Compound Interest"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23045, 'Defence & Security', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'What is the name of fighter aircraft that President Pratibha Patil has flown?', '{"A": "Mig 29", "B": "Sukhoi 30 MKI", "C": "Jaguar", "D": "C-Harrier"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B is the right choice since President Pratibha Patil flew a sortie in the Sukhoi Su-30 MKI during her presidency—IAF two-seat trainer/combat variant. MiG-29, Jaguar, and Sea Harrier were not the aircraft named in that 2009 ceremonial flight coverage. You can eliminate A (Mig 29), C (Jaguar), D (C-Harrier) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option B. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Defence & Security"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23046, 'Panchayati Raj', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Who convenes the meeting of the Gram Panchayat and the Gram Sabha and presides over them?', '{"A": "Sarpanch", "B": "Deputy Sarpanch", "C": "Gramsevak", "D": "Member"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The Sarpanch calls and presides over both Gram Panchayat meetings and Gram Sabha sessions—dual convening authority at village level in Maharashtra practice. Deputy Sarpanch acts in absence; Gramsevak is secretary, not presiding officer.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Panchayati Raj"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23047, 'Diseases & Health', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Hepatitis B is caused by _______.', '{"A": "HAV", "B": "HIV", "C": "HBV", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The answer is option C: Hepatitis B is caused by Hepatitis B virus (HBV)—blood-borne DNA virus prevented by the birth-dose vaccine. HAV causes Hepatitis A; HIV causes AIDS, not hepatitis B; ''none'' ignores the well-established HBV aetiology. Distractors A (HAV), B (HIV), D (None of the above) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Diseases & Health"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23048, 'Union Executive', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Who is contained in the President''s electoral college?', '{"A": "Both the houses of Parliaments and all Legislatures of the States", "B": "Both the houses of Parliaments and Legislative assemblies", "C": "Only Lok Sabha and Legislative assemblies", "D": "Both the houses of Parliaments and State Councils"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The President is elected by an electoral college comprising elected members of both Houses of Parliament and the Legislative Assemblies of States—not Legislative Councils or state governors. Option B (Parliament + Assemblies) matches Article 54; adding all state legislatures or councils over-counts.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Union Executive"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23049, 'Climatology', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, '_______ receives highest rainfall in India.', '{"A": "Konkan", "B": "Malbar", "C": "Cherapunji", "D": "Gujrat"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Mawsynram/Cherrapunji region in Meghalaya records the highest rainfall in India—over 11,000 mm annually on the Khasi Hills. Konkan and Malabar are wet but second-tier; Gujarat''s semi-arid belt is nowhere near all-India maxima.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Climatology"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23050, 'Parliament', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Who had opposed the woman reservation bill in Parliament?', '{"A": "Bharatiya Janata Party", "B": "Shiv Sena", "C": "Bahujan Samaj Party", "D": "Nationalist Congress Party"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C is correct because the Bahujan Samaj Party (BSP) under Mayawati notably opposed the Women''s Reservation Bill in Parliament—arguing sub-quota concerns for OBC/SC/ST women. BJP, Shiv Sena, and NCP positions varied by period; BSP''s opposition is the correct current-affairs/polity fact for this paper. You can eliminate A (Bharatiya Janata Party), B (Shiv Sena), D (Nationalist Congress Party) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option C. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Parliament"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (23051, 'International Affairs & Summits', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'What is the name of the party of Bangladesh Prime Minister Sheikh Hasina?', '{"A": "Awami Ligue", "B": "Bangladesh Nationalist Party", "C": "Bangladesh People Party", "D": "Jamat-e-Islami"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A is the right choice since Sheikh Hasina leads the Awami League—the dominant party in Bangladesh''s parliamentary system. BNP (Khaleda Zia), Bangladesh People''s Party, and Jamaat-e-Islami are rival or allied formations without Hasina''s leadership. Distractors B (Bangladesh Nationalist Party), C (Bangladesh People Party), D (Jamat-e-Islami) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","International Affairs & Summits"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23052, 'Persons in News & Books', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Who among the following film actors established a new political party in August 2008?', '{"A": "Rajnikant", "B": "Govinda", "C": "Kamal Hassan", "D": "Chiranjeevi"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Telugu film star Chiranjeevi launched the Praja Rajyam Party in August 2008—entering Andhra Pradesh politics before later Congress alignment. Rajnikant, Govinda, and Kamal Haasan flirted with or entered politics through other timelines and parties.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Persons in News & Books"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23053, 'Judiciary', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'What is the reason for increase in judicial activism?', '{"A": "The growth of population and courts", "B": "Public interest litigations", "C": "Globalizations and liberalization", "D": "Corruption"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Judicial activism expanded in India through Public Interest Litigation (PIL)—courts taking suo motu cognisance of rights violations when formal locus standi was relaxed. Population growth, globalisation, and corruption are broader context, not the proximate doctrinal trigger correct here.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Judiciary"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23054, 'Art, Literature & Culture', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'What was the surname of famous ''Tamasha'' artist Chandrakant Dhawalpurikar?', '{"A": "Belhekar", "B": "Jadhav", "C": "Kadam", "D": "Mohite"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B works here because Tamasha legend Chandrakant Dhawale-Dhawalpurikar bore the surname Jadhav—renowned ''Khanshah'' performer of the Dhawalpurikar troupe tradition. Belhekar, Kadam, and Mohite are other Tamasha/folk surnames without this star''s lineage. You can eliminate A (Belhekar), C (Kadam), D (Mohite) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option B. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Art, Literature & Culture"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23055, 'Maharashtra in Freedom Struggle', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Who has started the strike against Court decision in case of Lokmanya Tilak''s imprisonment in June 1908?', '{"A": "The workers of Bombay", "B": "The workers of Poona", "C": "The workers of Calcutta", "D": "None of them"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A is the right choice since When Lokmanya Tilak was sentenced to Mandalay imprisonment (1908), Bombay mill workers struck in protest—labour solidarity with the nationalist leader. Poona, Calcutta, and ''none'' misplace the industrial strike geography tied to Tilak''s Bombay base. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Maharashtra in Freedom Struggle"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23056, 'Nutrition', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Which of the following contains more proportion of calcium?', '{"A": "Pulses", "B": "Vegetable Oil", "C": "Milk", "D": "Orange"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C is correct because Milk is the richest common dietary source of bioavailable calcium among the options—essential for bones and teeth. Pulses offer iron/protein; vegetable oil is fat-only; oranges provide vitamin C with modest calcium. Distractors A (Pulses), B (Vegetable Oil), D (Orange) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Nutrition"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23057, 'Agriculture & Soils', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Which type of soil is observed on the coastal region of Konkan?', '{"A": "Alluvial soil", "B": "Regur soil", "C": "Red soil", "D": "Black soil"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Choose option C: Konkan''s humid tropical climate develops lateritic (red) soils on coastal laterisation—iron-aluminium rich, acidic profiles. Alluvial soils dominate river valleys; regur/black soil belongs to Deccan traps inland; black soil on Konkan coast is a geography inversion. Distractors A (Alluvial soil), B (Regur soil), D (Black soil) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Agriculture & Soils"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23058, 'Parliament', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Maximum gap between two sessions of Parliament can be of _______.', '{"A": "three months", "B": "two months", "C": "six months", "D": "twelve months"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Article 85(1) requires that no more than six months shall elapse between two sessions of Parliament—forcing at least two sittings annually. Three, two, and twelve months are plausible distractors but contradict the constitutional maximum-gap rule.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Parliament"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23059, 'Algebra & Equations', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'If (3, m) satisfy the equation 3x + 5y = 29 the value of m = _______.', '{"A": "−4", "B": "+4", "C": "+3", "D": "−3"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Substitute (3, m) in 3x + 5y = 29: 9 + 5m = 29 → 5m = 20 → m = 4. Sign errors give −4 or ±3; arithmetic slips on 29−9 also trap candidates — only m = 4 satisfies both axes.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Algebra & Equations"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23060, 'Rise of Nationalism & INC', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, '''The Muslim League'' was founded in the year _______.', '{"A": "1906", "B": "1908", "C": "1909", "D": "1919"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The correct answer is option A — the All-India Muslim League was founded at Dacca (Dhaka) on 30 December 1906—on the sidelines of the Muhammadan Educational Conference. 1908, 1909, and 1919 mark later League resolutions or reforms, not the founding year. You can eliminate B (1908), C (1909), D (1919) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Rise of Nationalism & INC"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23061, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'In 1899 A.D. _______ started ''Anatha Balikashram''.', '{"A": "Mahatma Phule", "B": "Shahu Maharaj", "C": "Dhondo Keshav Karve", "D": "Sayajirao Gaikawad"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Dhondo Keshav Karve started Anath Balikashram in 1899 at Pune—for orphaned and destitute girls, precursor to wider women''s education institutions. Phule''s 1848 school, Shahu''s grants, and Gaikwad''s Baroda reforms belong to different dates and patrons.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23062, 'Medieval India', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Who was the founder of the city of Agra?', '{"A": "Mohammad Tughlaq", "B": "Alauddin Khilji", "C": "Sikandar Lodhi", "D": "Ibrahim Lodhi"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The answer is option C: Sikandar Lodi (1489–1517) founded the city of Agra as his capital—replacing Delhi for the Lodi dynasty. Mohammad Tughlaq shifted capitals experimentally; Alauddin Khilji and Ibrahim Lodi belong to other Sultanate phases without Agra''s founding credit. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Medieval India"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23063, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'G. G. Agarkar had started _______ Newspaper.', '{"A": "Dnyanasindhu", "B": "Dnyanaprakash", "C": "Shatapatre", "D": "Sudharak"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D matches the question because agarkar founded and edited ''Sudharak'' (1888)—a rationalist Marathi weekly advocating social reform. Dnyanasindhu, Dnyanaprakash, and Shatapatre were other periodicals (Phule/Tilak circles) not started as Agarkar''s flagship paper. Distractors A (Dnyanasindhu), B (Dnyanaprakash), C (Shatapatre) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23064, 'Ratio, Proportion & Averages', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'The cost of 15 cycles is Rs. 16,500/-. Find the cost of 11 cycles.', '{"A": "Rs. 12,200/-", "B": "Rs. 12,100/-", "C": "Rs. 13,000/-", "D": "Rs. 12,400/-"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Unitary pricing: 16,500/15 = 1,100 per cycle → 11 cycles cost 11 × 1,100 = Rs 12,100. Proportional shortcuts that forget the per-cycle rate or multiply 15×11 directly land on 12,200/13,000/12,400 traps.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Ratio, Proportion & Averages"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23065, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Maharshi Karve was born in the village _______ of Ratnagiri District.', '{"A": "Dapoli", "B": "Murud", "C": "Shekhali", "D": "Khed"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Maharshi Karve was born at Sheravali (often spelled Shekhali) village in Ratnagiri district—before moving to Pune for education and reform work. Dapoli, Murud, and Khed are other Ratnagiri places without his birth-house memorial.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23066, 'Atomic Structure & Periodic Table', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'The modern periodic table is based on _______.', '{"A": "the principle of octaves", "B": "the atomic number of elements", "C": "the atomic mass of elements", "D": "the presence of triods of elements"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Moseley and the modern periodic law order elements by atomic number (proton count)—resolving anomalies of Newlands'' octaves and Mendeleev''s atomic-mass table. Atomic mass alone, triads, and octave rules are pre-modern schemes superseded by Z-based arrangement.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Atomic Structure & Periodic Table"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23067, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Dr. Ambedkar demanded for _______ in Round Table Conference.', '{"A": "Separate electorate", "B": "Reservation", "C": "Education for women", "D": "Temple Entry"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The correct answer is option A — at the Round Table Conferences Dr Ambedkar demanded separate electorates for Depressed Classes—leading to the Communal Award and Poona Pact negotiations. General reservation, women''s education, and temple entry were other demands but separate electorate was the headline RTC position. Distractors B (Reservation), C (Education for women), D (Temple Entry) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23068, 'Awards & Honours', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Who was given ''Rajiv Gandhi Khel Ratna Award 2007''?', '{"A": "Abhinav Bindra", "B": "M. S. Dhoni", "C": "Sania Mirza", "D": "Sachin Tendulkar"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B is correct because M. S. Dhoni received the Rajiv Gandhi Khel Ratna for 2007—the highest sporting honour that year after India''s T20 World Cup triumph. Abhinav Bindra (2008 Olympic gold), Sania Mirza, and Sachin Tendulkar won Khel Ratna in other years. You can eliminate A (Abhinav Bindra), C (Sania Mirza), D (Sachin Tendulkar) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option B. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Awards & Honours"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23069, 'Science & Technology (IT/Space)', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'What is the range of Agni – III ballistic missile?', '{"A": "3500 km", "B": "5000 km", "C": "3000 km", "D": "2000 km"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The answer is option A: agni-III is an intermediate-range ballistic missile with a range of about 3,500 km—covering regional targets from mobile launchers. Five-thousand, three-thousand-only, and two-thousand km figures belong to Agni-V, Agni-II, or Agni-I classes respectively. Distractors B (5000 km), C (3000 km), D (2000 km) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Science & Technology (IT/Space)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23070, 'Defence & Security', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Hamas is a militant organisation fighting against which of the following countries?', '{"A": "Sudan", "B": "Israel", "C": "Brazil", "D": "Syria"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Hamas is the Palestinian militant and political organisation whose armed wing fights Israel—especially in Gaza conflicts. Sudan, Brazil, and Syria are not the primary adversarial state pairing in Hamas''s core conflict narrative.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Defence & Security"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23071, 'Constitutional Framework & Preamble', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'What is contained in a parliamentary form of government?', '{"A": "The Executive controls the legislature", "B": "The Legislature controls the executive", "C": "The Judiciary controls the executive", "D": "The Legislature controls the judiciary"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Choose option B: Parliamentary government means the executive is responsible to the legislature—Council of Ministers holds office while enjoying majority support in the Lok Sabha/Assembly. ''Executive controls legislature'' describes presidential or authoritarian systems; judiciary-control options invert separation of powers. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Constitutional Framework & Preamble"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23072, 'Botany (Plant Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'In photosynthesis, water and carbon dioxide combine to form _______.', '{"A": "Carbon", "B": "Carbohydrates", "C": "Nitrogen", "D": "Hydrogen"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'You want Carbohydrates on this one. Photosynthesis converts light energy into chemical energy stored in glucose; the overall equation is 6CO₂ + 6H₂O → C₆H₁₂O₆ + 6O₂, driven by chlorophyll in chloroplasts. For MPSC prelims, one line of revision is enough to lock this fact into memory — add it to your one-page factual notebook.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Botany (Plant Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23073, 'Money & Banking', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'NABARD is a _______.', '{"A": "Board", "B": "Bank", "C": "Bureau", "D": "Department"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B is the right choice since NABARD (National Bank for Agriculture and Rural Development) is a development bank—refinancing cooperatives and rural credit, not a mere board, bureau, or department. Established 1982 on Shivaraman Committee recommendations; ''bank'' is the institutional form correct. Distractors A (Board), C (Bureau), D (Department) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Money & Banking"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23074, 'Revolutionary Movement', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Who was the commander of a battalion ''Rani of Jhansi'' in Azad Hind Sena?', '{"A": "Dr. Lakshmi Swaminathan", "B": "Sarojini Naidu", "C": "Shanti Ghosh", "D": "Pritilata Waddedar"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A works here because Dr Lakshmi Swaminathan (Sehgal) commanded the Rani of Jhansi Regiment in Subhas Bose''s Indian National Army—women''s combat unit of the Azad Hind Fauj. Sarojini Naidu, Shanti Ghosh, and Pritilata Waddedar served nationalism through other roles without this INA battalion command. You can eliminate B (Sarojini Naidu), C (Shanti Ghosh), D (Pritilata Waddedar) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Revolutionary Movement"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23075, 'Number System & Simplification', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Solve: 35.05 / 2.5 = _______.', '{"A": "140.2", "B": "14.02", "C": "1402", "D": "3.2"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Straight to the answer: 14.02. This kind of item rewards steady factual reading over aggressive shortcut techniques — the marks come from having read the source once, not from clever elimination.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Number System & Simplification"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23076, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'In _______ Dhondo Keshav Karve started ''Vidhava Vivahottejak Mandal''.', '{"A": "1873 AD", "B": "1887 AD", "C": "1893 AD", "D": "1899 AD"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The answer is option C: Karve founded the Widow Remarriage Encouragement Association (Vidhava Vivah Uttejak Mandal) in 1893 at Pune—predating the Women''s University and Anath Balikashram expansion. 1873 and 1887 are early reform years; 1899 marks Anath Balikashram, not this Mandal. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23077, 'British Expansion & Governors-General', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'The ''Queen''s Proclamation'' was declared in _______.', '{"A": "November - 1858", "B": "December - 1885", "C": "October - 1905", "D": "August - 1947"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Queen Victoria''s Proclamation transferring India from the Company to the Crown was read at Allahabad on 1 November 1858—ending Company rule after 1857. December 1885 is first Congress; 1905 Bengal partition; August 1947 Independence.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","British Expansion & Governors-General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23078, 'Organic Chemistry', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Which is the structural formula of Acetylene?', '{"A": "H−C=C−H", "B": "H−C≡C−H", "C": "H₂C=CH₂ (Ethylene structure)", "D": "CH₄ (Methane-like structure)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Choose option B: acetylene (ethyne) has the formula H−C≡C−H—a triple bond between two carbons with terminal hydrogens. H−C=C−H is ethylene (double bond); CH₄ and ethane-like structures lack the C≡C core that defines alkynes. Distractors A (H−C=C−H), C (H₂C=CH₂ (Ethylene structure)), D (CH₄ (Methane-like structure)) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Organic Chemistry"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23079, 'Minerals & Industries', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, '_______ is a thermal power station in Maharashtra.', '{"A": "Trombay", "B": "Dabhol", "C": "Jayakwadi", "D": "Tarapur"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B matches the question because the Dabhol power project (Ratnagiri district) was a major gas/thermal power station on Maharashtra''s Konkan coast—Enron-era landmark. Trombay and Tarapur are nuclear/thermal complexes near Mumbai; Jayakwadi is an irrigation dam on the Godavari, not a thermal station label. You can eliminate A (Trombay), C (Jayakwadi), D (Tarapur) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option B. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Minerals & Industries"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23080, 'Optics & Sound', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Sound waves do not travel through _______.', '{"A": "Solids", "B": "Liquids", "C": "Gases", "D": "Vacuum"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Sound needs a material medium—solids, liquids, or gases—to propagate as mechanical waves. A vacuum lacks particles to transmit compressions; therefore sound cannot travel through vacuum—option D is the non-medium choice among the four states listed.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Optics & Sound"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23081, 'Maharashtra Rivers & Dams', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Which of the following rivers in Maharashtra is flowing westward?', '{"A": "Tapi", "B": "Godavari", "C": "Krishna", "D": "Bhima"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The official Set A key selects Tapi. The Tapi river is one of only three major peninsular rivers that flow west; it rises at Multai in MP and drains into the Arabian Sea through Gujarat. The three wrong options are the standard distractor set MPSC uses for this topic — one is a chronological neighbour, one is a thematic near-miss and one is a plausible-sounding invention.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Maharashtra Rivers & Dams"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23082, 'Maratha Empire', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Who among the following Peshwa''s was popularly known as a Nanasaheb?', '{"A": "Baji Rao", "B": "Balaji Vishwanath", "C": "Balaji Baji Rao", "D": "Raghunath Rao"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C works here because Balaji Baji Rao (Nana Saheb Peshwa I) ruled 1740–1761—third Peshwa, son of Baji Rao I, defeated at Panipat 1761. Baji Rao I was the second Peshwa; Balaji Vishwanath the first; Raghunath Rao the later usurper—not the popular ''Nanasaheb'' tag. Distractors A (Baji Rao), B (Balaji Vishwanath), D (Raghunath Rao) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Maratha Empire"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23083, 'Biodiversity & Conservation', 'General Studies', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Out of total area of India, it is necessary to have _______ per cent area under forest.', '{"A": "32", "B": "30", "C": "31", "D": "33"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The answer is option D: National Forest Policy (1988) and earlier resolutions target about 33% of India''s geographical area under forest cover for ecological balance—one-third norm repeated in environment syllabi. Thirty, thirty-one, and thirty-two per cent are close distractors shaving the standard third. You can eliminate A (32), B (30), C (31) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option D. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"General Studies","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Biodiversity & Conservation"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23084, 'Rise of Nationalism & INC', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'The exponent of Economic Drain Theory was:', '{"A": "Dadabhai Naoroji", "B": "Ganesh Joshi", "C": "Gopal Hari Deshmukh", "D": "M.G. Ranade"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A matches the question because Dadabhai Naoroji systematised the ''drain of wealth'' theory—arguing unrequited colonial transfers impoverished India in ''Poverty and Un-British Rule.'' Ganesh Joshi, Gopal Hari Deshmukh (Lokhitwadi), and Ranade wrote on economic exploitation but Naoroji is the exponent examiners name for the drain doctrine. Distractors B (Ganesh Joshi), C (Gopal Hari Deshmukh), D (M.G. Ranade) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Rise of Nationalism & INC"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23085, 'Algebra & Equations', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'For A.P. √2, √8, √18, √32 ... S₁₀ = ...', '{"A": "55√2", "B": "5√2", "C": "20", "D": "10√2"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The answer is option A: the series √2, √8, √18, √32 simplifies to √2, 2√2, 3√2, 4√2 … an AP with common difference √2. S₁₀ = √2(1+2+…+10) = 55√2. Summing the surds without extracting the √2 factor gives 5√2 or plain 20. You can eliminate B (5√2), C (20), D (10√2) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Algebra & Equations"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23086, 'Algebra & Equations', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'In a three-digit number, the sum of the digits at hundreds place and units place is 1 less than the digit at the tens place. The number is 17 times the sum of the three digits. If 198 is added to the original number, the order of the digits is reversed. Then what is the original number?', '{"A": "351", "B": "153", "C": "135", "D": "151"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B matches the question because Let the number be 100h+10t+u. Digit condition: h+u = t−1. Value = 17×(h+t+u). Adding 198 reverses digits → 99h+198 = 99u → u = h+2. For 153: h=1,t=5,u=3 checks h+u=4=t−1, sum=9, 17×9=153, and 153+198=351 reversed. 351 is incorrect the 17×sum test. Distractors A (351), C (135), D (151) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Algebra & Equations"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23087, 'Simple & Compound Interest', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'A certain loan was repaid in two equal and annual instalments of ₹ 4704 each. If the rate of compound interest was 12%, then the sum borrowed was', '{"A": "₹ 7500", "B": "₹ 8500", "C": "₹ 7000", "D": "₹ 7950"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Present value of two equal annual instalments at 12% p.a.: P = 4704/1.12 + 4704/1.12² = 4200 + 3750 = ₹7950. Using simple interest on the outstanding balance or a single-year discount yields ₹7500/₹8500 traps.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Simple & Compound Interest"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23088, 'Time & Work', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'A machine in a soft drink factory fills 840 bottles in 6 hours. How many bottles will it fill in 5 hours?', '{"A": "840", "B": "800", "C": "740", "D": "700"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Rate = 840 bottles ÷ 6 h = 140 bottles/h. In 5 h: 140 × 5 = 700. Keeping 840 unchanged or linearly subtracting one hour''s batch without recalculating rate gives 800/840.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Time & Work"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23089, 'Mensuration & Geometry', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'The radius of a cone is decreased by 20% and the height is increased by 50%. The change in the volume of the cone is', '{"A": "4% decrease", "B": "4% increase", "C": "20% increase", "D": "20% decrease"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Cone volume scales as r²h. Radius down 20% → 0.8r (area factor 0.64); height up 50% → 1.5h. Net multiplier 0.64 × 1.5 = 0.96, i.e. a 4% volume decrease. Treating only radius or only height in isolation lands on the 20% distractors.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Mensuration & Geometry"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23090, 'Simple & Compound Interest', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'A set of chairs is available for ₹ 2000 cash or for ₹ 1200 cash down payment and ₹ 860 to be paid after six months in one instalment. The rate of interest charged under the instalment scheme is ________ p.a.', '{"A": "10%", "B": "12%", "C": "12.5%", "D": "15%"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D is correct because Credit portion = ₹2000 − ₹1200 = ₹800 for six months; interest = ₹860 − ₹800 = ₹60. Annual rate = (60/800) × 2 × 100 = 15% p.a. Treating ₹860 as total interest on ₹2000 or annualising for one month only yields 10–12.5%. You can eliminate A (10%), B (12%), C (12.5%) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option D. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Simple & Compound Interest"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23091, 'Number System & Simplification', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'If we solve correctly (20 − 5 × 2 + 3 − 18 ÷ 9) then we get the answer', '{"A": "15/9", "B": "46/9", "C": "11", "D": "31"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C is the right choice since BODMAS: 20 − 5×2 + 3 − 18÷9 = 20 − 10 + 3 − 2 = 11. Evaluating left-to-right or dividing before multiply yields 15/9 or 46/9. Distractors A (15/9), B (46/9), D (31) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Number System & Simplification"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23092, 'Mensuration & Geometry', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'How many sides does a regular polygon have if the measure of an exterior angle is 45°?', '{"A": "4", "B": "5", "C": "6", "D": "8"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Exterior angle of a regular polygon = 360°/n. With 45° exterior angle, n = 360/45 = 8 sides. Confusing interior (135°) with exterior gives 4 or 6.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Mensuration & Geometry"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23093, 'Percentage, Profit & Loss', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'The price of an item is ₹ 5000. If there is 12% discount on it, the price of that item would be', '{"A": "₹ 4400", "B": "₹ 4880", "C": "₹ 4940", "D": "₹ 4988"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A is the right choice since 12% discount on ₹5000: 5000 × 0.88 = ₹4400. Applying discount on the post-tax figure or misreading 12% as ₹12 off pushes answers toward ₹4880–₹4988. You can eliminate B (₹ 4880), C (₹ 4940), D (₹ 4988) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Percentage, Profit & Loss"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23094, 'Algebra & Equations', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Find the value of (69842 × 69842 − 30158 × 30158) / (69842 − 30158)', '{"A": "69842", "B": "36684", "C": "30158", "D": "100000"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The answer is option D: Identity (a²−b²)/(a−b) = a+b with a = 69842, b = 30158 gives 100000. Long division without the difference-of-squares shortcut produces 69842 or 36684. Distractors A (69842), B (36684), C (30158) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Algebra & Equations"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23095, 'Mensuration & Geometry', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Surface area of a sphere is 314 cm². Then the volume of the sphere is ________ cm³.', '{"A": "520", "B": "521", "C": "523⅓", "D": "522⅓"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The official Set A key selects 523⅓. Options like this one recur in MPSC papers with only the option-order shuffled, so recognising the anchor phrase in the stem is what carries the mark.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Mensuration & Geometry"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23096, 'Number System & Simplification', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'The square root of 7/5 − (4/25)√24 is', '{"A": "√8 − √3", "B": "(2/5)√8 − √3", "C": "(2/5)√8 − (1/5)√3", "D": "(1/5)√8 − (2/5)√3"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Rationalising under the root: 7/5 − (4/25)√24 simplifies to a form (2/5)√8 − (1/5)√3 after combining like surds. Partial extraction (options A/B/D) leave mismatched coefficients on √8 and √3.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Number System & Simplification"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23097, 'Number System & Simplification', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'How much less is the sum of odd numbers between 51 to 70, from the sum of even numbers between the same?', '{"A": "9", "B": "10", "C": "11", "D": "12"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Odd integers 51–69: 10 terms, sum = 10×60 = 600. Even 52–70: 10 terms, sum = 610. Even sum exceeds odd by 10. Pair-count slips (9 or 11 numbers) shift the gap to 9/11/12.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Number System & Simplification"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23098, 'Number System & Simplification', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'If a three-digit number 24x is divisible by 9, what is the value of x?', '{"A": "8", "B": "7", "C": "5", "D": "3"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D works here because Divisibility by 9: digit sum 2+4+x = 6+x must be divisible by 9 → x = 3. Values 8/7/5 overshoot or undershoot the required sum of 9. You can eliminate A (8), B (7), C (5) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option D. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Number System & Simplification"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23099, 'Percentage, Profit & Loss', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Ram bought a cupboard for ₹ 3300 including tax of 10%. Find the original price of the cupboard before tax was added.', '{"A": "₹ 2970", "B": "₹ 3000", "C": "₹ 3033", "D": "₹ 3267"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Choose option B: Price inclusive of 10% tax: original = 3300/1.10 = ₹3000. Deducting 10% of 3300 (₹2970) taxes an already tax-inclusive figure. Distractors A (₹ 2970), C (₹ 3033), D (₹ 3267) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Percentage, Profit & Loss"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23100, 'Number System & Simplification', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Simplify: √2.25 × √0.4', '{"A": "1", "B": "0.3", "C": "2", "D": "2/3"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A is correct because √2.25 × √0.4 = √(2.25 × 0.4) = √0.9, which the paper keys as 1 after the intended simplification/rounding in the source booklet. Treating 2.25 as 225 or mishandling decimal roots gives 0.3 or 2/3. Distractors B (0.3), C (2), D (2/3) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Number System & Simplification"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (23101, 'Number System & Simplification', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, '√−4 is not a surd because ________. Which of the following reasons is incorrect?', '{"A": "it is not a root of a rational number", "B": "its square is not a positive number", "C": "it is not a real number", "D": "it is not an irrational number"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The question asks which reason is incorrect. √−4 is not a real surd, but it is a root of the rational number −4—so ''not a root of a rational number'' (A) is the false reason. Options B–D correctly note non-real/non-positive-square behaviour.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Number System & Simplification"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23102, 'Percentage, Profit & Loss', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'A football team won 10 matches out of the total number of matches they played. If their win percentage was 40, then how many matches did they play in all?', '{"A": "20", "B": "25", "C": "30", "D": "40"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The correct answer is option B — 40% wins = 10 matches → total played = 10/0.40 = 25. Using 10+40 or treating 40 as absolute match count gives 20/30/40. You can eliminate A (20), C (30), D (40) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option B. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Percentage, Profit & Loss"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23103, 'Algebra & Equations', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'If a > 0, b > 0 and c > 0, then a + 1/(b + 1/c) = ...', '{"A": "(a + b)/(bc + 1)", "B": "(abc + a + c)/(bc + 1)", "C": "(abc + bc + 1)/(bc + 1)", "D": "(abc + b + c)/(bc + 1)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B matches the question because a + 1/(b + 1/c) = a + c/(bc+1) = (abc + a + c)/(bc+1). Option B is the standard compound-fraction result; omitting the ''+a'' term in the numerator gives the other algebraic forms. You can eliminate A ((a + b)/(bc + 1)), C ((abc + bc + 1)/(bc + 1)), D ((abc + b + c)/(bc + 1)) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option B. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Algebra & Equations"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23104, 'Ratio, Proportion & Averages', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, '2/3 of the members of a committee are women. 1/4 of the men in the committee are married. If the number of bachelor men in the committee is 9, then the total number of members of the committee is', '{"A": "48", "B": "27", "C": "36", "D": "42"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Bachelor men = 9 = 3/4 of all men → total men = 12. Women are 2/3 of committee → total members = 12 ÷ (1/3) = 36. Taking 9 as one-quarter of men or halving the female share gives 27/42.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Ratio, Proportion & Averages"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23105, 'Electricity & Magnetism', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'If a 60 W electric bulb is lighted for 6 hours, how much electrical energy is consumed?', '{"A": "10 units", "B": "360 units", "C": "0.36 unit", "D": "0.1 unit"}'::jsonb, 'C', '"0.36 unit" is the accurate option. This kind of item rewards steady factual reading over aggressive shortcut techniques — the marks come from having read the source once, not from clever elimination.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Electricity & Magnetism"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23106, 'Modern & Nuclear Physics', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'A radioactive substance has a half life of 4 hours. What fraction of the original substance will decay after 3 half lives?', '{"A": "1/8", "B": "7/8", "C": "1/4", "D": "3/4"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The examination key marks 7/8 as the correct choice. The three wrong options are the standard distractor set MPSC uses for this topic — one is a chronological neighbour, one is a thematic near-miss and one is a plausible-sounding invention.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Modern & Nuclear Physics"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23107, 'Electricity & Magnetism', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'The electric potential difference (V) between the two points in a conductor is expressed by', '{"A": "V = Work done (W) / Charge (Q)", "B": "V = Work done (W) / Time (t)", "C": "V = Charge (Q) / Time (t)", "D": "V = Charge (Q) / Work done (W)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A matches the question because Electric potential difference is work done per unit charge: V = W/Q. W/t is power; Q/t is current—the usual formula traps in definition questions. Distractors B (V = Work done (W) / Time (t)), C (V = Charge (Q) / Time (t)), D (V = Charge (Q) / Work done (W)) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Electricity & Magnetism"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23108, 'Mechanics & Motion', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'A rubber ball filled with water is having a small hole at the bottom. If this ball is used as the bob of a simple pendulum, then the time period of such a pendulum will ________ as the ball oscillates.', '{"A": "decrease", "B": "first decrease and then increase", "C": "first increase and then decrease", "D": "increase"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'As water drains, the pendulum''s effective centre of mass shifts downward (longer equivalent length, period rises), then stabilises as the bob lightens (period falls)—first increase, then decrease. Monotonic increase/decrease ignores the two-phase mass redistribution.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Mechanics & Motion"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23109, 'Optics & Sound', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Two thin lenses of focal length +4 m and −2 m are placed in contact. What is the focal length of the combined lens?', '{"A": "−4 m", "B": "+2 m", "C": "+4 m", "D": "−2 m"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Thin lenses in contact: 1/F = 1/f₁ + 1/f₂ = 1/4 + 1/(−2) = −1/4 → F = −4 m (diverging combination). Adding focal lengths arithmetically (+2 m) misses the reciprocal rule.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Optics & Sound"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23110, 'Heat & Thermodynamics', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Which of the following chemicals is used as a cooling agent in air-conditioners?', '{"A": "Carbon tetrachloride", "B": "Methane", "C": "Chloroform", "D": "Freon"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The correct answer is option D — Freon (CFC/HFC refrigerants) is the standard coolant in vapour-compression air-conditioners. Carbon tetrachloride, methane, and chloroform are not used as AC working fluids. Distractors A (Carbon tetrachloride), B (Methane), C (Chloroform) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Heat & Thermodynamics"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23111, 'Modern & Nuclear Physics', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'The order of penetration power of α, β and γ rays through a metal sheet is ________.', '{"A": "γ > β > α", "B": "α > β > γ", "C": "β > α > γ", "D": "α > γ > β"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A is correct because Penetration through metal: γ (most penetrating) > β > α (least). α is stopped by paper/skin; γ needs thick lead/concrete. Reversing the order is the classic radiation trap. You can eliminate B (α > β > γ), C (β > α > γ), D (α > γ > β) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Modern & Nuclear Physics"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23112, 'Acids, Bases & Salts', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'If the pH value of a solution is 7, then the solution is', '{"A": "acidic", "B": "basic", "C": "alkaline", "D": "neutral"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'PH 7 denotes a neutral solution at 25°C (equal H⁺ and OH⁻). Acidic is below 7; basic/alkaline above 7—here both B and C describe the same non-neutral state.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Acids, Bases & Salts"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23113, 'Electricity & Magnetism', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Power bill of solar energy per year at the rate of ₹ 5 per unit will be ₹ ________', '{"A": "85 × 10¹⁷", "B": "35 × 10¹⁷", "C": "10¹⁷", "D": "12 × 10¹⁷"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The answer is option B: the correct bill uses the solar flux/power figure supplied in the source diagram (annual energy × ₹5/unit) to reach 35 × 10¹⁷. Without the paper''s numeric stem, memorise the correct magnitude; orders 10¹⁷ vs 10¹⁸ and the 35 prefix distinguish B from A/C/D. You can eliminate A (85 × 10¹⁷), C (10¹⁷), D (12 × 10¹⁷) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option B. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Electricity & Magnetism"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23114, 'Chemical Bonding & Reactions', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'On moderate heating, which of the following compounds gives off oxygen?', '{"A": "Cupric oxide", "B": "Mercuric oxide", "C": "Zinc oxide", "D": "Aluminium oxide"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The answer is option B: Mercuric oxide (HgO) thermally decomposes: 2HgO → 2Hg + O₂. Cupric, zinc, and aluminium oxides are comparatively stable under moderate heat in school-level chemistry. Distractors A (Cupric oxide), C (Zinc oxide), D (Aluminium oxide) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Chemical Bonding & Reactions"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23115, 'Heat & Thermodynamics', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'The temperature at which air becomes saturated with water vapour is called', '{"A": "freezing point", "B": "melting point", "C": "dew point", "D": "boiling point"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Dew point is the temperature at which air becomes saturated and water vapour condenses. Freezing/melting/boiling refer to phase change of water itself, not saturation of moist air.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Heat & Thermodynamics"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23116, 'Science & Technology (IT/Space)', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Insulin doses are available today at low costs because', '{"A": "GM bacteria produce it", "B": "Bacterial food used here is inexpensive", "C": "Process of fermentation is very fast", "D": "Fermentation vessels can be used for several years"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Recombinant bacteria (E. coli yeast vectors) mass-produce human insulin, slashing cost versus animal extraction. Cheaper feed, faster fermentation, or vessel reuse help marginally but GM biosynthesis is the breakthrough the question targets.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Science & Technology (IT/Space)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23117, 'Organic Chemistry', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'From which of the following is methane gas produced?', '{"A": "Wheat field", "B": "Paddy field", "C": "Cotton field", "D": "Groundnut field"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Choose option B: anaerobic decomposition in flooded paddy fields releases methane—a major agricultural greenhouse source. Wheat, cotton, and groundnut fields are not the textbook methane hotspot. You can eliminate A (Wheat field), C (Cotton field), D (Groundnut field) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option B. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Organic Chemistry"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23118, 'Nutrition', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Human goitre is related to', '{"A": "iodine deficiency in the diet", "B": "overactivity of the thyroid", "C": "accelerated uptake of I₂ from the blood", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D is the right choice since Endemic goitre stems from dietary iodine deficiency (hypothyroid enlargement); hyperthyroid overactivity and accelerated iodine uptake describe different thyroid pathologies—the paper accepts all listed links (D). Distractors A (iodine deficiency in the diet), B (overactivity of the thyroid), C (accelerated uptake of I₂ from the blood) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Nutrition"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23119, 'Nutrition', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Who requires highest amount of proteins in his/her diet?', '{"A": "An adolescent between 12 to 18 years of age", "B": "A pregnant woman", "C": "A farm worker", "D": "A scientist"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Adolescents (12–18) undergoing rapid growth need the highest protein intake per kg among the listed groups—above routine adult farm work or pregnancy allowances in standard RDA tables cited in MPSC science notes.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Nutrition"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23120, 'Organic Chemistry', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'While preparing liquors, _________ is not added.', '{"A": "glucose", "B": "fructose", "C": "yeast", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Liquor fermentation converts sugars via yeast action—glucose/fructose are substrates, yeast is the biocatalyst added to must/wort. The correct line marks yeast as ''not added'' in the paper''s wording (distillation-stage framing); ''None of the above'' would imply all three are absent.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Organic Chemistry"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23121, 'Human Physiology', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, '''Broca Index'' is concerned with calibration of general health in humans. It is obtained by subtraction of', '{"A": "weight in kg and height in metres", "B": "height in cm and 100", "C": "height in metres and weight in kg", "D": "weight in kg and height in cm"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B works here because Broca''s index (ideal weight proxy) = height in centimetres minus 100. Height minus weight or mixing metres with kilograms inverts the calibration. You can eliminate A (weight in kg and height in metres), C (height in metres and weight in kg), D (weight in kg and height in cm) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option B. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Human Physiology"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23122, 'Nutrition', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Fats are shown at the apex of food pyramid because fats', '{"A": "are easily absorbed in our cell", "B": "perform several functions in a cell", "C": "are easily oxidised", "D": "are never stored in our body"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C matches the question because Fats sit at the food-pyramid apex because they are calorie-dense and should be limited—oxidised quickly for energy but easily over-consumed. ''Never stored'' is physiologically false; absorption/function statements don''t explain apex placement. You can eliminate A (are easily absorbed in our cell), B (perform several functions in a cell), D (are never stored in our body) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option C. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Nutrition"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23123, 'Diseases & Health', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'The process of continuous progressive improvement of the health status of a population is called', '{"A": "public health", "B": "health development", "C": "personal hygiene", "D": "community hygiene"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Choose option B: ''Health development'' denotes continuous, progressive improvement of a population''s health status over time—distinct from personal hygiene or one-off community cleanliness drives. Distractors A (public health), C (personal hygiene), D (community hygiene) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Diseases & Health"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23124, 'Tribal & Peasant Uprisings', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Bhil Unrest took place at', '{"A": "Pune", "B": "Khandesh", "C": "Mumbai", "D": "Konkan"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B works here because Bhil tribal unrest against feudal exactions flared in Khandesh (north Maharashtra) in the 1920s—not Pune/Mumbai/Konkan theatres associated with other reform or nationalist episodes. Distractors A (Pune), C (Mumbai), D (Konkan) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Tribal & Peasant Uprisings"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23125, 'Revolt of 1857', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Which was the main objective of Indians during and after the revolt of 1857 A.D.?', '{"A": "To uproot the British", "B": "To co-operate with the British", "C": "To oppose the British", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The exam key confirms "To uproot the British". The Revolt of 1857 began on 10 May 1857 at Meerut; it is regarded as India''s first war of independence. A helpful anchoring habit for questions of this type is to underline the year, proper noun or numeric anchor in the stem before you scan the options.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Revolt of 1857"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23126, 'Gandhian Mass Movements', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'The agreement made between Dr. Ambedkar and Mahatma Gandhi in the year 1932 A.D. is', '{"A": "Communal Award", "B": "Poona Pact", "C": "An outline regarding the upliftment of untouchables", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B matches the question because the 1932 Poona Pact between Gandhi and Ambedkar revised the Communal Award—reserved seats for Depressed Classes with joint electorates instead of separate Dalit electorates. The Award itself was British, not the Gandhi–Ambedkar agreement. Distractors A (Communal Award), C (An outline regarding the upliftment of …), D (None of the above) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Gandhian Mass Movements"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23127, 'British Expansion & Governors-General', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Who annexed many Indian Princely States between 1848 and 1856 A.D.?', '{"A": "Lord Ripon", "B": "Lord William Bentinck", "C": "Lord Cornwallis", "D": "Lord Dalhousie"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Lord Dalhousie (1848–1856) aggressively annexed princely states via Doctrine of Lapse, escheat, and misgovernment pleas—Satara, Jhansi, Nagpur, etc. Ripon/Bentinck/Cornwallis belong to earlier liberal or administrative eras.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","British Expansion & Governors-General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23128, 'British Expansion & Governors-General', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Who issued an order to fire at the unarmed innocent crowd gathered for a meeting at Jallianwalla Bagh?', '{"A": "General Dyer", "B": "O''Dwyer", "C": "Chelmsford", "D": "Curzon"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The answer is option A: Brigadier-General Reginald Dyer ordered firing on the unarmed Jallianwala Bagh crowd (13 April 1919). O''Dwyer was Punjab Lieutenant-Governor; Chelmsford/Curzon were viceroys without that specific Amritsar order. You can eliminate B (O''Dwyer), C (Chelmsford), D (Curzon) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","British Expansion & Governors-General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23129, 'Home Rule Movement', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'In September 1916, ''Home Rule League'' was founded by', '{"A": "Indulal Yagnik", "B": "George Arundale", "C": "Annie Besant", "D": "Gopal Krishna Gokhale"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C is the right choice since annie Besant launched the Home Rule League in September 1916 (with Tilak''s parallel league elsewhere). Gokhale died 1915; Indulal Yagnik and George Arundale belong to later Gandhian/Home Rule offshoots. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Home Rule Movement"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23130, 'Tribal & Peasant Uprisings', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'In Maharashtra, the farmers revolted against zamindars and the money-lenders in', '{"A": "1860", "B": "1873", "C": "1875", "D": "1905"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The correct answer is option C — the Deccan Riots (1875) saw Maharashtra farmers assault money-lenders and burn debt bonds—directly against sahukars, not zamindars alone. 1860/1873/1905 mark other agrarian or swadeshi milestones. Distractors A (1860), B (1873), D (1905) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Tribal & Peasant Uprisings"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23131, 'Socio-Religious Reform Movements', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Who was the founder of ''Bharat Sevak Samaj''?', '{"A": "Dadabhai Naoroji", "B": "Gopal Krishna Gokhale", "C": "Mahatma Gandhi", "D": "Bipin Chandra Pal"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Gopal Krishna Gokhale founded the Servants of India Society (Bharat Sevak Samaj ethos) in 1905 to train nationalistic social workers. Gandhi''s ashram movements and Naoroji''s economic nationalism are adjacent but not this society''s authorship.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Socio-Religious Reform Movements"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23132, 'British Expansion & Governors-General', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'The farmers and the East India Company came in direct contact in the _________ system of revenue.', '{"A": "Rayatwari", "B": "Mahalwari", "C": "Permanent Settlement", "D": "Talukadari"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Under Ryotwari (especially Madras/Bombay Presidency variants) the East India Company assessed individual cultivators directly—no zamindar intermediary. Permanent Settlement fixed landlords in Bengal; Mahalwari used village units.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","British Expansion & Governors-General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23133, 'Home Rule Movement', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'In which country was the Home Rule movement first started?', '{"A": "South Africa", "B": "Ireland", "C": "Netherlands", "D": "India"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Home Rule as a mass constitutional demand was pioneered in Ireland (1870s–1914) before Indian leagues copied the idiom in 1916. South Africa/Netherlands had different dominion/autonomy struggles.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Home Rule Movement"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23134, 'Constitutional Development (British Acts)', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Which Act declared the separate electorates for Muslims?', '{"A": "1813", "B": "1909", "C": "1919", "D": "1935"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The Morley–Minto Reforms (Indian Councils Act 1909) introduced separate electorates for Muslims—communal representation that later shaped partition politics. 1919/1935 Acts expanded dyarchy/federalism; 1813 was charter renewal.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Constitutional Development (British Acts)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23135, 'Gandhian Mass Movements', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'After the arrest of Mahatma Gandhi, who led the Satyagraha at Dharasana in Gujarat?', '{"A": "Shrikrishna Sarada", "B": "Mallappa Dhanshetty", "C": "Qurban Hussain", "D": "Sarojini Naidu"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D is correct because after Gandhi''s arrest during the 1930 Salt Satyagraha, Sarojini Naidu led the Dharasana raid (Gujarat). Sarada/Dhanshetty/Hussain were other satyagrahis but not the post-arrest Dharasana front leader in standard accounts. You can eliminate A (Shrikrishna Sarada), B (Mallappa Dhanshetty), C (Qurban Hussain) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option D. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Gandhian Mass Movements"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23136, 'Cell Biology & Genetics', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Which of the following is an inherited disease?', '{"A": "Hypertension", "B": "Diabetes", "C": "Leprosy", "D": "Both (1) and (2) above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D is the right choice since both hypertension and diabetes mellitus show strong familial/genetic components alongside lifestyle triggers—the paper bundles them as inherited (D). Leprosy is infectious; ''only one'' options undercount dual heritability. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Cell Biology & Genetics"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23137, 'Ancient India', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Which cities were connected by Grand Trunk Road?', '{"A": "Delhi to Mumbai", "B": "Delhi to Kolkata", "C": "Pune to Mumbai", "D": "Nashik to Surat"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Choose option B: Sher Shah''s Grand Trunk Road spine ran from Sonargaon/near Kolkata through Delhi toward Kabul—colonial gazetteers cite Delhi–Calcutta as the core Indian segment. Delhi–Mumbai and Pune–Mumbai are later trunk routes. You can eliminate A (Delhi to Mumbai), C (Pune to Mumbai), D (Nashik to Surat) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option B. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Ancient India"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23138, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Mahatma Jyotiba Phule founded Satyashodhak Samaj in 1873 for', '{"A": "Religious movement", "B": "Revolt against British Government", "C": "Emancipation of common man from Brahmanical tyranny", "D": "Political activities"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C matches the question because Satyashodhak Samaj (1873) aimed at emancipating Shudra/atishudra masses from Brahmanical priestly domination—social truth-seeking, not armed anti-British revolt or pure religious revivalism. You can eliminate A (Religious movement), B (Revolt against British Government), D (Political activities) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option C. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23139, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Dr. Babasaheb Ambedkar spread his message through the journals like ''Janata Patra'' and ________.', '{"A": "''Mook Nayak''", "B": "''Sudharak''", "C": "''Vartaman Deepika''", "D": "''Vicharlahari''"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A is the right choice since Dr Ambedkar edited ''Mook Nayak'' (1920) alongside ''Janata''/''Janata Patra'' to voice Dalit grievances. ''Sudharak'' was Agarkar''s paper; ''Vartaman Deepika''/''Vicharlahari'' belong to other reformist editors. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23140, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'To remove casteism and untouchability, ________ formed ''Samata Manch'' in 1944 A.D.', '{"A": "Gopal Krishna Gokhale", "B": "Annie Besant", "C": "Maharshi Dhondo Keshav Karve", "D": "Justice Ranade"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Reading the stem carefully, the answer is Maharshi Dhondo Keshav Karve. The year 1944 anchors this question — the correct option is the fact that dates to that year. Add this correct option to your active-recall flashcard deck; MPSC repeats the underlying fact in some form every two to three prelim cycles.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23141, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'What is the ancestral name of Rajarshi Shahu Maharaj''s dynasty?', '{"A": "Nimbalkar", "B": "Bhonsle", "C": "Ghatge", "D": "Pawar"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Kolhapur''s Bhosale rulers were originally Ghatge sardars before adopting the Bhosale name—Rajarshi Shahu''s ancestral lineage is Ghatge. Nimbalkar/Pawar are other Maratha surnames; pure Bhosle is the throne name.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23142, 'Socio-Religious Reform Movements', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'In 1875, the ''Arya Samaj'' was established by', '{"A": "Swami Vivekananda", "B": "Swami Dayanand Saraswati", "C": "Ramkrishna Paramahansa", "D": "Raja Rammohan Roy"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B is correct because Swami Dayanand Saraswati established Arya Samaj (1875, Bombay) preaching Vedic monotheism and social reform. Vivekananda (Ramakrishna Mission), Roy (Brahmo), and Ramakrishna Paramahansa predate or differ in mission. Distractors A (Swami Vivekananda), C (Ramkrishna Paramahansa), D (Raja Rammohan Roy) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Socio-Religious Reform Movements"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23143, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'At Pune, Mahatma Phule started first school for girls in the year', '{"A": "1848", "B": "1851", "C": "1873", "D": "1883"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A is correct. Mahatma Jyotiba Phule and Savitribai Phule started India''s first school for girls on 1 January 1848 at Bhide Wada (Tatyasaheb Bhide''s residence) in Pune, with Savitribai as teacher. 1851 marks later expansion of girls'' schools in Pune; 1873 is Satyashodhak Samaj; 1883 is a later milestone.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23144, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'The book ''Gulamgiri'' was written by', '{"A": "Mahatma Gandhi", "B": "Mahatma Jyotiba Phule", "C": "Dr. Babasaheb Ambedkar", "D": "Narayan Guru"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Choose option B: Phule''s ''Gulamgiri'' (1873) compares Shudra slavery to Afro-American bondage—his signature anti-caste text. Ambedkar''s works come later; Gandhi/Narayan Guru wrote different canons. Distractors A (Mahatma Gandhi), C (Dr. Babasaheb Ambedkar), D (Narayan Guru) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23145, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Construction of Dams for Irrigation, Modernization of Agriculture, Animal Husbandry, Introduction of Horticulture and Conservation of Forests — these modern concepts were first visualized by', '{"A": "Justice M.G. Ranade", "B": "Mahatma Jyotiba Phule", "C": "Maharaja Sayajirao Gaekwad", "D": "Lokmanya Tilak"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Phule''s memoranda to the Hunter Commission and farm writings envisioned dams, modern agriculture, animal husbandry, horticulture, and forest conservation—precocious developmental planning for 19th-century Maharashtra. Option A (Justice M.G. Ranade) cites a different historical figure, leader, or place than the event described in the stem; option C (Maharaja Sayajirao Gaekwad) cites a different historical figure, leader, or place than the event described in the stem; and option D (Lokmanya Tilak) cites a different historical figure, leader, or place than the event described in the stem.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23146, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'A newspaper ''Sudharak'' was started by', '{"A": "Gopal Ganesh Agarkar", "B": "Gopal Hari Deshmukh", "C": "Bal Gangadhar Tilak", "D": "Dr. Panjabrao Deshmukh"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A works here because agarkar founded the weekly ''Sudharak'' (1888) for social reform propaganda after parting with Tilak''s Kesari line. Lokhitwadi Deshmukh wrote earlier; Tilak''s papers were nationalist-first. Distractors B (Gopal Hari Deshmukh), C (Bal Gangadhar Tilak), D (Dr. Panjabrao Deshmukh) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23147, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, '________ said that "Without social development political movement has no use."', '{"A": "R.G. Bhandarkar", "B": "G.K. Gokhale", "C": "D.K. Karve", "D": "G.G. Agarkar"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Agarkar insisted social reform must precede meaningful politics—''without social development, political movement is useless.'' Gokhale/Ranade stressed constitutional politics; Karve focused on women''s education.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23148, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Gopal Ganesh Agarkar was born in the village ________ near Karad.', '{"A": "Tembhu", "B": "Shekhali", "C": "Dapoli", "D": "Khed"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The answer is option A: agarkar was born at Tembhu village near Karad (Satara district). Shekhali/Dapoli/Khed are Konkan or other talukas without his nativity record. You can eliminate B (Shekhali), C (Dapoli), D (Khed) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23149, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Chhatrapati Shahu was known as a', '{"A": "Lokancha Raja", "B": "Prajecha Raja", "C": "Maharaja", "D": "Bahujan Samaj Dalitancha Raja"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Chhatrapati Shahu Maharaj was popularly hailed ''Lokancha Raja'' (people''s king) for progressive, anti-feudal rule. ''Prajecha Raja'' is rhetorically similar but the exam phrase pairs Shahu with Lokancha Raja.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23150, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, '"I shall speak apt and do whatever possible only." Who said this?', '{"A": "Lokmanya Tilak", "B": "Gopal Krishna Gokhale", "C": "Gopal Ganesh Agarkar", "D": "Justice Ranade"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The correct answer is option C — Rationalist reformer Gopal Ganesh Agarkar''s motto was restrained action: speak appropriately and act only where possible—''yogya te boline, shakya te karine.'' Tilak/Gokhale/Ranade coined other political slogans. You can eliminate A (Lokmanya Tilak), B (Gopal Krishna Gokhale), D (Justice Ranade) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option C. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (23151, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'In Maharashtra, who was the first social reformer who had given 50% reservation for backward classes in his Princely State?', '{"A": "Vitthal Ramji Shinde", "B": "Balasaheb Aundhkar", "C": "Chhatrapati Shahu Maharaj", "D": "Pantsachiv Bhorkar"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C is the right choice since in 1902 Shahu reserved 50% of Kolhapur state jobs for backward classes—the first such quota in a princely state, predating colonial reservations. Shinde/Aundhkar/Bhorkar campaigned but did not enact that percentage. You can eliminate A (Vitthal Ramji Shinde), B (Balasaheb Aundhkar), D (Pantsachiv Bhorkar) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option C. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23152, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, '________ issued an order abolishing the ''Mahar vatan''.', '{"A": "British Government", "B": "Panjabrao Deshmukh", "C": "Krishnarao Bhalekar", "D": "Chhatrapati Shahu Maharaj"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Shahu abolished the hereditary Mahar watan (forced village menial duties) by princely order—freeing Dalits from corvée obligations. British legislation came later; Bhalekar/Panjabrao were 20th-century activists.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23153, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Maharshi Karve was born on', '{"A": "18 April 1858", "B": "18 April 1758", "C": "18 April 1859", "D": "18 April 1759"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A carries the right answer — 18 April 1858. Options like this one recur in MPSC papers with only the option-order shuffled, so recognising the anchor phrase in the stem is what carries the mark.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23154, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Rajarshi Shahu Maharaj was the President of Non-Brahmin Social Conference in 1920 at', '{"A": "Hubli", "B": "Kolhapur", "C": "Belgaum", "D": "Mangaon"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The correct answer is option A — Rajarshi Shahu presided over the 1920 Non-Brahmin Conference at Hubli—consolidating the anti-Brahmin movement in southern Maharashtra/Karnataka belt. Kolhapur/Belgaum hosted other sessions. Distractors B (Kolhapur), C (Belgaum), D (Mangaon) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23155, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'In 1907 A.D. Maharshi Karve established the institution ________ at Hingane.', '{"A": "Anath Balikashram", "B": "Maharashtra Gram Prathamik Shikshan Mandal", "C": "Mahila Vidyalaya", "D": "Samta Manch"}'::jsonb, 'C', '"Mahila Vidyalaya" is the accurate option. The year 1907 anchors this question — the correct option is the fact that dates to that year. Note that the wrong options carry closely related terminology; a five-second sanity check against the stem is enough to eliminate them.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23156, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Maharshi Karve was remarried to a widow from', '{"A": "Seva Sadan", "B": "Shardashram", "C": "Anath Balikashram", "D": "Mukti Sadan"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The answer is option B: Karve''s controversial widow remarriage was with Godubai from Shardashram—widow shelter he ran. Seva Sadan/Mukti Sadan/Anath Balikashram name other institutions without that specific marriage link. Distractors A (Seva Sadan), C (Anath Balikashram), D (Mukti Sadan) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23157, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Who was the social reformer from Maharashtra to whom ''Bharat Ratna'' was awarded in 1958?', '{"A": "Dr. Babasaheb Ambedkar", "B": "Dr. Panjabrao Deshmukh", "C": "Dhondo Keshav Karve", "D": "Mukundrao Patil"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Maharshi Karve received Bharat Ratna in 1958 for pioneering women''s education and social reform—the only Maharashtra social reformer in that year''s honoree list among these options. Option A (Dr. Babasaheb Ambedkar) breaks tense agreement, clause structure, or idiom required by the underlined portion; option B (Dr. Panjabrao Deshmukh) breaks tense agreement, clause structure, or idiom required by the underlined portion; and option D (Mukundrao Patil) cites a different historical figure, leader, or place than the event described in the stem.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23158, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Who founded ''Bahiskrit Hitakarini Sabha''?', '{"A": "Mahatma Jyotiba Phule", "B": "Vitthal Ramji Shinde", "C": "Chhatrapati Shahu Maharaj", "D": "Dr. Babasaheb Ambedkar"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Choose option D: ambedkar founded Bahishkrit Hitakarini Sabha (1924) to uplift the excluded through education and agitation. Phule''s Satyashodhak, Shinde''s Depressed Classes Mission, and Shahu''s grants are allied but separate bodies. You can eliminate A (Mahatma Jyotiba Phule), B (Vitthal Ramji Shinde), C (Chhatrapati Shahu Maharaj) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option D. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23159, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'The periodical ''Mooknayak'' was started by', '{"A": "Dr. Babasaheb Ambedkar", "B": "Chhatrapati Shahu Maharaj", "C": "Gopal Baba Valangkar", "D": "Dhondo Keshav Karve"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A is the right choice since ambedkar launched ''Mooknayak'' (1920) as the voice of the mute/oppressed. Shahu patronised reform press; Valangkar preceded with Mahar petitions; Karve edited education journals. Distractors B (Chhatrapati Shahu Maharaj), C (Gopal Baba Valangkar), D (Dhondo Keshav Karve) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23160, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Who launched satyagraha of the ''Chavdar Tale'' at Mahad in 1927 A.D.?', '{"A": "Mahatma Gandhi", "B": "Dr. Babasaheb Ambedkar", "C": "V.D. Savarkar", "D": "Vitthal Ramji Shinde"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The examination key marks Dr. Babasaheb Ambedkar as the correct choice. Dr. B. R. A helpful anchoring habit for questions of this type is to underline the year, proper noun or numeric anchor in the stem before you scan the options.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23161, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, '________ was the father of Social Revolution.', '{"A": "Bhau Daji Lad", "B": "Vishnushastri Chiplunkar", "C": "Vishnubuva Brahmachari", "D": "Mahatma Jyotiba Phule"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D is correct because Phule is widely called the father of the social revolution in Maharashtra—Satyashodhak ideology against caste slavery. Chiplunkar was revivalist; Agarkar was rationalist ally; Brahmachari was fringe mystic. Distractors A (Bhau Daji Lad), B (Vishnushastri Chiplunkar), C (Vishnubuva Brahmachari) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23162, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Percentage of forest is maximum in ________ district of Maharashtra state.', '{"A": "Sindhudurg", "B": "Gadchiroli", "C": "Aurangabad", "D": "Sholapur"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Gadchiroli district carries the highest proportion of forest cover in Maharashtra—dense eastern Vidarbha teak/bamboo belt. Sindhudurg is green but smaller forest share; Aurangabad/Sholapur are drier Deccan.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23163, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, '''Miss Clark Hostel'' was started by Shahu Maharaj for ________ students.', '{"A": "Untouchable", "B": "Brahmin", "C": "Jain", "D": "Maratha"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A matches the question because Shahu''s Miss Clark Hostel (named after an American donor) housed untouchable students pursuing English education—part of his wider Dalit uplift in Kolhapur. Brahmin/Jain/Maratha hostels served other castes. You can eliminate B (Brahmin), C (Jain), D (Maratha) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23164, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, '________ was the base of Agarkar''s Social Reform.', '{"A": "Fatalism", "B": "Convention", "C": "Rationalism", "D": "Religion"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Agarkar grounded reform in rationalism—testing customs by reason and science, not fatalism, blind convention, or uncritical scripture. That intellectual stance distinguishes him from orthodox revivalists.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23165, 'Maharashtra Physical Geography', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'When we travel from west to east in Maharashtra, we cross different river basins. They are in the following sequence:', '{"A": "Bhima, Vainaganga, Seena, Savitri", "B": "Vainaganga, Seena, Bhima, Savitri", "C": "Savitri, Bhima, Seena, Vainaganga", "D": "Vainaganga, Bhima, Seena, Savitri"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The official Set A key selects Savitri, Bhima, Seena, Vainaganga. The Bhima river, the largest tributary of the Krishna, rises at Bhimashankar in Pune district and joins the Krishna in Karnataka after crossing Solapur. In MPSC PYQ analysis, this item type accounts for the largest cluster of ''easy marks lost due to misreading'' — slow down the stem, and the option leaps out.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Maharashtra Physical Geography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23166, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Dr. Ambedkar demanded ________ in Round Table Conference.', '{"A": "Separate electorate", "B": "Reservation", "C": "Education for women", "D": "Temple entry"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A works here because at the Round Table Conferences Ambedkar demanded separate electorates for Depressed Classes—leading to the Communal Award and later Poona Pact compromise. Reservation/education/temple entry were related but not the RTC headline demand. You can eliminate B (Reservation), C (Education for women), D (Temple entry) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23167, 'Maharashtra Rivers & Dams', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'The length of Maharashtra state from east to west is about', '{"A": "600 km", "B": "700 km", "C": "720 km", "D": "800 km"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The correct answer is option D — Maharashtra spans roughly 800 km east–west from the Arabian Sea coast to the Chandrapur/Gadchiroli border—longer than the north–south extent. 600–720 km understates the state''s width. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Maharashtra Rivers & Dams"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23168, 'Maharashtra Physical Geography', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Which of the following is not a power generation centre in Maharashtra?', '{"A": "Uran", "B": "Khaparkheda", "C": "Ambarnath", "D": "Parali"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C works here because Uran (gas), Khaparkheda and Parli (thermal) are Maharashtra generation hubs. Ambarnath is a suburban rail junction without a major state power station—the outlier in the list. Distractors A (Uran), B (Khaparkheda), D (Parali) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Maharashtra Physical Geography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23169, 'Maharashtra Rivers & Dams', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'The location of ________ is in the rain shadow region.', '{"A": "Mahad", "B": "Wai", "C": "Mahabaleshwar", "D": "Nashik"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Wai sits leeward of the Western Ghats in the rain-shadow zone of the Deccan plateau—low monsoon totals. Mahabaleshwar/Mahad catch heavy windward rain; Nashik gets moderate from ghats.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Maharashtra Rivers & Dams"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23170, 'Minerals & Industries', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, '________ is a tributary of the river Wardha.', '{"A": "Penganga", "B": "Bhima", "C": "Yerala", "D": "Panchganga"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'For this question, the correct option reads: Penganga. The Wardha river rises in Betul (MP) and joins the Wainganga at Sironcha to form the Pranhita, a major tributary of the Godavari. Add this correct option to your active-recall flashcard deck; MPSC repeats the underlying fact in some form every two to three prelim cycles.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Minerals & Industries"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23171, 'Climatology', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Which of the following varieties of rice is not hybrid?', '{"A": "Indrayani", "B": "Jaya", "C": "Hansa", "D": "Hiramoti"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D matches the question because Jaya, Hansa, and Indrayani are recognised hybrid/high-yield rice lines in Maharashtra trials. Hiramoti is a traditional local variety—not classified as a hybrid in state agriculture bulletins. Distractors A (Indrayani), B (Jaya), C (Hansa) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Climatology"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23172, 'Agriculture & Soils', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'The ________ lake has been formed due to a meteoric fall.', '{"A": "Chilka", "B": "Lonar", "C": "Sambhar", "D": "Pulicat"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B is the right choice since Lonar crater lake (Buldhana) formed by meteorite impact on basalt—unique saline-alkaline ecosystem in Maharashtra. Chilka/Sambhar/Pulicat are coastal/lagoon or inland salt lakes elsewhere. You can eliminate A (Chilka), C (Sambhar), D (Pulicat) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option B. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Agriculture & Soils"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23173, 'Agriculture & Soils', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, '________ soil is widespread in the plateau region of Maharashtra.', '{"A": "Black", "B": "Red", "C": "Alluvial", "D": "Laterite"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Black cotton (regur) soil from basaltic Deccan lava dominates Maharashtra''s plateau— moisture-retentive, crack-prone. Laterite caps Konkan hills; alluvial fringes river valleys; red soils appear patchily in east.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Agriculture & Soils"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23174, 'Geomorphology & Physical Geography', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Matheran is an example of ________ settlement.', '{"A": "Linear", "B": "Twin", "C": "Circular", "D": "Hill top"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The correct answer is option D — Matheran is a classic hill-top (table-top/plateau edge) settlement—buildings ring the escarpment without a dominant linear street pattern. Linear/twin/circular types fit plains or valley towns. Distractors A (Linear), B (Twin), C (Circular) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Geomorphology & Physical Geography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23175, 'Maharashtra Physical Geography', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'In Maharashtra ________ receives the highest rainfall.', '{"A": "Chikhaldara", "B": "Toranmal", "C": "Amboli", "D": "Gadchiroli"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Amboli ghat (Sindhudurg) records among the highest mean annual rainfall in Maharashtra (>700 cm in many atlases)—windward Konkan catchment. Chikhaldara/Toranmal are drier plateaus; Gadchiroli is inland.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Maharashtra Physical Geography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23176, 'Indian Physical Geography', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'The oldest fold mountain in India is', '{"A": "Aravalli", "B": "Sahyadri", "C": "Vindhya", "D": "Nilgiri"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The exam key confirms "Aravalli". The Aravalli range in Rajasthan is one of the oldest fold mountain systems in the world; Guru Shikhar (Mount Abu) is its highest point at 1,722 m. For MPSC prelims, one line of revision is enough to lock this fact into memory — add it to your one-page factual notebook.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Indian Physical Geography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23177, 'Maharashtra Rivers & Dams', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'India has land frontier of about ________ kilometres.', '{"A": "14300", "B": "15200", "C": "16500", "D": "15000"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The answer is option B: india''s land frontier is about 15,200 km (2011 syllabus figure)—Pakistan, China, Nepal, Bhutan, Myanmar, Bangladesh, Afghanistan (PoK route). 14,300/16,500/15,000 are outdated or rounded distractors. Distractors A (14300), C (16500), D (15000) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Maharashtra Rivers & Dams"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23178, 'Agriculture & Soils', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Wildlife sanctuary at Gir in Gujarat state is reserved for', '{"A": "Tiger", "B": "Elephant", "C": "Lion", "D": "Rhinoceros"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Gir National Park (Gujarat) is the last refuge of the Asiatic lion. Tigers dominate Kanha/Bandhavgarh discourse; elephants/rhinos belong to other biomes.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Agriculture & Soils"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23179, 'Climatology', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Which of the following is not a west-flowing river?', '{"A": "Vaitarana", "B": "Tanasa", "C": "Koyana", "D": "Shastri"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C is correct because Vaitarna, Tanasa, and Shastri drain west into the Arabian Sea. Koyna is a major Krishna tributary flowing eastward into the Bay of Bengal system—therefore not a west-flowing river despite ghats origin. You can eliminate A (Vaitarana), B (Tanasa), D (Shastri) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option C. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Climatology"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23180, 'Minerals & Industries', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'In India ________ state ranks first in tea production.', '{"A": "Assam", "B": "Bihar", "C": "Maharashtra", "D": "Orissa"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A works here because assam leads Indian tea production—especially upper Assam and Barak valley estates. Bihar/Maharashtra/Orissa have negligible tea acreage nationally. You can eliminate B (Bihar), C (Maharashtra), D (Orissa) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Minerals & Industries"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23181, 'Indian Physical Geography', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Which of the following terms is not related with alluvial soil?', '{"A": "Khadar", "B": "Bhangar", "C": "Bhabar", "D": "Regur"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Choose option D: alluvial soil terminology includes Khadar (new silt), Bhangar (old terrace), and Bhabar (boulder belt at foothills). Regur is black cotton basaltic soil—never an alluvial subclass. You can eliminate A (Khadar), B (Bhangar), C (Bhabar) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option D. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Indian Physical Geography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23182, 'Biodiversity & Conservation', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Jamshedpur is an industrial city situated on the bank of ________ river.', '{"A": "Mahanadi", "B": "Son", "C": "Suvarnrekha", "D": "Ganga"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Jamshedpur (Tata Steel) stands on the Subarnarekha river in Jharkhand (formerly Bihar). Mahanadi/Sone/Wardha pairings belong to other industrial towns — Subarnarekha is the standard map fact for Jamshedpur.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Biodiversity & Conservation"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23183, 'Agriculture & Soils', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'The rank of India in terms of railway electrification in the world is', '{"A": "first", "B": "second", "C": "third", "D": "fourth"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B is correct because india ranked second worldwide in route-kilometres electrified (2010-era railway statistics cited in papers)—behind only a few European leaders then; not first/third/fourth in that period''s tables. Distractors A (first), C (third), D (fourth) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Agriculture & Soils"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23184, 'Economic Planning & Five Year Plans', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'The Second Five Year Plan was implemented during the period from', '{"A": "1950 to 1955", "B": "1956 to 1961", "C": "1952 to 1957", "D": "1961 to 1966"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Choose option B: india''s Second Five-Year Plan ran 1956–1961 under Mahalanobis heavy-industry strategy. 1950–55 was the First Plan; 1952–57 overlaps First/early Second; 1961–66 opens the Third Plan. Distractors A (1950 to 1955), C (1952 to 1957), D (1961 to 1966) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Economic Planning & Five Year Plans"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23185, 'Economic Planning & Five Year Plans', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'In which year was the Fourth Five Year Plan started?', '{"A": "1974", "B": "1966", "C": "1969", "D": "1970"}'::jsonb, 'C', '"1969" is the fact the question is pointing at. India''s Five Year Plans (1951–2017) ran from the First (1951–56) under Nehru to the Twelfth (2012–17); post-2017 planning shifted to three-year action agendas under NITI Aayog. MPSC''s editorial habit for this topic is to test the same fact in two-year cycles, so seeing this once is often enough to catch it again.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Economic Planning & Five Year Plans"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23186, 'Minerals & Industries', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'River Ganga enters the plains at', '{"A": "Rudraprayag", "B": "Rishikesh", "C": "Allahabad", "D": "Garhwal"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The Ganga debouches onto the plains at Rishikesh/Haridwar where the Himalayan gradient flattens. Rudraprayag is a headstream confluence; Allahabad is mid-plain; Garhwal is a region not a single entry point.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Minerals & Industries"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23187, 'Economic Planning & Five Year Plans', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Who is the Chairman of State Planning Commission?', '{"A": "Governor", "B": "Chief Minister", "C": "Finance Minister", "D": "Planning Minister"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The correct answer is option B — in states with a Planning Commission/Planning Board, the Chief Minister traditionally chairs it—integrating plan formulation with executive authority. Governor is constitutional head; Finance/Planning ministers assist but do not chair. You can eliminate A (Governor), C (Finance Minister), D (Planning Minister) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option B. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Economic Planning & Five Year Plans"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23188, 'Economic Planning & Five Year Plans', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'The Second Five Year Plan could not be implemented fully because of the', '{"A": "acute shortage of food grains", "B": "acute shortage of foreign exchange", "C": "over expenditure on war", "D": "political crisis"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B works here because the Second Plan''s import-substituting industrial push strained foreign exchange—war with China/Pakistan and drought compounded the balance-of-payments crisis, forcing curtailment. Food shortage was real but the correct bottleneck is forex. Distractors A (acute shortage of food grains), C (over expenditure on war), D (political crisis) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Economic Planning & Five Year Plans"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23189, 'Constitutional Framework & Preamble', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'When was the first meeting of the Constituent Assembly held in India?', '{"A": "8th December, 1946", "B": "9th December, 1946", "C": "15th December, 1946", "D": "15th August, 1947"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified pick here is 9th December, 1946. The Constituent Assembly first met on 9 December 1946; it adopted the Constitution on 26 November 1949 (Constitution Day) and it came into force on 26 January 1950. Note that the wrong options carry closely related terminology; a five-second sanity check against the stem is enough to eliminate them.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Constitutional Framework & Preamble"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23190, 'Economic Planning & Five Year Plans', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'The formation of Damodar Valley Project is the result of ________ Five Year Plan.', '{"A": "First", "B": "Second", "C": "Third", "D": "Fifth"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Correct: option A — "First". India''s Five Year Plans (1951–2017) ran from the First (1951–56) under Nehru to the Twelfth (2012–17); post-2017 planning shifted to three-year action agendas under NITI Aayog. Options like this one recur in MPSC papers with only the option-order shuffled, so recognising the anchor phrase in the stem is what carries the mark.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Economic Planning & Five Year Plans"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23191, 'Constitutional Development (British Acts)', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'How many Justices are there in the Supreme Court of India including the Chief Justice?', '{"A": "25", "B": "26", "C": "27", "D": "17"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B is the right choice since as of the 2011 exam frame, Supreme Court strength was sanctioned at 26 judges including the CJI (post-2009 expansion). 25/27/17 reflect earlier benches or partial headcounts. You can eliminate A (25), C (27), D (17) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option B. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Constitutional Development (British Acts)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23192, 'Constitutional Development (British Acts)', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'If any Central Minister doesn''t offer his resignation despite the directions of the Prime Minister, then', '{"A": "the President can dismiss him", "B": "the Prime Minister can dismiss him", "C": "the Prime Minister may resign", "D": "the Lok Sabha will pass resolution against him/her"}'::jsonb, 'A', '"the President can dismiss him" is what the question is looking for. The Prime Minister of India, appointed by the President under Article 75, is the head of government and leader of the majority in the Lok Sabha. For MPSC prelims, one line of revision is enough to lock this fact into memory — add it to your one-page factual notebook.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Constitutional Development (British Acts)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23193, 'Parliament', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'What is federal form of government?', '{"A": "There is centralisation of power", "B": "There is decentralisation of power", "C": "There is only one central government", "D": "There are only provincial governments"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B matches the question because Federalism implies division and decentralisation of power between Union and States—not centralisation (A/C) or provinces-only (D). India''s quasi-federal Constitution still embeds a strong Centre with state lists. Distractors A (There is centralisation of power), C (There is only one central government), D (There are only provincial governments) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Parliament"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23194, 'Judiciary', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Who was nominated as Vice-President of the Constituent Assembly in its first session?', '{"A": "K. Santhanam", "B": "Abul Kalam Azad", "C": "John Matthai", "D": "Frank Anthony"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'This resolves to Frank Anthony. The Constituent Assembly first met on 9 December 1946; it adopted the Constitution on 26 November 1949 (Constitution Day) and it came into force on 26 January 1950. The examiner rewards precision on this item — every option is engineered to feel plausible, but only the marked one matches the exact wording of the source document.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Judiciary"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23195, 'Union Executive', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Which State in India has its own separate Constitution?', '{"A": "Jammu and Kashmir", "B": "Maharashtra", "C": "Bihar", "D": "Andhra Pradesh"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A is correct because Jammu & Kashmir (pre-2019 framework) alone had a separate constitution under Article 370—distinct from the single Indian Constitution applying elsewhere. No other state listed carries a parallel constitutional document. You can eliminate B (Maharashtra), C (Bihar), D (Andhra Pradesh) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Union Executive"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23196, 'State Government', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'How many languages are constitutionally approved in India?', '{"A": "14", "B": "18", "C": "20", "D": "22"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D is the right choice since the Eighth Schedule lists 22 official languages (post-2004 Bodo/Dogri/Maithili/Santhali additions to the 18 baseline). 14/18/20 are pre-amendment counts. Distractors A (14), B (18), C (20) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","State Government"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23197, 'State Government', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, '________ was the President of the Constituent Assembly of India.', '{"A": "Dr. Babasaheb Ambedkar", "B": "Vallabhbhai Patel", "C": "Dr. Rajendra Prasad", "D": "Pt. Nehru"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The answer is option C: Dr Rajendra Prasad was elected permanent President of the Constituent Assembly—presiding over drafting and signing. Ambedkar chaired the Drafting Committee; Patel/Nehru were executive deputies, not CA president. Distractors A (Dr. Babasaheb Ambedkar), B (Vallabhbhai Patel), D (Pt. Nehru) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","State Government"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23198, 'Constitutional Development (British Acts)', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'The total number of talukas in Maharashtra is ________.', '{"A": "350", "B": "355", "C": "351", "D": "357"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Maharashtra had 357 talukas/tehsils in the administrative count referenced in 2011 papers (pre-2014 reorganisations). 350/351/355 are stale or rounded figures.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Constitutional Development (British Acts)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23199, 'Maharashtra Districts & Administration', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'How many members of the Vidhan Parishad are elected from teachers'' constituency?', '{"A": "1/2", "B": "1/4", "C": "1/12", "D": "1/3"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Maharashtra Legislative Council: teachers'' graduates constituency elects 1/12 of MLC strength (similar pattern for local bodies and graduates). Halves/quarters/thirds belong to other reserved categories.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Maharashtra Districts & Administration"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23200, 'Economic Planning & Five Year Plans', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'For how many maximum days can the Rajya Sabha keep the Money Bill?', '{"A": "7", "B": "15", "C": "16", "D": "14"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The answer is option D: article 109: Rajya Sabha may withhold a Money Bill for at most 14 days—return with or without recommendations; Lok Sabha may ignore suggestions. Seven/fifteen/sixteen confuse with other bicameral deadlines. You can eliminate A (7), B (15), C (16) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option D. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Economic Planning & Five Year Plans"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (23201, 'Constitutional Framework & Preamble', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'To whom is the Governor responsible?', '{"A": "The Chief Minister", "B": "The Home Minister", "C": "The Prime Minister", "D": "The President of India"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Governors are appointed by and hold office during the pleasure of the President (Article 156)—not the CM, Home Minister, or PM directly, though Centre coordinates through Union Home ministry.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Constitutional Framework & Preamble"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23202, 'Post-Independence India', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, '________ can use his powers on the advice of the Chief Minister and the Council of Ministers.', '{"A": "President", "B": "Prime Minister", "C": "Governor", "D": "The Chief Justice"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C is correct because article 163: Governor exercises most powers on the aid and advice of the CM and Council of Ministers—real executive authority rests with the elected state government. Distractors A (President), B (Prime Minister), D (The Chief Justice) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Post-Independence India"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23203, 'State Government', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Who selects the Gramsevaks?', '{"A": "Panchayat Samiti", "B": "Gram Panchayat", "C": "State Government", "D": "District Selection Board"}'::jsonb, 'D', '"District Selection Board" is what the question is looking for. The safest way to lock this item into recall is to write the correct option next to its associated year or body in your revision notebook and skim it weekly.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","State Government"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23204, 'Panchayati Raj', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Who can sanction the loan to Gram Panchayats?', '{"A": "State Government", "B": "Collector", "C": "Zilla Parishad", "D": "Panchayat Samiti"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Choose option C: Zilla Parishad may sanction loans to Gram Panchayats for approved schemes—financial oversight at district tier. State government sets policy; Collector executes revenue; Panchayat Samiti is block level. Distractors A (State Government), B (Collector), D (Panchayat Samiti) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Panchayati Raj"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23205, 'Panchayati Raj', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Which is the final decision-making authority regarding the development of a village?', '{"A": "Gram Panchayat", "B": "Gramsevak", "C": "Sarpanch", "D": "Gram Sabha"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The correct answer is option D — Gram Sabha (all registered voters in the village) is the supreme body approving plans and social audit—final say on village development. Sarpanch/Gramsevak execute; Gram Panchayat is the elected council. You can eliminate A (Gram Panchayat), B (Gramsevak), C (Sarpanch) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option D. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Panchayati Raj"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23206, 'State Government', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, '________ became the 25th state in India.', '{"A": "Goa", "B": "Mizoram", "C": "Sikkim", "D": "Jharkhand"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A works here because Goa became India''s 25th state on 30 May 1987 (after UT status post-1961 liberation). Mizoram/Sikkim/Jharkhand became states later (26th–28th sequence). You can eliminate B (Mizoram), C (Sikkim), D (Jharkhand) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","State Government"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23207, 'Panchayati Raj', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Zilla Parishad was started in Maharashtra in the year', '{"A": "1960", "B": "1950", "C": "1947", "D": "1924"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Three-tier Panchayat Raj with Zilla Parishads was implemented in Maharashtra from 1 May 1960 (state formation) under Bombay Panchayat Act extensions—not 1924 (local-board era) or 1947.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Panchayati Raj"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23208, 'Panchayati Raj', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Which movie received the Oscar Award in the Best Movie category in 2010?', '{"A": "The Hurt Locker", "B": "An Education", "C": "Inglorious Basterds", "D": "The Secret in Their Eyes"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The Hurt Locker is the correct option here. The year 2010 anchors this question — the correct option is the fact that dates to that year. The three wrong options are the standard distractor set MPSC uses for this topic — one is a chronological neighbour, one is a thematic near-miss and one is a plausible-sounding invention.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Panchayati Raj"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23209, 'Awards & Honours', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Who was the coach of the Indian Hockey team in 2010?', '{"A": "Flourisan Fuex", "B": "Jose Brasa", "C": "Lombi", "D": "Benzamin Base"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Jose Brasa of Spain coached the Indian men''s hockey team around the 2010 World Cup/ Commonwealth cycle—replacing earlier foreign coaches. Florisan/Lombi/Benzamin are OCR variants of other staff names in the paper.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Awards & Honours"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23210, 'Panchayati Raj', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'How many members can be in the Zilla Parishad?', '{"A": "50 to 75", "B": "60 to 75", "C": "20 to 75", "D": "35 to 75"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A matches the question because Zilla Parishad composition is prescribed roughly 50–75 elected members depending on district population—statutory band in Maharashtra ZP Acts. Wider 20–75 or 35–75 bands misquote the lower limit. You can eliminate B (60 to 75), C (20 to 75), D (35 to 75) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Panchayati Raj"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23211, 'Sports', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'What will be number of the amendment in the Constitution of India for women''s reservation?', '{"A": "104th", "B": "108th", "C": "107th", "D": "106th"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The answer is option B: Women''s Reservation Bill was introduced as the Constitution (108th Amendment) Bill in the Lok Sabha—33% reservation in legislatures. 104th/106th/107th covered GST, OBC lists, and other subjects. You can eliminate A (104th), C (107th), D (106th) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option B. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Sports"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23212, 'Constitutional Amendments', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'The autobiography ''Prakashwata'' is by the following famous personality:', '{"A": "Dr. Prakash Amte", "B": "Dr. Anil Awachat", "C": "Dr. Raghunath Mashelkar", "D": "Madhav Kanitkar"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A matches the question because Dr Prakash Amte''s autobiography ''Prakashwata'' chronicles Lok Biradari tribal health work in Gadchiroli (following Baba Amte''s legacy). Awachat/Mashelkar/Kanitkar wrote on social issues/science elsewhere. Distractors B (Dr. Anil Awachat), C (Dr. Raghunath Mashelkar), D (Madhav Kanitkar) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Constitutional Amendments"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23213, 'National Appointments & Reports', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'The name Soumya Swaminathan is related to', '{"A": "Tennis", "B": "Chess", "C": "Trekking", "D": "Marathon"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The examination key marks Chess as the correct choice. The three wrong options are the standard distractor set MPSC uses for this topic — one is a chronological neighbour, one is a thematic near-miss and one is a plausible-sounding invention.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","National Appointments & Reports"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23214, 'Persons in News & Books', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Which power project is being constructed at Madban near Jaitapur?', '{"A": "Tidal energy", "B": "Nuclear energy", "C": "Hydro-electric power", "D": "Windmill"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Jaitapur (Madban site, Ratnagiri) is planned for French EPR nuclear reactors—6000+ MW coastal project announced in late 2000s. Tidal/hydro/wind were not the Jaitapur technology choice.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Persons in News & Books"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23215, 'Persons in News & Books', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Rangarajan Committee is related to', '{"A": "National Savings and Investment", "B": "Gujarat Riots", "C": "Mumbai Attack", "D": "Rajiv Gandhi Assassination"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'C Rangarajan chaired the high-level committee on household savings and investment patterns in India (post-2008 financial sector review)—not riot/attack/assassination commissions bearing his name.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Persons in News & Books"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23216, 'Money & Banking', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Which is the largest Public Sector Bank in India?', '{"A": "Reserve Bank of India", "B": "State Bank of India", "C": "Bank of India", "D": "Canara Bank"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The answer is option B: State Bank of India is the largest public-sector commercial bank by assets and branch network. RBI is the central bank, not a PSB; BOI/Canara are smaller PSBs. Distractors A (Reserve Bank of India), C (Bank of India), D (Canara Bank) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Money & Banking"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23217, 'Persons in News & Books', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'In which district are Dr. Abhay Bang and Dr. Rani Bang working to improve the health conditions of tribals?', '{"A": "Nandurbar", "B": "Thane", "C": "Gadchiroli", "D": "Yeotmal"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Choose option C: Dr Abhay and Dr Rani Bang run the Society for Education, Action and Research in Community Health (SEARCH) among Madia-Gond tribals in Gadchiroli—community-based maternal/child mortality reduction. You can eliminate A (Nandurbar), B (Thane), D (Yeotmal) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option C. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Persons in News & Books"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23218, 'Industry, Trade & Reforms', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Which one of the following places is famous for production of railway coaches?', '{"A": "Nashik", "B": "Kapurthala", "C": "Kanpur", "D": "Kochi"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Rail Coach Factory at Kapurthala (Punjab) produces passenger coaches for Indian Railways. Integral Coach Factory is Chennai; Diesel Loco Works Varanasi; Nashik/Kanpur/Kochi are other industrial nodes.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Industry, Trade & Reforms"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23219, 'Government Schemes & Yojanas', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Which is the correct pair in terms of the Agricultural University and its location?', '{"A": "Marathwada Agricultural University – Rahuri", "B": "Dr. Panjabrao Deshmukh Agricultural University – Akola", "C": "Dr. Babasaheb Ambedkar Agricultural University – Parbhani", "D": "Mahatma Phule Agricultural University – Dapoli"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B is the right choice since Dr Panjabrao Deshmukh Krishi Vidyapeeth is headquartered at Akola (Vidarbha). Rahuri hosts MPKV; Parbhani has Vasantrao Naik Marathwada Agri University; Dapoli is Dr Balasaheb Sawant Konkan Krishi Vidyapeeth. Distractors A (Marathwada Agricultural University – Ra…), C (Dr. Babasaheb Ambedkar Agricultural Uni…), D (Mahatma Phule Agricultural University –…) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Government Schemes & Yojanas"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23220, 'Persons in News & Books', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'For which party has freedom fighter Ahilyabai Rangnekar worked?', '{"A": "Communist Marxist", "B": "Samajwadi Party", "C": "Congress", "D": "Janata Party"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The correct answer is option A — Freedom fighter Ahilyabai Rangnekar was active in the Communist Party of India (Marxist) stream in Maharashtra labour/peasant politics—not Congress/Janata/Samajwadi affiliations. Distractors B (Samajwadi Party), C (Congress), D (Janata Party) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Persons in News & Books"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23221, 'Government Schemes & Yojanas', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Which scheme has the Government of Maharashtra decided to implement from February 2011?', '{"A": "Nirmal Swarajya Mohim", "B": "Swarnjayanti Gram Swarozgar Yojana", "C": "Yashwant Gram Samriddhi Yojana", "D": "M. Gandhi Rozgar Yojana"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A is correct because Maharashtra launched ''Nirmal Swarajya Mohim'' (clean governance/sanitation drive) from February 2011—state branding distinct from central SGSY/MGNREGA schemes listed as distractors. You can eliminate B (Swarnjayanti Gram Swarozgar Yojana), C (Yashwant Gram Samriddhi Yojana), D (M. Gandhi Rozgar Yojana) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Government Schemes & Yojanas"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23222, 'Art, Literature & Culture', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Where was the A.I. Marathi Literary Conference 2010 held?', '{"A": "Sangli", "B": "Mumbai", "C": "U.S.A.", "D": "Thane"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'You want Thane on this one. The year 2010 anchors this question — the correct option is the fact that dates to that year. MPSC''s editorial habit for this topic is to test the same fact in two-year cycles, so seeing this once is often enough to catch it again.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Art, Literature & Culture"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23223, 'Government Schemes & Yojanas', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Dhanalaxmi Scheme for Girl Child was started in March 2008. a. It was initially launched in 7 states. b. The girl child gets upto 2 lakh rupees.', '{"A": "a and b both are correct", "B": "a is correct and b is wrong", "C": "a and b are incorrect", "D": "a is wrong and b is correct"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A works here because Dhanalaxmi girl-child scheme (2008) piloted in seven states with insurance/savings benefits scaling up to ₹2 lakh maturity—both statements (a) and (b) match RBI/Ministry notifications of the launch year. You can eliminate B (a is correct and b is wrong), C (a and b are incorrect), D (a is wrong and b is correct) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Government Schemes & Yojanas"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23224, 'Persons in News & Books', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, '________ is the inventor of ''Jaipur Foot''.', '{"A": "Dr. Pramod Karan Sethi", "B": "Dr. M. Khalilullah", "C": "Dr. V. Swaminathan", "D": "Dr. P.K. Banerjee"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Orthopaedic surgeon Dr Pramod Karan Sethi co-developed the Jaipur Foot prosthesis with artisan Ram Chander Sharma—low-cost mobility device from SMS Medical College/Jaipur.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Persons in News & Books"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23225, 'Constitutional Amendments', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Which Constitutional Amendment provides for Free and Compulsory Primary Education for the children aged between 6 to 14 years?', '{"A": "42nd Amendment", "B": "73rd Amendment", "C": "86th Amendment", "D": "91st Amendment"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The exam key confirms "86th Amendment". The 86th Amendment (2002) inserted Article 21A making free and compulsory education a fundamental right for children 6–14, along with Article 45 and 51A(k). Note that the wrong options carry closely related terminology; a five-second sanity check against the stem is enough to eliminate them.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Constitutional Amendments"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23226, 'Economic Planning & Five Year Plans', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Which of the following is not an objective of India''s economic planning?', '{"A": "Population growth", "B": "Industrial growth", "C": "Self-reliance", "D": "Employment generation"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A matches the question because Planning objectives target growth, self-reliance, employment, equity—not raw population growth, which planners seek to stabilise via family welfare. Choosing industrial growth/self-reliance/employment states the obvious aims. You can eliminate B (Industrial growth), C (Self-reliance), D (Employment generation) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option A. If the question asks what is incorrect, identify the false statement first and then match it to the answer choice.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Economic Planning & Five Year Plans"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23227, 'Awards & Honours', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, '"Oscar Award" is given for the excellence in the field of', '{"A": "Films", "B": "Literature", "C": "Sports", "D": "Politics"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Choose option A: academy Awards (Oscars) recognise excellence in cinema—films/technical crafts. Literature has Nobel/Booker; sports have Olympics/Arjuna; politics has no Oscar parallel. Distractors B (Literature), C (Sports), D (Politics) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Awards & Honours"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23228, 'Art, Literature & Culture', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Match the columns: a. Pandit Ravi Shankar - (i) Tabla; b. Zakir Hussain - (ii) Sarod; c. Amjad Ali Khan - (iii) Sitar; d. Hari Prasad Chaurasia - (iv) Flute', '{"A": "a-iv, b-i, c-ii, d-iii", "B": "a-iii, b-i, c-ii, d-iv", "C": "a-ii, b-iii, c-i, d-iv", "D": "a-iii, b-i, c-iv, d-ii"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Instrument pairings: Pandit Ravi Shankar–sitar (iii); Ustad Zakir Hussain–tabla (i); Ustad Amjad Ali Khan–sarod (ii); Pandit Hariprasad Chaurasia–bansuri/flute (iv). Grid B: a-iii, b-i, c-ii, d-iv. Swapping sarod/sitar or flute/sitar breaks Hindustani iconography.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Art, Literature & Culture"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23229, 'International Affairs & Summits', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'The 15th SAARC Summit of August 2008 was held at', '{"A": "New Delhi", "B": "Colombo", "C": "Kathmandu", "D": "Islamabad"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Answer: Colombo. The year 2008 anchors this question — the correct option is the fact that dates to that year. Add this correct option to your active-recall flashcard deck; MPSC repeats the underlying fact in some form every two to three prelim cycles.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","International Affairs & Summits"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23230, 'Defence & Security', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Which of the following missiles was test-fired from the launch site in Orissa in March 2008?', '{"A": "Agni-I", "B": "Agni-II", "C": "Agni-III", "D": "Prithvi"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Reading the stem carefully, the answer is Agni-I. The year 2008 anchors this question — the correct option is the fact that dates to that year. The three incorrect options are close-sounding distractors; anchoring on the exact keyword in the stem eliminates them in seconds.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Defence & Security"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23231, 'Art, Literature & Culture', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Which gharana of Indian music is represented by Pandit Bhimsen Joshi?', '{"A": "Dagar", "B": "Kirana", "C": "Jaipur", "D": "Carnatic"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The answer is option B: Pandit Bhimsen Joshi was the towering Kirana gharana vocalist—Abdul Karim Khan/Barkat Ali Khan lineage through Sawai Gandharva. Dagar is dhrupad; Jaipur-Atrauli is another khayal school; Carnatic is South Indian. You can eliminate A (Dagar), C (Jaipur), D (Carnatic) — each one conflicts with the principle or calculation that leads to option B. Store the reasoning behind the answer, not just the letter, because topic packs revisit the same idea in different forms.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Art, Literature & Culture"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23232, 'Persons in News & Books', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Kavi Kulguru Kalidas Sanskrit University is located at', '{"A": "Sewagram", "B": "Sangamner", "C": "Wai", "D": "Ramtek"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D matches the question because Kavi Kulguru Kalidas Sanskrit University is established at Ramtek (Nagpur district)—Maharashtra''s dedicated Sanskrit university named after the classical poet. Sewagram/Sangamner/Wai host other institutions without this university charter. Distractors A (Sewagram), B (Sangamner), C (Wai) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. Keep the name, formula, and unit together in your notes — that helps you spot incomplete distractors quickly.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Persons in News & Books"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23233, 'Mensuration & Geometry', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'एका शंकूची त्रिज्या 20% ने कमी केली व उंची 50% ने वाढविली. तर त्याच्या आकारमानात होणारा बदल', '{"A": "4% घट", "B": "4% वाढ", "C": "20% वाढ", "D": "20% घट"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Radius down 20% → 0.8r (area factor 0.64); height up 50% → 1.5h. Net multiplier 0.64 × 1.5 = 0.96, i.e. a 4% volume decrease. Treating फक्त radius or फक्त height in isolation lands on the 20% चुकीचे पर्याय पर्याय B (4% वाढ) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (20% वाढ) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D (20% घट) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Mensuration & Geometry"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23234, 'Algebra & Equations', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, '√2, √8, √18, √32 ... या अंकगणिती श्रेणीकरिता S₁₀ = ...', '{"A": "55√2", "B": "5√2", "C": "20", "D": "10√2"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'पर्याय A (55√2) — श्रेणी √2, √8, √18, √32 simplify — √2, 2√2, 3√2, 4√2 … AP common difference √2 पर्याय B (5√2) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (20) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; पर्याय D (10√2) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Algebra & Equations"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23235, 'Percentage, Profit & Loss', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'एका वस्तूची किंमत ₹ 5000 आहे. जर त्यावस्तूवर 12% सूट मिळाल्यास त्या वस्तूची किंमत ________ होईल.', '{"A": "₹ 4400", "B": "₹ 4880", "C": "₹ 4940", "D": "₹ 4988"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'सोडवत गेल्यास. म्हणून पर्याय A (₹4400) पर्याय B (₹ 4880) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (₹ 4940) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही; पर्याय D (₹ 4988) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Percentage, Profit & Loss"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23236, 'Industry, Trade & Reforms', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'Where is Tata Motors Nano Car Project in Gujarat located?', '{"A": "Rajkot", "B": "Anand", "C": "Sanand", "D": "Baroda"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C works here because Tata Nano plant relocated to Sanand (Ahmedabad district, Gujarat) after Singur agitation—announced 2008, production from 2010. Rajkot/Anand/Baroda were speculation sites. Distractors A (Rajkot), B (Anand), D (Baroda) look plausible but do not follow from the facts stated in the question. MPSC papers often recycle this type of detail, so read the question carefully before you commit to an option.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Industry, Trade & Reforms"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23237, 'Simple & Compound Interest', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'कर्ज घेतलेल्या एका रकमेची दोन समान वार्षिक हप्त्यात परत फेड केली. प्रत्येक हप्ता ₹ 4704 होता. जर चक्रवाढ व्याजाचा दर 12% असेल तर कर्ज घेतलेली रक्कम =', '{"A": "₹ 7500", "B": "₹ 8500", "C": "₹ 7000", "D": "₹ 7950"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'पर्याय D (₹ 7950) — सोडवत गेल्यास — two equal annual instalments 12% p.a. present value: P = 4704/1.12 + 4704/1.12² = 4200 + 3750 = ₹7950 पर्याय A (₹ 7500) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B (₹ 8500) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही; पर्याय C (₹ 7000) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Simple & Compound Interest"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23238, 'Algebra & Equations', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'एका तीन अंकी संख्येतील शतम स्थानाचा अंक व एकम स्थानाचा अंक यांची बेरीज ही दहम स्थानाच्या अंकापेक्षा 1 ने कमी आहे. ती संख्या अंकाच्या बेरजेच्या 17 पट आहे. त्या संख्येत 198 मिळविले असता संख्येतील अंकाचे क्रम उलट होतात. तर ती मूळ संख्या कोणती?', '{"A": "351", "B": "153", "C": "135", "D": "151"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'गणितात हे सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय B येतो. पर्याय B (153) — सोडवत गेल्यास — number 100h+10t+u. Digit condition: h+u = t−1 पर्याय A (351) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर B (153) आहे; पर्याय C (135) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; पर्याय D (151) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे. पर्याय A (351) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; पर्याय C (135) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; पर्याय D (151) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Algebra & Equations"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23239, 'Time & Work', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'एका साधेपेय कारखान्यात एक यंत्र 840 बॉटल 6 तासात भरते. 5 तासात ते यंत्र किती बॉटल भरेल?', '{"A": "840", "B": "800", "C": "740", "D": "700"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'या प्रश्नात एका साधेपेय कारखान्यात एक यंत्र 840 बॉटल 6 तासात भरते। 5 तासात ते यंत… — पर्याय D (700) बरोबर आहे पर्याय A (840) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर D (700) आहे; पर्याय B (800) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर D (700) आहे; पर्याय C (740) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर D (700) आहे।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Time & Work"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23240, 'Ratio, Proportion & Averages', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'एका समितीतील 2/3 सदस्य स्त्रिया आहेत. पुरूष सदस्यांपैकी 1/4 विवाहित आहेत. पुरूषांपैकी 9 अविवाहित आहेत. तर त्या समितीतील सदस्यांची एकूण संख्या', '{"A": "48", "B": "27", "C": "36", "D": "42"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'या प्रश्नात एका समितीतील 2/3 सदस्य स्त्रिया आहेत. पुरूष सदस्यांपैकी 1/4 विवाहित आ… — पर्याय C (36) बरोबर आहे पर्याय A (48) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर C (36) आहे; पर्याय B (27) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर C (36) आहे; पर्याय D (42) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर C (36) आहे।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Ratio, Proportion & Averages"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23241, 'Mensuration & Geometry', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'एका गोलाचे वक्रपृष्ठफळ 314 सेमी² आहे. तर त्या गोलाचे घनफळ ________ सेमी³.', '{"A": "520", "B": "521", "C": "523⅓", "D": "522⅓"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'या प्रश्नात एका गोलाचे वक्रपृष्ठफळ 314 सेमी² आहे. तर त्या गोलाचे घनफळ ________ से… — पर्याय C (523⅓) बरोबर आहे पर्याय A (520) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर C (523⅓) आहे; पर्याय B (521) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर C (523⅓) आहे; पर्याय D (522⅓) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Mensuration & Geometry"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23242, 'Simple & Compound Interest', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'खुर्च्यांचा एक संच रोखीने ₹ 2000 ला मिळतो. किंवा हप्ता योजनेत ₹ 1200 सुरुवातीचा हप्ता भरून ₹ 860 सहा महिन्यानंतर एका हप्त्यांत भरावे लागतात. तर हप्त्याने घेण्याच्या व्यवहारातील व्याज आकारणीचा दर प्र.व. ________ असेल.', '{"A": "10%", "B": "12%", "C": "12.5%", "D": "15%"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'पर्याय D (15%) — सोडवत गेल्यास — श्रेय portion = ₹2000 − ₹1200 = ₹800 six months पर्याय A (10%) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर D (15%) आहे; पर्याय B (12%) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर D (15%) आहे; पर्याय C (12.5%) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर D (15%) आहे. पर्याय A (10%) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर D (15%) आहे; पर्याय B (12%) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; पर्याय C (12.5%) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Simple & Compound Interest"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23243, 'Number System & Simplification', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, '7/5 − (4/25)√24 याचे वर्गमूळ ________ आहे.', '{"A": "√8 − √3", "B": "(2/5)√8 − √3", "C": "(2/5)√8 − (1/5)√3", "D": "(1/5)√8 − (2/5)√3"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पर्याय C ((2/5)√8 − (1/5)√3) — Rationalising under the root: 7/5 − (4/25)√24 simplifies to a form (2/5)√8 − (1/5)√3 after combining like surds। अर्धवट extraction (options A/B/D) leave mismatched coefficients on √8 and √3 पर्याय A (√8 − √3) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B ((2/5)√8 − √3) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय D ((1/5)√8 − (2/5)√3) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Number System & Simplification"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23244, 'Mensuration & Geometry', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'जर एका नियमीत बहुकोनाचे बाहेरील कोनाचे माप 45° असल्यास त्या बहुकोनाला किती बाजू असतील?', '{"A": "4", "B": "5", "C": "6", "D": "8"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'पर्याय A (4) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर D (8) आहे; पर्याय B (5) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; पर्याय C (6) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे. पर्याय A (4) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; पर्याय B (5) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; पर्याय C (6) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Mensuration & Geometry"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23245, 'Number System & Simplification', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'जर आपण (20 − 5 × 2 + 3 − 18 ÷ 9) ला बरोबर सोडवू तर आपल्याला ________ हे उत्तर मिळते.', '{"A": "15/9", "B": "46/9", "C": "11", "D": "31"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'गणितात हे सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय C येतो. प्रश्नातील विधाने तपासल्यास पर्याय C बरोबर आहे। BODMAS: 20 − 5×2 + 3 − 18÷9 = 20 − 10 + 3 − 2 = 11. म्हणून पर्याय C पर्याय A (15/9) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय B (46/9) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही; पर्याय D (31) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Number System & Simplification"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23246, 'Algebra & Equations', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, '(69842 × 69842 − 30158 × 30158) / (69842 − 30158) ची किंमत किती?', '{"A": "69842", "B": "36684", "C": "30158", "D": "100000"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'सोडवत गेल्यास — identity (a²−b²)/(a−b) = a+b. a = 69842, b = 30158 — 100000 पर्याय A (69842) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर D (100000) आहे; पर्याय B (36684) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; पर्याय C (30158) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे. पर्याय A (69842) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; पर्याय B (36684) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; पर्याय C (30158) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Algebra & Equations"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23247, 'Number System & Simplification', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, '51 ते 70 संख्ये पर्यंत येणाऱ्या विषम संख्यांची बेरीज त्याच दरम्यान येणाऱ्या सम संख्यांच्या बेरजेपेक्षा कितीने कमी आहे?', '{"A": "9", "B": "10", "C": "11", "D": "12"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'गणितात हे सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय B येतो। Odd integers 51–69: 10 terms, sum = 10×60 = 600. Even 52–70: 10 terms, sum = 610 पर्याय A (9) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर B (10) आहे; पर्याय C (11) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; पर्याय D (12) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे. पर्याय A (9) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; पर्याय C (11) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; पर्याय D (12) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Number System & Simplification"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23248, 'Algebra & Equations', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'जर a > 0, b > 0 आणि c > 0 तर a + 1/(b + 1/c) = ...', '{"A": "(a + b)/(bc + 1)", "B": "(abc + a + c)/(bc + 1)", "C": "(abc + bc + 1)/(bc + 1)", "D": "(abc + b + c)/(bc + 1)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'पर्याय B ((abc + a + c)/(bc + 1)) — पर्याय A ((a + b)/(bc + 1)) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C ((abc + bc + 1)/(bc + 1)) /(bc + 1)) प्रश्नातील तथ्ये/गणना/व्याख्येशी विरोधाभासी आहे; पर्याय D ((abc + b + c)/(bc + 1)) /(bc + 1)) प्रश्नातील तथ्ये/गणना/व्याख्येशी विरोधाभासी आहे. पर्याय A ((a + b)/(bc + 1)) /(bc + 1)) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C ((abc + bc + 1)/(bc + 1)) /(bc + 1)) /(bc + 1)) प्रश्नातील तथ्ये/गणना/व्याख्येशी विरोधाभासी आहे; पर्याय D ((abc + b + c)/(bc + 1)) /(bc + 1)) /(bc + 1)) प्रश्नातील तथ्ये/गणना/व्याख्येशी विरोधाभासी आहे।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Algebra & Equations"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23249, 'Number System & Simplification', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'सरळरूप द्या: √2.25 × √0.4', '{"A": "1", "B": "0.3", "C": "2", "D": "2/3"}'::jsonb, 'A', '√2.25 × √0.4 = √(2.25 × 0.4) = √0.9 — source booklet intended simplification/rounding नुसार paper keys 1 पर्याय B (0.3) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर A (1) आहे; पर्याय C (2) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर A (1) आहे; पर्याय D (2/3) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही. पर्याय B (0.3) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; योग्य उत्तर A (1) आहे; पर्याय C (2) मध्ये चुकीची संख्या/टक्केवारी दिली आहे; पर्याय D (2/3) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Number System & Simplification"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (23250, 'Percentage, Profit & Loss', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2011, 'राम ने एक आलमारी 10% करासहील ₹ 3300 ला विकत घेतली. त्या आलमारीची कर लावण्यापूर्वीची किंमत किती?', '{"A": "₹ 2970", "B": "₹ 3000", "C": "₹ 3033", "D": "₹ 3267"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'सोडवत गेल्यास. म्हणून पर्याय B (₹3000) पर्याय A (₹ 2970) या प्रश्नात विचारलेल्या व्याख्या/तथ्याशी जुळत नाही; पर्याय C (₹ 3033) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही; पर्याय D (₹ 3267) या प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेशी सुसंगत नाही।', '{"Reasoning","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2011","Percentage, Profit & Loss"}'::text[], 'Medium')
