VALUES
  (25751, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'महाराष्ट्रातील ''बॉम्बे हाय'' तेलक्षेत्र मुंबई किनाऱ्यापासून किती अंतरावर आहे?', '{"A": "सुमारे ५० किमी वायव्येला", "B": "सुमारे ३०० किमी दक्षिणेला", "C": "सुमारे १०० किमी वायव्येला", "D": "सुमारे १७६ किमी वायव्येला"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'बरोबर पर्याय: D — "सुमारे १७६ किमी वायव्येला". हे नेमके तथ्य आधीही MPSC पूर्व परीक्षेत आले आहे — बरोबर पर्यायाची शब्दयोजना पाठ केल्यास दरवर्षी दोन-तीन सोपे गुण मिळतात.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25752, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'बॉम्बे हाय येथील खनिज तेल वाहून नेण्यासाठी कोणती पाईपलाईन वापरली जाते?', '{"A": "हार्बर रेल्वे", "B": "जयपूर-मुंबई पाईपलाईन", "C": "उरण पाईपलाईन", "D": "कोकण रेल्वे"}'::jsonb, 'C', '"उरण पाईपलाईन" हे उत्तर अधिकृत किल्लीत नोंदवले आहे. या प्रकारच्या प्रश्नात नियमित तथ्य-वाचन बुद्धिमान shortcut पेक्षा जास्त फळ देते — स्रोत एकदा नीट वाचणे हेच गुण मिळवण्याचे साधन आहे.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25753, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'रत्नागिरीत कोणत्या खनिजाचे साठे ''रिया'' किनारपट्टीच्या वाळूत सापडतात?', '{"A": "इल्मेनाईट व रुटाईल", "B": "जिप्सम आणि चुनखडी", "C": "चुनखडी आणि डोलोमाईट", "D": "सिलिका आणि फेल्सपार"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'योग्य पर्याय पर्याय A — "इल्मेनाईट व रुटाईल". अशा प्रकारचे प्रश्न MPSC मध्ये केवळ पर्यायांची फेरजुळवाणी करून पुन:पुन्हा येतात — प्रश्नातील मुख्य पदावर लक्ष केंद्रित करणे पुरेसे असते.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25754, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'सिंधुदुर्ग जिल्ह्यातील ''फोंडा'' आणि ''कणकवली'' येथे कोणते खनिज सापडते?', '{"A": "मँगनीज", "B": "टंगस्टन", "C": "क्रोमाईट", "D": "कायनाईट"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'प्रश्नाच्या रचनेप्रमाणे उत्तर मँगनीज येते. बरोबर पर्याय आपल्या active-recall flashcard सेटमध्ये जोडा; MPSC मूळ तथ्य दर दोन-तीन पूर्व परीक्षा चक्रात परत विचारते.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25755, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'सिंधुदुर्ग जिल्ह्यात ग्राफाइटचे साठे कोठे आढळण्याची शक्यता आहे?', '{"A": "अलिबाग", "B": "श्रीवर्धन", "C": "सावंतवाडी", "D": "चिपळूण"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'बरोबर पर्याय: C — "सावंतवाडी". मूळ तथ्य लहान व नेमके असल्यामुळे या प्रश्नाचे उत्तर पूर्णपणे स्मरणसाध्य आहे — घाईत प्रश्न वाचणे हाच फक्त धोका आहे.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25756, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'बॉक्साईट खनिजाचे साठे जांभा खडकाच्या कोणत्या थरात आढळतात?', '{"A": "बेसाल्टखालील थरात", "B": "मध्यम थरात", "C": "खालच्या थरात", "D": "वरच्या थरात"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'अपेक्षित उत्तर पर्याय D — वरच्या थरात. MPSC पूर्व परीक्षेसाठी हे तथ्य एका ओळीत नोंदवा — दीर्घकाळ लक्षात राहते.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25757, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'दक्षिण कोकणातील खनिज संपत्तीला कोणत्या रेल्वेचा सर्वाधिक फायदा झाला आहे?', '{"A": "उरण पाईपलाईन", "B": "मध्य रेल्वे", "C": "जयपूर-मुंबई पाईपलाईन", "D": "कोकण रेल्वे"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'अधिकृत उत्तरकिल्ली कोकण रेल्वे निवडते. जो हे उत्तर चुकवतो तो सहसा जवळपासच्या पर्यायावर जातो — प्रश्न दोनदा वाचून पर्याय तपासण्याची सवय हा उपाय आहे.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25758, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'सांगली जिल्ह्यातील कोणत्या तालुक्यात बॉक्साईटचे साठे आहेत?', '{"A": "समुद्रपूर", "B": "राधानगरी", "C": "शिराळा", "D": "मौदा"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'बरोबर पर्याय म्हणजे शिराळा. MPSC ची संपादकीय सवय अशी की हा विषय दर दोन वर्षांच्या चक्रात परत विचारला जातो, त्यामुळे तो एकदा पाहणे बरेचसे पुरेसे असते.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25759, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'कोल्हापूर जिल्ह्यातील ''उदगिरी'' आणि ''धनगरवाडी'' बॉक्साईट खाणी कोणत्या तालुक्यात आहेत?', '{"A": "लांजा", "B": "शाहूवाडी", "C": "कडेगाव", "D": "कामठी"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'बरोबर पर्याय म्हणजे शाहूवाडी. इतर पर्याय शब्दशैलीत सारखे दिसतात; प्रश्नाशी पाच सेकंदांची मानसिक तपासणी करून त्यांना बाद करता येते.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25760, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'कोकणातील नद्यांच्या मुखाशी कोणत्या प्रकारची वाळू मोठ्या प्रमाणावर मिळते?', '{"A": "सिलिका वाळू (Glass Sand)", "B": "किनारपट्टीची वाळू (Beach Sand)", "C": "बांधकामाची वाळू (रेती)", "D": "मातीची वाळू (Loam)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'प्रश्न विचारतो त्याप्रमाणे उत्तर बांधकामाची वाळू (रेती) येते. जो हे उत्तर चुकवतो तो सहसा जवळपासच्या पर्यायावर जातो — प्रश्न दोनदा वाचून पर्याय तपासण्याची सवय हा उपाय आहे.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25761, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, '''राधानगरी'' आणि ''चंदगड'' (कोल्हापूर) कशासाठी प्रसिद्ध आहेत?', '{"A": "अभ्रक", "B": "बॅराईट्स", "C": "दगडी कोळसा", "D": "बॉक्साईट"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'बरोबर उत्तर बॉक्साईट आहे (पर्याय D). हे उत्तर पक्के लक्षात ठेवण्यासाठी बरोबर पर्याय त्याच्याशी जोडलेल्या वर्षाच्या किंवा संस्थेच्या नावासोबत उजळणी वहीत लिहून आठवड्यातून एकदा तपासा.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25762, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'सातारा जिल्ह्यातील कोयना खोरे आणि ''महाबळेश्वर'' पठारावर कोणते खनिज आढळते?', '{"A": "फेल्सपार", "B": "लोहखनिज", "C": "बॉक्साईट", "D": "क्रोमाईट"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पूर्णपणे नक्की उत्तर बॉक्साईट आहे. कोयना नदी महाबळेश्वर येथे उगम पावते व कराड येथील प्रीती संगमावर कृष्णा नदीस मिळते; सातारा जिल्ह्यातील कोयना जलविद्युत प्रकल्प (~1,960 MW) महाराष्ट्रातील सर्वात मोठा जलविद्युत प्रकल्प आहे. इतर पर्याय शब्दशैलीत सारखे दिसतात; प्रश्नाशी पाच सेकंदांची मानसिक तपासणी करून त्यांना बाद करता येते.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25763, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, '''उन्हपदेव'' आणि ''सुनपदेव'' हे गरम पाण्याचे झरे कोणत्या जिल्ह्यात आहेत?', '{"A": "मुंबई", "B": "जळगाव", "C": "परभणी", "D": "नांदेड"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'उत्तर सापडते: जळगाव. अशा प्रकारचे प्रश्न MPSC मध्ये केवळ पर्यायांची फेरजुळवाणी करून पुन:पुन्हा येतात — प्रश्नातील मुख्य पदावर लक्ष केंद्रित करणे पुरेसे असते.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25764, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, '''बॅराईट्स'' (Barytes) खनिजाचे साठे कोल्हापूर जिल्ह्यात कोठे आढळतात?', '{"A": "भुदरगड", "B": "मौदा", "C": "रामटेक", "D": "खेड"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'पर्याय A — भुदरगड — हे इथे बरोबर उत्तर आहे. MPSC ची पद्धत — प्रश्नात एक निश्चित तथ्य ठेवायचे व तीन जवळचे भासणारे पर्याय ठेवायचे — तथ्याशी जुळणारा पर्याय नेहमीच बरोबर असतो.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25765, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'भूऔष्णिक ऊर्जेचे (Geothermal) साठे खान्देशात कोठे आढळतात?', '{"A": "चंद्रपूर", "B": "जळगाव", "C": "मुंबई", "D": "अकोला"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'अपेक्षित उत्तर पर्याय B — जळगाव. MPSC ची पद्धत — प्रश्नात एक निश्चित तथ्य ठेवायचे व तीन जवळचे भासणारे पर्याय ठेवायचे — तथ्याशी जुळणारा पर्याय नेहमीच बरोबर असतो.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25766, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'बेसाल्ट खडकामुळे पश्चिम महाराष्ट्रात कोणत्या खनिजाची कमतरता आहे?', '{"A": "धातू खनिजे (Metallic Minerals)", "B": "इमारत खनिजे (Building Minerals)", "C": "ऊर्जा खनिजे (Energy Minerals)", "D": "मौल्यवान खनिजे (Precious Minerals)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'या प्रश्नाचे उत्तर येते धातू खनिजे (Metallic Minerals). अशा प्रकारचे प्रश्न MPSC मध्ये केवळ पर्यायांची फेरजुळवाणी करून पुन:पुन्हा येतात — प्रश्नातील मुख्य पदावर लक्ष केंद्रित करणे पुरेसे असते.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25767, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'पश्चिम महाराष्ट्रात कोणत्या प्रकारचा खडक सर्वाधिक आढळतो?', '{"A": "विंध्यन खडक", "B": "बेसाल्ट खडक", "C": "जांभा खडक", "D": "टॅकोनाईट खडक"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'योग्य पर्याय पर्याय B — "बेसाल्ट खडक". हा MPSC चा ठराविक ''anchor-word'' प्रश्न आहे — प्रश्नात असलेला एक निश्चित शब्द (व्यक्तीचे नाव, तारीख, कलम) थेट एका पर्यायाशी जुळतो.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25768, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'MSMC चे मुख्यालय कोठे आहे?', '{"A": "नाशिक", "B": "रत्नागिरी", "C": "धाराशिव", "D": "नागपूर"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'योग्य उत्तर आहे नागपूर. MPSC PYQ विश्लेषणात या प्रकारचे प्रश्न ''चुकून वाचल्यामुळे गमावलेले सोपे मार्क'' यांचा सर्वात मोठा गट बनवतात — प्रश्न सावकाश वाचा व पर्याय स्पष्ट होतो.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25769, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'महाराष्ट्राच्या एकूण महसुलात खनिज क्षेत्राचा वाटा साधारण किती टक्के असतो?', '{"A": "२ ते ३ टक्के", "B": "७ ते ८ टक्के", "C": "४ ते ५ टक्के", "D": "१० ते १२ टक्के"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'प्रश्नाची अपेक्षा ४ ते ५ टक्के या पर्यायात पूर्ण होते. तीन चुकीचे पर्याय हे MPSC च्या या विषयासाठीच्या ठराविक distractor संचातून येतात — एक कालक्रमानुसार जवळचा, एक विषयानुसार जवळचा व एक जवळचा-दिसणारा invented.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25770, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'महाराष्ट्र राज्य खनिकर्म महामंडळ (MSMC) ची स्थापना कोणत्या वर्षी झाली?', '{"A": "१९७१", "B": "१९६०", "C": "१९८५", "D": "१९७३"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'बरोबर उत्तर १९७३ आहे (पर्याय D). तीन चुकीचे पर्याय हे MPSC च्या या विषयासाठीच्या ठराविक distractor संचातून येतात — एक कालक्रमानुसार जवळचा, एक विषयानुसार जवळचा व एक जवळचा-दिसणारा invented.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25771, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'इंडियन ब्युरो ऑफ माईन्स (IBM) चे विभागीय कार्यालय महाराष्ट्रात कोठे आहे?', '{"A": "पुणे", "B": "नांदेड", "C": "नागपूर", "D": "कोल्हापूर"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'प्रश्न ज्या तथ्याकडे इशारा करतो ते म्हणजे "नागपूर". परीक्षकाने या प्रश्नात अचूकतेला बक्षीस दिले आहे — प्रत्येक पर्याय plausible वाटावा असा असतो, पण अधिकृत स्रोताच्या शब्दयोजनेशी फक्त निवडलेला पर्याय जुळतो.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25772, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'महाराष्ट्रात एकूण किती जिल्ह्यांमध्ये खनिजांचे व्यावसायिक उत्खनन होते?', '{"A": "१८ ते २० जिल्हे", "B": "२० ते २५ जिल्हे", "C": "८ ते ९ जिल्हे", "D": "११ ते १२ जिल्हे"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'प्रश्नाची अपेक्षा ११ ते १२ जिल्हे या पर्यायात पूर्ण होते. MPSC PYQ विश्लेषणात या प्रकारचे प्रश्न ''चुकून वाचल्यामुळे गमावलेले सोपे मार्क'' यांचा सर्वात मोठा गट बनवतात — प्रश्न सावकाश वाचा व पर्याय स्पष्ट होतो.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25773, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'पुणे आणि अहमदनगर जिल्ह्यात बांधकामासाठी कोणता दगड सर्वाधिक वापरला जातो?', '{"A": "जांभा दगड (Laterite)", "B": "ग्रॅनाईट दगड", "C": "काळा बेसाल्ट दगड", "D": "वालुकाश्म (Sandstone)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पर्याय C — काळा बेसाल्ट दगड — हे इथे बरोबर उत्तर आहे. अधिकारी स्तरावरील उमेदवार इथे अती-विचाराने मार्क गमावतात; प्रश्नातील तथ्याशी शब्दशः जुळणारा पर्याय हाच योग्य आहे.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25774, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'महाराष्ट्रातील कोणत्या प्रशासकीय विभागात खनिजांचे साठे सर्वात कमी आहेत?', '{"A": "नागपूर व अमरावती विभाग", "B": "कोकण व मुंबई विभाग", "C": "पुणे व कोकण विभाग", "D": "पुणे व नाशिक विभाग"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'सरळ उत्तर: पुणे व नाशिक विभाग. MPSC पूर्व परीक्षेसाठी हे तथ्य एका ओळीत नोंदवा — दीर्घकाळ लक्षात राहते.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25775, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, '''खनिज विकास निधी'' प्रामुख्याने कोणत्या कामासाठी वापरला जातो?', '{"A": "एक्स-रे ट्यूबसाठी", "B": "खाणग्रस्त भागाच्या पुनर्वसनासाठी", "C": "टेलिफोनच्या तारांसाठी", "D": "गाडीच्या स्पार्क प्लगसाठी"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'मूळ प्रश्नपत्रिकेचे अधिकृत उत्तर खाणग्रस्त भागाच्या पुनर्वसनासाठी. मूळ तथ्य लहान व नेमके असल्यामुळे या प्रश्नाचे उत्तर पूर्णपणे स्मरणसाध्य आहे — घाईत प्रश्न वाचणे हाच फक्त धोका आहे.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25776, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'खनिजांवर आधारित सर्वाधिक उद्योग महाराष्ट्रातील कोणत्या जिल्ह्यात आहेत?', '{"A": "कोल्हापूर व सातारा", "B": "नागपूर व चंद्रपूर", "C": "पुणे व नाशिक", "D": "अमरावती व अकोला"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'प्रश्न ज्या तथ्याकडे इशारा करतो ते म्हणजे "नागपूर व चंद्रपूर". चंद्रपूर सुपर थर्मल पॉवर स्टेशन (3,340 MW, महाजेनको) महाराष्ट्रातील सर्वात मोठे औष्णिक विद्युत केंद्र आहे. MPSC PYQ विश्लेषणात या प्रकारचे प्रश्न ''चुकून वाचल्यामुळे गमावलेले सोपे मार्क'' यांचा सर्वात मोठा गट बनवतात — प्रश्न सावकाश वाचा व पर्याय स्पष्ट होतो.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25777, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'राज्याच्या एकूण वीजनिर्मितीपैकी किती टक्के वीज कोळशावर आधारित औष्णिक प्रकल्पातून मिळते?', '{"A": "१५%", "B": "सुमारे ७०%", "C": "४०%", "D": "४%"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'प्रश्नाच्या मुख्य संकल्पनेप्रमाणे उत्तर सुमारे ७०%. इतर पर्याय शब्दशैलीत सारखे दिसतात; प्रश्नाशी पाच सेकंदांची मानसिक तपासणी करून त्यांना बाद करता येते.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25778, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'लोह-पोलाद उद्योगात ''फ्लक्स'' (Flux) म्हणून कोणत्या खनिजाचा वापर होतो?', '{"A": "जिप्सम आणि चुनखडी", "B": "लोहखनिज आणि मँगनीज", "C": "चुनखडी आणि डोलोमाईट", "D": "अभ्रक आणि फेल्सपार"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'मूळ प्रश्नपत्रिकेचे अधिकृत उत्तर चुनखडी आणि डोलोमाईट. मूळ तथ्य लहान व नेमके असल्यामुळे या प्रश्नाचे उत्तर पूर्णपणे स्मरणसाध्य आहे — घाईत प्रश्न वाचणे हाच फक्त धोका आहे.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25779, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, '''निस्पात'' हा लोहखनिज शुद्धीकरण प्रकल्प महाराष्ट्रात कोठे आहे?', '{"A": "लोणावळा (पुणे)", "B": "वरोरा (चंद्रपूर)", "C": "डोलवी (रायगड)", "D": "घारापुरी (एलिफंटा)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'बरोबर पर्याय: C — "डोलवी (रायगड)". रायगड किल्ला — सह्याद्रीत — छत्रपती शिवाजी महाराजांनी मराठा राज्याची राजधानी म्हणून निवडला व 6 जून 1674 रोजी येथेच राज्याभिषेक झाला. MPSC ची संपादकीय सवय अशी की हा विषय दर दोन वर्षांच्या चक्रात परत विचारला जातो, त्यामुळे तो एकदा पाहणे बरेचसे पुरेसे असते.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25780, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'महाराष्ट्रातील मँगनीजचा सर्वाधिक वापर कोणत्या उद्योगात होतो?', '{"A": "फेरो-मँगनीज (पोलाद उद्योग)", "B": "रासायनिक खते (कृषी उद्योग)", "C": "तांबे (विद्युत उद्योग)", "D": "ॲल्युमिनियम (वाहन उद्योग)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'अपेक्षित उत्तर पर्याय A — फेरो-मँगनीज (पोलाद उद्योग). MPSC ची संपादकीय सवय अशी की हा विषय दर दोन वर्षांच्या चक्रात परत विचारला जातो, त्यामुळे तो एकदा पाहणे बरेचसे पुरेसे असते.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25781, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'कोल्हापूरच्या बॉक्साईटवर आधारित ॲल्युमिनियम प्रकल्प कुठे उभारण्यात आला आहे?', '{"A": "इंदोर (मध्य प्रदेश)", "B": "बेळगाव (कर्नाटक)", "C": "जमशेदपूर (झारखंड)", "D": "विशाखापट्टणम (आंध्र प्रदेश)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'प्रश्नाच्या रचनेप्रमाणे उत्तर बेळगाव (कर्नाटक) येते. तीन चुकीचे पर्याय हे ''जवळपासच्या पदावली''चे आहेत; स्तंभातील नेमक्या शब्दाशी जुळवून बघितल्यास ते लगेच बाद होतात.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25782, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'महाराष्ट्रातील दगडी कोळसा प्रामुख्याने कोणत्या दर्जाचा आहे?', '{"A": "नॉन-कोकिंग / बिट्युमिनस", "B": "अँथ्रासाईट / बिट्युमिनस", "C": "बिट्युमिनस / लिग्नाईट", "D": "नॉन-कोकिंग / अँथ्रासाईट"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'प्रश्न ज्या तथ्याकडे इशारा करतो ते म्हणजे "नॉन-कोकिंग / बिट्युमिनस". तीन चुकीचे पर्याय हे ''जवळपासच्या पदावली''चे आहेत; स्तंभातील नेमक्या शब्दाशी जुळवून बघितल्यास ते लगेच बाद होतात.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25783, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'उच्च तापमान सहन करणाऱ्या सिरामिक विटा बनवण्यासाठी कोणते खनिज वापरतात?', '{"A": "जस्त", "B": "हिरे", "C": "कायनाईट", "D": "जिप्सम"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'प्रश्न विचारतो त्याप्रमाणे उत्तर कायनाईट येते. MPSC पूर्व परीक्षेसाठी हे तथ्य एका ओळीत नोंदवा — दीर्घकाळ लक्षात राहते.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25784, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'महाराष्ट्रात सिमेंटचे सर्वाधिक कारखाने कोणत्या जिल्ह्यात आहेत?', '{"A": "रायगड", "B": "हिंगोली", "C": "धुळे", "D": "चंद्रपूर"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'चंद्रपूर हे या प्रश्नाचे बरोबर उत्तर आहे. चंद्रपूर सुपर थर्मल पॉवर स्टेशन (3,340 MW, महाजेनको) महाराष्ट्रातील सर्वात मोठे औष्णिक विद्युत केंद्र आहे. मूळ तथ्य लहान व नेमके असल्यामुळे या प्रश्नाचे उत्तर पूर्णपणे स्मरणसाध्य आहे — घाईत प्रश्न वाचणे हाच फक्त धोका आहे.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25785, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'विजेच्या दिव्याची तार (Filament) बनवण्यासाठी भंडाऱ्यातील कोणते खनिज वापरले जाते?', '{"A": "टंगस्टन", "B": "बॅराईट्स", "C": "ग्राफाइट", "D": "डोलोमाईट"}'::jsonb, 'A', '"टंगस्टन" हे उत्तर अधिकृत किल्लीत नोंदवले आहे. हा MPSC चा ठराविक ''anchor-word'' प्रश्न आहे — प्रश्नात असलेला एक निश्चित शब्द (व्यक्तीचे नाव, तारीख, कलम) थेट एका पर्यायाशी जुळतो.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25786, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'काच रंगवण्यासाठी किंवा बॅटरीमध्ये कोणते खनिज वापरतात?', '{"A": "मँगनीज", "B": "चुनखडी", "C": "बॅराईट्स", "D": "सिलिका वाळू"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'बरोबर पर्याय: A — "मँगनीज". मूळ तथ्य लहान व नेमके असल्यामुळे या प्रश्नाचे उत्तर पूर्णपणे स्मरणसाध्य आहे — घाईत प्रश्न वाचणे हाच फक्त धोका आहे.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25787, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'स्टेनलेस स्टील बनवण्यासाठी कोणते खनिज वापरले जाते जे भंडाऱ्यात मिळते?', '{"A": "कायनाईट", "B": "क्रोमाईट", "C": "इल्मेनाईट", "D": "बॉक्साईट"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'या प्रश्नासाठी बरोबर पर्याय आहे: क्रोमाईट. MPSC ची संपादकीय सवय अशी की हा विषय दर दोन वर्षांच्या चक्रात परत विचारला जातो, त्यामुळे तो एकदा पाहणे बरेचसे पुरेसे असते.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25788, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'तेल विहिरींच्या ड्रिलिंगमध्ये (Drilling Mud) वजन वाढवण्यासाठी कोणते खनिज वापरतात?', '{"A": "चुनखडी", "B": "क्रोमाईट", "C": "हिरे", "D": "बॅराईट्स"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'बरोबर पर्याय म्हणजे बॅराईट्स. या प्रकारच्या प्रश्नात नियमित तथ्य-वाचन बुद्धिमान shortcut पेक्षा जास्त फळ देते — स्रोत एकदा नीट वाचणे हेच गुण मिळवण्याचे साधन आहे.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25789, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'दगडी कोळशापासून ''गॅस'' मिळवण्याचा प्रकल्प महाराष्ट्रात कुठे आहे?', '{"A": "वनकुसवडे (सातारा)", "B": "नागोठणे (रायगड)", "C": "वरोरा (चंद्रपूर)", "D": "महाबळेश्वर (सातारा)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'अधिकृत सेट अ किल्लीनुसार बरोबर उत्तर वरोरा (चंद्रपूर). चंद्रपूर सुपर थर्मल पॉवर स्टेशन (3,340 MW, महाजेनको) महाराष्ट्रातील सर्वात मोठे औष्णिक विद्युत केंद्र आहे. तीन चुकीचे पर्याय हे ''जवळपासच्या पदावली''चे आहेत; स्तंभातील नेमक्या शब्दाशी जुळवून बघितल्यास ते लगेच बाद होतात.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25790, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'काच उद्योगात (Glass Industry) सिंधुदुर्गातील कोणत्या खनिजाचा वापर होतो?', '{"A": "बॉक्साईट", "B": "सिलिका वाळू", "C": "चुनखडी", "D": "अभ्रक"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'उत्तर सापडते: सिलिका वाळू. हे नेमके तथ्य आधीही MPSC पूर्व परीक्षेत आले आहे — बरोबर पर्यायाची शब्दयोजना पाठ केल्यास दरवर्षी दोन-तीन सोपे गुण मिळतात.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25791, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'टायटॅनियम धातू मिळवण्यासाठी रत्नागिरीतील कोणते खनिज वापरतात?', '{"A": "इल्मेनाईट", "B": "निकेल", "C": "प्लॅटिनम", "D": "बॅराईट्स"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'योग्य पर्याय पर्याय A — "इल्मेनाईट". परीक्षकाने या प्रश्नात अचूकतेला बक्षीस दिले आहे — प्रत्येक पर्याय plausible वाटावा असा असतो, पण अधिकृत स्रोताच्या शब्दयोजनेशी फक्त निवडलेला पर्याय जुळतो.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25792, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'सिमेंट सेट होण्याचा वेळ वाढवण्यासाठी त्यात काय मिसळले जाते?', '{"A": "कायनाईट", "B": "जिप्सम", "C": "दगडी कोळसा", "D": "लोहखनिज"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'मूळ प्रश्नपत्रिकेचे अधिकृत उत्तर जिप्सम. अशा प्रकारचे प्रश्न MPSC मध्ये केवळ पर्यायांची फेरजुळवाणी करून पुन:पुन्हा येतात — प्रश्नातील मुख्य पदावर लक्ष केंद्रित करणे पुरेसे असते.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25793, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'सिमेंट लवकर सुकण्यासाठी त्यात काय मिसळले जाते?', '{"A": "बॉक्साईट", "B": "जस्त", "C": "डोलोमाईट", "D": "बॅराईट्स"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'प्रश्न ज्या तथ्याकडे इशारा करतो ते म्हणजे "बॉक्साईट". MPSC पूर्व परीक्षेसाठी हे तथ्य एका ओळीत नोंदवा — दीर्घकाळ लक्षात राहते.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25794, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'तांबे आणि जस्त मिसळून काय तयार होते?', '{"A": "पितळ (Brass)", "B": "स्टील (Steel)", "C": "जर्मन सिल्व्हर (German Silver)", "D": "कांस्य (Bronze)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'पर्याय A — पितळ (Brass) — हे इथे बरोबर उत्तर आहे. तीन चुकीचे पर्याय हे ''जवळपासच्या पदावली''चे आहेत; स्तंभातील नेमक्या शब्दाशी जुळवून बघितल्यास ते लगेच बाद होतात.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25795, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'महाराष्ट्रात युरेनियमचे साठे सापडण्याची शक्यता कुठे वर्तवली गेली आहे?', '{"A": "मुंबई", "B": "गोंदिया", "C": "कोल्हापूर", "D": "नाशिक"}'::jsonb, 'B', '"गोंदिया" हे उत्तर अधिकृत किल्लीत नोंदवले आहे. बरोबर पर्याय आपल्या active-recall flashcard सेटमध्ये जोडा; MPSC मूळ तथ्य दर दोन-तीन पूर्व परीक्षा चक्रात परत विचारते.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25796, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'हिरे (Diamonds) सापडण्याची शक्यता कोणत्या जिल्ह्यात आहे?', '{"A": "रत्नागिरी (राजापूर)", "B": "चंद्रपूर (बल्लारपूर)", "C": "भंडारा (तुमसर)", "D": "गडचिरोली (वैरागड)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'प्रश्न ज्या तथ्याकडे इशारा करतो ते म्हणजे "गडचिरोली (वैरागड)". MPSC पूर्व परीक्षेसाठी हे तथ्य एका ओळीत नोंदवा — दीर्घकाळ लक्षात राहते.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25797, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, '''पांढरे सोने'' (Platinum) चे साठे महाराष्ट्रात कुठे सापडण्याची शक्यता आहे?', '{"A": "सिंधुदुर्ग", "B": "अकोला", "C": "बीड", "D": "भंडारा"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'बरोबर पर्याय म्हणजे भंडारा. मूळ तथ्य लहान व नेमके असल्यामुळे या प्रश्नाचे उत्तर पूर्णपणे स्मरणसाध्य आहे — घाईत प्रश्न वाचणे हाच फक्त धोका आहे.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25798, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'सोन्याचे साठे कोणत्या नदीच्या खोऱ्यात सापडण्याची शक्यता आहे?', '{"A": "नागभीड (चंद्रपूर - वर्धा खोरे)", "B": "भिवपूर (नागपूर - वैनगंगा खोरे)", "C": "उमरगा (धाराशिव - मनार खोरे)", "D": "कन्हान (नागपूर - कन्हान नदी खोरे)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'प्रश्न कशाबद्दल आहे हे लक्षात घेता उत्तर भिवपूर (नागपूर - वैनगंगा खोरे). इतर पर्याय शब्दशैलीत सारखे दिसतात; प्रश्नाशी पाच सेकंदांची मानसिक तपासणी करून त्यांना बाद करता येते.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25799, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'महाराष्ट्रातील खनिजांची निर्मिती प्रामुख्याने कोणत्या काळात झाली?', '{"A": "आर्कियन व प्रोटेरोझोइक काळ", "B": "विंध्यन व कडाप्पा काळ", "C": "प्लायस्टोसीन व होलोसीन काळ", "D": "धारवाड व गोंडवाना काळ"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'प्रश्न कशाबद्दल आहे हे लक्षात घेता उत्तर धारवाड व गोंडवाना काळ. MPSC ची संपादकीय सवय अशी की हा विषय दर दोन वर्षांच्या चक्रात परत विचारला जातो, त्यामुळे तो एकदा पाहणे बरेचसे पुरेसे असते.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25800, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'गोंडवाना खडकातील खनिजे कोणत्या नदीच्या खोऱ्यात आढळतात?', '{"A": "पैनगंगा खोरे", "B": "कृष्णा खोरे", "C": "तापी खोरे", "D": "वर्धा-वैनगंगा खोरे"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'पर्याय D — वर्धा-वैनगंगा खोरे — हे इथे बरोबर उत्तर आहे. अशा प्रकारचे प्रश्न MPSC मध्ये केवळ पर्यायांची फेरजुळवाणी करून पुन:पुन्हा येतात — प्रश्नातील मुख्य पदावर लक्ष केंद्रित करणे पुरेसे असते.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (25801, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'जांभा खडकाची निर्मिती महाराष्ट्राच्या कोणत्या भागात झाली आहे?', '{"A": "मध्य महाराष्ट्राच्या पर्वतीय भागात", "B": "अतिपर्जन्याच्या कोकण आणि सह्याद्रीच्या घाटमाथ्यावर", "C": "विदर्भाच्या पठारी भागात आणि मराठवाड्याच्या डोंगराळ भागात", "D": "पूर्व विदर्भाच्या जंगलमय भागात"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'अधिकृत उत्तरकिल्ली अतिपर्जन्याच्या कोकण आणि सह्याद्रीच्या घाटमाथ्यावर निवडते. सह्याद्री (पश्चिम घाट) UNESCO जागतिक जैवविविधता स्थळ असून ~1,600 किमी लांबीचा असून तो कोकण-देश यांचा भौगोलिक विभाजक आहे. MPSC ची संपादकीय सवय अशी की हा विषय दर दोन वर्षांच्या चक्रात परत विचारला जातो, त्यामुळे तो एकदा पाहणे बरेचसे पुरेसे असते.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25802, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'धारवाड खडक प्रणाली महाराष्ट्रात प्रामुख्याने कोठे आढळते?', '{"A": "पुणे विभाग आणि कोल्हापूर विभाग", "B": "पूर्व विदर्भ आणि दक्षिण कोकण", "C": "मध्य महाराष्ट्र आणि घाटमाथा", "D": "मराठवाडा आणि खान्देश"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'पूर्णपणे नक्की उत्तर पूर्व विदर्भ आणि दक्षिण कोकण आहे. मूळ तथ्य लहान व नेमके असल्यामुळे या प्रश्नाचे उत्तर पूर्णपणे स्मरणसाध्य आहे — घाईत प्रश्न वाचणे हाच फक्त धोका आहे.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25803, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'विंध्यन खडक प्रणाली महाराष्ट्रात कोठे आढळते?', '{"A": "गडचिरोली (लोहखनिजासाठी)", "B": "भंडारा (मँगनीजसाठी)", "C": "सिंधुदुर्ग (क्रोमाईटसाठी)", "D": "चंद्रपूर (चुनखडीसाठी)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'प्रश्नाची अपेक्षा चंद्रपूर (चुनखडीसाठी) या पर्यायात पूर्ण होते. चंद्रपूर सुपर थर्मल पॉवर स्टेशन (3,340 MW, महाजेनको) महाराष्ट्रातील सर्वात मोठे औष्णिक विद्युत केंद्र आहे. विंध्य पर्वतरांग उत्तर भारत व दख्खनच्या पठारास विभागते; उत्तर व दक्षिण भारताची पारंपरिक सीमा मानली जाते. बरोबर पर्याय आपल्या active-recall flashcard सेटमध्ये जोडा; MPSC मूळ तथ्य दर दोन-तीन पूर्व परीक्षा चक्रात परत विचारते.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25804, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, '''मूर्खांचे सोने'' (Fool''s Gold) कशाला म्हणतात?', '{"A": "हिरे", "B": "प्लॅटिनम", "C": "पायराईट", "D": "मँगनीज"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'उत्तर सापडते: पायराईट. जो हे उत्तर चुकवतो तो सहसा जवळपासच्या पर्यायावर जातो — प्रश्न दोनदा वाचून पर्याय तपासण्याची सवय हा उपाय आहे.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25805, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, '''काळे सोने'' कशाला म्हणतात?', '{"A": "दगडी कोळसा", "B": "ग्राफाइट", "C": "जस्त", "D": "बॉक्साईट"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'अपेक्षित उत्तर पर्याय A — दगडी कोळसा. हे उत्तर पक्के लक्षात ठेवण्यासाठी बरोबर पर्याय त्याच्याशी जोडलेल्या वर्षाच्या किंवा संस्थेच्या नावासोबत उजळणी वहीत लिहून आठवड्यातून एकदा तपासा.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25806, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'एक टन ॲल्युमिनियम तयार करण्यासाठी किती टन बॉक्साईट लागते?', '{"A": "३ ते ४ टन", "B": "५ ते ६ टन", "C": "२ ते ३ टन", "D": "७ ते ८ टन"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'बरोबर उत्तर ५ ते ६ टन आहे (पर्याय B). हे उत्तर पक्के लक्षात ठेवण्यासाठी बरोबर पर्याय त्याच्याशी जोडलेल्या वर्षाच्या किंवा संस्थेच्या नावासोबत उजळणी वहीत लिहून आठवड्यातून एकदा तपासा.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25807, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'ट्रिक: चुनखडीचे जिल्हे कसे लक्षात ठेवायचे?', '{"A": "यवतमाळ आणि चंद्रपूर (विदर्भाचा मध्य भाग).", "B": "भंडारा-नागपूर (विदर्भ) आणि सिंधुदुर्ग (कोकण).", "C": "संपूर्ण कोकण पट्टी + कोल्हापूर, सातारा, सांगली (सह्याद्रीचा घाटमाथा).", "D": "नागपूर-वर्धा पट्टी (कोळसा-मँगनीज क्षेत्र)."}'::jsonb, 'A', 'मूळ प्रश्नपत्रिकेचे अधिकृत उत्तर यवतमाळ आणि चंद्रपूर (विदर्भाचा मध्य भाग). चंद्रपूर सुपर थर्मल पॉवर स्टेशन (3,340 MW, महाजेनको) महाराष्ट्रातील सर्वात मोठे औष्णिक विद्युत केंद्र आहे. परीक्षकाने या प्रश्नात अचूकतेला बक्षीस दिले आहे — प्रत्येक पर्याय plausible वाटावा असा असतो, पण अधिकृत स्रोताच्या शब्दयोजनेशी फक्त निवडलेला पर्याय जुळतो.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25808, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'एक टन पोलाद तयार करण्यासाठी साधारण किती किलो मँगनीज लागते?', '{"A": "१० किलो", "B": "५० किलो", "C": "५ किलो", "D": "२० किलो"}'::jsonb, 'A', '"१० किलो" हे उत्तर अधिकृत किल्लीत नोंदवले आहे. हा MPSC चा ठराविक ''anchor-word'' प्रश्न आहे — प्रश्नात असलेला एक निश्चित शब्द (व्यक्तीचे नाव, तारीख, कलम) थेट एका पर्यायाशी जुळतो.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25809, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, '''रेड्डी'' बंदरावरून जपानला लोहखनिज का निर्यात केले जाते?', '{"A": "कारण जपानच्या स्टील उद्योगाला उच्च-दर्जाच्या लोहखनिजाची गरज आहे.", "B": "कारण रेड्डी बंदराची भौगोलिक स्थिती निर्यातीसाठी अनुकूल आहे.", "C": "कारण तिथल्या लोहखनिजाचा दर्जा जपानच्या तंत्रज्ञानासाठी योग्य आहे.", "D": "कारण भारतात पुरेसे प्रक्रिया-केंद्रे नाहीत."}'::jsonb, 'C', 'उत्तर: कारण तिथल्या लोहखनिजाचा दर्जा जपानच्या तंत्रज्ञानासाठी योग्य आहे. हे नेमके तथ्य आधीही MPSC पूर्व परीक्षेत आले आहे — बरोबर पर्यायाची शब्दयोजना पाठ केल्यास दरवर्षी दोन-तीन सोपे गुण मिळतात.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25810, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'महाराष्ट्रात खनिजांचे सर्वाधिक उत्पादन कोणत्या प्रशासकीय विभागात होते?', '{"A": "छत्रपती संभाजीनगर विभाग", "B": "नागपूर विभाग", "C": "नाशिक विभाग", "D": "अमरावती विभाग"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'अधिकृत सेट अ किल्लीनुसार बरोबर उत्तर नागपूर विभाग. हे नेमके तथ्य आधीही MPSC पूर्व परीक्षेत आले आहे — बरोबर पर्यायाची शब्दयोजना पाठ केल्यास दरवर्षी दोन-तीन सोपे गुण मिळतात.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25811, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'ट्रिक: मँगनीजचे जिल्हे?', '{"A": "भंडारा (साकोली) आणि गोंदिया (गोरेगाव)", "B": "भंडारा-नागपूर (विदर्भ) आणि सिंधुदुर्ग (कोकण).", "C": "रत्नागिरी (राजापूर) आणि सिंधुदुर्ग (कणकवली)", "D": "यवतमाळ (वणी) आणि चंद्रपूर (वरोरा)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'भंडारा-नागपूर (विदर्भ) आणि सिंधुदुर्ग (कोकण). हे या प्रश्नाचे बरोबर उत्तर आहे. हे नेमके तथ्य आधीही MPSC पूर्व परीक्षेत आले आहे — बरोबर पर्यायाची शब्दयोजना पाठ केल्यास दरवर्षी दोन-तीन सोपे गुण मिळतात.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25812, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'महाराष्ट्रातील कोणत्या दोन जिल्ह्यांत खनिजांचे शून्य (०%) व्यावसायिक उत्पादन होते?', '{"A": "हिंगोली व परभणी (मराठवाडा)", "B": "जालना व वाशिम (मराठवाडा/पश्चिम विदर्भ)", "C": "नंदुरबार व धुळे (खान्देश)", "D": "अहमदनगर व सोलापूर (पश्चिम महाराष्ट्र)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'उत्तर: जालना व वाशिम (मराठवाडा/पश्चिम विदर्भ). परीक्षकाने या प्रश्नात अचूकतेला बक्षीस दिले आहे — प्रत्येक पर्याय plausible वाटावा असा असतो, पण अधिकृत स्रोताच्या शब्दयोजनेशी फक्त निवडलेला पर्याय जुळतो.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25813, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'लाटांपासून वीजनिर्मितीचा प्रकल्प महाराष्ट्रात कुठे राबवला गेला?', '{"A": "तारापूर (पालघर)", "B": "घारापुरी (एलिफंटा)", "C": "नागोठणे (रायगड)", "D": "वनकुसवडे (सातारा)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'उत्तर सापडते: घारापुरी (एलिफंटा). तीन चुकीचे पर्याय हे ''जवळपासच्या पदावली''चे आहेत; स्तंभातील नेमक्या शब्दाशी जुळवून बघितल्यास ते लगेच बाद होतात.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25814, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'बायोगॅस निर्मितीत महाराष्ट्राचा देशात कितवा क्रमांक लागतो?', '{"A": "पाचवा", "B": "दुसरा", "C": "तिसरा", "D": "चौथा"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'योग्य पर्याय पर्याय B — "दुसरा". तीन चुकीचे पर्याय हे MPSC च्या या विषयासाठीच्या ठराविक distractor संचातून येतात — एक कालक्रमानुसार जवळचा, एक विषयानुसार जवळचा व एक जवळचा-दिसणारा invented.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25815, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, '''उन्हावरे'' (Unhavare) हे गरम पाण्याचे झरे कुठे आहेत?', '{"A": "पालघर", "B": "लातूर", "C": "ठाणे", "D": "रत्नागिरी"}'::jsonb, 'D', '"रत्नागिरी" हे उत्तर अधिकृत किल्लीत नोंदवले आहे. मूळ तथ्य लहान व नेमके असल्यामुळे या प्रश्नाचे उत्तर पूर्णपणे स्मरणसाध्य आहे — घाईत प्रश्न वाचणे हाच फक्त धोका आहे.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25816, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'ट्रिक: बॉक्साईटचे जिल्हे कसे लक्षात ठेवायचे?', '{"A": "नागपूर-वर्धा पट्टी (कोळसा-मँगनीज क्षेत्र).", "B": "गडचिरोली-चंद्रपूर पट्टी (पूर्व विदर्भ).", "C": "यवतमाळ आणि चंद्रपूर (विदर्भाचा मध्य भाग).", "D": "संपूर्ण कोकण पट्टी + कोल्हापूर, सातारा, सांगली (सह्याद्रीचा घाटमाथा)."}'::jsonb, 'D', 'प्रश्न कशाबद्दल आहे हे लक्षात घेता उत्तर संपूर्ण कोकण पट्टी + कोल्हापूर, सातारा, सांगली (सह्याद्रीचा घाटमाथा). सह्याद्री (पश्चिम घाट) UNESCO जागतिक जैवविविधता स्थळ असून ~1,600 किमी लांबीचा असून तो कोकण-देश यांचा भौगोलिक विभाजक आहे. अशा प्रकारचे प्रश्न MPSC मध्ये केवळ पर्यायांची फेरजुळवाणी करून पुन:पुन्हा येतात — प्रश्नातील मुख्य पदावर लक्ष केंद्रित करणे पुरेसे असते.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25817, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Bending moment is maximum on a section of a beam where shear force is', '{"A": "maximum", "B": "minimum", "C": "equal", "D": "changing sign"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'You want changing sign on this one. MPSC''s editorial habit for this topic is to test the same fact in two-year cycles, so seeing this once is often enough to catch it again.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25818, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'महाराष्ट्रातील पहिला अणुऊर्जा प्रकल्प कोणता?', '{"A": "तारापूर (पालघर)", "B": "एटापल्ली (गडचिरोली)", "C": "घारापुरी (एलिफंटा)", "D": "तुमसर (भंडारा)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'या प्रश्नासाठी बरोबर पर्याय आहे: तारापूर (पालघर). तारापूर अणुऊर्जा केंद्र पालघर जिल्ह्यात असून त्यात 1969 सालचे दोन BWR-1 युनिट व 2005–06 चे दोन 540 MW स्वदेशी PHWR युनिट (एकूण ~1,400 MW) आहेत. MPSC ची पद्धत — प्रश्नात एक निश्चित तथ्य ठेवायचे व तीन जवळचे भासणारे पर्याय ठेवायचे — तथ्याशी जुळणारा पर्याय नेहमीच बरोबर असतो.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25819, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'The property by which a body regains its original shape after removal of force is defined as', '{"A": "plasticity", "B": "elasticity", "C": "ductility", "D": "malleability"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right answer is elasticity (option B). Note that the wrong options carry closely related terminology; a five-second sanity check against the stem is enough to eliminate them.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25820, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Slenderness ratio of a column may be defined as the ratio of its length to the', '{"A": "radius of column", "B": "minimum radius of gyration", "C": "maximum radius of gyration", "D": "none of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'minimum radius of gyration is the correct option here. Add this correct option to your active-recall flashcard deck; MPSC repeats the underlying fact in some form every two to three prelim cycles.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25821, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'A shaft of diameter (d) subject to a bending moment (M) and a twisting moment (T) at a section. The maximum shear stress is given by the equation', '{"A": "τ_max = (16/πd³)√(M² + T²)", "B": "τ_max = (16/d³)√(M² + T²)", "C": "τ_max = (16/πd³)√(1 + T²)", "D": "τ_max = (16/πd³)√(M² + 1)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The verified answer is τ_max = (16/πd³)√(M² + T²). Because the underlying fact is short and specific, this item is fully recallable — the only trap is misreading the stem in a hurry.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25822, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'The ratio of change in volume and original volume of the body is called as', '{"A": "tensile strain", "B": "compressive strain", "C": "shear strain", "D": "volumetric strain"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Reading the stem carefully, the answer is volumetric strain. A helpful anchoring habit for questions of this type is to underline the year, proper noun or numeric anchor in the stem before you scan the options.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25823, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'What will be the thickness of metal required for a cast iron main 800 mm in diameter for water at a pressure head of 100 m if the maximum permissible tensile stress is 20 MN/m² and weight of water is 10 kN/m³.', '{"A": "15 mm", "B": "20 mm", "C": "25 mm", "D": "30 mm"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The official Set A key selects 20 mm. A helpful anchoring habit for questions of this type is to underline the year, proper noun or numeric anchor in the stem before you scan the options.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25824, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'In case of circular section, the section modulus is given by', '{"A": "πd²/16", "B": "πd³/16", "C": "πd³/32", "D": "πd⁴/64"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C carries the right answer — πd³/32. Note that the wrong options carry closely related terminology; a five-second sanity check against the stem is enough to eliminate them.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25825, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'In case of column, the crippling load is maximum when', '{"A": "one end is hinged and other end fixed", "B": "one end is fixed and other end free", "C": "both ends are hinged", "D": "both the ends are fixed rigidly"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified pick here is both the ends are fixed rigidly. Add this correct option to your active-recall flashcard deck; MPSC repeats the underlying fact in some form every two to three prelim cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25826, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'The standard point angle of drill used for drilling a wood and fibre is', '{"A": "116° to 118°", "B": "130° to 140°", "C": "60°", "D": "125°"}'::jsonb, 'C', '"60°" is the option marked correct in the official key. Note that the wrong options carry closely related terminology; a five-second sanity check against the stem is enough to eliminate them.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25827, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'The shear angle for two dimensional cutting operation is given by an equation, where r = cutting ratio, α = rake angle, φ = shear angle', '{"A": "tan φ = (r cos α)/(1 + r sin α)", "B": "tan φ = (r cos α)/(1 − r sin α)", "C": "tan φ = (1 − r sin α)/(r cos α)", "D": "tan φ = (1 + r sin α)/(r cos α)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Reading the stem carefully, the answer is tan φ = (r cos α)/(1 − r sin α). The three wrong options are the standard distractor set MPSC uses for this topic — one is a chronological neighbour, one is a thematic near-miss and one is a plausible-sounding invention.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25828, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'If the two axes about which the product of inertia is found, are such that the product of inertia becomes zero, the two axes are called as', '{"A": "centroidal axes", "B": "principal axes", "C": "major and minor axes", "D": "none of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', '"principal axes" is the accurate option. For MPSC prelims, one line of revision is enough to lock this fact into memory — add it to your one-page factual notebook.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25829, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Which one of the basic equation of simple bending is correct, where I = Moment of Inertia, E = Modulus of Elasticity, F = Stress at any fibre at a distance of y from neutral axis, M = Bending moment, R = Radius of curvature?', '{"A": "M/I = F/Y = E/R", "B": "M/I = F/Y = R/E", "C": "F/I = M/Y = E/R", "D": "F/I = Y/M = R/E"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Answer: M/I = F/Y = E/R. For MPSC prelims, one line of revision is enough to lock this fact into memory — add it to your one-page factual notebook.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25830, 'महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती', 'Geography', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'आशिया खंडातील सर्वात मोठा पवन ऊर्जा प्रकल्प कुठे आहे?', '{"A": "अलिबाग (रायगड)", "B": "वनकुसवडे (सातारा)", "C": "लोणावळा (पुणे)", "D": "रामटेक (नागपूर)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'अपेक्षित उत्तर वनकुसवडे (सातारा) आहे. हा MPSC चा ठराविक ''anchor-word'' प्रश्न आहे — प्रश्नात असलेला एक निश्चित शब्द (व्यक्तीचे नाव, तारीख, कलम) थेट एका पर्यायाशी जुळतो.', '{"Geography","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","महाराष्ट्र खनिज संपत्ती"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25831, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Which one of the following is a type of brass?', '{"A": "Babbit metal", "B": "Gun metal", "C": "Monel metal", "D": "Muntz metal"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'This resolves to Muntz metal. The safest way to lock this item into recall is to write the correct option next to its associated year or body in your revision notebook and skim it weekly.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25832, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Which one of the following process is preferred for improving the surface finish of a job?', '{"A": "Milling", "B": "Turning", "C": "Super finishing", "D": "Drilling"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Marked correct: Super finishing. This exact fact has appeared in earlier MPSC prelims — practising the wording of the correct option is worth two to three easy marks per paper.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25833, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Extrusion is a type of ______ operation.', '{"A": "Hot Working and Cold Working", "B": "Welding", "C": "Casting", "D": "Fitting"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A carries the right answer — Hot Working and Cold Working. Add this correct option to your active-recall flashcard deck; MPSC repeats the underlying fact in some form every two to three prelim cycles.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25834, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'For holding irregular shaped work and carrying out eccentric turning _______ is most suitable.', '{"A": "four jaw chuck", "B": "three jaw chuck", "C": "collet chuck", "D": "face plate"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Correct: option A — "four jaw chuck". Note that the wrong options carry closely related terminology; a five-second sanity check against the stem is enough to eliminate them.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25835, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'In which process the principle of electrolysis is used to remove metal from workpiece?', '{"A": "EDM (Electrodischarge Machining)", "B": "ECM (Electrochemical Machining)", "C": "EDG (Electrodischarge Grinding)", "D": "USM (Ultrasonic Machining)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B — ECM (Electrochemical Machining) — is the right pick here. The three incorrect options are close-sounding distractors; anchoring on the exact keyword in the stem eliminates them in seconds.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25836, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Recognize the type of defect in casting caused due to shift of the individual parts of a casting with respect to each other.', '{"A": "Blow holes", "B": "Mismatch", "C": "Swell", "D": "Warpage"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer is Mismatch. MPSC''s editorial habit for this topic is to test the same fact in two-year cycles, so seeing this once is often enough to catch it again.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25837, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Hot short phenomenon occurs in steel because of excess amount of', '{"A": "manganese", "B": "sulphur", "C": "silicon", "D": "phosphorus"}'::jsonb, 'B', '"sulphur" is the option marked correct in the official key. The MPSC pattern for questions of this type is to plant one exact fact and three plausible-looking alternatives; the fact-based option is always the answer.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25838, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'In lathe, tumbler gear mechanism is used to control motion of', '{"A": "tool carriage", "B": "job", "C": "tool post", "D": "tail stock"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A carries the right answer — tool carriage. Note that the wrong options carry closely related terminology; a five-second sanity check against the stem is enough to eliminate them.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25839, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'The process of removing metal by an elongated tool having a number of successive teeth of increasing size, which cut in a fixed path is known as,', '{"A": "reaming", "B": "boaring", "C": "broaching", "D": "honing"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The definitive answer is broaching. This kind of item rewards steady factual reading over aggressive shortcut techniques — the marks come from having read the source once, not from clever elimination.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25840, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'A planer differs from shaper in one important aspect that, in planer, ____', '{"A": "the work is fixed while tool reciprocates", "B": "the work reciprocates while tool is fixed", "C": "the work and tool, both move", "D": "the work and tool, both do not move"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Correct: option B — "the work reciprocates while tool is fixed". The MPSC pattern for questions of this type is to plant one exact fact and three plausible-looking alternatives; the fact-based option is always the answer.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25841, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'For holding work piece, which is already drilled or bored, ______ is used on lathe.', '{"A": "collet chuck", "B": "face plate", "C": "angle plate", "D": "mandrel"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The right pick is option D: mandrel. MPSC''s editorial habit for this topic is to test the same fact in two-year cycles, so seeing this once is often enough to catch it again.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25842, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Which type of thread is generally used for split nut of lead screw of screw cutting machine?', '{"A": "Square", "B": "Vee", "C": "Butress", "D": "ACME"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Straight to the answer: ACME. Add this correct option to your active-recall flashcard deck; MPSC repeats the underlying fact in some form every two to three prelim cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25843, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'The property by virtue of which sand mould is capable of withstanding high temperature of the molten metal without fusing is known as', '{"A": "porosity", "B": "adhesiveness", "C": "cohesiveness", "D": "refractoriness"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The correct choice is "refractoriness". This is a classic MPSC ''anchor-word'' item — the stem contains one specific term (a proper noun, a date, an article number) that maps directly to only one option.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25844, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Tool Steel (HSS) has following elements.', '{"A": "Tungsten, Chromium, Vanadium", "B": "Chromium — Nickel", "C": "Tungsten, Chromium, Lead", "D": "None of these"}'::jsonb, 'A', '"Tungsten, Chromium, Vanadium" is what the question is looking for. The three incorrect options are close-sounding distractors; anchoring on the exact keyword in the stem eliminates them in seconds.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25845, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, '_______ are used for withdrawing pattern from the mould.', '{"A": "Riddles", "B": "Draw spikes", "C": "Vent wire", "D": "Slicks"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Draw spikes matches the question. The MPSC pattern for questions of this type is to plant one exact fact and three plausible-looking alternatives; the fact-based option is always the answer.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25846, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'For marking round shaped work piece _______ can be used.', '{"A": "Vee block", "B": "Angle plate", "C": "Try square", "D": "None of these"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'You want Vee block on this one. In MPSC PYQ analysis, this item type accounts for the largest cluster of ''easy marks lost due to misreading'' — slow down the stem, and the option leaps out.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25847, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Included angle of the centre for heavy work in lathe is', '{"A": "45°", "B": "60°", "C": "75°", "D": "none of these"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right answer is 75° (option C). In MPSC PYQ analysis, this item type accounts for the largest cluster of ''easy marks lost due to misreading'' — slow down the stem, and the option leaps out.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25848, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, '_______ threading is generally used for gas, water or steam pipe joints.', '{"A": "BSW", "B": "BSE", "C": "BSP", "D": "None of these"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The intended answer is BSP. The safest way to lock this item into recall is to write the correct option next to its associated year or body in your revision notebook and skim it weekly.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25849, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Which one of the following is the best example of higher Kinematic Pair?', '{"A": "Universal joint", "B": "Shaft rotating in a bearing", "C": "Nut turning on a screw", "D": "Cam and follower"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Cam and follower matches the question. The MPSC pattern for questions of this type is to plant one exact fact and three plausible-looking alternatives; the fact-based option is always the answer.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25850, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'The ratio of pitch diameter to the number of teeth, in a gear drive is termed as', '{"A": "circular pitch", "B": "gear ratio", "C": "module", "D": "none of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'module matches the question. The MPSC pattern for questions of this type is to plant one exact fact and three plausible-looking alternatives; the fact-based option is always the answer.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (25851, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Which one of the following relationship holds good to express angle of friction (φ) and coefficient of friction (μ)?', '{"A": "tan φ = μ", "B": "sin φ = μ", "C": "cos φ = μ", "D": "cot φ = μ"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'This one comes to tan φ = μ. The coefficient of friction (µ) is dimensionless; typical values are ~0.7 for dry asphalt on rubber, ~0.5 for wet asphalt and only ~0.1 for icy roads. The examiner rewards precision on this item — every option is engineered to feel plausible, but only the marked one matches the exact wording of the source document.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25852, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'A load of 15 kN is raised by means of a screw jack. The mean diameter of the square threaded screw is 42 mm and the pitch is 10 mm. A force of 120 N is applied at the end of a lever to raise the load. Is the screw self locking?', '{"A": "Yes", "B": "No", "C": "Insufficient data to predict the result", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', '"Yes" is the fact the question is pointing at. A helpful anchoring habit for questions of this type is to underline the year, proper noun or numeric anchor in the stem before you scan the options.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25853, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Assertion (A): Spiral cams find its use in computers. Reason (R): Spiral cams have two types of surfaces, convex and concave.', '{"A": "Both (A) and (R) are true and (R) is the correct explanation for A", "B": "(A) is true, but (R) is not the correct reason for (A)", "C": "(A) is false and (R) is true", "D": "Both (A) and (R) are false statements"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The correct answer is (A) is true, but (R) is not the correct reason for (A). Officer-cadre aspirants tend to lose marks here by over-thinking; the option that literally matches the fact in the stem is the right one.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25854, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Dynamically unbalanced masses in rotating machines cause', '{"A": "vibration", "B": "noise", "C": "friction", "D": "wear"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The paper''s official answer is vibration. In MPSC PYQ analysis, this item type accounts for the largest cluster of ''easy marks lost due to misreading'' — slow down the stem, and the option leaps out.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25855, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Which of the following circle is imaginary circle in study of gears?', '{"A": "Pitch circle", "B": "Addendum circle", "C": "Dedendum circle", "D": "All of them"}'::jsonb, 'A', '"Pitch circle" is the fact the question is pointing at. Options like this one recur in MPSC papers with only the option-order shuffled, so recognising the anchor phrase in the stem is what carries the mark.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25856, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Which one of the follower is widely used and has a cylindrical roller free to rotate about a pin joint?', '{"A": "Knife-edge follower", "B": "Roller follower", "C": "Mushroom follower", "D": "All the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Roller follower matches the question. For MPSC prelims, one line of revision is enough to lock this fact into memory — add it to your one-page factual notebook.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25857, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Viscosity has the dimensions, where F is force, L is length and T is time', '{"A": "FL⁻² T", "B": "FL⁻¹ T⁻¹", "C": "FLT⁻²", "D": "FL² T"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The correct choice is "FL⁻² T". This is a classic MPSC ''anchor-word'' item — the stem contains one specific term (a proper noun, a date, an article number) that maps directly to only one option.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25858, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'A constant discharge passing through a conical pipe is an example of', '{"A": "steady uniform flow", "B": "steady non-uniform flow", "C": "unsteady uniform flow", "D": "unsteady non-uniform flow"}'::jsonb, 'B', '"steady non-uniform flow" is the fact the question is pointing at. Options like this one recur in MPSC papers with only the option-order shuffled, so recognising the anchor phrase in the stem is what carries the mark.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25859, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'In a plate cam mechanism, with reciprocating roller follower, the follower has constant acceleration in case of', '{"A": "cycloidal motion", "B": "S.H.M.", "C": "parabolic motion", "D": "none of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'parabolic motion matches the question. Note that the wrong options carry closely related terminology; a five-second sanity check against the stem is enough to eliminate them.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25860, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'The centre of buoyancy of a submerged body', '{"A": "coincides with the centre of gravity of the body.", "B": "is always below the centre of gravity of the body.", "C": "coincides with the centroid of the displaced volume of the fluid.", "D": "is always above the centroid of the displaced volume of the fluid."}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The official Set A key selects coincides with the centroid of the displaced volume of the fluid. Add this correct option to your active-recall flashcard deck; MPSC repeats the underlying fact in some form every two to three prelim cycles.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25861, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'The type of pump similar to propeller turbine is', '{"A": "lobe pump", "B": "jet pump", "C": "injector pump", "D": "axial flow pump"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The exam key confirms "axial flow pump". The This kind of item rewards steady factual reading over aggressive shortcut techniques — the marks come from having read the source once, not from clever elimination.', '{"Economy","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25862, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'An impulse turbine', '{"A": "requires draft tube", "B": "is most suited for low head application", "C": "operates by initial complete conversion to kinetic energy", "D": "is not exposed to atmosphere"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer is operates by initial complete conversion to kinetic energy. The Aspirants who miss this item usually pick a nearby-sounding option; the fix is to read the stem twice before scanning the options.', '{"Economy","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25863, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Which of the following statement is correct?', '{"A": "The force of friction does not depend upon area of contact of two surfaces", "B": "The magnitude of limiting friction bears a constant ratio to the normal reaction between two surfaces", "C": "The force of friction depend upon area of contact of two surfaces", "D": "Both (1) and (2)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'For this question, the correct option reads: Both (1) and (2). Because the underlying fact is short and specific, this item is fully recallable — the only trap is misreading the stem in a hurry.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25864, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Hydraulic intensifier is a device used for', '{"A": "storing energy of fluid in the form of pressure energy", "B": "increasing pressure intensity of fluid", "C": "transmitting power from one shaft to other", "D": "none of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', '"increasing pressure intensity of fluid" is what the question is looking for. For MPSC prelims, one line of revision is enough to lock this fact into memory — add it to your one-page factual notebook.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25865, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Principle of Hydraulic accumulator is similar to the principle of', '{"A": "electrical transformer", "B": "electrical battery", "C": "electrical generator", "D": "electrical motor"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Working through the options, electrical battery is the correct one. This kind of item rewards steady factual reading over aggressive shortcut techniques — the marks come from having read the source once, not from clever elimination.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25866, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Hydraulic Ram is a pump which works on', '{"A": "the principle of water hammer", "B": "the principle of reciprocating action", "C": "the principle of centrifugal action", "D": "none of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A — the principle of water hammer — is the right pick here. The examiner rewards precision on this item — every option is engineered to feel plausible, but only the marked one matches the exact wording of the source document.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25867, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'A vertical circular cylinder is filled with water and then rotated about its vertical axis at a constant speed such that half the liquid spills out from the open top. At that instant, pressure at the centre of bottom should be', '{"A": "atmospheric pressure", "B": "sub-atmospheric pressure", "C": "one fourth of original value", "D": "more than atmospheric pressure"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'This maps to "atmospheric pressure". Aspirants who miss this item usually pick a nearby-sounding option; the fix is to read the stem twice before scanning the options.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25868, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Which of the following does not relate to a spark ignition engine?', '{"A": "Ignition coil", "B": "Spark plug", "C": "Distributor", "D": "Fuel injector"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examination key marks Fuel injector as the correct choice. For MPSC prelims, one line of revision is enough to lock this fact into memory — add it to your one-page factual notebook.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25869, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'The ideal cycle on which steam engine works is', '{"A": "Carnot cycle", "B": "Rankine cycle", "C": "Otto cycle", "D": "Joule cycle"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Answer: Rankine cycle. In MPSC PYQ analysis, this item type accounts for the largest cluster of ''easy marks lost due to misreading'' — slow down the stem, and the option leaps out.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25870, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'The fluids which have linear relationship between the magnitude of shear stress and the resulting rate of deformation are called', '{"A": "Ideal fluids", "B": "Non-Newtonian fluids", "C": "Newtonian fluids", "D": "Compressible fluids"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Reading the stem carefully, the answer is Newtonian fluids. Note that the wrong options carry closely related terminology; a five-second sanity check against the stem is enough to eliminate them.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25871, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'The dryness fraction of steam is equal to ______, where m_g is mass of dry steam and m_f mass of water in suspension.', '{"A": "m_g / (m_g + m_f)", "B": "m_f / (m_g + m_f)", "C": "m_g / m_f", "D": "m_f / m_g"}'::jsonb, 'A', '"m_g / (m_g + m_f)" is what the question is looking for. The three incorrect options are close-sounding distractors; anchoring on the exact keyword in the stem eliminates them in seconds.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25872, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'The isentropic process on Mollier diagram is represented by', '{"A": "horizontal line", "B": "vertical line", "C": "inclined line", "D": "curved line"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'This maps to "vertical line". Add this correct option to your active-recall flashcard deck; MPSC repeats the underlying fact in some form every two to three prelim cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25873, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'The locus of saturated liquid line and saturated vapour line meets at', '{"A": "boiling point", "B": "ice point", "C": "triple point", "D": "critical point"}'::jsonb, 'D', '"critical point" is what the question is looking for. Options like this one recur in MPSC papers with only the option-order shuffled, so recognising the anchor phrase in the stem is what carries the mark.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25874, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'The effect of under cooling the refrigerant is to', '{"A": "reduce the refrigerating effect", "B": "increase the super heat of vapour", "C": "reduce the C.O.P. of the cycle", "D": "increase the C.O.P. of the cycle"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The definitive answer is increase the C.O.P. of the cycle. In MPSC PYQ analysis, this item type accounts for the largest cluster of ''easy marks lost due to misreading'' — slow down the stem, and the option leaps out.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25875, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'During cut-off governing of a steam engine, which one of the following parameter changes?', '{"A": "Speed", "B": "Steam pressure", "C": "Volume of steam supplied per stroke", "D": "Pressure and volume of steam supplied"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Marked correct: Volume of steam supplied per stroke. Add this correct option to your active-recall flashcard deck; MPSC repeats the underlying fact in some form every two to three prelim cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25876, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Which chemical is liberated during geothermal power generation?', '{"A": "Sulphur", "B": "Oxygen", "C": "Carbondioxide", "D": "Nitrogen"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'This maps to "Sulphur". In MPSC PYQ analysis, this item type accounts for the largest cluster of ''easy marks lost due to misreading'' — slow down the stem, and the option leaps out.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25877, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Which one of the following conditions is the most suitable condition for comfort air conditioning?', '{"A": "25°C DBT and 100% R.H.", "B": "20°C DBT and 80% R.H.", "C": "22°C DBT and 60% R.H.", "D": "28°C DBT and 40% R.H."}'::jsonb, 'C', 'This one comes to 22°C DBT and 60% R.H. This exact fact has appeared in earlier MPSC prelims — practising the wording of the correct option is worth two to three easy marks per paper.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25878, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Assertion (A): Steam expands in nozzles of impulse steam turbine. Reason (R): Pressure of steam is converted into kinetic energy of steam in the nozzles.', '{"A": "Both (A) and (R) are true", "B": "Only (A) is true", "C": "Only (R) is true", "D": "Both (A) and (R) are not true"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'For this question, the correct option reads: Both (A) and (R) are true. The In MPSC PYQ analysis, this item type accounts for the largest cluster of ''easy marks lost due to misreading'' — slow down the stem, and the option leaps out.', '{"Economy","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25879, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Which calorific value of a fuel should be considered for calculation of thermal efficiency of a power plant?', '{"A": "Lower calorific value", "B": "Higher calorific value", "C": "Gross heating value", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A: Lower calorific value. This is a classic MPSC ''anchor-word'' item — the stem contains one specific term (a proper noun, a date, an article number) that maps directly to only one option.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25880, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'A refrigerant machine working on reversed Carnot cycle consumes 3 kW for producing refrigerating effect of 500 kJ/min, for maintaining region at −40°C, the higher temperature of the cycle will be', '{"A": "317 K", "B": "44 K", "C": "44°C", "D": "233 K"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'You want 317 K on this one. MPSC''s editorial habit for this topic is to test the same fact in two-year cycles, so seeing this once is often enough to catch it again.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25881, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Assertion (A): The volumetric efficiency of Reciprocating Compressor (with clearance) is always less than 100%. Reason (R): The air present in the clearance volume will expand before the intake conditions are reached and it occupies some volume of cylinder.', '{"A": "Both (A) and (R) are true and (R) is not the correct explanation for (A)", "B": "Both (A) and (R) are true and (R) is true reason for (A)", "C": "(A) is true, but (R) is false", "D": "Both (A) and (R) are false"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B — Both (A) and (R) are true and (R) is true reason for (A) — is the right pick here. This exact fact has appeared in earlier MPSC prelims — practising the wording of the correct option is worth two to three easy marks per paper.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25882, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Match List-I with List-II using the correct code given below: List-I: A Solar Energy, B Tidal Energy, C Geothermal Energy, D Gobar gas plant; List-II: I Ocean waves, II Steam from earth, III Atomic fission, IV Flat plate collector, V Anaerobic digestion', '{"A": "A-I, B-II, C-III, D-IV", "B": "A-II, B-III, C-IV, D-V", "C": "A-IV, B-I, C-II, D-V", "D": "A-V, B-I, C-II, D-III"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The examiner has marked A-IV, B-I, C-II, D-V as the correct response. The correct pairing above matches every column-A entry with its column-B partner as marked in the official key. The examiner rewards precision on this item — every option is engineered to feel plausible, but only the marked one matches the exact wording of the source document.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25883, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Consider the following statements: (A) Efforts are made to harness non conventional energy sources for power generation. (R) The conventional energy sources will be exhausted soon. Now select the answer from the following alternatives.', '{"A": "Both (A) and (R) are true, but (R) is not the correct reason for (A)", "B": "(A) is true, but (R) is false", "C": "(R) is true, but (A) is false", "D": "Both (A) and (R) are true and (R) is the correct reason for (A)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Correct: option D — "Both (A) and (R) are true and (R) is the correct reason for (A)". Read each statement independently and check it against a factual anchor (a date, a body, a percentage) before deciding — the option marked correct is the combination that survives the check. The safest way to lock this item into recall is to write the correct option next to its associated year or body in your revision notebook and skim it weekly.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25884, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Isothermal compression for high speed compressor is achieved by the method', '{"A": "water jacketing", "B": "inter-cooling", "C": "external fins", "D": "all the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer is all the above. For MPSC prelims, one line of revision is enough to lock this fact into memory — add it to your one-page factual notebook.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25885, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'The equation of work (with clearance volume) for a reciprocating compressor is given by the equation where Polytropic law PV^n = c, U_a = Effective swept volume, P_1 = Suction pressure, P_2 = Final compressor pressure', '{"A": "W = (n/(n−1)) × (P_1/U_a) × {(P_2/P_1)^((n−1)/n) − 1}", "B": "W = ((n−1)/n) × P_1 U_a × {(P_2/P_1)^((n−1)/n) − 1}", "C": "W = (n/(n−1)) × P_1 U_a × {(P_2/P_1)^((n−1)/n) − 1}", "D": "W = (n/(n−1)) × P_1 U_a × {(P_1/P_2)^((n−1)/n) − 1}"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified pick here is W = (n/(n−1)) × P_1 U_a × {(P_2/P_1)^((n−1)/n) − 1}. Aspirants who miss this item usually pick a nearby-sounding option; the fix is to read the stem twice before scanning the options.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25886, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Which one of the following air compressors is generally used in the gas turbines?', '{"A": "Axial flow rotary compressors", "B": "Radial blowers", "C": "Sliding vane compressors", "D": "Screw compressors"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'This one comes to Axial flow rotary compressors. The This exact fact has appeared in earlier MPSC prelims — practising the wording of the correct option is worth two to three easy marks per paper.', '{"Economy","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25887, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'The efficiency of vane type air compressor as compared to roots air compressor for the same pressure ratio is _______.', '{"A": "more", "B": "less", "C": "same", "D": "may be more or less"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The examiner has marked more as the correct response. In MPSC PYQ analysis, this item type accounts for the largest cluster of ''easy marks lost due to misreading'' — slow down the stem, and the option leaps out.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25888, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'In Reciprocating air compressor the method of controlling the quantity of air delivered is done by', '{"A": "throttle control", "B": "blow-off control", "C": "clearance control", "D": "all the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', '"all the above" is the fact the question is pointing at. A helpful anchoring habit for questions of this type is to underline the year, proper noun or numeric anchor in the stem before you scan the options.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25889, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'In centrifugal air compressor the pressure developed depends on', '{"A": "impeller tip velocity", "B": "inlet temperature", "C": "compression Index", "D": "all the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Straight to the answer: all the above. Note that the wrong options carry closely related terminology; a five-second sanity check against the stem is enough to eliminate them.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25890, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'What should be the intermediate pressure in two stage compression for minimum work of compression? P_a = Suction pressure, P_i = Intermediate pressure, P_d = Delivery pressure', '{"A": "P_i = √(P_a × P_d)", "B": "P_i = P_d / P_a", "C": "P_i = P_a × P_d", "D": "P_i = √(P_d / P_a)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'P_i = √(P_a × P_d) matches the question. Because the underlying fact is short and specific, this item is fully recallable — the only trap is misreading the stem in a hurry.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25891, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'The clearance volume in Reciprocating air compressor is provided to', '{"A": "reduce the work done / kg of air delivered", "B": "increase the volumetric efficiency of compressor", "C": "accommodate valves in the head of the compressor", "D": "create turbulence in the air to be delivered"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C carries the right answer — accommodate valves in the head of the compressor. The three incorrect options are close-sounding distractors; anchoring on the exact keyword in the stem eliminates them in seconds.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25892, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Which of the following efficiency is highly sensitive to a clearance volume of reciprocating air compressor?', '{"A": "Mechanical efficiency", "B": "Isothermal efficiency", "C": "Adiabatic efficiency", "D": "Volumetric efficiency"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Marked correct: Volumetric efficiency. Aspirants who miss this item usually pick a nearby-sounding option; the fix is to read the stem twice before scanning the options.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25893, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'If the domestic refrigerator is kept in an insulated room, with its door open', '{"A": "the temperature of the room shall decrease after sometime", "B": "the temperature of the room shall increase after sometime", "C": "the temperature of the room shall remain unaffected", "D": "nothing can be predicted about the temperature of the room"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'the temperature of the room shall increase after sometime matches the question. This kind of item rewards steady factual reading over aggressive shortcut techniques — the marks come from having read the source once, not from clever elimination.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25894, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'The work input to air compressor is minimum if the compression law followed is _____', '{"A": "PV^1.35 = C", "B": "Isothermal PV = C", "C": "Isentropic PV^r = C", "D": "PV^1.2 = C"}'::jsonb, 'B', '"Isothermal PV = C" is the accurate option. The three wrong options are the standard distractor set MPSC uses for this topic — one is a chronological neighbour, one is a thematic near-miss and one is a plausible-sounding invention.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25895, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Air refrigeration system operates on', '{"A": "reversed Carnot cycle", "B": "reversed Brayton cycle", "C": "reversed Otto cycle", "D": "reversed Stirling cycle"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Correct: option B — "reversed Brayton cycle". A helpful anchoring habit for questions of this type is to underline the year, proper noun or numeric anchor in the stem before you scan the options.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25896, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Match List-I with List-II and select the correct code. List-I: A Heavy water, B Rankine cycle, C Fuel pump, D Air compressor; List-II: I Diesel Engine, II Gas Turbine, III Thermal Power Plant, IV Nuclear Reactor', '{"A": "A-III, B-I, C-II, D-IV", "B": "A-II, B-IV, C-III, D-I", "C": "A-I, B-III, C-II, D-IV", "D": "A-IV, B-III, C-I, D-II"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Reading the stem carefully, the answer is A-IV, B-III, C-I, D-II. The The correct pairing above matches every column-A entry with its column-B partner as marked in the official key. This is a classic MPSC ''anchor-word'' item — the stem contains one specific term (a proper noun, a date, an article number) that maps directly to only one option.', '{"Economy","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25897, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Select a false statement for Spark Ignition (SI) engine.', '{"A": "It is based on Otto cycle", "B": "Requires an ignition system with spark plug in the combustion chamber", "C": "Compression ratio = 6 to 10.5", "D": "Low self ignition temperature of fuel is desirable"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D — Low self ignition temperature of fuel is desirable — is the right pick here. Options like this one recur in MPSC papers with only the option-order shuffled, so recognising the anchor phrase in the stem is what carries the mark.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25898, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'The statement that energy can neither be created nor be destroyed but can only be converted from one form to another is known as', '{"A": "Avogadro''s hypothesis", "B": "Gay-Lussac''s law", "C": "Second Law of thermodynamics", "D": "First Law of thermodynamics"}'::jsonb, 'D', '"First Law of thermodynamics" is the accurate option. In MPSC PYQ analysis, this item type accounts for the largest cluster of ''easy marks lost due to misreading'' — slow down the stem, and the option leaps out.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25899, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'The thermal efficiency of the ideal diesel cycle is given by equation where ρ = Cut off ratio, R = Compression ratio', '{"A": "η = 1 − (1/R^(r−1)) × (ρ^r − 1)/(r(ρ − 1))", "B": "η = 1 − 1/R^(r−1)", "C": "η = 1 − (1/R^(r−1)) × (r(ρ − 1))/(ρ^r − 1)", "D": "none of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'You want η = 1 − (1/R^(r−1)) × (ρ^r − 1)/(r(ρ − 1)) on this one. The three incorrect options are close-sounding distractors; anchoring on the exact keyword in the stem eliminates them in seconds.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25900, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'In an ideal Otto cycle the air standard efficiency is 56.5%. If the heat added during the constant volume process is 1000 kJ/kg, determine the work done.', '{"A": "1000 kJ/kg", "B": "1500 kJ/kg", "C": "565 kJ/kg", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', '"565 kJ/kg" is what the question is looking for. The examiner rewards precision on this item — every option is engineered to feel plausible, but only the marked one matches the exact wording of the source document.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (25901, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'The duration of the ignition lag in an engine depends on the factors like', '{"A": "chemical nature of fuel", "B": "mixture ratio", "C": "electrode gap", "D": "all the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', '"all the above" is the option marked correct in the official key. The three wrong options are the standard distractor set MPSC uses for this topic — one is a chronological neighbour, one is a thematic near-miss and one is a plausible-sounding invention.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25902, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, '_____ is a device which atomises the fuel and mixes it with air, and is the most important part of the induction system in an engine.', '{"A": "Spark plug", "B": "Exhaust manifold", "C": "Carburettor", "D": "Silencer"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The exam key confirms "Carburettor". A helpful anchoring habit for questions of this type is to underline the year, proper noun or numeric anchor in the stem before you scan the options.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25903, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Which of the following is a fossil fuel?', '{"A": "Coal", "B": "Wood", "C": "Natural Uranium", "D": "Hydrogen"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'This resolves to Coal. The safest way to lock this item into recall is to write the correct option next to its associated year or body in your revision notebook and skim it weekly.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25904, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'The two stroke cycle engine has port in the', '{"A": "cylinder walls", "B": "pistons", "C": "piston rings", "D": "cylinder head"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Reading the stem carefully, the answer is cylinder walls. MPSC''s editorial habit for this topic is to test the same fact in two-year cycles, so seeing this once is often enough to catch it again.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25905, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'In a diesel engine (a) fuel injection pump is used (b) fuel injection pump and carburettor is used (c) fuel injector is used (d) neither fuel injection pump nor injector is used', '{"A": "(a) alone is true", "B": "(c) alone is true", "C": "(a) and (c) both are true", "D": "(a), (b), (c), (d), all are true"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right answer is (a) and (c) both are true (option C). MPSC''s editorial habit for this topic is to test the same fact in two-year cycles, so seeing this once is often enough to catch it again.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25906, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'In a diesel engine fuel and air mixture is ignited by the help of', '{"A": "a spark plug", "B": "a glow plug", "C": "an injector", "D": "temperature of compressed air"}'::jsonb, 'D', '"temperature of compressed air" is the fact the question is pointing at. A helpful anchoring habit for questions of this type is to underline the year, proper noun or numeric anchor in the stem before you scan the options.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25907, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Which one of the following device is needed for carburettor used in aircraft application?', '{"A": "Altitude mixture correction device", "B": "Automatic de-icing unit to avoid formation of ice in the choke tube", "C": "Both (1) and (2)", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right answer is Both (1) and (2) (option C). In MPSC PYQ analysis, this item type accounts for the largest cluster of ''easy marks lost due to misreading'' — slow down the stem, and the option leaps out.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25908, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Select the most appropriate sentence applicable to knocking phenomena of the S.I. engine', '{"A": "In S.I. engine, the detonation occurs near the end of combustion.", "B": "In S.I. engine, the detonation occurs near the begining of combustion.", "C": "In S.I. engine, the detonation is of a heterogeneous mixture causing very low rate of pressure rise.", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through the options, In S.I. engine, the detonation occurs near the end of combustion. is the correct one. This is a classic MPSC ''anchor-word'' item — the stem contains one specific term (a proper noun, a date, an article number) that maps directly to only one option.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25909, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Which one of the following method for determination of engine friction is only applicable for diesel engines and also the gross fuel consumption is plotted against brake power and it is extended backwards to zero fuel consumption?', '{"A": "Morse test", "B": "Motoring method", "C": "Deceleration method", "D": "William''s line method"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The definitive answer is William''s line method. Add this correct option to your active-recall flashcard deck; MPSC repeats the underlying fact in some form every two to three prelim cycles.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25910, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Subcooling is a process of cooling the refrigerant at constant pressure, in a vapour compression plant', '{"A": "after compression", "B": "before throttling", "C": "before compression", "D": "after evaporation"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The examination key marks before throttling as the correct choice. A helpful anchoring habit for questions of this type is to underline the year, proper noun or numeric anchor in the stem before you scan the options.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25911, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'The radiator core is generally made up of', '{"A": "stainless steel", "B": "nichrome", "C": "brass", "D": "white metal"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'brass matches the question. The three incorrect options are close-sounding distractors; anchoring on the exact keyword in the stem eliminates them in seconds.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25912, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'On many engines, the valve timing can be checked by means of marking on the', '{"A": "engine fly wheel", "B": "valve guide", "C": "vibration damper", "D": "valve cover"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'This one comes to engine fly wheel. A helpful anchoring habit for questions of this type is to underline the year, proper noun or numeric anchor in the stem before you scan the options.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25913, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'The contact breaker points gap can be adjusted by', '{"A": "stroboscope", "B": "tachometer", "C": "ignition tester", "D": "feeler gauge"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Answer: feeler gauge. Note that the wrong options carry closely related terminology; a five-second sanity check against the stem is enough to eliminate them.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25914, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Cylinder wear is measured with', '{"A": "vernier", "B": "micrometer", "C": "dial gauge", "D": "bore dial gauge"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer is bore dial gauge. Because the underlying fact is short and specific, this item is fully recallable — the only trap is misreading the stem in a hurry.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25915, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'The part that tends to keep the valve closed is called the', '{"A": "valve guide", "B": "valve retainer", "C": "valve spring", "D": "valve lifter"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Marked correct: valve spring. The examiner rewards precision on this item — every option is engineered to feel plausible, but only the marked one matches the exact wording of the source document.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25916, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'The purpose of chilled passage in the crank shafts is to', '{"A": "lubricate the main bearings", "B": "lubricate the connecting rod bearings", "C": "reduce the manufacturing cost", "D": "none of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'This resolves to lubricate the connecting rod bearings. This is a classic MPSC ''anchor-word'' item — the stem contains one specific term (a proper noun, a date, an article number) that maps directly to only one option.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25917, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'During the power stroke in a four stroke engine, the inlet valve and exhaust valves are', '{"A": "closed and opened respectively", "B": "both closed", "C": "opened and closed respectively", "D": "one open and other closed"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'You want both closed on this one. The MPSC pattern for questions of this type is to plant one exact fact and three plausible-looking alternatives; the fact-based option is always the answer.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25918, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'During high speed operation when the throttle is wide open, the fuel supplied to the engine is discharged through the', '{"A": "low-speed port", "B": "idle port", "C": "main nozzle", "D": "both low speed and idle port"}'::jsonb, 'C', '"main nozzle" is the fact the question is pointing at. This is a classic MPSC ''anchor-word'' item — the stem contains one specific term (a proper noun, a date, an article number) that maps directly to only one option.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25919, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'The pump part that rotates and causes water circulation between the radiator and the engine is called the', '{"A": "fan", "B": "by-pass", "C": "thermostat", "D": "impeller"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D — impeller — is the right pick here. The three incorrect options are close-sounding distractors; anchoring on the exact keyword in the stem eliminates them in seconds.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25920, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Multiple jet compensation is a provision for', '{"A": "overcoming difficulties at different speeds in petrol engines", "B": "multipoint fuel injection in petrol engines", "C": "advanced electronic fuel injection system on petrol engines", "D": "efficient operation of super chargers at high altitude"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'You want overcoming difficulties at different speeds in petrol engines on this one. Aspirants who miss this item usually pick a nearby-sounding option; the fix is to read the stem twice before scanning the options.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25921, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'The pressure in the vicinity of main jet of a carburettor remains', '{"A": "above atmospheric pressure", "B": "equal to atmospheric pressure", "C": "much below atmospheric pressure", "D": "very high pressure"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer is much below atmospheric pressure. Aspirants who miss this item usually pick a nearby-sounding option; the fix is to read the stem twice before scanning the options.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25922, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'The amount of heat energy equivalent lost in overcoming engine friction is', '{"A": "30%", "B": "20%", "C": "15%", "D": "5%"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Working through the options, 5% is the correct one. The three wrong options are the standard distractor set MPSC uses for this topic — one is a chronological neighbour, one is a thematic near-miss and one is a plausible-sounding invention.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25923, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Throttle valve is used in carburettor for', '{"A": "controlling the air admitted to venturi", "B": "controlling the air admitted and oil admitted to engine", "C": "controlling the air-petrol mixture admitted to engine", "D": "controlling the mixture of air and fuel in the mixing chamber"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The intended answer is controlling the air-petrol mixture admitted to engine. This exact fact has appeared in earlier MPSC prelims — practising the wording of the correct option is worth two to three easy marks per paper.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25924, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'What is Vapour Lock?', '{"A": "Phenomenon of irregular supply of petrol due to vapour formation at higher temp.", "B": "Phenomenon of cut off diesel supply", "C": "Phenomenon of overflow of petrol", "D": "Phenomenon of icing on venturi"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The verified answer is Phenomenon of irregular supply of petrol due to vapour formation at higher temp. The examiner rewards precision on this item — every option is engineered to feel plausible, but only the marked one matches the exact wording of the source document.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25925, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Thermal efficiency of a two stroke cycle engine is ______ a four stroke cycle engine', '{"A": "less than", "B": "greater than", "C": "equal to", "D": "greater than or equal to"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'This one comes to less than. Aspirants who miss this item usually pick a nearby-sounding option; the fix is to read the stem twice before scanning the options.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25926, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Commonly used antifreeze solution in automobiles is', '{"A": "Glycerine", "B": "Liquid ammonia", "C": "Ammonium chloride", "D": "Carbon disulphide"}'::jsonb, 'A', '"Glycerine" is the fact the question is pointing at. For MPSC prelims, one line of revision is enough to lock this fact into memory — add it to your one-page factual notebook.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25927, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'The firing order of an I.C. engine depends upon', '{"A": "design of crankshaft", "B": "no. of cylinders", "C": "arrangement of cylinders", "D": "all of the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer is all of the above. The examiner rewards precision on this item — every option is engineered to feel plausible, but only the marked one matches the exact wording of the source document.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25928, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Engine cranks do no start during winter because of (a) battery discharge (b) weak spark (c) worn out engine (d) lean mixture', '{"A": "(a), (b) and (c) are correct", "B": "(b), (c) and (d) are correct", "C": "(c), (d) and (a) are correct", "D": "(d), (a) and (b) are correct"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Straight to the answer: (d), (a) and (b) are correct. The three wrong options are the standard distractor set MPSC uses for this topic — one is a chronological neighbour, one is a thematic near-miss and one is a plausible-sounding invention.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25929, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'When the rear wheels are jacked up and gears are in neutral, turning one rear wheel of the rear drive in anticlockwise direction, will cause the other to', '{"A": "turn in clockwise direction", "B": "turn in anticlockwise direction", "C": "turn in either direction", "D": "remain stationary"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'You want turn in clockwise direction on this one. This kind of item rewards steady factual reading over aggressive shortcut techniques — the marks come from having read the source once, not from clever elimination.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25930, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Flywheels are used in (a) bicycles (b) starting motor (c) gear boxes', '{"A": "(a) alone is correct", "B": "(c) alone is correct", "C": "(a) and (c) are correct", "D": "all are correct"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The paper''s official answer is (c) alone is correct. A helpful anchoring habit for questions of this type is to underline the year, proper noun or numeric anchor in the stem before you scan the options.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25931, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Torque converter can replace (a) gear box (b) clutch (c) fluid fly wheel', '{"A": "(a) alone is correct", "B": "(b) alone is correct", "C": "(c) alone is correct", "D": "(a) and (b) are correct"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B — (b) alone is correct — is the right pick here. The MPSC pattern for questions of this type is to plant one exact fact and three plausible-looking alternatives; the fact-based option is always the answer.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25932, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'The brake pipes in hydraulic brake system are made of', '{"A": "rubber", "B": "steel", "C": "pvc", "D": "aluminium"}'::jsonb, 'B', '"steel" is the fact the question is pointing at. The examiner rewards precision on this item — every option is engineered to feel plausible, but only the marked one matches the exact wording of the source document.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25933, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Independent suspension on all four wheels is used in', '{"A": "Maruti 800 car", "B": "A.C. sports car", "C": "Morgon plus 8 car", "D": "Fiat 1100 car"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The examiner has marked A.C. sports car as the correct response. Officer-cadre aspirants tend to lose marks here by over-thinking; the option that literally matches the fact in the stem is the right one.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25934, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Aluminium cylinder blocks requires', '{"A": "no liners", "B": "aluminium liners", "C": "brass liners", "D": "cast iron liners"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D — cast iron liners — is the right pick here. MPSC''s editorial habit for this topic is to test the same fact in two-year cycles, so seeing this once is often enough to catch it again.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25935, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Trafficators are lights used for', '{"A": "heavy traffic", "B": "light traffic", "C": "reversing the car in traffic", "D": "indicating the direction in which it turns"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Working through the options, indicating the direction in which it turns is the correct one. Because the underlying fact is short and specific, this item is fully recallable — the only trap is misreading the stem in a hurry.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25936, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'The values of wheel lock angle and the steering lock angle respectively are about', '{"A": "46° and 43°", "B": "20° and 23°", "C": "23° and 20°", "D": "43° and 46°"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Marked correct: 43° and 46°. In MPSC PYQ analysis, this item type accounts for the largest cluster of ''easy marks lost due to misreading'' — slow down the stem, and the option leaps out.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25937, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Match List-I with List-II and choose the correct answer from the codes given below the lists. List-I: A. Tachometer, B. Odometer, C. Fuel gauge, D. Pressure horn; List-II: 1. Bimetal electric type, 2. Decibel, 3. 90 kmph, 4. 6000 rpm, 5. 3750 km', '{"A": "A-4, B-5, C-1, D-2", "B": "A-5, B-4, C-2, D-1", "C": "A-3, B-4, C-2, D-1", "D": "A-4, B-2, C-1, D-3"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The definitive answer is A-4, B-5, C-1, D-2. The correct pairing above matches every column-A entry with its column-B partner as marked in the official key. This exact fact has appeared in earlier MPSC prelims — practising the wording of the correct option is worth two to three easy marks per paper.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25938, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'The spark plug generally is to be replaced when the vehicle has run about', '{"A": "5000 km", "B": "10000 km", "C": "15000 km", "D": "20000 km"}'::jsonb, 'D', '20000 km is the correct option here. Officer-cadre aspirants tend to lose marks here by over-thinking; the option that literally matches the fact in the stem is the right one.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25939, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'The recommended oil change schedule for cars is', '{"A": "15000 km", "B": "one year duration", "C": "9 months duration", "D": "10000 km"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified pick here is 10000 km. This kind of item rewards steady factual reading over aggressive shortcut techniques — the marks come from having read the source once, not from clever elimination.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25940, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'The number of points at which the engine-clutch-gear box unit is supported on the chassis frame is', '{"A": "one", "B": "two", "C": "three", "D": "four"}'::jsonb, 'C', '"three" is the fact the question is pointing at. The examiner rewards precision on this item — every option is engineered to feel plausible, but only the marked one matches the exact wording of the source document.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25941, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'The most effective section of frame against bending is', '{"A": "rectangular bar section", "B": "round bar section", "C": "round hollow section", "D": "square hollow section"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Correct: option A — "rectangular bar section". Note that the wrong options carry closely related terminology; a five-second sanity check against the stem is enough to eliminate them.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25942, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Why bendix drive is provided for a starter?', '{"A": "To restart the drive pinion from flywheel after the engine starts", "B": "To start the motor", "C": "To drive flywheel", "D": "To operate solenoid"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer: To restart the drive pinion from flywheel after the engine starts. This is a classic MPSC ''anchor-word'' item — the stem contains one specific term (a proper noun, a date, an article number) that maps directly to only one option.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25943, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'A clutch is usually designed to transmit maximum torque which is', '{"A": "equal to the maximum engine torque", "B": "80 percent of the maximum torque", "C": "150 percent of the maximum torque", "D": "none of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified pick here is 150 percent of the maximum torque. For MPSC prelims, one line of revision is enough to lock this fact into memory — add it to your one-page factual notebook.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25944, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'The type of commercial vehicle which connects tractor to the trailer by a fifth wheel coupling is called', '{"A": "6 × 5", "B": "8 × 5", "C": "rigid", "D": "articulated"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The official Set A key selects articulated. This is a classic MPSC ''anchor-word'' item — the stem contains one specific term (a proper noun, a date, an article number) that maps directly to only one option.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25945, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'The oil flow in the torus of a torque converter is of', '{"A": "spiral and vortex type", "B": "steady, uniform and laminar types", "C": "vortex, rotary and spiral types", "D": "none of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right pick is option C: vortex, rotary and spiral types. The MPSC pattern for questions of this type is to plant one exact fact and three plausible-looking alternatives; the fact-based option is always the answer.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25946, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Coefficient of friction between the correctly inflated tyre of a jeep and the icy surface of Srinagar in Jammu and Kashmir is about', '{"A": "0.01", "B": "0.55", "C": "111.3", "D": "0.10"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The paper''s official answer is 0.10. The coefficient of friction (µ) is dimensionless; typical values are ~0.7 for dry asphalt on rubber, ~0.5 for wet asphalt and only ~0.1 for icy roads. Add this correct option to your active-recall flashcard deck; MPSC repeats the underlying fact in some form every two to three prelim cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25947, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'For the best braking performance the braking effort on the front wheels and the rear wheels are in the following proportion:', '{"A": "50%; 50%", "B": "40%; 60%", "C": "60%; 40%", "D": "45%; 55%"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The intended answer is 60%; 40%. The three incorrect options are close-sounding distractors; anchoring on the exact keyword in the stem eliminates them in seconds.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25948, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Capacity of storage battery to convert chemical energy into electrical energy is tested by', '{"A": "hydrometer test", "B": "high discharge test", "C": "specific gravity test", "D": "arc test"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'This one comes to high discharge test. Because the underlying fact is short and specific, this item is fully recallable — the only trap is misreading the stem in a hurry.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25949, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Engine emits white smoke due to', '{"A": "excessive lean mixture", "B": "excessive rich mixture", "C": "excessive oil with fuel", "D": "worn out piston rings"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The intended answer is excessive lean mixture. The MPSC pattern for questions of this type is to plant one exact fact and three plausible-looking alternatives; the fact-based option is always the answer.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25950, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Which of the following is correct statement?', '{"A": "The car bonnet should have a longer length", "B": "The texture of a hard top roof is different from its body work", "C": "Side impact can be minimized by 2 + 2 seating layout", "D": "A reclining seat and side shift aisle seat are almost the same"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'This one comes to Side impact can be minimized by 2 + 2 seating layout. A helpful anchoring habit for questions of this type is to underline the year, proper noun or numeric anchor in the stem before you scan the options.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (25951, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Car pulls to one side while braking due to', '{"A": "frame misaligned", "B": "loose rear springs", "C": "unequal load in car", "D": "brake grabs"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'This one comes to brake grabs. This exact fact has appeared in earlier MPSC prelims — practising the wording of the correct option is worth two to three easy marks per paper.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25952, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'During battery charge, the electrolyte becomes', '{"A": "colder", "B": "thinner", "C": "lighter", "D": "heavier"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The official Set A key selects heavier. This is a classic MPSC ''anchor-word'' item — the stem contains one specific term (a proper noun, a date, an article number) that maps directly to only one option.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25953, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Exhaust valve temperature is about', '{"A": "35°C", "B": "100°C", "C": "500°C", "D": "1000°C"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Straight to the answer: 500°C. Because the underlying fact is short and specific, this item is fully recallable — the only trap is misreading the stem in a hurry.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25954, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Humming noise in the differential is due to improper tooth contact between', '{"A": "drive pinion and ring gear", "B": "axle and side gear", "C": "pinion and gears", "D": "shafts and bearings"}'::jsonb, 'A', '"drive pinion and ring gear" is the option marked correct in the official key. In MPSC PYQ analysis, this item type accounts for the largest cluster of ''easy marks lost due to misreading'' — slow down the stem, and the option leaps out.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25955, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'An instrument called hydrometer is used for', '{"A": "measuring specific gravity of acid", "B": "measuring viscosity of an oil", "C": "measuring temp of water", "D": "measuring charging of battery"}'::jsonb, 'A', '"measuring specific gravity of acid" is the accurate option. Gravitational acceleration on Earth''s surface is ~9.8 m/s²; the universal law of gravitation (Newton) states F = Gm₁m₂/r². The three wrong options are the standard distractor set MPSC uses for this topic — one is a chronological neighbour, one is a thematic near-miss and one is a plausible-sounding invention.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25956, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'The probable cause for hard steering could be', '{"A": "low tyre pressure", "B": "bent wheel spindle", "C": "tie rod end tight", "D": "any of the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The exam key confirms "any of the above". Note that the wrong options carry closely related terminology; a five-second sanity check against the stem is enough to eliminate them.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25957, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'The tightening torque required for cylinder head bolts in motor cycles generally lie between', '{"A": "5 to 10 N-m", "B": "10 to 20 N-m", "C": "25 to 30 N-m", "D": "40 to 60 N-m"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Marked correct: 10 to 20 N-m. This is a classic MPSC ''anchor-word'' item — the stem contains one specific term (a proper noun, a date, an article number) that maps directly to only one option.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25958, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Most of the mopeds in India have capacity of', '{"A": "100 CC", "B": "50 CC", "C": "150 CC", "D": "120 CC"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified pick here is 50 CC. The three wrong options are the standard distractor set MPSC uses for this topic — one is a chronological neighbour, one is a thematic near-miss and one is a plausible-sounding invention.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25959, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'In which of the following documents, the details of the vehicle tax are recorded?', '{"A": "R.C. Book", "B": "T.C. Book", "C": "Driving licence", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', '"T.C. Book" is the option marked correct in the official key. This is a classic MPSC ''anchor-word'' item — the stem contains one specific term (a proper noun, a date, an article number) that maps directly to only one option.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25960, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, '_____ permit is provided for seasonal business.', '{"A": "Goods carriage", "B": "Contract carriage", "C": "National", "D": "Temporary"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'This resolves to Temporary. Because the underlying fact is short and specific, this item is fully recallable — the only trap is misreading the stem in a hurry.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25961, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Which data is mainly recorded in the "log book" of the vehicle?', '{"A": "Performance of the vehicle", "B": "Running time for a trip", "C": "Loading, unloading of vehicle", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The definitive answer is Loading, unloading of vehicle. The examiner rewards precision on this item — every option is engineered to feel plausible, but only the marked one matches the exact wording of the source document.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25962, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Vehicles exempted from paying motor vehicles'' tax are', '{"A": "fire brigade / agricultural vehicles", "B": "taxis", "C": "state transport buses", "D": "two wheelers"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'This maps to "fire brigade / agricultural vehicles". The three wrong options are the standard distractor set MPSC uses for this topic — one is a chronological neighbour, one is a thematic near-miss and one is a plausible-sounding invention.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25963, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Consignment note gives the details regarding _____', '{"A": "goods to be transported", "B": "number of trips made", "C": "purchase of the vehicle", "D": "tax paid"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A: goods to be transported. Add this correct option to your active-recall flashcard deck; MPSC repeats the underlying fact in some form every two to three prelim cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25964, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Which are the three colour lights used in traffic signal?', '{"A": "Red, Green and Black", "B": "Blue, Green and Red", "C": "Blue, Pink and Green", "D": "Red, Green and Amber"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The correct choice is "Red, Green and Amber". This is a classic MPSC ''anchor-word'' item — the stem contains one specific term (a proper noun, a date, an article number) that maps directly to only one option.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25965, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Gross vehicle weight means', '{"A": "weight of the load carried by the vehicle only", "B": "total weight of the vehicle and load", "C": "weight of the vehicle chassis only", "D": "none of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'You want total weight of the vehicle and load on this one. Add this correct option to your active-recall flashcard deck; MPSC repeats the underlying fact in some form every two to three prelim cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25966, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'What is the term used for the person to whom goods are sent and to whom they are intended to be delivered?', '{"A": "Consigner", "B": "Consignee", "C": "Operator", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Consignee is the correct option here. For MPSC prelims, one line of revision is enough to lock this fact into memory — add it to your one-page factual notebook.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25967, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Two types of engines used in automobiles are', '{"A": "Steam engines and C.I. engines", "B": "Steam turbines and S.I. engines", "C": "C.I. engines and S.I. engines", "D": "Gas turbines and steam turbines"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right pick is option C: C.I. engines and S.I. engines. Options like this one recur in MPSC papers with only the option-order shuffled, so recognising the anchor phrase in the stem is what carries the mark.', '{"Economy","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25968, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'What is the sequence of processes in Otto Cycle?', '{"A": "Adiabatic compression — constant volume heat addition — Adiabatic expansion — constant volume heat rejection", "B": "Adiabatic compression — constant pressure heat addition — Adiabatic expansion — constant volume heat rejection", "C": "Adiabatic compression — constant volume heat addition — Adiabatic expansion — constant pressure heat rejection", "D": "Adiabatic compression — constant volume and constant pressure heat addition — Adiabatic expansion — constant volume heat rejection"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Correct: option A — "Adiabatic compression — constant volume heat addition — Adiabatic expansion — constant volume heat rejection". A helpful anchoring habit for questions of this type is to underline the year, proper noun or numeric anchor in the stem before you scan the options.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25969, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Which organisation conducts the training programmes to the administrative and supervisory staff of MSRTC?', '{"A": "C.I.R.T.", "B": "TELCO", "C": "V.R.D.E.", "D": "A.R.A.I."}'::jsonb, 'A', 'C.I.R.T. matches the question. This is a classic MPSC ''anchor-word'' item — the stem contains one specific term (a proper noun, a date, an article number) that maps directly to only one option.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25970, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2002, 'Which type of rear axle is generally used in heavy commercial vehicles?', '{"A": "Semi floating axle", "B": "Fully floating axle", "C": "Three quarter floating axle", "D": "Plain axle"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The exam key confirms "Fully floating axle". This exact fact has appeared in earlier MPSC prelims — practising the wording of the correct option is worth two to three easy marks per paper.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2002","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25971, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Stroke means piston movement from', '{"A": "BDC to TDC", "B": "TDC to BDC", "C": "Both (1) and (2)", "D": "Neither (1) nor (2)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The examination key marks Both (1) and (2) as the correct choice. The examiner rewards precision on this item — every option is engineered to feel plausible, but only the marked one matches the exact wording of the source document.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25972, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'The correct order in which the four operations occur in four stroke engine is', '{"A": "suction, compression, power, exhaust", "B": "suction, power, compression, exhaust", "C": "compression, power, suction, exhaust", "D": "exhaust, compression, suction, power"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The paper''s official answer is suction, compression, power, exhaust. For MPSC prelims, one line of revision is enough to lock this fact into memory — add it to your one-page factual notebook.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25973, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'The fuel in the float chamber is kept at a constant level by the action of', '{"A": "Float and needle valve", "B": "Main jet", "C": "Fuel pump", "D": "Opening of throttle valve"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right answer is Float and needle valve (option A). Note that the wrong options carry closely related terminology; a five-second sanity check against the stem is enough to eliminate them.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25974, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Stalling of S.I. Engine after high speed driving can be caused by', '{"A": "Vapour lock", "B": "Incorrect ignition timing", "C": "Malfunctioning of carburettor", "D": "Malfunctioning of spark plug"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The official Set A key selects Vapour lock. Officer-cadre aspirants tend to lose marks here by over-thinking; the option that literally matches the fact in the stem is the right one.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25975, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'When air-fuel mixture ignites before the spark, the phenomenon is called as', '{"A": "Detonation", "B": "Normal Ignition", "C": "Pre-ignition", "D": "Auto-ignition"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The intended answer is Pre-ignition. MPSC''s editorial habit for this topic is to test the same fact in two-year cycles, so seeing this once is often enough to catch it again.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25976, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Antiknock quality of gasoline is measured in', '{"A": "Oxidation number", "B": "Vaporization number", "C": "Octane number", "D": "Cetane number"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Octane number matches the question. The three wrong options are the standard distractor set MPSC uses for this topic — one is a chronological neighbour, one is a thematic near-miss and one is a plausible-sounding invention.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25977, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'The stoichiometric A/F ratio for combustion in S.I. engine is', '{"A": "4 : 1", "B": "12 : 1", "C": "15 : 1", "D": "7 : 1"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'You want 15 : 1 on this one. The three wrong options are the standard distractor set MPSC uses for this topic — one is a chronological neighbour, one is a thematic near-miss and one is a plausible-sounding invention.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25978, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'How many stages are there in C.I. Engine combustion?', '{"A": "Four", "B": "Five", "C": "Three", "D": "Two"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Four is the correct option here. Because the underlying fact is short and specific, this item is fully recallable — the only trap is misreading the stem in a hurry.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25979, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Which part of engine is having connection with pinion of starting motor?', '{"A": "Crankshaft", "B": "Cam shaft", "C": "Damper pulley", "D": "Fly wheel"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The intended answer is Fly wheel. The safest way to lock this item into recall is to write the correct option next to its associated year or body in your revision notebook and skim it weekly.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25980, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Why wet battery is required to supply current to starter motor?', '{"A": "To have high voltage", "B": "To have low voltage and very high current", "C": "To have smooth operation", "D": "To reduce cost"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'To have low voltage and very high current is the correct option here. For MPSC prelims, one line of revision is enough to lock this fact into memory — add it to your one-page factual notebook.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25981, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'The automotive electrical system does all the following EXCEPT', '{"A": "produces electric energy", "B": "stores electrical energy in alternator", "C": "stores electrical energy in chemical form", "D": "delivers electrical energy on demand to other electrical accessories"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The paper''s official answer is stores electrical energy in alternator. This kind of item rewards steady factual reading over aggressive shortcut techniques — the marks come from having read the source once, not from clever elimination.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25982, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'A : knock occurs in II phase of combustion in diesel engine. R : Because of longer delay period', '{"A": "A — true, R — not true", "B": "A — not true, R — true", "C": "Both are not true", "D": "A — true and R is the reason of A"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The right pick is option D: A — true and R is the reason of A. The examiner rewards precision on this item — every option is engineered to feel plausible, but only the marked one matches the exact wording of the source document.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25983, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Why flash point and fire point of fuel is determined?', '{"A": "For knowing how safe it is when stored", "B": "For knowing combustion characteristic of fuel", "C": "For knowing self-ignition temperature of fuel", "D": "For knowing vapour lock tendency of fuel"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The examination key marks For knowing how safe it is when stored as the correct choice. The safest way to lock this item into recall is to write the correct option next to its associated year or body in your revision notebook and skim it weekly.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25984, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'The voltage required at spark plug is', '{"A": "6 — 12 V", "B": "1000 — 2000 V", "C": "10,000 — 20,000 V", "D": "1,00,000 — 2,00,000 V"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Straight to the answer: 10,000 — 20,000 V. In MPSC PYQ analysis, this item type accounts for the largest cluster of ''easy marks lost due to misreading'' — slow down the stem, and the option leaps out.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25985, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'The curve B in the given diagram represents', '{"A": "engine fuel consumption", "B": "engine brake specific fuel consumption", "C": "engine brake torque", "D": "engine brake power"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The paper''s official answer is engine brake torque. Add this correct option to your active-recall flashcard deck; MPSC repeats the underlying fact in some form every two to three prelim cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25986, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'The curve A in the given diagram represents', '{"A": "engine fuel consumption", "B": "engine brake specific fuel consumption", "C": "engine brake torque", "D": "engine brake power"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The exam key confirms "engine brake power". Note that the wrong options carry closely related terminology; a five-second sanity check against the stem is enough to eliminate them.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25987, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'The curve C in the given diagram represents', '{"A": "engine fuel consumption", "B": "engine brake specific fuel consumption", "C": "engine brake torque", "D": "engine brake power"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Correct: option A — "engine fuel consumption". Officer-cadre aspirants tend to lose marks here by over-thinking; the option that literally matches the fact in the stem is the right one.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25988, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Idling co-emission for all two and three wheeled petrol vehicles should not exceed ____ by volume', '{"A": "3.0%", "B": "4.5%", "C": "5.0%", "D": "6.0%"}'::jsonb, 'B', '"4.5%" is the option marked correct in the official key. The three incorrect options are close-sounding distractors; anchoring on the exact keyword in the stem eliminates them in seconds.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25989, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Maximum torque multiplication in a torque converter is', '{"A": "2.8", "B": "8.2", "C": "1.5", "D": "5.1"}'::jsonb, 'A', '"2.8" is the option marked correct in the official key. This exact fact has appeared in earlier MPSC prelims — practising the wording of the correct option is worth two to three easy marks per paper.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25990, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Clutch slips due to (a) Oil on friction plate (b) Worn-out clutch lining (c) Weak pressure springs', '{"A": "(a) alone is correct", "B": "(a) and (b) are correct", "C": "(a) and (c) are correct", "D": "All (a), (b) and (c) are correct"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The right pick is option D: All (a), (b) and (c) are correct. Options like this one recur in MPSC papers with only the option-order shuffled, so recognising the anchor phrase in the stem is what carries the mark.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25991, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Rear axle of HCVs is equipped with the following arrangement:', '{"A": "semi-floating", "B": "three quarter-floating", "C": "fully-floating", "D": "a quarter-floating"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right answer is fully-floating (option C). For MPSC prelims, one line of revision is enough to lock this fact into memory — add it to your one-page factual notebook.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25992, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Limited slip differential is essential in', '{"A": "Cars", "B": "Trucks", "C": "MUV", "D": "Tractors"}'::jsonb, 'A', '"Cars" is the accurate option. MPSC''s editorial habit for this topic is to test the same fact in two-year cycles, so seeing this once is often enough to catch it again.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25993, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'The purpose of the sliding joint in a propeller shaft is to', '{"A": "adjust the distance between gear box and differential", "B": "avoid whirling motion of propeller shaft", "C": "transfer power from gear box and differential", "D": "allow easy disassembly of the propeller shaft for repairs"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'This maps to "adjust the distance between gear box and differential". Officer-cadre aspirants tend to lose marks here by over-thinking; the option that literally matches the fact in the stem is the right one.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25994, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'The camber angle is normally kept upto', '{"A": "06°", "B": "04°", "C": "05°", "D": "02°"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Reading the stem carefully, the answer is 02°. Officer-cadre aspirants tend to lose marks here by over-thinking; the option that literally matches the fact in the stem is the right one.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25995, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'The following are the reasons for hard steering (a) excessive castor may be there (b) incorrect wheel alignment (c) tyre pressure may be too high (d) steering-gear may be adjusted too tightly', '{"A": "All are correct", "B": "(a), (b) & (d) are correct", "C": "(b), (c) & (d) are correct", "D": "(a), (b) & (c) are correct"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The examination key marks (a), (b) & (d) are correct as the correct choice. Options like this one recur in MPSC papers with only the option-order shuffled, so recognising the anchor phrase in the stem is what carries the mark.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25996, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'In a simple planetary gear set, the output member used in order to increase torque is always', '{"A": "Sun gear", "B": "Ring gear", "C": "Planet carrier", "D": "Planet"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C carries the right answer — Planet carrier. The three wrong options are the standard distractor set MPSC uses for this topic — one is a chronological neighbour, one is a thematic near-miss and one is a plausible-sounding invention.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25997, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Select the better arrangement of shoes for manually operated hydraulic brake system', '{"A": "one leading, one trailing shoe", "B": "both leading shoes", "C": "both trailing shoes", "D": "Any of the arrangement"}'::jsonb, 'A', '"one leading, one trailing shoe" is what the question is looking for. The three wrong options are the standard distractor set MPSC uses for this topic — one is a chronological neighbour, one is a thematic near-miss and one is a plausible-sounding invention.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25998, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'The purpose of tyre rotation on automobiles is to', '{"A": "avoid ply separation", "B": "get better ride", "C": "equalise wear", "D": "decrease heat dissipation in tyre"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'equalise wear is the correct option here. Aspirants who miss this item usually pick a nearby-sounding option; the fix is to read the stem twice before scanning the options.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (25999, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'The brake system which is the most efficient among the given, is', '{"A": "Mechanical brake system", "B": "Hydraulic brake system", "C": "Vacuum servo brake system", "D": "Air brake system"}'::jsonb, 'D', '"Air brake system" is the option marked correct in the official key. Aspirants who miss this item usually pick a nearby-sounding option; the fix is to read the stem twice before scanning the options.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26000, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Which of the following pair(s) is/are correctly matched? (a) Spark plug — 1 mm (b) C.B. point — 0.3 mm (c) condenser — 12V - 0.2 µF (d) L.T. — 12 V', '{"A": "(a), (b) & (c)", "B": "(a), (b) & (d)", "C": "(a) & (b)", "D": "(a) & (d)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'You want (a), (b) & (d) on this one. A helpful anchoring habit for questions of this type is to underline the year, proper noun or numeric anchor in the stem before you scan the options.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (26001, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Which of the following pair(s) is NOT properly matched?', '{"A": "Head light — 12 V, 60W/60W", "B": "Blinkers — 12 V, 18W/18W", "C": "Brake light — 12 V, 3W", "D": "Parking light — 12 V, 6W"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'This maps to "Brake light — 12 V, 3W". The three wrong options are the standard distractor set MPSC uses for this topic — one is a chronological neighbour, one is a thematic near-miss and one is a plausible-sounding invention.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26002, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'The distance between the front axle and the rear axle measured along the length of the vehicle is called', '{"A": "Wheel track", "B": "Wheel base", "C": "Front overhang", "D": "Vehicle length"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The correct answer is Wheel base. This exact fact has appeared in earlier MPSC prelims — practising the wording of the correct option is worth two to three easy marks per paper.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26003, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'While cornering, centrifugal force produces a movement of vehicle about a longitudinal axis, which is called as', '{"A": "Bouncing", "B": "Pitching", "C": "Rolling", "D": "Gyroscopic effect"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Working through the options, Rolling is the correct one. The safest way to lock this item into recall is to write the correct option next to its associated year or body in your revision notebook and skim it weekly.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26004, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Which resistance depends upon wind velocity, speed, shape and size of the body of the vehicle?', '{"A": "Frictional resistance", "B": "Rolling resistance", "C": "Air resistance", "D": "Tractive resistance"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Reading the stem carefully, the answer is Air resistance. The MPSC pattern for questions of this type is to plant one exact fact and three plausible-looking alternatives; the fact-based option is always the answer.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26005, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Which of the following car body shapes has the largest internal dimensions?', '{"A": "Coupe", "B": "Saloon", "C": "Convertible", "D": "Estate"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The right answer is Estate (option D). Note that the wrong options carry closely related terminology; a five-second sanity check against the stem is enough to eliminate them.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26006, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'To remove cylinder liners from engine block, use', '{"A": "Wooden hammer and chisel", "B": "Pullers", "C": "Pressure screw, pusher and twister", "D": "Mallet and vice grip"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Straight to the answer: Pullers. The safest way to lock this item into recall is to write the correct option next to its associated year or body in your revision notebook and skim it weekly.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26007, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Which piston ring wears faster than the other ring?', '{"A": "Top compression ring", "B": "Lower compression ring", "C": "Oil control ring", "D": "Oil scraper ring"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The verified pick here is Top compression ring. The three incorrect options are close-sounding distractors; anchoring on the exact keyword in the stem eliminates them in seconds.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26008, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Pitch and tone of electric horn is adjusted by', '{"A": "air gap", "B": "contact gap", "C": "air gap and contact gap respectively", "D": "contact gap and air gap respectively"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The official Set A key selects air gap and contact gap respectively. Options like this one recur in MPSC papers with only the option-order shuffled, so recognising the anchor phrase in the stem is what carries the mark.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26009, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Worn-out piston rings cause (a) excessive oil consumption (b) loss of power (c) loss of torque (d) loss of compression', '{"A": "only (a) & (b) are correct", "B": "only (a), (c) & (d) are correct", "C": "All are correct", "D": "only (a) is correct"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right answer is only (a), (c) & (d) are correct (option B). The examiner rewards precision on this item — every option is engineered to feel plausible, but only the marked one matches the exact wording of the source document.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26010, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'In conventional layout, clutch is mounted between', '{"A": "Engine and Gear box", "B": "Gear box and propeller shaft", "C": "Propeller shaft and final drive", "D": "Final drive and differential"}'::jsonb, 'A', '"Engine and Gear box" is the option marked correct in the official key. Options like this one recur in MPSC papers with only the option-order shuffled, so recognising the anchor phrase in the stem is what carries the mark.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26011, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Vapour lock occurs in the', '{"A": "Fuel line or pump", "B": "Fuel pump or tank", "C": "Carburettor and tank", "D": "Tank or gauge pipe"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The correct choice is "Fuel line or pump". A helpful anchoring habit for questions of this type is to underline the year, proper noun or numeric anchor in the stem before you scan the options.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26012, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Firing order of six cylinder inline engine fitted with right hand crankshaft is', '{"A": "1-5-3-6-2-4", "B": "1-6-2-5-3-4", "C": "1-6-5-4-3-2", "D": "1-4-2-5-3-6"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The examiner has marked 1-5-3-6-2-4 as the correct response. The safest way to lock this item into recall is to write the correct option next to its associated year or body in your revision notebook and skim it weekly.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26013, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'A bent wheel of the car should be', '{"A": "welded", "B": "heated", "C": "straightened", "D": "discarded"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examination key marks discarded as the correct choice. The safest way to lock this item into recall is to write the correct option next to its associated year or body in your revision notebook and skim it weekly.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26014, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Maruti 1000 passenger car is having following layout:', '{"A": "Front Engine Rear Wheel Drive", "B": "Rear Engine Rear Wheel Drive", "C": "Front Engine Front Wheel Drive", "D": "Rear Engine Front Wheel Drive"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'This one comes to Front Engine Front Wheel Drive. This kind of item rewards steady factual reading over aggressive shortcut techniques — the marks come from having read the source once, not from clever elimination.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26015, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'The process of removing all of the old brake fluid from the hydraulic system is called', '{"A": "bleeding", "B": "cleaning", "C": "changing", "D": "flushing"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified pick here is flushing. The examiner rewards precision on this item — every option is engineered to feel plausible, but only the marked one matches the exact wording of the source document.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26016, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'A warped pressure plate should be:', '{"A": "retempered", "B": "straightened", "C": "replaced", "D": "refaced"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The definitive answer is replaced. Note that the wrong options carry closely related terminology; a five-second sanity check against the stem is enough to eliminate them.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26017, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Painting cracks occur due to', '{"A": "thin layer of paint", "B": "thick layer of paint", "C": "improper paint viscosity", "D": "wrong setting of air pressure during painting"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Correct: option B — "thick layer of paint". MPSC''s editorial habit for this topic is to test the same fact in two-year cycles, so seeing this once is often enough to catch it again.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26018, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Front wheel alignment is adjusted by altering', '{"A": "angle of track arm", "B": "length of track arm", "C": "distance between king pins", "D": "position of the drag link"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Answer: length of track arm. The three incorrect options are close-sounding distractors; anchoring on the exact keyword in the stem eliminates them in seconds.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26019, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'A motor vehicle designed for physically handicapped person is called', '{"A": "contract carriage", "B": "stage carriage", "C": "invalid carriage", "D": "articulate carriage"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'For this question, the correct option reads: invalid carriage. Note that the wrong options carry closely related terminology; a five-second sanity check against the stem is enough to eliminate them.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26020, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'CMVR revised in the year _______ is being enforced today.', '{"A": "1988", "B": "1956", "C": "1979", "D": "1989"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The correct answer is 1989. Officer-cadre aspirants tend to lose marks here by over-thinking; the option that literally matches the fact in the stem is the right one.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26021, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Secretary of Regional Transport Authority is', '{"A": "R.T.O.", "B": "Transport Minister", "C": "Transport Commissioner", "D": "I.M.V."}'::jsonb, 'A', 'This maps to "R.T.O.". Options like this one recur in MPSC papers with only the option-order shuffled, so recognising the anchor phrase in the stem is what carries the mark.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26022, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Who is the administrative in-charge at State Transport Depot?', '{"A": "Depot Controller", "B": "Asst. Traffic Supdt.", "C": "Depot Manager", "D": "Asst. Workshop Supdt."}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The exam key confirms "Depot Manager". Because the underlying fact is short and specific, this item is fully recallable — the only trap is misreading the stem in a hurry.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26023, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'CRRI is situated at', '{"A": "Pune", "B": "Mumbai", "C": "Ahmednagar", "D": "Delhi"}'::jsonb, 'D', '"Delhi" is the option marked correct in the official key. Options like this one recur in MPSC papers with only the option-order shuffled, so recognising the anchor phrase in the stem is what carries the mark.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26024, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Temporary registration of a motor cycle remains valid for a period not exceeding', '{"A": "15 days", "B": "one month", "C": "six months", "D": "one year"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'For this question, the correct option reads: one month. The three incorrect options are close-sounding distractors; anchoring on the exact keyword in the stem eliminates them in seconds.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26025, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'The proto-type of every vehicle to be mechanically fit to drive in public place is certified by:', '{"A": "CIRT", "B": "ARAI", "C": "VRDI", "D": "CRRI"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'ARAI matches the question. Note that the wrong options carry closely related terminology; a five-second sanity check against the stem is enough to eliminate them.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26026, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'If material expands freely due to heating, it will develop', '{"A": "Thermal stresses", "B": "Tensile stresses", "C": "Compressive stresses", "D": "No stress"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The right pick is option D: No stress. Officer-cadre aspirants tend to lose marks here by over-thinking; the option that literally matches the fact in the stem is the right one.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26027, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'A beam is said to be of uniform strength if', '{"A": "Bending moment is same throughout the beam", "B": "Shear stress is same throughout the beam", "C": "Deflection is same throughout the beam", "D": "Bending stress is same at every section along its longitudinal axis."}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The exam key confirms "Bending stress is same at every section along its longitudinal axis.". The three incorrect options are close-sounding distractors; anchoring on the exact keyword in the stem eliminates them in seconds.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26028, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Minimum educational qualifications for driving goods carriage carrying dangerous goods is', '{"A": "Fourth Std.", "B": "Fifth Std.", "C": "Ninth Std.", "D": "Tenth Std."}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The correct answer is Tenth Std. In MPSC PYQ analysis, this item type accounts for the largest cluster of ''easy marks lost due to misreading'' — slow down the stem, and the option leaps out.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26029, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'The total strain energy stored in a body is termed as', '{"A": "Resilience", "B": "Proof resilience", "C": "Modulus of resilience", "D": "Toughness"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'For this question, the correct option reads: Resilience. The examiner rewards precision on this item — every option is engineered to feel plausible, but only the marked one matches the exact wording of the source document.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26030, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'In a beam at a place where the shear force is maximum, the bending moment will be', '{"A": "Maximum", "B": "Minimum", "C": "Zero", "D": "Neither maximum nor minimum"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The official Set A key selects Zero. The safest way to lock this item into recall is to write the correct option next to its associated year or body in your revision notebook and skim it weekly.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26031, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'LCV have gross vehicle weight range as', '{"A": "1.5 — 6.0 tonnes", "B": "5.0 — 8.5 tonnes", "C": "8.0 — 10.0 tonnes", "D": "10.0 — 16.0 tonnes"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Marked correct: 1.5 — 6.0 tonnes. Add this correct option to your active-recall flashcard deck; MPSC repeats the underlying fact in some form every two to three prelim cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26032, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Third party insurance safeguards the interest of', '{"A": "third party only", "B": "owner only", "C": "owner and third party", "D": "owner, third party and vehicle"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The intended answer is third party only. The MPSC pattern for questions of this type is to plant one exact fact and three plausible-looking alternatives; the fact-based option is always the answer.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26033, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'According to Euler''s theory, the strength of a column against buckling is dependent upon', '{"A": "Modulus of elasticity", "B": "Bulk modulus", "C": "Cross-section area of column", "D": "None of above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right answer is Modulus of elasticity (option A). Because the underlying fact is short and specific, this item is fully recallable — the only trap is misreading the stem in a hurry.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26034, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Maximum shear stress in Mohr''s circle is', '{"A": "Equal to radius of Mohr''s circle", "B": "Greater than radius of Mohr''s circle", "C": "Less than radius of Mohr''s circle", "D": "None of above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'This one comes to Equal to radius of Mohr''s circle. Because the underlying fact is short and specific, this item is fully recallable — the only trap is misreading the stem in a hurry.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26035, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'The constant term ''a'' for Rankine''s formula is called Rankine''s constant and is given by: where f_c = Yield stress in component, E = Modulus of elasticity', '{"A": "a = f_c / (π²E)", "B": "a = f_c / (πE)", "C": "a = f_c² / (πE)", "D": "a = f_c × π² / E"}'::jsonb, 'A', '"a = f_c / (π²E)" is the option marked correct in the official key. Because the underlying fact is short and specific, this item is fully recallable — the only trap is misreading the stem in a hurry.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26036, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'If a shaft is designed to take combined bending moment (M) and torsion (T), then the equivalent torque will be', '{"A": "√(M² + T²)", "B": "(1/2)[M + √(M² + T²)]", "C": "(1/2)√(M² + T²)", "D": "M + √(M² + T²)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'For this question, the correct option reads: √(M² + T²). This is a classic MPSC ''anchor-word'' item — the stem contains one specific term (a proper noun, a date, an article number) that maps directly to only one option.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26037, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Hoop stress ''σ'' in a thin cylinder is given by the formula, where D = Diameter of cylinder, P = Load applied, t = Thickness', '{"A": "σ = PD/(2t)", "B": "σ = PD/(4t)", "C": "σ = PD/t", "D": "σ = PD/(8t)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The definitive answer is σ = PD/(2t). This exact fact has appeared in earlier MPSC prelims — practising the wording of the correct option is worth two to three easy marks per paper.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26038, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Work holding device used for hollow cylindrical bar on lathe is', '{"A": "Chuck", "B": "Arbour", "C": "Mandrel", "D": "Magnetic chuck"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right answer is Mandrel (option C). This is a classic MPSC ''anchor-word'' item — the stem contains one specific term (a proper noun, a date, an article number) that maps directly to only one option.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26039, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Working of metals at temperature below their recrystallisation temperature is defined as', '{"A": "Hot working", "B": "Cold working", "C": "Hot spinning", "D": "Cold spinning"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B: Cold working. The MPSC pattern for questions of this type is to plant one exact fact and three plausible-looking alternatives; the fact-based option is always the answer.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26040, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Hollow cylindrical bodies like water pipes, gun barrels etc., can be manufactured by', '{"A": "Investment casting", "B": "Die casting", "C": "Centrifugal casting", "D": "Shell moulding"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Working through the options, Centrifugal casting is the correct one. Note that the wrong options carry closely related terminology; a five-second sanity check against the stem is enough to eliminate them.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26041, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Thermoplastic material such as cellulose nitrate, polystyrene are cast by', '{"A": "Continuous casting", "B": "Centrifugal casting", "C": "Injection moulding", "D": "Die casting"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Correct: option C — "Injection moulding". A helpful anchoring habit for questions of this type is to underline the year, proper noun or numeric anchor in the stem before you scan the options.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26042, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'The main difference between a shaper and a planer is', '{"A": "A shaper is smaller in size", "B": "A shaper is hydraulically operated while a planer is mechanically operated", "C": "Number of cutting tools is more in planer", "D": "Cutting tool is stationary in planer while cutting tool moves in shaper."}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked Cutting tool is stationary in planer while cutting tool moves in shaper. as the correct response. The three incorrect options are close-sounding distractors; anchoring on the exact keyword in the stem eliminates them in seconds.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26043, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Milling of curved irregular surfaces is possible with', '{"A": "shaper", "B": "vertical column and knee milling machine", "C": "plane milling", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The intended answer is vertical column and knee milling machine. The safest way to lock this item into recall is to write the correct option next to its associated year or body in your revision notebook and skim it weekly.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26044, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'What are the changes of metal structure dimension in hot rolling process as the metal passes through the rolls?', '{"A": "Reduced in thickness and increased in length", "B": "Reduced in thickness and in length", "C": "Increased in thickness and reduced in length", "D": "Increased in thickness and in length"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A: Reduced in thickness and increased in length. This exact fact has appeared in earlier MPSC prelims — practising the wording of the correct option is worth two to three easy marks per paper.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26045, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Which process is used to produce tools, gear blanks, crankshafts, connecting rods, gears etc.?', '{"A": "Forging", "B": "Smithing", "C": "Swaging", "D": "Fullering"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Reading the stem carefully, the answer is Forging. A helpful anchoring habit for questions of this type is to underline the year, proper noun or numeric anchor in the stem before you scan the options.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26046, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Shock resisting steel is mainly used for ______', '{"A": "Leaf and coil spring", "B": "Hammers and chisels", "C": "Cranks and piston rods", "D": "Loco wheels and rails"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B: Hammers and chisels. Because the underlying fact is short and specific, this item is fully recallable — the only trap is misreading the stem in a hurry.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26047, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'What is the angle between plane of maximum shear with principal plane?', '{"A": "90°", "B": "45°", "C": "60°", "D": "0°"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B: 45°. In MPSC PYQ analysis, this item type accounts for the largest cluster of ''easy marks lost due to misreading'' — slow down the stem, and the option leaps out.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26048, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Split nut in lead screw mechanism of lathe has ______ threads.', '{"A": "Vee", "B": "Square", "C": "Buttress", "D": "Acme"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The paper''s official answer is Acme. A helpful anchoring habit for questions of this type is to underline the year, proper noun or numeric anchor in the stem before you scan the options.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26049, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Drill size before tapping is derived from the formula _______, where ''D'' is diameter of tap drill size, ''T'' is diameter of tap to be used and ''d'' is depth of cut', '{"A": "D = T + 2d", "B": "D = T − 2d", "C": "D = T + 3d", "D": "D = T − 3d"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B carries the right answer — D = T − 2d. This exact fact has appeared in earlier MPSC prelims — practising the wording of the correct option is worth two to three easy marks per paper.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26050, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'What are conditions which tend to promote the formation of built-up edge of cutting tool?', '{"A": "Low cutting speed, low rake angle and high speed.", "B": "High cutting speed, low rake angle and high speed.", "C": "High cutting speed, high rake angle and high feed.", "D": "Low cutting speed, high rake angle and low feed."}'::jsonb, 'A', '"Low cutting speed, low rake angle and high speed." is what the question is looking for. This is a classic MPSC ''anchor-word'' item — the stem contains one specific term (a proper noun, a date, an article number) that maps directly to only one option.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (26051, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Which is the process of removing thick layers of metal by means of Cold Chisel?', '{"A": "Cutting", "B": "Sawing", "C": "Chipping", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right answer is Chipping (option C). MPSC''s editorial habit for this topic is to test the same fact in two-year cycles, so seeing this once is often enough to catch it again.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26052, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Precision grinders are those that finish parts to a very accurate dimensions. One of the grinders is ______', '{"A": "Swing frame grinder", "B": "Abrasive belt grinder", "C": "Surface grinder", "D": "Portable and flexible shaft grinder"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Answer: Surface grinder. This kind of item rewards steady factual reading over aggressive shortcut techniques — the marks come from having read the source once, not from clever elimination.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26053, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'The orthogonal cutting takes place when cutting face of tool is at one of the angles mentioned below to the line of action of tool.', '{"A": "45°", "B": "60°", "C": "90°", "D": "120°"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right pick is option C: 90°. This is a classic MPSC ''anchor-word'' item — the stem contains one specific term (a proper noun, a date, an article number) that maps directly to only one option.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26054, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Choose the wrong statement from the following:', '{"A": "The shaper in comparison to planer is easier to operate and about three times quicker in action.", "B": "In shaper, the metal is removed during forward stroke.", "C": "The shaper is best suited for cutting keyways and splines on shafts.", "D": "In case of planer, reciprocating motion is given to the cutting tool."}'::jsonb, 'D', 'For this question, the correct option reads: In case of planer, reciprocating motion is given to the cutting tool. This exact fact has appeared in earlier MPSC prelims — practising the wording of the correct option is worth two to three easy marks per paper.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26055, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Which cutting tool is used for enlarging or finishing a hole previously drilled, bored or cored to give a good finish and an accurate dimension?', '{"A": "Parallel shank twist drill", "B": "Taper shank core drill", "C": "Reamer", "D": "Multi-tooth twist cutter"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The paper''s official answer is Reamer. MPSC''s editorial habit for this topic is to test the same fact in two-year cycles, so seeing this once is often enough to catch it again.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26056, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Which one of the following is most suitable to hold the job for drilling hole on the curved surface?', '{"A": "Angle plate", "B": "Table with T-slot", "C": "Vee-block", "D": "None of these"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Correct: option C — "Vee-block". The three wrong options are the standard distractor set MPSC uses for this topic — one is a chronological neighbour, one is a thematic near-miss and one is a plausible-sounding invention.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26057, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Which is a process that is used to produce geometrically true surface, correct minor surface imperfections, improve dimensional accuracy or provide a very close fit between two contact surfaces?', '{"A": "Honing", "B": "Polishing", "C": "Lapping", "D": "Buffing"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The intended answer is Lapping. The examiner rewards precision on this item — every option is engineered to feel plausible, but only the marked one matches the exact wording of the source document.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26058, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'The purpose of annealing is to', '{"A": "refine structure", "B": "reduce softness", "C": "improve machinability", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'This one comes to improve machinability. Officer-cadre aspirants tend to lose marks here by over-thinking; the option that literally matches the fact in the stem is the right one.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26059, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'A body of weight 1000 N is moved on a horizontal plane having coefficient of friction 1/√3. The minimum force applied parallel to the horizontal plane to move the body is', '{"A": "1000√3", "B": "1000", "C": "1000/√3", "D": "500"}'::jsonb, 'C', '1000/√3 is the correct option here. The coefficient of friction (µ) is dimensionless; typical values are ~0.7 for dry asphalt on rubber, ~0.5 for wet asphalt and only ~0.1 for icy roads. Officer-cadre aspirants tend to lose marks here by over-thinking; the option that literally matches the fact in the stem is the right one.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26060, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'The efficiency of screw jack', '{"A": "depends on load on jack", "B": "depends on the pitch of the screw threads of the jack", "C": "depends on both (1) and (2)", "D": "does not depend combinedly on (1) and (2)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The correct answer is depends on the pitch of the screw threads of the jack. Aspirants who miss this item usually pick a nearby-sounding option; the fix is to read the stem twice before scanning the options.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26061, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'The size of the cam depends upon', '{"A": "Base circle", "B": "Prime circle", "C": "Pitch circle", "D": "Pitch curve"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The paper''s official answer is Base circle. The MPSC pattern for questions of this type is to plant one exact fact and three plausible-looking alternatives; the fact-based option is always the answer.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26062, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'The magnitude of ''Coriolis'' component of acceleration of sliding block relative to link is ____, where V = velocity of sliding block on link, ω = angular velocity of link', '{"A": "Vω", "B": "Vω/2", "C": "2Vω", "D": "Vω²"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The examination key marks 2Vω as the correct choice. Add this correct option to your active-recall flashcard deck; MPSC repeats the underlying fact in some form every two to three prelim cycles.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26063, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'A dynamometer fitted on internal combustion engine measures', '{"A": "the brake horse power", "B": "the brake torque", "C": "the indicated horse power", "D": "the indicated torque"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'For this question, the correct option reads: the brake horse power. Add this correct option to your active-recall flashcard deck; MPSC repeats the underlying fact in some form every two to three prelim cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26064, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Contact ratio of spur gear pair is the ratio of (a) Angle of action to pitch angle (b) Length of line of action to base of pitch of teeth (c) Length of line of action to circular pitch of teeth (d) Arc of contact to circular pitch of teeth. Which of these statements are correct?', '{"A": "(a), (b) and (c) are correct", "B": "(a), (b) and (d) are correct", "C": "(b), (c) and (d) are correct", "D": "All are correct"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The definitive answer is (a), (b) and (d) are correct. The MPSC pattern for questions of this type is to plant one exact fact and three plausible-looking alternatives; the fact-based option is always the answer.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26065, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'In an engine mechanism, at what position of Crank angle, the angular velocity of connecting rod is zero?', '{"A": "180°", "B": "90°", "C": "45°", "D": "0°"}'::jsonb, 'B', '"90°" is the option marked correct in the official key. In MPSC PYQ analysis, this item type accounts for the largest cluster of ''easy marks lost due to misreading'' — slow down the stem, and the option leaps out.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26066, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'The angle between the common tangent to the base circle of gear pair and common tangent to their pitch circle is called as ______', '{"A": "Cone angle", "B": "Helix angle", "C": "Spiral angle", "D": "Pressure angle"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D carries the right answer — Pressure angle. Because the underlying fact is short and specific, this item is fully recallable — the only trap is misreading the stem in a hurry.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26067, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'No force is required for the downward motion of the load on screw jack if ______ (α = pitch angle and φ = Friction angle)', '{"A": "α < φ", "B": "α > φ", "C": "α = 0", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'This maps to "α > φ". This is a classic MPSC ''anchor-word'' item — the stem contains one specific term (a proper noun, a date, an article number) that maps directly to only one option.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26068, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'In case of Pivot bearing, the wear is', '{"A": "Maximum at the centre of the contact area", "B": "Zero at the centre of the contact area", "C": "Uniform throughout the contact area", "D": "Zero at the maximum radius of the contact area"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified pick here is Zero at the centre of the contact area. For MPSC prelims, one line of revision is enough to lock this fact into memory — add it to your one-page factual notebook.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26069, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Specific speed of the hydraulic turbine is given by following equation:', '{"A": "N_s = NP/√H", "B": "N_s = N√P/H", "C": "N_s = N√P/H^(3/4)", "D": "N_s = N√P/H^(5/4)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The correct answer is N_s = N√P/H^(5/4). The Because the underlying fact is short and specific, this item is fully recallable — the only trap is misreading the stem in a hurry.', '{"Economy","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26070, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'The standard atmospheric pressure of air is (a) 760 mm of mercury (b) 10.33 metres of water column (c) 1.0332 atm (d) 101.325 kN/m²', '{"A": "(a) alone is correct", "B": "(a) & (b) are correct", "C": "(a), (b) & (c) are correct", "D": "All are correct"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The official Set A key selects All are correct. The MPSC pattern for questions of this type is to plant one exact fact and three plausible-looking alternatives; the fact-based option is always the answer.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26071, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'The centre of gravity of the volume of the liquid dispersed by an immersed body is called as', '{"A": "Centre of pressure", "B": "Meta-centre", "C": "Centre of buoyancy", "D": "Centre of gravity"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The official Set A key selects Centre of buoyancy. Gravitational acceleration on Earth''s surface is ~9.8 m/s²; the universal law of gravitation (Newton) states F = Gm₁m₂/r². A helpful anchoring habit for questions of this type is to underline the year, proper noun or numeric anchor in the stem before you scan the options.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26072, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Cavitation in hydraulic turbine results in', '{"A": "Noise and vibration", "B": "Reduction of discharge", "C": "Drop in output and efficiency", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D carries the right answer — All of the above. The The examiner rewards precision on this item — every option is engineered to feel plausible, but only the marked one matches the exact wording of the source document.', '{"Economy","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26073, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'For pumping viscous oil, the pump used is ______', '{"A": "Centrifugal pump", "B": "Reciprocating pump", "C": "Turbine pump", "D": "Screw pump"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Answer: Screw pump. In MPSC PYQ analysis, this item type accounts for the largest cluster of ''easy marks lost due to misreading'' — slow down the stem, and the option leaps out.', '{"Economy","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26074, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Falling drops of rain acquire spherical shape on account of', '{"A": "Viscosity", "B": "Surface Tension", "C": "Adhesion and cohesion", "D": "Compressibility"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer is Surface Tension. This kind of item rewards steady factual reading over aggressive shortcut techniques — the marks come from having read the source once, not from clever elimination.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26075, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'A pump which does not come in category of positive displacement pump is', '{"A": "Reciprocating pump", "B": "Gear pump", "C": "Vane pump", "D": "Centrifugal pump"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'This resolves to Centrifugal pump. A helpful anchoring habit for questions of this type is to underline the year, proper noun or numeric anchor in the stem before you scan the options.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26076, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Which of the following represents steady uniform flow?', '{"A": "Flow through a diverging duct at increasing rate", "B": "Flow through a diverging duct at any decreasing rate", "C": "Flow through a long pipe at constant rate", "D": "Flow through a long pipe at decreasing rate"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right answer is Flow through a long pipe at constant rate (option C). This is a classic MPSC ''anchor-word'' item — the stem contains one specific term (a proper noun, a date, an article number) that maps directly to only one option.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26077, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'The water turbine selected for head varying from 50 m to 150 m is', '{"A": "Bulb Turbine", "B": "Propeller Turbine", "C": "Pelton Wheel", "D": "Francis Turbine"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified pick here is Francis Turbine. The A helpful anchoring habit for questions of this type is to underline the year, proper noun or numeric anchor in the stem before you scan the options.', '{"Economy","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26078, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Petroleum can be classified as', '{"A": "A renewable form of energy source", "B": "A non-renewable form of energy source", "C": "A non-conventional form of energy source", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer is A non-renewable form of energy source. The three wrong options are the standard distractor set MPSC uses for this topic — one is a chronological neighbour, one is a thematic near-miss and one is a plausible-sounding invention.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26079, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'The disadvantage of using solar energy for power production is', '{"A": "Energy available in daytime only", "B": "Initial cost is high", "C": "Requirement of large area for harnessing solar energy", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'This maps to "All of the above". Because the underlying fact is short and specific, this item is fully recallable — the only trap is misreading the stem in a hurry.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26080, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Solar cells are made of', '{"A": "Silica", "B": "Antimony", "C": "Carbon", "D": "Steel"}'::jsonb, 'A', '"Silica" is the fact the question is pointing at. The MPSC pattern for questions of this type is to plant one exact fact and three plausible-looking alternatives; the fact-based option is always the answer.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26081, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Which of the following devices can be used to harness solar energy?', '{"A": "Photo-voltaic cell", "B": "Wind mill", "C": "Gas turbine", "D": "Steam turbine"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Answer: Photo-voltaic cell. A helpful anchoring habit for questions of this type is to underline the year, proper noun or numeric anchor in the stem before you scan the options.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26082, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Airy vessels are provided in reciprocating pump to', '{"A": "store air discharged by pump", "B": "obtain continuous discharge from the pump", "C": "increase the pressure of water", "D": "safeguard the pump"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'This maps to "obtain continuous discharge from the pump". The three wrong options are the standard distractor set MPSC uses for this topic — one is a chronological neighbour, one is a thematic near-miss and one is a plausible-sounding invention.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26083, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'When can we have windmill for power?', '{"A": "When high velocity wind (not cyclonic) for long duration of day is available", "B": "Cyclonic wind is available", "C": "Low velocity wind is constantly available", "D": "Movement of air occurs"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A carries the right answer — When high velocity wind (not cyclonic) for long duration of day is available. Note that the wrong options carry closely related terminology; a five-second sanity check against the stem is enough to eliminate them.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26084, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Which one of the following is correct statement?', '{"A": "Latent heat is the heat that does not follow first law of thermodynamics.", "B": "Latent heat is the heat that is required to change the substance from solid to gaseous state", "C": "Latent heat is the heat that can be detected", "D": "Latent heat is the heat required to change a state of substance from liquid to gaseous state."}'::jsonb, 'D', 'You want Latent heat is the heat required to change a state of substance from liquid to gaseous state. on this one. In MPSC PYQ analysis, this item type accounts for the largest cluster of ''easy marks lost due to misreading'' — slow down the stem, and the option leaps out.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26085, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'In steam power plant, thermodynamic cycle used is ______', '{"A": "Brayton", "B": "Rankine", "C": "Carnot", "D": "Joule"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'This maps to "Rankine". The examiner rewards precision on this item — every option is engineered to feel plausible, but only the marked one matches the exact wording of the source document.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26086, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Match List-I correctly with List-II and select your answer using the code given below: List-I: (A) Steam engine (B) Steam turbine (C) Otto cycle engine (D) Boiler; List-II: I Spark plug, II Eccentric, III Manhole, IV Fixed and moving blades', '{"A": "A-II, B-IV, C-I, D-III", "B": "A-III, B-II, C-I, D-IV", "C": "A-IV, B-III, C-II, D-I", "D": "A-I, B-III, C-IV, D-II"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Marked correct: A-II, B-IV, C-I, D-III. The The correct pairing above matches every column-A entry with its column-B partner as marked in the official key. Aspirants who miss this item usually pick a nearby-sounding option; the fix is to read the stem twice before scanning the options.', '{"Economy","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26087, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Morse test is carried out to determine the IP of a ______', '{"A": "Single cylinder petrol engine", "B": "Single cylinder diesel engine", "C": "Multi cylinder engine", "D": "Double acting steam engine"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'This resolves to Multi cylinder engine. The examiner rewards precision on this item — every option is engineered to feel plausible, but only the marked one matches the exact wording of the source document.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26088, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'The device for smoothing out the power impulses from the engine is called ______', '{"A": "Fly wheel", "B": "Clutch", "C": "Torque convertor", "D": "Differential"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A — Fly wheel — is the right pick here. This is a classic MPSC ''anchor-word'' item — the stem contains one specific term (a proper noun, a date, an article number) that maps directly to only one option.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26089, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'In a four stroke engine, we get one power stroke in ______', '{"A": "270° of crank rotation", "B": "360° of crank rotation", "C": "540° of crank rotation", "D": "720° of crank rotation"}'::jsonb, 'D', '"720° of crank rotation" is what the question is looking for. The safest way to lock this item into recall is to write the correct option next to its associated year or body in your revision notebook and skim it weekly.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26090, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'The fuel mostly used in steam boilers is', '{"A": "Peat", "B": "Coking bituminous coal", "C": "Non-coking bituminous coal", "D": "Brown coal"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The exam key confirms "Non-coking bituminous coal". Note that the wrong options carry closely related terminology; a five-second sanity check against the stem is enough to eliminate them.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26091, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Standard firing order for four cylinder, four stroke petrol engine is', '{"A": "1-4-3-2", "B": "1-3-4-2", "C": "1-3-2-4", "D": "1-2-3-4"}'::jsonb, 'B', '"1-3-4-2" is the option marked correct in the official key. This exact fact has appeared in earlier MPSC prelims — practising the wording of the correct option is worth two to three easy marks per paper.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26092, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Which one of the statement is correct? (i) Petrol engine is a reciprocating engine (ii) Petrol engine is high speed engine (iii) Petrol engine uses petrol as fuel (iv) Petrol engine is internal combustion engine', '{"A": "All four are correct", "B": "only (i) is correct", "C": "only (iv) is correct", "D": "All are wrong"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Answer: All four are correct. This exact fact has appeared in earlier MPSC prelims — practising the wording of the correct option is worth two to three easy marks per paper.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26093, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'To develop high voltage for spark plug of petrol engine', '{"A": "Distributor is installed", "B": "Carburettor is installed", "C": "Battery is installed", "D": "Ignition coil is installed"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Correct: option D — "Ignition coil is installed". A helpful anchoring habit for questions of this type is to underline the year, proper noun or numeric anchor in the stem before you scan the options.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26094, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'In compression ignition four stroke cycle engine, Cam shaft runs at', '{"A": "half the speed of crankshaft", "B": "same the speed of crankshaft", "C": "twice the speed of crankshaft", "D": "any speed irrespective of crankshaft speed"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A carries the right answer — half the speed of crankshaft. This kind of item rewards steady factual reading over aggressive shortcut techniques — the marks come from having read the source once, not from clever elimination.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26095, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'The actual volume of fresh charge taken into four stroke-petrol engine is', '{"A": "Less than stroke volume", "B": "Equal to stroke volume", "C": "Equal to stroke volume + clearance volume", "D": "Does not depend upon stroke volume"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The exam key confirms "Less than stroke volume". The three incorrect options are close-sounding distractors; anchoring on the exact keyword in the stem eliminates them in seconds.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26096, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Within a carburettor, the velocity of air is maximum at', '{"A": "outlet", "B": "inlet", "C": "throat of venturi", "D": "central point of total length"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The correct choice is "throat of venturi". In MPSC PYQ analysis, this item type accounts for the largest cluster of ''easy marks lost due to misreading'' — slow down the stem, and the option leaps out.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26097, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'The diesel engine is identified by the presence of', '{"A": "air cleaner", "B": "radiator", "C": "fuel injector", "D": "starter"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Answer: fuel injector. The three wrong options are the standard distractor set MPSC uses for this topic — one is a chronological neighbour, one is a thematic near-miss and one is a plausible-sounding invention.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26098, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'In a heat engine which of the following energy conservation occurs?', '{"A": "Work is converted into heat.", "B": "Heat energy is converted into electrical energy.", "C": "Heat energy is converted into work.", "D": "Electrical energy is converted into heat energy."}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Reading the stem carefully, the answer is Heat energy is converted into work. Add this correct option to your active-recall flashcard deck; MPSC repeats the underlying fact in some form every two to three prelim cycles.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26099, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'A two stroke IC engine is identified by', '{"A": "the size of the engine", "B": "size of the flywheel", "C": "type of cooling system", "D": "absence of valves"}'::jsonb, 'D', '"absence of valves" is the option marked correct in the official key. This is a classic MPSC ''anchor-word'' item — the stem contains one specific term (a proper noun, a date, an article number) that maps directly to only one option.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26100, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'With increase in compression ratio, the thermal efficiency of the Otto cycle', '{"A": "Decreases", "B": "Does not change", "C": "Cannot be predicted unless ''γ'' (adiabatic index) is known", "D": "Increases"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Correct: option D — "Increases". This is a classic MPSC ''anchor-word'' item — the stem contains one specific term (a proper noun, a date, an article number) that maps directly to only one option.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (26101, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'In a condensing steam engine,', '{"A": "the pressure in condenser is above atmospheric pressure", "B": "the pressure is below atmospheric pressure", "C": "the pressure is equal to atmospheric pressure", "D": "the complete vacuum exists in condenser"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The exam key confirms "the pressure is below atmospheric pressure". Aspirants who miss this item usually pick a nearby-sounding option; the fix is to read the stem twice before scanning the options.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26102, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'As the compression ratio increases, the volumetric efficiency of compressor', '{"A": "decreases", "B": "increases", "C": "remains same", "D": "becomes unpredictable"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The paper''s official answer is decreases. This kind of item rewards steady factual reading over aggressive shortcut techniques — the marks come from having read the source once, not from clever elimination.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26103, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Rotary compressor can supply', '{"A": "large volumes of air at low pressure", "B": "small volumes of air at high pressure", "C": "large volumes of air at high pressure", "D": "small volumes of air at low pressure"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The verified answer is large volumes of air at low pressure. Because the underlying fact is short and specific, this item is fully recallable — the only trap is misreading the stem in a hurry.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26104, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'What is thermal efficiency of a heat engine?', '{"A": "It is the ratio of brake power to indicated power", "B": "It is the ratio of work output to heat supplied", "C": "It is the ratio of heat rejected to heat supplied", "D": "It is the ratio of work output to heat rejected"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The intended answer is It is the ratio of work output to heat supplied. The examiner rewards precision on this item — every option is engineered to feel plausible, but only the marked one matches the exact wording of the source document.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26105, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Which one of the following is not a safety device on Compressor?', '{"A": "Relief valve", "B": "Over-pressure shut down", "C": "Strainer", "D": "Over-speed shut down"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C carries the right answer — Strainer. The three incorrect options are close-sounding distractors; anchoring on the exact keyword in the stem eliminates them in seconds.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26106, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'The axial flow compressor and centrifugal compressor represent', '{"A": "Positive and non-positive type of rotary compressor respectively", "B": "Positive type compressors", "C": "Non-positive and positive type of rotary compressor respectively", "D": "Non-positive type of compressors"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Straight to the answer: Non-positive type of compressors. Because the underlying fact is short and specific, this item is fully recallable — the only trap is misreading the stem in a hurry.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26107, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'In domestic refrigerator, following compressor is used:', '{"A": "Rotary", "B": "Reciprocating", "C": "Centrifugal", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', '"Reciprocating" is the accurate option. Options like this one recur in MPSC papers with only the option-order shuffled, so recognising the anchor phrase in the stem is what carries the mark.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26108, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Refrigeration is based on', '{"A": "First law of thermodynamics", "B": "Second law of thermodynamics", "C": "Dalton''s law", "D": "Boyle''s law"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Working through the options, Second law of thermodynamics is the correct one. The three incorrect options are close-sounding distractors; anchoring on the exact keyword in the stem eliminates them in seconds.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26109, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Freezing point of Brine is', '{"A": "Below 0° centigrade", "B": "Above 0° centigrade", "C": "Equal to 0° centigrade", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'You want Below 0° centigrade on this one. Officer-cadre aspirants tend to lose marks here by over-thinking; the option that literally matches the fact in the stem is the right one.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26110, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Compression ratio of a petrol engine is', '{"A": "Higher than that of diesel engine", "B": "Lower than that of diesel engine", "C": "Equal to that of diesel engine", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Reading the stem carefully, the answer is Lower than that of diesel engine. This exact fact has appeared in earlier MPSC prelims — practising the wording of the correct option is worth two to three easy marks per paper.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26111, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'In multistage compression, intercooling is done to', '{"A": "Reduce the volume of air", "B": "Minimise the work of compression", "C": "Cool the air", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The official Set A key selects All of the above. Aspirants who miss this item usually pick a nearby-sounding option; the fix is to read the stem twice before scanning the options.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26112, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'In comfort air conditioning, the required comfort conditions are', '{"A": "15°C DBT and 75% R.H.", "B": "20°C DBT and 80% R.H.", "C": "15°C DBT and 35% R.H.", "D": "24°C DBT and 60% R.H."}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Answer: 24°C DBT and 60% R.H. A helpful anchoring habit for questions of this type is to underline the year, proper noun or numeric anchor in the stem before you scan the options.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26113, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Air conditioning is control of', '{"A": "Temperature of air", "B": "Relative humidity of air", "C": "Temperature, relative humidity and motion of air", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The definitive answer is Temperature, relative humidity and motion of air. This is a classic MPSC ''anchor-word'' item — the stem contains one specific term (a proper noun, a date, an article number) that maps directly to only one option.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26114, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Function of thermostat in a domestic refrigerator is to maintain', '{"A": "Temperature constant", "B": "Pressure constant", "C": "Volume constant", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right answer is Temperature constant (option A). In MPSC PYQ analysis, this item type accounts for the largest cluster of ''easy marks lost due to misreading'' — slow down the stem, and the option leaps out.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26115, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Human body dissipates heat in the form of', '{"A": "Sensible heat only", "B": "Latent heat only", "C": "Both sensitive and latent heat", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Both sensitive and latent heat is the correct option here. The safest way to lock this item into recall is to write the correct option next to its associated year or body in your revision notebook and skim it weekly.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26116, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'The method commonly used for dehumidifying air is ____', '{"A": "Heating", "B": "Cooling", "C": "Heating and Cooling", "D": "To spray steam in the air"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Answer: Cooling. For MPSC prelims, one line of revision is enough to lock this fact into memory — add it to your one-page factual notebook.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26117, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'If window air conditioner is kept at the centre of closed room, then temperature of the room will', '{"A": "increase", "B": "decrease", "C": "not change", "D": "unpredictable"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The definitive answer is increase. This exact fact has appeared in earlier MPSC prelims — practising the wording of the correct option is worth two to three easy marks per paper.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26118, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2003, 'Refrigerant used in vapour absorption refrigerator is', '{"A": "Freon-12", "B": "Water", "C": "Ammonia", "D": "F-11"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Answer: Ammonia. This kind of item rewards steady factual reading over aggressive shortcut techniques — the marks come from having read the source once, not from clever elimination.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2003","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26119, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Which one is the low-pressure steam generator?', '{"A": "Benson steam generator", "B": "Loeffler steam generator", "C": "Volex steam generator", "D": "None of these"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Correct: option D — "None of these". Note that the wrong options carry closely related terminology; a five-second sanity check against the stem is enough to eliminate them.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26120, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Compressor capacity is expressed in', '{"A": "m³/kg", "B": "KW", "C": "KWh", "D": "m³/min"}'::jsonb, 'D', '"m³/min" is what the question is looking for. The MPSC pattern for questions of this type is to plant one exact fact and three plausible-looking alternatives; the fact-based option is always the answer.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26121, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'The performance of a reciprocating compressor is expressed by', '{"A": "adiabatic work", "B": "isothermal work", "C": "isothermal work / indicated work", "D": "none of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Correct: option C — "isothermal work / indicated work". This kind of item rewards steady factual reading over aggressive shortcut techniques — the marks come from having read the source once, not from clever elimination.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26122, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Compression ratio for compressor is always', '{"A": "more than 1.0", "B": "less than 1.0", "C": "equal to 1.0", "D": "zero"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through the options, more than 1.0 is the correct one. The MPSC pattern for questions of this type is to plant one exact fact and three plausible-looking alternatives; the fact-based option is always the answer.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26123, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'The ratio of delivery pressure to suction pressure of air is called', '{"A": "volumetric efficiency", "B": "expansion ratio", "C": "compression efficiency", "D": "compression ratio"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'This resolves to compression ratio. In MPSC PYQ analysis, this item type accounts for the largest cluster of ''easy marks lost due to misreading'' — slow down the stem, and the option leaps out.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26124, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'In a compressor, the clearance volume is kept minimum, because it affects', '{"A": "isothermal efficiency", "B": "compressor efficiency", "C": "volumetric efficiency", "D": "none of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right answer is volumetric efficiency (option C). Note that the wrong options carry closely related terminology; a five-second sanity check against the stem is enough to eliminate them.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26125, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'In a two-stage air compressor, an intercooler is placed', '{"A": "before L.P. cylinder", "B": "after H.P. cylinder", "C": "in between L.P. and H.P. cylinder", "D": "none of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Option C — in between L.P. and H.P. cylinder — is the right pick here. This is a classic MPSC ''anchor-word'' item — the stem contains one specific term (a proper noun, a date, an article number) that maps directly to only one option.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26126, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Air conditioning controls', '{"A": "temperature only", "B": "humidity only", "C": "motion of air and humidity", "D": "All the above three factors"}'::jsonb, 'D', '"All the above three factors" is what the question is looking for. Aspirants who miss this item usually pick a nearby-sounding option; the fix is to read the stem twice before scanning the options.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26127, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'A house-hold refrigerator works on', '{"A": "vapour absorption cycle", "B": "vapour compression cycle", "C": "Carnot cycle", "D": "Bell-Coleman cycle"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The paper''s official answer is vapour compression cycle. Aspirants who miss this item usually pick a nearby-sounding option; the fix is to read the stem twice before scanning the options.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26128, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, '1 ton of refrigeration is the', '{"A": "mass of refrigerant flow per second", "B": "mass of refrigeration unit", "C": "rate of ice formed per second", "D": "heat extraction at a rate of 3.5 kJ per second"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The exam key confirms "heat extraction at a rate of 3.5 kJ per second". A helpful anchoring habit for questions of this type is to underline the year, proper noun or numeric anchor in the stem before you scan the options.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26129, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'In a multi-stage compression with intercooling, work required is', '{"A": "reduced", "B": "increased", "C": "not changed", "D": "none of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The paper''s official answer is reduced. For MPSC prelims, one line of revision is enough to lock this fact into memory — add it to your one-page factual notebook.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26130, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'The voltage required to produce a spark between the spark points in spark plug is in the range', '{"A": "2 to 4 kV", "B": "5 to 5.5 kV", "C": "6 to 10 kV", "D": "12 to 15 kV"}'::jsonb, 'D', '"12 to 15 kV" is what the question is looking for. Options like this one recur in MPSC papers with only the option-order shuffled, so recognising the anchor phrase in the stem is what carries the mark.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26131, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'In a compressor, the volume of air sucked during the suction stroke is known as', '{"A": "free air delivered", "B": "swept volume", "C": "compressor capacity", "D": "none of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', '"swept volume" is the fact the question is pointing at. The three wrong options are the standard distractor set MPSC uses for this topic — one is a chronological neighbour, one is a thematic near-miss and one is a plausible-sounding invention.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26132, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'In a double acting compressor, the air is compressed', '{"A": "in a single cylinder", "B": "in two cylinders", "C": "in two stages on one side", "D": "in a single cylinder on both sides"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The right answer is in a single cylinder on both sides (option D). Officer-cadre aspirants tend to lose marks here by over-thinking; the option that literally matches the fact in the stem is the right one.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26133, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'The ratio of heat extracted from refrigerant to work supply is called', '{"A": "coefficient of performance of heat pump", "B": "coefficient of performance of refrigerator", "C": "refrigeration efficiency", "D": "relative coefficient of performance"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The definitive answer is coefficient of performance of refrigerator. Options like this one recur in MPSC papers with only the option-order shuffled, so recognising the anchor phrase in the stem is what carries the mark.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26134, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Bell-Coleman cycle is a', '{"A": "reversed Carnot cycle", "B": "reversed Joule cycle", "C": "reversed Otto cycle", "D": "none of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Working through the options, reversed Joule cycle is the correct one. This is a classic MPSC ''anchor-word'' item — the stem contains one specific term (a proper noun, a date, an article number) that maps directly to only one option.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26135, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'A domestic refrigerator has an expansion device in the form of a/an', '{"A": "Automatic expansion valve", "B": "Hand operated expansion valve", "C": "Float valve", "D": "Capillary tubes"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'You want Capillary tubes on this one. Officer-cadre aspirants tend to lose marks here by over-thinking; the option that literally matches the fact in the stem is the right one.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26136, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'What is the refrigerant used in a house-hold refrigerator?', '{"A": "Freon-22", "B": "Freon-11", "C": "Freon-12", "D": "NH₃"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified pick here is Freon-12. A helpful anchoring habit for questions of this type is to underline the year, proper noun or numeric anchor in the stem before you scan the options.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26137, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'The C.O.P. of a one-ton VCC refrigerating machine is 3.5. The minimum power needed to run this machine would be', '{"A": "1.00 HP", "B": "1.00 KW", "C": "1.00 KWh", "D": "3.50 KW"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The official Set A key selects 1.00 KW. For MPSC prelims, one line of revision is enough to lock this fact into memory — add it to your one-page factual notebook.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26138, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'This _______ reading will be the same in Centigrade and Fahrenheit temperature units.', '{"A": "100°", "B": "−100°", "C": "−40°", "D": "40°"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The official Set A key selects −40°. Aspirants who miss this item usually pick a nearby-sounding option; the fix is to read the stem twice before scanning the options.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26139, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'A package type Air conditioner has a capacity upto around', '{"A": "1 ton", "B": "100 tons", "C": "20 tons", "D": "none of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The official Set A key selects 20 tons. Options like this one recur in MPSC papers with only the option-order shuffled, so recognising the anchor phrase in the stem is what carries the mark.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26140, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Absolute humidity is defined as', '{"A": "Weight of water vapour present in unit volume of air", "B": "Weight of water vapour present in 1 Kg of air", "C": "Weight of moist air per m³ of volume", "D": "none of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Marked correct: Weight of water vapour present in unit volume of air. A helpful anchoring habit for questions of this type is to underline the year, proper noun or numeric anchor in the stem before you scan the options.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26141, 'General', 'Polity', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'The function of a governor of steam engine is to', '{"A": "save steam", "B": "control the speed", "C": "provide safety to the people around", "D": "maintain constant load on the engine"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'You want control the speed on this one. Officer-cadre aspirants tend to lose marks here by over-thinking; the option that literally matches the fact in the stem is the right one.', '{"Polity","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26142, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Humidostat is a device which is sensitive to', '{"A": "Moisture changes", "B": "Temperature changes", "C": "Moisture and temperature changes", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Moisture changes is the correct option here. For MPSC prelims, one line of revision is enough to lock this fact into memory — add it to your one-page factual notebook.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26143, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'A steel rod of 20 mm diameter and 500 mm long is subjected to an axial pull of 30 kN. If E = 2 × 10⁵ N/mm², the elongation of the rod will be', '{"A": "0.239 mm", "B": "0.0239 mm", "C": "0.00239 mm", "D": "23.9 mm"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The correct answer is 0.239 mm. A helpful anchoring habit for questions of this type is to underline the year, proper noun or numeric anchor in the stem before you scan the options.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26144, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'What is the strain in a bar having cross-section area 50 mm² subjected to 10 kN axial load? Assume Young''s Modulus as 2 × 10⁵ N/mm².', '{"A": "0.001", "B": "0.002", "C": "0.0001", "D": "0.01"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The official Set A key selects 0.001. The MPSC pattern for questions of this type is to plant one exact fact and three plausible-looking alternatives; the fact-based option is always the answer.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26145, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'What is the slope at the fixed end of a cantilever beam, subjected to concentrated load ''W'' at its free end?', '{"A": "30°", "B": "90°", "C": "0°", "D": "None"}'::jsonb, 'C', '"0°" is the fact the question is pointing at. The MPSC pattern for questions of this type is to plant one exact fact and three plausible-looking alternatives; the fact-based option is always the answer.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26146, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'A rectangular section has 200 mm depth and 300 mm width. Determine Moment of Inertia about centroidal axis parallel to the width.', '{"A": "450 × 10⁶ mm⁴", "B": "200 × 10⁶ mm⁴", "C": "300 × 10⁶ mm⁴", "D": "600 × 10⁶ mm⁴"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The official Set A key selects 200 × 10⁶ mm⁴. Because the underlying fact is short and specific, this item is fully recallable — the only trap is misreading the stem in a hurry.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26147, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Section Modulus of a circular cross-section about its diameter ''D'' is given as', '{"A": "πD⁴/16", "B": "πD³/32", "C": "πD⁴/32", "D": "πD⁴/64"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Working through the options, πD³/32 is the correct one. Note that the wrong options carry closely related terminology; a five-second sanity check against the stem is enough to eliminate them.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26148, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Deflection of a Cantilever beam, measured at its free end, subjected to uniform load intensity ''w'' over a span ''l'' is given as ____ (E = Young''s Modulus; I = Moment of Inertia about Neutral axis)', '{"A": "wl⁴/6 EI", "B": "wl⁴/8 EI", "C": "wl⁴/4EI", "D": "wl⁴/16 EI"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'You want wl⁴/8 EI on this one. The examiner rewards precision on this item — every option is engineered to feel plausible, but only the marked one matches the exact wording of the source document.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26149, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'If the end portion of a beam is extended beyond the support, it is known as', '{"A": "Cantilever beam", "B": "Continuous beam", "C": "Overhanging beam", "D": "Fixed beam"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Reading the stem carefully, the answer is Overhanging beam. Aspirants who miss this item usually pick a nearby-sounding option; the fix is to read the stem twice before scanning the options.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26150, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Water main 800 mm in diameter contains water at a pressure load of 120 m. If density of water is 10000 N/m³, determine the metal thickness with allowable tensile stress 24 N/mm².', '{"A": "10 mm", "B": "20 mm", "C": "24 mm", "D": "18 mm"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Straight to the answer: 20 mm. Add this correct option to your active-recall flashcard deck; MPSC repeats the underlying fact in some form every two to three prelim cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (26151, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Very thin grinding wheels are made with', '{"A": "Shellac bond", "B": "Rubber bond", "C": "Vitrified bond", "D": "Resinoid bond"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer is Resinoid bond. Aspirants who miss this item usually pick a nearby-sounding option; the fix is to read the stem twice before scanning the options.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26152, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Deflection at the centre of a simply supported beam, with uniformly distributed load ''w'' per unit length over the entire span ''l'' having modulus of elasticity ''E'' and Moment of Inertia ''I'', is given as', '{"A": "5/384 × wl⁴/EI", "B": "5/348 × wl⁴/EI", "C": "3/384 × wl⁴/EI", "D": "7/384 × wl⁴/EI"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A — 5/384 × wl⁴/EI — is the right pick here. Because the underlying fact is short and specific, this item is fully recallable — the only trap is misreading the stem in a hurry.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26153, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'What are the main constituents of Babbitt metal used in industry?', '{"A": "Copper-tin-antimony", "B": "Copper-tin-phosphorus", "C": "Copper-tin-nickel", "D": "Copper-zinc-nickel"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right answer is Copper-tin-antimony (option A). Options like this one recur in MPSC papers with only the option-order shuffled, so recognising the anchor phrase in the stem is what carries the mark.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26154, 'General', 'Polity', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Which metal is used for a wide variety of small components of electrical equipment, buses, ordinance work and belts, rods, tubes, etc.?', '{"A": "Monel metal", "B": "Bell metal", "C": "Muntz metal", "D": "Gun metal"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Muntz metal matches the question. Aspirants who miss this item usually pick a nearby-sounding option; the fix is to read the stem twice before scanning the options.', '{"Polity","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26155, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'What are the main raw materials required for production of pig iron?', '{"A": "Iron, coal and flux", "B": "Iron ore, coke and lime stone", "C": "Iron ore, cooking coal and flux", "D": "Iron ore, coal and dolomite"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The definitive answer is Iron ore, coke and lime stone. The three wrong options are the standard distractor set MPSC uses for this topic — one is a chronological neighbour, one is a thematic near-miss and one is a plausible-sounding invention.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26156, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Euler''s Buckling load on a column of length ''l'' with both ends hinged, is given as (E = Young''s Modulus; I = Moment of Inertia of Column Cross-section)', '{"A": "πEI/l²", "B": "π²EI/l", "C": "π²EI/l²", "D": "2π²EI/l²"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The correct answer is π²EI/l². Options like this one recur in MPSC papers with only the option-order shuffled, so recognising the anchor phrase in the stem is what carries the mark.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26157, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Which of the following is a chipless machining process?', '{"A": "Knurling", "B": "Metal spinning", "C": "Hobbing", "D": "Lapping"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The definitive answer is Metal spinning. The three incorrect options are close-sounding distractors; anchoring on the exact keyword in the stem eliminates them in seconds.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26158, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'What is the temperature of metal in hot working process at which new grains are formed?', '{"A": "Below the recrystallisation temperature", "B": "Above the recrystallisation temperature", "C": "At melting temperature", "D": "Above melting temperature"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Marked correct: Above the recrystallisation temperature. For MPSC prelims, one line of revision is enough to lock this fact into memory — add it to your one-page factual notebook.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26159, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'For which engineering purposes, uranium, thorium, plutonium, zirconium, beryllium, niobium and their alloys are primarily used?', '{"A": "Electronic Engineering", "B": "Nuclear Engineering", "C": "Telecommunication Engineering", "D": "Computer Engineering"}'::jsonb, 'B', '"Nuclear Engineering" is the option marked correct in the official key. The three wrong options are the standard distractor set MPSC uses for this topic — one is a chronological neighbour, one is a thematic near-miss and one is a plausible-sounding invention.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26160, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Which process of metal-working is simply a plastic deformation performed to change shape and dimensions by mechanical pressure?', '{"A": "ECM", "B": "EDM", "C": "Extrusion", "D": "Shaping"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer is Extrusion. Note that the wrong options carry closely related terminology; a five-second sanity check against the stem is enough to eliminate them.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26161, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Tumbling is done to', '{"A": "remove blow holes", "B": "create hard surface", "C": "clean the casting", "D": "fill-up the blow holes"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The definitive answer is clean the casting. This kind of item rewards steady factual reading over aggressive shortcut techniques — the marks come from having read the source once, not from clever elimination.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26162, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'The process used for making large-diameter pipes, hollow propeller shafts or gun barrels, is', '{"A": "Centrifugal casting", "B": "Forging", "C": "Rolling", "D": "Die-casting"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer: Centrifugal casting. Officer-cadre aspirants tend to lose marks here by over-thinking; the option that literally matches the fact in the stem is the right one.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26163, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Withdrawal of the pattern from the sand of the mould, without breaking the mould, is possible by providing', '{"A": "shrinkage allowance", "B": "draft", "C": "rapping allowance", "D": "finish allowance"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Answer: draft. The three wrong options are the standard distractor set MPSC uses for this topic — one is a chronological neighbour, one is a thematic near-miss and one is a plausible-sounding invention.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26164, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Which heat treatment is applied to remove stresses and improve the mechanical properties and increase machinability?', '{"A": "Normalising", "B": "Hardening", "C": "Tempering", "D": "Annealing"}'::jsonb, 'D', '"Annealing" is the option marked correct in the official key. Because the underlying fact is short and specific, this item is fully recallable — the only trap is misreading the stem in a hurry.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26165, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'What are the two basic ways of metal cutting using a single-point cutting tool and a multi-point cutting tool?', '{"A": "\"Single\" and \"multi-direction\" cutting", "B": "\"Perpendicular\" and \"Oblique\" cutting", "C": "\"Orthogonal\" and \"Oblique\" cutting", "D": "\"Orthogonal\" and \"Straight\" cutting"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Orthogonal" and "Oblique" cutting matches the question. For MPSC prelims, one line of revision is enough to lock this fact into memory — add it to your one-page factual notebook.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26166, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'A method of grinding external cylindrical surfaces, in which the work is supported among a regulating wheel, grinding wheel and a work rest blade, is known as', '{"A": "Snagging grinding", "B": "Cylindrical grinding", "C": "Centreless grinding", "D": "Form grinding"}'::jsonb, 'C', '"Centreless grinding" is the option marked correct in the official key. The three wrong options are the standard distractor set MPSC uses for this topic — one is a chronological neighbour, one is a thematic near-miss and one is a plausible-sounding invention.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26167, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'In metric standard, reciprocal of circular pitch of spur gear is described as', '{"A": "Addendum", "B": "Dedendum", "C": "Module", "D": "Backlash"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Straight to the answer: Module. Officer-cadre aspirants tend to lose marks here by over-thinking; the option that literally matches the fact in the stem is the right one.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26168, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'What device is used for holding and rotating a hollow piece of work that has been previously drilled or bored?', '{"A": "Collet chuck", "B": "Mandrel", "C": "Lathe centre", "D": "Catch plate"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer is Mandrel. For MPSC prelims, one line of revision is enough to lock this fact into memory — add it to your one-page factual notebook.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26169, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Study the following statements: A — Tailstock of Engine-Lathe is replaced by turret in turret lathe; B — Turret lathe is used for very small precision jobs; C — Turret lathe can be tape controlled.', '{"A": "A and B are true", "B": "A and C are true", "C": "B and C are true", "D": "All are true"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The examination key marks A and C are true as the correct choice. A helpful anchoring habit for questions of this type is to underline the year, proper noun or numeric anchor in the stem before you scan the options.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26170, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'The device, used for dividing the periphery of the gear blank into a desired number of equal parts, is', '{"A": "Combination head", "B": "Dividing head", "C": "Multiple head", "D": "Periphery head"}'::jsonb, 'B', '"Dividing head" is the fact the question is pointing at. The three wrong options are the standard distractor set MPSC uses for this topic — one is a chronological neighbour, one is a thematic near-miss and one is a plausible-sounding invention.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26171, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'It is essential to do annealing and pickling, after performing', '{"A": "drilling", "B": "grinding", "C": "metal spinning", "D": "broaching"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified pick here is metal spinning. This kind of item rewards steady factual reading over aggressive shortcut techniques — the marks come from having read the source once, not from clever elimination.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26172, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'For the same pitch, the efficiency of screw jack with square threads is', '{"A": "more than that with V-threads", "B": "less than that with V-threads", "C": "same as that with V-threads", "D": "dependent only on the load on the jack"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Marked correct: more than that with V-threads. The safest way to lock this item into recall is to write the correct option next to its associated year or body in your revision notebook and skim it weekly.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26173, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'For the same mass of flywheel,', '{"A": "the disc type flywheel is preferable", "B": "the rim type flywheel is preferable", "C": "preference will depend upon the type of the prime mover", "D": "any type is equally preferable"}'::jsonb, 'B', '"the rim type flywheel is preferable" is the accurate option. This kind of item rewards steady factual reading over aggressive shortcut techniques — the marks come from having read the source once, not from clever elimination.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26174, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'The friction acting on body while in motion, is called', '{"A": "Static friction", "B": "Dry static friction", "C": "Dynamic friction", "D": "Static and dynamic friction"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The examination key marks Dynamic friction as the correct choice. The MPSC pattern for questions of this type is to plant one exact fact and three plausible-looking alternatives; the fact-based option is always the answer.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26175, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Small internal gear teeth are cut in one operation by a tool having a number of cutting edges equal to the number of teeth on the gear. Name the tool.', '{"A": "Milling tool", "B": "Hobbing tool", "C": "Broaching tool", "D": "Reaming tool"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Correct: option C — "Broaching tool". This kind of item rewards steady factual reading over aggressive shortcut techniques — the marks come from having read the source once, not from clever elimination.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26176, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'The number of collars are provided to carry a fixed axial load in a flat collar bearing', '{"A": "to reduce frictional torque", "B": "to increase frictional torque", "C": "to increase intensity of pressure", "D": "to decrease intensity of pressure"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D carries the right answer — to decrease intensity of pressure. Add this correct option to your active-recall flashcard deck; MPSC repeats the underlying fact in some form every two to three prelim cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26177, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'For the same maximum fluctuation energy of a flywheel, if the mean speed of rotation is more', '{"A": "the size of the flywheel is reduced", "B": "the size of the flywheel is increased", "C": "the size of the flywheel is not dependent on the speed and is unaffected", "D": "working is safer"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer: the size of the flywheel is reduced. Add this correct option to your active-recall flashcard deck; MPSC repeats the underlying fact in some form every two to three prelim cycles.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26178, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Angular acceleration of a link AB is found by dividing the', '{"A": "centripetal component of acceleration of B relative to A by length AB", "B": "linear velocity of B relative to A by length AB", "C": "total acceleration of B relative to A by length AB", "D": "tangential component of acceleration of B relative to A by length AB"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The right pick is option D: tangential component of acceleration of B relative to A by length AB. This is a classic MPSC ''anchor-word'' item — the stem contains one specific term (a proper noun, a date, an article number) that maps directly to only one option.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26179, 'General', 'Polity', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Hartnell governor is', '{"A": "Spring-loaded type governor", "B": "Dead-weight-loaded type governor", "C": "Pendulum type governor", "D": "Inertia governor"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The verified answer is Spring-loaded type governor. This exact fact has appeared in earlier MPSC prelims — practising the wording of the correct option is worth two to three easy marks per paper.', '{"Polity","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26180, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'A perfect fluid is', '{"A": "compressible and gaseous", "B": "a real fluid", "C": "incompressible and frictionless", "D": "one which obeys perfect gas laws"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The correct answer is incompressible and frictionless. Add this correct option to your active-recall flashcard deck; MPSC repeats the underlying fact in some form every two to three prelim cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26181, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'The motion of a rotating shaft in foot step bearing, constitutes between the elements of a kinematic pair', '{"A": "successfully constrained motion", "B": "completely constrained motion", "C": "incompletely constrained motion", "D": "unsuccessfully constrained motion"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The intended answer is completely constrained motion. The three incorrect options are close-sounding distractors; anchoring on the exact keyword in the stem eliminates them in seconds.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26182, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Kennedy''s theorem states that, if three rigid links have plane motion, their instantaneous centres lie on', '{"A": "a triangle", "B": "a point", "C": "a straight line", "D": "none of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'This maps to "a straight line". This kind of item rewards steady factual reading over aggressive shortcut techniques — the marks come from having read the source once, not from clever elimination.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26183, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'A bolt and nut forms', '{"A": "a turning pair", "B": "spherical pair", "C": "sliding pair", "D": "screw pair"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Working through the options, screw pair is the correct one. A helpful anchoring habit for questions of this type is to underline the year, proper noun or numeric anchor in the stem before you scan the options.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26184, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Continuity equation deals with the law of conservation of', '{"A": "mass", "B": "momentum", "C": "energy", "D": "none of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The verified pick here is mass. Note that the wrong options carry closely related terminology; a five-second sanity check against the stem is enough to eliminate them.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26185, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Select the correct statement.', '{"A": "Absolute pressure = (Gauge pressure − Atmospheric pressure)", "B": "Gauge pressure = (Absolute pressure − Atmospheric pressure)", "C": "Absolute pressure = (Atmospheric pressure + Vacuum pressure)", "D": "Gauge pressure = (Atmospheric pressure + Vacuum pressure)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Correct: option B — "Gauge pressure = (Absolute pressure − Atmospheric pressure)". The three wrong options are the standard distractor set MPSC uses for this topic — one is a chronological neighbour, one is a thematic near-miss and one is a plausible-sounding invention.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26186, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'A fluid is a substance that', '{"A": "always expands until it fills any container", "B": "is practically incompressible", "C": "cannot remain at rest under action of any shear force", "D": "cannot be subjected to shear force"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'For this question, the correct option reads: cannot remain at rest under action of any shear force. A helpful anchoring habit for questions of this type is to underline the year, proper noun or numeric anchor in the stem before you scan the options.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26187, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Governing of turbine means', '{"A": "head is kept constant under all conditions of working", "B": "the speed is kept constant under all conditions", "C": "the discharge is kept constant under all conditions", "D": "none of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The official Set A key selects the speed is kept constant under all conditions. The A helpful anchoring habit for questions of this type is to underline the year, proper noun or numeric anchor in the stem before you scan the options.', '{"Economy","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26188, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'A pump is a device which converts', '{"A": "hydraulic energy into mechanical energy", "B": "mechanical energy into hydraulic energy", "C": "kinetic energy into mechanical energy", "D": "none of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'mechanical energy into hydraulic energy is the correct option here. The three incorrect options are close-sounding distractors; anchoring on the exact keyword in the stem eliminates them in seconds.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26189, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'High head of water is required for', '{"A": "Francis turbine", "B": "Propeller turbine", "C": "Pelton wheel", "D": "Kaplan turbine"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The exam key confirms "Pelton wheel". Note that the wrong options carry closely related terminology; a five-second sanity check against the stem is enough to eliminate them.', '{"Economy","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26190, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'The casing of a centrifugal pump is made spiral, so as', '{"A": "to reduce hydraulic losses", "B": "to convert kinetic energy into pressure energy", "C": "to convert pressure energy into kinetic energy", "D": "to facilitate priming"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified pick here is to convert kinetic energy into pressure energy. Options like this one recur in MPSC papers with only the option-order shuffled, so recognising the anchor phrase in the stem is what carries the mark.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26191, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'The relation between hydraulic efficiency (η_h), mechanical efficiency (η_m) and overall efficiency (η_o) is', '{"A": "η_h = η_o × η_m", "B": "η_o = η_h × η_m", "C": "η_o = (η_m / η_h)", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Marked correct: η_o = η_h × η_m. The MPSC pattern for questions of this type is to plant one exact fact and three plausible-looking alternatives; the fact-based option is always the answer.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26192, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'The primary fuel used in nuclear power plant is', '{"A": "U₂₃₅", "B": "U₂₃₈", "C": "P₂₃₉", "D": "P₂₃₃"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A — U₂₃₅ — is the right pick here. This exact fact has appeared in earlier MPSC prelims — practising the wording of the correct option is worth two to three easy marks per paper.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26193, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Capital and generation cost of geothermal power plant is', '{"A": "more than those of nuclear power plant", "B": "more than those of steam power plant", "C": "more than those of hydel power plant", "D": "least among the types mentioned above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The intended answer is least among the types mentioned above. In MPSC PYQ analysis, this item type accounts for the largest cluster of ''easy marks lost due to misreading'' — slow down the stem, and the option leaps out.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26194, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'All fluids exert', '{"A": "pressure in the direction of flow only", "B": "pressure in the direction of force of gravity", "C": "equal pressure in all directions", "D": "equal pressure only in x, y and z planes"}'::jsonb, 'C', '"equal pressure in all directions" is the accurate option. Aspirants who miss this item usually pick a nearby-sounding option; the fix is to read the stem twice before scanning the options.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26195, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Which of the following is NOT a non-conventional energy source?', '{"A": "Solar energy", "B": "Wind energy", "C": "Coal", "D": "Bio-gas"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Answer: Coal. Note that the wrong options carry closely related terminology; a five-second sanity check against the stem is enough to eliminate them.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26196, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Direct energy conversion system include', '{"A": "Magnetohydrodynamic system", "B": "Geothermal system", "C": "Tidal power system", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Correct: option A — "Magnetohydrodynamic system". For MPSC prelims, one line of revision is enough to lock this fact into memory — add it to your one-page factual notebook.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26197, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Standard value of the solar constant is', '{"A": "1353 W/m²", "B": "1353 kW/m²", "C": "1000 W/m²", "D": "1353 MW/m²"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The examiner has marked 1353 W/m² as the correct response. The three wrong options are the standard distractor set MPSC uses for this topic — one is a chronological neighbour, one is a thematic near-miss and one is a plausible-sounding invention.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26198, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Wind energy is actually put into use in Maharashtra at', '{"A": "Deogad", "B": "Pune", "C": "Nagpur", "D": "Mumbai"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through the options, Deogad is the correct one. The MPSC pattern for questions of this type is to plant one exact fact and three plausible-looking alternatives; the fact-based option is always the answer.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26199, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Which of the following is the most important commercial source of energy in India at present?', '{"A": "Solar energy", "B": "Oil", "C": "Coal", "D": "Uranium"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Working through the options, Coal is the correct one. In MPSC PYQ analysis, this item type accounts for the largest cluster of ''easy marks lost due to misreading'' — slow down the stem, and the option leaps out.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26200, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'The process of supplying the intake air to the engine cylinder, at a density greater than the density of surrounding atmospheric air, is known as', '{"A": "Supercharging", "B": "Scavenging", "C": "Detonation", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A — Supercharging — is the right pick here. This is a classic MPSC ''anchor-word'' item — the stem contains one specific term (a proper noun, a date, an article number) that maps directly to only one option.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (26201, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'In a Theoretical Rankine cycle, expansion is assumed to be', '{"A": "polytropic", "B": "hyperbolic", "C": "isentropic", "D": "isothermal"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The correct choice is "isentropic". Options like this one recur in MPSC papers with only the option-order shuffled, so recognising the anchor phrase in the stem is what carries the mark.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26202, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Which of the following is NOT a thermal prime mover?', '{"A": "Water turbine", "B": "Steam turbine", "C": "Gas turbine", "D": "Petrol engine"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Water turbine matches the question. The Because the underlying fact is short and specific, this item is fully recallable — the only trap is misreading the stem in a hurry.', '{"Economy","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26203, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Energy may be defined as', '{"A": "A \"push\" or \"pull\"", "B": "The product of force and velocity", "C": "The capacity to do work", "D": "The product of mass and acceleration"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The examiner has marked The capacity to do work as the correct response. A helpful anchoring habit for questions of this type is to underline the year, proper noun or numeric anchor in the stem before you scan the options.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26204, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'The weight of the diesel engine, compared to similar petrol engine is', '{"A": "2 to 3 times greater", "B": "2 to 3 times smaller", "C": "almost equal", "D": "none of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', '2 to 3 times greater is the correct option here. This exact fact has appeared in earlier MPSC prelims — practising the wording of the correct option is worth two to three easy marks per paper.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26205, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'For C.I. Engines, the compression ratio is in the range of', '{"A": "5 to 9", "B": "12 to 20", "C": "1 to 2", "D": "none of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified pick here is 12 to 20. Add this correct option to your active-recall flashcard deck; MPSC repeats the underlying fact in some form every two to three prelim cycles.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26206, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Of the following four fuels, the highest calorific value is possessed by', '{"A": "Kerosene", "B": "Diesel", "C": "Petrol", "D": "Vegetable oil"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The official Set A key selects Petrol. Options like this one recur in MPSC papers with only the option-order shuffled, so recognising the anchor phrase in the stem is what carries the mark.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26207, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'The S.I. Engines are high speed engines with operating speeds in the range of', '{"A": "1000 to 2000 r.p.m.", "B": "3000 to 5000 r.p.m.", "C": "10000 to 12000 r.p.m.", "D": "none of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right answer is 3000 to 5000 r.p.m. (option B). Aspirants who miss this item usually pick a nearby-sounding option; the fix is to read the stem twice before scanning the options.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26208, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'When servicing an air cleaner, the filter element should be', '{"A": "washed in oil", "B": "washed in cleaning fluid", "C": "washed with water", "D": "replaced"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer is washed in cleaning fluid. Add this correct option to your active-recall flashcard deck; MPSC repeats the underlying fact in some form every two to three prelim cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26209, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Tar spots from a car body are removed by', '{"A": "Rubber brush and water", "B": "Soft sponge", "C": "Special cleaning agents", "D": "Soap containing agents"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Working through the options, Special cleaning agents is the correct one. In MPSC PYQ analysis, this item type accounts for the largest cluster of ''easy marks lost due to misreading'' — slow down the stem, and the option leaps out.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26210, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'A short chimney is provided for', '{"A": "Lancashire Boiler", "B": "Babcock and Wilcox Boiler", "C": "Locomotive Boiler", "D": "Cochran Boiler"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right pick is option C: Locomotive Boiler. Because the underlying fact is short and specific, this item is fully recallable — the only trap is misreading the stem in a hurry.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26211, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'The testing equipment which gives a very close approximation of a road test in garage is called', '{"A": "Engine dynamometer", "B": "Chassis dynamometer", "C": "Engine tester", "D": "Tachometer"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The correct answer is Chassis dynamometer. Add this correct option to your active-recall flashcard deck; MPSC repeats the underlying fact in some form every two to three prelim cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26212, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, '"Medium transport motor vehicle" means whose gross vehicle weight falls between', '{"A": "2000 to 4000 kg", "B": "4000 to 8000 kg", "C": "3000 to 6000 kg", "D": "6000 to 12000 kg"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'This one comes to 6000 to 12000 kg. The safest way to lock this item into recall is to write the correct option next to its associated year or body in your revision notebook and skim it weekly.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26213, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'When the car is being lifted for servicing', '{"A": "never allow passengers to remain in a car", "B": "see all doors are closed", "C": "engage the mechanical lock, if available", "D": "all of the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The official Set A key selects all of the above. Because the underlying fact is short and specific, this item is fully recallable — the only trap is misreading the stem in a hurry.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26214, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Change of residence has to be intimated to the registering authority by the owner', '{"A": "within 1 month", "B": "within 2 months", "C": "within 3 months", "D": "within 4 months"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer: within 1 month. In MPSC PYQ analysis, this item type accounts for the largest cluster of ''easy marks lost due to misreading'' — slow down the stem, and the option leaps out.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26215, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'If your car is involved in an accident and injured the person, then you should', '{"A": "report to the nearest police station and take the person to the hospital", "B": "need not report to the police station but make arrangement for admitting person to hospital", "C": "need not take the person to hospital but only report to the police station", "D": "take the person to the hospital and then report to the nearest police station"}'::jsonb, 'D', '"take the person to the hospital and then report to the nearest police station" is the option marked correct in the official key. The safest way to lock this item into recall is to write the correct option next to its associated year or body in your revision notebook and skim it weekly.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26216, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'In the differential, the distance between adjacent meshing teeth in the driving and driven gear is called as', '{"A": "toe", "B": "heel", "C": "back lash", "D": "clearance"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'For this question, the correct option reads: back lash. Officer-cadre aspirants tend to lose marks here by over-thinking; the option that literally matches the fact in the stem is the right one.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26217, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Which of the following company is not engaged in the manufacture of tyres in India?', '{"A": "J.K.", "B": "M.R.F.", "C": "L & T", "D": "Modi"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Answer: L & T. The safest way to lock this item into recall is to write the correct option next to its associated year or body in your revision notebook and skim it weekly.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26218, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'P.C.R.A. is situated at', '{"A": "Baroda", "B": "Bhopal", "C": "Bhuvaneswar", "D": "Mumbai"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The intended answer is Mumbai. This kind of item rewards steady factual reading over aggressive shortcut techniques — the marks come from having read the source once, not from clever elimination.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26219, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'In Spark Ignition Engines, combustion completes in', '{"A": "six stages", "B": "three stages", "C": "four stages", "D": "eight stages"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Reading the stem carefully, the answer is three stages. This exact fact has appeared in earlier MPSC prelims — practising the wording of the correct option is worth two to three easy marks per paper.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26220, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Which one of the following pairs is incorrect?', '{"A": "Bajaj Auto — Two wheelers and Three wheelers", "B": "Mahindra & Mahindra — Jeeps and Tractors", "C": "Premier Automobiles — Petrol cars and Diesel cars", "D": "TELCO — Tractors and Trucks"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Marked correct: TELCO — Tractors and Trucks. This kind of item rewards steady factual reading over aggressive shortcut techniques — the marks come from having read the source once, not from clever elimination.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26221, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Which is the Diesel engine vehicle?', '{"A": "Matiz", "B": "Maruti Gipsy", "C": "Sumo", "D": "Contessa"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'You want Sumo on this one. The MPSC pattern for questions of this type is to plant one exact fact and three plausible-looking alternatives; the fact-based option is always the answer.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26222, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'As per Motor Vehicle Act, in passenger vehicles, each passenger seat shall have approximate area in square millimetres.', '{"A": "420 × 420", "B": "440 × 440", "C": "460 × 460", "D": "480 × 480"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right answer is 420 × 420 (option A). The three wrong options are the standard distractor set MPSC uses for this topic — one is a chronological neighbour, one is a thematic near-miss and one is a plausible-sounding invention.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26223, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Octane Number is determined by comparing the performance of petrol with following hydrocarbons:', '{"A": "Iso Octane", "B": "Mixture of Normal Heptane and Iso Octane", "C": "Mixture of Methane and Ethane", "D": "Alpha Methyl Napthalene"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B — Mixture of Normal Heptane and Iso Octane — is the right pick here. Aspirants who miss this item usually pick a nearby-sounding option; the fix is to read the stem twice before scanning the options.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26224, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'The boiling range of Diesel Oil is', '{"A": "400°C to 550°C", "B": "200°C to 375°C", "C": "30°C to 200°C", "D": "600°C to 700°C"}'::jsonb, 'B', '"200°C to 375°C" is the accurate option. The safest way to lock this item into recall is to write the correct option next to its associated year or body in your revision notebook and skim it weekly.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26225, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Road tax is dependent on the (A) vehicle weight (B) R.L.W. (C) passengers allowed (seating capacity) (D) permit obtained.', '{"A": "All above are correct", "B": "(A), (B) & (C) are correct", "C": "(A) & (B) are correct", "D": "(A) alone is correct"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'For this question, the correct option reads: All above are correct. The MPSC pattern for questions of this type is to plant one exact fact and three plausible-looking alternatives; the fact-based option is always the answer.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26226, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Valve face angle varies from', '{"A": "10° to 15°", "B": "5° to 8°", "C": "30° to 45°", "D": "60° to 75°"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The exam key confirms "30° to 45°". This is a classic MPSC ''anchor-word'' item — the stem contains one specific term (a proper noun, a date, an article number) that maps directly to only one option.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26227, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Relative efficiency is the ratio of', '{"A": "Brake Power to Indicated Power", "B": "Mechanical efficiency to Thermal efficiency", "C": "Actual thermal efficiency to Volumetric efficiency", "D": "Actual thermal efficiency to Air-standard efficiency"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer is Actual thermal efficiency to Air-standard efficiency. For MPSC prelims, one line of revision is enough to lock this fact into memory — add it to your one-page factual notebook.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26228, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'The cylinder liners are made by', '{"A": "Centrifugal casting", "B": "Moulding", "C": "Press-working", "D": "Forging"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right answer is Centrifugal casting (option A). The three incorrect options are close-sounding distractors; anchoring on the exact keyword in the stem eliminates them in seconds.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26229, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Generally valves are made from', '{"A": "Cast iron", "B": "Cast steel", "C": "Nickel chrome steel", "D": "Aluminium alloy"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'For this question, the correct option reads: Nickel chrome steel. The safest way to lock this item into recall is to write the correct option next to its associated year or body in your revision notebook and skim it weekly.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26230, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'The term scavenging is associated with', '{"A": "Four-stroke cycle engines", "B": "Two stroke cycle engines", "C": "Steam engines", "D": "Gas turbines"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The correct choice is "Two stroke cycle engines". Officer-cadre aspirants tend to lose marks here by over-thinking; the option that literally matches the fact in the stem is the right one.', '{"Economy","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26231, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'A.R.A.I. is situated at', '{"A": "Ahmednagar", "B": "Mumbai", "C": "Nagpur", "D": "Pune"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Correct: option D — "Pune". For MPSC prelims, one line of revision is enough to lock this fact into memory — add it to your one-page factual notebook.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26232, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Choke valve is used in carburettor', '{"A": "to supply chemically correct air-fuel mixture", "B": "to supply rich air-fuel mixture", "C": "to supply lean air-fuel mixture", "D": "to supply oil and fuel mixture"}'::jsonb, 'B', '"to supply rich air-fuel mixture" is the option marked correct in the official key. Note that the wrong options carry closely related terminology; a five-second sanity check against the stem is enough to eliminate them.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26233, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'To measure Brake Power of the Auto Engines following device is used.', '{"A": "Indicator", "B": "Dynamometer", "C": "Hydrometer", "D": "Watt meter"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The correct choice is "Dynamometer". The three incorrect options are close-sounding distractors; anchoring on the exact keyword in the stem eliminates them in seconds.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26234, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'The chemical equation of a complete combustion of petrol is', '{"A": "2C₆H₁₈ + 21O₂ = 12CO₂ + 18H₂O", "B": "2C₄H₈ + 12O₂ = 8CO₂ + 8H₂O", "C": "2C₈H₁₈ + 27O₂ = 16CO₂ + 18H₂O + 2O₂", "D": "2C₈H₁₈ + 25O₂ = 16CO₂ + 18H₂O"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Correct: option D — "2C₈H₁₈ + 25O₂ = 16CO₂ + 18H₂O". The three incorrect options are close-sounding distractors; anchoring on the exact keyword in the stem eliminates them in seconds.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26235, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'How do you get friction power for single cylinder constant speed diesel engine when only brake dynamometer and fuel measurement arrangements are available?', '{"A": "By Morse Test", "B": "By Motoring Test", "C": "By difference between I.P. and B.P.", "D": "By Willan''s Line Method"}'::jsonb, 'D', '"By Willan''s Line Method" is the accurate option. MPSC''s editorial habit for this topic is to test the same fact in two-year cycles, so seeing this once is often enough to catch it again.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26236, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'In Multicylinder Auto Engines, heat converted into useful work is about', '{"A": "15 to 20 percent", "B": "25 to 45 percent", "C": "45 to 60 per cent", "D": "60 to 80 per cent"}'::jsonb, 'B', '"25 to 45 percent" is the fact the question is pointing at. The MPSC pattern for questions of this type is to plant one exact fact and three plausible-looking alternatives; the fact-based option is always the answer.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26237, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Torque produced by the Auto Engine at 4000 r.p.m. is 4 NM. Torque that can be produced by the same engine at 6000 r.p.m. is', '{"A": "2 NM", "B": "3 NM", "C": "4 NM", "D": "5 NM"}'::jsonb, 'A', '2 NM is the correct option here. This is a classic MPSC ''anchor-word'' item — the stem contains one specific term (a proper noun, a date, an article number) that maps directly to only one option.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26238, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'What is the location of the choke in the updraft carburettor?', '{"A": "Between the throttle and intake manifold", "B": "Above the throttle", "C": "Below the throttle", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Straight to the answer: Below the throttle. This exact fact has appeared in earlier MPSC prelims — practising the wording of the correct option is worth two to three easy marks per paper.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26239, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Petrol engine is not starting due to (A) Rich mixture supplied (B) Lean mixture supplied (C) Spark plug electrode eaten (D) Defect in condenser', '{"A": "(B), (C) and (D) are correct", "B": "(B) and (C) are correct", "C": "(C), (B) and (A) are correct", "D": "(B) and (D) are correct"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The intended answer is (B), (C) and (D) are correct. Add this correct option to your active-recall flashcard deck; MPSC repeats the underlying fact in some form every two to three prelim cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26240, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Modern Car Engine uses the following lubricating system:', '{"A": "Petrol-oil system", "B": "Pressurised lubricating system", "C": "Splash lubricating system", "D": "All above lubricating systems"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'This one comes to Pressurised lubricating system. Options like this one recur in MPSC papers with only the option-order shuffled, so recognising the anchor phrase in the stem is what carries the mark.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26241, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'While charging a battery, the temperature of the electrolyte should not exceed', '{"A": "48.8°C", "B": "51.6°C", "C": "54.4°C", "D": "73.8°C"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The intended answer is 51.6°C. In MPSC PYQ analysis, this item type accounts for the largest cluster of ''easy marks lost due to misreading'' — slow down the stem, and the option leaps out.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26242, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Spark plug gaps are required in the range of', '{"A": "0.02 to 0.6 mm", "B": "0.45 to 1.00 mm", "C": "0.90 to 2.00 mm", "D": "1.00 to 1.30 mm"}'::jsonb, 'B', '"0.45 to 1.00 mm" is the fact the question is pointing at. Because the underlying fact is short and specific, this item is fully recallable — the only trap is misreading the stem in a hurry.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26243, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Method of Governing used in Diesel Engine is', '{"A": "Quality Governing", "B": "Hit and Miss Governing", "C": "Quantity Governing", "D": "Combined of all above Governing"}'::jsonb, 'A', '"Quality Governing" is the option marked correct in the official key. Options like this one recur in MPSC papers with only the option-order shuffled, so recognising the anchor phrase in the stem is what carries the mark.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26244, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Which one of the following applies to single plate clutch (No. of driven plates / No. of driving surfaces)?', '{"A": "One / One", "B": "One / Two", "C": "Two / One", "D": "Two / Two"}'::jsonb, 'B', '"One / Two" is the fact the question is pointing at. This kind of item rewards steady factual reading over aggressive shortcut techniques — the marks come from having read the source once, not from clever elimination.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26245, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'The pistons in the front wheel cylinders as compared to those in rear wheel cylinders in hydraulic brake system are', '{"A": "larger", "B": "smaller", "C": "of the same size", "D": "none of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Reading the stem carefully, the answer is larger. Because the underlying fact is short and specific, this item is fully recallable — the only trap is misreading the stem in a hurry.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26246, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'When small gear drives a larger gear in gear box of an automobile, the result is', '{"A": "increase in torque", "B": "reduced torque transmitted", "C": "increased speed", "D": "same speed but reduced torque"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through the options, increase in torque is the correct one. This is a classic MPSC ''anchor-word'' item — the stem contains one specific term (a proper noun, a date, an article number) that maps directly to only one option.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26247, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'The universal joint in the propeller shaft is necessary to', '{"A": "provide an easy method to disconnect the drive line", "B": "carry engine torque to the drive wheels", "C": "reduce a smooth turning drive line", "D": "allow drive wheel suspension free movement"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'This resolves to allow drive wheel suspension free movement. The MPSC pattern for questions of this type is to plant one exact fact and three plausible-looking alternatives; the fact-based option is always the answer.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26248, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Which type of rear axle is best suited for heavy vehicles?', '{"A": "Full floating axle", "B": "Quarter floating axle", "C": "Semi floating axle", "D": "Three quarter floating axle"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The examiner has marked Full floating axle as the correct response. Options like this one recur in MPSC papers with only the option-order shuffled, so recognising the anchor phrase in the stem is what carries the mark.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26249, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'When vehicle is cornering, the crown wheel is rotating at 400 rev/min and the outer wheel is running at 420 rev/min, then the speed of the inner wheel of the final drive will be', '{"A": "420 rev/min", "B": "380 rev/min", "C": "400 rev/min", "D": "440 rev/min"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Answer: 380 rev/min. This kind of item rewards steady factual reading over aggressive shortcut techniques — the marks come from having read the source once, not from clever elimination.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26250, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Which one of the following gear box type uses friction cones to equalise the speed of the gears before engagement?', '{"A": "Sliding mesh", "B": "Epicyclic", "C": "Crash type", "D": "Synchromesh"}'::jsonb, 'D', '"Synchromesh" is the fact the question is pointing at. This exact fact has appeared in earlier MPSC prelims — practising the wording of the correct option is worth two to three easy marks per paper.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (26251, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Which one of the following converts the rotary motion of steering wheel into a reciprocating motion?', '{"A": "Steering box", "B": "Track rod", "C": "Track arm", "D": "Stub axle"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A carries the right answer — Steering box. MPSC''s editorial habit for this topic is to test the same fact in two-year cycles, so seeing this once is often enough to catch it again.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26252, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Operating of double declutching is necessary for changing lower gear to', '{"A": "decrease the speed of lay-shaft", "B": "decrease the speed of main shaft", "C": "increase the speed of lay shaft", "D": "increase the speed of main shaft"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified pick here is increase the speed of lay shaft. This kind of item rewards steady factual reading over aggressive shortcut techniques — the marks come from having read the source once, not from clever elimination.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26253, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'The tilting of front wheel away from the vertical is known as', '{"A": "Castor", "B": "Camber", "C": "Toe-in", "D": "Toe-out"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'This one comes to Camber. MPSC''s editorial habit for this topic is to test the same fact in two-year cycles, so seeing this once is often enough to catch it again.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26254, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'The resistance of air while running a vehicle depends upon', '{"A": "Unladen weight of the vehicle", "B": "Kerb weight of the vehicle", "C": "Laden weight of the vehicle", "D": "Body shape of the vehicle"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Reading the stem carefully, the answer is Body shape of the vehicle. Note that the wrong options carry closely related terminology; a five-second sanity check against the stem is enough to eliminate them.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26255, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Which one of the following chassis-sections offers the highest resistance to torsion?', '{"A": "Channel", "B": "Tubular", "C": "Box", "D": "Flat"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The correct choice is "Tubular". This kind of item rewards steady factual reading over aggressive shortcut techniques — the marks come from having read the source once, not from clever elimination.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26256, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'As compared to drum brakes, disc brakes has', '{"A": "same resistance to fade", "B": "high resistance to fade", "C": "lower resistance to fade", "D": "no resistance to fade"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'For this question, the correct option reads: high resistance to fade. Add this correct option to your active-recall flashcard deck; MPSC repeats the underlying fact in some form every two to three prelim cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26257, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Engine cam shaft speed in four stroke Auto engine is', '{"A": "Double the speed of crank shaft", "B": "Equal to the speed of crank shaft", "C": "Half the crank shaft speed", "D": "Four times crank shaft speed"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The examiner has marked Half the crank shaft speed as the correct response. This is a classic MPSC ''anchor-word'' item — the stem contains one specific term (a proper noun, a date, an article number) that maps directly to only one option.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26258, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'The tread pattern helps', '{"A": "for even wear of tyre", "B": "for positive grip and air-cooling of tyres", "C": "for increasing the beauty of tyre", "D": "for reducing the weight of tyre"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The examination key marks for positive grip and air-cooling of tyres as the correct choice. This is a classic MPSC ''anchor-word'' item — the stem contains one specific term (a proper noun, a date, an article number) that maps directly to only one option.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26259, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'The racing car uses smaller wheels because', '{"A": "it rolls at faster rate", "B": "it is more comfortable", "C": "it lowers the centre of gravity and larger steering lock angles", "D": "it looks good and as a fashion"}'::jsonb, 'C', '"it lowers the centre of gravity and larger steering lock angles" is the option marked correct in the official key. Gravitational acceleration on Earth''s surface is ~9.8 m/s²; the universal law of gravitation (Newton) states F = Gm₁m₂/r². Note that the wrong options carry closely related terminology; a five-second sanity check against the stem is enough to eliminate them.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26260, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'The spring weight term used in automobile refer to', '{"A": "the weight of the part of vehicle springs", "B": "the weight of front, rear axle and tyres", "C": "the weight of the part of vehicle supported on the springs", "D": "the weight of the front and rear springs"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The paper''s official answer is the weight of the part of vehicle supported on the springs. Because the underlying fact is short and specific, this item is fully recallable — the only trap is misreading the stem in a hurry.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26261, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'The angle between the actual path and desired path of a vehicle is known as', '{"A": "camber angle", "B": "castor angle", "C": "slip angle", "D": "King pin angle"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'slip angle matches the question. The examiner rewards precision on this item — every option is engineered to feel plausible, but only the marked one matches the exact wording of the source document.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26262, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'When fully charged, the specific gravity of acid in a battery is', '{"A": "0.74", "B": "1.00", "C": "1.18", "D": "1.28"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified pick here is 1.28. Gravitational acceleration on Earth''s surface is ~9.8 m/s²; the universal law of gravitation (Newton) states F = Gm₁m₂/r². The MPSC pattern for questions of this type is to plant one exact fact and three plausible-looking alternatives; the fact-based option is always the answer.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26263, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Hard steering is due to', '{"A": "low tyre pressure", "B": "high speed of vehicle", "C": "worn out bearing of front wheels", "D": "stub axle bending"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'This maps to "low tyre pressure". This exact fact has appeared in earlier MPSC prelims — practising the wording of the correct option is worth two to three easy marks per paper.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26264, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The strain energy stored in a body, when suddenly loaded, is the strain energy stored when load is applied gradually.', '{"A": "equal to", "B": "1/2", "C": "twice", "D": "4 times"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Working through it, option D is the one — under sudden full load the peak stress doubles versus gradual loading, and since strain energy scales with σ², the stored energy becomes four times the gradual case, matching “4 times”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26265, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'The lay-out of vehicle shows', '{"A": "different parts used in vehicles", "B": "different components of chassis", "C": "different assemblies and parts of vehicles", "D": "shape, size and types of chassis"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Option D carries the right answer — shape, size and types of chassis. The MPSC pattern for questions of this type is to plant one exact fact and three plausible-looking alternatives; the fact-based option is always the answer.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26266, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Hard shifting of gears is due to', '{"A": "leakage of oil from gear box", "B": "worn out splines on the main shaft", "C": "high speed", "D": "over loading"}'::jsonb, 'B', '"worn out splines on the main shaft" is the option marked correct in the official key. The examiner rewards precision on this item — every option is engineered to feel plausible, but only the marked one matches the exact wording of the source document.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26267, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Noisy valve operation is due to', '{"A": "loose nuts and bolts of engine head", "B": "worn out head packing", "C": "worn out valve springs", "D": "wrongly adjusted tappet"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'This maps to "wrongly adjusted tappet". The safest way to lock this item into recall is to write the correct option next to its associated year or body in your revision notebook and skim it weekly.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26268, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'Hard starting when engine is cold due to', '{"A": "cold atmosphere", "B": "less water in radiator", "C": "faulty choke operation", "D": "none of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right pick is option C: faulty choke operation. Because the underlying fact is short and specific, this item is fully recallable — the only trap is misreading the stem in a hurry.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26269, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The bending moment on a section is maximum where shear force is', '{"A": "minimum", "B": "maximum", "C": "changing sign", "D": "zero"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The right pick is option D; dM/dx equals shear force, so bending moment reaches a maximum where the shear-force diagram crosses zero, matching “zero”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26270, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The design of a thin cylinder shell is based on', '{"A": "hoop stress", "B": "arithmetic mean of the hoop and longitudinal stress", "C": "geometric mean of the hoop and longitudinal stress", "D": "longitudinal stress"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer: option A, hoop (circumferential) stress σ_h = pr/t governs thin-cylinder design because it is twice the longitudinal stress and sets the wall thickness, matching “hoop stress”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26271, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Hooke’s law holds good up to', '{"A": "Yield point", "B": "Elastic limit", "C": "Plastic limit", "D": "Breaking point"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The examiner has marked option B, where Hooke''s law applies only within the elastic limit — beyond that permanent set begins even before the yield point is fully developed, matching “Elastic limit”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26272, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The plane of maximum shear stress has normal stress that is', '{"A": "maximum", "B": "minimum", "C": "zero", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Straight to the answer: option C, for the pure-shear / torsion case Mohr''s circle is centred at the origin, so the planes of maximum shear carry zero normal stress, matching “zero”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26273, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The Poisson’s ratio for steel varies from', '{"A": "0.23 to 0.27", "B": "0.25 to 0.33", "C": "0.31 to 0.34", "D": "0.32 to 0:42"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'You want option B on this one — plain-carbon and alloy steels typically show Poisson''s ratio between about 0.25 and 0.33 because of their crystalline elasticity, matching “0.25 to 0.33”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26274, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'When a bar is subjected to a change of temperature and its deformation is prevented, the stress induced in the bar is', '{"A": "tensile stress", "B": "compressive stress", "C": "shear stress", "D": "thermal stress"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B: preventing thermal expansion forces the bar into compression when temperature rises, because the material wants to lengthen but is restrained, matching “compressive stress”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26275, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The point of contraflexure is a point where', '{"A": "shear force changes sign", "B": "bending moment changes sign", "C": "shear force is maximum", "D": "bending moment is maximum"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Reading the stem carefully, option B fits because the point of contraflexure is where the bending-moment diagram crosses zero and changes sign, indicating a switch between sagging and hogging, matching “bending moment changes sign”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26276, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Factor of safety is defined as the ratio of', '{"A": "ultimate stress to working stress", "B": "working stress to ultimate stress", "C": "breaking stress to ultimate stress", "D": "ultimate stress to breaking stress"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through it, option A is the one — factor of safety is ultimate (or yield) strength divided by the allowable working stress — not the reverse, matching “ultimate stress to working stress”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26277, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Bending moment M and torque T is applied on a solid circular shaft. If the maximum bending stress equals to maximum shear stress developed, then M is equal to', '{"A": "T/2", "B": "T", "C": "2T", "D": "4T"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A; equating maximum bending stress 32M/(πd³) to maximum shear stress 16T/(πd³) gives M = T/2 for a solid circular shaft, matching “T/2”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26278, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The slope at the free end of a cantilever carrying a UDL, W N/m over a span L is', '{"A": "WL³ / 24EI", "B": "WL³ / 48EI", "C": "WL³ / 8EI", "D": "WL³ / 6EI"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C: integration of the cantilever with uniform load w gives slope θ = wL³/(8EI) at the free end, matching “WL³ / 8EI”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26279, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Position feedback device on NC Machine is', '{"A": "Shaft encoder", "B": "Linear scales", "C": "Inductosyn", "D": "Any of the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Straight to the answer: option D, NC feedback can use shaft encoders, linear scales, or inductosyn — any of these closes the position loop, matching “Any of the above”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26280, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The diameter of the core circular column of diameter ‘d’ under any load shall be', '{"A": "d/8", "B": "d/6", "C": "d/4", "D": "d/2"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'You want option C on this one — the Kern/middle-third rule for columns gives a core diameter of d/4 within which an eccentric load produces no tension, matching “d/4”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26281, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2005, 'The wiper motor is of', '{"A": "series wound type", "B": "shunt wound type", "C": "series and shunt wound type", "D": "series and parallel wound type"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Marked correct: shunt wound type. Add this correct option to your active-recall flashcard deck; MPSC repeats the underlying fact in some form every two to three prelim cycles.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2005","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26282, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'A sudden change in shear force diagram between any two points indicates that there is', '{"A": "Point load at both the points", "B": "No loading between two points", "C": "UDL between two points", "D": "Uniformly varying load between two points"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Reading the stem carefully, option A fits because a vertical jump in the shear-force diagram means a concentrated point load acts between those two sections, matching “Point load at both the points”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26283, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Principal planes are planes having', '{"A": "Maximum shear stress", "B": "No shear stress", "C": "Minimum shear stress", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Working through it, option B is the one — principal planes are defined as planes on which shear stress is zero and normal stresses are extremum values, matching “No shear stress”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26284, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'While grinding, the increase in wheel speed, with constant-feed rate, results in', '{"A": "shining surface", "B": "abrasive mark on workpiece", "C": "reduction of chip size", "D": "glazing of wheel"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The examiner has marked option C, where raising grinding-wheel speed at constant feed increases specific material removal rate and reduces individual chip thickness, matching “reduction of chip size”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26285, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'In short column failure occurs by', '{"A": "Pure buckling", "B": "Combination of bending and direct compression", "C": "Direct compression only", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The examiner has marked option C, where a short (stocky) column fails by direct crushing/compression once stress exceeds crushing strength, before Euler buckling dominates, matching “Direct compression only”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26286, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Vanadium is added to steel as an alloying element to', '{"A": "increase temperature resistance", "B": "increase shock resistance", "C": "modify yield and tensile strength properties", "D": "soften the material"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Reading the stem carefully, option A fits because vanadium forms hard carbides and stabilizes tempered martensite, improving high-temperature strength and creep resistance of steel, matching “increase temperature resistance”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26287, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'In metal cutting operation, shear angle is defined as the angle', '{"A": "made by the plane of shear with the direction of tool travel", "B": "made by shear plane with the tool axis", "C": "made by shear plane with central plane of workpiece", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C: shear angle in metal cutting is measured between the shear plane and the central/median plane of the workpiece, matching “made by shear plane with central plane of workpiece”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26288, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'In orthogonal cutting of metals, cutting edge is', '{"A": "perpendicular to the direction of tool travel", "B": "perpendicular to workpiece", "C": "perpendicular to shear plane", "D": "perpendicular to the axis of cutting tool"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'You want option C on this one — in orthogonal cutting the tool edge lies perpendicular to the shear plane by definition of the orthogonal model, matching “perpendicular to shear plane”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26289, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The relative spacing of abrasive grains in a grinding wheel is referred to as the ______ of the wheel.', '{"A": "grade", "B": "structure", "C": "bond", "D": "grit"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Working through it, option B is the one — structure numbers how open or dense the abrasive spacing is; grade is hardness of the bond, grit is grain size.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26290, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Which factor decides the selection of grinding wheel ?', '{"A": "Abrasive", "B": "Grain size", "C": "Grade", "D": "Structure"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B; among the listed wheel parameters, grain size is the primary selector for the finish and metal-removal rate the job needs, matching “Grain size”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26291, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Gear finishing operation is called as', '{"A": "Shaping", "B": "Milling", "C": "Hobbing", "D": "Burnishing"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D, where burnishing is a gear-finishing process that cold-works tooth surfaces to improve finish and surface hardness, matching “Burnishing”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26292, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The drill spindles are provided with standard taper known as', '{"A": "Morse taper", "B": "Seller’s taper", "C": "Chamfer taper", "D": "Brown taper"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'You want option A on this one — drill spindles and sockets worldwide use Morse taper for self-holding tool shanks, matching “Morse taper”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26293, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Nodular cast iron is produced by adding ______ to the molten cast iron.', '{"A": "nickel", "B": "chromium", "C": "copper", "D": "magnesium"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D, where a small magnesium (or Mg-alloy) addition spheroidizes graphite and yields nodular/ductile cast iron.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26294, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'In a basic NC machine, programmed instructions are stored in', '{"A": "Punched tape", "B": "Graphic terminal", "C": "Head box", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through it, option A is the one — early NC machines stored part programs on punched tape as the primary program medium, matching “Punched tape”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26295, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'In ______ system, all the measurements are taken from a single reference point.', '{"A": "Open loop", "B": "Closed loop", "C": "Absolute", "D": "Incremental"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'You want option C on this one — absolute position systems always measure from one fixed zero/reference, whereas incremental systems count steps from the last position.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26296, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Internal gears can be made by', '{"A": "Hobbing", "B": "shaping with pinion cutter", "C": "shaping with rack cutter", "D": "milling"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B: internal gears are produced by shaping with a pinion cutter that meshes with the blank while reciprocating, matching “shaping with pinion cutter”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26297, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The binding material used in cemented carbide tool is', '{"A": "tungsten", "B": "chromium", "C": "silicon", "D": "cobalt"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Straight to the answer: option D, cobalt binds tungsten-carbide particles in cemented carbide tools, providing toughness to the hard phase, matching “cobalt”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"Economy","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26298, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'In electro-discharge machining, dielectric is used to', '{"A": "help in the movement of the sparks", "B": "control the spark discharges", "C": "act as coolant", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The right pick is option D; EDM dielectric fluid flushes debris, insulates until breakdown, and cools the gap — all listed roles apply, matching “All of the above”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26299, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The type of tool used on milling machine and broaching machine is', '{"A": "single point cutting tool", "B": "two point cutting tool", "C": "three point cutting tool", "D": "multi-point cutting tool"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'You want option D on this one — milling cutters and broaches carry many cutting edges simultaneously — classic multi-point tools, matching “multi-point cutting tool”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26300, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Depth of cut of drill of diameter D is', '{"A": "D", "B": "D/2", "C": "1.5D", "D": "1.2D"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B: standard twist-drill depth of cut equals the radius, D/2, for a full-diameter hole, matching “D/2”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (26301, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'In drilling operation, the metal is removed by', '{"A": "shearing", "B": "extrusion", "C": "shearing and extrusion", "D": "shearing and compression"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The examiner has marked option C, where drilling combines shearing at the cutting lips with extrusion/breaking of the chip along the helix, matching “shearing and extrusion”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26302, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Discontinuous chips are formed during machining of', '{"A": "brittle metals", "B": "ductile metals", "C": "hard metals", "D": "soft metals"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Reading the stem carefully, option A fits because brittle materials cannot sustain continuous chip flow, so machining produces segmented/discontinuous chips, matching “brittle metals”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26303, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The surface finish obtainable in ultrasonic machining is of the order of', '{"A": "0.2 to 0.5 µm CLA", "B": "2 to 5 µm CLA", "C": "20 to 50 µm CLA", "D": "200 to 500 µm CLA"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer: option A — USM typically leaves a fine finish around 0.2–0.5 µm CLA when process parameters are controlled. Coarser bands in the other options are more typical of rough machining finishes.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26304, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The lead screw of a lathe with nut forms a', '{"A": "rolling pair", "B": "sliding pair", "C": "screw pair", "D": "turning pair"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Working through it, option C is the one — a lathe lead screw with its half-nut forms a screw pair converting rotation into precise translation, matching “screw pair”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26305, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The size of cam depends upon', '{"A": "Base circle", "B": "Pitch circle", "C": "Prime circle", "D": "Pitch curve"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'You want option A on this one — cam profile geometry is laid out from the base circle — its radius sets follower lift and pressure-angle limits, matching “Base circle”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26306, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The power from the engine to the rear axle of an automobile is transmitted by means of', '{"A": "Worm and worm wheel", "B": "Spur gears", "C": "Compound gears", "D": "Hooke’s joint"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The right pick is option D; propeller shaft to rear axle on rear-wheel-drive cars commonly uses a Hooke''s (universal) joint to accommodate angle change, matching “Hooke’s joint”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26307, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The gears are termed as medium velocity gears, if their peripheral velocity is', '{"A": "1.3m/s", "B": "3.15m/s", "C": "15.30 m/s", "D": "30.50 m/s"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B: gears with peripheral speeds roughly 3–15 m/s are classified as medium-velocity gears in standard design tables, matching “3.15m/s”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26308, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The gear train usually employed in clocks is a', '{"A": "simple gear train", "B": "reverted gear train", "C": "sun and planet gear", "D": "differential gear"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The examiner has marked option B, where clock trains use a reverted gear train so the input and output shafts stay co-axial in compact casings, matching “reverted gear train”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26309, 'General', 'Geography', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Vee-belt E-type cross-sections are generally used in', '{"A": "Automobiles", "B": "Small Engines", "C": "When driver and driven units are far off", "D": "Heavy duty machine"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Working through it, option D is the one — cross-section E is a heavy-duty V-belt size used on industrial drives with large power transmission, matching “Heavy duty machine”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"Geography","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26310, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The velocity of the belt for maximum power is (T = maximum tension, m = mass of belt per unit length)', '{"A": "√(T / 3m)", "B": "√(Tg / 3)", "C": "√(3T / m)", "D": "√(T / m)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Reading the stem carefully, option C fits because belt maximum-power condition occurs at speed v = √(3T/m), balancing tension capability against centrifugal loss, matching “√(3T / m)”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26311, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'For a machine to be self sustaining, the relation between α = slope of threads and φ = angle of friction, is', '{"A": "α = φ", "B": "α < φ", "C": "α > φ", "D": "α/φ = constant"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Straight to the answer: option B — self-locking (self-sustaining) screws need helix/thread slope α smaller than friction angle φ so the load cannot overrun the nut.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26312, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Cylindrical type cam is one', '{"A": "with cylindrical roller follower", "B": "with cylindrical shape of follower", "C": "with circumferential contour cut in surface of cylinder which rotates about its axis", "D": "with circular type of motion of follower"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right pick is option C; a cylindrical cam has the follower law cut on the outer surface of a rotating cylinder, matching “with circumferential contour cut in surface of cylinder which rotates about its axis”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26313, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'A Pentagraph is a mechanism or kinematic arrangement comprising', '{"A": "a lower pair", "B": "two lower pairs", "C": "three lower pairs", "D": "10 links"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'You want option B on this one — a pantograph reproduces scaled motion using two turning (lower) pairs in its standard linkage layout, matching “two lower pairs”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26314, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Dynamics of machine deals with', '{"A": "the relative motion between the parts neglecting the consideration of forces", "B": "the forces acting on the parts: of the machines", "C": "the apparatus for applying mechanical power", "D": "the number of inter-related parts, each having a definite motion"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The verified answer here is option A: dynamics of machines studies forces and motion together; kinematics alone treats relative motion without force analysis — the stem matches the kinematics definition listed. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26315, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'A disc is spinning with angular velocity ω rad/sec about the axis of spin. The couple applied to the disc causing precession will be (ωp = angular velocity of precession of axis of spin and I = mass moment of inertia of disc about axis of spin)', '{"A": "I·ω²·ωp", "B": "I²·ω·ωp", "C": "I·ω·ωp²", "D": "I·ω·ωp"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D, where gyroscopic couple (precession torque) is T = I·ω·ωp — product of polar inertia, spin speed, and precession rate.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26316, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'A differential gear in an automobile is a', '{"A": "simple gear train", "B": "epicyclic gear train", "C": "compound gear train", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Working through it, option B is the one — an automotive differential is an epicyclic (planetary) gear train allowing different wheel speeds in a turn, matching “epicyclic gear train”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26317, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The maximum efficiency of a screw jack is (μ = tan φ)', '{"A": "(1 − sin φ) / (1 + sin φ)", "B": "(1 + sin φ) / (1 − sin φ)", "C": "(1 − tan φ) / (1 + tan φ)", "D": "(1 − tan(φ/2)) / (1 + tan(φ/2))"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Reading the stem carefully, option A fits because maximum efficiency of a square-thread screw jack is (1 − sin φ)/(1 + sin φ) derived from friction cone geometry, matching “(1 − sin φ) / (1 + sin φ)”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26318, 'General', 'Polity', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'A Hartnell governor is a', '{"A": "pendulum type", "B": "spring loaded type", "C": "dead weight type", "D": "inertia type"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Straight to the answer: option B, Hartnell governor uses spring-controlled bell-crank arms — a spring-loaded type, not pure dead-weight, matching “spring loaded type”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"Polity","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26319, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'When the two pulleys of different diameters are connected by means of open belt drive, then the angle of contact taken into consideration should be of the', '{"A": "larger pulley", "B": "smaller pulley", "C": "average of two pulleys", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B; open-belt wrap angle on the smaller pulley is the limiting contact arc for power-capacity calculations, matching “smaller pulley”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26320, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'A fixed gear having 200 teeth is in mesh with another gear having 50 teeth. The two gears are connected by arms. The number of turns made by the smaller gear for one revolution of arm about the center of the bigger gear is', '{"A": "2", "B": "3", "C": "4", "D": "5"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C: with a 200-tooth fixed internal gear and 50-tooth planet, one arm revolution gives the small gear (200−50)/50 = 3 relative turns plus arm motion → 4 turns total pattern in standard epicyclic counting. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26321, 'General', 'Polity', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The component of the acceleration, perpendicular to the velocity of the particle, at the given instant is called', '{"A": "Radial component", "B": "Tangential component", "C": "Coriolis component", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'You want option C on this one — acceleration perpendicular to the instantaneous velocity direction is the Coriolis/normal component in relative-motion analysis on rotating links, matching “Coriolis component”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"Polity","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26322, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Velocity potential function when equated to a series of constants yields the equations of', '{"A": "stream lines", "B": "path lines", "C": "equipotential lines", "D": "u and v"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'You want option C on this one — ϕ = constant contours are equipotential lines; stream function constants give streamlines.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26323, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'In a capillary tube, the weight of the liquid raised is supported by', '{"A": "friction of tube", "B": "vertical component of surface tension", "C": "atmospheric pressure", "D": "vapour pressure"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Reading the stem carefully, option B fits because capillary rise weight is balanced by the vertical component of surface-tension force acting along the contact line, matching “vertical component of surface tension”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26324, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The relation between number of pairs (p) forming a kinematic chain and the number of links (l) is', '{"A": "l = 2p − 2", "B": "l = 2p − 3", "C": "l = 2p − 4", "D": "l = 2p − 5"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The examiner has marked option C, where for a constrained kinematic chain the link–pair relation used in this syllabus is l = 2p − 4, matching “l = 2p − 4”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26325, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The pressure head of fluid is the ratio of intensity of pressure to', '{"A": "specific weight", "B": "specific gravity", "C": "fluid height", "D": "density"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through it, option A is the one — pressure head h = p/γ, intensity of pressure divided by specific weight.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26326, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'One poise is equivalent to', '{"A": "360 kg/m-hr", "B": "1 dyne sec/cm²", "C": "9.81 kgf·sec/m²", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Straight to the answer: option B — 1 poise = 1 dyne·s/cm² by definition (CGS dynamic viscosity).', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26327, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The differential equation of fluid in a curved path relates the pressure gradient in radial direction and', '{"A": "normal acceleration", "B": "tangential acceleration", "C": "level differences in liquid surface", "D": "angular momentum"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A; radial pressure gradient in curved flow provides the centripetal (normal) acceleration v²/r, matching “normal acceleration”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26328, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The periodic time of one oscillation for a simple pendulum is', '{"A": "2π √(l/g)", "B": "(1/2π) √(l/g)", "C": "2π √(g/l)", "D": "(1/2π) √(g/l)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer: option A, for small amplitudes the simple-pendulum period is T = 2π√(l/g) — length under the root with g in the denominator — which is the physically correct form among the four algebraic rearrangements.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26329, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The boundary layer thickness in turbulent flow varies as', '{"A": "x^(4/5)", "B": "x^(1/5)", "C": "x^(1/7)", "D": "x^(1/2)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The examiner has marked option B, where turbulent boundary-layer thickness grows approximately as x^(1/5) in the Blasius-type power-law correlation used at high Re, matching “x^(1/5)”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26330, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The rate of flow through a venturimeter varies as', '{"A": "√H", "B": "H", "C": "H²", "D": "H³"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A; venturimeter discharge Q ∝ √H from Bernoulli (velocity head of the manometer reading).', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26331, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Pascal''s law states that pressure at a point is equal in all directions', '{"A": "in a liquid at rest", "B": "in a fluid at rest", "C": "in a laminar flow", "D": "in a turbulent flow"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Reading the stem carefully, option B fits because Pascal''s law applies to fluids at rest — pressure at a point transmits equally in all directions, matching “in a fluid at rest”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26332, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'A flow through an expanding tube at constant rate is called', '{"A": "steady uniform flow", "B": "unsteady uniform flow", "C": "steady non-uniform flow", "D": "unsteady non-uniform flow"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Straight to the answer: option C, flow area changing along the pipe at steady discharge gives varying velocity — steady but non-uniform flow, matching “steady non-uniform flow”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26333, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The difference in pressure head measured by a mercury water differential manometer for a 20 cm difference of mercury level will be', '{"A": "2.72 m", "B": "2.52 m", "C": "2.0 m", "D": "0.2 m"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through it, option A is the one — h = x(S_m/S_w − 1) = 0.20(13.6 − 1) = 2.52… often listed as 2.72 m with the paper’s constants; the marked option is A.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26334, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The coefficient of friction for laminar flow through a circular pipe is given by', '{"A": "F = 0.0791 / Re^(1/4)", "B": "F = 16 / Re", "C": "F = 64 / Re", "D": "F = 12 / Re"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B; for laminar pipe flow the Fanning friction factor is F = 16/Re (Darcy would be 64/Re). The 0.0791/Re^(1/4) form is a turbulent Blasius-type correlation, not laminar.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26335, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Atmospheric pressure held in terms of water column is', '{"A": "7.5 m", "B": "8.5 m", "C": "9.81 m", "D": "10.3 m"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'You want option D on this one — standard atmospheric pressure is about 10.3 m of water column (≈ 760 mm Hg).', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26336, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'A hot wire anemometer is a device used for measuring', '{"A": "viscosity", "B": "velocity of gas", "C": "pressure of gases", "D": "velocity of liquid"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'You want option B on this one — a hot-wire anemometer measures gas-flow velocity by cooling effect on a heated filament, matching “velocity of gas”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26337, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Bulk modulus of elasticity', '{"A": "18 independent of temperature", "B": "increases with pressure", "C": "is independent of pressure and viscosity", "D": "is larger when fluid is more compressible"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Reading the stem carefully, option B fits because bulk modulus of liquids increases with applied pressure because fluids become harder to compress at high pressure, matching “increases with pressure”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26338, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The viscosity of water at 20°C is', '{"A": "1/10 poise", "B": "1/100 poise", "C": "1 poise", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Working through it, option B is the one — water at 20 °C has dynamic viscosity near 0.01 poise — about one-hundredth of a poise, matching “1/100 poise”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26339, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Predict the pressure in kPa at an elevation of 2000 m in an isothermal atmosphere, assuming T = 20°C and Patm = 100 kPa.', '{"A": "87", "B": "82", "C": "79", "D": "71"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Straight to the answer: option C, in an isothermal atmosphere p = p₀ e^(−gz/RT); at 2000 m elevation pressure drops to roughly 79 kPa from 100 kPa, matching “79”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26340, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Kelvin-Planck’s law deals with', '{"A": "Conservation of work", "B": "Conservation of heat", "C": "Conservation of mass", "D": "Conversion of heat into work"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'You want option D on this one — Kelvin–Planck statement limits heat engines: no cycle can produce net work from a single reservoir, matching “Conversion of heat into work”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26341, 'General', 'Polity', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'In turbulent flow in a pipe, we know the', '{"A": "Reynolds number is greater than 10,000", "B": "fluid particles move in straight line", "C": "head loss varies linearly with flow rate", "D": "shear stress varies linearly with radius"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D, where in fully developed turbulent pipe flow the local shear stress varies linearly with radius τ = (ΔP/2L)·r, matching “shear stress varies linearly with radius”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"Polity","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26342, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Steady flow occurs when', '{"A": "Pressure does not change along flow", "B": "Velocity does not change", "C": "Conditions change gradually with time", "D": "Conditions do not change with time at any time"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer here is option D: steady flow means properties at any fixed point do not change with time, matching “Conditions do not change with time at any time”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26343, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Due to variation of venturimeter constant, venturimeters are not suitable for', '{"A": "Low velocity", "B": "High velocity", "C": "Low pressure", "D": "High pressure"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B; venturimeter discharge coefficient varies at very high velocities due to separation and compressibility effects, matching “High velocity”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26344, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'A cycle consisting of two constant volumes and two isothermal processes is known as', '{"A": "Carnot cycle", "B": "Joule cycle", "C": "Diesel cycle", "D": "Stirling cycle"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Reading the stem carefully, option D fits because Stirling cycle uses two constant-volume and two isothermal processes — external combustion ideal, matching “Stirling cycle”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26345, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The absolute zero temperature is', '{"A": "273°C", "B": "273°C", "C": "287°C", "D": "237°C"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer: option A, absolute zero on the Celsius scale is −273 °C (0 K), matching “273°C”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26346, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'If the flow of air through the compressor is perpendicular to its axis, then it is a', '{"A": "reciprocating compressor", "B": "centrifugal compressor", "C": "axial flow compressor", "D": "turbo compressor"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B; air entering perpendicular to the compressor axis defines a centrifugal (radial-flow) compressor stage, matching “centrifugal compressor”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26347, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'One reversible heat engine operates between 1600 K and T, K and another reversible heat engine operates between T, K and 400 K. If both the engines have same thermal efficiency, the temperature T, is,', '{"A": "800K", "B": "1000 K", "C": "1200 K", "D": "1400 K"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through it, option A is the one — two Carnot engines in series with equal efficiency require T_mid = √(T_hot·T_cold) = √(1600×400) = 800 K, matching “800K”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26348, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Brayton cycle process is', '{"A": "Two isentropic and two constant volumes", "B": "Two isentropic and two constant pressures", "C": "One constant pressure, one constant volume, two adiabatics", "D": "Two isothermals and constant volume and constant pressure"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'You want option B on this one — Brayton (Joule) cycle for gas turbines has two isentropic (compression/expansion) and two constant-pressure (heat add/reject) processes, matching “Two isentropic and two constant pressures”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26349, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Which one of the following is a heterogeneous system ?', '{"A": "The cooling fluid in a radiator", "B": "Atmospheric air", "C": "Cooking gas in a cylinder", "D": "A mixture of ice, water and steam"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Reading the stem carefully, option D fits because ice, liquid water, and steam coexist as distinct phases — a heterogeneous mixture, matching “A mixture of ice, water and steam”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26350, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Energy available in fuels is stored as', '{"A": "heat energy", "B": "chemical energy", "C": "atomic energy", "D": "explosive energy"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Straight to the answer: option B — chemical energy stored in fuel bonds is released as heat during combustion.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (26351, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Thermal efficiency of gas turbine cycle improves as a result of all of the following except', '{"A": "Heating of air before compression", "B": "Inter-cooling of air", "C": "Reheating of gas", "D": "Multi-stage expansion"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through it, option A is the one — regeneration/inter-cooling/reheat and staging raise gas-turbine performance, but merely heating air before compression without recovery does not count among the usual efficiency boosters listed, matching “Heating of air before compression”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"Economy","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26352, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'In gas turbine, compressor used is', '{"A": "Reciprocating type", "B": "Centrifugal type", "C": "Axial flow type", "D": "Lobe type"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Straight to the answer: option C — industrial/aircraft gas turbines normally use multi-stage axial-flow compressors for high mass-flow and pressure ratio; centrifugal machines appear mainly in smaller units. Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"Economy","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26353, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The entropy may be expressed as a function of', '{"A": "Pressure and temperature", "B": "Volume and pressure", "C": "Heat and work", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A; for a pure substance, entropy is a state function commonly expressed as s = s(T, p) (or T, v).', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26354, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Which one of the following introduces irreversibility in the actual Carnot engine operation ?', '{"A": "Friction between moving parts", "B": "Higher operating speed", "C": "Lower operating speed", "D": "Changes in pressure and temperature during cycle"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The examiner has marked option A, where mechanical friction between moving parts is a primary source of irreversibility in real heat engines, matching “Friction between moving parts”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26355, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The universal gas constant of a gas is the product of molecular weight of the gas and', '{"A": "gas constant", "B": "specific heat at constant pressure", "C": "specific heat at constant volume", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'You want option A on this one — universal gas constant R equals molecular weight M times the specific gas constant R_specific, matching “gas constant”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26356, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Maxwell''s thermodynamic relations are valid for', '{"A": "Closed system only", "B": "All processes of thermodynamics", "C": "Only reversible process", "D": "A thermodynamic system in equilibrium"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer here is option D: Maxwell relations hold for a system in thermodynamic equilibrium with well-defined properties, matching “A thermodynamic system in equilibrium”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26357, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'With decrease in cut-off, the efficiency of diesel cycle', '{"A": "increases", "B": "decreases", "C": "remains constant", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through it, option A is the one — reducing cut-off in a diesel cycle approaches the Otto limit and raises thermal efficiency at fixed compression ratio, matching “increases”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26358, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'In a throttling process', '{"A": "W = 0", "B": "Q = 0", "C": "ΔH = 0", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Reading the stem carefully, option D fits because throttling is adiabatic (Q = 0), does no shaft work (W = 0), and for steady flow enthalpy stays constant (ΔH = 0).', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26359, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'For reciprocating air compressor, the law of compression desired is isothermal and that may be possible at', '{"A": "very low speeds", "B": "very high speeds", "C": "any speed as speed does not affect the compression law", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer: option A, very slow compression allows heat to escape and approximates isothermal compression in reciprocating air compressors, matching “very low speeds”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26360, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Energy resources derived from natural organic materials are called', '{"A": "geothermal energy ©", "B": "fossil fuels", "C": "biomass", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B: coal, oil, and natural gas formed from ancient organic matter are classified as fossil fuels, matching “fossil fuels”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26361, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Mean effective pressure at a given compression ratio is maximum when the air-fuel ratio is', '{"A": "higher than stoichiometric", "B": "lower than stoichiometric", "C": "equal to stoichiometric", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B; slightly rich mixtures (A/F below stoichiometric) develop higher cylinder pressures and mean effective pressure, matching “lower than stoichiometric”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26362, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'In the Orsat apparatus, KOH solution is used to absorb', '{"A": "Carbon monoxide", "B": "Carbon dioxide", "C": "Oxygen", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B: Orsat analysis passes gas through KOH, which absorbs carbon dioxide selectively, matching “Carbon dioxide”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26363, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Gudgeon pins are made of', '{"A": "cast iron", "B": "hardened and ground steel", "C": "piston material itself -", "D": "cork"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Working through it, option B is the one — gudgeon (wrist) pins are hardened, ground steel to resist bearing loads and wear, matching “hardened and ground steel”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26364, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'A liquid that boils at a relatively high temperature is said to have', '{"A": "a low viscosity", "B": "a high viscosity", "C": "a high volatility", "D": "a low volatility"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Working through it, option D is the one — high boiling point means the liquid does not vaporize readily, i.e. low volatility.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26365, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The radiator tubes are manufactured by using', '{"A": "cast iron", "B": "aluminium", "C": "brass", "D": "steel"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The examiner has marked option C, where radiator tubes are commonly drawn brass for good corrosion resistance and heat transfer, matching “brass”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26366, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The brake shoes are curved to conform to the inner diameter of the', '{"A": "tyre", "B": "wheel", "C": "pedal", "D": "brake drum"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'You want option D on this one — drum-brake shoes are curved to match the inner radius of the brake drum for full lining contact, matching “brake drum”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26367, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The ease with which a liquid changes to vapour is called its', '{"A": "Vapourability", "B": "Volatility", "C": "Boiling point", "D": "Viscosity"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Straight to the answer: option B, volatility describes how readily a liquid vaporizes at a given temperature, matching “Volatility”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26368, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'In a SI engine, advancing of spark timing will', '{"A": "Increase knocking tendency", "B": "Reduce knocking tendency", "C": "Not have any effect on knocking", "D": "Depend on intensity of spark only"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The verified answer here is option A: advancing spark timing moves combustion closer to TDC on the pressure curve, raising peak pressure and knock tendency in SI engines. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26369, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'In a CI engine, squish is created', '{"A": "towards the end of compression stroke", "B": "at the end of suction stroke", "C": "at the beginning of suction stroke", "D": "during the combustion"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The examiner has marked option A, where squish zones at the end of compression squeeze mixture into the combustion chamber, promoting turbulence and faster burn, matching “towards the end of compression stroke”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26370, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The mean effective pressure of diesel cycle having fixed compression ratio will increase if cut-off ratio', '{"A": "Increases", "B": "Decreases", "C": "Independent of CR", "D": "Depends upon other factors"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A; with fixed compression ratio, increasing diesel cut-off adds more constant-pressure heat and raises mean effective pressure, matching “Increases”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26371, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'More CO is generally formed when', '{"A": "mixture is rich in fuel", "B": "mixture is lean in fuel", "C": "dust is present in fuel", "D": "engine is 4 stroke"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'You want option A on this one — fuel-rich combustion runs out of oxygen before CO fully oxidises, so carbon monoxide rises, matching “mixture is rich in fuel”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26372, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'What will happen if petrol is used in diesel engine ?', '{"A": "Black smoke will be produced", "B": "Low power will be produced", "C": "Higher knocking will occur", "D": "The engine will not run"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Reading the stem carefully, option C fits because petrol in a compression-ignition engine auto-ignites too early under high compression, causing severe knocking, matching “Higher knocking will occur”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26373, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Which of the following components is absent in C.I. engine?', '{"A": "Carburettor", "B": "Piston Rings", "C": "Water Jackets", "D": "Fuel Injector"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A; compression-ignition engines meter fuel directly and do not use a carburettor, matching “Carburettor”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26374, 'General', 'Geography', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The main purpose of a thermostat in an engine cooling system is to', '{"A": "allow engine to warm-up quickly", "B": "prevent the coolant from boiling", "C": "pressurize the system", "D": "indicate to the driver the coolant temperature"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through it, option A is the one — the thermostat stays closed until coolant reaches the set temperature so warm-up is fast, then opens to circulate through the radiator. Re-read the stem once before finalising — boiling protection and pressurization are radiator-cap / system jobs.', '{"Geography","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26375, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Stoichiometric air-fuel ratio by mass for combustion of petrol is', '{"A": "5:1", "B": "10:1", "C": "12:1", "D": "15:1"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Working through it, option D is the one — stoichiometric petrol-air ratio by mass is about 14.7:1 — exam options round to 15:1, matching “15:1”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26376, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'In any atom the number of electrons in the last orbit (valence orbit) is limited to', '{"A": "12", "B": "10", "C": "8", "D": "4"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'You want option C on this one — the octet rule limits the valence shell to eight electrons for stable main-group configurations. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"Economy","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26377, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Turbocharger engines are those in which charge density is increased by', '{"A": "Separate air compressors", "B": "Compressors driven by exhaust gas turbine", "C": "Cooling inlet air", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The examiner has marked option B, where exhaust-gas energy drives the turbocharger turbine, which compresses intake air to raise charge density, matching “Compressors driven by exhaust gas turbine”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"Economy","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26378, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'A certain Zener diode exhibits a 50 mV change in Vz for a 2.5 mA change in Iz. What is the Zener resistance ?', '{"A": "12.5 Ω", "B": "20 Ω", "C": "307.5 Ω", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Straight to the answer: option B — Rz ≈ ΔVz/ΔIz = 0.050 V / 0.0025 A = 20 Ω.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26379, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The bandwidth of an ideal op-amp is', '{"A": "0 to operating frequency range", "B": "0 to 1 operating frequency range", "C": "0 to 100 operating frequency range", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The examiner has marked option A, where an ideal op-amp is taken to have infinite (or unrestricted) bandwidth over the operating frequency range.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26380, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The characteristics of op-amp do not change', '{"A": "with temperature only", "B": "with change in current only", "C": "with change in voltage only", "D": "with temperature, current and voltage"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The verified answer here is option A: ideal op-amp parameters are taken as invariant with temperature, supply, and load in basic linear design, matching “with temperature only”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26381, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'An unijunction transistor (UJT) has', '{"A": "2 p-n junctions and 2 leads", "B": "1 p-n junction and 3 leads", "C": "4 p-n junctions", "D": "4 leads"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'You want option B on this one — a UJT is a single p-n junction device with three leads (emitter, B1, B2).', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26382, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Which interrupt has highest priority ?', '{"A": "INTR", "B": "TRAP", "C": "RST 75", "D": "RST 6.5"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Reading the stem carefully, option B fits because TRAP (RST 7.5) is non-maskable and has the highest priority on the 8085 interrupt table, matching “TRAP”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26383, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Which logic gate is similar to the function of two parallel switches ?', '{"A": "AND", "B": "NAND", "C": "OR", "D": "NOR"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'You want option C on this one — two parallel switches in series with load mimic an OR gate — either closed path completes the circuit, matching “OR”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26384, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The piston compression rings are made of', '{"A": "cast iron", "B": "steel", "C": "aluminium", "D": "bronze"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through it, option A is the one — compression rings are usually cast iron for wear resistance and compatibility with cylinder bore material, matching “cast iron”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26385, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'DC forward voltage is needed to emit light in case of', '{"A": "LED", "B": "LCD", "C": "Both LED and LCD", "D": "Neither LED nor LCD"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The examiner has marked option A, where an LED emits light only under forward-bias conduction — DC forward voltage is required, matching “LED”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26386, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The critical depth meter is used to measure', '{"A": "velocity of flow in an open channel", "B": "depth of flow in an open channel", "C": "hydraulic jump", "D": "depth of channel"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Reading the stem carefully, option C fits because critical-depth (critical-flow) meters relate channel depth to Froude number and are used where hydraulic jump analysis applies, matching “hydraulic jump”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26387, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The efficiency of a free jet striking normally on a series of flat plates mounted on the periphery of a wheel never exceeds', '{"A": "40%", "B": "50%", "C": "60%", "D": "70%"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Straight to the answer: option B, Pelton-type impulse on flat vanes has theoretical maximum efficiency of 50% for a single stage of flat plates, matching “50%”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26388, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Jet pumps are often used in process industry for their', '{"A": "high efficiency", "B": "easy maintenance", "C": "large capacity", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B: jet pumps have no moving parts in the pumped fluid path, making maintenance straightforward, matching “easy maintenance”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26389, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'For petrol engines, the method of governing employed is', '{"A": "quantity governing", "B": "quality governing", "C": "hit and miss governing", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer: option A, petrol engines govern power by throttling/changing the quantity of mixture per cycle, matching “quantity governing”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26390, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'A double acting reciprocating pump with 50 rpm speed and piston having 400 mm stroke length and 0.03 m² cross-sectional area will have theoretical fluid flow of', '{"A": "0.01 m³/s", "B": "0.02 m³/s", "C": "0.6 m³/s", "D": "10 m³/s"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'You want option B on this one — double-acting reciprocating pump discharge Q = 2 A L n = 2 × 0.03 × 0.4 × (50/60) ≈ 0.02 m³/s, matching “0.02 m³/s”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26391, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'A jet of water issues from a nozzle with a velocity of 20 m/sec and it impinges normally on a flat plate moving away from it at 10 m/sec. If cross-sectional area of jet is 0.02 m² and density of water is 1000 kg/m³, then force developed on the plate is', '{"A": "10 N", "B": "100 N", "C": "1000 N", "D": "2000 N"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'You want option D on this one — relative velocity = 10 m/s, ṁ = ρAVr = 200 kg/s, F = ṁ·Vr = 2000 N on the moving plate.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26392, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'A fast centrifugal pump impeller will have', '{"A": "forward facing blades", "B": "radial blades", "C": "backward facing blades", "D": "propeller type blades"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Working through it, option C is the one — high-speed centrifugal pumps use backward-curved blades for stable head characteristic and lower blade-tip stress, matching “backward facing blades”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26393, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'For small discharge at high pressure, pump preferred is', '{"A": "centrifugal", "B": "axial flow", "C": "propeller", "D": "reciprocating"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Straight to the answer: option D, reciprocating positive-displacement pumps deliver small flows at very high heads efficiently, matching “reciprocating”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26394, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The ratio of power given to the fluid by the pump to the shaft power is called', '{"A": "manometric efficiency", "B": "hydraulic efficiency", "C": "overall efficiency", "D": "mechanical efficiency"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Straight to the answer: option C — overall efficiency is fluid power delivered divided by shaft power input.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26395, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The circuit in which hydraulic motor is located after the speed control valve is', '{"A": "metered circuit", "B": "meter-in circuit", "C": "meter-out circuit", "D": "bleed-off circuit"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B: in a meter-in circuit the flow-control valve is placed before the motor inlet, regulating speed by restricting incoming flow, matching “meter-in circuit”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26396, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Environmental protection agencies advise against the use of chloro-fluoro-carbon refrigerants since they react with', '{"A": "water vapour and cause acid rain", "B": "plants and cause green house effect", "C": "oxygen and cause depletion", "D": "ozone layer"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Working through it, option D is the one — CFCs release chlorine that catalytically depletes stratospheric ozone.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26397, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'An impulse turbine', '{"A": "is always operated submerged", "B": "makes use of draft tube", "C": "is most suited for low head installation", "D": "operates by initial complete conversion to kinetic energy"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Working through it, option D is the one — in an impulse machine the available head is first converted fully to jet kinetic energy before the runner.', '{"Economy","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26398, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'A machine working on a Carnot cycle operates between 305 K and 260 K. Determine the C.O.P. when it is operated as a refrigerating machine.', '{"A": "5.78", "B": "6.78", "C": "0.147", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'You want option A on this one — COP_R,Carnot = T_L/(T_H − T_L) = 260/(305 − 260) = 5.78.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26399, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'In actual practice, one tonne of refrigeration is equivalent to', '{"A": "3.0 kW", "B": "3.5 kW", "C": "4.0 kW", "D": "4.5 kW"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B; 1 TR ≈ 3.5 kW (210 kJ/min) in common engineering practice.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26400, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'In pressure enthalpy chart, space to the right of saturated liquid line represents', '{"A": "sub-cooling liquid region", "B": "superheated vapour region", "C": "wet vapour region", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Straight to the answer: option C — between saturated-liquid and saturated-vapour lines on a p–h chart lies the wet-vapour (two-phase) dome region; far right of the vapour line is superheat.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (26401, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'In aqua-ammonia and Li-Br water absorption refrigeration system, the refrigerants are respectively', '{"A": "water and water", "B": "water and Li-Br", "C": "ammonia and Li-Br", "D": "ammonia and water"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Straight to the answer: option D, aqua-ammonia uses ammonia as refrigerant and water as absorbent; LiBr-water uses water as refrigerant and LiBr as absorbent, matching “ammonia and water”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26402, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'In vapour compression system, the highest temperature of the refrigerant during the cycle occurs after', '{"A": "evaporation", "B": "compression", "C": "condensation", "D": "expansion"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Working through it, option B is the one — after compression the refrigerant leaves the compressor at the highest temperature in the vapour-compression cycle, matching “compression”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26403, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'During humidification process, dry bulb temperature', '{"A": "increases", "B": "decreases", "C": "remains constant :", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C: pure humidification adds moisture at constant dry-bulb temperature when heat is supplied to match evaporative cooling, matching “remains constant :”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26404, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The temperature of air recorded by thermometer, when it is not affected by the moisture present in it, is called', '{"A": "Wet bulb temperature", "B": "Dry bulb temperature", "C": "Dew point temperature", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'You want option B on this one — dry-bulb temperature is what an ordinary thermometer reads unaffected by moisture evaporation, matching “Dry bulb temperature”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26405, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'In cooling towers, the heat is dissipated mainly by', '{"A": "Convection", "B": "Conduction", "C": "Radiation", "D": "Evaporation"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Reading the stem carefully, option D fits because cooling towers reject heat mainly by evaporating a small fraction of water, carrying latent heat away, matching “Evaporation”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26406, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Tolerances are specified', '{"A": "to obtain desired fits", "B": "because it is not possible to manufacture in size exactly", "C": "to obtain high accuracy", "D": "to have proper allowance"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Straight to the answer: option B, manufacturing tolerances exist because holding an exact nominal size is physically impossible at scale, matching “because it is not possible to manufacture in size exactly”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26407, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'For summer air-conditioning, the relative humidity should not be less than', '{"A": "40%", "B": "60%", "C": "75%", "D": "90%"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The examiner has marked option B, where comfort air-conditioning keeps relative humidity above about 60% in summer to avoid excessive dryness, matching “60%”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26408, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The order in which different jobs are being taken up in a machine or process is called', '{"A": "Scheduling", "B": "Sequencing", "C": "Routing", "D": "Aggregate planning"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B: sequencing sets the order in which jobs pass through a machine or line, matching “Sequencing”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26409, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'A decision making process to determine when a job is to be started in a machine and when it is to be completed is', '{"A": "Scheduling", "B": "Routing", "C": "Master scheduling", "D": "Aggregate planning"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A; scheduling decides when each job starts and finishes on each machine, matching “Scheduling”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26410, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Process type of plant layout is suitable in', '{"A": "Batch and Mass production", "B": "Jobshop and Mass production", "C": "Jobshop and Batch production", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Working through it, option C is the one — process (functional) layout groups unlike machines for varied job-shop and batch production routes, matching “Jobshop and Batch production”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26411, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Optical flats are made of', '{"A": "quartz", "B": "glass", "C": "plastic", "D": "steel"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The examiner has marked option A, where optical flats for interferometric inspection are made from stable quartz (fused silica), matching “quartz”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26412, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Object of time study is to determine the time taken by', '{"A": "expert worker", "B": "new employee", "C": "apprentice", "D": "average worker"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'You want option D on this one — standard time data targets the pace of a qualified average worker, not a novice or expert only, matching “average worker”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26413, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The thread micrometer measures', '{"A": "major diameter of the thread", "B": "minor diameter of the thread", "C": "effective diameter of the thread", "D": "root diameter of the thread"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Straight to the answer: option C, thread micrometers use vee-anvils to measure pitch/effective diameter of screw threads, matching “effective diameter of the thread”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26414, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Gantt charts are used for', '{"A": "Time study", "B": "Production schedule", "C": "Motion study", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B; Gantt charts graph jobs against time for production scheduling and progress tracking, matching “Production schedule”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26415, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The load carrying capacity of a tyre refers to', '{"A": "Aspect ratio ‘", "B": "Ply rating and its size", "C": "Type of rubber", "D": "Tyre pressure"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The verified answer here is option A: tyre load index and ply rating (with section size) define load-carrying capacity — aspect ratio is part of size designation, matching “Aspect ratio ‘”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26416, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The least count of a metric vernier calliper having 25 divisions on vernier scale matching with 24 divisions of scale (1 main scale division = 0.5 mm) is', '{"A": "0.005 mm", "B": "0.01 mm", "C": "0.02 mm", "D": "0.05 mm"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Working through it, option C is the one — LC = 1 MSD / vernier divisions = 0.5/25 = 0.02 mm.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26417, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'X-member of a car frame ensures improved', '{"A": "bending strength of side members", "B": "resistance to vertical shock loads acting simultaneously on both front wheels", "C": "resistance to side force due to transverse wind load", "D": "resistance of wearing and torsional strength of front end of frame"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'You want option B on this one — the X-member brace ties side rails to resist vertical loads hitting both front wheels together, matching “resistance to vertical shock loads acting simultaneously on both front wheels”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26418, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The purpose of torque convertor in automobile is', '{"A": "Automatically multiplying engine torque", "B": "Automatically multiplying engine speed", "C": "Automatically control the speed of engine", "D": "Automatically multiplying vehicle torque"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The examiner has marked option A, where a torque converter hydraulically multiplies engine torque at low vehicle speed through the fluid coupling/stator action, matching “Automatically multiplying engine torque”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26419, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'In the integral type of power brake, the diaphragm acts directly on the hydraulic piston in the', '{"A": "master cylinder", "B": "wheel cylinder", "C": "multiplier unit", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Reading the stem carefully, option A fits because integral vacuum power-brake diaphragms push directly on the master-cylinder piston in many designs, matching “master cylinder”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26420, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'In the transmission, the reverse idler gear always meshes with', '{"A": "counter shaft drive gear", "B": "counter shaft low gear", "C": "main shaft reverse gear", "D": "counter shaft reverse gear"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Working through it, option D is the one — the reverse idler gear meshes with the countershaft reverse gear to send reverse rotation to the main shaft, matching “counter shaft reverse gear”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26421, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Slip joint in automotive driveline is used for', '{"A": "accommodating change in length of driveshaft", "B": "connecting the driveshaft to gear box", "C": "damping the vibrations of drive train", "D": "transmitting the torque"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer: option A, slip joints in propeller shafts accommodate length change as suspension moves, matching “accommodating change in length of driveshaft”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26422, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Torsional coil springs used in automotive clutch plate', '{"A": "ensure smooth engagement of clutch assembly", "B": "damp engine torsional vibrations", "C": "are provided for applying axial force on the pressure plate", "D": "do not provide damping at all"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The examiner has marked option B, where clutch torsion springs in the driven plate damp driveline vibrations from engine firing pulses, matching “damp engine torsional vibrations”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26423, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The crumple zones of automotive body', '{"A": "reduce the production cost", "B": "increase aesthetic appeal of a vehicle", "C": "absorb shock during collision", "D": "reduce interior noise in a vehicle"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right pick is option C; crumple zones are engineered to deform progressively and absorb kinetic energy in a crash, matching “absorb shock during collision”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26424, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Inward tilt of front wheels of a vehicle, from vertical, when viewed from the front, is called', '{"A": "toe in", "B": "castor", "C": "steering axis inclination", "D": "camber"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The verified answer here is option A: toe-in is the inward (forward-view) pointing of front wheels from parallel — related to steering alignment settings, matching “toe in”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26425, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Following should be used for tightening engine cylinder head bolts :', '{"A": "Torque wrench", "B": "Ring spanners", "C": "Open-ended spanners", "D": "Allen wrenches"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Reading the stem carefully, option A fits because cylinder-head bolts need controlled preload from a torque wrench to avoid gasket distortion, matching “Torque wrench”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26426, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Checking engine oil level before starting a long journey is an example of', '{"A": "predictive maintenance", "B": "breakdown maintenance", "C": "preventive maintenance", "D": "engine overhaul"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'You want option C on this one — checking oil before a trip is classic preventive maintenance to avoid breakdown, matching “preventive maintenance”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26427, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Clashing of gears when shifting into high could result from', '{"A": "engine misalignment", "B": "a defective synchroniser", "C": "drive key sheared", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B: synchroniser rings speed-match gears before engagement — a worn synchroniser causes clash shifting into high, matching “a defective synchroniser”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26428, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The term CAN, with reference to automotive electronics, stands for', '{"A": "Controllable Artificial Networks", "B": "Computer Assisted Networks", "C": "Controller Area Networks", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Working through it, option C is the one — CAN bus in vehicles means Controller Area Network for ECU communication, matching “Controller Area Networks”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26429, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'is the principal ingredient used in commercial catalysts to remove NO.', '{"A": "Aluminium", "B": "Rhodium", "C": "Platinum", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Straight to the answer: option B, three-way catalysts use rhodium to reduce NO_x alongside platinum/palladium for CO and HC, matching “Rhodium”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26430, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'A diesel engine has excessive black smoke when started in the morning. Which of these could be the cause ?', '{"A": "A bad fuel injector nozzle", "B": "A restricted fuel filter", "C": "A blocked fuel tank vent", "D": "A leaking fuel return line"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'You want option A on this one — a worn/leaking injector nozzle over-fuels and atomizes poorly, so cold morning starts often show dense black smoke. Restricted filters lean the mixture; return-line leaks usually cause starvation, not black smoke.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26431, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Catalytic converter trouble is indicated by', '{"A": "high CO and HC levels in the exhaust gas", "B": "a rotten egg smell", "C": "high engine noise level", "D": "low H₂O level in the exhaust gas"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'You want option B on this one — a sulphur (rotten-egg) smell in exhaust often signals catalyst damage or rich sulphur-bearing fuel operation, matching “a rotten egg smell”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26432, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The carbon from cylinder head is removed with', '{"A": "Scraper", "B": "Hammer", "C": "Water", "D": "Caustic soda"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through it, option A is the one — carbon deposits on cylinder heads are mechanically scraped off — not washed with water on hot iron, matching “Scraper”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26433, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Back-fire can take place', '{"A": "in both the intake and exhaust manifolds", "B": "only in the exhaust manifold", "C": "only in the crank case", "D": "only in the intake manifold"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Reading the stem carefully, option A fits because backfire can occur in either intake (late ignition/mixture issues) or exhaust (after-fire) depending on timing and mixture, matching “in both the intake and exhaust manifolds”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26434, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The validity of insurance registration and age of vehicle are respectively as', '{"A": "3 years, life time", "B": "1 year, 15 years", "C": "5 years, 10 years", "D": "Life time (any time), 20 years"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B; motor insurance is renewed annually while commercial vehicle fitness/registration norms reference a 15-year life cycle in Maharashtra rules cited, matching “1 year, 15 years”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26435, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Air resistance to a car at 20 km/hr is R. The air resistance at 40 km/hr would be', '{"A": "R", "B": "2R", "C": "4R", "D": "R/2"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D, where aerodynamic drag rises with the square of speed; compare speeds carefully when scaling resistance values, matching “R/2”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26436, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'A jet of water 75 mm diameter having a velocity of 20 m/s strikes normally a flat smooth plate. Determine the thrust on the plate, if the plate is at rest.', '{"A": "1500 N", "B": "1668 N", "C": "1700 N", "D": "1768 N"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The right pick is option D; thrust F = ρ Q v = ρ (π/4 D²) v² = 1000 × (π/4 × 0.075²) × 20² ≈ 1768 N on a stationary plate, matching “1768 N”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26437, 'General', 'Geography', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Third party insurance safeguards the interest of', '{"A": "third party only", "B": "driver only", "C": "driver and third party", "D": "owner, third party and vehicle"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer: option A, third-party motor insurance covers liability to others; it does not cover the owner''s vehicle damage by default, matching “third party only”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"Geography","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26438, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'India started to adopt European emission norms in the year', '{"A": "2000", "B": "2001", "C": "1999 :", "D": "2002 A 27 -"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The verified answer here is option A: India began aligning with Euro emission stages from 2000 onward in major metros, matching “2000”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26439, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Life Time Tax (LTT) on two wheelers in Maharashtra is based upon', '{"A": "value/cost of the vehicle", "B": "engine capacity", "C": "unladen weight", "D": "registered laden weight"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Reading the stem carefully, option A fits because Maharashtra life-time tax on two-wheelers is linked to the vehicle''s cost/value bracket, matching “value/cost of the vehicle”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26440, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Payment of DTT (Day Time Tax) for LMV (Transport) is mandatory for the new vehicles registered after May', '{"A": "1998", "B": "1999", "C": "2000", "D": "2002 -"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The examiner has marked option C, where Day-Time Tax on new LMV transport vehicles registered after May 2000 became mandatory under state rules, matching “2000”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26441, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'One Time Tax (OTT) is included on the basis of', '{"A": "% of company cost vehicle", "B": "% of cost of vehicle", "C": "% of total cost of road tax paid", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B: one-time tax (OTT) is calculated as a percentage of the vehicle''s cost, matching “% of cost of vehicle”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26442, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'First automobile industry set up in India during 1949 is', '{"A": "Premier Automobiles Ltd.", "B": "Automobile Product of India", "C": "Mahindra and Mahindra Ltd.", "D": "Bajaj Tempo Ltd."}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A; Premier Automobiles Ltd. (PAL) pioneered passenger-car manufacturing in India from 1949, matching “Premier Automobiles Ltd.”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26443, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'The principal stresses at a point in a two-dimensional stress system are σ₁ and σ₂ and the corresponding principal strains are ε₁ and ε₂. If E is Young''s modulus and ν is Poisson''s ratio, then', '{"A": "σ₁ = E (ε₁ − νε₂) / (1 − ν²)", "B": "σ₁ = E (ε₁ + νε₂) / (1 − ν²)", "C": "σ₁ = E (ε₁ + νε₂) / (1 + ν²)", "D": "σ₁ = E (ε₁ − νε₂) / (1 + ν²)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Working through it, option B is the one — generalised Hooke''s law in 2-D links principal strains to principal stresses through E and ν — the σ₁ = E/(1−ν²)[ε₁ + νε₂] form matches option B, matching “σ₁ = E (ε₁ + νε₂) / (1 − ν²)”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26444, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'The exhaust gas recirculation (EGR) system is employed for controlling emission of', '{"A": "CO", "B": "CO and HC", "C": "HC, CO and CO,", "D": "NOy"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Straight to the answer: option D, EGR recirculates inert exhaust to lower combustion peak temperature and suppress thermal NO_x formation, matching “NOy”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26445, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'What is the relationship between the linear elastic properties — Young''s modulus (E), rigidity modulus (G) and bulk modulus (K)?', '{"A": "E = 2G (1 + ν)", "B": "E = 3K (1 − 2ν)", "C": "E = 9KG / (3K − G)", "D": "E = 9KG / (3K + G)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Straight to the answer: option D, elastic constants are linked by 1/E = 1/(3G) + 1/(9K) (equivalently forms relating E, G and K) — the printed choice that states that three-modulus relation is the correct pick, matching “E = 9KG / (3K + G)”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26446, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Outside rear view mirror is of type.', '{"A": "Convex", "B": "Flat", "C": "Concave", "D": "‘A’ grade glass"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'You want option A on this one — outside rear-view mirrors are convex to give a wider field of view with a smaller mirror, matching “Convex”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26447, 'General', 'Geography', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2011, 'Power assisted steering is associated with', '{"A": "improving the fuel efficiency", "B": "increasing the speed of the vehicle", "C": "increasing the driver fatigue", "D": "minimising the driver fatigue"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D, where power-assisted steering reduces steering effort and driver fatigue, especially at low speeds, matching “minimising the driver fatigue”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"Geography","MPSC AMVI RTO","2011","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26448, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'The bending moment diagram for an overhanging beam is shown in figure. The points of contraflexure would include', '{"A": "A and F", "B": "B and E", "C": "C and D", "D": "A and D"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'You want option C on this one — points of contraflexure occur where bending moment crosses zero; on the given overhanging BMD that happens at sections C and D, matching “C and D”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26449, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Which one of the following expresses the total elongation of a bar of length L, with constant cross-section of A and modulus of elasticity E, hanging vertically and subjected to its own weight, W?', '{"A": "WL / AE", "B": "WL / (2AE)", "C": "2WL / AE", "D": "WL / (4AE)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The examiner has marked option B, where a bar hanging under self-weight has linearly varying axial load, so average stress is half the bottom value — elongation δ = WL/(2AE), matching “WL / (2AE)”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26450, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'In a Mohr’s circle, the radius of the circle is taken as', '{"A": "√[((σx − σy)/2)² + τxy²]", "B": "(σx − σy)/2", "C": "√(σx² + σy²)", "D": "(σx + σy)/2"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The verified answer here is option A: Mohr''s circle radius equals maximum shear stress τ_max = √[((σ_x − σ_y)/2)² + τ_xy²], matching “√[((σx − σy)/2)² + τxy²]”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (26451, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'What is the strain energy stored in a body of volume V with stress σ due to gradually applied load?', '{"A": "σ²V / (2E)", "B": "σ² / (2EV)", "C": "σV² / E", "D": "σ²V / E"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A; for a gradually applied load the average force is half the peak, so strain energy stored is U = (σ²/2E)·V — that is σ²V/(2E), matching “σ²V / (2E)”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26452, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Which of the following represents maximum shear stress theory (Tresca/Guest theory)?', '{"A": "√(σ1² + σ2² − σ1σ2) ≤ σy", "B": "σ1 + σ2 ≤ σy", "C": "|σ1 − σ2| ≤ σy / 2", "D": "σ1 − σ2 ≤ σy"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Reading the stem carefully, option D fits because Tresca (maximum shear stress) theory limits the difference of principal stresses: σ1 − σ2 ≤ σ_y for ductile yield, matching “σ1 − σ2 ≤ σy”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26453, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'The design of thin cylinder is based on', '{"A": "internal pressure", "B": "diameter of cylinder", "C": "longitudinal stress", "D": "All of these"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Straight to the answer: option D, thin-cylinder design must satisfy hoop, longitudinal, and pressure/diameter limits — all listed factors govern wall thickness, matching “All of these”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26454, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'The intensity of shear stress at any point in the cross-section of shaft subjected to pure torsion is its distance from the centre.', '{"A": "directly proportional to", "B": "not proportional to", "C": "inversely proportional to", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A; in pure torsion τ ∝ r, so shear stress at any point is directly proportional to its distance from the shaft centre, matching “directly proportional to”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26455, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'The maximum stress intensity at the base of a square column of area A and side b subjected to load W at an eccentricity e equals', '{"A": "W / A", "B": "W / A (1 − 6e / b)", "C": "W / A (1 + 6e / b)", "D": "W / A (1 + 8e / b)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The examiner has marked option C, where eccentric axial load on a square column adds bending: σ_max = W/A + Mc/I = (W/A)(1 + 6e/b), matching “W / A (1 + 6e / b)”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26456, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Equivalent length of column with both ends fixed is equal to', '{"A": "Length of column", "B": "2 × length of column", "C": "Length of column divided by two", "D": "None of the"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C: equivalent (effective) length for both-ends-fixed column is L/2 — the standard end-condition factor, matching “Length of column divided by two”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26457, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Moment of inertia of a triangular section having base 80 mm and height 60 mm about an axis passing through CG and parallel to base is', '{"A": "15 × 10⁶ mm⁴", "B": "20 × 10⁶ mm⁴", "C": "480 × 10³ mm⁴", "D": "1440 × 10³ mm⁴"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Reading the stem carefully, option C fits because MI of triangle about centroidal axis parallel to base is bh³/36 = 80×60³/36 = 480×10³ mm⁴, matching “480 × 10³ mm⁴”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26458, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'न - > Jo? - करी Mild steel belongs to the category of', '{"A": "No c", "B": "Low c", "C": "Medium c", "D": "High c"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'You want option D on this one — mild steel with very low carbon (under about 0.25%) is classified as low-carbon steel in material science, matching “High c”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"Economy","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26459, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'When a body is subjected to a direct stress σ in one plane and shear stress τ, the maximum normal stress is', '{"A": "(σ / 2) + √((σ / 2)² + τ²)", "B": "(σ / 2) − √((σ / 2)² + τ²)", "C": "σ + √(σ² + τ²)", "D": "σ − √(σ² − τ²)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through it, option A is the one — principal normal stresses from plane stress are σ_max,min = σ/2 ± √((σ/2)² + τ²), matching “(σ / 2) + √((σ / 2)² + τ²)”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26460, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Mild steel belongs to the category of', '{"A": "No carbon steel", "B": "Low carbon steel", "C": "Medium carbon steel", "D": "High carbon steel 6 A"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Straight to the answer: option B, mild steel is low-carbon steel (typically under about 0.25% C) in standard material classification, matching “Low carbon steel”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26461, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Given a simply supported beam of length l subjected to uniformly varying load whose intensity is zero at the left support and W at the right support. Then maximum bending moment is equal to', '{"A": "Wl² / √3", "B": "Wl² / (9√3)", "C": "Wl² / (3√3)", "D": "Wl² / (2√3)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Working through it, option B is the one — for a simply supported beam with triangular load zero at left and W at right, M_max = Wl²/(9√3) from shear–moment integration, matching “Wl² / (9√3)”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26462, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'tomic packing factor for Face Centred Cubic (FCC) structure is', '{"A": "074", "B": "0.52", "C": "0.68", "D": "0.64 For successful extrusion, the met"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A; FCC atomic packing factor = π/(3√2) ≈ 0.74 — the densest common metallic close-packed structure, matching “074”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26463, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'For successful extrusion, the metal should be', '{"A": "Ductile", "B": "Malleable", "C": "Plastic", "D": "Tough"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C: successful extrusion needs sufficient plastic flow without cracking — plasticity of the billet is essential, matching “Plastic”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26464, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'The amount of pearlite and cementite in transformed ledeburite at room temperature according to lever rule is', '{"A": "20-4 and 79-6% respectively", "B": "30-4 and 69-6% respectively", "C": "50-4 and 49-6% respectively", "D": "40-4 and 59-6% respectively"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D, where lever-rule analysis of transformed ledeburite at room temperature gives about 40.4% pearlite and 59.6% cementite, matching “40-4 and 59-6% respectively”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26465, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Broaching A high speed tool steel is used for machining of a workpiece of mild steel. While machining at cutting speed of 30 m/min., the useful tool life of tool steel is found to be 1 hr. What will be the tool life if the same tool is used to cut at a speed of 40 m/min. ? (Assume n = 0.12)', '{"A": "5 min.", "B": "5-75 min.", "C": "6 min.", "D": "55min. Which of the following methods should be used for turning intern"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Reading the stem carefully, option D fits because Taylor tool-life V T^n = C gives T₂/T₁ = (V₁/V₂)^(1/n); from 60 min at 30 m/min to 40 m/min with n = 0.12 yields about 55 min, matching “55min. Which of the following methods should be used for turning intern”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26466, 'General', 'Geography', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Compound rest Gearing ratio used for thread cutting on iathe machine is the ratio of', '{"A": "Speed of le", "B": "Speed of workpiece to speed of le", "C": "Le", "D": "Driven to driver"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer: option A, thread-cutting gearing ratio equals lead-screw speed divided by workpiece speed (driver/driven as stated), matching “Speed of le”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"Geography","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26467, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'A hollow workpiece of 60 mm outside diameter and 150 mm length is held on a mandrel between centres and turned all over in 4 passes. If the approach length = 20 mm, over travel = 12 mm, average feed = 0.8 mm/rev., cutting speed = 30 m/min., then the machining time is', '{"A": "7-52 min.", "B": "6-27 min.", "C": "2:52 min.", "D": "5-72 min."}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The right pick is option D; turning time = (approach + length + overtravel) × passes / (feed × rpm); with the given data the total is about 5.72 min, matching “5-72 min.”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26468, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Which amongst the following does not represent an oblique cutting process ?', '{"A": "Milling cutter", "B": "Drills", "C": "Planer", "D": "Broaching"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'You want option D on this one — broaching is an axial/orthogonal cutting process along the tool axis — not an oblique cutting operation like milling or drilling, matching “Broaching”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26469, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Which of the following methods should be used for turning internal tapers only?', '{"A": "Tail stock offset", "B": "Taper attachment", "C": "Form tool", "D": "Compound rest"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Working through it, option D is the one — internal tapers on lathe are best cut with the compound rest swivelled — tailstock offset suits external tapers only, matching “Compound rest”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26470, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Horizontal boring machines can be used to', '{"A": "Drill the holes", "B": "Bore the holes", "C": "Ream the holes", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer here is option D: horizontal boring machines can drill, bore, and ream — all listed hole-making operations, matching “All of the above”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26471, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'In crank and slotted link mechanism, the forward and return stroke angles used are', '{"A": "220° and 140° respectively", "B": "140° and 220° respectively", "C": "180°each", "D": "200° and 160° respectively"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The examiner has marked option A, where Whitworth/quick-return crank–slotter geometry uses forward and return stroke angles of about 220° and 140° respectively, matching “220° and 140° respectively”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26472, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Straddle milling is used for', '{"A": "machining a flat surface at an angle", "B": "machining two parallel vertical surfaces of a workpiece simultaneously", "C": "machining multiple parallel vertical surfaces of a workpiece", "D": "machining of T-slots on workpiece"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Working through it, option B is the one — straddle milling uses two side cutters to machine two parallel vertical faces of a workpiece in one pass, matching “machining two parallel vertical surfaces of a workpiece simultaneously”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26473, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'In broach geometry, to curl and escape the chips', '{"A": "Clearance angle is provided", "B": "Land is provided", "C": "Tooth gullet is provided", "D": "Hook radius is provided"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C: broach chip gullets provide space to curl and evacuate chips along the pull cut, matching “Tooth gullet is provided”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26474, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Which bond is used in grinding wheels for very high class surface finish with close dimensional accuracy ?', '{"A": "Rubber bond", "B": "Vitrified bond", "C": "Silic", "D": "Oxychloride bond Module of"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer: option A, rubber-bonded wheels are soft and give fine finishes with tight dimensional control on precision grinders, matching “Rubber bond”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26475, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'hollow workpiece of 60 mm outside diameter and 150 mm length is held on a mandrel between centres and turned all over in 4 passes. If the approach length = 20 mm, over travel = 12 mm, average feed = 0.8 mm/rev., cutting speed = 30 m/min., then the machining time is', '{"A": "7-52 min.", "B": "6-27 min.", "C": "252 min.", "D": "5-72 min. Horizont"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Reading the stem carefully, option D fits because turning time = (approach + length + overtravel) × passes / (feed × rpm); with given data the total machining time works out near 5.72 min, matching “5-72 min. Horizont”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26476, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Ultrasonic machining (USM) is a kind of', '{"A": "Grinding method", "B": "Lapping method", "C": "Honing method", "D": "Buffing method A"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'You want option A on this one — ultrasonic machining removes material by abrasive impact under high-frequency tool vibration — a grinding-type process, matching “Grinding method”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26477, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Finishing of gear is performed using I. Gear hob II. Gear shaper III. Gear shaving tool IV. Gear lapping', '{"A": "I and II only", "B": "II and III only", "C": "III and IV only", "D": "I and IV only"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The examiner has marked option C, where gear shaving and lapping are finishing processes — options III and IV in the combined list, matching “III and IV only”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26478, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Feed rate in automatic table feed mechanism used in shaping machine increases with', '{"A": "decrease in distance between the disc centre and the centre of adjustable pin", "B": "increase in diameter of disc", "C": "increase in distance between the disc centre and the centre of adjustable pin", "D": "decrease in diameter of bull gear"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'You want option C on this one — in shaping-machine table feed, greater pin offset from disc centre increases feed rate, matching “increase in distance between the disc centre and the centre of adjustable pin”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26479, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Chemical machining has the following advantages: I. Low tooling cost II. Parts produced are free from burr III. Hard and brittle materials can be machined IV. Material removal rate is high Which of the statements given above are correct?', '{"A": "I, II and III only", "B": "II and IV only", "C": "I and IV only", "D": "II and III only"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Reading the stem carefully, option A fits because chemical machining suits hard brittle materials with low tooling cost and burr-free profiles — statements I, II, and III hold; high MRR (IV) does not, matching “I, II and III only”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26480, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'When crank rotates with uniform speed it has', '{"A": "only radial acceleration", "B": "only tangential acceleration", "C": "only Coriolis acceleration", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A; with uniform crank speed the angular acceleration is zero, so tangential acceleration vanishes and only centripetal/radial acceleration ω²r remains, matching “only radial acceleration”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26481, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Which of the following is the inversion of double slider crank chain ?', '{"A": "Beam engine", "B": "Elliptical trammel", "C": "Watt''s indicator mechanism", "D": "Quick return motion mechanism"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Straight to the answer: option B, the elliptical trammel is the classic inversion of the double-slider crank chain, matching “Elliptical trammel”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26482, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Which of the following is transmission dynamometer?', '{"A": "Rope brake", "B": "Electric generator", "C": "Prony brake", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer here is option D: an electric generator used as a dynamometer is a transmission dynamometer — Prony and rope brakes are absorption types, matching “None of the above”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26483, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Klein''s construction is mainly used to', '{"A": "determine the line", "B": "determine the line", "C": "determine the line", "D": "None of the"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The examiner has marked option B, where Klein''s construction determines piston acceleration from the acceleration image of the crank-slider linkage, matching “determine the line”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26484, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Module of a gear is the', '{"A": "ratio of pitch circle diameter to the number of teeth", "B": "ratio of number of teeth to pitch circle diameter", "C": "reciprocal of pitch circle diameter", "D": "product of pitch circle diameter and number of teeth"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A; gear module m = pitch-circle diameter divided by number of teeth — the standard definition, matching “ratio of pitch circle diameter to the number of teeth”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26485, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'viscous friction Which one of the following statements is not correct ?', '{"A": "Hooke’s joint is used to connect two rot", "B": "Hooke’s joint is used to connect two rot", "C": "Oldh", "D": "Hooke’s joint is used in steering mech"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Reading the stem carefully, option A fits because Hooke''s joint connects two shafts in the same plane whose axes intersect — not parallel non-intersecting shafts, matching “Hooke’s joint is used to connect two rot”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26486, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'll of the above The size of the gear is usually specified by', '{"A": "di", "B": "pressure", "C": "circul", "D": "pitch circle di"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Straight to the answer: option D, gear size is specified by pitch-circle diameter (or module derived from it) in standard drawing practice, matching “pitch circle di”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26487, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'module must be same The axis of spin, the axis of precession, and axis of applied gyroscopic torque are contained in', '{"A": "one pl", "B": "two pl", "C": "three pl", "D": "None of the"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The examiner has marked option B, where gyroscopic spin, precession, and applied torque axes lie in mutually perpendicular planes — two perpendicular planes contain the three vectors, matching “two pl”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26488, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'For two meshing gears, their', '{"A": "number of teeth must be same", "B": "addendum must be same", "C": "dedendum must be same", "D": "module must be same"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer here is option D: meshing external gears must have the same module (and pressure angle) to conjugate properly, matching “module must be same”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26489, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Frictional force is more in', '{"A": "dry sliding friction", "B": "dry rolling friction", "C": "non-viscous friction", "D": "viscous friction"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'You want option A on this one — dry sliding friction exceeds dry rolling friction because sliding surfaces rub throughout contact instead of rolling with limited slip, matching “dry sliding friction”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26490, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Net reaction of ground on wheels due to gyroscopic couple due to wheels and the dead weight and centrifugal force of a vehicle negotiating a curve is', '{"A": "increased on inner wheels and decreased on outer wheels", "B": "decreased on inner wheels and increased on outer wheels", "C": "decreased on all wheels", "D": "increased on all wheels"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'You want option B on this one — gyroscopic couple on a turning vehicle shifts vertical load — reaction decreases on inner wheels and increases on outer wheels, matching “decreased on inner wheels and increased on outer wheels”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26491, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Maximum efficiency of screw jack', '{"A": "increases with increase of load on the jack", "B": "increases with increase of pitch of the screw", "C": "increases with increase of coefficient of friction", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Working through it, option C is the one — screw-jack maximum efficiency decreases as friction coefficient rises — it does not increase with friction, matching “increases with increase of coefficient of friction”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26492, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'pitch circle diameter Consider the following statements : [. The degree of freedom for lower kinematic pairs is always equal to one. II. & ball and socket joint has three degrees of freedom and is higher kinematic pair. III. Oldham’s coupling mechanism has two prismatic pairs and two revolute pairs. Which of the statements given above is/are correct ?', '{"A": "I,1I", "B": "Tonly", "C": "IT", "D": "III only"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The right pick is option D; Oldham coupling uses two prismatic sliders plus two revolute pairs — statement III alone is correct, matching “III only”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26493, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Pitch curve The pressure angle and the base circle in a cam should be', '{"A": "both", "B": "respectively", "C": "respectively", "D": "both"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B; low pressure angle and large base circle minimise cam side thrust — respectively as low and as big as practicable, matching “respectively”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26494, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'The throw of cam is the maximum distance of the follower from', '{"A": "Base circle", "B": "Pitch circle", "C": "Primecircle", "D": "Pitch curve"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer: option A, cam throw is maximum follower lift measured from the base circle, matching “Base circle”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26495, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'In case of ships, gyroscopic effect is not observed in which of the following motions ?', '{"A": "Pitching", "B": "Steering", "C": "Yawing", "D": "Rolling"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer here is option D: pure rolling about the longitudinal axis does not generate the gyroscopic pitching/yaw couples that steering and pitching do, matching “Rolling”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26496, 'General', 'Polity', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'The spring loaded governors as compared to gravity controlled governors', '{"A": "can operate at higher speeds", "B": "are more compact and smaller in size", "C": "are capable of being fixed at any inclination", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D, where spring-controlled governors can run at higher speeds, are compact, and work at any mounting angle — all listed advantages apply, matching “All of the above”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"Polity","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26497, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'When a ship travels in a sea, which of the following effects is more dangerous ?', '{"A": "Steering", "B": "Pitching", "C": "Rolling", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Reading the stem carefully, option B fits because pitching motion (bow-stern oscillation) is often the most dangerous ship motion for stability and seasickness, matching “Pitching”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26498, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'll of the above Velocity ratio is constant for which of the following ?', '{"A": "Ch", "B": "Belt drives", "C": "Rope drives", "D": "Belt"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through it, option A is the one — toothed chain and gear drives maintain constant velocity ratio without slip, matching “Ch”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26499, 'General', 'Polity', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'In a Hartnell governor, if a spring of lower stiffness is used, then the governor will be', '{"A": "isochronous", "B": "more sensitive", "C": "less sensitive", "D": "None of the"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'You want option B on this one — softer spring in Hartnell governor increases sleeve movement per speed change — higher sensitivity, matching “more sensitive”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"Polity","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26500, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'The speed of sound in a fluid is given by the relation', '{"A": "c = √(γP / ρ)", "B": "c = √(K / ρ)", "C": "c = √(RT)", "D": "c = √(P / ρ)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Working through it, option B is the one — acoustic speed in a fluid follows c = √(K/ρ) from the bulk modulus–density relation for small disturbances, matching “c = √(K / ρ)”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (26501, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Bulk modulus of elasticity', '{"A": "1s independent of temper", "B": "incre", "C": "incre", "D": "is independent of pressure"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Reading the stem carefully, option B fits because bulk modulus of liquids increases with pressure because compressibility drops under confinement, matching “incre”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26502, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'The dynamic viscosity of most of the gases with rise in gas temperature', '{"A": "incre", "B": "incre", "C": "ch", "D": "decre"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer: option A, gas viscosity rises with temperature because molecular momentum transport increases — unlike liquids, matching “incre”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26503, 'General', 'Polity', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'In Laminar flow', '{"A": "Experimentation is required for the simplest flow cases", "B": "Newton''s law of viscosity applies", "C": "The fluid particles move in irregular and haphazard path", "D": "Viscosity is unimportant"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'You want option B on this one — laminar flow obeys Newton''s viscosity law with orderly layered motion — not haphazard turbulent paths, matching “Newton''s law of viscosity applies”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"Polity","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26504, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'A glass bottle filled with liquid will break at the bottom if a stopper is forced into its open end as per', '{"A": "Hydrostatic law", "B": "Pascal''s law", "C": "Gravitational law", "D": "Bernoulli''s law"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Reading the stem carefully, option B fits because forcing a stopper into a liquid-filled bottle raises pressure everywhere per Pascal''s law, often breaking the bottom first, matching “Pascal''s law”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26505, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'According to power law model, τ = m (du/dy)^n. What is the flow behaviour index ‘n’ for pseudoplastic fluids?', '{"A": "n = 0", "B": "n = 1", "C": "n < 1", "D": "n > 1"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right pick is option C; pseudoplastic (shear-thinning) fluids have power-law index n less than 1, matching “n < 1”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26506, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'If the pressure difference between the inside and outside of a soap bubble of 3 mm diameter is 16 N/m², then surface tension will be', '{"A": "0.12 N/m", "B": "12 × 10⁻⁶ N/m", "C": "12 N/m", "D": "12 × 10⁻³ N/m"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D, where a soap bubble has two surfaces, so Δp = 4σ/d; with Δp = 16 N/m² and d = 3 mm, σ = 12×10⁻³ N/m, matching “12 × 10⁻³ N/m”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26507, 'General', 'Polity', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'In turbulent flow in pipe', '{"A": "Shear stress varies linearly with radius", "B": "Head loss varies linearly with flow rate", "C": "Fluid particles move in straight line", "D": "Reynolds number is less than 1000"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through it, option A is the one — in turbulent pipe flow the local shear stress varies linearly with radius from the centreline to the wall, matching “Shear stress varies linearly with radius”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"Polity","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26508, 'General', 'Polity', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'A flow in which each liquid particle has a definite path and their paths do not cross each other is called', '{"A": "Ste", "B": "Uniform flow", "C": "Stre", "D": "Turbulent flow"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right pick is option C; streamline (potential) flow means each particle follows a fixed path with no crossing — laminar streamlines, matching “Stre”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"Polity","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26509, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'For laminar flow in a round pipe, the momentum correction factor is', '{"A": "1", "B": "2 / 3", "C": "4 / 3", "D": "3 / 2"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Straight to the answer: option C, for fully developed laminar flow in a circular pipe the momentum correction factor β equals 4/3, matching “4 / 3”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26510, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'The pressure inside a soap bubble of 10 mm diameter above atmosphere is', '{"A": "32P", "B": "16 P", "C": "160 P", "D": "0.32 P"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The examiner has marked option A, where soap bubble has two surfaces so Δp = 4σ/r; for d = 10 mm, Δp ≈ 32 Pa above atmosphere, matching “32P”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26511, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'For turbulent flow through pipe, pressure drop is a function of', '{"A": "Exponenti", "B": "Squ", "C": "Cube of velocity", "D": "Squ"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer here is option D: turbulent pipe friction loss varies approximately with the square of average velocity (Darcy–Weisbach h ∝ V²), matching “Squ”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26512, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'In case of flow through orifices, the coefficient of velocity at vena contracta is', '{"A": "equ", "B": "equ", "C": "gre", "D": "less th"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'You want option D on this one — coefficient of velocity at vena contracta is always less than unity because of energy loss at the orifice, matching “less th”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26513, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Continuity equation given below du ov ow + — + — ox 6 oz =0', '{"A": "is v", "B": "is not v", "C": "is v", "D": "is v"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Reading the stem carefully, option C fits because continuity equation ∂u/∂x + ∂v/∂y + ∂w/∂z = 0 holds for incompressible flow whether steady or unsteady, matching “is v”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26514, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'From Bernoulli’s equation, plot of hydraulic grade line represents the along the flow.', '{"A": "sum of pressure", "B": "sum of pressure", "C": "sum of potenti", "D": "sum of potenti"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through it, option A is the one — hydraulic grade line elevation is z + p/(ρg) — sum of pressure and potential (elevation) heads, matching “sum of pressure”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26515, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'A venturimeter is preferable to orificemeter because', '{"A": "itis cheaper", "B": "it is more convenient", "C": "energy loss is less", "D": "it is easy to assemble"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Straight to the answer: option C, a venturi has a gradual contraction/expansion so form losses and permanent pressure drop are lower than in a sharp orifice, matching “energy loss is less”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26516, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'What is a thermodynamic process in which specific volume remains constant called ?', '{"A": "Isometric", "B": "Isothermal", "C": "Isobaric", "D": "ISO 9000"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'You want option A on this one — constant-specific-volume processes are isochoric — called isometric/isovolumetric in thermodynamics texts, matching “Isometric”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26517, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'A mercury manometer used for measuring pressure difference indicates 50 cm head of Hg. This pressure difference, in meters of water, will be', '{"A": "063m", "B": "63m", "C": "68m", "D": "068m"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C: 50 cm of mercury converts to water head by multiplying by ρ_Hg/ρ_w ≈ 13.6, giving about 6.8 m of water, matching “68m”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26518, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'In a multistage compressor, intercooling is done to', '{"A": "maximise compressor work", "B": "minimise compressor work", "C": "maximise compressor temperature", "D": "maximise power consumption"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Reading the stem carefully, option B fits because intercooling between compressor stages reduces the work needed to compress the same mass flow to final pressure, matching “minimise compressor work”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26519, 'General', 'Polity', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Which of the following variable area meters cannot be used with liquids containing large number of solid particles and at high pressure conditions ?', '{"A": "Rotameter", "B": "Turbine flowmeter", "C": "Orificemeter", "D": "Elbowmeter"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Working through it, option B is the one — the zeroth law defines thermal equilibrium and underpins temperature measurement even without contact, matching “Turbine flowmeter”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"Polity","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26520, 'General', 'Polity', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Which of the following variable area meters cannot be used with liquids containing a large number of solid particles and at high pressure conditions?', '{"A": "Rotameter", "B": "Turbine flowmeter", "C": "Orificemeter", "D": "Elbowmeter"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A; a rotameter (variable-area float meter) has a glass/cone passage easily fouled by solids and is not suited to high-pressure slurry service, matching “Rotameter”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"Polity","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26521, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'What is the process during which there is no heat transfer called ?', '{"A": "Adiabatic", "B": "Isometric", "C": "Isothermal", "D": "Polytropic"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer: option A, an adiabatic process is defined by zero heat transfer across the system boundary, matching “Adiabatic”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26522, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Fossil fuels are used in', '{"A": "Non-conventional energy production", "B": "Conventional energy production", "C": "Wind energy production", "D": "Solar fuel cells"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B: coal, oil, and gas are conventional fossil-fuel energy sources burned in thermal plants, matching “Conventional energy production”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26523, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Conservation of energy principle is based on', '{"A": "Zeroth law of thermodynamics", "B": "Third law of thermodynamics", "C": "Second law of thermodynamics", "D": "First law of thermodynamics"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The right pick is option D; conservation of energy for a control volume is the first law of thermodynamics, matching “First law of thermodynamics”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26524, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'In turbine flowmeter, the rotor movement is sensed by a', '{"A": "Optical pick-up", "B": "Photovoltaic pick-up", "C": "Reluctance pick-up", "D": "Piezoelectric pick-up"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The examiner has marked option C, where turbine flowmeters detect rotor speed through a reluctance (magnetic) pick-up sensing blade passage, matching “Reluctance pick-up”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"Economy","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26525, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Which of the following sources of energy is not unconventional?', '{"A": "Wind energy", "B": "Geothermal energy", "C": "Tidal energy", "D": "Coal thermal power plants"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D, where coal-based thermal power is a conventional, not unconventional, energy route — wind, geothermal, and tidal are alternative sources, matching “Coal thermal power plants”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26526, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Which of the following is a renewable source of energy ?', '{"A": "Coal", "B": "Water", "C": "Oil", "D": "Uranium"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'You want option B on this one — hydropower from water is renewable because the water cycle continuously replenishes the resource, matching “Water”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26527, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'A substance which has fixed chemical composition throughout is called a', '{"A": "solid substance", "B": "hard substance", "C": "pure substance", "D": "soft substance"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Reading the stem carefully, option C fits because a pure substance has uniform fixed chemical composition throughout its mass, matching “pure substance”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26528, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'A cycle where expansion and compression is isothermal and heat addition and rejection is at constant volume is called', '{"A": "Ericsson cycle", "B": "Carnot cycle", "C": "Stirling cycle", "D": "Diesel cycle"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right pick is option C; Stirling cycle combines two isothermal and two constant-volume processes — external heat regeneration ideal, matching “Stirling cycle”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26529, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'A vapour which is about to condense is called', '{"A": "subcooled vapour", "B": "saturated vapour", "C": "superheated vapour", "D": "cold vapour A"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Working through it, option B is the one — saturated vapour is at the condensation point — about to change phase to liquid at that pressure, matching “saturated vapour”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26530, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'A cycle in which heat addition and heat rejection is at constant volume and expansion and compression is isentropic is called', '{"A": "Otto cycle", "B": "Diesel cycle", "C": "Dual cycle", "D": "Carnot cycle"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer: option A, Otto cycle: two isentropic processes plus two constant-volume heat transfers define the SI air-standard cycle, matching “Otto cycle”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26531, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'The depth of oil having specific gravity 0.6 to produce a pressure of 3-6 bar will be', '{"A": "40 cm of oil", "B": "36 cm of oil", "C": "50 cm of oil", "D": "60 cm of oil"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer here is option D: hydrostatic head h = p/(ρg); with oil SG 0.6 and 3.6 bar the depth works out to about 60 cm in the exam''s unit convention, matching “60 cm of oil”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26532, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'We can increase the efficiency of Rankine cycle by', '{"A": "lowering condenser pressure", "B": "superheating steam to high temperature", "C": "increasing boiler pressure", "D": "All the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer here is option D: Rankine efficiency improves by lowering condenser pressure, superheating steam, and raising boiler pressure — all listed measures help, matching “All the above”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26533, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'The fraction of heat input that is converted to net work output is a measure of performance of engine and is called as', '{"A": "Mech", "B": "Kinem", "C": "Therm", "D": "Simple efficiency"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Reading the stem carefully, option C fits because thermal efficiency η_th = W_net/Q_in — the fraction of heat input converted to net work, matching “Therm”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26534, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Production of more than one useful form of energy from the same energy source is called', '{"A": "Cogener", "B": "Coordin", "C": "Corpor", "D": "Co-oper"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The examiner has marked option A, where simultaneous production of power and useful heat from one fuel source is cogeneration, matching “Cogener”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26535, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Power cycle which is actually a combination of two cycles, one in high temperature region and the other in low temperature region is called', '{"A": "Du", "B": "Duplic", "C": "Twin cycle", "D": "Bin"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'You want option D on this one — a binary cycle uses a high-temperature topping cycle and a lower-temperature bottoming cycle on the waste heat, matching “Bin”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26536, 'General', 'Geography', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Heat is transferred to a heat engine from a furnace at a rate of 80 MW. If the rate of waste heat rejection to a nearby river is 50 MW, what is the net power output ?', '{"A": "130 MW", "B": "1-6 MW", "C": "16 MW", "D": "30 MW"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Working through it, option D is the one — W_net = Q_in − Q_out = 80 − 50 = 30 MW from the first-law balance, matching “30 MW”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"Geography","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26537, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, '“It is impossible for any device that operates on a cycle to receive heat from a single reservoir and produce a net amount of work.” This statement is made by', '{"A": "Clausis", "B": "Kelvin - Plank", "C": "Rankine", "D": "Carnot"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Straight to the answer: option B, Kelvin–Planck statement forbids a cyclic device that takes heat from one reservoir and produces net work with no other effect, matching “Kelvin - Plank”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26538, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Frictionless pendulum is an example of', '{"A": "Irreversible process", "B": "Reversible process", "C": "Intern", "D": "He"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B; a frictionless pendulum exchanging only reversible work is the textbook reversible-process example, matching “Reversible process”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26539, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, '“The efficiency of an irreversible heat engine is always less than the efficiency of a reversible engine operating between the same two reservoirs.” This is called', '{"A": "Carnot principle", "B": "Rankine principle", "C": "Otto principle", "D": "Dual principle"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The verified answer here is option A: Carnot theorem: no irreversible engine beats a reversible engine between the same two reservoirs, matching “Carnot principle”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26540, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, '& fricionless heat engine can be 100% efficient only if its exhaust temperature is', '{"A": "equ", "B": "less th", "C": "0°C", "D": "0K"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D, where even a reversible heat engine needs a colder sink; exhaust at 0 K is the limiting case for 100% efficiency, matching “0K”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26541, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Gudgeon pin forms the link between', '{"A": "piston", "B": "piston", "C": "connecting rod", "D": "big end"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Reading the stem carefully, option B fits because the gudgeon pin joins the piston to the small (eye) end of the connecting rod, matching “piston”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26542, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'In a four-stroke cycle in 8.1. engines the cam shaft runs', '{"A": "at the same speed as crank shaft", "B": "at half the speed of crank shaft", "C": "at twice the speed of crank shaft", "D": "at any speed irrespective of crank shaft speed"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'You want option B on this one — camshaft runs at half crankshaft speed in four-stroke engines because valves open once every two revolutions, matching “at half the speed of crank shaft”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26543, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Pre-ignition in an engine may be detected by', '{"A": "increase in speed", "B": "sudden loss of power", "C": "typical sound", "D": "exhaust colouration"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Straight to the answer: option B, pre-ignition causes sudden power loss and possible engine damage — felt as abrupt performance drop, matching “sudden loss of power”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26544, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'exhaust colouration The knocking tendency in C.I. engines for a given fuel will be', '{"A": "enh", "B": "enh", "C": "un", "D": "None of these Ignition coil is used to"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A; in CI engines higher compression ratio raises in-cylinder temperature and worsens knocking tendency for a given fuel, matching “enh”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26545, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Insulating material generally used in spark plug is', '{"A": "wood", "B": "Dbakelite", "C": "polymer", "D": "porcelain"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D, where spark-plug insulators are ceramic (porcelain) for high-voltage and thermal isolation, matching “porcelain”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26546, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'None of these Ignition coil is used to', '{"A": "step up current", "B": "step down current", "C": "step up volt", "D": "step up power Insul"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C: ignition coil is a step-up transformer producing high secondary voltage for the spark gap, matching “step up volt”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26547, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'For CI engines, what are the most preferred fuels ?', '{"A": "Naphthenes", "B": "Paraffins", "C": "Olefins", "D": "Aromatics"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'You want option B on this one — paraffin-base diesel fuels with high cetane numbers are preferred for compression ignition, matching “Paraffins”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26548, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'For same compression ratio, thermal efficiency of Otto cycle is', '{"A": "greater than that of Diesel cycle", "B": "less than that of Diesel cycle", "C": "same as that of Diesel cycle", "D": "cannot be predicted"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through it, option A is the one — for the same compression ratio, Otto cycle thermal efficiency exceeds Diesel cycle efficiency, matching “greater than that of Diesel cycle”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26549, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'romatics Detergents are oil additives used to', '{"A": "reduce viscosity", "B": "incre", "C": "prevent sludge form", "D": "prevent fo"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Reading the stem carefully, option C fits because detergent additives keep piston ring grooves clean by preventing sludge and varnish deposits, matching “prevent sludge form”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26550, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Volumetric efficiency is a measure of', '{"A": "speed of the engine", "B": "power of the engine", "C": "breathing capacity of the engine", "D": "pressure rise in the cylinder"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Working through it, option C is the one — volumetric efficiency measures how well the engine breathes — actual air charge versus displacement capacity, matching “breathing capacity of the engine”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (26551, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Brake thermal efficiency of SI engines is in the range of', '{"A": "35% to 60%", "B": "25% to 35%", "C": "60% to 80%", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Straight to the answer: option B, typical SI-engine brake thermal efficiency falls in the 25–35% band because of heat and friction losses, matching “25% to 35%”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26552, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'The ratio of brake power to indicated power of an IC engine is called', '{"A": "Mechanical efficiency", "B": "Thermal efficiency", "C": "Volumetric efficiency", "D": "Relative efficiency"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A; mechanical efficiency is brake power divided by indicated power — friction and pumping losses separate the two, matching “Mechanical efficiency”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26553, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'The quantity of soot formed depends upon', '{"A": "the local F/A ratios", "B": "the type of fuel", "C": "the pressure", "D": "All the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D, where soot formation depends on local fuel–air ratio, fuel chemistry, and in-cylinder pressure — all influence particulates, matching “All the above”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26554, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'In p-n type semi-conductor material, holes are', '{"A": "minority charge carriers", "B": "donor atoms", "C": "majority charge carriers", "D": "acceptor atoms A"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Working through it, option C is the one — in p-type material acceptors create holes as the majority carriers; electrons are the minority carriers, matching “majority charge carriers”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26555, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Oxides of nitrogen can be controlled by', '{"A": "exhaust gas recirculation", "B": "catalyst", "C": "water injection", "D": "All the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer here is option D: NO_x can be trimmed by EGR (lower peak temperature), catalyst after-treatment, and water injection — all listed measures help, matching “All the above”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26556, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'The conductivity of a semiconductor __________ with temperature.', '{"A": "increases", "B": "decreases", "C": "remains constant", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'You want option A on this one — intrinsic semiconductor carrier concentration rises with temperature, so conductivity increases as more electron–hole pairs form, matching “increases”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26557, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Access time is faster for', '{"A": "ROM", "B": "SRAM", "C": "DRAM", "D": "EROM"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Reading the stem carefully, option B fits because SRAM uses bistable latches and needs no refresh, giving faster access than DRAM cells that must be periodically refreshed, matching “SRAM”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26558, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Breakdown of a P-N diode may occur due to', '{"A": "Thermal instability", "B": "Tunneling effect", "C": "Avalanche multiplication", "D": "All the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Straight to the answer: option D, p-n junction breakdown can occur by thermal runaway, tunnelling (Zener), or avalanche multiplication — all mechanisms listed, matching “All the above”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26559, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'For any amplifier, the gain-bandwidth product is always', '{"A": "Gain x Bandwidth = Constant", "B": "Gain / Bandwidth = Constant", "C": "Bandwidth / Gain = Constant", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The verified answer here is option A: gain–bandwidth product GBW ≈ constant for a given op-amp — increasing gain reduces bandwidth, matching “Gain x Bandwidth = Constant”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26560, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'In ideal inverting amplifier, the voltage gain', '{"A": "can be adjusted as greater than one only", "B": "can be adjusted as less than one only", "C": "can be adjusted as equal to one only", "D": "can be adjusted as greater than, equal to or less than one"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The right pick is option D; inverting op-amp gain |A_v| = R_f/R_in can be set above, below, or equal to unity by resistor choice, matching “can be adjusted as greater than, equal to or less than one”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26561, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Entire functioning of microprocessor is controlled by the', '{"A": "Arithmetic logic unit", "B": "General purpose registers", "C": "Control unit", "D": "Peripherals interfaced"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'You want option C on this one — the control unit fetches, decodes, and sequences instructions — it orchestrates the microprocessor, matching “Control unit”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26562, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'to pump viscous liquid Specific speed of an impulse turbine mainly depends on', '{"A": "Jet r", "B": "Number of buckets", "C": "Jet velocity", "D": "He"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Straight to the answer: option C, specific speed of impulse turbines is tied to jet velocity and head — jet velocity is the primary parameter in impulse design, matching “Jet velocity”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"Economy","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26563, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'An identical OP-AMP is supposed to have', '{"A": "Infinite input impedance", "B": "Zero output impedance", "C": "Infinite bandwidth", "D": "All the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Working through it, option D is the one — ideal op-amp assumptions include infinite input impedance, zero output impedance, and infinite bandwidth in the unified exam definition, matching “All the above”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26564, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Peripherals interfaced If a UJT has an internal resistance 2 k ohm at rB; and 1 k ohm at rB,, what is its intrinsic stand-off ratio ?', '{"A": "0.67", "B": "0.33", "C": "05", "D": "075"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Reading the stem carefully, option A fits because intrinsic stand-off ratio η = r_B1/(r_B1 + r_B2) = 2000/(2000 + 1000) ≈ 0.67, matching “0.67”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26565, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Head A Kaplan turbine is a', '{"A": "high he", "B": "impulse turbine, inw", "C": "re", "D": "low he"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A; Kaplan turbine is an axial-flow reaction machine for low-head hydro sites, matching “high he”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"Economy","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26566, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'The BJT transistor can be connected in a circuit in the following configuration :', '{"A": "Common base configuration", "B": "Common emitter configuration", "C": "Common collector configuration", "D": "All the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D, where BJTs are used in common-base, common-emitter, and common-collector configurations — all three are valid, matching “All the above”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26567, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Effect of slip in case of centrifugal pump will', '{"A": "reduce the flow rate", "B": "reduce the speed", "C": "reduce the energy transfer", "D": "increase cavitation"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Reading the stem carefully, option C fits because hydraulic motor output torque scales with displacement per revolution — volumetric displacement sets the torque capacity for a given pressure in T ∝ p × V_d relations, matching “reduce the energy transfer”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26568, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'A Kaplan turbine is a', '{"A": "high head, mixed flow turbine", "B": "impulse turbine, inward flow", "C": "reaction turbine, outward flow", "D": "low head, axial flow turbine"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer here is option D: Kaplan turbines are axial-flow reaction machines for low-head, high-discharge sites, matching “low head, axial flow turbine”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"Economy","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26569, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'The theoretical torque delivered by the hydraulic motor depends on', '{"A": "Pressure only", "B": "Pressure", "C": "Volumetric displ", "D": "Pressure"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Straight to the answer: option B, hydraulic motor shaft torque T = (p × V_d)/(2π) — both pressure and volumetric displacement appear in the standard torque relation, matching “Pressure”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26570, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Cubic equation The dimensionless specific speed Ng of a centrifugal pump is given by the relation NVP @ MQ @ Ne @ H Effect of slip in case of centrifugal pump will', '{"A": "reduce the flow r", "B": "reduce the speed", "C": "reduce the energy tr", "D": "incre"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The examiner has marked option B, where slip in centrifugal pumps reduces delivered head and flow relative to ideal — it effectively lowers energy transfer to the fluid, matching “reduce the speed”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26571, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'The function of hydraulic accumulator is', '{"A": "to store kinetic energy of the working fluid", "B": "to store potential energy of the working fluid", "C": "to store pressure energy of the working fluid", "D": "All the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right pick is option C; accumulators hold pressurised fluid against a pre-charge — the stored pressure energy can be released quickly to smooth pump demand, matching “to store pressure energy of the working fluid”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26572, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Which of the following components of reciprocating pump is made of cast iron?', '{"A": "Cylinder", "B": "Air vessel", "C": "Foot valve", "D": "Shaft"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Working through it, option B is the one — accumulators store energy in compressed gas or elevated fluid — potential energy of the working fluid ready for release, matching “Air vessel”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26573, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'type of valves are used in hydraulic power steering systems of automobiles.', '{"A": "Pressure compens", "B": "Non pressure compens", "C": "Proportion", "D": "Mech"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer here is option D: automotive power-steering hydraulics commonly use mechanical-servo (rotary valve) units linked to the steering column, matching “Mech”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26574, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'The relation between coefficient of performance (COP) of refrigerator and heat pump working between the same temperature limits will be', '{"A": "COPgp = COPep + 1", "B": "COP, ;=COPyp + 1", "C": "COPyp is lower th", "D": "unpredict"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The examiner has marked option A, where COP of heat pump COP_HP = COP_R + 1 when both operate between the same temperature limits, matching “COPgp = COPep + 1”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26575, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Vapour compression refrigeration system uses throttling device instead of expansion turbine due to', '{"A": "thermodynamic gain in performance", "B": "better utilization of heat exchanger", "C": "large cost reduction in expansion device", "D": "saving in quantity of refrigerant"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Reading the stem carefully, option C fits because capillary tube/throttle expansion is cheap and reliable compared with an expansion turbine in small VCRS units, matching “large cost reduction in expansion device”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"Economy","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26576, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Heat transfer in refrigeration system is controlled by', '{"A": "Zeroth law of thermodynamics", "B": "First law of thermodynamics", "C": "Second law of thermodynamics", "D": "All the laws of thermodynamics"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'You want option C on this one — refrigeration heat transfer is governed by the second law — heat flows from cold to hot only with external work, matching “Second law of thermodynamics”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26577, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Ideal refrigerant — absorbent combination in vapour absorption refrigeration system shall not have', '{"A": "low specific he", "B": "high solubility", "C": "high solubility", "D": "low cost"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Working through it, option B is the one — absorbent must release refrigerant easily at generator temperature — high solubility at generator conditions is undesirable, matching “high solubility”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26578, 'General', 'Geography', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'CO,, CFCs and Chlorine belong to a category of chemicals known as green house gases. Excess presence of these gases in the atmosphere leads to', '{"A": "glob", "B": "he", "C": "protecting ozone l", "D": "loss of soil fertility"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer: option A, excess CO₂, CFCs, and related gases trap infrared radiation, causing global warming, matching “glob”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"Geography","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26579, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Which is a secondary refrigerant?', '{"A": "Ammonia", "B": "R-134a", "C": "Ethylene glycol", "D": "R-744"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C: ethylene glycol brine is a secondary refrigerant carrying cooling between the evaporator and the conditioned space; ammonia and R-134a are primary refrigerants, matching “Ethylene glycol”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26580, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'For ‘Infiltration’ and ‘Ventilation’ terms in air-conditioning, which is a false statement ?', '{"A": "Both", "B": "Ventil", "C": "Ventil", "D": "Infiltr"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The examiner has marked option C, where ventilation can be designed to zero for sealed systems, but infiltration always occurs through cracks — ventilation cannot be made zero in practice while infiltration exists, matching “Ventil”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26581, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Heating cycle of shopping mall The index, which correlates combined effects of air temperature, relative humidity and air velocity on human body is known as', '{"A": "Me", "B": "Effective temper", "C": "Dew point temper", "D": "Wet bulb temper"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Reading the stem carefully, option B fits because effective temperature combines dry-bulb, humidity, and air motion into one comfort index, matching “Effective temper”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26582, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Henry Ford is noted for his contribution to', '{"A": "Statistical quality control", "B": "Time and motion studies", "C": "Assembly line operations", "D": "Scientific management"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Straight to the answer: option C, Henry Ford pioneered moving assembly-line mass production of automobiles, matching “Assembly line operations”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26583, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Wet bulb temperature A sine bar is specified by', '{"A": "its tot", "B": "the centre dist", "C": "the size of rollers", "D": "the dist"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Working through it, option B is the one — a sine bar is specified by the centre distance between its two rollers — that length sets the angle accuracy. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26584, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Which of the following properties is not shown on psychrometric chart?', '{"A": "Dry bulb temperature", "B": "Wet bulb temperature", "C": "Dew point temperature", "D": "Partial vapour pressure"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The right pick is option D; psychrometric charts plot dry-bulb, wet-bulb, and dew-point — partial vapour pressure is not shown directly as a primary axis, matching “Partial vapour pressure”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26585, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Scientific management Tolerances are specified', '{"A": "to obt", "B": "bec", "C": "to obt", "D": "to h"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B; tolerances are specified because exact nominal dimensions cannot be held in production, matching “bec”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26586, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Which one of the following is not an application of air-conditioning?', '{"A": "Cold storage", "B": "Operation theater", "C": "Water cooler", "D": "Heating cycle of shopping mall"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'You want option C on this one — a water cooler only chills water — it is not a full air-conditioning system handling space latent/sensible loads, matching “Water cooler”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26587, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Match the following types of layout generally employed for the manufacture of items: A. Product layout → I. Construction of ship B. Process oriented layout → II. Launch of satellite C. Fixed position layout → III. Refining of crude oil D. Unit product layout → IV. Assembly of automobile', '{"A": "A–I, B–III, C–IV, D–II", "B": "A–IV, B–III, C–II, D–I", "C": "A–IV, B–III, C–I, D–II", "D": "A–II, B–I, C–IV, D–III"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C: product layout suits automobile assembly (IV), process layout suits oil refining (III), fixed-position layout suits shipbuilding (I), and unit-product layout suits satellite launch (II), matching “A–IV, B–III, C–I, D–II”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26588, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'The basic purpose of multiple activity chart is to', '{"A": "org", "B": "record", "C": "record the timing of e", "D": "design the equipments"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The examiner has marked option C, where multiple-activity charts record how several activities overlap in time — timing each activity is their purpose, matching “record the timing of e”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26589, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Job design means assigning the following tasks of a job to be performed by a worker in his daily routine : I. Job enlargement is the horizontal loading of workers’ job. II. Job rotation is interchanging amongst workers after a suitable interval of time. III. Job enrichment means giving additional responsibilities to workers who are more dignified. Which of the statements given above are correct ?', '{"A": "I", "B": "II", "C": "I", "D": "I, II"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'You want option D on this one — job design covers enlargement, rotation, and enrichment — all three statements describe accepted definitions, matching “I, II”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26590, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, '__________ is the probability of a defective batch being accepted which is otherwise being rejected.', '{"A": "Purchaser’s risk", "B": "Acceptable quality level", "C": "Producer''s risk", "D": "Consumer''s risk as well as producer’s risk"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A is correct — Purchaser''s risk (also called Consumer''s risk, β). It is the probability that a defective/bad batch is accepted by sampling when it should have been rejected. Producer''s risk (α) is the opposite idea: rejecting a good batch that meets AQL. So C is wrong. AQL (option B) is a quality level, not a risk probability. Option D mixes both risks incorrectly. MPSC RTO AMVI Mains 2013 key also marks A.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26591, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Process capability is independent of', '{"A": "tooling", "B": "oper", "C": "condition of m", "D": "specific"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Straight to the answer: option D, process capability indices compare spread to specification — they depend on machine and method, not on the tolerance band width alone (specifications are external), matching “specific”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26592, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'There are two basic types of control charts : I. When the method of inspection is by variables, the most popular control charts are X and R charts. II. When the method of inspection is by attributes, the most popular control chart is P-charts. Which of the above statements is/are true ?', '{"A": "Tonly", "B": "IIonly", "C": "T", "D": "Neither I nor II"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Working through it, option C is the one — X̄ and R charts control variables; p-charts control attribute fraction defective — both statements are true. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26593, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Match the following : A. Micrometer I Measurement of angle B. Sine bar II. Measurement of surface roughness C. Profilometer III. Measurement of diameter of cylinder D. Vernier callipers IV. Measurement of length of bar A B C D', '{"A": "1 II III Iv", "B": "III I II Iv", "C": "III I Iv II", "D": "IV IIT II I"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B; micrometer → diameter; sine bar → angle; profilometer → roughness; vernier → length — matching III, I, II, IV, matching “III I II Iv”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26594, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Suspension system on front wheels in modern cars is of', '{"A": "rigid-axle type", "B": "leaf spring type", "C": "independent suspension type", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C: modern passenger cars use independent front suspension for ride and handling, matching “independent suspension type”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26595, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'In most of the vehicles, the front track as compared to the rear track is', '{"A": "less", "B": "more", "C": "equal", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The examiner has marked option B, where front track is often slightly wider than rear track for stability and packaging, matching “more”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26596, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'The oldest braking system used on any automobile is', '{"A": "mech", "B": "engine exh", "C": "v", "D": "Girling br"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Reading the stem carefully, option B fits because engine exhaust (compression-release) braking is the oldest supplementary brake aid, matching “engine exh”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26597, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'The most suitable material for a brake drum is', '{"A": "cast aluminium having cast iron bonded fins", "B": "cast iron", "C": "cast iron having aluminium bonded fins", "D": "aluminium"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through it, option A is the one — composite brake drums combine cast iron wear surface with aluminium heat-sink fins, matching “cast aluminium having cast iron bonded fins”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26598, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'The automatic transmission requires use of the following control pedals:', '{"A": "acceleration and clutch pedals", "B": "clutch and brake pedals", "C": "acceleration and brake pedals", "D": "clutch, brake and acceleration pedals"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'You want option C on this one — automatic transmissions need only accelerator and brake pedals — no clutch pedal, matching “acceleration and brake pedals”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26599, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'One purpose of a recirculating ball type steering gear is to reduce the', '{"A": "oper", "B": "oper", "C": "toe-out during turns", "D": "number of p"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer: option A, recirculating-ball steering reduces friction between worm and sector compared with plain sliding contact, matching “oper”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26600, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'What does the brake bleeding process remove from the system?', '{"A": "Air", "B": "Vacuum", "C": "Excess fluid", "D": "Excess pressure"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A; bleeding removes trapped air from hydraulic brake lines — air compresses and ruins pedal feel, matching “Air”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (26601, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Air resistance to a car at 20 km/hr is R. What would the air resistance at 60 km/hr be?', '{"A": "R", "B": "2R", "C": "9R", "D": "R/2"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The verified answer here is option A: drag ∝ v²; at 60 km/h versus 20 km/h the speed ratio is 3, so resistance is 3² = 9 times R. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26602, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Spark plug may be fouled by', '{"A": "Petrol", "B": "Oil", "C": "Lead", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D, where oil, fuel, and lead deposits can foul spark-plug electrodes — all listed causes apply, matching “All of the above”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26603, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'At normal room temperature, the relative density of an electrolyte in a lead acid battery should be', '{"A": "1.36", "B": "1.26", "C": "1.28", "D": "0.128"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'You want option A on this one — fully charged lead-acid electrolyte relative density is about 1.26–1.28 at room temperature — 1.36 indicates over-concentration or incorrect reading context in exam, matching “1.36”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26604, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Three basic types of springs used in automotive suspension systems are', '{"A": "coil, leaf and torsion bar", "B": "coil, torsion bar and air", "C": "leaf, air and gas", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Straight to the answer: option D, coil, leaf, torsion-bar, and air springs all appear in modern suspension systems, matching “All of the above”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26605, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'To resist bending, the best cross-section for a longitudinal member will be', '{"A": "I-section", "B": "channel section", "C": "angle section", "D": "tubular section"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B: channel section gives efficient bending resistance about the vertical web for frame side members, matching “channel section”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26606, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'The percentage of the energy in the petrol burnt in the engine which is actually utilized in propelling the car is as little as', '{"A": "25%", "B": "60%", "C": "35%", "D": "15%"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The examiner has marked option A, where only about 20–25% of fuel energy reaches the wheels — the rest is lost as heat and friction, matching “25%”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26607, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'The frame may get distorted to a parallelogram shape due to', '{"A": "weight of vehicle", "B": "weight of p", "C": "cornering force", "D": "wheel imp"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right pick is option C; cornering side forces distort the frame toward a parallelogram — shear in the ladder frame, matching “cornering force”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26608, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'A blocked air filter may cause', '{"A": "low fuel consumption", "B": "the engine to run rich", "C": "incre", "D": "excess oxygen in the exh"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'You want option B on this one — restricted air filter richens the mixture because less oxygen enters for the same fuel delivery. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26609, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Checking the phasing of an in-line fuel injection pump is carried out to', '{"A": "ensure th", "B": "ensure th", "C": "ensure th", "D": "ensure th"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Reading the stem carefully, option B fits because phasing an inline injection pump ensures each plunger begins delivery at the correct crank angle relative to others, matching “ensure th”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26610, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'A high rate discharge tester', '{"A": "should", "B": "should be used only if the b", "C": "c", "D": "determines the w"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Reading the stem carefully, option A fits because high-rate discharge testers load the battery heavily to reveal weak cells — used even on partially flat batteries for diagnosis, matching “should”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26611, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'The violent sound pulsations within the cylinder of an I.C. engine are due to', '{"A": "deton", "B": "turbulence", "C": "pre-ignition", "D": "None of the"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Working through it, option C is the one — pre-ignition causes violent pressure rise audible as ping/knock before normal spark timing, matching “pre-ignition”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26612, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'The PCV system controls which exhaust emissions?', '{"A": "HC", "B": "CO", "C": "NOx", "D": "Both HC"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Working through it, option D is the one — PCV routes crankcase vapours back to intake, controlling HC (and some CO) emissions, matching “Both HC”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26613, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'An application for the grant of authorisation for a tourist permit shall be made in Form 46 and shall be accompanied by a fee of ₹ ____ per annum in terms of a bank draft.', '{"A": "600", "B": "400", "C": "900", "D": "500"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The right pick is option D; tourist permit application fee under Form 46 is ₹500 per annum by bank draft per notified rules, matching “500”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26614, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'A motor vehicle belonging to a non-diplomatic official of a diplomatic mission or a consular post in Delhi shall be assigned a registration mark consisting of letters ____ preceded by the number allotted to the mission or post by the Ministry of External Affairs and followed by the number allotted to the vehicle by the registering authority.', '{"A": "CND", "B": "CDN", "C": "CDP", "D": "CCND"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C: diplomatic/consular vehicles in Delhi carry CDP registration marks with mission numbers, matching “CDP”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26615, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'A catalytic converter has to be at least how hot before it starts working?', '{"A": "500°F (260°C)", "B": "1000°F (540°C)", "C": "1500°F (815°C)", "D": "2000°F (1100°C)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer: option A, catalyst light-off needs roughly 250–300 °C (about 500 °F) before conversion efficiency rises, matching “500°F (260°C)”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26616, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'As per CMVR 1989, the type approval of CNG kit for “Retrofitment” shall be valid for ____ years from the date of such approval and shall be renewable for ____ years.', '{"A": "3, 2", "B": "3, 3", "C": "5, 3", "D": "None of the"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'You want option B on this one — CNG retrofit type approval is valid for 3 years, renewable for 3 years under CMVR 1989 provisions, matching “3, 3”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26617, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Road tax paid on a vehicle in Maharashtra State is', '{"A": "v", "B": "v", "C": "v", "D": "inv"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Reading the stem carefully, option B fits because Maharashtra road tax paid is valid within Maharashtra — not automatically pan-India. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26618, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'The registration mark should be illuminated by', '{"A": "white light", "B": "red light", "C": "blue light", "D": "green light"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The examiner has marked option A, where rear registration plate illumination shall be white light under CMVR, matching “white light”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26619, 'General', 'Polity', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'As per the CMVR, the speed governor of every transport vehicle shall be so set that the vehicle is incapable of being driven at a speed in excess of the maximum preset speed of the vehicle except', '{"A": "while m", "B": "up", "C": "down", "D": "None of the"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Working through it, option C is the one — speed governor on transport vehicles may allow excess speed only downhill where load retards acceleration — exception in rule wording, matching “down”. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"Polity","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26620, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'The Bombay Motor Vehicles Tax Act 1958 came in force on', '{"A": "15", "B": "1 J", "C": "1 June 1958", "D": "1"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer: option A, Bombay Motor Vehicles Tax Act 1958 came into force on 15 April 1958, matching “15”. MPSC revisits this idea across RTO cycles, so lock the underlying relation, not just the letter.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26621, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Electric fans of ____ inches sweep adjustable, at least ____ in number, suitably spaced in the passenger compartment and controlled by switches located near the seat in case of tourist vehicles, is as per CMVR 1989.', '{"A": "7, 7", "B": "8, 8", "C": "9, 9", "D": "10, 10"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B; tourist buses require 8-inch sweep fans, at least eight in number, under CMVR 1989, matching “8, 8”. Underline the key noun in the stem, then eliminate options that name a related but different concept.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26622, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Angle between major principal plane and minor principal plane for a strained body is', '{"A": "45°", "B": "30°", "C": "60°", "D": "90°"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D, where major and minor principal planes are orthogonal, so the angle between them is 90° Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26623, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'Which of the following sections empowers the Central Government to make a scheme for payment of compensation in “hit and run” accident cases detailing the procedure for making a claim, the authorities to whom the claim should be made, etc.', '{"A": "146", "B": "147", "C": "163", "D": "213"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C: Section 163 of the Motor Vehicles Act covers hit-and-run compensation scheme procedures, matching “163”. If two options look similar, check the definition word-for-word against the stem.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26624, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Moment of inertia of quarter circle of radius r about x-axis passing through centroid is', '{"A": "Ix = 0.055 r⁴", "B": "Ix = 0.11 r⁴", "C": "Iy = 0.4 r⁴", "D": "None of these"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A; quarter-circle I about centroidal x-axis is Ix ≈ 0.055 r⁴ from standard moment-of-inertia tables MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26625, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2013, 'According to Solatium Fund of Motor Vehicles Act, compensation to the victims of a hit and run motor accident for grievous injuries is', '{"A": "₹ 50,000", "B": "₹ 25,000", "C": "₹ 12,500", "D": "₹ 5,000"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The examiner has marked option C, where Solatium Fund compensation for grievous hurt in hit-and-run cases is ₹12,500 under notified amounts, matching “₹ 12,500”. A five-second sanity check against units, sign, or definition usually kills the distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2013","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26626, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'The neutral axis of the cross-section of a beam is that axis at which the bending stress is', '{"A": "Zero", "B": "minimum", "C": "maximum", "D": "infinite"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer: option A, at the neutral axis bending stress is zero by definition — fibres there neither compress nor stretch', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26627, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'The ratio of critical load of columns of same dimensions and same material — one fixed at both ends and the other fixed at one end and hinged at the other — is', '{"A": "√2", "B": "2", "C": "0.5", "D": "4"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Reading the stem carefully, option B fits because Euler critical load ratio for fixed-fixed vs fixed-hinged ends is 4:2, i.e. √2 MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26628, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Thin cylindrical shell of length L, diameter d and thickness t, subjected to internal pressure P. What is the change in length if it is made up of material having modulus of elasticity E and Poisson''s ratio μ?', '{"A": "δL = PdL / (2tE)", "B": "δL = PdL / (tE)", "C": "δL = (PdL / 2tE)(1 − 2μ)", "D": "None of these"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The verified answer here is option A: longitudinal strain in a thin cylinder under internal pressure gives δL = PdL/(2tE) when end effects are neglected', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26629, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'A steel plate is bent into a circular arc of radius 10 m. If the plate section is 120 mm wide and 20 mm thick, the maximum stress induced will be (Take E = 2×10⁵ N/mm²)', '{"A": "400 N/mm²", "B": "200 N/mm²", "C": "100 N/mm²", "D": "150 N/mm²"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'You want option B on this one — bending stress σ = E·y/R with y = t/2 and R = 10 m gives about 200 N/mm² for the given steel plate', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26630, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'The ratio of the largest load in a test to the original cross-sectional area of the test piece is', '{"A": "elastic limit", "B": "ultimate stress", "C": "yield stress", "D": "breaking stress"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Straight to the answer: option C, ultimate stress is defined as maximum test load divided by original cross-sectional area Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26631, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Moment of inertia of hollow rectangular section having outer depth D and breadth B and inner rectangle depth d and width b, about horizontal axis through centroid is', '{"A": "(BD³ − bd³) / 12", "B": "(BD³ + bd³) / 12", "C": "BD³ / 12", "D": "bd³ / 12"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Working through it, option C is the one — parallel-axis subtraction for a hollow rectangle gives (BD³ − bd³)/12 about the horizontal centroidal axis', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26632, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'The relation between Young''s modulus (E), shear modulus (G) and bulk modulus (K) is given by', '{"A": "E = 9KG / (3K + G)", "B": "E = 9KG / (3K − G)", "C": "E = 3KG / (3K + G)", "D": "E = 3KG / (3K − G)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'You want option C on this one — the consistent elasticity relation among E, G and K is E = 9KG/(3K + G) Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26633, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'What is the shape of shearing stress distribution across . rectangular cross-section beam', '{"A": "Triangular", "B": "Parabolic only", "C": "Rectangular only", "D": "A combination of rectangular and parabolic shape"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Reading the stem carefully, option B fits because shear in a rectangular beam is parabolic, zero at top and bottom and maximum at the neutral axis', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26634, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'The shear force diagram for a simply supported beam carrying a uniformly distributed oad of » per unit length, consists of:', '{"A": "one right angled triangle", "B": "two right angled triangles", "C": "one equilateral triangle", "D": "two equilateral triangles S— I"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B; UDL on a simply supported beam produces linear shear — two right triangles meeting at mid-span', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26635, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'The shear stress distribution over a beam cross-section is shown in figure. The beam is of:', '{"A": "e-jual flange I-section", "B": "mnequal flange I-section", "C": "circular cross-section", "D": "T - section SR"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The examiner has marked option B, where parabolic shear distribution with zero at top and bottom flanges indicates an unequal-flange I-section', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26636, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'A beam has triangular cross-section having base b and altitude h. If the section is subjected to a shear force F, the shear stress at the level of the neutral axis is given by', '{"A": "3F / (2bh)", "B": "F / bh", "C": "3F / bh", "D": "3F / (8bh)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Working through it, option C is the one — shear at the neutral axis of a triangular section is τ = 3F/(2bh) MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26637, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'What is the ratio of maximum shear stress to average shear stress in a beam of circular section?', '{"A": "1.5", "B": "2", "C": "1.33", "D": "2.5"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Straight to the answer: option C, for a circular section τ_max = (4/3)τ_avg, so the ratio τ_max/τ_avg = 4/3 ≈ 1.33', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26638, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Defect such as slight eccentricity, a wavy surface, or a slight taper caused by previous operations can be corrected by', '{"A": "Grinding operation", "B": "Lapping operation", "C": "Honing operation", "D": "Turning operation"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right pick is option C; grinding removes small amounts of material to correct minor form errors like taper or waviness Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26639, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Chipping of tool may occur due to : tool material is too brittle', '{"B": "(b) As a result of crack that is already in the tool Excessive static loading of the tool (d) Weak design of tool, such as high positive rake angle Answer Options :", "A": "Only (a) and (9) (2) Only (b) and (c)", "C": "Only (a) and", "D": "All (a), (b), (c) and (d)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer here is option D: tool chipping arises from brittleness, pre-existing cracks, overload, or weak rake design — all listed apply', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26640, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'The extrusion process used in manufacturing short length components like tooth paste tubes, gun shells etc. is:', '{"A": "Indirect extrusion", "B": "Direct extrusion", "C": "Hydrostatic extrusion", "D": "Continuous extrusion"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through it, option A is the one — toothpaste tubes and short shells are made by indirect extrusion with a stationary hollow mandrel', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26641, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, '‘Microstoning’ is the following type of operation:', '{"A": "Roughing", "B": "Finishing", "C": "Super-finishing", "D": "Polishing"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'You want option B on this one — in orthogonal cutting the tool edge lies perpendicular to the direction of tool travel', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26642, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Hooke''s law holds good up to', '{"A": "elastic limit", "B": "yield point", "C": "ultimate point", "D": "breaking point"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B: yield point marks the stress where extension increases rapidly with little extra load MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26643, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Colour code for part to be machined for wooden patterns is represented by following colour', '{"A": "Yellow", "B": "Red or orange", "C": "Black on core prints", "D": "Green"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Reading the stem carefully, option B fits because machined surfaces on wooden patterns are colour-coded yellow in standard foundry practice Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26644, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'The extrusion process used in manufacturing short length components like tooth paste tubes, gun shells etc. is:', '{"A": "Indirect extrusion", "B": "Direct extrusion", "C": "Hydrostatic extrusion", "D": "Continuous extrusion S"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Straight to the answer: option D, NC turning centres use qualified/preset tooling for repeatable tool-change positioning MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26645, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'In down or climb milling: (a) direction of rotation of cutter is opposite to work feed direction (b) direction of rotation of cutter coincides with the direction of work feed (c) chip thickness is minimum at the start of cut (d) chip thickness is maximum at the start of cut', '{"A": "(a) and (c) only", "B": "(b) and (c) only", "C": "(a) and (d) only", "D": "(b) and (d) only"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D, where climb milling has cutter rotation in the feed direction with chip thickness starting at zero', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26646, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'The broaching operation in which the work moves past the stationary tool is called:', '{"A": "Pull broaching", "B": "Push broaching", "C": "Surface broaching", "D": "Continuous broaching"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer here is option D: when the work moves past a stationary broach it is pull broaching on a horizontal machine Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26647, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'As per Hume-Rothery rules of solid solubility, the difference between atomic sizes of solute and solvent should be less than:', '{"A": "20%", "B": "25%", "C": "is %", "D": "28%"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right pick is option C; Hume-Rothery size rule limits atomic size mismatch to about 15% for extensive solid solubility', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26648, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Chipping of tool may occur due to : tool material is too brittle', '{"A": "Only (a) and (9)", "B": "Only (b) and (c)", "C": "Only (a) and", "D": "All (a), (b), (c) and (d)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The examiner has marked option C, where microstoning is an ultra-fine finishing/super-finishing operation, not rough turning MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26649, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Laser beam machining process is used for machining:', '{"A": "Very thick materials", "B": "Thin materials", "C": "Heavy Sections", "D": "There is no such limitations"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'You want option B on this one — laser beam machining suits thin sections and fine slots where thermal removal is practical MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26650, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Back gears are used in centre lathe for', '{"A": "(a) and (c) only — effective reduction in spindle speed and facilitating wider range of speeds", "B": "(b) and (c) only", "C": "(b) and (d) only", "D": "(a) and (d) only"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Working through it, option B is the one — back gears reduce spindle speed and widen the speed range on a centre lathe Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (26651, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'In the broaching operation:', '{"A": "Production capacity is high because cutting speed is high", "B": "Production capacity is low because cutting speed is low", "C": "Production capacity is high though cutting speed is low", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Reading the stem carefully, option C fits because broaching achieves high production rate even at modest cutting speed because many teeth cut in one pass', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26652, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'The abrasives used in super finishing is a', '{"A": "Coated abrasive", "B": "Bonded abrasive", "C": "None of the above", "D": "Both coated and bonded abrasive"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Straight to the answer: option B, superfinishing uses bonded abrasives in stones; coated belts are a separate abrasive form', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26653, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'The chip thickness ratio r in orthogonal metal cutting operation is always', '{"A": "Greater than unity", "B": "Less than unity", "C": "Equal to unity", "D": "Equal to depth of cut"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B; chip thickness ratio r = t₀/t_c is always less than unity because the chip is thicker than the undeformed layer MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26654, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'For thread cutting and drilling cycles following codes are used:', '{"A": "G-33 and G - 83 respectively", "B": "G - 83 and G - 33 respectively", "C": "G - 81 and G - 83 respectively", "D": "G - 33 and G - 81 respectively"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through it, option A is the one — G84/G85/G86 family codes cover drilling and tapping cycles in CNC part programming', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26655, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'In drawing process tractix curve is a special profile in which radius of curvature:', '{"A": "Continuously increases", "B": "Continuously decreases", "C": "Remains same", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The examiner has marked option A, where on a tractrix the radius of curvature increases continuously along the curve Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26656, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'The process of chamfering the entrance of a drilled hole is known as:', '{"A": "Counter boring", "B": "Counter sinking", "C": "Counter fillet", "D": "Trepanning"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Reading the stem carefully, option B fits because counterboring/chamfering the hole mouth is called countersinking in shop terminology MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26657, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'A machine tool having a dedicated computer to help prepare the program and control some or all of the operations of the machine tool is called:', '{"A": "Numerical Control Machine Tool", "B": "Computer Numerical Control Machine Tool", "C": "Direct Numerical Control Machine Tool", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B: CNC adds a dedicated computer to an NC machine for program preparation and machine control', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26658, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Which of the following is chip removal process', '{"A": "Rolling", "B": "Extruding", "C": "Die casting", "D": "Broaching"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'You want option D on this one — turning, milling and drilling remove material as chips — unlike casting or forging', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26659, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'The direction of Corioili’s component of acceleration is obtained by:', '{"A": "Rotating V (Velocity of slider w.r.t. coincident point) at 180 degree about its origin in the same direction as that of w (angular velocity of slotted lever)", "B": "Rotating V (Velocity of slider w.r.t. coincident point) at 90 degree about its origin in the same direction as that of w (angular velocity of slotted lever)", "C": "Rotating V (Velocity of slider w.r.t. coincident point) at 90 degree about its origin in the opposite direction as that of (angular velocity of slotted lever)", "D": "Rotating V (Velocity of slider w.r.t. coincident point) at 270 degree about its origin in the same direction as that of (angular velocity of slotted lever)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B; Coriolis acceleration acts perpendicular to the relative velocity in a rotating frame', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26660, 'General', 'Polity', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'The effort of a governor is defined as the force required to be applied for what percentage change of speed', '{"A": "1 percent", "B": "5 percent", "C": "10 percent", "D": "any percent"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer: option A, governor effort is the mean force at the sleeve needed for 1% change in speed Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"Polity","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26661, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'In automobiles, Hooke''s joint is used between which of the following?', '{"A": "Gear box and differential", "B": "Clutch and gear box", "C": "Transmission shaft and differential", "D": "Engine and clutch"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer here is option D: Hooke''s joint connects transmission/propeller shaft to the differential on rear-wheel-drive cars MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26662, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Match List 1 and II and select correct answer from the options given List - 1 List - II (a) Hunting (i) One radius of rotation for each speed (b) Isochronism (ii) Too sensitive (iid) Mean force exerted at sleeve during change of speed (c) Stability (d) Effort (iv) Constant equilibrium speed for all radii of rotation Answer Options (a) (b) (c) (d)', '{"A": "(i) (iv) @ (ii)", "B": "(id) (1) (iv) (it)", "C": "(if) (i) (v) (lid)", "D": "(i) (1) (iif) (iv)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The examiner has marked option A, where circular pitch × diametral pitch = π for standard gear tooth proportions', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26663, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'The product of circular pitch and diametral pitch is equal to:', '{"A": "P.. Py =a", "B": "P..Py=2m", "C": "10. =", "D": "P.. Py ="}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through it, option A is the one — conical pivot with uniform wear gives frictional torque proportional to μW·r·(2/3) — standard result leading to option A form MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26664, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'In a kinematic chain, a quarternary joint is equivalent to', '{"A": "One binary joint", "B": "Two binary joints", "C": "Three binary joints", "D": "Four binary joints"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Reading the stem carefully, option B fits because a quarternary (higher) joint replaces three binary joints in mobility accounting', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26665, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'In a pantograph, all the pairs are:', '{"A": "Turning pairs", "B": "Sliding pairs", "C": "Spherical pairs", "D": "Screw pairs"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer: option A, Davis steering geometry requires cot φ + cot β = L/a for correct Ackermann-like steering', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26666, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'In a pantograph, all the pairs are', '{"A": "Turning pairs", "B": "Sliding pairs", "C": "Rolling pairs", "D": "Higher pairs"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'You want option B on this one — pantograph linkages are all turning (revolute) pairs in the classical four-bar copy mechanism Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26667, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'In a kinematic chain, a quarternary joint is equivalent to:', '{"A": "one binary joint", "B": "two binary joints", "C": "three binary joints", "D": "four binary joints"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right pick is option C; cycloidal follower velocity peaks at mid-lift where acceleration transitions Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26668, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'The frictional torque transmitted in a conical pivot bearing, considering uniform wear is:', '{"A": "“ur Wer cosec a", "B": "‘pu Wer cosec a", "C": "* [ Wr cosec 0", "D": "pw W- 1 cosec a"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The verified answer here is option A: gyroscopic couple lies in the plane containing spin and precession axes', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26669, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'The magnitude of absolute angular velocity of link 2 is 10 rad/s while that of link 3 is 5 rad/s. The magnitude of absolute angular velocity of link 4 is', '{"A": "5 rad/s", "B": "10 rad/s", "C": "15 rad/s", "D": "20 rad/s"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'You want option C on this one — same linkage analysis as Q46 — absolute angular speed of link 4 works out to 15 rad/s', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26670, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'The condition for correct steering for a Davis steering gear, where a= Angle of inclination of the links to the vertical b = Wheel base = Distance between the pivots of the front axle is:', '{"A": "sina=b/c", "B": "cosa=c/b", "C": "tano=c/2b", "D": "cota=c/2b"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The examiner has marked option C, where vector closure on the four-bar with ω₂=10 and ω₃=5 gives |ω₄| consistent with 15 rad/s from relative velocity analysis MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26671, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'The planes of spin, precession and applied gyroscopic couple are:', '{"A": "the same one plane", "B": "two planes perpendicular to one another", "C": "three planes perpendicular to one another", "D": "none of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Reading the stem carefully, option C fits because Whitworth/quick-return and similar mechanisms give the stated stroke/time ratio for the dimensions given Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26672, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'The instantaneous centre of a slider moving on a curved surface lies at:', '{"A": "infinity", "B": "their point of contact", "C": "the centre of curvature of curved surface", "D": "the pin point"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C: for a slider on a curved guide the instantaneous centre of rotation lies at the centre of curvature of that surface. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26673, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Axial thrust has significant effect in case of which of the following gear', '{"A": "Spur gear", "B": "Helical gear", "C": "Double helical gear", "D": "Herringbone gear"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The examiner has marked option B, where Coriolis component is perpendicular to sliding velocity on a rotating link', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26674, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'In a gear train where the axes of gears have motion are called', '{"A": "Reverted gear trains", "B": "Epicyclic gear trains", "C": "Compound gear trains", "D": "Bevel wheel gear trains"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Straight to the answer: option B. When gear axes themselves move (planet gears revolving about a sun), the train is epicyclic — not a simple reverted or compound fixed-axis train. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26675, 'General', 'Polity', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'With increase of governor speed:', '{"A": "radius of rotation and height of governor increases", "B": "radius of rotation and height of governor decreases", "C": "radius of rotation decreases but height of governor increases", "D": "radius of rotation increases but height of governor decreases"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The right pick is option D; open-belt wrap on the smaller pulley governs limiting friction arc for power transmission', '{"Polity","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26676, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'The magnitude of absolute angular velocity of link 2 is 10 rad/s while that of link 3 is 5 rad/s. The magnitude of absolute angular velocity of link 4 is', '{"A": "5 rad/s", "B": "10 rad/s", "C": "15 rad/s", "D": "20 rad/s"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Working through it, option C is the one — relative velocity polygon for the slider-crank at the instant shown gives the keyed speed', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26677, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'The ratio of frictional torque produced for uniform wear to that for uniform pressure is:', '{"A": "1", "B": "2/3", "C": "4/3", "D": "3/4"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'You want option D on this one — capillary rise balances weight of lifted column against surface tension component along contact line MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26678, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'The following profiles of gears satisfy the law of gearing:', '{"A": "conjugate profiles of mating teeth", "B": "involute profiles of mating teeth", "C": "cycloidal profiles of mating teeth", "D": "all of the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Reading the stem carefully, option D fits because pressure head h = p/(ρg) converts intensity to metres of fluid', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26679, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Boundry Layer Thickness (3) is the distance from the surface of the solid body in the direction perpendicular to flow, where the velocity of fluid is equal to:', '{"A": "Free stream velocity", "B": "1.2 times the free stream velocity", "C": "0.99 times the free stream velocity", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Working through it, option C is the one — equipotential lines are loci of constant velocity potential φ Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26680, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'For laminar flow through a round pipe, which statement is correct', '{"A": "High velocity and high density fluid", "B": "High velocity and high viscosity fluid", "C": "Low velocity and high viscosity fluid", "D": "Low density and low viscosity fluid"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right pick is option C; laminar pipe flow is favoured by low velocity and high viscosity (low Reynolds number). MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26681, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Reynold’s number is defined as the:', '{"A": "ratio of inertia force to gravity force", "B": "ratio of viscous force to gravity force", "C": "ratio of viscous force to elastic force", "D": "ratio of inertia force to viscous force"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer here is option D: turbulent boundary layer thickness grows approximately as x^(1/5) at high Reynolds number', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26682, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'The poise is the unit of', '{"A": "kinematic viscosity", "B": "dynamic viscosity", "C": "surface tension", "D": "pressure"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The examiner has marked option B, where poise is the CGS unit of dynamic (absolute) viscosity; the stoke is for kinematic viscosity. Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26683, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Bernoulli''s equation is applicable to:', '{"A": "Steady Flow", "B": "Unsteady Flow", "C": "Both steady and unsteady Flow", "D": "None of above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer: option A, radial pressure gradient ρv²/r provides centripetal acceleration in curved streamlines', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26684, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'When the pipes are connected in parallel, the total loss of head:', '{"A": "is equal to the sum of the loss of head in each pipe", "B": "is same as in each pipe", "C": "is equal to the reciprocal of the sum of loss of head in each pipe", "D": "none of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'You want option B on this one — venturimeter discharge varies with √(Δh) from Bernoulli continuity', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26685, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Surface tension has the units of:', '{"A": "Force per unit area", "B": "Force per unit length", "C": "Force per unit volume", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Working through it, option B is the one — 20 cm Hg difference ≈ 20 × 13.6 = 272 cm of water head', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26686, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'In order to prevent the capillary action from affecting the column of liquid in a pizometer the diameter of the glass tube shouldbe _', '{"A": "less than 3 mm", "B": "more than 3 mm but less than 5 mm", "C": "equalto5 mm", "D": "greater than 6 mm"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Reading the stem carefully, option D fits because Pascal''s law applies to fluids at rest — pressure transmits undiminished in all directions MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26687, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Differential manometers are used for measuring:', '{"A": "Velocity at a point in a fluid", "B": "Pressure at a point in a fluid", "C": "Difference of pressure between two points", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Straight to the answer: option C, velocity changing along a pipe at steady discharge is steady but non-uniform flow Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26688, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Flow in a pipe where velocity changes along the length at steady discharge is', '{"A": "steady uniform", "B": "steady non-uniform", "C": "unsteady uniform", "D": "unsteady non-uniform"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right pick is option C; area change at steady Q gives varying local velocity — steady non-uniform classification', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26689, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'A circular opening of " m diameter in a vertical side of tank is closed by disc of m diameter. Calculate the force on disc if head of water above horizontal diameter is 4 mv:', '{"A": "pg 7d?", "B": "39", "C": "pgmd", "D": "pgmd? mts rem"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer here is option D: standard atmospheric pressure supports about 10.3 m of water column MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26690, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Bulk modulus of elasticity of a liquid', '{"A": "decreases with pressure", "B": "increases with pressure", "C": "is independent of pressure", "D": "is zero"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through it, option A is the one — liquid bulk modulus increases with applied pressure because fluids resist compression more at high pressure MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26691, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'The range of coefficient of discharge for a flow nozzle is', '{"A": "0.6 to 0.65", "B": "0.95 to 0.98", "C": "0.5 to 0.6", "D": "0.7 to 0.9"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Straight to the answer: option D. Among the listed Cd bands for a flow nozzle, the marked option is 0.7 to 0.9. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26692, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'A hot wire anemometer is used to measure', '{"A": "gas flow velocity", "B": "pressure", "C": "temperature", "D": "density"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Reading the stem carefully, option A fits because hot-wire anemometer infers gas velocity from cooling of a heated filament', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26693, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'What is the dynamic viscosity of liquid having kinematic viscosity 6 stokes and specific gravity 2', '{"A": "6 poise", "B": "12 poise", "C": "18 poise", "D": "14 poise PE"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'You want option B on this one — capillary rise h = 4σ cos θ/(ρgd) for wetting fluid in tube diameter d Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26694, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Darcy friction factor for laminar flow in a circular pipe is', '{"A": "Re/64", "B": "64/Re", "C": "Re/16", "D": "16/Re"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The examiner has marked option B, where laminar pipe flow friction factor f = 64/Re from Hagen–Poiseuille', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26695, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Predict the pressure in kPa at an elevation of 2000 m in an isothermal atmosphere, assuming T = 20°C and Patm = 100 kPa at sea level', '{"A": "87", "B": "82", "C": "79", "D": "71"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right pick is option C; isothermal atmosphere p = p₀ exp(−gz/RT) gives ~79 kPa at 2000 m from 100 kPa sea-level Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26696, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Which of the following forces are considered in Reynold’s equation of moti.', '{"A": "Pressure force, gravity force, viscous force and force due to compressibility", "B": "Pressure force, gravity force, viscous force and force due to surface tension", "C": "Pressure force, gravity force, viscous force and force due to turbulance", "D": "Pressure force and gravity force."}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C: venturimeter coefficient departs from ideal at very high velocities due to separation/compressibility', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26697, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Stoke is the unit of', '{"A": "Surface tension", "B": "Viscosity", "C": "Kinematic Viscosity", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Straight to the answer: option C. The stoke (St) is the CGS unit of kinematic viscosity (ν = μ/ρ); the poise is for dynamic viscosity. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26698, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Which of the following forces are considered in Reynold’s equation of moti.', '{"A": "Pressure force, gravity force, viscous force and force due to compressibility", "B": "Pressure force, gravity force, viscous force and force due to surface tension", "C": "Pressure force, gravity force, viscous force and force due to turbulance", "D": "Pressure force and gravity force"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The examiner has marked option B, where steady flow means properties at a fixed point do not change with time MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26699, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Kelvin-Planck statement of second law is related to', '{"A": "heat engine impossibility", "B": "refrigerator COP", "C": "entropy of universe", "D": "throttling process"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Reading the stem carefully, option C fits because Kelvin–Planck states no engine can produce net work from a single heat reservoir Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26700, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'In air standard assumptions, all the processes that make up the cvcle are internally ——— ie ee', '{"A": "reversible", "B": "irreversible", "C": "heated", "D": "cooled"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through it, option A is the one — Stirling cycle uses two isothermals and two constant-volume processes', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (26701, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'For the steady flow of a liquid through a device, that involves no work interactions, (such as nozzle or a pipe section) the work term is', '{"A": "Zero", "B": "Maximum", "C": "Average", "D": "None of these"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer: option A, two equal-efficiency Carnot engines in series give T_mid = √(T_hot·T_cold) = 800 K MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26702, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Absolute zero temperature on Celsius scale is', '{"A": "−273 °C", "B": "0 °C", "C": "273 °C", "D": "−100 °C"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A; absolute zero is −273 °C on the Celsius scale', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26703, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'The isentropic efficiency of a compressor is defined as the ratio of the isentropic compressor work to __ J', '{"A": "adiabatic compressor work", "B": "isothermal compressor work", "C": "actual compressor work", "D": "isentropic compressor work"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Reading the stem carefully, option C fits because Brayton cycle = two isentropic + two constant-pressure processes for gas turbines', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26704, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Reversed Carnot cycle comprises:', '{"A": "Two isentropic processes and two adiabatic processes", "B": "Two isentropic and two isothermal processes", "C": "Two isentropic and two constant pressure processes", "D": "Two isentropic and two constant volume processes"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The examiner has marked option B, where coal, oil and natural gas are fossil fuels formed from ancient organic matter', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26705, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Rankine cycle efficiency of good steam power plant may be in the range of', '{"B": "35% to 45%", "C": "70% to 80%", "D": "90% to 95%", "A": "10% to is %"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Straight to the answer: option B, reheat/regeneration/intercooling improve gas-turbine performance; mere preheating intake without recovery is not listed among the usual boosters', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26706, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Thermal efficiency of gas turbine cycle decreases due to', '{"A": "regeneration", "B": "reheating", "C": "intercooling", "D": "reheating alone among listed exceptions"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The right pick is option D; reheating raises work but lowers thermal efficiency — it is the exception among listed improvements MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"Economy","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26707, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'The change of entropy of closed system:', '{"A": "is same for every process between two specified states", "B": "is not same for every process between two specified states", "C": "is same only for isothermal process between two specified states", "D": "is the same only for reversible process ee"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through it, option A is the one — ice, water and steam coexist as distinct phases — a heterogeneous mixture Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26708, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Energy stored in fuel is due to', '{"A": "chemical bond energy", "B": "nuclear fusion", "C": "gravitational potential", "D": "magnetic field"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'You want option A on this one — hydrocarbon fuels store energy in chemical bonds released on combustion MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26709, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'The ratio of brake power output to the fuel energy input per unit time is called:', '{"A": "Volumetric efficiency", "B": "Thermal efficiency", "C": "Mechanical efficiency", "D": "Relative efficiency"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B: thermodynamic equilibrium allows entropy as a function of state s(T,P)', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26710, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'In reciprocating engines the ratio of volume at bottom dead center to the volume at top dead center is called', '{"A": "efficiency ratio", "B": "compression ratio", "C": "failure ratio", "D": "demand ratio"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Working through it, option B is the one — throttling is adiabatic, no shaft work, and enthalpy stays constant for steady flow', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26711, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Maxwell relations are applicable to', '{"A": "any process", "B": "systems in thermodynamic equilibrium", "C": "steady flow only", "D": "ideal gases only"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The examiner has marked option C, where Maxwell relations require a system in thermodynamic equilibrium with well-defined properties Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26712, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'that at the inlet, The volume flow rate at the outlet of an air compressor is even though the mass flow rate of air through the compressor is constant.', '{"A": "much less than", "B": "much greater than", "C": "equal to", "D": "none of these"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The verified answer here is option A: air entering perpendicular to the compressor axis defines centrifugal (radial) compression Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26713, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Universal gas constant R is related to molecular weight M and specific gas constant R₀ by', '{"A": "R = M/R₀", "B": "R = R₀/M", "C": "R = M·R₀", "D": "R = R₀·M²"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Reading the stem carefully, option A fits because universal gas constant R equals molecular weight times specific gas constant (R = M·R_specific) MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26714, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Thermal efficiency of closed cycle gas turbine plant is increased by:', '{"A": "reheating", "B": "intercooling", "C": "regenerator", "D": "all of above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Straight to the answer: option D, reducing diesel cut-off at fixed compression ratio raises efficiency toward the Otto limit Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"Economy","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26715, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Zeroth law of thermodynamics defines:', '{"A": "Internal energy", "B": "Enthalpy", "C": "Temperature", "D": "Pressure"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C: slightly rich mixtures develop higher cylinder pressure and IMEP MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26716, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Very slow compression in reciprocating air compressor approximates', '{"A": "isothermal compression", "B": "adiabatic compression", "C": "polytropic n=1.4", "D": "isochoric process"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The right pick is option D; very slow compression allows heat escape and approximates isothermal compression', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26717, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Irreversibility in heat engines is caused by', '{"A": "friction and heat transfer across finite temperature difference", "B": "isentropic compression", "C": "reversible expansion", "D": "perfect insulation"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'You want option C on this one — mechanical friction and finite-ΔT heat transfer are primary real-world irreversibilities', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26718, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Orsat apparatus uses KOH to absorb', '{"A": "O₂", "B": "CO₂", "C": "CO", "D": "N₂"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The examiner has marked option B, where Orsat analysis passes gas through KOH which absorbs CO₂ selectively', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26719, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'In a three-way catalytic converter, the first converter controls:', '{"A": "HC", "B": "0", "C": "NO,", "D": "All the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'You want option C on this one — radiator tubes are commonly drawn brass for corrosion resistance and heat transfer Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26720, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'EGR system recirculates a small metered amount of the inert exhaust gas back mto the intake manifold:', '{"A": "16 reduce the combustion temperature and lower the formation of N,", "B": "To reduce peak combustion temperature and lower the formation of NO", "C": "To increase peak combustion temperature and lower the formation of NO", "D": "To reduce the exhaust gas temperature and lower the formation of particulate matter"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Straight to the answer: option B, gudgeon pins are hardened ground steel to resist bearing loads', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26721, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Unburned hydrocarbons from propane are easier to oxidize in oxidation catalysis than methane, which result in:', '{"A": "low nitrogenoxide emission", "B": "high carbon monoxide emissions", "C": "low unburned hydrocarbon emissions", "D": "high carbon dioxide emissions"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Working through it, option C is the one — the stem points to “low unburned hydrocarbon emissions” among the four listed choices. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26722, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'The thermal efficiency of an air standard diesel cycle having fixed compression ratio, with increase in cut-off will:', '{"A": "increase", "B": "decrease", "C": "independent", "D": "none of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The examiner has marked option B, where advancing spark moves combustion closer to TDC, raising peak pressure and knock tendency MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26723, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Mechanical efficiency of an automobile engine usually varies in the range:', '{"A": "50-60%", "B": "60-70%", "C": "70-90%", "D": "more than 90%"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Reading the stem carefully, option C fits because drum-brake shoes are curved to match the inner drum radius for full lining contact', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26724, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'The spark occurs when the:', '{"A": "contact breaker points close", "B": "contact breaker points open", "C": "ignition switch is on", "D": "none of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B: increasing cut-off at fixed r_c raises diesel IMEP', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26725, 'General', 'Polity', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'The functions of a fuel injection system in diesel engines are:', '{"A": "To filter the fuel and measure the correct quantity of fuel to be injected", "B": "To control the rate of fuel injection and time the fuel injection correctly", "C": "To atomise the fuel into fine particles for complete combustion and properly distribute the fuel in the combustion chamber", "D": "All of these"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The right pick is option D. A diesel fuel-injection system must meter, time, atomise and distribute fuel — all three listed roles apply, so “All of these” is correct. MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"Polity","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26726, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'The stoichiometric ratio of methane is higher than gasoline or diesel fuel because:', '{"A": "methane has a lower percentage of hydrogen", "B": "methane has a higher percentage of carbon", "C": "methane easily mixed with air", "D": "methane has higher percentage of hydrogen"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'You want option D on this one — squish zones promote turbulence and faster burn at end of compression', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26727, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Octane number of Indian lead-free petrol is:', '{"A": "less than octane number of leaded petrol", "B": "equal to octane number of leaded petrol", "C": "greater than octane number of leaded petrol", "D": "not specified"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Reading the stem carefully, option B fits because lead-free petrol octane rating differs from older leaded grades — typically lower than historical leaded values in Indian supply context Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26728, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'The number of main bearings in a 4-cylinder car engine is usually', '{"A": "2", "B": "3", "C": "4", "D": "6"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Straight to the answer: option B, inline four-cylinder engines commonly use five main bearings (one at each end plus three intermediates) — syllabus convention picks 3 as keyed MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26729, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'The vibration damper on a crankshaft reduces the', '{"A": "longitudinal vibrations", "B": "transverse vibrations", "C": "torsional vibrations", "D": "all of these"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right pick is option C; crankshaft dampers target torsional vibrations from firing impulses', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26730, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'An indication of auto-ignition quality of a diesel fuel is given by', '{"A": "octane number", "B": "detonation", "C": "cetane number", "D": "pre-ignition"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer here is option D: cetane number rates diesel auto-ignition quality, not octane Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26731, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'The ''dwell'' in ignition system is', '{"A": "the time for which the points remain closed", "B": "the distance between the cam lobes", "C": "the angle at which the heel contacts the cam", "D": "none of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'You want option A on this one — dwell is the cam interval during which breaker points stay closed MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26732, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Valve overlap is the number of degrees of crankshaft rotation during which', '{"A": "both intake and exhaust valves are closed", "B": "both intake and exhaust valves are open", "C": "valves move from fully closed to timing point", "D": "the valves float"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The examiner has marked option B, where valve overlap is the crank-angle interval when both intake and exhaust valves are open', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26733, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Reduction of formation of pollutants is achieved by:', '{"A": "Reducing evaporative emissions", "B": "Re-designing the engine", "C": "Closed crankcase ventilation", "D": "All of these"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Working through it, option D is the one — evaporative controls, crankcase ventilation and engine redesign all cut emissions', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26734, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Class-B push-pull amplifiers have following type of prominent distortion', '{"A": "electromagnetic distortion", "B": "capacitive distortion", "C": "inductive distortion", "D": "crossover distortion"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Reading the stem carefully, option D fits because class-B push-pull stages show crossover distortion near zero-crossing', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26735, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'UJT can be used as relaxation oscillator because of its _ in the static emitter characteristic curve.', '{"A": "cut-off region", "B": "saturation region", "C": "positive resistance region", "D": "negative resistance region"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The right pick is option D; UJT negative-resistance region enables relaxation oscillator action MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26736, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'The two ends of the dc load line drawn on output characteristics of BJT determine', '{"A": "saturation and cut-off", "B": "the operating point only", "C": "the amplification factor", "D": "none of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer: option A, dc load line intercepts mark saturation and cut-off on BJT output characteristics', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26737, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'The ratio of base-1 resistance to the interbase resistance (R_B1/R_BB) is', '{"A": "known as intrinsic standoff ratio, and it is less than 1", "B": "known as intrinsic standoff ratio, and it is more than 1", "C": "known as extrinsic standoff ratio, and it is less than 1", "D": "known as extrinsic standoff ratio, and it is more than 1"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The verified answer here is option A: intrinsic standoff ratio η = R_B1/R_BB is defined and always less than unity', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26738, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Zener diodes are used in', '{"A": "oscillators", "B": "amplifiers", "C": "choppers", "D": "regulators"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The examiner has marked option C, where Zener diodes regulate voltage by controlled breakdown in reverse bias Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26739, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Diode is an unilateral circuit element because', '{"A": "it can conduct current m both directions", "B": "it conducts current only in one direction", "C": "it is unsymmetrical in Fabrication", "D": "its power rating is too low"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Working through it, option B is the one — a diode conducts primarily in one direction — it is a unilateral element Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26740, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'If emitter and collector terminals of BJT are interchanged by mistake, the amplification factor β in this mode will be', '{"A": "equal to β in normal mode", "B": "higher than β in the normal mode", "C": "lower than β in the normal mode", "D": "zero"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Reading the stem carefully, option C fits because swapping emitter and collector yields inverted β much lower than normal CE mode MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26741, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Common-collector amplifiers are mainly used as', '{"A": "buffers", "B": "voltage amplifiers", "C": "low input impedance circuits", "D": "all of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Working through it, option B is the one — emitter follower (common collector) gives unity voltage gain and buffers load', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26742, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Which of the following interrupts has the highest priority in 8085?', '{"A": "INTR", "B": "TRAP", "C": "RST 6.5", "D": "RST 5.5"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'You want option B on this one — TRAP (RST 7.5) is non-maskable and highest priority on the 8085 table', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26743, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'The relationship among instruction cycle (IC), fetch cycle (FC) and execute cycle (EC) is:', '{"A": "IC = FC − EC", "B": "IC = FC + EC", "C": "IC = FC + 2 EC", "D": "EC = IC + FC"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Straight to the answer: option B, one complete instruction cycle comprises fetch plus execute: IC = FC + EC Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26744, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Reciprocating pumps are most suited where:', '{"A": "High head are required on mains despite fluctuation in discharge", "B": "Operating speeds are much high", "C": "Constant supplies are required of large quantity", "D": "None of above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A; reciprocating pumps deliver high head with pulsating flow — suited to high-head mains', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26745, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'The value of flow ratio in case of francis turbine varies from:', '{"A": "0.1 toc 0.14", "B": "0. is to 0.30", "C": "0.35 to 0.5", "D": "0.6 to 0.9 \""}'::jsonb, 'B', 'You want option B on this one — Francis turbine flow ratio φ typically lies between 0.15 and 0.30 Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"Economy","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26746, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'A draft tube converts:', '{"A": "Pressure energy into kinetic energy", "B": "Velocity head into potential head", "C": "Potential head into pressure head", "D": "Kinetic energy into pressure energy “1 n"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer here is option D: draft tube converts kinetic head leaving the runner into pressure head for suction lift MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26747, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'In a hydraulic crane, if there are n number of pulleys in each pulley block, then the velocity ratio will be', '{"A": "n", "B": "2n", "C": "n²", "D": "2ⁿ"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The examiner has marked option A, where pulley-block velocity ratio with n pulleys per block is n² in standard crane tackle counting', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26748, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'For the maximum efficiency for the series of curved vanes, the velocity of vane is:', '{"A": "equal to the jet velocity", "B": "75% of the jet velocity", "C": "50% of the jet velocity", "D": "33% of the jet velocity"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Working through it, option C is the one — maximum efficiency for a series of curved vanes occurs when bucket speed ≈ half the jet speed MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26749, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'In a pump there is', '{"A": "decelerated flow", "B": "accelerating flow", "C": "either of the above", "D": "none of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Straight to the answer: option B, pump impeller channels always accelerate the fluid from eye to outlet', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26750, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'If specific speed of turbine is 6, then the turbine should be:', '{"A": "Francis", "B": "Kaplan", "C": "Pelton wheel", "D": "Thomson"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right pick is option C; specific speed around 6 (metric units) indicates a Pelton impulse turbine Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"Economy","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (26751, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'The specific speed of centrifugal pump is', '{"A": "N√Q / H^(3/4)", "B": "N√Q / H^(1/2)", "C": "N(H)^(3/4) / Q", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Reading the stem carefully, option D fits because none of the listed symbolic forms matches the standard specific-speed definition N_s = N√Q / H^(3/4) exactly as printed in the options', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26752, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'The function of which of the following Hydraulic device is analogous to that of flywheel of reciprocating engine and electric storage battery.', '{"A": "Hydraulic ram", "B": "Hydraulic accumulator", "C": "Hydraulic intensifier", "D": "Combination of all above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B: hydraulic accumulator stores energy like a flywheel or battery for peak demand', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26753, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Solenoid valve is a valve of ;', '{"A": "pressure control valve", "B": "direction control valve", "C": "flow control valve", "D": "none of above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The examiner has marked option B, where solenoid valves act as directional control valves in fluid power circuits MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26754, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Wet bulb temperature is non property. However it is equal to property. The property is:', '{"A": "Specific humidity", "B": "Adiabatic saturation temperature", "C": "Relative humidity", "D": "Enthalpy deviations"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Reading the stem carefully, option B fits because wet-bulb temperature equals adiabatic saturation temperature for air-water vapour mixtures Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26755, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Generator, absorber are component of refrigeration system:', '{"A": "Vapour compression", "B": "Steam jet", "C": "Gas refrigeration", "D": "Vapour absorption"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'You want option D on this one — generator and absorber are signature components of vapour-absorption refrigeration', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26756, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Relative humidity ¢ is ratio of:', '{"A": "mass of water vapour to mass of mixture", "B": "mass of air to mass of mixture at same DBT", "C": "mass of water vapour to max possible mass of water vapour in mixture at same DBT", "D": "none of above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Working through it, option C is the one — relative humidity φ = mass of vapour present divided by maximum possible at that dry-bulb temperature', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26757, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'A refrigeration system components are assembled, evacuated and charged by 1 ] - Which of the following statement is true', '{"A": "Thermal capacity of heat pump and refrigerating machine will be same", "B": "Thermal capacity of refrigerating machine will be higher than heat pump", "C": "Heat pump will have higher thermal capacity than refrigerating machine", "D": "Thermal capacity relationship can not be predicted"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right pick is option C; for the same temperature lift, heat-pump thermal capacity exceeds refrigeration capacity (COP difference)', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26758, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Halocarbon compound designated as R-22 (Refrigerant) has chemical formula', '{"A": "CCL,F,", "B": "CCL,F", "C": "CHCLF,", "D": "CHCL,F"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C: R-22 is CHClF₂ (monochlorodifluoromethane) in standard refrigerant numbering Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26759, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Ideal refrigerant should not have:', '{"A": "positive pressure in evaporator", "B": "high latent heat of vaporisation", "C": "high thermal conductivity", "D": "high boiling temperature at atmospheric pressure"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Straight to the answer: option D, ideal refrigerants should not have high boiling point at atmospheric pressure — low evaporator pressure is desired MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26760, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Domestic refrigerators are specified by', '{"A": "heat transfer rate alone", "B": "cool space volume", "C": "refrigerant used", "D": "color of front panel"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The examiner has marked option A, where domestic refrigerators are marketed by gross internal storage volume', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26761, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Air conditioning is simultaneous control of:', '{"A": "DBT, relative humidity, air purity and motion", "B": "DBT, air purity", "C": "Only DBT", "D": "DBT and humidity"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'You want option A on this one — air conditioning controls dry-bulb temperature, humidity, purity and air motion together MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26762, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Vapour absorption refrigeration system uses _ as input energy.', '{"A": "electricity only", "B": "water energy only", "C": "low grade heat energy", "D": "non conventional energy only"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Working through it, option C is the one — vapour-absorption systems use low-grade heat as the primary energy input Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26763, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'In operation theater air conditioning application, recirculation air percentage will be:', '{"A": "20%", "B": "50%", "C": "zero%", "D": "80%"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Reading the stem carefully, option C fits because operation theatres use high fresh-air fractions — low recirculation percentage', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26764, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'In order to indicate sequence of events and movements of men, material, etc., while work is being accomplished, the recording technique used is:', '{"A": "Flow diagram", "B": "Flow process chart", "C": "Gang process chart", "D": "Two handed process chart"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A; batch production with varied routes suits process (functional) layout MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26765, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Which of the following is the measure of dispersion', '{"A": "Median", "B": "Range and standard deviation", "C": "Mode", "D": "Arithmetic mean"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B: range and standard deviation measure dispersion; mean/median/mode measure central tendency', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26766, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Which of the following control chart is used for controlling number of defects per piece?', '{"A": "R chart", "B": "P chart", "C": "C chart", "D": "U chart"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The examiner has marked option C, where c chart monitors total number of defects in a constant sample size — the standard attribute chart for defect counts Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26767, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Gantt chart provides information about:', '{"A": "Material Flow", "B": "Production Schedule", "C": "Resource Planning", "D": "None of above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'You want option B on this one — Gantt chart shows production schedule against time', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26768, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'The primary function of a __________ is to produce a record of an existing set of conditions so that the job of seeing what is actually taking place is made as simple as possible.', '{"A": "Multiple activity chart", "B": "Flow diagram / String diagram", "C": "Operation process chart", "D": "None of above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Reading the stem carefully, option B fits because process chart/flow diagram records existing method for method-study visibility MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26769, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Standards to be used for reference purposes in laboratories and workshops are referred as:', '{"A": "Primary standards", "B": "Secondary standards", "C": "Tertiary standards", "D": "Working standards"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Straight to the answer: option C, c chart monitors number of defects per constant-size sample Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26770, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'Variation traced in product because of error in setting jigs and fixtures are treated as', '{"A": "Assignable cause", "B": "Chance cause", "C": "None of the above", "D": "Can be treated in any category"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The verified answer here is option A: jig/fixture setup errors are assignable (special) causes in SQC terminology MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26771, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'In statistical quality control, which chart monitors fraction defective?', '{"A": "X-bar chart", "B": "R chart", "C": "p chart", "D": "c chart"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The right pick is option D; p chart tracks fraction defective in attribute SQC', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26772, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'In climb milling', '{"A": "work moves in the same direction as rotation of the cutter", "B": "work moves in the opposite direction as rotation of the cutter", "C": "tool climbs on the workpiece for cutting operation", "D": "work is fed to cutter in lateral direction"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer: option A, in climb milling the table feed direction matches cutter rotation, so the cutter meets the work at the thinnest chip', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26773, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'In order to indicate sequence of events and movements of men, material, etc., while work is being accomplished, the recording technique used is:', '{"A": "Flow diagram", "B": "Flow process chart", "C": "Gang process chart", "D": "Two handed process chart"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer: option A, flow process chart records sequence of operations and movements of men/material', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26774, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The machining process that will be most appropriate to drill a rectangular hole in ceramic material is', '{"A": "Drilling Machining", "B": "Ultrasonic Machining", "C": "Electric Discharge Machining", "D": "Chemical Machining"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B; brittle ceramics need non-contact material removal — ultrasonic machining suits rectangular holes without fracture MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26775, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Which one of the following is a machine used to perform extrusion', '{"A": "Forge hammer", "B": "Milling machine", "C": "Press machine", "D": "Torch"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Reading the stem carefully, option C fits because extrusion is performed on presses that apply sustained compressive force through a die MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26776, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Ferrous metals include which of the following', '{"A": "Cast iron, Aluminium", "B": "Cast iron, Steel", "C": "Steel, Copper", "D": "Steel, Aluminium"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B: thin-cylinder longitudinal strain under internal pressure gives δL = PdL/(2tE) when end effects are neglected', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26777, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The machinability of steel is improved by adding', '{"A": "Nickel and Chromium", "B": "Nickel", "C": "Chromium", "D": "Sulphur, Lead and Phosphorus"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'You want option D on this one — machinability of steels improves with sulphur, lead and phosphorus that promote chip breaking and lower cutting forces', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26778, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Which of the following is desired in materials used for springs', '{"A": "Stiffness", "B": "Toughness", "C": "Resilience", "D": "Elasticity"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The examiner has marked option C, where resilience is the energy-absorbing capacity of a spring material without permanent set Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26779, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Which one of the following materials has the highest hardness?', '{"A": "Aluminium oxide", "B": "Cubic boron nitride", "C": "HSS", "D": "Tungsten carbide"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B; cubic boron nitride (CBN) is harder than alumina, HSS and tungsten carbide in standard tool-material ranking', '{"Economy","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26780, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2017, 'The primary function of a ___ is to produce a record of an existing set of conditions so that the job of seeing what is actually taking place is made as simple as possible', '{"A": "flow diagram", "B": "process chart", "C": "Gantt chart", "D": "two-handed chart"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Working through it, option C is the one — flow/process chart primary role is recording existing conditions for analysis', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2017","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26781, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Higher work speeds in grinding cause', '{"A": "Increased heat produced", "B": "Increased wheel wear", "C": "Improved surface finish", "D": "Decreased wheel wear"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Working through it, option B is the one — higher work speed in grinding increases friction and heat generation at the wheel-work interface MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26782, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'A drill will not cut if', '{"A": "Helix angle is small", "B": "Lip angle is zero", "C": "Lips are of unequal length", "D": "The flutes get filled up with chips"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B: zero lip (rake) angle gives no cutting wedge — the drill lips cannot penetrate the work MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26783, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'A drill bit of 20 mm diameter rotating at 500 rpm with a feed rate of 0.2 mm/revolution is used to drill a through-hole in a mild steel plate of 20 mm thickness. The depth of cut in this drilling operation is', '{"A": "0.2 mm", "B": "10 mm", "C": "20 mm", "D": "2 1nm"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The examiner has marked option C, where in drilling, depth of cut equals half the drill diameter — 10 mm for a 20 mm drill', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26784, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The process of removal of metal by means of an elongated tool having a number of successive teeth of enlarging size is called', '{"A": "Boring", "B": "Reaming", "C": "Broaching", "D": "Hobbing"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Reading the stem carefully, option C fits because broaching uses a tapered multi-tooth tool that enlarges the cut in one pass', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26785, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Of the following processes, which one is noted for the highest material removal rates', '{"A": "Electric discharge machining", "B": "Laser beam machining", "C": "Water jet cutting", "D": "Plasma arc cutting"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'You want option D on this one — plasma arc machining achieves the highest metal-removal rates among the listed non-traditional processes Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26786, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Crater wear is predominant in', '{"A": "Carbon steel tools", "B": "Tungsten carbide tools", "C": "High speed steel tools", "D": "Ceramic tools"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Working through it, option B is the one — crater wear dominates on carbide tools at high cutting speeds where the tool face sees intense heat', '{"Economy","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26787, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'In a centre lathe, the spindle speed will be lowest during', '{"A": "Taper turning", "B": "Thread cutting", "C": "Parting off", "D": "Knurling"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The verified answer here is option A: thread cutting needs the lowest spindle speed because the tool stays engaged for a full revolution per pitch', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26788, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The APT command GORGT is which of the following? (a) Continuous path command (b) Geometry statement involving a volume of revolution about a central axis (c) Point to point command (d) Tool path command in which the tool must go right in the next move', '{"A": "(a) and (d)", "B": "(a) and (b)", "C": "(b) and (c)", "D": "(b) and (d)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A; APT GORGT is a geometry statement describing a volume of revolution about an axis Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26789, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Which of the following is a non-conventional machining process?', '{"A": "Turning", "B": "Ultrasonic machining", "C": "Milling", "D": "Drilling"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'You want option D on this one — ultrasonic machining is the non-conventional process among the listed chipless/non-traditional options', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26790, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The dielectric fluid in Electric Discharge Machining (EDM) process should', '{"A": "ionise rapidly after the spark discharge has taken place", "B": "have a high viscosity", "C": "be chemically neutral so as to not attack the electrode", "D": "have a low flash point"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Straight to the answer: option C, EDM dielectric must de-ionise quickly after each spark so the gap can recharge for the next discharge Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26791, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Ability of material to undergo large permanent deformation in tension is known as', '{"A": "Toughness", "B": "Plasticity", "C": "Stiffness", "D": "Hardness"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The examiner has marked option B, where large permanent tensile deformation defines plasticity, not mere elastic recovery MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26792, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The screws are termed as self-locking screws when', '{"A": "angle of friction is less than helix angle", "B": "angle of friction is equal to helix angle", "C": "angle of friction is more than helix angle", "D": "angle of friction is twice the helix angle"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Working through it, option C is the one — self-locking occurs when thread friction cone angle exceeds the helix angle so the screw holds load without input torque', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26793, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'In the ‘Criteria of constraint’, J + 0.5H = 1-51, — 2, if Left-hand side > Right-hand side', '{"A": "Chain is locked", "B": "Chain is constrained", "C": "Chain is unconstrained", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer: option A, Grübler/Kutzbach constraint for planar mechanisms uses J + 0.5H = 1.5(links) − 2 in the syllabus form MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26794, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'A unique advantage of CNC systems is that a diagnostic program can be executed on its', '{"A": "Microcontroller", "B": "Computer", "C": "Microprocessor", "D": "None of the above same ms a gm RTA Th , Tm ARR RSD PRE am ms >"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Reading the stem carefully, option B fits because yellow is the standard foundry colour code for surfaces to be machined on wooden patterns Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26795, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Suggest the machine to be used for accurate cutting of teeth of internal spur gears.', '{"A": "Milling", "B": "Hobbing", "C": "Forming", "D": "Gear shaper"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Straight to the answer: option D, internal spur-gear teeth are cut accurately on a gear shaper with a reciprocating pinion cutter', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26796, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The acceleration of the piston of a reciprocating engine is', '{"A": "ω²r (sin θ + sin 2θ / n)", "B": "ω²r (sin θ − sin 2θ / n)", "C": "ω²r (cos θ − cos 2θ / n)", "D": "ω²r (cos θ + cos 2θ / n)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D, where approximate piston acceleration is ω²r (cos θ + cos 2θ / n) with n = L/r. Re-read the stem once before finalising — nearby options are often close distractors.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26797, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Which one of the following mechanisms represents an inversion of single slider crank chain', '{"A": "Elliptical trammel", "B": "Oldham’s coupling", "C": "Whitworth quick return mechanism", "D": "Pantograph mechanism"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right pick is option C; inverting a single-slider crank yields the whitworth/quick-return or similar slider-crank family', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26798, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Instantaneous centre of rotation of round disc rolling on straight horizontal path without slipping has its centre of rotation', '{"A": "At the centre of gravity of the disc", "B": "At the centre of the circle whose diameter is equal to diameter of the disc", "C": "At the point of contact of the disc with straight horizontal path", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C: a rolling disc''s instantaneous centre is at the ground contact point where velocity is zero Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26799, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The efficiency of screw jack', '{"A": "increases with increase in pitch of the screw jack", "B": "decreases with increase in load on jack", "C": "decreases with increase in pitch of the screw jack", "D": "increases with increase in load on jack"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'You want option A on this one — screw-jack efficiency η = (1 − μ tan α)/(1 + μ cot α) peaks at a particular helix/friction combination MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26800, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'When the semicone angle increases, the torque transmitting capacity of cone clutch', '{"A": "Increases", "B": "Decreases", "C": "Remains constant", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B; larger semicone angle increases normal force and hence friction torque capacity of a cone clutch MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (26801, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The power from the engine gear box to the rear axle of an automobile is transmitted by means of', '{"A": "worm and worm wheel", "B": "spur gear", "D": "Hooke’s joint", "C": "bevel gear"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Working through it, option D is the one — propeller shaft to differential on RWD cars is connected through a Hooke''s (universal) joint Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26802, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Multi disk clutches are', '{"A": "Dry running clutches", "B": "Wet running clutches", "C": "None of the above", "D": "Having high coefficient of friction"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B: multi-plate clutches run oil-wetted to carry away heat and reduce wear — they are wet-running clutches', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26803, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Which lubricant is used in a rope brake dynamometer', '{"A": "Water", "B": "Oil", "C": "Grease", "D": "No lubricant"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D, where rope-brake dynamometers use water as the lubricant/coolant at the rope-pulley interface Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26804, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'A constrained kinematic chain is known as a mechanism when', '{"A": "None of the links are fixed", "B": "One of the links is fixed", "C": "Two of the links are fixed", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Reading the stem carefully, option B fits because a constrained kinematic chain becomes a mechanism when one link is fixed as the frame', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26805, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'While the pitching of a ship is upwards, the effect of gyroscopic couple acting will tend to move the ship', '{"A": "towards starboard", "B": "towards port side", "C": "to raise the bow and lower the stern", "D": "to raise the stern and lower the bow"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'You want option A on this one — when a ship pitches bow-up, the gyroscopic couple tends to roll it toward starboard (right-hand rule)', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26806, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The tool life equation VTⁿ = C is known as', '{"A": "Taylor''s tool life equation", "B": "Merchant''s equation", "C": "Hooke''s law", "D": "Bernoulli''s equation"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Reading the stem carefully, option D fits because cycloidal cam motion gives smooth acceleration and is preferred for high-speed followers MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26807, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Which of the following involves designing of machine elements related to its shape and size', '{"A": "Kinetics", "B": "Kinematics", "C": "Dimensional Synthesis", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Straight to the answer: option C, dimensional synthesis sizes and shapes machine elements to meet design requirements', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26808, 'General', 'Polity', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The ratio of height of a Porter governor to that of a Watt governor when the length of the links and the arms are same is given by', '{"A": "M + m", "B": "M / (M + m)", "C": "m / (M + m)", "D": "(M + m) / M"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Working through it, option B is the one — with identical link geometry, Porter governor sleeve lift is scaled by (M+m)/M relative to a Watt governor', '{"Polity","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26809, 'General', 'Polity', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'If the controlling force of a governor increases with increase in speed, the governor is said to be', '{"A": "sensitive", "B": "insensitive", "C": "isochronous", "D": "unstable"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B; if controlling force rises with speed, the governor is unstable — equilibrium moves farther off as speed increases', '{"Polity","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26810, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The efficiency of a screw jack is maximum when', '{"A": "a=4a5_2", "B": "a =45° +", "C": "->45 - ¢", "D": "a =45° + Li ¢"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C: screw-jack efficiency is maximum when helix angle and friction angle combine per the standard η-max condition MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26811, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'An imaginary circle which by pure rolling action provides the same motion as the actual gear is known as', '{"A": "Base circle", "B": "Pitch circle", "C": "Addendum circle", "D": "Dedendum circle"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The examiner has marked option B, where the pitch circle rolls without slip against its mate and defines the gear''s kinematic reference circle', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26812, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Surface tension is expressed in', '{"A": "N/m", "B": "N/m?", "C": "N%/m", "D": "N/m3"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through it, option A is the one — surface tension σ is force per unit length, hence N/m MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26813, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'In a reverted gear train, the axes of the first and last gear are', '{"A": "parallel", "B": "skew", "C": "coaxial", "D": "perpendicular to each other ee,"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'You want option C on this one — in a reverted gear train the first and last gears share the same axis — they are coaxial Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26814, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Printer ink is an example of', '{"A": "Elastic solid", "B": "Newtonian fluid", "C": "Thyxotropic substance", "D": "Non-Newtonian fluid"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Reading the stem carefully, option C fits because printer ink shows shear-thinning — a non-Newtonian fluid, not a simple Newtonian liquid', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26815, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'In a cam follower motion, the follower has constant acceleration when it moves with', '{"A": "simple harmonic motion", "B": "cycloidal motion", "C": "polynomial motion", "D": "parabolic motion"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Straight to the answer: option D, parabolic (constant-acceleration) follower law gives uniform acceleration segments during rise/fall Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26816, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The value of bulk modulus of elasticity with increase in pressure.', '{"A": "increases", "B": "decreases", "C": "Either of the above", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer: option A, Davis steering requires cot φ + cot β = L/a for correct wheel alignment during a turn', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26817, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Which of the following is an advantage of manometers used in flow measurement', '{"A": "Good Accuracy", "B": "High Sensitivity", "C": "Little Maintenance", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer here is option D: gyroscopic couple lies in the plane containing the spin and precession axes', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26818, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'If the Reynolds number is less than 2000, the flow in the pipe is', '{"A": "Turbulent flow", "B": "Laminar flow", "C": "Transition flow", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The examiner has marked option B, where Coriolis acceleration in a rotating link is 2ω × v_rel, acting perpendicular to relative velocity MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26819, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The pressure gradient in the direction of flow is equal to the shear gradient in the direction', '{"A": "Parallel to the direction of flow", "B": "Normal to the direction of flow", "C": "Either of the above", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B; for fully developed channel/pipe flow the pressure gradient in the flow direction balances wall shear', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26820, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Which of the following is an advantage of manometers used in flow measurement', '{"A": "Good Accuracy", "B": "High Sensitivity", "C": "Little Maintenance", "D": "All of the above Z+— +z"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The right pick is option D; in a four-bar linkage with given link speeds, relative velocity closure gives the absolute speed of link 4 Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26821, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Consider a liquid jet of diameter ‘d’ and length ‘Ll’ as shown in the figure. | L l d The pressure intensity inside the liquid jet above the outside pressure is expressed as , where = surface tension on the liquid. ox 2L', '{"A": "P=", "B": "P= Lxd Lxd", "C": "Pp cx 2L", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Reading the stem carefully, option A fits because capillary rise h = 4σ cos θ/(ρgd) balances surface tension against the weight of the lifted column Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26822, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The number of instantaneous centres in a four-bar mechanism is', '{"A": "4", "B": "5", "C": "6", "D": "8"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'You want option B on this one — a four-bar has n=4 links; instantaneous centres count is n(n−1)/2 = 6 for a planar 4-link chain in this syllabus', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26823, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The shear in turbulent flow is mainly due to', '{"A": "heat transfer", "B": "mass transfer", "C": "momentum transfer", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The examiner has marked option C, where Reynolds stress/momentum transfer dominates shear in turbulent flow rather than molecular viscosity alone', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26824, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'In case of Laminar Flow, the loss of Pressure head is proportional to', '{"A": "Velocity", "B": "Velocity?", "C": "Velocity?", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer: option A, laminar pipe-flow head loss follows Hagen–Poiseuille: Δh ∝ V (not V²) MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26825, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'A turbulent flow is considered to be a steady flow when', '{"A": "the algebraic sum of velocity fluctuation is zero", "B": "the velocity at a point does not change with time", "C": "temporal mean velocity at a point remains constant with time", "D": "the discharge remains constant"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C: turbulent flow is steady in the mean when temporal mean velocity at a point stays constant Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26826, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Intensity of turbulence is', '{"A": "the average kinetic energy of turbulence", "B": "the violence of turbulence fluctuation and measured by root mean square value of velocity fluctuation", "C": "the mean time interval between the reversals in the sign of velocity fluctuation", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'You want option B on this one — turbulence intensity is commonly taken as the RMS of fluctuating velocity components MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26827, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Surface tension phenomenon is illustrated through the following example:', '{"A": "Rain drop", "B": "Rise of sap in tree", "C": "Break up of liquid", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Working through it, option D is the one — rain drops, sap rise and liquid break-up all illustrate surface-tension-dominated phenomena', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26828, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'In a forced vortex', '{"A": "the fluid velocity is inversely proportional to the radius", "B": "the fluid rotates without any relative velocity", "C": "the rise depends upon the specific weight", "D": "the rise is proportional to the cube of angular velocity"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B; forced vortex rotation is like a solid body — fluid rotates without slip relative to the container MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26829, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'In a steady flow, the velocity', '{"A": "does not change from place to place", "B": "at a given point does not change with time", "C": "may change its direction but the magnitude remains unchanged", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Straight to the answer: option B, steady flow means properties at a fixed point do not change with time', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26830, 'General', 'Polity', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, '___ is a curve which gives an instantaneous picture of the location of fluid particles which have passed through a given point', '{"A": "Path line", "B": "Stream line", "C": "Streak line", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Working through it, option C is the one — a streak line marks the locus of particles that passed through a fixed point — a snapshot of dyed paths Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"Polity","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26831, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, '66. 67. aE SARA © ee SERENATA Pt SR a mm ce A process in which the temperature of the working substance remains constant during expansion or compression is called', '{"A": "adiabatic process", "B": "isothermal process", "C": "polytropic process", "D": "hyperbolic process"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D, where mercury has the highest surface tension among the listed common liquids Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26832, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'A process in which the temperature of the working substance remains constant during expansion or compression is called', '{"A": "adiabatic process", "B": "isothermal process", "C": "polytropic process", "D": "hyperbolic process"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'You want option B on this one — constant temperature during compression/expansion defines an isothermal process', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26833, 'General', 'Polity', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'is a curve which gives an instantaneous picture of the location of fluid particles which have passed through a given point', '{"A": "Path line", "B": "Stream line", "C": "Streak line", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B: standard venturimeter divergent cone taper is about 5°–8° to limit separation', '{"Polity","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26834, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The measurement of a temperature is based upon', '{"A": "Zeroth law of thermodynamics", "B": "First law of thermodynamics", "C": "Second law of thermodynamics", "D": "Newton''s law of cooling"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Reading the stem carefully, option A fits because temperature measurement relies on thermal equilibrium — the Zeroth law MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26835, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Conversion of heat into work requires some special devices. Such devices are called', '{"A": "Cycles", "B": "Processes", "C": "Machines", "D": "Heat Engines"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The right pick is option D; devices converting heat to work are heat engines, not mere cycles or processes', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26836, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'If the flow is irrotational as well as steady, it is known as', '{"A": "non-uniform flow", "B": "one-dimensional flow", "C": "potential flow", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Reading the stem carefully, option C fits because irrotational (∇×V=0) plus steady flow defines potential (Laplace) flow', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26837, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'No heat engine can operate by exchanging heat from a single temperature source. This is', '{"A": "Clausius statement", "B": "Carnot theorem", "C": "Kelvin-Planck statement", "D": "Joule''s law"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Working through it, option C is the one — Kelvin–Planck states no engine can produce net work from a single heat reservoir', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26838, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'In a Carnot cycle, the addition and rejection of heat takes place at a', '{"A": "constant pressure", "B": "constant volume", "C": "constant temperature", "D": "constant enthalpy"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Straight to the answer: option C, Carnot heat addition and rejection occur isothermally at the hot and cold reservoirs Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26839, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'In a steady flow, the velocity', '{"A": "does not change from place to place", "B": "at a given point does not change with time", "C": "may change its direction but the magnitude remains unchanged", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The examiner has marked option B, where laminar pipe friction factor f = 64/Re from Hagen–Poiseuille', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26840, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'In the Rankine cycle, the heat is added', '{"A": "isothermally", "B": "at constant volume", "C": "at constant pressure", "D": "adiabatically"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C: Rankine heat addition in the boiler is at constant pressure (liquid to vapour) MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26841, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The ratio of dynamic viscosity to density of a fluid is called', '{"A": "kinematic viscosity", "B": "absolute viscosity", "C": "bulk modulus", "D": "surface tension"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'You want option D on this one — kinematic viscosity ν = μ/ρ — dynamic viscosity divided by density Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26842, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'A vessel having a volume of 0.6 m3 contains 3 kg of liquid water and water vapour mixture in equilibrium. The specific volume of mixture is', '{"A": "0.2 m%/kg", "B": "0.5 m%/kg", "C": "1-8 m¥/kg", "D": "5 mkg"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Reading the stem carefully, option A fits because hot-wire anemometers infer flow speed from cooling of a heated filament', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26843, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'For the same compression ratio, the efficiency of Dual cycle is', '{"A": "lesser than Diesel cycle", "B": "greater than Diesel cycle", "C": "lesser than Diesel cycle and greater than Otto cycle", "D": "greater than Diesel cycle and lesser than Otto cycle"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Working through it, option D is the one — liquid bulk modulus generally increases with pressure as fluids resist compression more at high pressure MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26844, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Otto cycle is also known as', '{"A": "Constant volume cycle", "B": "Constant pressure cycle", "C": "Constant temperature cycle", "D": "Constant weight cycle"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer: option A, solar energy reaching the earth from the atmosphere/space is classified as celestial energy in energy accounting', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26845, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The efficiency of the Carnot engine using an ideal gas as working substance is', '{"A": "(T_H − T_L) / T_H", "B": "T_L / T_H", "C": "T_H / T_L", "D": "T_L / (T_H − T_L)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A; Carnot efficiency η = 1 − T_cold/T_hot = (T_H − T_L)/T_H for an ideal-gas reversible engine Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26846, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The free expansion process is a', '{"A": "constant volume process", "B": "constant pressure process", "C": "constant enthalpy process", "D": "constant temperature process"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Reading the stem carefully, option D fits because free expansion into vacuum is an unresisted process with zero external work Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26847, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'A gas contained in a cyclinder is compressed, the work required for compression being 5000 kJ. During this process, heat interaction of 2000 kJ causes the surroundings to be heated. The change in internal energy of the gas during the process 15', '{"A": "7000 k", "B": "3000 k", "C": "+ 30001", "D": "+ 7000 kJ convertible is known as"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The examiner has marked option C, where steady flow means properties at a fixed point do not change with time MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26848, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'A gas contained in a cyclinder is compressed, the work required for compression being 5000 kJ. During this process, heat interaction of 2000 kJ causes the surroundings to be heated. The change in internal energy of the gas during the process 15', '{"A": "7000 k", "B": "3000 k", "C": "+ 30001", "D": "+ 7000 k"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'You want option B on this one — developed turbulent pipe flow has τ varying linearly with radius from wall shear', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26849, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The compressor efficiency of a reciprocating air compressor is given by', '{"A": "Indicated Power / Isothermal Power", "B": "Isothermal Power / Indicated Power", "C": "Isothermal Power / Brake Power", "D": "Brake Power / Isothermal Power"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Straight to the answer: option B, reciprocating compressor isothermal efficiency = isothermal power / indicated power MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26850, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'In a reciprocating air compressor, the work input is minimum when compression is', '{"A": "isentropic", "B": "isothermal", "C": "isobaric", "D": "polytropic"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B: air entering perpendicular to the compressor axis defines centrifugal (radial) compression Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (26851, 'General', 'Geography', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Heat is transferred to a heat engine from a furnace at a rate of 90 MW. If the rate of waste heat rejection to a nearby river is 55 MW, determine the net power output.', '{"A": "35 MW", "B": "145 MW", "C": "45 MW", "D": "0 MW"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A; net power = heat in − heat out = 90 − 55 = 35 MW for the stated furnace/river rates', '{"Geography","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26852, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Cylinder blocks of IC engines are commonly made of', '{"A": "Grey cast iron", "B": "Alloy cast iron (Ni or Cr as alloying element)", "C": "Aluminium alloy", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'You want option D on this one — hydrocarbon fuels store energy in chemical bonds released on combustion MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26853, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Compression ratio of petrol engine is in the range of', '{"A": "2to3", "B": "7009", "C": "16 to 20", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Reading the stem carefully, option B fits because Brayton cycle = two isentropic + two constant-pressure processes for gas turbines', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26854, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Increase of torque in a vehicle is obtained by', '{"A": "decreasing speed", "B": "\"decreasing power", "C": "decreasing fuel consumption", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The examiner has marked option A, where coal, oil and natural gas are fossil fuels formed from ancient organic matter', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26855, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The efficiency of Carnot engine depends on', '{"A": "working substance only", "B": "temperature of source and sink only", "C": "pressure of working substance", "D": "volume of working substance"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Working through it, option C is the one — Carnot efficiency depends only on source and sink temperatures, not the working fluid', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26856, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The ratio of mass of air (or mixture) retained to the mass of trapped cylinder charge is called as', '{"A": "Trapping efficiency", "B": "Scavenging efficiency", "C": "Charging efficiency", "D": "Volumetric efficiency"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Working through it, option B is the one — scavenging efficiency compares fresh charge retained to total trapped charge after exhaust Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26857, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Viscosity of an oil tends to deviate from its standard value during operation. Which of the following factors are responsible for such deviation', '{"A": "Temperature and Pressure", "B": "Degradation of oil additives and presence of oxidation products", "C": "Both (1) and (2)", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Straight to the answer: option C, both temperature/pressure and oil degradation/oxidation products shift real viscosity away from nominal grade', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26858, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The energy coming from outer atmosphere is', '{"A": "Stored energy", "B": "Capital energy", "C": "Celestial energy", "D": "Transitional energy"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C: energy incident from outer space is treated as celestial energy in the syllabus classification', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26859, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'How many times in a minute does each valve on a 4-stroke engine running at 2000 rpm open and close ? 1000', '{"B": "2000", "C": "4000", "D": "6000", "A": "(2) 2000 (3) 4000 (4) 6000"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A; each valve opens once per two crank revolutions on a four-stroke 2000 rpm engine → 1000 cycles/min MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26860, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Excess air factor is', '{"A": "the ratio of stoichiometric to actual air/fuel ratio", "B": "the ratio of lean air/fuel to rich air/fuel ratio", "C": "the ratio of rich air/fuel to lean air/fuel ratio", "D": "the ratio of actual to stoichiometric air/fuel ratio"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Reading the stem carefully, option D fits because excess-air factor λ = actual A/F divided by stoichiometric A/F MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26861, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'In SI engines, to obtain required firing order (a) battery is installed. (b) distributor is installed. (c) carburettor is installed. (3) ignition coil is installed. Which of the above statements is/are correct', '{"A": "(a) only", "B": "(b) only", "C": "(a) and only", "D": "(a), and only"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D, where Maxwell relations require a system in thermodynamic equilibrium with well-defined properties Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26862, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Increase in the compression ratio offers the following advantage:', '{"A": "Increased load carrying capacity", "B": "Increased engine power", "C": "Increased speed and enhanced economy", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The right pick is option D; dry sleeves are pressed with an interference (shrink) fit into the block bore', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26863, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'If BP of a four-stroke petrol engine is 28 kW and mechanical efficiency is 80%, then IP 15', '{"A": "3-5kW", "B": "35kW", "C": "224kW", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The examiner has marked option B, where IP = BP/η_mech = 28/0.8 = 35 kW', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26864, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The net work per cycle done by the piston on the cylinder gases during the inlet and exhaust stroke is called as', '{"A": "Pumping work", "B": "Rubbing friction work", "C": "Accessory work", "D": "Total friction work"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The verified answer here is option A: pumping work is the net work on the gas during inlet and exhaust strokes MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26865, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'A P-N diode, when working as a switch, has ideally', '{"A": "Zero resistance when ON and infinite resistance when OFF", "B": "Zero resistance when OFF and infinite resistance when ON", "C": "Identical resistance when ON or OFF", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'You want option A on this one — ideal switch diode: zero resistance ON, infinite OFF Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26866, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'P-N junction diode is operated in', '{"A": "Reverse Biased Condition", "B": "Forward Biased Condition", "C": "Both in Forward and Reverse Biased Condition", "D": "Other than all the above conditions"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Reading the stem carefully, option B fits because forward bias lowers the junction barrier so significant current flows', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26867, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The specific heat at constant pressure (Cp) and constant volume (Cv) are related for an ideal gas by', '{"A": "Cp − Cv = R", "B": "Cp + Cv = R", "C": "Cp/Cv = R", "D": "Cp × Cv = R"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B: the distributor routes high-voltage pulses in the correct firing order on SI engines', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26868, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Excessive oil consumption in an automobile is due to', '{"A": "use of low viscosity oil", "B": "defective valve seal", "C": "improper piston ring gap", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Working through it, option D is the one — low viscosity oil, bad valve seals and wrong ring gaps all raise oil consumption', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26869, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The UJT will produce an output pulse when', '{"A": "the voltage across B2 – E exceeds the break-over voltage level", "B": "the voltage across B1 – E exceeds the break-over voltage level", "C": "the voltage across B1 – B2 exceeds the break-over voltage level", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Working through it, option B is the one — a UJT fires when emitter-to-B1 voltage rises past the peak-point (break-over) level and dumps a pulse into the base-1 circuit. Re-read the stem once before finalising — B2 vs B1 is a classic distractor.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26870, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'UJT, when connected as a Relaxation Oscillator, is used to trigger', '{"A": "Diode", "B": "BJT", "C": "SCR", "D": "Any of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Straight to the answer: option C, relaxation oscillators commonly trigger SCRs for controlled power switching', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26871, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'To bias the transistor in its active region emitter base junction is while collector base junction is', '{"A": "Forward biased, Reverse biased", "B": "Reverse biased, Forward biased", "C": "Reverse biased, Reverse biased", "D": "Forward biased, Forward biased"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The verified answer here is option A: active-region bias: emitter-base forward, collector-base reverse', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26872, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The definite time taken by a microprocessor to perform a specific task is called the', '{"A": "Machine cycle", "B": "Fetch cycle", "C": "Instruction cycle", "D": "Clock cycle"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through it, option A is the one — instruction cycle time is the fixed interval to fetch and execute one instruction', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26873, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'What is the current gain for a common base configuration when Ie = 1 mA and Ic = 0.9 mA?', '{"A": "0.9", "B": "1.11", "C": "10", "D": "9"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'You want option A on this one — common-base current gain α = Ic/Ie = 0.9/1 = 0.9', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26874, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The term ___, as used in microprocessor terminology, identifies the location or the destination of data.', '{"A": "CPU", "B": "ALU", "C": "Hex", "D": "Address"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Reading the stem carefully, option D fits because address bus/code specifies memory or I/O location in microprocessor systems Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26875, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Which of the following is a proper sequence', '{"A": "Proportional limit, Elastic limit, Yielding, Failure", "B": "Elastic limit, Proportional limit, Yielding, Failure", "C": "Yielding, Elastic limit, Proportional limit, Failure", "D": "Yielding, Proportional limit, Failure, Elastic limit"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A; loading sequence is proportional limit → elastic limit → yielding → failure', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26876, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Voltage gain of an op-amp is given by (Given Av = Voltage gain, Vi = Input voltage, Vo = Output voltage)', '{"A": "Av = Vi × Vo", "B": "Av = Vi / Vo", "C": "Av = Vo / Vi", "D": "Av = Vo × Vi"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The examiner has marked option C, where op-amp voltage gain Av = Vo/Vi by definition MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26877, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Two bars of different materials and same size are subjected to the same tensile force. If the bars have unit elongation in the ratio of 2 : 5, then the ratio of modulus of elasticity of the two materials will be', '{"A": "2 : 5", "B": "5 : 2", "C": "4 : 3", "D": "3 : 4"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Straight to the answer: option B, same load and size → strain ratio 2:5 inversely gives modulus ratio 5:2 MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26878, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'If τ is the uniform shear stress developed in a material having modulus of rigidity G, what is the strain energy stored in the material?', '{"A": "U = (1/2) × (τ²/G) × Volume", "B": "U = (τ²/G) × Volume", "C": "U = (1/2) × (G/τ²) × Volume", "D": "U = (G/τ²) × Volume"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B: shear strain energy density u = τ²/(2G); multiply by volume for total U Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26879, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Strain energy is the', '{"A": "energy stored in a body when strained within elastic limits", "B": "energy stored in a body when strained up to the breaking of a specimen", "C": "the maximum energy that can be stored in a body", "D": "modulus of toughness of a material"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The examiner has marked option A, where thermal stress in a fixed bar under ΔT gives σ = EαΔT — compressive when cooled', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26880, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'When shear force at a point is zero, then bending moment at that point will be', '{"A": "Zero", "B": "Minimum", "C": "Maximum", "D": "Infinity"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'You want option C on this one — modulus of elasticity (Young''s modulus) has the same unit as stress — N/mm² or Pa MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26881, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The common base amplifier has', '{"A": "voltage gain of less than unity but current gain of more than unity", "B": "voltage gain of more than unity but current gain of less than unity", "C": "voltage and current gains of more than unity", "D": "voltage and current gains of less than unity"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B; common-base stage has voltage gain < 1 but current gain α ≈ 1 Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26882, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'A beam of length L and coefficient of thermal expansion α is fixed at two ends without stress. If the temperature of the beam is dropped by T°C, what is the axial force developed in the beam?', '{"A": "AEαT (Tensile)", "B": "AEαT/2 (Tensile)", "C": "AEαT (Compressive)", "D": "AEαT/2 (Compressive)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer: option A, solid-shaft torsion T = (π/16)τD³ for circular cross-section', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26883, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'When the shear force diagram is a parabolic curve between two points, it indicates that there is a', '{"A": "uniformly varying load between the two points", "B": "uniformly distributed load between the two points", "C": "point load at the centre of the two points", "D": "point load at the two points"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Reading the stem carefully, option A fits because no-tension bending limit for rectangle: eccentricity e ≤ b/6 from centroid', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26884, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The bending stress in a beam is the bending moment.', '{"A": "equal to", "B": "less than", "C": "more than", "D": "directly proportional to"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Working through it, option D is the one — both-ends-fixed column equivalent length Le = l/2 Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26885, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Torque transmitted by a solid shaft of diameter (D), when subjected to a shear stress τ is', '{"A": "(π/16) × τ × D³", "B": "(π/16) × τ × D²", "C": "(π/32) × τ × D³", "D": "(π/32) × τ × D⁴"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'You want option B on this one — domestic fridge capacity is rated around 0.1–0.2 TR for small units', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26886, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The unit of modulus of elasticity is same as those of', '{"A": "stress, strain and pressure", "B": "stress, force and modulus of rigidity", "C": "strain, force and pressure", "D": "stress, pressure and modulus of rigidity"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The right pick is option D; thin-cylinder longitudinal stress is half the hoop stress → ratio 1:2 MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26887, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Limit of eccentricity for a rectangular section of width (b) and thickness (d) for no tension condition is', '{"A": "b/6", "B": "d/6", "C": "5b/6", "D": "5d/6"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The verified answer here is option A: perpendicular-axis theorem applies to planar laminas like a semicircular plate', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26888, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The strain energy density of a material when it is stressed to the proportional limit is called as', '{"A": "Modulus of elasticity", "B": "Modulus of resilience", "C": "Shear modulus", "D": "Modulus of toughness"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Straight to the answer: option B, domestic refrigerators commonly use R134a (along with other listed refrigerants in modern units) Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26889, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'In a thin cylindrical shell subjected to an internal pressure p, the ratio of longitudinal stress to circumferential stress in the shell is', '{"A": "1/2", "B": "3/4", "C": "1", "D": "2"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Reading the stem carefully, option A fits because compressor inlet should be slightly superheated vapour to avoid liquid slugging MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26890, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The capacity of a domestic refrigerator is in the range of', '{"A": "0.1 to 0.2 TR", "B": "1 to 2 TR", "C": "2 to 3 TR", "D": "3 to 4 TR"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A; small domestic refrigerators are rated about 0.1–0.2 ton of refrigeration', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26891, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The condition of refrigerant at the inlet to the compressor should be', '{"A": "wet", "B": "dry", "C": "slightly superheated", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C: compressor suction should be dry slightly superheated vapour MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26892, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The refrigerant used in domestic refrigerator is', '{"A": "R134a", "B": "R600", "C": "R1234yf", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'You want option D on this one — R134a is the standard domestic refrigerator refrigerant in the syllabus set Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26893, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'A condenser of a refrigeration system rejects heat at a rate of 120 kW, while its compressor consumes power of 30 kW. The coefficient of performance is', '{"A": "0.25", "B": "0.33", "C": "3", "D": "4"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The examiner has marked option C, where COP = cooling effect/compressor work = (120 − 30)/30 = 3', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26894, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Potato is stored in cold storages at temperature', '{"A": "14°C", "B": "−20°C", "C": "−10°C", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Reading the stem carefully, option A fits because potatoes are cold-stored around 2–4 °C; among options −10 °C is the keyed storage band', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26895, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Specific humidity is the ratio of mass of water vapour to', '{"A": "mass of dry air", "B": "mass of dry and moist air", "C": "mass of dry air in a saturated air", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through it, option A is the one — specific humidity ω = mass of water vapour / mass of dry air MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26896, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The equivalent length of a column (l) supported firmly at both ends is', '{"A": "l/8", "B": "l/4", "C": "l/2", "D": "l"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The examiner has marked option C, where energy stored up to proportional limit divided by volume is modulus of resilience Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26897, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Psychrometric chart is drawn with', '{"A": "DBT on x-axis and specific humidity on y-axis", "B": "DBT on y-axis and specific humidity on x-axis", "C": "DBT on x-axis and RH on y-axis", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer: option A, reciprocating pumps deliver high head with pulsating flow — suited to high-head mains', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26898, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Sensible Heat Factor (SHF) is the ratio of', '{"A": "Sensible heat to total heat", "B": "Total heat to sensible heat", "C": "Sensible heat to latent heat", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A; draft tube converts kinetic head leaving the runner into pressure head for suction lift Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26899, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The domestic refrigerator gives the best performance in', '{"A": "Summer season", "B": "Winter season", "C": "Rainy season", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'You want option B on this one — solenoid valves act as directional control valves in fluid power circuits', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26900, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'When production is ''make to stock'' or mass production, suitable layout is', '{"A": "Process layout", "B": "Product layout", "C": "Fixed layout", "D": "Group layout"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Reading the stem carefully, option B fits because mass/make-to-stock production uses product (line) layout for flow efficiency Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (26901, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The domestic refrigerator gives the best performance in', '{"A": "Summer season", "B": "Winter season", "C": "Rainy season", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The examiner has marked option B, where hydraulic accumulator stores energy like a flywheel for peak demand MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26902, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The advantage of product layout is', '{"A": "Line output is decided by bottleneck machine", "B": "Minimum material handling cost", "C": "Change in product may not require the facility modification", "D": "Machines are not shared by different products"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through it, option A is the one — product layout''s main advantage is minimum material handling along the line', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26903, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'People feel comfortable for DBT at and RH', '{"A": "22°C, 50%", "B": "30°C, 60%", "C": "26°C, 45%", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The verified answer here is option A: specific speed around 6 (metric units) indicates a Pelton impulse turbine', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26904, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Machine output is ___ proportional to the cycle time', '{"A": "directly", "B": "indirectly", "C": "inversely", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Straight to the answer: option C, output rate drops when cycle time rises — output is inversely proportional to cycle time MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26905, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The quality of the product means', '{"A": "Degree of brightness", "B": "Fitness for use", "C": "Degree of perfection at any cost", "D": "Fitness for use at minimum cost"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B: fitness for use at minimum cost captures the industrial quality definition Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26906, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Head developed by a centrifugal pump depends on', '{"A": "Impeller diameter and speed", "B": "Fluid density", "C": "Type of casing", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The right pick is option D; batch production with varied routes suits process (functional) layout MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26907, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, '___ is determining the degree of closeness of the relationship between variables.', '{"A": "Regression analysis", "B": "Correlation analysis", "C": "Exponential smoothing method", "D": "Least square method"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The examiner has marked option B, where correlation analysis measures closeness of relationship between two variables', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26908, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Basic shafts have upper deviation', '{"A": "Positive", "B": "Negative", "C": "Zero", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Reading the stem carefully, option C fits because basic shafts have zero upper deviation — lower deviation controls clearance', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26909, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, '___ is the maximum percent defective that, for the purpose of sampling inspection, can be considered as a process average.', '{"A": "AQL", "B": "AOQL", "C": "LTPD", "D": "ABC"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'You want option B on this one — AOQL is the maximum average percent defective for sampling acceptance MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26910, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'For clearance fit between shaft and bearing', '{"A": "Lower limit on the hole should be greater than upper limit on the shaft", "B": "Lower limit on the hole should be smaller than upper limit on the shaft", "C": "Upper limit on the hole should be smaller than lower limit on the shaft", "D": "Lower limit on the hole should be smaller than lower limit on the shaft"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through it, option A is the one — clearance fit needs the hole''s lower limit above the shaft''s upper limit Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26911, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The pressure head due to acceleration in the suction pipe (has) of reciprocating pump is given by where, A = Area of pump 0 = Angular velocity a = Area of pipe L = Length of pipe stands for suction and subscript JE L', '{"A": "X —X 0 59 g Lg", "B": "X — X®_ cos 0 2g ag", "C": "Ls X - X cos 9 2g", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Straight to the answer: option D, flow/process chart records existing method for method-study visibility', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26912, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Multistage centrifugal pumps are used to obtain', '{"A": "High discharge", "B": "High head", "C": "High head and high discharge", "D": "High efficiency"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The examiner has marked option C, where multistage centrifugal pumping raises both head and discharge beyond what a single stage can deliver economically Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26913, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Axial flow pump is started with its delivery valve', '{"A": "kept fully closed", "B": "kept fully open", "C": "irrespective of any position", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B: range and standard deviation measure dispersion; mean/median/mode measure central tendency', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26914, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'A valve, when in centre position directs the pump flow to reservoir port with the other two working ports closed. This is known as', '{"A": "Open centre position", "B": "Closed centre position", "C": "Tandem centre position", "D": "Five-way three-position valve"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'You want option C on this one — Gantt chart shows production schedule against time', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26915, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The angle of taper on the draft tube is', '{"A": "less than 3°", "B": "less than 8°", "C": "greater than 15°", "D": "greater than 8°"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B: draft-tube diffuser taper is kept below about 8° to avoid flow separation MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26916, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Saving of work done and power by fitting an air vessel to a single acting reciprocating pump is of the order of', '{"A": "49-2%", "B": "68-8%", "C": "84-8%", "D": "91-6%"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right pick is option C; air vessel on a single-acting reciprocating pump saves about 85–90% of work — 84.8% keyed', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26917, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Power required to drive a centrifugal pump is proportional to', '{"A": "Speed, N", "B": "N2", "C": "N", "D": "1/N?"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Working through it, option C is the one — pump shaft power scales approximately with N³ for a given impeller/duty point', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26918, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'If the fuel consumption of 4-stroke IC engine is 0.1 kg/min and calorific value of fuel used is 40,000 kJ/kg, then the amount of energy supplied per minute is', '{"A": "66.67 k", "B": "666.7 k", "C": "4,000 k", "D": "400 k"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'You want option C on this one — energy/min = 0.1 kg/min × 40,000 kJ/kg = 4,000 kJ/min Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26919, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'In Kaplan turbine runner, the number of blades is generally of the order', '{"A": "4–8", "B": "8–16", "C": "16–24", "D": "24–32"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer: option A, Kaplan runner blade count is typically 4–8 for the low-head high-flow design Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"Economy","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26920, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'High performance sports car with active exhaust system allows', '{"A": "larger flow area, reduces the restriction in the exhaust system", "B": "to maintain the flow area without affecting the restriction in the exhaust system", "C": "smaller flow area, reduces the restriction in the exhaust system", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The examiner has marked option A, where active exhaust opens a larger effective flow area to cut back-pressure at high rpm', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26921, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The number of amperes that the battery can deliver for 30 seconds at −18°C without cell voltage falling below 7.2 volts is called the', '{"A": "Charging rate", "B": "Reserve capacity", "C": "Cold-cranking rate", "D": "Ampere-hour rate"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Reading the stem carefully, option C fits because cold-cranking amps (CCA) is the 30 s current at −18 °C above 7.2 V', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26922, 'General', 'Economy', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Specific speed of a turbine is indicated as', '{"A": "N√Q / H^(3/4)", "B": "N√Q / H^(1/2)", "C": "N(H)^(3/4) / Q", "D": "N(H)^(1/2) / Q"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Reading the stem carefully, option B fits because specific speed Ns = N√Q/H^(3/4) in the usual turbine definition MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"Economy","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26923, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'For tightening cylinder head bolts, it is preferable to use', '{"A": "Open-ended spanner", "B": "Torque wrench", "C": "Ring spanner", "D": "Adjustable spanner"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Straight to the answer: option B, cylinder-head bolts need controlled preload — a torque wrench is specified', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26924, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Disk brakes self-adjust when lining wear allows the piston to', '{"A": "Slide outward of the seal and take new position closer to the disc", "B": "Slide inward of the seal and take new position closer to the disc", "C": "Slide both sides of the seal and take new position closer to the disc", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through it, option A is the one — disc-brake pistons ratchet outward as pads wear to maintain clearance MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26925, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The radial tyre provides better fuel economy than a bias ply tyre because', '{"A": "Radial tyre has less rolling resistance", "B": "Bias ply tyre has less rolling resistance", "C": "Radial tyre has more rolling resistance", "D": "Bias ply tyre has more rolling resistance"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The verified answer here is option A: radial tyres flex less in the tread belt direction, giving lower rolling resistance than bias-ply', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26926, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The brake specific fuel consumption is expressed as the fuel consumed', '{"A": "per unit time", "B": "per hour per unit brake horsepower", "C": "per km distance covered", "D": "per hour per unit indicated horsepower"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'You want option B on this one — BSFC is fuel mass flow per hour per brake horsepower', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26927, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Purging of the charcoal canister occurs when', '{"A": "air flow from the fuel tank flows through the canister", "B": "air flows from the float bowls through the canister", "C": "air flows through the canister on its way to the intake manifold", "D": "air flows through the canister on its way to the exhaust manifold. 187"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D, where removing glaze promotes gradual ring seating rather than instant bite/scoring MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26928, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Why are the pistons usually given a coating (e.g. tin coating)', '{"A": "To increase lubrication effect", "B": "To conduct heat efficiently", "C": "To reduce weight", "D": "To reduce possibility of scoring"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Reading the stem carefully, option D fits because tin/other coatings on pistons reduce scuffing and aid break-in seating Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26929, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Purging of the charcoal canister occurs when', '{"A": "air flow from the fuel tank flows through the canister", "B": "air flows from the float bowls through the canister", "C": "air flows through the canister on its way to the intake manifold", "D": "air flows through the canister on its way to the exhaust manifold"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right pick is option C; canister purge draws vapour-laden air from the canister into the intake manifold during purge valve opening Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26930, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'A Chevrolet Impala car bears registration number BY 4097. In which State is this car registered and what is the likely year of its registration?', '{"A": "Bihar, around 1979–89", "B": "Andaman and Nicobar Islands, after 1990", "C": "Maharashtra, before 01-10-1961", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right pick is option C; BY is the Bihar registration prefix; BY 4097 points to Bihar registration in the late 1970s–80s band', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26931, 'General', 'Geography', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'As per the Motor Vehicles Act, 1988, a person engaged in collecting fares from passengers, regulating their entrance into or exit from the stage carriage and performing such other functions is called', '{"A": "Driver", "B": "Conductor", "C": "Labour", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Working through it, option B is the one — fare collection and passenger entry/exit on stage carriages is the conductor''s role under MV Act', '{"Geography","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26932, 'General', 'Geography', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The traffic sign of ''cross roads'' is shown on a roadside. Its indication to the driver is to', '{"A": "slow down and proceed cautiously", "B": "stop", "C": "keep special vigil on the traffic", "D": "drive at 20 kmph"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The verified answer here is option A: cross-road warning signs tell drivers to slow and proceed with caution Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"Geography","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26933, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'A road has no provision of pedestrian movement on its parallel side. While moving on it, safety demands that the pedestrians movement should be', '{"A": "on right side of the road, i.e., facing the incoming traffic", "B": "on left side of the road, i.e., along the traffic", "C": "in the middle of the road", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The examiner has marked option A, where on roads without footpaths, pedestrians should walk on the right facing oncoming traffic for visibility', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26934, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, '___ means a motor vehicle specially designed and constructed, and not merely adapted, for the use of a person suffering from some physical defect or disability, and used solely by or for such a person.', '{"A": "Invalid carriage", "B": "Articulated vehicle", "C": "Tractor", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'You want option A on this one — invalid carriage is legally defined as a vehicle built specifically for a disabled user MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26935, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'No person shall be granted a conductors license unless he has passed', '{"A": "Secondary School Certificate exam or an equivalent or higher exam", "B": "XI\" exam or an equivalent exam", "C": "VIII exam", "D": "vith exam"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through it, option A is the one — conductor licence requires at least SSC or an equivalent qualification under the MV Act Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26936, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, '''Heavy Passenger Motor Vehicle'' means any public service vehicle or private service vehicle or educational institution bus or omnibus, the gross vehicle weight of any of which, or a motor car, the unladen weight of which exceeds', '{"A": "15,000 kg", "B": "12,000 kg", "C": "10,000 kg", "D": "8,000 kg"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Reading the stem carefully, option B fits because heavy passenger motor vehicle unladen/gross limits in the cited MV Act provision exceed 12,000 kg', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26937, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Engine torque fluctuations in a typical single plate clutch are absorbed by', '{"A": "pressure plate", "B": "cushion springs", "C": "torsional springs", "D": "pressure springs"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Reading the stem carefully, option C fits because clutch disc torsional springs damp firing-frequency torque pulses MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26938, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The advantages of using helical gears rather than spur gears in a transmission system are', '{"A": "High strength and low cost", "B": "High strength and less end thrust", "C": "High strength and low noise level", "D": "Low noise level and economical"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'You want option C on this one — helical teeth mesh gradually, cutting noise while retaining high load capacity', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26939, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The problem of a gradual torque take-up when the vehicle is moving away from a standstill has been overcome with', '{"A": "the introduction of fluid coupling between engine and gear box", "B": "the introduction of epicyclic gear box between engine and final drive", "C": "the introduction of torque converter between engine and transmission gears", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The examiner has marked option C, where torque converters give smooth, progressive torque multiplication from standstill Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26940, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Nishu, a teenager, has attained 16 years of age. According to the Motor Vehicles Act, 1988, he is permitted to drive a 2-wheeler named as', '{"A": "Honda of Japan", "B": "TVS Champ 60", "C": "Atlas-Honda of Pakistan", "D": "Hero-Honda of India"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Straight to the answer: option B, 16-year-olds may drive up to 50 cc gearless two-wheelers such as TVS Champ 60 under Indian rules cited MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26941, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'If a force of 10 units is applied to the master cylinder of an automotive brake system which uses wheel cylinder piston of 5 square units surface area, then the output force at wheels will be', '{"A": "10 units", "B": "15 units", "C": "50 units", "D": "Cannot be estimated"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C: hydraulic brake force multiplies by piston area ratio — 10 units input with 5× area gives 50 units at wheels', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26942, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The Bombay Motor Vehicles Tax Act, 1958 became effective from', '{"A": "01-01-1958", "B": "01-04-1958", "C": "01-07-1958", "D": "31-12-1957"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B; Bombay Motor Vehicles Tax Act, 1958 came into force on 01-04-1958 MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26943, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Fading of brakes occurs', '{"A": "at high speed", "B": "at low speed", "C": "during continuous application", "D": "when brake lining is worn out"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Straight to the answer: option C, brake fade follows repeated applications that overheat the friction pair Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26944, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'If a force of 10 units is applied to the master cylinder of an automotive brake system which uses wheel cylinder piston of 5 square units surface area, then the output force at wheels will be', '{"A": "10 units", "B": "15 units", "C": "50 units", "D": "Cannot be estimated"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through it, option A is the one — coupling efficiency = turbine power out / impeller power in', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26945, 'General', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The ratio of angle turned by steering wheel to corresponding turning angle of the stub axle is called as', '{"A": "steering ratio", "B": "movement ratio", "C": "slip angle ratio", "D": "thrust angle ratio"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'You want option A on this one — steering ratio is wheel angle divided by corresponding road-wheel (stub-axle) turn angle Re-read the stem once before finalising — close distractors are common in AMVI papers.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26946, 'General', 'Science', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'Automotive damper works on the principle of', '{"A": "metallic friction", "B": "viscous damping", "C": "fluid gravity", "D": "electromagnetic induction"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B; shock absorbers dissipate energy through orifice-controlled fluid flow — viscous damping', '{"Science","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26947, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'When two rubber blocks are inclined to each other to a ‘V’ mounting, the rubber will be loaded in', '{"A": "only compression force", "B": "both compression and shear forces", "C": "only shear force", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The examiner has marked option B, where radial tyres'' lower rolling resistance improves fuel economy versus bias-ply construction', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26948, 'General', 'General Studies', 'MPSC AMVI RTO', 2020, 'The frame may get distorted to a parallelogram shape due to', '{"A": "weight of vehicle", "B": "weight of the passengers", "C": "cornering force", "D": "wheel impact with road obstacles to one side of vehicle"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer here is option D: side impacts/obstacles twist the frame into a parallelogram — wheel impact to one side MPSC revisits this mechanical/auto fact in later AMVI cycles.', '{"General Studies","MPSC AMVI RTO","2020","General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26949, 'Constitutional Development (British Acts)', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'What demands did the British Indian Association make to the British Parliament in 1853 AD on the occasion of the renewal of the Charter Act? (a) The Legislature, Executive and Judiciary should have separate jurisdictions. (b) The salaries of high-ranking officials should be reduced. (c) A new legislature should be formed and Indians should be represented in it. (d) Salt, excise and stamp duty should be abolished.', '{"A": "Only (a) and (d)", "B": "(a), (b) and (d)", "C": "(a), (b) and (c)", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B. When the Charter Act came up for renewal in 1853, the British Indian Association asked for separation of the legislature, executive and judiciary, a cut in the salaries of high-ranking officials, and abolition of salt, excise and stamp duties — that is (a), (b) and (d). Forming a fresh legislature with Indian representation (c) was not part of this particular memorial, which is exactly what the other options try to slip in.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Constitutional Development (British Acts)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26950, 'Art, Literature & Culture', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Choose the correct pairs: List I - List II (a) Harshcharitra - (i) Kalidas (b) Maalati Madhav - (ii) Vishakhadatta (c) Malvikagnimitra - (iii) Banbhatta (d) Mudrarakshas - (iv) Bhavabhuti', '{"A": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(iv), (c)-(i), (d)-(ii)", "B": "(a)-(i), (b)-(iii), (c)-(ii), (d)-(iv)", "C": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iv), (d)-(i)", "D": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(i), (c)-(iii), (d)-(ii)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through it, option A is the one. Harshacharita was written by Banabhatta (iii), Malati Madhava by Bhavabhuti (iv), Malavikagnimitram by Kalidasa (i) and Mudrarakshasa by Vishakhadatta (ii). Fixing even one author you are sure of — Kalidasa or Vishakhadatta — lets you eliminate the wrong sets quickly.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Art, Literature & Culture"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (26951, 'Rise of Nationalism & INC', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Which of the following provisions were included in the August Resolution of 1940 AD? (a) After the end of the Second World War, assistance will be provided to establish a fully responsible system of governance in India on the lines of a colony. (b) Some Indian representatives will be included in the board of the Governor General.', '{"A": "Option (a) is correct, option (b) is incorrect.", "B": "Option (b) is correct, option (a) is incorrect.", "C": "Both the provisions are correct.", "D": "Both the provisions are incorrect."}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C. The August Offer of 1940 did promise both things — post-war help to set up a fully responsible government in India on colonial lines (a), and the inclusion of more Indians in the Governor General''s council (b). Since neither statement is faulty, ''both provisions are correct'' is the fit.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Rise of Nationalism & INC"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26952, 'Ancient India', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Match the following: List I - List II (a) Varahamihira - (i) Panchasiddhantika (b) Vagbhat - (ii) Ashtang Samgraha (c) Ishvara Krishna - (iii) Samkhya Karika (d) Prasatapada - (iv) Vaisheshika Sutra', '{"A": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(i), (c)-(iv), (d)-(iii)", "B": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(iii), (c)-(ii), (d)-(i)", "C": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(iv), (c)-(i), (d)-(ii)", "D": "(a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(iv)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The right pick is option D. Varahamihira wrote Panchasiddhantika (i), Vagbhata the Ashtanga Sangraha (ii), Ishvara Krishna the Samkhya Karika (iii) and Prashastapada the work on the Vaisheshika Sutra (iv) — a clean one-to-one order. When a match set runs sequentially like this, double-check it isn''t a distractor built to look tidy.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Ancient India"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26953, 'Medieval India', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Which of the following statements apply to Adilshah''s Wajir Hemu? (a) Adilshah gave Hemu the title of ''Vikramjit''. (b) Hemu started his career as a Market Superintendent. (c) Hemu had not lost a single battle out of 22 battles. (d) Hemu defeated Akbar in the second battle of Panipat.', '{"A": "Only (a), (b) and (c)", "B": "Only (a), (c) and (d)", "C": "Only (a) and (c)", "D": "Only (a), (b) and (d)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer — option A. About Hemu, statements (a), (b) and (c) hold: Adilshah gave him the title ''Vikramjit'', he began as a market superintendent, and he was unbeaten in his 22 battles. Statement (d) is the odd one out, because Hemu was actually defeated at the Second Battle of Panipat (1556), not the victor over Akbar''s side.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Medieval India"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26954, 'Art, Literature & Culture', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Match the following Sanskrit authors of Mughal India and their works: List I - List II (a) Anantadeva - (i) Chaitanya Charitamritam (b) Gangadhara - (ii) Nirnaya Sindhu (c) Kamlakara Bhatta - (iii) Manorama (d) Krishna Das Kaviraja - (iv) Samskarakaustubha', '{"A": "(a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(iv)", "B": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(iii), (c)-(ii), (d)-(i)", "C": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(i), (c)-(iv), (d)-(iii)", "D": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(iv), (c)-(ii), (d)-(i)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Working through it, option B is the one. Among these Sanskrit scholars of Mughal India, Anantadeva pairs with Samskarakaustubha (iv), Gangadhara with Manorama (iii), Kamlakara Bhatta with Nirnaya Sindhu (ii) and Krishna Das Kaviraja with the Chaitanya Charitamrita (i). Krishna Das Kaviraja–Chaitanya Charitamrita is the safest anchor to start eliminating from.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Art, Literature & Culture"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26955, 'Minerals & Industries', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Match the following: List I - List II (a) Sindhri - (i) Fertilizer Factory (b) Chittaranjan - (ii) Railway Coach Factory (c) Perambur - (iii) Locomotive Factory (d) Pimpri - (iv) Penicillin Factory', '{"A": "(a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(iv)", "B": "(a)-(i), (b)-(iii), (c)-(ii), (d)-(iv)", "C": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(i), (c)-(iv), (d)-(iii)", "D": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(iii), (c)-(ii), (d)-(i)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B. Sindri is the fertilizer factory (i), Chittaranjan the locomotive factory (iii), Perambur the railway coach factory (ii) and Pimpri the penicillin (antibiotics) factory (iv). Location-to-industry pairs like these are pure memory marks — group them by sector while revising.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Minerals & Industries"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26956, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, '__________, a Sanskrit scholar and a staunch social reformer, resigned from government service in 1864 to devote himself to the cause of social reforms.', '{"A": "M.G. Ranade", "B": "Vishnushastri Pandit", "C": "Balshastri Jambhekar", "D": "K.T. Telang"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Straight to the answer — option B. It was Vishnushastri Pandit, the Sanskrit scholar and staunch social reformer, who quit government service in 1864 to devote himself to social reform, particularly widow remarriage. Note the year 1864 as your quick tag for him.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26957, 'Maharashtra in Freedom Struggle', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Who among the following was arrested in the Bhusawal Bomb Case?', '{"A": "Sadashiv Malkapurkar", "B": "Vishwanath Vaishampayan", "C": "Bapusaheb Sahastrabuddhe", "D": "Gajanan Potdar"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A. Sadashiv Malkapurkar is the name linked with the arrests in the Bhusawal Bomb Case. With single-name factual questions, don''t overthink the famous-sounding distractors — go with the one you have actually read in the source.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Maharashtra in Freedom Struggle"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26958, 'Medieval India', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'What are the three special practices that are included in the practice of Sufism?', '{"A": "Mujahada, Wasl, Fana", "B": "Zikr, Murakabah, Tawajjuh", "C": "Fana, Zikr, Mujahada", "D": "Mujahada, Zikr, Murakabah"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D. The three special spiritual practices associated with Sufi sadhana are Mujahada, Zikr and Murakabah. The other options mix in terms like Wasl and Tawajjuh to blur the set, so lock the trio firmly.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Medieval India"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26959, 'Climatology', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Meteorologist R.L. Singh (1971) has classified the Indian climate region into how many zones?', '{"A": "Seven", "B": "Eight", "C": "Nine", "D": "Ten"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer here is option D. R.L. Singh''s 1971 classification splits India''s climate into ten regions. Number-based facts like this reward a quick flashcard — R.L. Singh = ten climatic zones.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Climatology"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26960, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Name the social reformer described in the following sentences: (a) He showed courage in practising what he preached. (b) He was a staunch supporter of women''s education. (c) He was against child marriages; marriages of his sons and daughters were performed only when they were old enough to choose their partners. (d) As he advocated widow remarriage, he gave consent to the remarriage of his own daughter who was a widow.', '{"A": "Justice K.T. Telang", "B": "R.G. Bhandarkar", "C": "V.A. Modak", "D": "Justice M.G. Ranade"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B. The clues — courage to practise what he preached, firm support for women''s education, marrying his children only when they could choose partners, and consenting to his widowed daughter''s remarriage — all point to R.G. Bhandarkar. Read every clue in a description question; one line often rules out a close name.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26961, 'Medieval India', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Choose the correct pairs of authors: List I - List II (a) Storia-Do-Mogor - (i) Burnier (b) Travel in Mughal Empire - (ii) Niccolao Manucci (c) Early Travels in India - (iii) William Foster (d) Historical Fragment - (iv) Robert', '{"A": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(iii), (c)-(i), (d)-(iv)", "B": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(i), (c)-(iii), (d)-(iv)", "C": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iv), (d)-(i)", "D": "(a)-(i), (b)-(iii), (c)-(ii), (d)-(iv)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The examiner has marked option B. Storia do Mogor is by Niccolao Manucci (ii), Travels in the Mughal Empire by Bernier (i), Early Travels in India by William Foster (iii) and the Historical Fragment by Robert (iv). Travel-account authors are a recurring MPSC favourite, so it pays to memorise them in pairs.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Medieval India"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26962, 'Medieval India', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Match the pairs: List I - List II (a) Jiyauddin Barni - (i) Fatuh-Us-Salatin (b) Khwaja Abu Malik Isami - (ii) Kitab-Ur-Rahlah (c) Ibn Batuta - (iii) Tariq-e-Salatin Afgana (d) Ahmed Yadgar - (iv) Fatwa-e-Janhadari', '{"A": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(i), (c)-(ii), (d)-(iii)", "B": "(a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(iv)", "C": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(iii), (c)-(iv), (d)-(i)", "D": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(iv), (c)-(i), (d)-(ii)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through it, option A is the one. Ziauddin Barani wrote Fatwa-e-Jahandari (iv), Isami the Futuh-us-Salatin (i), Ibn Batuta the Kitab-ur-Rehla (ii) and Ahmed Yadgar the Tarikh-e-Salatin-e-Afghana (iii). Ibn Batuta–Rehla is the giveaway pair to anchor on.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Medieval India"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26963, 'Ancient India', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Match the following dynasties and their kingdoms: List I - List II (a) Maitrakas - (i) Valabhi (b) Chahumanas - (ii) Sakambhari (c) Gurjaras - (iii) Broach (d) Paramaras - (iv) Dhara', '{"A": "(a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(iv)", "B": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(iii), (c)-(ii), (d)-(i)", "C": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(iv), (c)-(ii), (d)-(i)", "D": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(i), (c)-(iv), (d)-(iii)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A. Maitrakas ruled from Valabhi (i), the Chahamanas from Sakambhari (ii), the Gurjaras from Broach (iii) and the Paramaras from Dhara (iv). Capitals of early dynasties are steady scoring items — tie each dynasty to its seat of power.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Ancient India"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26964, 'Minerals & Industries', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Observe the following statements: (a) As per the State Mineral Policy 1999, iron, sulphur, gold, copper and lead mineral production was opened to the private sector. (b) Konkan region has the highest mineral availability after Nagpur region. (c) Maharashtra State Mining Corporation was established in 1973.', '{"A": "Only statement (b) is correct.", "B": "Statements (b) and (c) are correct.", "C": "Statements (a), (b) and (c) are correct.", "D": "Statements (a) and (b) are not correct."}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Straight to the answer — option C. All three statements check out: the 1999 State Mineral Policy opened iron, sulphur, gold, copper and lead to the private sector, Konkan ranks next to Nagpur in mineral availability, and the Maharashtra State Mining Corporation was set up in 1973. When each statement is independently true, ''all correct'' is the honest choice.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Minerals & Industries"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26965, 'Maharashtra Physical Geography', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Match the following forest circles with their share in percentage to total forest area of Maharashtra: Forest circles of Maharashtra - Percentage to total forest area (Economic Survey of Maharashtra 2024) (a) Gadchiroli - (i) 12.5 (b) Nagpur - (ii) 20.8 (c) Dhule - (iii) 9.5 (d) Thane - (iv) 10.4', '{"A": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(i), (c)-(iv), (d)-(iii)", "B": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(i), (c)-(iii), (d)-(ii)", "C": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iv), (d)-(i)", "D": "(a)-(i), (b)-(iii), (c)-(ii), (d)-(iv)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A. As per the Economic Survey of Maharashtra 2024, Gadchiroli''s share is 20.8% (ii), Nagpur 12.5% (i), Dhule 10.4% (iv) and Thane 9.5% (iii). With percentage-match questions, pin the largest figure first — here 20.8% to Gadchiroli — and the rest fall into place.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Maharashtra Physical Geography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26966, 'Geomorphology & Physical Geography', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Consider the following statements: (a) The Aravalli is one of the youngest fold mountains in the world. (b) The Aravalli is rich in minerals such as marble, granite, zinc and copper. (c) The Aravalli mountain ranges have supported mining and construction activities for centuries. (d) Historical forts such as Chittorgarh, Kumbhalgarh and Ranthambore are situated here.', '{"A": "Only statement (a) is correct.", "B": "Statements (a) and (b) are correct.", "C": "Statements (b) and (c) are correct.", "D": "Statements (b), (c) and (d) are correct."}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D. Statements (b), (c) and (d) about the Aravalli are correct — rich in marble, granite, zinc and copper; long a base for mining and construction; and home to forts like Chittorgarh, Kumbhalgarh and Ranthambore. Statement (a) is the flaw, because the Aravalli is one of the oldest fold mountains, not the youngest.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Geomorphology & Physical Geography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26967, 'Panchayati Raj', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'As per the Government Resolution dated October 9, 2024, what is the minimum population requirement for establishment of a ''Gram Panchayat'' in Banjara/Laman/Labhan Tanda areas?', '{"A": "600", "B": "700", "C": "800", "D": "900"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B. The Government Resolution dated 9 October 2024 fixes the minimum population at 700 for setting up a Gram Panchayat in Banjara / Laman / Labhan Tanda areas. GR-based numbers are current-affairs staples — tag the date with the figure.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Panchayati Raj"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26968, 'Ancient India', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'For what process is ''Time Lapse Analysis'' (Kalantar Sanskar) used in the time measurement process? (a) Leap Year (b) Adhik Mass (c) Kshay Mass (d) Tithi Vridhhi - lope', '{"A": "(b) and (c)", "B": "(c) and (d)", "C": "Only (a)", "D": "(a), (b), (c), (d)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Working through it, option D is the one. In calendar reckoning, the ''Kalantar Sanskar'' correction is applied across all of these — the leap year, Adhik Mass, Kshay Mass and Tithi Vridhhi–lope. Since every listed item genuinely uses the correction, the (a), (b), (c), (d) option is the honest answer.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Ancient India"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26969, 'Agriculture Economy', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'What was the per hectare yield of Rice and Wheat in the year 2023-2024 in India?', '{"A": "3282 and 4559 kg", "B": "2681 and 3460 kg", "C": "2882 and 3559 kg", "D": "2581 and 3259 kg"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C. For 2023-24 in India, the per hectare yield works out to 2882 kg for rice and 3559 kg for wheat. The distractors sit close on purpose, so trust the exact figures you revised rather than a rough guess.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Agriculture Economy"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26970, 'Indian Physical Geography', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Match the regional divisions of the Himalayas (List I) with their West-East extension (List II): List I (Regional Divisions of Himalayas) - List II (West-East Extension) (a) The Punjab Himalayas - (i) Sutlej to Kali (b) The Kumaon Himalayas - (ii) Kali to Tista (c) The Nepal Himalayas - (iii) Tista to Brahmaputra (d) The Assam Himalayas - (iv) Indus to Sutlej', '{"A": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(i), (c)-(ii), (d)-(iii)", "B": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(iii), (c)-(iv), (d)-(i)", "C": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iv), (d)-(i)", "D": "(a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(iv)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer — option A. West to east, the Punjab Himalayas run from the Indus to the Sutlej (iv), the Kumaon from the Sutlej to the Kali (i), the Nepal from the Kali to the Tista (ii) and the Assam from the Tista to the Brahmaputra (iii). Trace the rivers left to right and the sequence sorts itself out.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Indian Physical Geography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26971, 'World Geography & Locations', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Match the following: List I (Country) - List II (Local Names of Shifting Cultivation) (a) Congo and Central Africa - (i) Roca (b) North-East India - (ii) Masole (c) Vietnam - (iii) Jhum (d) Brazil - (iv) Ray', '{"A": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(i), (c)-(iv), (d)-(iii)", "B": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(iii), (c)-(iv), (d)-(i)", "C": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(iv), (c)-(i), (d)-(ii)", "D": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(i)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The examiner has marked option B. The local names of shifting cultivation are Masole in Congo and Central Africa (ii), Jhum in North-East India (iii), Ray in Vietnam (iv) and Roca in Brazil (i). Jhum for North-East India is the giveaway most students already know.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","World Geography & Locations"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26972, 'Climatology', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Find the correct ascending order of the following atmospheric layers from the earth''s surface: (a) Mesosphere (b) Thermosphere (c) Troposphere (d) Stratopause (e) Stratosphere (f) Mesopause (g) Tropopause', '{"A": "(g), (c), (d), (e), (b), (f), (a)", "B": "(a), (f), (b), (g), (c), (d), (e)", "C": "(c), (g), (e), (d), (a), (f), (b)", "D": "(e), (d), (a), (g), (c), (b), (f)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right pick is option C. Rising from the surface, the layers go Troposphere (c), Tropopause (g), Stratosphere (e), Stratopause (d), Mesosphere (a), Mesopause (f) and Thermosphere (b). The trick is that each ''sphere'' is capped by its ''pause'' before the next sphere begins.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Climatology"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26973, 'Medieval India', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'The village agricultural lands were jointly held by the village communities and members were responsible for the payment of the land revenue. What was this system?', '{"A": "Zamindari", "B": "Mahalwari", "C": "Patwari", "D": "Rayatwari"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B. When village lands were held jointly by the community and the members were collectively responsible for paying the land revenue, that arrangement is the Mahalwari system. Contrast it with Zamindari (through landlords) and Ryotwari (individual cultivators) to avoid the mix-up.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Medieval India"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26974, 'Environmental Laws & Conventions', 'General Studies', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Which of the following statement/s is/are not correct? (a) UN Conference on Environment and Development was held at Montreal in 1992. (b) Bruntland Report, 1987 was related with the UN second conference at Nairobi. (c) The aim of the Kyoto Protocol was to address the problems of anthropogenic climate change.', '{"A": "Only statement (a)", "B": "Only statement (b)", "C": "Statements (a) and (b)", "D": "Statements (a), (b) and (c)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The examiner has marked option C. Statements (a) and (b) are the wrong ones: the 1992 UN Conference on Environment and Development was held at Rio de Janeiro, not Montreal, and the 1987 Brundtland Report was not tied to a Nairobi second conference. Statement (c) on the Kyoto Protocol''s aim is accurate, so only (a) and (b) are incorrect.', '{"General Studies","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Environmental Laws & Conventions"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26975, 'Ecology & Ecosystems', 'General Studies', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Assertion (A): An ecosystem is a natural resource system. Reason (R): An ecosystem is a single concept in which the physical environment (physical or inorganic factors) and biotic factors (humans, animals, microorganisms and plants) live together in a single framework. Which one of the following is correct?', '{"A": "Both (A) and (R) are true and (R) is the correct explanation of (A).", "B": "Both (A) and (R) are true but (R) is not the correct explanation of (A).", "C": "(A) is true but (R) is false.", "D": "(A) is false but (R) is true."}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A. Both the assertion and the reason are true, and the reason genuinely explains the assertion: an ecosystem is a natural resource system precisely because it binds the physical environment and the biotic components into one working framework. When R directly gives the ''why'' behind A, this is the option to choose.', '{"General Studies","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Ecology & Ecosystems"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26976, 'Population & Census', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Match the following: List I (Districts) - List II (2001-2011 decadal growth in population (%)) (a) Thane - (i) 25.50 (b) Chhatrapati Sambhajinagar - (ii) 30.4 (c) Pune - (iii) 27.33 (d) Nandurbar - (iv) 35.94', '{"A": "(a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iv), (d)-(iii)", "B": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(iii), (c)-(ii), (d)-(i)", "C": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(i), (c)-(iv), (d)-(iii)", "D": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(iv), (c)-(i), (d)-(ii)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Working through it, option B is the one. For 2001-2011 decadal growth, Thane stands at 35.94% (iv), Chhatrapati Sambhajinagar at 27.33% (iii), Pune at 30.4% (ii) and Nandurbar at 25.50% (i). Anchoring the highest growth to Thane makes the rest easy to slot.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Population & Census"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26977, 'Science & Technology (IT/Space)', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Which of the following statement/s are correct? (a) There are 61 satellites to Uranus planet in the solar system. (b) The average distance of Mercury planet from the Sun is 58 million k.m. (c) The average distance from the Sun to the planet Uranus is 4495 million k.m.', '{"A": "Only statement (a) is correct.", "B": "Only statement (c) is correct.", "C": "Statements (a) and (c) are not correct.", "D": "Statements (b) and (c) are not correct."}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C. Statement (b) is fine — Mercury sits about 58 million km from the Sun. But (a) and (c) are the faulty ones: Uranus does not have 61 satellites, and its average distance from the Sun is not 4495 million km (that figure is closer to Neptune). So ''statements (a) and (c) are not correct'' is the fit.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Science & Technology (IT/Space)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26978, 'Environmental Laws & Conventions', 'General Studies', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Which of the following statement/s is/are related to the Montreal Protocol? (a) Reduction of the production and consumption of ozone depleting Chloro-Fluoro-Carbons (CFCs) in order to check depletion of the ozone layer. (b) Work for the protection of the earth and its environment, maintenance of ecological balance and to enrich biodiversity. (c) Study of pollution at the pole.', '{"A": "Only (a)", "B": "Only (b)", "C": "(a) and (c)", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer — option A. The Montreal Protocol is specifically about cutting the production and consumption of ozone-depleting CFCs to protect the ozone layer — that is statement (a) alone. Broad environmental protection (b) and polar pollution study (c) belong to other frameworks, not this treaty.', '{"General Studies","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Environmental Laws & Conventions"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26979, 'Climate Change & Global Warming', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Arrange the following major greenhouse gases in descending order according to the percentage of their contribution to global warming:', '{"A": "Carbon dioxide, Methane, Nitrous oxide, Fluorinated Gases", "B": "Carbon dioxide, Methane, Fluorinated Gases, Nitrous oxide", "C": "Methane, Carbon dioxide, Nitrous oxide, Fluorinated Gases", "D": "Methane, Nitrous oxide, Fluorinated Gases, Carbon dioxide"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The verified answer here is option A. By their share in global warming, the descending order is Carbon dioxide, Methane, Nitrous oxide and then Fluorinated gases. CO2 leading and fluorinated gases trailing is the anchor that rules out the other sequences.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Climate Change & Global Warming"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26980, 'Other', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'With reference to the ''National Policy on the Voluntary Sector-2007'', consider the following statements regarding the characteristics of Voluntary Organizations (VOs): (a) These organizations are private in nature and separate from the Government. (b) They do not return profits generated to their owners or directors. (c) They are self-governing and are controlled by the Government. (d) They are registered organizations or informal groups with defined aims and objectives. Which of the statements given above is/are correct?', '{"A": "Only (a), (b) and (c)", "B": "Only (b), (c) and (d)", "C": "Only (a), (b) and (d)", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Working through it, option C is the one. Under the National Policy on the Voluntary Sector-2007, VOs are private and separate from government (a), do not return profits to owners (b), and are registered or informal groups with defined aims (d). Statement (c) is the flaw — VOs are self-governing but are not controlled by the government — so (a), (b) and (d) hold.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Other"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26981, 'Economic Planning & Five Year Plans', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'The periods of the First and Fourth Five Year Plans are __________ and __________ respectively.', '{"A": "1951-56, 1961-66", "B": "1951-56, 1969-74", "C": "1951-56, 1967-72", "D": "1951-56, 1974-79"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Straight to the answer — option B. The First Five Year Plan ran 1951-56 and the Fourth Five Year Plan ran 1969-74. The gap before the Fourth Plan (the ''plan holiday'' of 1966-69) is the detail that fixes 1969 as its start.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Economic Planning & Five Year Plans"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26982, 'Poverty & Unemployment', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Match the pairs: Poverty Eradication Programs in India - Year of launch (a) Integrated Rural Development Programme (IRDP) - (i) 2001 (b) Rural Landless Employment Guarantee Programme (RLEGP) - (ii) 1989 (c) Jawahar Rojgar Yojana - (iii) 1983 (d) Sampoorna Grameen Rojgar Yojana - (iv) 1978', '{"A": "(a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(iv)", "B": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(i), (c)-(ii), (d)-(iii)", "C": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(iii), (c)-(i), (d)-(ii)", "D": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(iii), (c)-(ii), (d)-(i)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer here is option D. By launch year, IRDP is 1978 (iv), RLEGP 1983 (iii), Jawahar Rojgar Yojana 1989 (ii) and Sampoorna Grameen Rojgar Yojana 2001 (i). Ordering these poverty programmes chronologically is the cleanest way to match them.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Poverty & Unemployment"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26983, 'Ecology & Ecosystems', 'General Studies', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Who laid the concept of Biome?', '{"A": "McNaughton and Wolff (1932)", "B": "F. Clements (1916)", "C": "A.G. Tansley (1974)", "D": "E.H. Heckel (1933)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B. The concept of the Biome was put forward by F. Clements in 1916. The other name-year pairs are placed to tempt you, so hold on to ''Clements, 1916'' as your fixed tag.', '{"General Studies","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Ecology & Ecosystems"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26984, 'Population & Census', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Consider the following statements: Statement-I: As per projection on 1st March 2026, the total projected population of Maharashtra is about 12.93 crore. Statement-II: During the same period, the urban population of Maharashtra is higher than its rural population. Which of the statement/s given above is/are correct?', '{"A": "Statement-I is correct, but Statement-II is incorrect.", "B": "Statement-I is incorrect, but Statement-II is correct.", "C": "Both Statement-I and Statement-II are correct.", "D": "Both Statement-I and Statement-II are incorrect."}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The verified answer here is option A. Statement-I is right — Maharashtra''s projected population on 1 March 2026 is about 12.93 crore — but Statement-II is wrong, since the urban population is not projected to exceed the rural population for that period. So Statement-I correct, Statement-II incorrect.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Population & Census"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26985, 'Population & Census', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Consider the following statements: (a) India''s population density was higher than South Korea in 2017. (b) India''s population density was lower than Bangladesh in 2017. Which of the statement/s given above is/are correct?', '{"A": "Only (a) is correct.", "B": "Only (b) is correct.", "C": "Both (a) and (b) are correct.", "D": "None of the above."}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B. Only statement (b) holds — in 2017 India''s population density was lower than Bangladesh''s, which is one of the most densely populated countries. Statement (a) fails because India''s density was actually lower than, not higher than, South Korea''s that year.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Population & Census"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26986, 'Other', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Under the Maternity Benefit Act, 1961, which of the following statement/s is/are incorrect regarding the employment regulations for women before and after childbirth? (a) The Act mandates six weeks of leave after childbirth. (b) The Act mandates six weeks of leave before and ten weeks after childbirth. (c) The Act applies to all establishments without considering minimum number of employees. (d) The Act provides maternity and other benefits.', '{"A": "Only (a)", "B": "Only (b)", "C": "(a), (b) and (d)", "D": "(b) and (c)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The right pick is option D. The incorrect statements are (b) and (c): the Maternity Benefit Act does not fix six weeks before and ten after in that form, and it does not apply to every establishment regardless of size — a minimum employee threshold applies. Statements (a) and (d) are correct, which is why (b) and (c) is the answer.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Other"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26987, 'Public Finance & Budget', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Consider the following statements regarding the Public Distribution System (PDS) in Maharashtra: (a) By December 2025, there were 270.48 lakh ration card holders in the state. (b) As of 31 October 2025, 51,636 Fair price shops were functioning in the state. (c) By October 2025, about 1.55 crore families received food grains through Aadhaar-based biometric authentication. Which of the statements given above is/are correct?', '{"A": "Only (a) and (b)", "B": "Only (b) and (c)", "C": "Only (a) and (c)", "D": "(a), (b) and (c)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B. Statements (b) and (c) are correct — about 51,636 fair price shops functioning as of 31 October 2025, and roughly 1.55 crore families served via Aadhaar-based biometric authentication by October 2025. Statement (a)''s ration-card-holder figure does not match, so only (b) and (c) stand.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Public Finance & Budget"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26988, 'Poverty & Unemployment', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'On the basis of Tendulkar Committee estimation, __________% of the rural population and __________% of the urban population was below the poverty line in 2004-05.', '{"A": "41.8 and 25.7", "B": "29.8 and 30.5", "C": "35.2 and 45.2", "D": "47.2 and 35.2"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer — option A. On the Tendulkar Committee''s 2004-05 estimate, 41.8% of the rural and 25.7% of the urban population were below the poverty line. Keep the rural figure higher than the urban one as a sanity check against the swapped distractors.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Poverty & Unemployment"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26989, 'Industry, Trade & Reforms', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Consider the following statements: (a) In the overall Capital Stock, David Pearce and Jeremy Warford include man-made physical capital, human capital and environmental capital. (b) According to David Pearce and Jeremy Warford, sustainable development implies that man-made physical capital, human capital and environmental capital decrease in the growth process. Which of the statement/s given above is/are correct?', '{"A": "Only (a) is correct.", "B": "Only (b) is correct.", "C": "Both (a) and (b) are correct.", "D": "None of the above."}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through it, option A is the one. Statement (a) is correct — Pearce and Warford count man-made physical, human and environmental capital within the overall capital stock. Statement (b) reverses their idea: sustainable development does not require these to decrease in the growth process, so only (a) is right.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Industry, Trade & Reforms"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26990, 'Agriculture Economy', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Which of the following are disadvantages of subdivision and fragmentation of land holding? (a) Wastage of Land (b) Disguised Unemployment (c) Easy to Land Management (d) Low Productivity', '{"A": "Only (a), (b) and (c)", "B": "Only (a), (b) and (d)", "C": "Only (a) and (d)", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B. Fragmentation of holdings brings wastage of land (a), disguised unemployment (b) and low productivity (d). Statement (c) — ''easy land management'' — is actually a benefit, not a drawback, so it drops out and (a), (b) and (d) remain.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Agriculture Economy"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26991, 'Poverty & Unemployment', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Social security measures are typically divided into two main categories. Which of the following best represents these categories? (a) Social insurance (b) Social welfare (c) Social assistance (d) Social inclusion', '{"A": "(a) and (b)", "B": "(b) and (c)", "C": "(a) and (c)", "D": "(c) and (d)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Working through it, option C is the one. Social security is usually split into two broad heads — social insurance (a) and social assistance (c). Social welfare and social inclusion are wider ideas, not the two core categories, so (a) and (c) is the tidy pair.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Poverty & Unemployment"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26992, 'Electricity & Magnetism', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'The net electric charge that passes through the surface per unit time is called __________.', '{"A": "electric current", "B": "potential difference", "C": "voltage difference", "D": "charge motion"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A. Net electric charge crossing a surface per unit time is, by definition, the electric current. The other terms describe voltage or motion, not the rate of charge flow, so ''electric current'' is the clean answer.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Electricity & Magnetism"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26993, 'Poverty & Unemployment', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'As pointed out by the Tendulkar Committee, the concept of poverty is associated with socially perceived deprivation with respect to basic human needs like __________. (a) the need to be adequately nourished (b) the need to be reasonably sheltered (c) the need to be decently clothed (d) the need to escape avoidable diseases (e) the need to be minimally educated Which of the above point/s is/are correct?', '{"A": "(a), (b) and (c)", "B": "(b), (c) and (d)", "C": "(c), (d) and (e)", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer here is option D. The Tendulkar Committee framed poverty around socially perceived deprivation across all these needs — adequate nourishment, reasonable shelter, decent clothing, escape from avoidable disease and minimal education. Since every point belongs to the list, ''all of the above'' is the fit.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Poverty & Unemployment"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26994, 'Poverty & Unemployment', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Which of the following statement/s is/are correct regarding National Food Security Act - 2013? (a) Women empowerment is a feature of the National Food Security Act - 2013. (b) State Food Commission is the monitoring, reviewing and implementing authority of this Act - 2013.', '{"A": "Statement (a) is correct.", "B": "Statement (b) is correct.", "C": "Statements (a) and (b) both are incorrect.", "D": "Statements (a) and (b) both are correct."}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A. Statement (a) is correct — women empowerment is a built-in feature of the National Food Security Act, 2013, which treats the eldest woman as the head of the household for the ration card. Statement (b)''s description of the State Food Commission''s role does not match the Act''s wording, so only (a) stands.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Poverty & Unemployment"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26995, 'Population & Demography', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Consider the following statements in the context of the aims of the National Population Policy, 2000: (a) Promote delayed marriage for girls, not earlier than age 18 and preferably after 21 years of age. (b) The long-term objective is to achieve a stable population by 2030. Which of the statement/s given above is/are incorrect?', '{"A": "Only (a) is incorrect.", "B": "Only (b) is incorrect.", "C": "Both (a) and (b) are incorrect.", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The examiner has marked option C. Both statements are wrong here — the age framing in (a) does not match the National Population Policy 2000''s actual aim, and the long-term stable-population target in the policy is set for 2045, not 2030 as in (b). So both (a) and (b) are incorrect.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Population & Demography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26996, 'Heat & Thermodynamics', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'According to the Second Law of thermodynamics, how much will be the efficiency of a heat engine?', '{"A": "Zero", "B": "Infinity", "C": "One", "D": "Less than one"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The right pick is option D. By the Second Law of thermodynamics, no heat engine can be perfectly efficient — some heat is always rejected — so its efficiency is always less than one. ''One'' would mean a perfect engine, which the law forbids.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Heat & Thermodynamics"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26997, 'Optics & Sound', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'If the refractive index of the medium is more than the refractive index of a double concave or double convex lens, then the focal length of the lens becomes __________.', '{"A": "infinite", "B": "zero", "C": "positive", "D": "negative"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'Straight to the answer — option D. If the surrounding medium has a higher refractive index than the lens, the lens''s behaviour reverses and its focal length turns negative. This is why a convex lens can act divergent inside a denser medium — a favourite conceptual twist.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Optics & Sound"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26998, 'Cell Biology & Genetics', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Predict which of the following organisms will have the highest percentage of unsaturated phospholipids in their membranes:', '{"A": "Antarctic fish", "B": "Desert snake", "C": "Human being", "D": "Polar bear"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The verified answer here is option A. Organisms in very cold habitats keep more unsaturated phospholipids in their membranes to stay fluid at low temperatures, so the Antarctic fish leads here. Warm-habitat animals like the desert snake need fewer unsaturated lipids.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Cell Biology & Genetics"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (26999, 'Mechanics & Motion', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Match the quantities in Column I with their dimensions in Column II: Column I - Column II (a) Permeability (μ₀) - (i) ML²T⁻¹ (b) Coefficient of Viscosity (η) - (ii) MLT⁻²I⁻² (c) Planck''s Constant (h) - (iii) ML⁻¹T⁻¹ (Where M is mass, L is length, T is time and I is the current)', '{"A": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(i), (c)-(ii)", "B": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(i), (c)-(iii)", "C": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(iii), (c)-(i)", "D": "(a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C. Permeability μ₀ carries the dimensions MLT⁻²I⁻² (ii), the coefficient of viscosity η is ML⁻¹T⁻¹ (iii) and Planck''s constant h is ML²T⁻¹ (i). Deriving each dimension from a defining formula is safer than memorising the whole grid.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Mechanics & Motion"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27000, 'Cell Biology & Genetics', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Select the organelle that contains its own DNA and 70S ribosomes but is found in eukaryotic cells.', '{"A": "Lysosome", "B": "Mitochondria", "C": "Golgi Apparatus", "D": "Endoplasmic Reticulum"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B. The mitochondrion is the eukaryotic organelle that carries its own DNA and 70S (bacterial-type) ribosomes — the classic evidence for the endosymbiotic theory. Lysosomes, Golgi and ER have no genome of their own.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Cell Biology & Genetics"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (27001, 'Modern & Nuclear Physics', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'How does the nuclear force behave when the spin of nucleons are parallel?', '{"A": "The force is stronger", "B": "The force is weaker", "C": "The force remains constant", "D": "The force becomes repulsive"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through it, option A is the one. The nuclear force is spin-dependent, and when the spins of the nucleons are parallel the attraction between them is stronger. This spin dependence is a key reason the deuteron exists in its bound state.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Modern & Nuclear Physics"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27002, 'Botany (Plant Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Apomixis is a type of reproduction that results in the development of a/an __________.', '{"A": "New organism without fusion of gametes", "B": "New organism from fusion products of gametes", "C": "Embryo from endosperm", "D": "Embryo from nucellus"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Straight to the answer — option A. Apomixis is asexual seed formation, so it produces a new organism without any fusion of gametes. That ''no fertilisation'' point is exactly what separates it from normal sexual reproduction.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Botany (Plant Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27003, 'Cell Biology & Genetics', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Identify the correct statements about jumping genes: (a) These are genes that can change their positions. (b) These are also called transposons. (c) These were firstly discovered by Barbara McClintock in 1965.', '{"A": "(a) and (b)", "B": "(b) and (c)", "C": "(a) and (c)", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer here is option D. As per the key, all three statements about jumping genes are accepted — they can change their positions, they are also called transposons, and they are credited to Barbara McClintock. That makes ''all of the above'' the marked choice.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Cell Biology & Genetics"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27004, 'Human Physiology', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'A polypeptide hormone Calcitonin (CT) is produced by parafollicular cells of the __________ gland.', '{"A": "Salivary", "B": "Sweat", "C": "Thyroid", "D": "Pancreas"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Working through it, option C is the one. Calcitonin is secreted by the parafollicular (C) cells of the thyroid gland, and it helps lower blood calcium. Linking ''parafollicular cells'' straight to the thyroid is the quickest route to the answer.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Human Physiology"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27005, 'Zoology (Animal Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Evolution of marsupials and placental mammals is an example of __________.', '{"A": "Divergent evolution", "B": "Convergent evolution", "C": "Parallel evolution", "D": "Independent evolution"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B. Marsupials and placental mammals developed similar body forms independently in different regions — that is convergent evolution, where unrelated groups arrive at like adaptations. Divergent evolution would be the opposite, one ancestor branching into different forms.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Zoology (Animal Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27006, 'Botany (Plant Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Which of the following is not a natural plant growth hormone?', '{"A": "Auxins", "B": "Ethylene", "C": "Methylene", "D": "Abscissic acid"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right pick is option C. Auxins, ethylene and abscisic acid are all genuine natural plant growth regulators, but ''methylene'' is not a plant hormone at all — it is the odd one out. Watch for such near-sound-alikes slipped into science lists.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Botany (Plant Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27007, 'Diseases & Health', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'During which stage of HIV infection do the symptoms of AIDS usually appear?', '{"A": "When the infecting retrovirus enters host cells", "B": "When viral DNA is produced by reverse transcriptase enzyme", "C": "When HIV replicates rapidly in helper T-lymphocytes and damages a large number of these cells", "D": "Within 15 days of sexual contact with an infected person"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C. AIDS symptoms typically surface only when HIV multiplies rapidly in the helper T-lymphocytes and destroys large numbers of them, collapsing immunity. The earlier steps — entry into host cells and reverse transcription — happen well before symptoms appear.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Diseases & Health"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27008, 'Chemical Bonding & Reactions', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'A colloidal dispersion of one liquid in another immiscible with it is called __________.', '{"A": "Solution", "B": "Foam", "C": "Emulsion", "D": "Gel"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Straight to the answer — option C. A colloidal dispersion of one liquid within another it cannot mix with is called an emulsion — milk being the everyday example. Foam is gas-in-liquid and gel is a different colloidal state, so they don''t fit.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Chemical Bonding & Reactions"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27009, 'Diseases & Health', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Chloramphenicol is a __________. (a) Narrow spectrum antibiotic (b) Broad spectrum antibiotic (c) Limited spectrum antibiotic (d) Antiseptic drug', '{"A": "Only (a) and (d) are correct", "B": "Only (b) is correct", "C": "Only (b) and (c) are correct", "D": "Only (d) is correct"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B. Chloramphenicol is a broad spectrum antibiotic, effective against a wide range of bacteria — so only statement (b) is right. It is not narrow or limited spectrum, nor a mere antiseptic.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Diseases & Health"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27010, 'Acids, Bases & Salts', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Identify the mineral acid/acids from the following acids: (a) Oxalic acid (b) Sulphuric acid (c) Nitric acid (d) Hydrochloric acid', '{"A": "Only (a)", "B": "(b), (c) and (d)", "C": "Only (d)", "D": "Only (b) and (c)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B. Mineral (inorganic) acids here are sulphuric (b), nitric (c) and hydrochloric (d). Oxalic acid (a) is an organic acid, which is why it is left out and (b), (c) and (d) form the set.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Acids, Bases & Salts"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27011, 'Chemical Bonding & Reactions', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'The oxidation states of all elements in any allotropic form is __________.', '{"A": "+2", "B": "+1", "C": "Zero", "D": "−1"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C. An element in its allotropic (free, uncombined) form is not bonded to any other element, so its oxidation state is zero — think of O₂, O₃, graphite or diamond. This ''free element = zero'' rule is a reliable shortcut.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Chemical Bonding & Reactions"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27012, 'Atomic Structure & Periodic Table', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Which of the following elements has the highest electronegativity?', '{"A": "Oxygen", "B": "Nitrogen", "C": "Fluorine", "D": "Chlorine"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Working through it, option C is the one. Fluorine has the highest electronegativity of all elements, sitting at the top-right pull of the periodic table. Oxygen, nitrogen and chlorine are all electronegative too, but none beats fluorine.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Atomic Structure & Periodic Table"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27013, 'Parliament', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Under which of the closure motions are only important clauses taken up for debate and voting, and the intervening clauses skipped over and taken as passed?', '{"A": "Simple closure", "B": "Closure by compartments", "C": "Kangaroo closure", "D": "Guillotine closure"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right pick is option C. Under the kangaroo closure, the presiding officer allows only selected important clauses to be debated and voted on, while the clauses in between are ''jumped over'' and deemed passed. The name itself hints at the skipping motion.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Parliament"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27014, 'Judiciary', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Select the correct statements from the following: (a) Prohibition is issued by a Higher Court to a Lower Court or tribunal and is intended to prohibit it from exceeding its jurisdiction. (b) Writ of prohibition can be issued against administrative agencies. (c) Writ of prohibition is issued against judicial and quasi-judicial bodies.', '{"A": "Only (a), (b)", "B": "Only (a), (c)", "C": "Only (b), (c)", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B. Statements (a) and (c) are correct — a writ of prohibition is issued by a higher court to a lower court or tribunal to keep it within jurisdiction, and it lies against judicial and quasi-judicial bodies. It does not run against purely administrative agencies, so (b) drops out.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Judiciary"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27015, 'Constitutional Framework & Preamble', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Which of the following statement/s is/are incorrect? (a) B.N. Rau was advisor of the Constituent Assembly. (b) B.N. Rau prepared draft Constitution in October, 1947. (c) A draft Constitution prepared by B.N. Rau contained 310 Articles and 8 Schedules. (d) A draft Constitution prepared by B.N. Rau contained 243 Articles and 13 Schedules.', '{"A": "(a) and (c)", "B": "(b) and (c)", "C": "Only (d)", "D": "Only (c)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer here is option D. Only statement (c) is incorrect — B.N. Rau''s draft Constitution did not contain 310 Articles and 8 Schedules. His draft is placed at 243 Articles and 13 Schedules, so statement (d) is the correct figure and (c) is the flawed one.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Constitutional Framework & Preamble"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27016, 'Parliament', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Select the incorrect statement from the following:', '{"A": "The President can pardon sentences inflicted by Court Martial while the Governor cannot.", "B": "The President is bound to give reasons for pardoning power.", "C": "The petitioner for mercy has no right to an oral hearing by the President.", "D": "The pardoning power is to be exercised by the President on the advice of the Union Cabinet."}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B, because the question asks for the incorrect statement. The President is not bound to give reasons while exercising the pardoning power, so that claim is false. The other three — pardoning court-martial sentences, no right to an oral hearing, and acting on the Cabinet''s advice — are all accurate.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Parliament"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27017, 'State Government', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Who determines the remuneration of the Advocate General for the State?', '{"A": "Parliament", "B": "President", "C": "Legislative Assembly", "D": "Governor"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer here is option D. Under Article 165, the Advocate General holds office during the Governor''s pleasure and receives such remuneration as the Governor determines. So it is the Governor, not Parliament or the President, who fixes the pay.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","State Government"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27018, 'Urban Local Bodies', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Which of the following matters are included in the 12th Schedule of the Constitution of India? (a) Promotion of artistic vision, fire fighting services (b) Cremation ground and electric crematorium (c) Market & fairs, rural housing (d) Protection of the interest of the handicapped and mentally retarded, protection of the environment.', '{"A": "Only (a), (b) and (d)", "B": "Only (c) and (d)", "C": "Only (a), (b) and (c)", "D": "Only (b), (c) and (d)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A. The Twelfth Schedule subjects here include promotion of artistic vision and fire services (a), cremation grounds and electric crematoria (b), and protection of the interests of the handicapped and the environment (d). Statement (c) is the one that does not belong in this set, so (a), (b) and (d) stand.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Urban Local Bodies"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27019, 'Centre-State Relations', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Find the correct statements regarding Inter-State Council: (a) It is mentioned in Article 263. (b) The President is empowered to establish it. (c) The President of India has never exercised this power and has not so far established any such Inter-State Council under power of Article 263.', '{"A": "(a), (b), (c)", "B": "(a), (b)", "C": "(b), (c)", "D": "(a), (c)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B. Statements (a) and (b) hold — the Inter-State Council is mentioned in Article 263 and the President is empowered to establish it. Statement (c) is false, because the Council was in fact set up in 1990, so the ''never established'' claim doesn''t survive.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Centre-State Relations"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27020, 'DPSP & Fundamental Duties', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'The National Commission to review the working of the Constitution has recommended that, for effectuating fundamental duties, these are __________. (a) Duty to vote at elections (b) To pay taxes (c) Duty of industrial organisations to provide education to children of their employees (d) To foster a spirit of family values and responsible parenthood in the matter of education, physical and moral well-being of children', '{"A": "Only (a), (b)", "B": "Only (c), (d)", "C": "Only (a), (c), (d)", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through it, option A is the one. The National Commission to Review the Working of the Constitution recommended adding the duty to vote (a) and the duty to pay taxes (b) among the fundamental duties. The industrial-education and parenthood ideas in (c) and (d) were not part of that recommendation.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","DPSP & Fundamental Duties"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27021, 'Union Executive', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Which of the following statements about the Veto power of the President are correct? (a) He/she can withhold his/her assent to the bill. (b) Governor may reserve a bill for consideration of the President in any case he/she thinks fit. (c) President can return a bill to Parliament for reconsideration with a message to both houses.', '{"A": "Only (a) and (b)", "B": "Only (b) and (c)", "C": "Only (a) and (c)", "D": "(a), (b), (c)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer here is option D. All three points about the President''s veto are correct — withholding assent to a bill, the Governor reserving a bill for the President''s consideration, and the President returning a bill to Parliament with a message for reconsideration. So (a), (b) and (c) together is the answer.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Union Executive"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27022, 'Centre-State Relations', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Which of the following statement/s are correct? (a) According to K.C. Wheare, Indian Federalism is ''quasi-federal''. (b) According to Morris Jones, Indian Federalism is ''bargaining federalism''. (c) According to C.F. Strong, Indian Federalism is ''less federalism''. (d) According to Granville Austin, Indian Federalism is ''Cooperative federalism''.', '{"A": "Only (a) and (d)", "B": "Only (a), (b) and (c)", "C": "Only (a)", "D": "(a), (b), (c) and (d)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer here is option D. Each label matches its scholar — Wheare called Indian federalism ''quasi-federal'', Morris Jones ''bargaining federalism'', C.F. Strong ''less federalism'' and Granville Austin ''cooperative federalism''. Since all four descriptions are correctly attributed, everything holds.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Centre-State Relations"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27023, 'Constitutional & Statutory Bodies', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Which of the following Article of the Indian Constitution establishes the independent office of the Comptroller and Auditor General (CAG) of India?', '{"A": "Article 141", "B": "Article 144", "C": "Article 148", "D": "Article 149"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'Working through it, option C is the one. Article 148 sets up the independent office of the Comptroller and Auditor General of India. Don''t confuse it with the neighbouring articles — 149 deals with the CAG''s duties and powers, not the creation of the office.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Constitutional & Statutory Bodies"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27024, 'Constitutional Amendments', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'According to simple majority of the Parliament, which types of Constitutional Amendments shall be made? Choose the correct statement/s: (a) Establishment of new States. (b) Amendment related to President''s emoluments and allowances. (c) Amendment related to Directive Principles of State Policy. (d) Delimitation of Constituencies.', '{"A": "(a) and (c)", "B": "(c) and (d)", "C": "(a), (b) and (d)", "D": "(a), (c) and (d)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right pick is option C. Amendments made by simple majority include the formation of new states (a), changes to the President''s emoluments and allowances (b) and delimitation of constituencies (d). The DPSP amendment in (c) is not in this simple-majority basket, so (a), (b) and (d) is the set.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Constitutional Amendments"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27025, 'Constitutional Framework & Preamble', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'The provision of double citizenship to overseas citizens of India applies only to those in some specified countries. These are: (a) Finland (b) Israel (c) Republic of Cyprus (d) Portugal', '{"A": "Only (a), (b), (c)", "B": "Only (b), (c), (d)", "C": "Only (a), (c), (d)", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer here is option D. Per the key, the overseas-citizenship (double citizenship) provision applies to those in all the listed countries — Finland, Israel, Republic of Cyprus and Portugal. So ''all of the above'' is the marked choice.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Constitutional Framework & Preamble"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27026, 'Parliament', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Which of the following statement/s is incorrect about the Committee on Public Undertakings of the Parliament? (a) Pandit Nehru recommended the creation of this Committee in 1963. (b) The Chairman of this Committee is appointed only from amongst its members who are drawn from the Lok Sabha. (c) From 1974, 15 members are elected from Lok Sabha and 7 members are elected from Rajya Sabha on this Committee. (d) The tenure of members of this Committee is two years.', '{"A": "(a) and (b)", "B": "(a) and (d)", "C": "(c) and (d)", "D": "(b), (c) and (d)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B. The incorrect statements are (a) and (d): the Committee on Public Undertakings was set up in 1964 (not on a 1963 Nehru recommendation), and the tenure of its members is one year, not two. Statements (b) and (c) about its composition are accurate.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Parliament"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27027, 'International Affairs & Summits', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Who among the following became the 38th President of Chile?', '{"A": "Gabriel Boric", "B": "Sebastian Pinera", "C": "Jose Antonio Kast Rist", "D": "Ricardo Lagos"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C. Jose Antonio Kast Rist is the one recorded as the 38th President of Chile. With current-affairs ''who became'' questions, pair the name firmly with the office and number to shake off familiar distractors.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","International Affairs & Summits"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27028, 'Constitutional Framework & Preamble', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Match the correct pairs of the following articles of the Constitution of India with the subject: Subject - Articles (a) Language to be used in the complaint for redressal of grievances - (i) 350 A (b) Facilities for education in mother tongue at primary level - (ii) 351 (c) Special officer for linguistic minority communities - (iii) 350 (d) Directive for development of Hindi Language - (iv) 350 B', '{"A": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(iii), (c)-(i), (d)-(iv)", "B": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(iv), (c)-(i), (d)-(iii)", "C": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(i)", "D": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(i), (c)-(iv), (d)-(ii)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The right pick is option D. Article 350 covers the language for grievance representations (a), Article 350A the mother-tongue instruction at primary stage (b), Article 350B the special officer for linguistic minorities (c) and Article 351 the directive to develop Hindi (d). Grouping the 350 family together makes this match quick.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Constitutional Framework & Preamble"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27029, 'International Affairs & Summits', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'State the correct statements regarding Chabahar Port: (a) Chabahar port in Iran gives India direct access to Afghanistan, bypassing Pakistan. (b) Chabahar port provides a strategic counterweight to China, which has built Karachi port in Pakistan. (c) India Ports Global Limited is the special purpose vehicle created to operate and develop the Chabahar Port. (d) The 2026-27 budget has not allocated any funds for the Chabahar Port. Which of the above statements are correct?', '{"A": "(a), (b), (c) and (d)", "B": "(b), (c) and (d)", "C": "(a), (c) and (d)", "D": "(a), (b) and (c)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right pick is option C. Statements (a), (c) and (d) about Chabahar hold — it gives India access to Afghanistan bypassing Pakistan, India Ports Global Limited is the SPV running it, and the specified budget point is accurate. Statement (b) is the flaw, since China''s port project in the region is Gwadar, not Karachi.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","International Affairs & Summits"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27030, 'National Appointments & Reports', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Select the correct and incorrect statement/s from the following: (a) The 31st National Children''s Science Congress (NCSC) was held in Bhopal, Madhya Pradesh from 3rd to 6th January, 2026. (b) The 31st National Children''s Science Congress (NCSC) was held on theme "Understanding ecosystem for Health and Wellbeing".', '{"A": "(a) is correct, (b) is incorrect", "B": "(b) is correct, (a) is incorrect", "C": "Both (a) and (b) are correct", "D": "Both (a) and (b) are incorrect"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B. Statement (b) is correct — the 31st National Children''s Science Congress carried the theme on understanding the ecosystem for health and wellbeing. Statement (a) is the incorrect one, as its venue/date details do not match, so ''b correct, a incorrect'' is the fit.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","National Appointments & Reports"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27031, 'National Appointments & Reports', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Which of the following is proposed as the third new district of Goa by the Chief Minister of Goa?', '{"A": "Kushavati", "B": "Cana Cona", "C": "Dharbandora", "D": "Sanguem"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A. Kushavati is the one proposed as Goa''s third new district by the Chief Minister. When close-sounding Goan place names are offered together, go strictly with the one named in the announcement.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","National Appointments & Reports"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27032, 'Government Schemes & Yojanas', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Select the correct statements from the following about PM Dhan-Dhaanya Krishi Yojana: (a) The Union Cabinet approved the PM Dhan-Dhaanya Krishi Yojana on 16th July, 2025. (b) The scheme identifies 100 districts based on low productivity, low cropping intensity and less credit disbursement. (c) The scheme will be governed through a four-tier implementation structure.', '{"A": "Only (a), (b)", "B": "Only (b), (c)", "C": "Only (a), (c)", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A. Statements (a) and (b) are correct — the Union Cabinet approved the PM Dhan-Dhaanya Krishi Yojana on 16 July 2025, and it targets 100 districts chosen for low productivity, low cropping intensity and low credit disbursement. The four-tier structure claim in (c) does not match, so only (a) and (b) hold.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Government Schemes & Yojanas"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27033, 'National Appointments & Reports', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'According to the Economic Survey of India 2025-26: (a) An increase in immigration control across countries favoured by Indian emigrants may reduce the growth in remittances. (b) Global trade is being increasingly influenced by geopolitical alignments and economic statecraft. (c) Trade policy at the global level is driven by protectionist and retaliatory tariffs. (d) Geoeconomic factors are now critical determinants in shaping key bilateral trade patterns. Which of the above statement is/are correct?', '{"A": "(a), (b) and (c)", "B": "(a), (c) and (d)", "C": "(a) and (d)", "D": "(a), (b), (c) and (d)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer here is option D. All four observations of the Economic Survey of India 2025-26 hold — tighter immigration control can slow remittance growth, global trade is shaped by geopolitical alignments and statecraft, protectionist and retaliatory tariffs drive trade policy, and geoeconomic factors now steer bilateral trade patterns. So every statement is correct.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","National Appointments & Reports"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27034, 'Government Schemes & Yojanas', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Women Technology Parks (WTPs) have been set up in which of the following states to promote gender equality and empower women through science and technology based solutions? (a) Gujarat (b) Tamilnadu (c) Sikkim (d) Maharashtra (e) Uttar Pradesh', '{"A": "Only (b), (c), (e)", "B": "Only (a), (d), (e)", "C": "Only (a), (c), (d)", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer here is option D. Women Technology Parks have been set up in all the states listed — Gujarat, Tamilnadu, Sikkim, Maharashtra and Uttar Pradesh — to empower women through science and technology solutions. Hence ''all of the above''.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Government Schemes & Yojanas"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27035, 'Awards & Honours', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Match the pairs: (Nobel Prize, 2025) List A - List B (a) Discovery of macroscopic quantum mechanical tunnelling and energy quantisation in an electric circuit - (i) Maria Carina Machado (b) The development of metal-organic frameworks - (ii) Fred Ramsdell (c) Discoveries concerning peripheral immune tolerance - (iii) Richard Robson (d) Promoting democratic rights for the people of Venezuela - (iv) John Clarke', '{"A": "(a)-(i), (b)-(iii), (c)-(ii), (d)-(iv)", "B": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(iii), (c)-(ii), (d)-(i)", "C": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(ii), (c)-(i), (d)-(iii)", "D": "(a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iv), (d)-(iii)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Working through it, option B is the one. For the 2025 Nobel Prizes, the quantum-tunnelling-in-a-circuit work goes to John Clarke (iv), metal-organic frameworks to Richard Robson (iii), peripheral immune tolerance to Fred Ramsdell (ii) and the Venezuela democracy award to Maria Corina Machado (i). Anchoring the Peace laureate to Venezuela fixes the whole chain.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Awards & Honours"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27036, 'Sports', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'During which tenure did Shri Suresh Kalmadi hold the presidency of the ''Asian Athletics Association''?', '{"A": "1990 to 2000", "B": "1992 to 2008", "C": "1996 to 2012", "D": "2000 to 2013"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The right pick is option D. Suresh Kalmadi headed the Asian Athletics Association during the 2000 to 2013 tenure. For sports-administration questions, tie the person to the exact term of office rather than a rough decade.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Sports"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27037, 'National Appointments & Reports', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Which of the following statement/s given is/are correct? (a) The National Institutional Ranking Framework provides a methodology to rank educational institutions across the country. (b) The National Institutional Ranking Framework (NIRF) was launched in 2020. (c) The ranking is based on five parameters. (d) Indian Institute of Technology Madras tops in the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) category.', '{"A": "(a), (b) and (c)", "B": "(a), (b) and (d)", "C": "(b), (c) and (d)", "D": "(a), (c) and (d)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer here is option D. Statements (a), (c) and (d) hold — NIRF provides a methodology to rank institutions nationwide, the ranking rests on five parameters, and IIT Madras tops the SDG category. Statement (b) is the slip, since NIRF was launched in 2015, not 2020, so (a), (c) and (d) is correct.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","National Appointments & Reports"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27038, 'Art, Literature & Culture', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Arrange the classical languages of India in an appropriate order as per their recognition: (a) Telugu (b) Sanskrit (c) Pali (d) Odia (e) Tamil', '{"A": "(d), (e), (a), (b), (c)", "B": "(a), (e), (b), (c), (d)", "C": "(b), (a), (e), (d), (c)", "D": "(e), (b), (a), (d), (c)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer here is option D. By order of classical-language recognition, Tamil came first (e), then Sanskrit (b), Telugu (a), Odia (d) and Pali (c). Anchoring Tamil as the earliest recognised classical language fixes the whole sequence.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Art, Literature & Culture"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27039, 'Sports', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'How many gold, silver and bronze medals did India secure at the ''World Para Athletics Grand Prix 2026'', New Delhi?', '{"A": "Gold - 64, Silver - 69, Bronze - 75", "B": "Gold - 75, Silver - 69, Bronze - 64", "C": "Gold - 75, Silver - 64, Bronze - 69", "D": "Gold - 69, Silver - 75, Bronze - 64"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B. At the World Para Athletics Grand Prix 2026 in New Delhi, India secured 75 gold, 69 silver and 64 bronze. Note that gold outnumbers silver and silver outnumbers bronze here — a quick check against the swapped options.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Sports"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27040, 'Constitutional Development (British Acts)', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'ब्रिटीश इंडियन असोसिएशन या संस्थेने इ.स. 1853 मध्ये चार्टर कायद्याच्या नूतनीकरण प्रसंगी संसदेकडे कोणत्या मागण्या केल्या होत्या? (a) कायदेमंडळ, कार्यकारी मंडळ व न्यायमंडळ यांचे कार्यक्षेत्र स्वतंत्र असावे. (b) मोठमोठ्या उच्च पदांचे वेतन कमी करण्यात यावे. (c) नव्या कायदेमंडळाची निर्मिती करून त्यात भारतीयांना प्रतिनिधीत्व द्यावे. (d) मीठ, अबकारी व मुद्रा कर समाप्त करण्यात यावा.', '{"A": "फक्त (a) आणि (d)", "B": "(a), (b) आणि (d)", "C": "(a), (b) आणि (c)", "D": "वरीलपैकी कोणतेही नाही"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'इथे बरोबर पर्याय B आहे. 1853 मध्ये चार्टर कायद्याच्या नूतनीकरणाच्या वेळी ब्रिटीश इंडियन असोसिएशनने कायदेमंडळ, कार्यकारी व न्यायमंडळ यांचे कार्यक्षेत्र वेगळे असावे, उच्च पदांचे वेतन कमी करावे आणि मीठ, अबकारी व मुद्रा कर रद्द करावेत अशा मागण्या केल्या — म्हणजेच (a), (b) व (d). नव्या कायदेमंडळात भारतीयांना प्रतिनिधित्व (c) ही मागणी या निवेदनात नव्हती, आणि नेमका तोच इतर पर्यायांतला सापळा आहे.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Constitutional Development (British Acts)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27041, 'Rise of Nationalism & INC', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'इ.स. 1940 मधील ऑगस्ट प्रस्तावात खालीलपैकी कोणत्या तरतुदी होत्या? (a) दुसरे महायुद्ध संपल्यानंतर भारतात वसाहतीच्या धर्तीची पूर्णपणे जबाबदार शासन व्यवस्था स्थापण्यास मदत केली जाईल. (b) गव्हर्नर जनरलच्या मंडळात आणखी काही भारतीयांचा समावेश केला जाईल.', '{"A": "पर्याय (a) योग्य व पर्याय (b) चुकीचा आहे.", "B": "पर्याय (b) योग्य व पर्याय (a) चुकीचा आहे.", "C": "दोन्ही तरतुदी बरोबर आहेत.", "D": "दोन्ही तरतुदी चुकीच्या आहेत."}'::jsonb, 'C', 'इथले पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय C आहे. 1940 च्या ऑगस्ट प्रस्तावात दोन्ही तरतुदी होत्या — युद्धानंतर भारतात वसाहतीच्या धर्तीवर पूर्णपणे जबाबदार शासन उभे करण्यास मदत (a), आणि गव्हर्नर जनरलच्या मंडळात आणखी भारतीयांचा समावेश (b). दोन्ही विधाने बिनचूक असल्याने ''दोन्ही तरतुदी बरोबर'' हेच योग्य ठरते.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Rise of Nationalism & INC"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27042, 'National Appointments & Reports', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Which of the following statement/s are correct? (a) The Global Multidimensional Poverty Index report is released by World Bank. (b) The 2025 report is focused on the relationship between poverty & climate change. (c) The 2025 report examines four key climate hazards: high heat, drought, flood & air pollution. (d) The report states that poverty in South Asia has greatly increased.', '{"A": "(a), (b), (c) and (d)", "B": "(a), (b) and (c)", "C": "(b), (c) and (d)", "D": "(b) and (c)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer here is option D. Statements (b) and (c) are correct — the 2025 report centres on the poverty–climate change link and examines four key climate hazards: high heat, drought, flood and air pollution. Statement (a) is wrong (the Global MPI is published by UNDP and OPHI, not the World Bank) and (d) overstates the finding, so only (b) and (c) stand.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","National Appointments & Reports"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27043, 'International Affairs & Summits', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'The flagship priorities of Brazil''s BRICS Chairship, 2025 include the following: (a) Global Health Cooperation (b) Climate change (c) Promotion of women''s emancipation (d) Reform of the Multilateral System (e) Trade, Investment and Finance', '{"A": "Only (a), (c), (d)", "B": "Only (b), (d), (e)", "C": "Only (a), (b), (e)", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right pick is option C. Brazil''s BRICS Chairship 2025 flagged Global Health Cooperation (a), Climate change (b) and Trade, Investment and Finance (e) among its priorities. The women''s-emancipation and multilateral-reform items in (c) and (d) are not on that flagship list, so (a), (b) and (e) is the set.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","International Affairs & Summits"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27044, 'Art, Literature & Culture', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'योग्य जोड्या जुळवा: सूची I - सूची II (a) हर्षचरित्र - (i) कालिदास (b) मालती माधव - (ii) विशाखादत्त (c) मालविकाग्निमित्र - (iii) बाणभट्ट (d) मुद्राराक्षस - (iv) भवभूती', '{"A": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(iv), (c)-(i), (d)-(ii)", "B": "(a)-(i), (b)-(iii), (c)-(ii), (d)-(iv)", "C": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iv), (d)-(i)", "D": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(i), (c)-(iii), (d)-(ii)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय A येतो. हर्षचरित्र बाणभट्टाचे (iii), मालती माधव भवभूतीचे (iv), मालविकाग्निमित्र कालिदासाचे (i) आणि मुद्राराक्षस विशाखादत्ताचे (ii). ज्या एका लेखकाबद्दल खात्री आहे — कालिदास किंवा विशाखादत्त — तो निश्चित केला की चुकीचे संच पटकन बाद करता येतात.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Art, Literature & Culture"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27045, 'National Appointments & Reports', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'Which state has become the first Indian state to constitute its 8th State Pay Commission, ahead of the January 1, 2026 expiry of the 7th Pay Commission?', '{"A": "Nagaland", "B": "Meghalaya", "C": "Manipur", "D": "Assam"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The right pick is option D. Assam became the first Indian state to constitute its 8th State Pay Commission ahead of the 7th Pay Commission''s 1 January 2026 expiry. Tag the ''first state'' fact to Assam to keep it distinct from the other north-eastern options.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","National Appointments & Reports"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27046, 'Medieval India', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'अदिलशाहचा वजीर हेमूच्या बाबतीत लागू असलेली विधाने कोणती? (a) अदिलशाह याने हेमू यास ''विक्रमाजीत'' ही उपाधी दिली होती. (b) हेमूने आपल्या कारकीर्दीचा प्रारंभ बाजार अधिक्षक म्हणून केला. (c) हेमू 22 लढायांपैकी एकही लढाई पराभूत झाला नव्हता. (d) हेमूने पानीपतच्या दुसऱ्या लढाईत अकबरावर विजय मिळविला.', '{"A": "फक्त (a), (b) आणि (c)", "B": "फक्त (a), (c) आणि (d)", "C": "फक्त (a) आणि (c)", "D": "फक्त (a), (b) आणि (d)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'थेट उत्तराकडे — पर्याय A. हेमूबाबत (a), (b) व (c) ही विधाने बरोबर आहेत: अदिलशाहने त्याला ''विक्रमाजीत'' उपाधी दिली, त्याने कारकीर्दीची सुरुवात बाजार अधिक्षक म्हणून केली आणि 22 लढायांत तो अपराजित राहिला. (d) मात्र चुकीचे, कारण पानीपतच्या दुसऱ्या लढाईत (1556) हेमूचा पराभव झाला होता, विजय नव्हे.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Medieval India"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27047, 'Medieval India', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'लेखकांच्या योग्य जोड्या जुळवा: सूची I - सूची II (a) स्टोरिआ-द-मोगोर - (i) बर्नियर (b) ट्रॅव्हल-इन-मुघल एम्पायर - (ii) निकोलाओ मनुची (c) अर्ली ट्रॅव्हल इन इंडिया - (iii) विल्यम फॉस्टर (d) हिस्टॉरिकल फ्रॅग्मेंट - (iv) रॉबर्ट', '{"A": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(iii), (c)-(i), (d)-(iv)", "B": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(i), (c)-(iii), (d)-(iv)", "C": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iv), (d)-(i)", "D": "(a)-(i), (b)-(iii), (c)-(ii), (d)-(iv)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'परीक्षकाने पर्याय B निवडला आहे. स्टोरिआ-द-मोगोर निकोलाओ मनुचीचे (ii), ट्रॅव्हल्स इन मुघल एम्पायर बर्नियरचे (i), अर्ली ट्रॅव्हल्स इन इंडिया विल्यम फॉस्टरचे (iii) आणि हिस्टॉरिकल फ्रॅग्मेंट रॉबर्टचे (iv). प्रवासवर्णनांचे लेखक हा MPSC चा आवडता विषय आहे, त्यामुळे जोड्यांच्या स्वरूपात लक्षात ठेवणे फायद्याचे.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Medieval India"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27048, 'Minerals & Industries', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'पुढील जोड्या जुळवा: सूची I - सूची II (a) सिंद्री - (i) खताचा कारखाना (b) चित्तरंजन - (ii) रेल्वे डब्यांचा कारखाना (c) पेरांबूर - (iii) रेल्वे इंजीनांचा कारखाना (d) पिंपरी - (iv) पेनीसिलीनचा कारखाना', '{"A": "(a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(iv)", "B": "(a)-(i), (b)-(iii), (c)-(ii), (d)-(iv)", "C": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(i), (c)-(iv), (d)-(iii)", "D": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(iii), (c)-(ii), (d)-(i)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय B आहे. सिंद्री हा खताचा कारखाना (i), चित्तरंजन रेल्वे इंजिनांचा कारखाना (iii), पेरांबूर रेल्वे डब्यांचा कारखाना (ii) आणि पिंपरी पेनिसिलीन (प्रतिजैविक) कारखाना (iv). ठिकाण–उद्योग अशा जोड्या म्हणजे शुद्ध पाठांतराचे गुण — उजळणी करताना क्षेत्रानुसार गटवार लक्षात ठेवाव्यात.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Minerals & Industries"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27049, 'Ancient India', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'पुढील जोड्या जुळवा: सूची I - सूची II (a) वराहमिहीर - (i) पंचसिद्धांतिका (b) वाग्भट्ट - (ii) अष्टांग संग्रह (c) ईश्वरकृष्ण - (iii) सांख्य कारीका (d) प्रसतपद - (iv) वैशेषीक सुत्र', '{"A": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(i), (c)-(iv), (d)-(iii)", "B": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(iii), (c)-(ii), (d)-(i)", "C": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(iv), (c)-(i), (d)-(ii)", "D": "(a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(iv)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'बरोबर पर्याय D आहे. वराहमिहीरने पंचसिद्धांतिका (i), वाग्भट्टाने अष्टांग संग्रह (ii), ईश्वरकृष्णाने सांख्य कारिका (iii) आणि प्रशस्तपादाने वैशेषिक सूत्रावरील ग्रंथ (iv) लिहिला — अगदी क्रमवार जोडी. अशी क्रमवार जोडी दिसली की ती मुद्दाम नीटनेटकी दिसणारी फसवणूक नाही ना, हे एकदा तपासावे.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Ancient India"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27050, 'Art, Literature & Culture', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'पुढील मुघलकालीन भारतातील संस्कृत लेखक आणि त्यांचे ग्रंथ यांच्या जोड्या जुळवा: सूची I - सूची II (a) अनंतदेव - (i) चैतन्य चरितामृतम् (b) गंगाधर - (ii) निर्णय सिंधू (c) कमलाकर भट्ट - (iii) मनोरमा (d) कृष्णदास कवीराज - (iv) संस्कारकौस्तुभ', '{"A": "(a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(iv)", "B": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(iii), (c)-(ii), (d)-(i)", "C": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(i), (c)-(iv), (d)-(iii)", "D": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(iv), (c)-(ii), (d)-(i)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय B येतो. मुघलकालीन या संस्कृत विद्वानांपैकी अनंतदेव–संस्कारकौस्तुभ (iv), गंगाधर–मनोरमा (iii), कमलाकर भट्ट–निर्णय सिंधू (ii) आणि कृष्णदास कवीराज–चैतन्य चरितामृत (i). कृष्णदास कवीराज–चैतन्य चरितामृत ही जोडी सर्वात पक्की, तिथूनच बाद करायला सुरुवात करावी.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Art, Literature & Culture"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (27051, 'Climatology', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'हवामान अभ्यासक, आर.एल. सिंग (1971) यांनी भारताच्या हवामान प्रदेशाची किती क्षेत्रांत विभागणी केली?', '{"A": "सात", "B": "आठ", "C": "नऊ", "D": "दहा"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय D आहे. आर.एल. सिंग यांच्या 1971 च्या वर्गीकरणात भारताचे हवामान दहा प्रदेशांत विभागले जाते. अशा संख्यात्मक तथ्यांसाठी झटपट फ्लॅशकार्ड उपयोगी — आर.एल. सिंग = दहा हवामान प्रदेश.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Climatology"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27052, 'Maharashtra in Freedom Struggle', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'भुसावळ बॉम्ब खटल्यात खालीलपैकी कोणास पकडण्यात आले होते?', '{"A": "सदाशिव मलकापूरकर", "B": "विश्वनाथ वैशंपायन", "C": "बापूसाहेब सहस्त्रबुद्धे", "D": "गजानन पोतदार"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'बरोबर पर्याय A आहे. भुसावळ बॉम्ब खटल्यातील अटकेशी सदाशिव मलकापूरकर हे नाव जोडले जाते. एकनाम प्रकारच्या तथ्यात्मक प्रश्नात प्रसिद्ध वाटणाऱ्या पर्यायांच्या मागे न लागता, स्रोतात प्रत्यक्ष वाचलेला पर्यायच निवडावा.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Maharashtra in Freedom Struggle"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27053, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'इ.स. 1864 मध्ये __________ या संस्कृत विद्वानाने व कट्टर समाज सुधारकाने समाज सुधारणांच्या कार्यास वाहून घेण्यासाठी सरकारी सेवेचा राजीनामा दिला.', '{"A": "म.गो. रानडे", "B": "विष्णुशास्त्री पंडीत", "C": "बाळशास्त्री जांभेकर", "D": "का.त्र्यं. तेलंग"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'थेट उत्तराकडे — पर्याय B. विष्णुशास्त्री पंडीत या संस्कृत विद्वानाने व कट्टर समाजसुधारकाने 1864 मध्ये सरकारी नोकरी सोडून, विशेषतः विधवा पुनर्विवाहाच्या, समाजसुधारणेला वाहून घेतले. 1864 हे वर्ष त्यांच्यासाठी झटपट खूण म्हणून लक्षात ठेवा.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27054, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'पुढील वाक्यात वर्णन केलेले समाजसुधारक ओळखा: (a) आपण जे शिकवतो ते आचरणात आणण्याचे धैर्य त्यांनी दाखवले. (b) ते स्त्री शिक्षणाचे कट्टर समर्थक होते. (c) ते बालविवाहाच्या विरोधात होते; त्यांनी त्यांच्या मुलांचे व मुलींचे विवाह ते त्यांचा जोडीदार निवडण्यास समर्थ झाले तेव्हाच केले. (d) त्यांनी विधवा पुनर्विवाहाचे समर्थन केले, त्यांनी त्यांच्या विधवा मुलीच्या पुनर्विवाहाला संमती दिली होती.', '{"A": "न्यायमूर्ती का.त्र्यं. तेलंग", "B": "रा.गो. भांडारकर", "C": "वा.आ. मोडक", "D": "न्यायमूर्ती म.गो. रानडे"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'बरोबर पर्याय B आहे. जे शिकवले ते आचरणात आणण्याचे धैर्य, स्त्री शिक्षणाचे कट्टर समर्थन, मुलांचे विवाह ती जोडीदार निवडण्याइतकी सक्षम झाल्यावरच करणे आणि विधवा मुलीच्या पुनर्विवाहाला संमती — हे सर्व संकेत रा.गो. भांडारकर यांच्याकडे बोट दाखवतात. वर्णनात्मक प्रश्नात प्रत्येक संकेत वाचा; एखादी ओळ जवळचे नाव बाद करते.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27055, 'Medieval India', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'जोड्या जुळवा: सूची I - सूची II (a) जियाउद्दीन बरनी - (i) फतूह-उस-सलातीन (b) ख्वाजा अबू मलीक इसामी - (ii) किताब-उर-रहलह (c) इब्न बतूता - (iii) तारीख-ए-सलातीन अफगाणा (d) अहमद यादगार - (iv) फतवा-ए-जहाँदरी', '{"A": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(i), (c)-(ii), (d)-(iii)", "B": "(a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(iv)", "C": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(iii), (c)-(iv), (d)-(i)", "D": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(iv), (c)-(i), (d)-(ii)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय A येतो. जियाउद्दीन बरनीने फतवा-ए-जहाँदरी (iv), इसामीने फुतूह-उस-सलातीन (i), इब्न बतूताने किताब-उर-रहला (ii) आणि अहमद यादगारने तारीख-ए-सलातीन-ए-अफगाणा (iii) लिहिले. इब्न बतूता–रहला ही खात्रीशीर जोडी आधार म्हणून घ्या.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Medieval India"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27056, 'Minerals & Industries', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'खालील विधाने पहा: (a) राज्य खनिज धोरण 1999 प्रमाणे लोह, गंधक, सोने, तांबे आणि शिसे खनिज उत्पादनासाठी खाजगी क्षेत्रांना खुली करण्यात आली. (b) नागपूर विभागानंतर सर्वात जास्त खनिज उपलब्धता कोकण विभागात आहे. (c) महाराष्ट्र राज्य खाण महामंडळाची स्थापना 1973 मध्ये केली.', '{"A": "फक्त विधान (b) बरोबर आहे.", "B": "विधाने (b) आणि (c) बरोबर आहेत.", "C": "विधाने (a), (b) आणि (c) बरोबर आहेत.", "D": "विधाने (a) आणि (b) बरोबर नाहीत."}'::jsonb, 'C', 'थेट उत्तराकडे — पर्याय C. तिन्ही विधाने बरोबर आहेत: 1999 च्या राज्य खनिज धोरणाने लोह, गंधक, सोने, तांबे व शिसे खाजगी क्षेत्राला खुले केले, खनिज उपलब्धतेत नागपूरनंतर कोकण विभाग येतो आणि महाराष्ट्र राज्य खाण महामंडळाची स्थापना 1973 मध्ये झाली. प्रत्येक विधान स्वतंत्रपणे बरोबर असल्याने ''सर्व बरोबर'' हाच प्रामाणिक पर्याय.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Minerals & Industries"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27057, 'Ancient India', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'पुढील राजघराणी आणि त्यांची राज्ये यांच्या जोड्या जुळवा: सूची I - सूची II (a) मैत्रक - (i) वल्लभी (b) चहुमान - (ii) शाकंभरी (c) गुर्जर - (iii) भ्रोच (d) परमार - (iv) धार', '{"A": "(a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(iv)", "B": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(iii), (c)-(ii), (d)-(i)", "C": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(iv), (c)-(ii), (d)-(i)", "D": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(i), (c)-(iv), (d)-(iii)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'बरोबर पर्याय A आहे. मैत्रकांचे राज्य वल्लभी (i), चहुमानांचे शाकंभरी (ii), गुर्जरांचे भ्रोच (iii) आणि परमारांचे धार (iv) येथे होते. प्राचीन राजघराण्यांच्या राजधान्या हे हमखास गुण देणारे मुद्दे — प्रत्येक घराणे त्याच्या सत्ताकेंद्राशी जोडा.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Ancient India"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27058, 'Maharashtra Physical Geography', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'महाराष्ट्रातील खालील वनपरिमंडळे आणि त्यांची महाराष्ट्रातील एकूण वनक्षेत्राशी असणारी टक्केवारी यांच्या जोड्या लावा: महाराष्ट्रातील वनपरिमंडळे - एकूण वनक्षेत्राशी टक्केवारी (महाराष्ट्राची आर्थिक पाहणी 2024) (a) गडचिरोली - (i) 12.5 (b) नागपूर - (ii) 20.8 (c) धुळे - (iii) 9.5 (d) ठाणे - (iv) 10.4', '{"A": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(i), (c)-(iv), (d)-(iii)", "B": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(i), (c)-(iii), (d)-(ii)", "C": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iv), (d)-(i)", "D": "(a)-(i), (b)-(iii), (c)-(ii), (d)-(iv)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'बरोबर पर्याय A आहे. महाराष्ट्राची आर्थिक पाहणी 2024 नुसार गडचिरोलीचा वाटा 20.8% (ii), नागपूर 12.5% (i), धुळे 10.4% (iv) आणि ठाणे 9.5% (iii). टक्केवारीच्या जोड्यांत आधी सर्वात मोठा आकडा निश्चित करा — इथे 20.8% गडचिरोलीला — मग बाकीच्या जोड्या आपोआप जुळतात.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Maharashtra Physical Geography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27059, 'Panchayati Raj', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'दिनांक 9 ऑक्टोबर, 2024 रोजीच्या शासन निर्णयानुसार बंजारा/लमाण/लभाण तांडा भागासाठी ग्रामपंचायत स्थापन करण्यासाठी किमान किती लोकसंख्या आवश्यक आहे?', '{"A": "600", "B": "700", "C": "800", "D": "900"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय B आहे. 9 ऑक्टोबर 2024 च्या शासन निर्णयानुसार बंजारा / लमाण / लभाण तांडा भागात ग्रामपंचायत स्थापनेसाठी किमान लोकसंख्या 700 निश्चित केली आहे. शासन निर्णयातील आकडे हे चालू घडामोडींचे हुकमी मुद्दे — तारीख आणि आकडा एकत्र लक्षात ठेवा.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Panchayati Raj"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27060, 'Geomorphology & Physical Geography', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'पुढील विधाने विचारात घ्या: (a) अरवली हा जगातील सर्वात तरूण वली पर्वत आहे. (b) अरवली हा पर्वत संगमरवर, ग्रॅनाइट, जस्त आणि तांबे यांसारख्या खनिजांनी समृद्ध आहे. (c) या पर्वतरांगांनी शतकानुशतके खाणकाम आणि बांधकाम व्यवसायांना आधार दिला आहे. (d) चित्तोडगड, कुंभलगड आणि रणथंबोर यांसारखे ऐतिहासिक किल्ले या पर्वतरांगेत आहेत.', '{"A": "फक्त विधान (a) बरोबर आहे.", "B": "विधाने (a) आणि (b) बरोबर आहेत.", "C": "विधाने (b) आणि (c) बरोबर आहेत.", "D": "विधाने (b), (c) आणि (d) बरोबर आहेत."}'::jsonb, 'D', 'परीक्षकाने पर्याय D निवडला आहे. अरवलीबाबत (b), (c) व (d) ही विधाने बरोबर — संगमरवर, ग्रॅनाइट, जस्त व तांबे यांनी समृद्ध; शतकानुशतके खाणकाम व बांधकामाचा आधार; आणि चित्तोडगड, कुंभलगड व रणथंबोरसारखे किल्ले येथेच. (a) मात्र चुकीचे, कारण अरवली हा सर्वात जुन्या वली पर्वतांपैकी आहे, तरूण नव्हे.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Geomorphology & Physical Geography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27061, 'Ancient India', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'कालमापन प्रक्रियेमध्ये ''कालांतर संस्कार'' ही प्रक्रिया कशासाठी वापरली जाते? (a) लीप इयर (b) अधिक मास (c) क्षय मास (d) तिथी वृद्धी-लोप', '{"A": "(b) आणि (c)", "B": "(c) आणि (d)", "C": "फक्त (a)", "D": "(a), (b), (c), (d)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय D येतो. कालमापनात ''कालांतर संस्कार'' हे सुधारण या सर्वांसाठी लावले जाते — लीप इयर, अधिक मास, क्षय मास आणि तिथी वृद्धी–लोप. यादीतील प्रत्येक घटक ही प्रक्रिया वापरतो, त्यामुळे (a), (b), (c), (d) हाच प्रामाणिक पर्याय.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Ancient India"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27062, 'Agriculture Economy', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'भारतामध्ये तांदूळ आणि गव्हाचे प्रति हेक्टरी उत्पन्न 2023-2024 वर्षात किती होते?', '{"A": "3282 आणि 4559 कि.ग्रा.", "B": "2681 आणि 3460 कि.ग्रा.", "C": "2882 आणि 3559 कि.ग्रा.", "D": "2581 आणि 3259 कि.ग्रा."}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय C आहे. भारतात 2023-24 मध्ये प्रति हेक्टरी उत्पन्न तांदळासाठी 2882 कि.ग्रा. व गव्हासाठी 3559 कि.ग्रा. आहे. पर्याय मुद्दाम जवळचे आहेत, त्यामुळे अंदाजापेक्षा उजळणी केलेल्या नेमक्या आकड्यांवर विश्वास ठेवा.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Agriculture Economy"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27063, 'Medieval India', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'सुफी संप्रदायातील साधनेत कोणत्या तीन विशेष क्रियांचा समावेश होतो?', '{"A": "मुजाहदा, वस्ल, फना", "B": "जिक्र, मराकबह, तवज्जूह", "C": "फना, जिक्र, मुजाहदा", "D": "मुजाहदा, जिक्र, मराकबह"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'परीक्षकाने पर्याय D निवडला आहे. सुफी साधनेतील तीन विशेष क्रिया म्हणजे मुजाहदा, जिक्र आणि मराकबह. इतर पर्यायांत वस्ल व तवज्जूह असे शब्द मिसळून संच धूसर केला आहे, त्यामुळे ही त्रयी पक्की करा.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Medieval India"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27064, 'Indian Physical Geography', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'हिमालयाचे प्रादेशिक विभाग (यादी-I) आणि त्यांचा पश्चिम-पूर्व विस्तार (यादी-II) यांच्या जोड्या लावा: यादी-I (हिमालयाचे प्रादेशिक विभाग) - यादी-II (पश्चिम-पूर्व विस्तार) (a) पंजाब हिमालय - (i) सतलज ते काली (b) कुमाऊँ हिमालय - (ii) काली ते तिस्ता (c) नेपाळ हिमालय - (iii) तिस्ता ते ब्रह्मपुत्रा (d) आसाम हिमालय - (iv) सिंधू ते सतलज', '{"A": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(i), (c)-(ii), (d)-(iii)", "B": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(iii), (c)-(iv), (d)-(i)", "C": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iv), (d)-(i)", "D": "(a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(iv)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'थेट उत्तराकडे — पर्याय A. पश्चिमेकडून पूर्वेकडे: पंजाब हिमालय सिंधू ते सतलज (iv), कुमाऊँ सतलज ते काली (i), नेपाळ काली ते तिस्ता (ii) आणि आसाम तिस्ता ते ब्रह्मपुत्रा (iii). नद्या डावीकडून उजवीकडे रेखल्या की क्रम आपोआप लागतो.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Indian Physical Geography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27065, 'Climatology', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'पृथ्वीच्या पृष्ठ भागापासून खालील वातावरणीय थरांचा योग्य चढता क्रम शोधा: (a) मध्यांबर (b) थर्मोस्फिअर (c) तपांबर (d) स्थितसतब्धी (e) स्थितांबर (f) मध्यसतब्धी (g) तपसतब्धी', '{"A": "(g), (c), (d), (e), (b), (f), (a)", "B": "(a), (f), (b), (g), (c), (d), (e)", "C": "(c), (g), (e), (d), (a), (f), (b)", "D": "(e), (d), (a), (g), (c), (b), (f)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'बरोबर पर्याय C आहे. पृष्ठभागापासून वर जाताना थर असे येतात — तपांबर (c), तपसतब्धी (g), स्थितांबर (e), स्थितसतब्धी (d), मध्यांबर (a), मध्यसतब्धी (f) आणि थर्मोस्फिअर (b). मुद्दा हा की प्रत्येक ''अंबर'' नंतर त्याची ''सतब्धी'' येते आणि मग पुढचा थर सुरू होतो.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Climatology"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27066, 'Environmental Laws & Conventions', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'खालीलपैकी कोणते/ती विधान/ने माँट्रीयल कराराशी संबंधित आहे/त? (a) ओझोन थराचा ऱ्हास थांबविण्यासाठी क्लोरो-फ्ल्युरोकार्बनची निर्मिती व वापर कमी करणे. (b) पृथ्वी आणि तिच्या पर्यावरणाच्या संरक्षणासाठी परिस्थितीकी संतुलन व जैवविविधता समृद्ध करण्यासाठी कार्य करणे. (c) ध्रुवातील प्रदुषणाचा अभ्यास.', '{"A": "फक्त (a)", "B": "फक्त (b)", "C": "(a) आणि (c)", "D": "वरील सर्व"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'थेट उत्तराकडे — पर्याय A. माँट्रीयल करार नेमका ओझोन थराच्या रक्षणासाठी क्लोरो-फ्ल्युरोकार्बन (CFC) चे उत्पादन व वापर कमी करण्याबाबत आहे — म्हणजेच फक्त विधान (a). व्यापक पर्यावरण रक्षण (b) व ध्रुवीय प्रदूषण अभ्यास (c) हे इतर करारांचे विषय आहेत, या कराराचे नव्हे.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Environmental Laws & Conventions"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27067, 'Population & Census', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'जोड्या लावा: यादी-I (जिल्हे) - यादी-II (लोकसंख्येतील 2001-2011 मधील दशवार्षिक वाढ (%)) (a) ठाणे - (i) 25.50 (b) छत्रपती संभाजीनगर - (ii) 30.4 (c) पुणे - (iii) 27.33 (d) नंदूरबार - (iv) 35.94', '{"A": "(a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iv), (d)-(iii)", "B": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(iii), (c)-(ii), (d)-(i)", "C": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(i), (c)-(iv), (d)-(iii)", "D": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(iv), (c)-(i), (d)-(ii)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय B येतो. 2001-2011 दशवार्षिक वाढीत ठाणे 35.94% (iv), छत्रपती संभाजीनगर 27.33% (iii), पुणे 30.4% (ii) आणि नंदूरबार 25.50% (i). सर्वाधिक वाढ ठाण्याला जोडली की बाकीच्या जोड्या सहज बसतात.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Population & Census"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27068, 'Ecology & Ecosystems', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'प्रतिपादन (A): परिसंस्था ही नैसर्गिक संसाधन प्रणाली आहे. कारण (R): परिसंस्था ही एकल संकल्पना असून भौतिक पर्यावरण (भौतिक आणि अजैविक घटक) आणि जैविक घटक (मानव, प्राणी, सूक्ष्मजीव आणि वनस्पती) एकाच चौकटीत एकत्र राहतात. खालीलपैकी कोणते बरोबर आहे?', '{"A": "दोन्ही, (A) व (R) अचूक असून (R) हे (A) चे योग्य स्पष्टीकरण आहे.", "B": "दोन्ही, (A) व (R) अचूक आहेत, परंतु (R) हे (A) चे अचूक स्पष्टीकरण नाही.", "C": "(A) अचूक आहे, परंतु (R) हे चूक आहे.", "D": "(A) चूक आहे, परंतु (R) हे अचूक आहे."}'::jsonb, 'A', 'बरोबर पर्याय A आहे. प्रतिपादन व कारण दोन्ही बरोबर असून कारण हे प्रतिपादनाचे खरे स्पष्टीकरण देते: परिसंस्था ही नैसर्गिक संसाधन प्रणाली आहे कारण ती भौतिक पर्यावरण व जैविक घटक एकाच कार्यचौकटीत बांधते. जेव्हा R हे A मागचे ''का'' थेट सांगते, तेव्हा हाच पर्याय निवडावा.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Ecology & Ecosystems"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27069, 'World Geography & Locations', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'जोड्या लावा: यादी I (देश) - यादी-II (स्थलांतरित शेतीची स्थानिक नावे) (a) कांगो व मध्य आफ्रिका - (i) रोका (b) ईशान्य भारत - (ii) मासोले (c) व्हिएतनाम - (iii) झूम (d) ब्राझील - (iv) रे', '{"A": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(i), (c)-(iv), (d)-(iii)", "B": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(iii), (c)-(iv), (d)-(i)", "C": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(iv), (c)-(i), (d)-(ii)", "D": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(i)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'परीक्षकाने पर्याय B निवडला आहे. स्थलांतरित शेतीची स्थानिक नावे — कांगो व मध्य आफ्रिकेत मासोले (ii), ईशान्य भारतात झूम (iii), व्हिएतनाममध्ये रे (iv) आणि ब्राझीलमध्ये रोका (i). ईशान्य भारतासाठी झूम ही बहुतेकांना माहीत असलेली खूण.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","World Geography & Locations"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27070, 'Environmental Laws & Conventions', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'खालीलपैकी कोणते विधान/ने बरोबर नाही/त? (a) 1992 मध्ये माँट्रीयल येथे पर्यावरण आणि विकास विषयक संयुक्त राष्ट्र परिषद आयोजित करण्यात आली होती. (b) 1987 चा ब्रंटलँड अहवाल नैरोबी येथील संयुक्त राष्ट्रांच्या दुसऱ्या परिषदेशी संबंधित आहे. (c) मानव निर्मित हवामान बदलाच्या समस्यांचे निराकरण करणे हा क्योटो प्रोटोकॉलचा उद्देश होता.', '{"A": "फक्त विधान (a)", "B": "फक्त विधान (b)", "C": "विधान (a) आणि (b)", "D": "विधान (a), (b) आणि (c)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'परीक्षकाने पर्याय C निवडला आहे. विधाने (a) व (b) चुकीची: 1992 ची पर्यावरण व विकास परिषद रिओ दी जानेरो येथे झाली, माँट्रीयल येथे नव्हे, आणि 1987 चा ब्रंटलँड अहवाल नैरोबी दुसऱ्या परिषदेशी संबंधित नव्हता. क्योटो प्रोटोकॉलच्या उद्देशाबाबत विधान (c) बरोबर आहे, म्हणून फक्त (a) व (b) चुकीची.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Environmental Laws & Conventions"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27071, 'Climate Change & Global Warming', 'General Studies', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'खालील प्रमुख हरितगृह वायूंना त्यांच्या जागतिक तापमान वाढीस कारणीभूत असणाऱ्या टक्केवारीनुसार उतरता क्रम लावा:', '{"A": "कार्बन डायऑक्साईड, मिथेन, नायट्रस ऑक्साईड, फ्लोरिनेटेड वायू", "B": "कार्बन डायऑक्साईड, मिथेन, फ्लोरिनेटेड वायू, नायट्रस ऑक्साईड", "C": "मिथेन, कार्बन डायऑक्साईड, नायट्रस ऑक्साईड, फ्लोरिनेटेड वायू", "D": "मिथेन, नायट्रस ऑक्साईड, फ्लोरिनेटेड वायू, कार्बन डायऑक्साईड"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय A आहे. जागतिक तापमानवाढीतील वाट्यानुसार उतरता क्रम — कार्बन डायऑक्साईड, मिथेन, नायट्रस ऑक्साईड आणि मग फ्लोरिनेटेड वायू. CO2 आघाडीवर व फ्लोरिनेटेड वायू शेवटी, ही खूण इतर क्रम बाद करते.', '{"General Studies","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Climate Change & Global Warming"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27072, 'Medieval India', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'गावातील शेतजमीनी गावातील समुदायांच्या संयुक्त मालकिच्या होत्या आणि जमीन महसूल भरण्याची जबाबदारी सदस्यावर संयुक्तपणे होती. ही पद्धत काय होती?', '{"A": "जमीनदारी", "B": "महालवारी", "C": "पटवारी", "D": "रयतवारी"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'बरोबर पर्याय B आहे. गावातील जमिनी समुदायाच्या संयुक्त मालकीच्या आणि जमीन महसुलाची जबाबदारी सदस्यांवर संयुक्तपणे — ही व्यवस्था म्हणजे महालवारी पद्धत. जमीनदारी (जमीनदारांमार्फत) व रयतवारी (वैयक्तिक शेतकरी) यांच्याशी तुलना केल्यास गोंधळ टळतो.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Medieval India"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27073, 'Other', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'मातृत्व लाभ अधिनियम 1961 अंतर्गत, बाळंतपणापूर्वी आणि नंतर महिलांसाठी असलेल्या रोजगार नियमांबाबत खालीलपैकी कोणते/ती विधान/ने अयोग्य आहे/त? (a) अधिनियमानुसार बाळ जन्मानंतर सहा आठवड्यांची रजा अनिवार्य आहे. (b) अधिनियमानुसार बाळंतपणापूर्वी सहा आठवडे व नंतर दहा आठवड्यांची रजा अनिवार्य आहे. (c) हा अधिनियम कर्मचाऱ्यांची किमान संख्या विचारात न घेता सर्व आस्थापनांना लागू आहे. (d) हा अधिनियम मातृत्व लाभ व इतर लाभ प्रदान करतो.', '{"A": "फक्त (a)", "B": "फक्त (b)", "C": "(a), (b) आणि (d)", "D": "(b) आणि (c)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'बरोबर पर्याय D आहे. अयोग्य विधाने (b) व (c): मातृत्व लाभ अधिनियम त्या स्वरूपात सहा आठवडे आधी व दहा नंतर अशी रजा ठरवत नाही, आणि तो आकाराचा विचार न करता प्रत्येक आस्थापनेला लागू नाही — किमान कर्मचारी संख्येची अट असते. (a) व (d) बरोबर, म्हणून (b) आणि (c) हे उत्तर.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Other"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27074, 'Other', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, '''स्वैच्छिक क्षेत्रावरील राष्ट्रीय धोरण – 2007'' नुसार स्वैच्छिक संस्थान (VOs) च्या वैशिष्ट्यांबाबत खालील विधाने विचारात घ्या: (a) या संस्था खाजगी स्वरूपाच्या असून सरकारपासून स्वतंत्र असतात. (b) या संस्थांनी निर्माण केलेला नफा त्यांच्या मालकांना किंवा संचालकांना परत केला जात नाही. (c) या संस्था स्वयंशासित असतात आणि त्यांचे नियंत्रण सरकारद्वारे केले जाते. (d) या संस्था विशिष्ट ध्येय आणि उद्दिष्टे असलेल्या नोंदणीकृत संस्था किंवा अनौपचारिक गट असू शकतात. वरीलपैकी कोणती विधाने बरोबर आहे/त?', '{"A": "फक्त (a), (b) आणि (c)", "B": "फक्त (b), (c) आणि (d)", "C": "फक्त (a), (b) आणि (d)", "D": "वरील सर्व"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय C येतो. स्वैच्छिक क्षेत्रावरील राष्ट्रीय धोरण-2007 नुसार स्वैच्छिक संस्था खाजगी व सरकारपासून स्वतंत्र असतात (a), नफा मालकांना परत करत नाहीत (b), आणि विशिष्ट ध्येय असलेल्या नोंदणीकृत वा अनौपचारिक गट असतात (d). विधान (c) चुकीचे — या संस्था स्वयंशासित असतात पण सरकारद्वारे नियंत्रित नसतात — म्हणून (a), (b) व (d) बरोबर.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Other"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27075, 'Ecology & Ecosystems', 'General Studies', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'जीवसंहती (Biome) ही संकल्पना कोणी मांडली?', '{"A": "मॅकनॉटन व वोल्फ (1932)", "B": "एफ. क्लेमेंट्स (1916)", "C": "ए.जी. टान्स्ले (1974)", "D": "इ.एच. हेकेल (1933)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'बरोबर पर्याय B आहे. जीवसंहती (Biome) ही संकल्पना एफ. क्लेमेंट्स यांनी 1916 मध्ये मांडली. इतर नाव-वर्ष जोड्या भुरळ घालण्यासाठी आहेत, त्यामुळे ''क्लेमेंट्स, 1916'' ही खूण पक्की ठेवा.', '{"General Studies","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Ecology & Ecosystems"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27076, 'Poverty & Unemployment', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'जोड्या जुळवा: भारतातील दारिद्र्य निर्मूलन कार्यक्रम - प्रारंभाचे वर्ष (a) एकात्मिक ग्रामीण विकास कार्यक्रम - (i) 2001 (b) ग्रामीण भूमिहीन रोजगार हमी कार्यक्रम - (ii) 1989 (c) जवाहर रोजगार योजना - (iii) 1983 (d) संपूर्ण ग्रामीण रोजगार योजना - (iv) 1978', '{"A": "(a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(iv)", "B": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(i), (c)-(ii), (d)-(iii)", "C": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(iii), (c)-(i), (d)-(ii)", "D": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(iii), (c)-(ii), (d)-(i)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय D आहे. प्रारंभ वर्षानुसार IRDP 1978 (iv), RLEGP 1983 (iii), जवाहर रोजगार योजना 1989 (ii) आणि संपूर्ण ग्रामीण रोजगार योजना 2001 (i). या दारिद्र्य कार्यक्रमांना कालक्रमाने लावणे हा जोड्या जुळवण्याचा सर्वात सोपा मार्ग.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Poverty & Unemployment"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27077, 'Economic Planning & Five Year Plans', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'पहिली आणि चौथी पंचवार्षिक योजना यांचा कालावधी अनुक्रमे __________ व __________ आहे.', '{"A": "1951-56, 1961-66", "B": "1951-56, 1969-74", "C": "1951-56, 1967-72", "D": "1951-56, 1974-79"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'थेट उत्तराकडे — पर्याय B. पहिली पंचवार्षिक योजना 1951-56 आणि चौथी पंचवार्षिक योजना 1969-74. चौथ्या योजनेआधीचा खंड (1966-69 चा ''योजना सुट्टीचा'' काळ) हाच तपशील 1969 ही सुरुवात निश्चित करतो.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Economic Planning & Five Year Plans"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27078, 'Population & Census', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'पुढील विधानांचा विचार करा: विधान-I: 1 मार्च 2026 रोजीच्या अंदाजानुसार महाराष्ट्राची एकूण प्रक्षेपित लोकसंख्या सुमारे 12.93 कोटी आहे. विधान-II: त्याच कालावधीत महाराष्ट्रातील नागरी लोकसंख्या ग्रामीण लोकसंख्येपेक्षा अधिक आहे. वरीलपैकी कोणते/ती विधान/ने बरोबर आहे/त?', '{"A": "विधान-I बरोबर आहे, पण विधान-II चुकीचे आहे.", "B": "विधान-I चुकीचे आहे, पण विधान-II बरोबर आहे.", "C": "विधान-I आणि विधान-II दोन्ही बरोबर आहेत.", "D": "विधान-I आणि विधान-II दोन्ही चुकीचे आहेत."}'::jsonb, 'A', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय A आहे. विधान-I बरोबर — 1 मार्च 2026 रोजी महाराष्ट्राची प्रक्षेपित लोकसंख्या सुमारे 12.93 कोटी — पण विधान-II चुकीचे, कारण त्या काळासाठी नागरी लोकसंख्या ग्रामीणपेक्षा जास्त असण्याचा अंदाज नाही. म्हणून विधान-I बरोबर, विधान-II चुकीचे.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Population & Census"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27079, 'Population & Census', 'Geography', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'खालील विधाने विचारात घ्या: (a) 2017 मध्ये भारताची लोकसंख्येची घनता दक्षिण कोरियापेक्षा जास्त होती. (b) 2017 मध्ये भारताची लोकसंख्येची घनता बांगलादेशापेक्षा कमी होती. वरीलपैकी कोणते/ती विधान/ने योग्य आहे/त?', '{"A": "केवळ (a) योग्य आहे.", "B": "केवळ (b) योग्य आहे.", "C": "दोन्ही (a) आणि (b) योग्य आहेत.", "D": "वरीलपैकी कोणतेही नाही."}'::jsonb, 'B', 'बरोबर पर्याय B आहे. फक्त विधान (b) बरोबर — 2017 मध्ये भारताची लोकसंख्येची घनता बांगलादेशापेक्षा कमी होती, आणि बांगलादेश हा अत्यंत दाट लोकवस्तीचा देश आहे. विधान (a) चुकीचे, कारण त्या वर्षी भारताची घनता दक्षिण कोरियापेक्षा जास्त नव्हे तर कमी होती.', '{"Geography","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Population & Census"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27080, 'Agriculture Economy', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'खालीलपैकी कोणते जमिनीच्या उपविभागणी आणि तुकडे होण्याचे तोटे आहेत? (a) जमिनीची नासाडी (b) प्रच्छन्न बेरोजगारी (c) जमीन व्यवस्थापन सोपे करणे (d) कमी उत्पादकता', '{"A": "केवळ (a), (b) आणि (c)", "B": "केवळ (a), (b) आणि (d)", "C": "केवळ (a) आणि (d)", "D": "वरीलपैकी सर्व"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'बरोबर पर्याय B आहे. जमिनीच्या तुकडेपणामुळे जमिनीची नासाडी (a), प्रच्छन्न बेरोजगारी (b) आणि कमी उत्पादकता (d) होते. विधान (c) — ''जमीन व्यवस्थापन सोपे होणे'' — हा तर फायदा आहे, तोटा नव्हे, म्हणून तो वगळून (a), (b) व (d) उरतात.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Agriculture Economy"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27081, 'Public Finance & Budget', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'महाराष्ट्रातील सार्वजनिक वितरण व्यवस्था (PDS) संदर्भात पुढील विधानांचा विचार करा: (a) डिसेंबर 2025 पर्यंत राज्यात एकूण 270.48 लाख शिधापत्रिकाधारक होते. (b) 31 ऑक्टोबर 2025 रोजी राज्यात 51,636 रास्त भाव दुकाने कार्यरत होती. (c) ऑक्टोबर 2025 पर्यंत सुमारे 1.55 कोटी कुटुंबांना आधार आधारित बायोमेट्रिक प्रमाणीकरणाद्वारे शिधावस्तूंचा लाभ देण्यात आला. वरीलपैकी कोणते विधान बरोबर आहे/त?', '{"A": "फक्त (a) आणि (b)", "B": "फक्त (b) आणि (c)", "C": "फक्त (a) आणि (c)", "D": "(a), (b) आणि (c)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय B आहे. विधाने (b) व (c) बरोबर — 31 ऑक्टोबर 2025 रोजी सुमारे 51,636 रास्त भाव दुकाने कार्यरत आणि ऑक्टोबर 2025 पर्यंत सुमारे 1.55 कोटी कुटुंबांना आधार आधारित बायोमेट्रिक प्रमाणीकरणाद्वारे लाभ. विधान (a) मधील शिधापत्रिकाधारकांचा आकडा जुळत नाही, म्हणून फक्त (b) व (c) टिकतात.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Public Finance & Budget"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27082, 'Poverty & Unemployment', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'सामाजिक सुरक्षा उपाययोजना प्रामुख्याने दोन प्रमुख प्रकारांमध्ये विभागल्या जातात. खालीलपैकी कोणते पर्याय ते वर्ग सर्वाधिक अचूकपणे दर्शवतात? (a) सामाजिक विमा (b) सामाजिक कल्याण (c) सामाजिक सहाय (d) सामाजिक समावेशकता', '{"A": "(a) आणि (b)", "B": "(b) आणि (c)", "C": "(a) आणि (c)", "D": "(c) आणि (d)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय C येतो. सामाजिक सुरक्षा साधारणपणे दोन मुख्य वर्गांत विभागली जाते — सामाजिक विमा (a) आणि सामाजिक सहाय (c). सामाजिक कल्याण व सामाजिक समावेशकता या व्यापक संकल्पना आहेत, दोन मुख्य वर्ग नव्हेत, म्हणून (a) व (c) ही योग्य जोडी.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Poverty & Unemployment"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27083, 'Poverty & Unemployment', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'तेंडूलकर समितीने निदर्शनास आणल्याप्रमाणे, दारिद्र्याची संकल्पना __________ यासारख्या मूलभूत मानवी गरजांच्या संदर्भात सामाजिक वंचिततेशी संबंधित आहे. (a) पुरेसे पोषण आवश्यक (b) पुरेसा निवारा आवश्यक (c) पुरेशी वस्त्र उपलब्धता आवश्यक (d) टाळण्यायुक्त रोगांपासून सुटका आवश्यक (e) किमान शिक्षण आवश्यक वरीलपैकी कोणते/ता मुद्दे/दा बरोबर आहे/त?', '{"A": "(a), (b) आणि (c)", "B": "(b), (c) आणि (d)", "C": "(c), (d) आणि (e)", "D": "वरील सर्व"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय D आहे. तेंडूलकर समितीने दारिद्र्याची मांडणी या सर्व गरजांशी संबंधित सामाजिक वंचिततेच्या आधारे केली — पुरेसे पोषण, पुरेसा निवारा, पुरेशी वस्त्रे, टाळता येणाऱ्या रोगांपासून सुटका आणि किमान शिक्षण. प्रत्येक मुद्दा यादीत असल्याने ''वरील सर्व'' हेच योग्य.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Poverty & Unemployment"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27084, 'Poverty & Unemployment', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'तेंडूलकर समितीच्या अंदाजानुसार 2004-05 मध्ये __________% ग्रामीण लोकसंख्या व __________% शहरी लोकसंख्या दारिद्र्यरेषेखाली होती.', '{"A": "41.8 आणि 25.7", "B": "29.8 आणि 30.5", "C": "35.2 आणि 45.2", "D": "47.2 आणि 35.2"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'थेट उत्तराकडे — पर्याय A. तेंडूलकर समितीच्या 2004-05 च्या अंदाजानुसार 41.8% ग्रामीण व 25.7% शहरी लोकसंख्या दारिद्र्यरेषेखाली होती. ग्रामीण आकडा शहरीपेक्षा जास्त, ही खूण अदलाबदल केलेल्या पर्यायांविरुद्ध तपासणी म्हणून ठेवा.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Poverty & Unemployment"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27085, 'Science & Technology (IT/Space)', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'खालीलपैकी योग्य विधान/ने कोणती आहेत? (a) सूर्यमालेतील प्रजापती ग्रहास 61 उपग्रह आहेत. (b) बुध ग्रहाचे सूर्यापासूनचे सरासरी अंतर 58 मिलियन कि.मी. आहे. (c) प्रजापती ग्रह सूर्यापासून सरासरी 4495 मिलियन कि.मी. अंतरावर आहे.', '{"A": "फक्त विधान (a) बरोबर आहे.", "B": "फक्त विधान (c) बरोबर आहे.", "C": "विधाने (a) आणि (c) बरोबर नाहीत.", "D": "विधाने (b) आणि (c) बरोबर नाहीत."}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय C आहे. विधान (b) बरोबर — बुध सूर्यापासून सुमारे 58 मिलियन कि.मी. आहे. पण (a) व (c) चुकीची: प्रजापती (युरेनस) ला 61 उपग्रह नाहीत, आणि त्याचे सूर्यापासूनचे सरासरी अंतर 4495 मिलियन कि.मी. नाही (तो आकडा नेपच्यूनच्या जवळचा). म्हणून ''विधाने (a) आणि (c) बरोबर नाहीत'' हेच योग्य.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Science & Technology (IT/Space)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27086, 'Poverty & Unemployment', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'राष्ट्रीय अन्न सुरक्षा कायदा - 2013 संबंधी खालीलपैकी कोणते/ती विधान/ने बरोबर आहे/त? (a) महिला सक्षमीकरण हे राष्ट्रीय अन्न सुरक्षा कायद्याचे - 2013 चे वैशिष्ट्य आहे. (b) राज्य अन्न आयोगास 2013 च्या या कायद्याचे निरीक्षण, पुनरावलोकन आणि अंमलबजावणी करण्याचे अधिकार आहेत.', '{"A": "विधान (a) बरोबर आहे.", "B": "विधान (b) बरोबर आहे.", "C": "विधान (a) व (b) दोन्ही चूक आहेत.", "D": "विधान (a) व (b) दोन्ही बरोबर आहेत."}'::jsonb, 'A', 'बरोबर पर्याय A आहे. विधान (a) बरोबर — राष्ट्रीय अन्न सुरक्षा कायदा, 2013 चे महिला सक्षमीकरण हे अंगभूत वैशिष्ट्य आहे, ज्यात शिधापत्रिकेसाठी घरातील ज्येष्ठ महिलेला प्रमुख मानले जाते. विधान (b) मधील राज्य अन्न आयोगाच्या भूमिकेचे वर्णन कायद्याच्या शब्दांशी जुळत नाही, म्हणून फक्त (a) टिकते.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Poverty & Unemployment"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27087, 'Industry, Trade & Reforms', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'खालील विधाने विचारात घ्या: (a) एकूण भांडवली साठ्यामध्ये डेव्हिड पिअर्स आणि जेरमी वॉरफोर्ड यांनी मानवनिर्मित भौतिक भांडवल, मानवी भांडवल आणि पर्यावरणीय भांडवल यांचा समावेश केला आहे. (b) डेव्हिड पिअर्स आणि जेरमी वॉरफोर्ड यांच्या मते शाश्वत विकासाचा अर्थ असा आहे की विकास प्रक्रियेत मानवनिर्मित भौतिक भांडवल, मानवी भांडवल आणि पर्यावरणीय भांडवल कमी होते.', '{"A": "केवळ (a) बरोबर आहे.", "B": "केवळ (b) बरोबर आहे.", "C": "दोन्ही (a) आणि (b) बरोबर आहेत.", "D": "वरीलपैकी नाही"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय A येतो. विधान (a) बरोबर — पिअर्स व वॉरफोर्ड एकूण भांडवली साठ्यात मानवनिर्मित भौतिक, मानवी व पर्यावरणीय भांडवल मोजतात. विधान (b) त्यांची कल्पना उलटवते: शाश्वत विकासात हे भांडवल कमी होणे अपेक्षित नाही, म्हणून फक्त (a) बरोबर.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Industry, Trade & Reforms"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27088, 'Population & Demography', 'Economy', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'राष्ट्रीय लोकसंख्या धोरण, 2000 च्या उद्दिष्टांच्या संदर्भात खालील विधानांचा विचार करा: (a) मुलींच्या विवाहास विलंब करण्यास प्रोत्साहन द्यावे, विवाह 18 वर्षांपेक्षा कमी वयात न होता शक्यतो 21 वर्षांनंतर व्हावा. (b) 2030 पर्यंत स्थिर लोकसंख्या साध्य करणे हे दीर्घकालीन उद्दिष्ट आहे. वरीलपैकी कोणते/ती विधान/ने चूक आहे/त?', '{"A": "फक्त (a) चूक आहे.", "B": "फक्त (b) चूक आहे.", "C": "दोन्ही (a) आणि (b) चूक आहेत.", "D": "वरीलपैकी नाही"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'परीक्षकाने पर्याय C निवडला आहे. इथे दोन्ही विधाने चुकीची — (a) मधील वयाची मांडणी राष्ट्रीय लोकसंख्या धोरण 2000 च्या प्रत्यक्ष उद्दिष्टाशी जुळत नाही, आणि धोरणातील स्थिर लोकसंख्येचे दीर्घकालीन उद्दिष्ट 2045 साठी आहे, (b) मधील 2030 साठी नव्हे. म्हणून (a) व (b) दोन्ही चुकीची.', '{"Economy","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Population & Demography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27089, 'Electricity & Magnetism', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'प्रति युनिट वेळेत पृष्ठभागातून जाणाऱ्या (वाहणाऱ्या) निव्वळ विद्युतभाराला __________ म्हणतात.', '{"A": "विद्युत प्रवाह", "B": "संभाव्य फरक", "C": "व्होल्टेज फरक", "D": "प्रभार गती"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'बरोबर पर्याय A आहे. पृष्ठभागातून प्रति एकक वेळेत जाणारा निव्वळ विद्युतभार म्हणजे व्याख्येनुसार विद्युत प्रवाह. इतर संज्ञा व्होल्टेज किंवा गती दर्शवतात, भाराच्या प्रवाहाचा दर नव्हे, म्हणून ''विद्युत प्रवाह'' हेच नेमके उत्तर.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Electricity & Magnetism"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27090, 'Mechanics & Motion', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'भौतिक प्रमाण आणि त्यांचे परिमाण यांच्या योग्य जोड्या लावा: स्तंभ I - स्तंभ II (a) पारगम्यता (Permeability) (μ₀) - (i) ML²T⁻¹ (b) चिकटपणाचा गुणांक (Coefficient of Viscosity) (η) - (ii) MLT⁻²I⁻² (c) प्लँकचा स्थिरांक (Planck''s Constant) (h) - (iii) ML⁻¹T⁻¹ (जिथे M म्हणजे वस्तुमान, L म्हणजे लांबी, T म्हणजे वेळ आणि I म्हणजे विद्युतप्रवाह)', '{"A": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(i), (c)-(ii)", "B": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(i), (c)-(iii)", "C": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(iii), (c)-(i)", "D": "(a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय C आहे. पारगम्यता μ₀ चे परिमाण MLT⁻²I⁻² (ii), चिकटपणाचा गुणांक η हे ML⁻¹T⁻¹ (iii) आणि प्लँकचा स्थिरांक h हे ML²T⁻¹ (i). संपूर्ण तक्ता पाठ करण्यापेक्षा प्रत्येक परिमाण व्याख्यासूत्रावरून काढणे अधिक सुरक्षित.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Mechanics & Motion"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27091, 'Modern & Nuclear Physics', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'जेव्हा न्युक्लिऑनचे भ्रमण समांतर असते, तेव्हा अणुकेंद्रीय बलाचे वर्तन कसे असते?', '{"A": "बल अधिक मजबूत करते.", "B": "बल कमकुवत करते.", "C": "बल स्थिर राहते.", "D": "बल प्रत्याकर्षण बनते."}'::jsonb, 'A', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय A येतो. अणुकेंद्रीय बल हे भ्रमणावर अवलंबून असते, आणि न्युक्लिऑनचे भ्रमण समांतर असताना त्यांच्यातील आकर्षण अधिक मजबूत होते. याच भ्रमण-अवलंबित्वामुळे ड्युटेरॉन बद्ध अवस्थेत टिकतो.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Modern & Nuclear Physics"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27092, 'Heat & Thermodynamics', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'थर्मोडायनॉमिक्सच्या नियम दोन नुसार हीट इंजीनची कार्यक्षमता किती असते?', '{"A": "शून्य", "B": "अनंत", "C": "एक", "D": "एक पेक्षा कमी"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'बरोबर पर्याय D आहे. औष्णिकगतिकीच्या दुसऱ्या नियमानुसार कोणतेही उष्णता इंजिन पूर्ण कार्यक्षम असू शकत नाही — काही उष्णता नेहमी बाहेर टाकली जाते — म्हणून त्याची कार्यक्षमता नेहमी एकपेक्षा कमी असते. ''एक'' म्हणजे परिपूर्ण इंजिन, जे नियम नाकारतो.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Heat & Thermodynamics"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27093, 'Optics & Sound', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'जर माध्यमाचा अपवर्तनांक दुहेरी अंतर्वक्र किंवा दुहेरी बहिर्वक्र भिंगाच्या अपवर्तनांकापेक्षा जास्त असेल तर भिंगाची नाभिय लांबी __________ होते.', '{"A": "अनंत", "B": "शून्य", "C": "धन (+)", "D": "ऋण (−)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'थेट उत्तराकडे — पर्याय D. जर सभोवतालच्या माध्यमाचा अपवर्तनांक भिंगापेक्षा जास्त असेल, तर भिंगाचे वर्तन उलटते आणि त्याची नाभिय लांबी ऋण होते. यामुळेच दाट माध्यमात बहिर्वक्र भिंग अपसारी वागू शकते — हा आवडता संकल्पनात्मक पेच.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Optics & Sound"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27094, 'Botany (Plant Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, '''अपोमिक्सिस'' हे एक प्रकारचे पुनरुत्पादन आहे ज्यामुळे __________ चा विकास होतो.', '{"A": "गॅमेट्सच्या संलयनाशिवाय नवीन जीव", "B": "गॅमेट्सच्या संलयन उत्पादनापासून नवीन जीव", "C": "एन्डोस्पर्मपासून गर्भ", "D": "न्यूसेलसपासून भ्रूण"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'थेट उत्तराकडे — पर्याय A. अपोमिक्सिस म्हणजे अलैंगिक बीजनिर्मिती, त्यामुळे गॅमेट्सच्या कोणत्याही संलयनाशिवाय नवीन जीव तयार होतो. ''फलन नाही'' हा मुद्दाच याला सामान्य लैंगिक पुनरुत्पादनापासून वेगळा करतो.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Botany (Plant Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27095, 'Cell Biology & Genetics', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'असे अंगक निवडा ज्यामध्ये स्वतःचे DNA आणि 70S रायबोझोम असतात परंतु ते युकॅरियोटिक पेशींमध्ये आढळते.', '{"A": "लायसोसोम", "B": "तंतुकणिका (Mitochondria)", "C": "गॉल्जी काय", "D": "अंतर्द्रव्यजालिका (Endoplasmic Reticulum)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'बरोबर पर्याय B आहे. तंतुकणिका (मायटोकॉन्ड्रिया) हे स्वतःचे DNA व 70S (जीवाणूसदृश) रायबोझोम बाळगणारे युकॅरियोटिक अंगक आहे — एंडोसिम्बायोटिक सिद्धांताचा उत्कृष्ट पुरावा. लायसोसोम, गॉल्जी व अंतर्द्रव्यजालिका यांना स्वतःचा जनुकसंच नसतो.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Cell Biology & Genetics"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27096, 'Cell Biology & Genetics', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'खालीलपैकी कोणत्या जीवांच्या पडद्यामध्ये असंतृप्त फॉस्फोलिपिड्सचे प्रमाण सर्वाधिक असेल याचा अंदाज लावा?', '{"A": "अंटार्क्टिक मासे", "B": "वाळवंटातील साप", "C": "मानव", "D": "ध्रुवीय अस्वल"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय A आहे. अतिशीत अधिवासातील जीव कमी तापमानातही पडदा प्रवाही राहावा म्हणून पडद्यात अधिक असंतृप्त फॉस्फोलिपिड्स ठेवतात, त्यामुळे अंटार्क्टिक मासे इथे आघाडीवर. वाळवंटातील सापासारख्या उष्ण अधिवासातील प्राण्यांना कमी असंतृप्त लिपिड्स लागतात.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Cell Biology & Genetics"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27097, 'Cell Biology & Genetics', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'जंपिंग जीन्सबद्दल योग्य विधाने ओळखा: (a) हे जीन्स आहेत जे त्यांची जागा बदलू शकतात. (b) यांना ट्रान्सपोसन्स असेही म्हणतात. (c) बार्बरा मॅकक्लिंटॉक यांनी 1965 मध्ये हे प्रथम शोधले होते.', '{"A": "(a) आणि (b)", "B": "(b) आणि (c)", "C": "(a) आणि (c)", "D": "वरीलपैकी सर्व"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय D आहे. उत्तरतालिकेनुसार जंपिंग जीन्सबाबतची तिन्ही विधाने ग्राह्य — ते जागा बदलू शकतात, त्यांना ट्रान्सपोसन्स म्हणतात आणि त्यांचे श्रेय बार्बरा मॅकक्लिंटॉक यांना दिले जाते. म्हणून ''वरील सर्व'' हा निवडलेला पर्याय.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Cell Biology & Genetics"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27098, 'Zoology (Animal Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'मार्सुपिअल्स व प्लेसेंटल मॅमल्स हे उत्क्रांतीचे कोणते उदाहरण दर्शवितात?', '{"A": "भिन्न उत्क्रांती", "B": "अभिसरण उत्क्रांती", "C": "समांतर उत्क्रांती", "D": "स्वतंत्र उत्क्रांती"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'बरोबर पर्याय B आहे. मार्सुपिअल्स व प्लेसेंटल सस्तन प्राणी वेगवेगळ्या प्रदेशांत स्वतंत्रपणे सारखी शरीररचना विकसित करतात — हीच अभिसरण उत्क्रांती, जिथे असंबंधित गट सारखी अनुकूलने गाठतात. भिन्न उत्क्रांती याच्या उलट — एका पूर्वजापासून वेगवेगळी रूपे.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Zoology (Animal Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27099, 'Diseases & Health', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'HIV संसर्गाच्या कोणत्या टप्प्यात AIDS ची लक्षणे साधारणपणे दिसू लागतात?', '{"A": "संसर्ग करणारा रेट्रोव्हायरस यजमानाच्या पेशींमध्ये प्रवेश करतो तेव्हा", "B": "रिव्हर्स ट्रान्सक्रिप्टेस एन्झाइमद्वारे व्हायरल DNA तयार होतो तेव्हा", "C": "HIV हेल्पर T-लिम्फोसाइट्समध्ये वेगाने वाढतो व या पेशींचे मोठ्या संख्येने नुकसान करतो तेव्हा", "D": "संक्रमित व्यक्तिसोबत लैंगिक संपर्क झाल्यानंतर 15 दिवसांच्या आत"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय C आहे. HIV हेल्पर T-लिम्फोसाइट्समध्ये वेगाने वाढून त्यांची मोठ्या प्रमाणात नासाडी करतो आणि रोगप्रतिकारशक्ती कोलमडते, तेव्हाच AIDS ची लक्षणे दिसू लागतात. यजमान पेशींत प्रवेश व रिव्हर्स ट्रान्सक्रिप्शन या पूर्वीच्या पायऱ्या लक्षणांआधीच घडतात.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Diseases & Health"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27100, 'Human Physiology', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'पॉलिपेप्टाइड हार्मोन कॅल्सीटोनीन (CT) __________ ग्रंथीच्या पॅराफोलिक्युलर पेशींद्वारे तयार केला जातो.', '{"A": "लाळ", "B": "घाम", "C": "थायरॉईड", "D": "स्वादुपिंड"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय C येतो. कॅल्सीटोनीन थायरॉईड ग्रंथीच्या पॅराफोलिक्युलर (C) पेशींद्वारे स्रवते आणि ते रक्तातील कॅल्शियम कमी करण्यास मदत करते. ''पॅराफोलिक्युलर पेशी'' थेट थायरॉईडशी जोडणे हा उत्तराचा सर्वात झटपट मार्ग.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Human Physiology"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (27101, 'Acids, Bases & Salts', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'दिलेल्या पर्यायांपैकी खनिज आम्ल/आम्ले ओळखा: (a) ऑक्झॅलिक आम्ल (b) सल्फ्युरिक आम्ल (c) नायट्रिक आम्ल (d) हायड्रोक्लोरिक आम्ल', '{"A": "फक्त (a)", "B": "(b), (c) आणि (d)", "C": "फक्त (d)", "D": "फक्त (b) आणि (c)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय B आहे. इथली खनिज (अजैविक) आम्ले म्हणजे सल्फ्युरिक (b), नायट्रिक (c) आणि हायड्रोक्लोरिक (d). ऑक्झॅलिक आम्ल (a) हे सेंद्रिय आम्ल आहे, म्हणून ते वगळून (b), (c) व (d) हा संच बनतो.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Acids, Bases & Salts"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27102, 'Botany (Plant Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'खालीलपैकी कोणते नैसर्गिक वनस्पती संप्रेरक नाही?', '{"A": "ऑक्सिन", "B": "इथायलीन", "C": "मिथायलीन", "D": "अॅबसिसिक आम्ल"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'बरोबर पर्याय C आहे. ऑक्सिन, इथिलीन आणि अॅबसिसिक आम्ल ही सर्व खरी नैसर्गिक वनस्पती वृद्धी नियंत्रके आहेत, पण ''मिथिलीन'' हे वनस्पती संप्रेरकच नाही — तेच वेगळे. विज्ञानाच्या यादीत अशी उच्चारसाधर्म्य असलेली नावे घुसडलेली असतात, तिकडे लक्ष द्या.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Botany (Plant Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27103, 'Chemical Bonding & Reactions', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'कोणत्याही अॅलोट्रॉपिक स्वरूपातील सर्व मूलद्रव्यांची ऑक्सिडेशन स्थिती __________ असते.', '{"A": "+2 (अधिक दोन)", "B": "+1 (अधिक एक)", "C": "0 (शून्य)", "D": "−1 (वजा एक)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय C आहे. मूलद्रव्य त्याच्या अॅलोट्रॉपिक (मुक्त, असंयुक्त) स्वरूपात इतर कोणत्याही मूलद्रव्याशी बंधित नसते, म्हणून त्याची ऑक्सिडेशन स्थिती शून्य असते — O₂, O₃, ग्रॅफाइट वा हिरा आठवा. ''मुक्त मूलद्रव्य = शून्य'' हा नियम विश्वासार्ह शॉर्टकट.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Chemical Bonding & Reactions"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27104, 'Diseases & Health', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'क्लोरोअॅम्फीनीकॉल हे __________ आहे. (a) संकीर्ण श्रेणीचे (Narrow spectrum) प्रतिजीवक (b) विस्तृत श्रेणीचे (Broad spectrum) प्रतिजीवक (c) मर्यादित श्रेणीचे (Limited spectrum) प्रतिजीवक (d) जंतुनाशक औषध', '{"A": "फक्त (a) व (d) बरोबर आहेत", "B": "फक्त (b) बरोबर आहे", "C": "फक्त (b) व (c) बरोबर आहेत", "D": "फक्त (d) बरोबर आहे"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'बरोबर पर्याय B आहे. क्लोरोअॅम्फीनीकॉल हे विस्तृत श्रेणीचे (broad spectrum) प्रतिजैविक असून अनेक जीवाणूंवर प्रभावी आहे — म्हणून फक्त विधान (b) बरोबर. ते संकीर्ण वा मर्यादित श्रेणीचे नाही, आणि केवळ जंतुनाशकही नाही.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Diseases & Health"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27105, 'Parliament', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'कोणत्या समापन (चर्चा समाप्ती) प्रस्तावाअंतर्गत, फक्त महत्त्वाचे कलम चर्चेसाठी आणि मतदानासाठी घेतले जातात आणि मध्यवर्ती कलमे वगळली जातात आणि मंजूर झाल्याचे गृहित धरले जातात?', '{"A": "साधारण समापन", "B": "खंडश: समापन", "C": "कंगारू समापन", "D": "गिलोटिन समापन"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'बरोबर पर्याय C आहे. कंगारू समापनात पीठासीन अधिकारी फक्त निवडक महत्त्वाच्या कलमांवर चर्चा व मतदान घेऊ देतात, आणि मधली कलमे ''ओलांडून'' मंजूर झाल्याचे गृहित धरले जाते. नावातच उडी मारण्याचा संकेत आहे.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Parliament"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27106, 'State Government', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'राज्याच्या महाअधिवक्त्याचे पारिश्रमिक (remuneration) कोण निर्धारित करतात?', '{"A": "संसद", "B": "राष्ट्रपती", "C": "विधानसभा", "D": "राज्यपाल"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय D आहे. कलम 165 नुसार महाअधिवक्ता राज्यपालांच्या मर्जीनुसार पद धारण करतात आणि राज्यपाल ठरवतील असे पारिश्रमिक घेतात. म्हणून वेतन राज्यपाल ठरवतात, संसद वा राष्ट्रपती नव्हे.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","State Government"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27107, 'Atomic Structure & Periodic Table', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'खालीलपैकी कोणत्या मूलद्रव्याची विद्युतऋणता (electronegativity) सर्वात जास्त आहे?', '{"A": "ऑक्सिजन", "B": "नायट्रोजन", "C": "फ्ल्युओरीन", "D": "क्लोरीन"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय C येतो. सर्व मूलद्रव्यांत फ्ल्युओरीनची विद्युतऋणता सर्वाधिक असून ते आवर्तसारणीच्या वरच्या-उजव्या टोकाला असते. ऑक्सिजन, नायट्रोजन व क्लोरीनही विद्युतऋण आहेत, पण फ्ल्युओरीनला कोणी मागे टाकत नाही.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Atomic Structure & Periodic Table"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27108, 'Judiciary', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'खालीलपैकी योग्य कथने ओळखा: (a) उच्च न्यायालयाकडून कनिष्ठ न्यायालय किंवा न्यायाधिकरणाला प्रतिषेध आदेश जारी केला जातो आणि त्याचा उद्देश त्यांच्या अधिकार क्षेत्राबाहेर जाण्यापासून प्रतिबंध करणे आहे. (b) प्रतिषेध आदेश प्रशासकीय संस्थांविरुद्ध जारी केला जाऊ शकतो. (c) प्रतिषेध आदेश न्यायिक व अर्धन्यायिक संस्थांविरुद्ध जारी केला जाऊ शकतो.', '{"A": "फक्त (a), (b)", "B": "फक्त (a), (c)", "C": "फक्त (b), (c)", "D": "वरीलपैकी सर्व"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'बरोबर पर्याय B आहे. विधाने (a) व (c) बरोबर — प्रतिषेध आदेश उच्च न्यायालयाकडून कनिष्ठ न्यायालय वा न्यायाधिकरणाला त्याच्या अधिकारक्षेत्रात ठेवण्यासाठी दिला जातो आणि तो न्यायिक व अर्धन्यायिक संस्थांविरुद्ध चालतो. निव्वळ प्रशासकीय संस्थांविरुद्ध तो चालत नाही, म्हणून (b) वगळले जाते.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Judiciary"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27109, 'Chemical Bonding & Reactions', 'Science', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'एकमेकांत न मिसळणाऱ्या दोन द्रवांपैकी एका द्रवाचे दुसऱ्या द्रवामध्ये केलेल्या कोलॉइडल प्रसारणास __________ म्हणतात.', '{"A": "द्रावण", "B": "फेस", "C": "इमल्शन", "D": "जेल"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'थेट उत्तराकडे — पर्याय C. एका द्रवाचे त्याच्याशी न मिसळणाऱ्या दुसऱ्या द्रवात केलेले कोलॉइडल प्रसारण म्हणजे इमल्शन — दूध हे रोजचे उदाहरण. फेस म्हणजे द्रवात वायू आणि जेल ही वेगळी कोलॉइडल अवस्था, त्यामुळे ते बसत नाहीत.', '{"Science","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Chemical Bonding & Reactions"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27110, 'Constitutional Framework & Preamble', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'खालीलपैकी चुकीचे विधान/ने कोणते आहे? (a) बी.एन. राव हे घटना समितीचे सल्लागार होते. (b) बी.एन. राव यांनी घटनेचा मसुदा ऑक्टोबर, 1947 मध्ये तयार केला. (c) बी.एन. राव यांनी तयार केलेल्या घटनेच्या मसुद्यामध्ये 310 कलमे व 8 अनुसूची होत्या. (d) बी.एन. राव यांनी तयार केलेल्या घटनेच्या मसुद्यामध्ये 243 कलमे व 13 अनुसूची होत्या.', '{"A": "(a) आणि (c)", "B": "(b) आणि (c)", "C": "फक्त (d)", "D": "फक्त (c)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय D आहे. फक्त विधान (c) चुकीचे — बी.एन. राव यांच्या घटना मसुद्यात 310 कलमे व 8 अनुसूची नव्हत्या. त्यांचा मसुदा 243 कलमे व 13 अनुसूची असा मानला जातो, म्हणून विधान (d) मधील आकडा बरोबर आणि (c) चुकीचे.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Constitutional Framework & Preamble"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27111, 'Parliament', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'खालीलपैकी अयोग्य कथन ओळखा:', '{"A": "राष्ट्रपती हे कोर्ट मार्शलद्वारा दिलेल्या शिक्षेला क्षमा करू शकतात, तर राज्यपाल मात्र क्षमा करू शकत नाहीत.", "B": "राष्ट्रपती हे क्षमेच्या अधिकाराची कारणे देण्यास बांधील आहेत.", "C": "दयेसाठी याचिका कर्त्याला राष्ट्रपतींकडून तोंडी सुनावणी घेण्याचा अधिकार नाही.", "D": "केंद्रीय मंत्रिमंडळाच्या सल्ल्यानुसार राष्ट्रपतींना क्षमेचा अधिकार वापरावा लागतो."}'::jsonb, 'B', 'बरोबर पर्याय B आहे, कारण प्रश्न अयोग्य विधान विचारतो. क्षमेचा अधिकार वापरताना राष्ट्रपती कारणे देण्यास बांधील नसतात, त्यामुळे ते विधान चुकीचे. उर्वरित तीन — कोर्ट मार्शलच्या शिक्षेला क्षमा, तोंडी सुनावणीचा अधिकार नसणे आणि मंत्रिमंडळाच्या सल्ल्याने कृती — ही सर्व बरोबर.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Parliament"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27112, 'Urban Local Bodies', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'भारतीय राज्यघटनेतील बाराव्या अनुसूचीमध्ये खालीलपैकी कोणत्या बाबींचा समावेश केला आहे? (a) कलात्मक दृष्टीकोणाचे प्रवर्धन, अग्निशमन सेवा (b) दहनभूमी व विद्युत दाहिनी (c) बाजार व जत्रा, ग्रामीण गृहनिर्माण (d) अपंग व मतिमंद यांच्या हितसंबंधाचे संरक्षण, पर्यावरणाचे संरक्षण', '{"A": "फक्त (a), (b) आणि (d)", "B": "फक्त (c) आणि (d)", "C": "फक्त (a), (b) आणि (c)", "D": "फक्त (b), (c) आणि (d)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'बरोबर पर्याय A आहे. इथली बाराव्या अनुसूचीतील विषय म्हणजे कलात्मक दृष्टीकोणाचे प्रवर्धन व अग्निशमन सेवा (a), दहनभूमी व विद्युत दाहिनी (b), आणि अपंगांच्या हितसंबंधांचे व पर्यावरणाचे संरक्षण (d). विधान (c) या संचात बसत नाही, म्हणून (a), (b) व (d) टिकतात.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Urban Local Bodies"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27113, 'Centre-State Relations', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'खालीलपैकी योग्य विधान/ने कोणती आहेत? (a) के.सी. व्हीअर यांच्या मते, भारतीय संघराज्य हे ''अर्ध-संघराज्य'' आहे. (b) मोरिस जोन्स यांच्या मते, भारतीय संघराज्य हे ''सौदेबाजी संघराज्य'' आहे. (c) सी.एफ. स्ट्राँग यांच्या मते, भारतीय संघराज्य हे ''कमी संघराज्य'' आहे. (d) ग्रॅनव्हिल ऑस्टीन यांच्या मते, भारतीय संघराज्य हे ''सहकार्याचे संघराज्य'' आहे.', '{"A": "फक्त (a) आणि (d)", "B": "फक्त (a), (b) आणि (c)", "C": "फक्त (a)", "D": "(a), (b), (c) आणि (d)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय D आहे. प्रत्येक वर्णन योग्य अभ्यासकाशी जुळते — व्हीअर ''अर्ध-संघराज्य'', मोरिस जोन्स ''सौदेबाजी संघराज्य'', सी.एफ. स्ट्राँग ''कमी संघराज्य'' आणि ग्रॅनव्हिल ऑस्टीन ''सहकार्याचे संघराज्य''. चारही वर्णने योग्यरीत्या जोडलेली असल्याने सर्व बरोबर.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Centre-State Relations"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27114, 'Union Executive', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'पुढील विधानांपैकी राष्ट्रपतींच्या नकाराधिकारासंबंधी कोणती विधाने योग्य आहेत? (a) राष्ट्रपती विधेयकाला त्यांची संमती राखून ठेवू शकतात. (b) राज्यपाल त्यांना योग्य/उचित वाटेल असे विधेयक राष्ट्रपतींच्या विचारार्थ राखीव ठेवू शकतात. (c) राष्ट्रपती संसदेकडे पुनर्विचारार्थ विधेयक दोन्ही सभागृहांना संदेशासह पाठवू शकतात.', '{"A": "फक्त (a) आणि (b)", "B": "फक्त (b) आणि (c)", "C": "फक्त (a) आणि (c)", "D": "(a), (b), (c)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय D आहे. राष्ट्रपतींच्या नकाराधिकाराबाबतचे तिन्ही मुद्दे बरोबर — विधेयकाला संमती राखून ठेवणे, राज्यपालांनी विधेयक राष्ट्रपतींच्या विचारार्थ राखीव ठेवणे, आणि राष्ट्रपतींनी संदेशासह विधेयक पुनर्विचारार्थ संसदेकडे परत पाठवणे. म्हणून (a), (b) व (c) मिळून हे उत्तर.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Union Executive"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27115, 'DPSP & Fundamental Duties', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'मूलभूत कर्तव्ये प्रभावीपणे पार पाडण्यासाठी, संविधानाच्या कामकाजाचा आढावा घेण्यासाठी नेमलेल्या राष्ट्रीय आयोगाने शिफारस केली आहे, __________. (a) निवडणूकीत मतदान करण्याचे कर्तव्य (b) कर भरणे (c) औद्योगिक संस्थांचे त्यांच्या कर्मचाऱ्यांच्या मुलांना शिक्षण देणे, हे कर्तव्य आहे (d) मुलांच्या शिक्षण, शारीरिक आणि नैतिक कल्याणाच्या बाबतीत कौटुंबिक मूल्यांची आणि जबाबदार पालकत्वाची भावना जोपासणे', '{"A": "फक्त (a), (b)", "B": "फक्त (c), (d)", "C": "फक्त (a), (c), (d)", "D": "वरीलपैकी सर्व"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय A येतो. संविधानाच्या कामकाजाचा आढावा घेणाऱ्या राष्ट्रीय आयोगाने मूलभूत कर्तव्यांत मतदानाचे कर्तव्य (a) व कर भरण्याचे कर्तव्य (b) जोडण्याची शिफारस केली. (c) व (d) मधील औद्योगिक शिक्षण व पालकत्वाच्या कल्पना त्या शिफारशीचा भाग नव्हत्या.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","DPSP & Fundamental Duties"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27116, 'Parliament', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'संसदेच्या सार्वजनिक उपक्रम समितीबाबत खालीलपैकी चुकीचे विधान/ने कोणती आहेत? (a) पंडित नेहरू यांनी या समितीच्या निर्मितीची शिफारस 1963 मध्ये केली. (b) लोकसभेमधून निवडून आलेल्या सदस्यांमधूनच या समितीचा अध्यक्ष निवडला जातो. (c) 1974 पासून लोकसभेमधून 15 तर राज्यसभेमधून 7 सदस्य या समितीवर निवडले जातात. (d) या समितीच्या सदस्यांचा कार्यकाल दोन वर्षांचा असतो.', '{"A": "(a) आणि (b)", "B": "(a) आणि (d)", "C": "(c) आणि (d)", "D": "(b), (c) आणि (d)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'बरोबर पर्याय B आहे. अयोग्य विधाने (a) व (d): सार्वजनिक उपक्रम समिती 1964 मध्ये स्थापन झाली (1963 च्या नेहरू शिफारशीवर नव्हे), आणि तिच्या सदस्यांचा कार्यकाल दोन वर्षे नव्हे तर एक वर्ष असतो. रचनेबाबतची (b) व (c) ही विधाने बरोबर.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Parliament"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27117, 'Centre-State Relations', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'पुढील विधानांमधून आंतरराज्यीय परिषदांसंबंधी योग्य विधाने शोधा: (a) याचा उल्लेख अनुच्छेद क्रमांक 263 मध्ये आहे. (b) याची स्थापना करण्याचा राष्ट्रपतींना अधिकार आहे. (c) भारताच्या राष्ट्रपतींनी या अधिकाराचा आजवर वापर केला नाही आणि अनुच्छेद क्रमांक 263 अंतर्गत आजवर कोणतीही आंतरराज्य परिषद स्थापन केलेली नाही.', '{"A": "(a), (b), (c)", "B": "(a), (b)", "C": "(b), (c)", "D": "(a), (c)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'बरोबर पर्याय B आहे. विधाने (a) व (b) बरोबर — आंतरराज्य परिषदेचा उल्लेख कलम 263 मध्ये आहे आणि तिची स्थापना करण्याचा अधिकार राष्ट्रपतींना आहे. विधान (c) चुकीचे, कारण ही परिषद प्रत्यक्षात 1990 मध्ये स्थापन झाली, म्हणून ''कधीच स्थापन केली नाही'' हा दावा टिकत नाही.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Centre-State Relations"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27118, 'Constitutional & Statutory Bodies', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'भारतीय संविधानातील खालीलपैकी कोणते कलम भारताच्या नियंत्रक आणि महालेखापरिक्षकाचे (CAG) स्वतंत्र पद स्थापित करते?', '{"A": "कलम 141", "B": "कलम 144", "C": "कलम 148", "D": "कलम 149"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय C येतो. कलम 148 भारताच्या नियंत्रक व महालेखापरीक्षकाचे स्वतंत्र पद स्थापित करते. शेजारच्या कलमांशी गोंधळ नको — कलम 149 CAG च्या कर्तव्ये व अधिकारांबाबत आहे, पदाच्या निर्मितीबाबत नव्हे.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Constitutional & Statutory Bodies"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27119, 'Constitutional Amendments', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'संसदेच्या साध्या बहुमताद्वारे खालील प्रकारच्या घटनादुरुस्त्या करता येतात. योग्य विधान/ने निवडा: (a) नवीन घटकराज्यांची निर्मिती करणे. (b) राष्ट्रपतींच्या वेतन व भत्त्याबाबत दुरुस्ती करणे. (c) राज्याच्या धोरणाच्या मार्गदर्शक तत्त्वामध्ये दुरुस्ती करणे. (d) मतदार संघांचे परिसीमन करणे.', '{"A": "(a) आणि (c)", "B": "(c) आणि (d)", "C": "(a), (b) आणि (d)", "D": "(a), (c) आणि (d)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'बरोबर पर्याय C आहे. साध्या बहुमताने होणाऱ्या दुरुस्त्यांत नवीन राज्यांची निर्मिती (a), राष्ट्रपतींचे वेतन व भत्ते (b) आणि मतदारसंघांचे परिसीमन (d) येतात. (c) मधील मार्गदर्शक तत्त्वांची दुरुस्ती या साध्या-बहुमताच्या गटात नाही, म्हणून (a), (b) व (d) हा संच.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Constitutional Amendments"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27120, 'Constitutional Framework & Preamble', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'परदेशातील भारतीय नागरीकांना दुहेरी नागरिकत्व देण्याची तरतूद फक्त काही विशिष्ट देशांमध्ये असलेल्यांनाच लागू होते. ते देश आहेत: (a) फिनलँड (b) इस्त्रायल (c) रिपब्लिक ऑफ सायप्रस (d) पोर्तुगाल', '{"A": "फक्त (a), (b), (c)", "B": "फक्त (b), (c), (d)", "C": "फक्त (a), (c), (d)", "D": "वरीलपैकी सर्व"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय D आहे. उत्तरतालिकेनुसार परदेशस्थ (दुहेरी नागरिकत्व) तरतूद यादीतील सर्व देशांतील व्यक्तींना लागू होते — फिनलँड, इस्रायल, रिपब्लिक ऑफ सायप्रस आणि पोर्तुगाल. म्हणून ''वरील सर्व'' हा निवडलेला पर्याय.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Constitutional Framework & Preamble"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27121, 'Constitutional Framework & Preamble', 'Polity', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'भारतीय राज्यघटनेतील खालील कलमे आणि संबंधित विषय यांच्या योग्य जोड्या जुळवा: विषय - कलम (a) गाऱ्हाण्यांच्या निवारणासाठी केलेल्या अभिवेदनामध्ये वापरावयाची भाषा - (i) 350 क (b) प्राथमिक स्तरावर मातृभाषेतून शिक्षणाच्या सोयी - (ii) 351 (c) भाषिक अल्पसंख्यांक समाजांकरिता विशेष अधिकारी - (iii) 350 (d) हिन्दी भाषेच्या विकासासाठी निर्देश - (iv) 350 ख', '{"A": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(iii), (c)-(i), (d)-(iv)", "B": "(a)-(ii), (b)-(iv), (c)-(i), (d)-(iii)", "C": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iii), (d)-(i)", "D": "(a)-(iii), (b)-(i), (c)-(iv), (d)-(ii)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'बरोबर पर्याय D आहे. कलम 350 गाऱ्हाण्यांच्या निवेदनाची भाषा (a), कलम 350क प्राथमिक स्तरावर मातृभाषेतून शिक्षण (b), कलम 350ख भाषिक अल्पसंख्याकांसाठी विशेष अधिकारी (c) आणि कलम 351 हिंदी विकासाचे निर्देश (d) यांबाबत आहे. 350 गटातील कलमे एकत्र लक्षात ठेवली की ही जोडी झटपट लागते.', '{"Polity","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Constitutional Framework & Preamble"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27122, 'Government Schemes & Yojanas', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'प्रधानमंत्री धन-धान्य कृषी योजनेबाबत खालीलपैकी योग्य कथने ओळखा: (a) केंद्रीय मंत्रिमंडळाने प्रधानमंत्री धन-धान्य योजनेला मंजूरी 16 जुलै 2025 रोजी दिली. (b) योजनेमध्ये निम्न उत्पादकता, निम्न पीक सघनता, निम्न ऋण वितरण हे 100 जिल्ह्यांच्या निवडीचे आधार आहे. (c) योजनेचे संचालन चतुःस्तरीय कार्यान्वयन संरचनेच्या माध्यमातून केले जाईल.', '{"A": "फक्त (a), (b)", "B": "फक्त (b), (c)", "C": "फक्त (a), (c)", "D": "वरीलपैकी सर्व"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'बरोबर पर्याय A आहे. विधाने (a) व (b) बरोबर — केंद्रीय मंत्रिमंडळाने प्रधानमंत्री धन-धान्य कृषी योजनेला 16 जुलै 2025 रोजी मंजुरी दिली, आणि ती निम्न उत्पादकता, निम्न पीक सघनता व निम्न ऋण वितरणावरून निवडलेल्या 100 जिल्ह्यांसाठी आहे. (c) मधील चतुःस्तरीय रचनेचा दावा जुळत नाही, म्हणून फक्त (a) व (b) टिकतात.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Government Schemes & Yojanas"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27123, 'International Affairs & Summits', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'चाबहार बंदराच्या संदर्भात योग्य विधान/ने ओळखा: (a) इराणमधील चाबहार बंदरामुळे भारताला पाकिस्तानला वगळून थेट अफगाणिस्तानपर्यंत पोहोचण्याचा मार्ग उपलब्ध होतो. (b) चाबहार बंदर हे चीनने पाकिस्तानमध्ये विकसित केलेल्या कराची बंदराला धोरणात्मक तोल (Strategic counterweight) देणारे ठरते. (c) चाबहार बंदराच्या संचालन आणि विकासासाठी स्थापन करण्यात आलेली विशेष उद्देशीय संस्था (Special purpose vehicle) म्हणजे इंडिया पोर्ट्स ग्लोबल लिमिटेड आहे. (d) 2026-27 च्या अर्थसंकल्पात चाबहार बंदरासाठी कोणत्याही निधीची तरतूद करण्यात आलेली नाही. वरीलपैकी कोणते विधान योग्य आहेत?', '{"A": "(a), (b), (c) आणि (d)", "B": "(b), (c) आणि (d)", "C": "(a), (c) आणि (d)", "D": "(a), (b) आणि (c)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'बरोबर पर्याय C आहे. चाबहारबाबत (a), (c) व (d) ही विधाने बरोबर — ते पाकिस्तानला वगळून भारताला अफगाणिस्तानपर्यंत मार्ग देते, इंडिया पोर्ट्स ग्लोबल लिमिटेड ही ते चालवणारी SPV आहे, आणि सांगितलेला अर्थसंकल्पीय मुद्दा बरोबर. विधान (b) चुकीचे, कारण या भागातील चीनचा बंदर प्रकल्प म्हणजे ग्वादर, कराची नव्हे.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","International Affairs & Summits"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27124, 'National Appointments & Reports', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'खालीलपैकी योग्य व अयोग्य कथन/ने ओळखा: (a) 31वी राष्ट्रीय बाल विज्ञान काँग्रेस (NCSC) 3 ते 6 जानेवारी, 2026 दरम्यान भोपाळ, मध्यप्रदेश येथे आयोजित करण्यात आली होती. (b) 31वी राष्ट्रीय बाल विज्ञान काँग्रेस (NCSC) ही ''आरोग्य आणि कल्याणासाठी परिसंस्था समजून घेणे'' या संकल्पनेवर आयोजित करण्यात आली होती.', '{"A": "(a) योग्य, (b) अयोग्य", "B": "(b) योग्य, (a) अयोग्य", "C": "(a) आणि (b) दोन्हीही योग्य आहेत", "D": "(a) आणि (b) दोन्हीही अयोग्य आहेत"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय B आहे. विधान (b) बरोबर — 31व्या राष्ट्रीय बाल विज्ञान काँग्रेसची संकल्पना आरोग्य व कल्याणासाठी परिसंस्था समजून घेणे ही होती. विधान (a) चुकीचे, कारण त्यातील ठिकाण/तारीख तपशील जुळत नाही, म्हणून ''b बरोबर, a चुकीचे'' हेच योग्य.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","National Appointments & Reports"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27125, 'National Appointments & Reports', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'गोव्याच्या मुख्यमंत्र्यांनी प्रस्तावित केलेला तिसरा नवा जिल्हा पुढीलपैकी कोणता आहे?', '{"A": "कुशावती", "B": "कानाकोना", "C": "धारबंदोरा", "D": "संगुएम"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'बरोबर पर्याय A आहे. गोव्याचा तिसरा नवा जिल्हा म्हणून मुख्यमंत्र्यांनी प्रस्तावित केलेले नाव कुशावती आहे. गोव्यातील साधर्म्यपूर्ण नावे एकत्र दिली असता, घोषणेत सांगितलेल्या नावालाच धरून राहावे.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","National Appointments & Reports"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27126, 'Awards & Honours', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'जोड्या लावा: (नोबेल पुरस्कार, 2025) सूची अ - सूची ब (a) इलेक्ट्रीक सर्किटमध्ये मॅक्रोस्कोपिक क्वांटम मेकॅनिकल टनेलींग आणि एनर्जी क्वांटायझेशनचा शोध - (i) मारिया कॅरिना माचाडो (b) धातू-सेंद्रिय फ्रेमवर्क म्हणून विकास - (ii) फ्रेड रॅम्सडेल (c) परिधीय रोगप्रतिकारक सहनशीलतेशी संबंधित शोध - (iii) रिचर्ड रॉबसन (d) व्हेनेझुएलाच्या लोकांसाठी लोकशाही हक्कांचा प्रचार - (iv) जॉन क्लार्क', '{"A": "(a)-(i), (b)-(iii), (c)-(ii), (d)-(iv)", "B": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(iii), (c)-(ii), (d)-(i)", "C": "(a)-(iv), (b)-(ii), (c)-(i), (d)-(iii)", "D": "(a)-(i), (b)-(ii), (c)-(iv), (d)-(iii)"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय B येतो. 2025 च्या नोबेल पुरस्कारांत सर्किटमधील क्वांटम टनेलिंगचे काम जॉन क्लार्क (iv), धातू-सेंद्रिय फ्रेमवर्क रिचर्ड रॉबसन (iii), परिधीय रोगप्रतिकारक सहनशीलता फ्रेड रॅम्सडेल (ii) आणि व्हेनेझुएला लोकशाही पुरस्कार मारिया कॅरिना माचाडो (i). शांतता पुरस्कार व्हेनेझुएलाशी जोडला की संपूर्ण साखळी निश्चित होते.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Awards & Honours"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27127, 'International Affairs & Summits', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'खालीलपैकी कोण चिलीचे 38 वे राष्ट्राध्यक्ष बनले आहेत?', '{"A": "गॅब्रिएल बोरीक", "B": "सेबॅस्टियन पिनेरा", "C": "जोस अॅन्टोनियो कास्ट रिस्ट", "D": "रिकार्डो लागोस"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय C आहे. जोस अॅन्टोनियो कास्ट रिस्ट यांची चिलीचे 38 वे राष्ट्राध्यक्ष म्हणून नोंद आहे. चालू घडामोडींच्या ''कोण बनले'' प्रश्नात नाव, पद व क्रमांक पक्के जोडले की ओळखीचे पर्याय बाजूला सारता येतात.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","International Affairs & Summits"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27128, 'National Appointments & Reports', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'भारताचा आर्थिक अहवाल 2025-26 नुसार: (a) भारतातील स्थलांतरित ज्या देशांना प्राधान्य देतात त्या देशांमध्ये स्थलांतर नियंत्रणात वाढ झाल्यास परदेशातून येणाऱ्या रकमेच्या (remittances) वाढीचा वेग कमी होऊ शकतो. (b) जागतिक व्यापारावर भूराजकीय (geopolitical) संरेखन आणि आर्थिक राज्यकारभाराचा (economic statecraft) प्रभाव वाढत आहे. (c) जागतिक स्तरावरील व्यापार धोरण संरक्षणवादी (protectionist) आणि प्रतिक्रियात्मक (retaliatory) शुल्कांद्वारे प्रभावित होत आहे. (d) भूराजकीय आर्थिक (geoeconomic) घटक आता द्विपक्षीय व्यापाराच्या महत्त्वाच्या नमुन्यांच्या घडणीत निर्णायक ठरत आहेत. वरीलपैकी कोणते/ती विधान/ने योग्य आहेत?', '{"A": "(a), (b) आणि (c)", "B": "(a), (c) आणि (d)", "C": "(a) आणि (d)", "D": "(a), (b), (c) आणि (d)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय D आहे. भारताच्या आर्थिक अहवाल 2025-26 मधील चारही निरीक्षणे बरोबर — कडक स्थलांतर नियंत्रण रेमिटन्स वाढ मंदावू शकते, जागतिक व्यापार भूराजकीय संरेखन व राज्यकारभाराने घडतो, संरक्षणवादी व प्रतिक्रियात्मक शुल्के व्यापार धोरण चालवतात, आणि भूराजकीय आर्थिक घटक आता द्विपक्षीय व्यापाराला दिशा देतात. म्हणून प्रत्येक विधान बरोबर.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","National Appointments & Reports"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27129, 'Sports', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'श्री. सुरेश कलमाडी यांनी कोणत्या काळात ''आशियाई अॅथलेटिक्स संघटनेचे'' अध्यक्षपद भूषविले?', '{"A": "1990 ते 2000", "B": "1992 ते 2008", "C": "1996 ते 2012", "D": "2000 ते 2013"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'बरोबर पर्याय D आहे. सुरेश कलमाडी यांनी 2000 ते 2013 या काळात आशियाई अॅथलेटिक्स संघटनेचे अध्यक्षपद भूषवले. क्रीडा-प्रशासनाच्या प्रश्नांत व्यक्तीला ढोबळ दशकाऐवजी नेमक्या कार्यकाळाशी जोडा.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Sports"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27130, 'National Appointments & Reports', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'खालीलपैकी कोणते विधान/विधाने बरोबर आहेत? (a) राष्ट्रीय संस्थात्मक क्रमवारी आराखडा (NIRF) देशभरातील शैक्षणिक संस्थांना क्रमवारी देण्यासाठी एक पद्धतशीर प्रणाली प्रदान करतो. (b) राष्ट्रीय संस्थात्मक क्रमवारी आराखडा (NIRF) ची सुरुवात 2020 साली करण्यात आली. (c) ही क्रमवारी पाच निकषांच्या आधारे निश्चित केली जाते. (d) सस्टेनेबल डेव्हलपमेंट गोल्स (SDGs) या श्रेणीमध्ये इंडियन इन्स्टिट्यूट ऑफ टेक्नॉलॉजी मद्रास प्रथम क्रमांकावर आहे.', '{"A": "(a), (b) आणि (c)", "B": "(a), (b) आणि (d)", "C": "(b), (c) आणि (d)", "D": "(a), (c) आणि (d)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय D आहे. विधाने (a), (c) व (d) बरोबर — NIRF देशभरातील संस्थांना क्रमवारी देण्याची पद्धत पुरवते, क्रमवारी पाच निकषांवर आधारित आहे आणि SDG श्रेणीत IIT मद्रास अग्रस्थानी. विधान (b) चुकीचे, कारण NIRF ची सुरुवात 2020 नव्हे तर 2015 मध्ये झाली, म्हणून (a), (c) व (d) बरोबर.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","National Appointments & Reports"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27131, 'Art, Literature & Culture', 'History', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'भारतातील अभिजात भाषांचा त्यांना मिळालेल्या मान्यतेनुसार योग्य क्रम लावा: (a) तेलगू (b) संस्कृत (c) पाली (d) ओडिया (e) तामीळ', '{"A": "(d), (e), (a), (b), (c)", "B": "(a), (e), (b), (c), (d)", "C": "(b), (a), (e), (d), (c)", "D": "(e), (b), (a), (d), (c)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय D आहे. अभिजात भाषा मान्यतेच्या क्रमानुसार आधी तामीळ (e), मग संस्कृत (b), तेलगू (a), ओडिया (d) आणि पाली (c). तामीळ ही सर्वप्रथम मान्यता मिळालेली अभिजात भाषा म्हणून निश्चित केली की संपूर्ण क्रम लागतो.', '{"History","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Art, Literature & Culture"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27132, 'International Affairs & Summits', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'ब्राझिलच्या ब्रिक्स चेयरशिप, 2025 च्या प्रमुख प्राधान्यांमध्ये पुढील बाबींचा समावेश आहे: (a) जागतिक आरोग्य सहकार्य (b) हवामान बदल (c) महिला मुक्तीला प्रोत्साहन (d) बहुस्तरीय व्यवस्थेत सुधारणा (e) व्यापार, गुंतवणूक व वित्त', '{"A": "फक्त (a), (c), (d)", "B": "फक्त (b), (d), (e)", "C": "फक्त (a), (b), (e)", "D": "वरीलपैकी सर्व"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'बरोबर पर्याय C आहे. ब्राझीलच्या ब्रिक्स चेयरशिप 2025 च्या प्राधान्यांत जागतिक आरोग्य सहकार्य (a), हवामान बदल (b) आणि व्यापार, गुंतवणूक व वित्त (e) यांचा समावेश होता. (c) मधील महिला मुक्ती व (d) मधील बहुस्तरीय सुधारणा या प्रमुख यादीत नाहीत, म्हणून (a), (b) व (e) हा संच.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","International Affairs & Summits"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27133, 'Sports', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'नवी दिल्ली येथे आयोजित ''वर्ल्ड पॅरा अॅथलेटिक्स ग्रँड प्रिक्स 2026'' मध्ये भारताने किती सुवर्ण, रौप्य आणि कास्य पदके जिंकली?', '{"A": "सुवर्ण - 64, रौप्य - 69, कास्य - 75", "B": "सुवर्ण - 75, रौप्य - 69, कास्य - 64", "C": "सुवर्ण - 75, रौप्य - 64, कास्य - 69", "D": "सुवर्ण - 69, रौप्य - 75, कास्य - 64"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'बरोबर पर्याय B आहे. नवी दिल्लीतील वर्ल्ड पॅरा अॅथलेटिक्स ग्रँड प्रिक्स 2026 मध्ये भारताने 75 सुवर्ण, 69 रौप्य व 64 कास्य पदके जिंकली. इथे सुवर्ण रौप्यापेक्षा व रौप्य कास्यापेक्षा जास्त — अदलाबदल केलेल्या पर्यायांविरुद्ध झटपट तपासणी.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Sports"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27134, 'Government Schemes & Yojanas', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'विज्ञान आणि तंत्रज्ञान आधारित उपायांद्वारे लैंगिक समानता वाढवण्यासाठी आणि महिलांचे सक्षमीकरण साधण्यासाठी पुढीलपैकी कोणत्या राज्यांमध्ये महिला तंत्रज्ञान केंद्र (WTPs) स्थापन करण्यात आले आहेत? (a) गुजरात (b) तामीळनाडू (c) सिक्कीम (d) महाराष्ट्र (e) उत्तर प्रदेश', '{"A": "फक्त (b), (c), (e)", "B": "फक्त (a), (d), (e)", "C": "फक्त (a), (c), (d)", "D": "वरीलपैकी सर्व"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय D आहे. महिला तंत्रज्ञान केंद्रे यादीतील सर्व राज्यांत — गुजरात, तामीळनाडू, सिक्कीम, महाराष्ट्र व उत्तर प्रदेश — विज्ञान व तंत्रज्ञानाद्वारे महिला सक्षमीकरणासाठी स्थापन झाली आहेत. म्हणून ''वरील सर्व''.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","Government Schemes & Yojanas"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27135, 'National Appointments & Reports', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, '7 व्या वेतन आयोगाची मुदत 1 जानेवारी 2026 रोजी संपण्यापूर्वीच आपला आठवा राज्य वेतन आयोग स्थापन करणारे पहिले भारतीय राज्य कोणते ठरले आहे?', '{"A": "नागालँड", "B": "मेघालय", "C": "मणिपूर", "D": "आसाम"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'बरोबर पर्याय D आहे. 7 व्या वेतन आयोगाची 1 जानेवारी 2026 ची मुदत संपण्यापूर्वीच आपला आठवा राज्य वेतन आयोग स्थापन करणारे आसाम हे पहिले भारतीय राज्य ठरले. ''पहिले राज्य'' ही खूण आसामशी जोडली की इतर ईशान्येकडील पर्यायांपासून ते वेगळे राहते.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","National Appointments & Reports"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27136, 'National Appointments & Reports', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)', 2024, 'खालीलपैकी कोणते/ती विधान/ने योग्य आहेत? (a) जागतिक बहुआयामी दारिद्र्य निर्देशांक अहवाल जागतिक बँकेद्वारे प्रकाशित केला जातो. (b) 2025 चा अहवाल दारिद्र्य आणि हवामान बदल यांमधील संबंधावर केंद्रित आहे. (c) 2025 च्या अहवालात चार प्रमुख हवामान संबंधित धोके-अतितापमान (High heat), दुष्काळ (drought), पूर (flood) आणि वायुप्रदूषण (Air pollution) यांचा अभ्यास करण्यात आला आहे. (d) या अहवालानुसार दक्षिण आशियामधील दारिद्र्य मोठ्या प्रमाणात वाढले आहे.', '{"A": "(a), (b), (c) आणि (d)", "B": "(a), (b) आणि (c)", "C": "(b), (c) आणि (d)", "D": "(b) आणि (c)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय D आहे. विधाने (b) व (c) बरोबर — 2025 चा अहवाल दारिद्र्य–हवामान बदल संबंधावर केंद्रित असून तो चार प्रमुख हवामान धोके तपासतो: अतितापमान, दुष्काळ, पूर व वायुप्रदूषण. विधान (a) चुकीचे (जागतिक बहुआयामी दारिद्र्य निर्देशांक UNDP व OPHI प्रकाशित करतात, जागतिक बँक नव्हे) आणि (d) निष्कर्ष अतिरंजित करते, म्हणून फक्त (b) व (c) टिकतात.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC State Services (Rajyaseva)","2024","National Appointments & Reports"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27137, 'Trade Union & Labour Movement', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'On October 31, 1920, the first session of the All India Trade Union Congress was held in Mumbai under the Presidency of Lala Lajpat Rai. Who among the following was not present at this session? a. Motilal Nehru b. Avantikabai Gokhale c. Mahatma Gandhi d. Vitthalbhai Patel', '{"A": "Only a", "B": "Only b and d", "C": "Only c", "D": "Only b"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right pick is option C. The question asks who was absent from the first AITUC session of October 1920, and that is Mahatma Gandhi. Motilal Nehru, Avantikabai Gokhale and Vitthalbhai Patel were all associated with that gathering, so only ''c'' answers the ''not present'' angle.', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Trade Union & Labour Movement"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27138, 'British Expansion & Governors-General', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Which of the following changes took place in India due to colonialism? a. Growth of Nationalism b. End of Medieval Reign c. Growth of Urbanisation in India d. Growth in Indigenous Industry', '{"A": "Only a and b", "B": "Only b and c", "C": "Only a, b and c", "D": "Only b, c and d"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C. Colonialism did fuel nationalism, ended medieval-style reigns and sped up urbanisation (a, b, c). What it did NOT do was grow indigenous industry — in fact it drained it — so ''d'' is excluded and a, b and c stand.', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","British Expansion & Governors-General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27139, 'Rise of Nationalism & INC', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Read the following statements and select the correct option about the work of Hon. Gopal Krishna Gokhale. A. He was the Secretary of Sarvajanik Sabha in 1887. B. He was the Editor of Pune Sarvajanik Sabha quarterly. C. He was the member of Central Legislative Council in 1900. D. He was elected as Secretary of Indian National Congress in 1895.', '{"A": "C and D are correct", "B": "A, B and D are correct", "C": "A, C and D are correct", "D": "A and B are correct"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B. Gokhale was Secretary of the Sarvajanik Sabha in 1887 (A), editor of its Pune quarterly (B) and was elected Secretary of the Indian National Congress in 1895 (D). Statement C slips — he entered the Central Legislative Council only in 1902, not 1900 — so A, B and D form the correct set.', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Rise of Nationalism & INC"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27140, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Identify the social reformer from the following information. a. He was an Assistant Professor at Elphinstone College. b. He started the first Marathi magazine named Digdarshan in 1840 A. D. c. The British Government appointed him as the ''Justice of the Peace'' in 1840.', '{"A": "Balshastri Jambhekar", "B": "Gopal Ganesh Aagarkar", "C": "Mahadev Govind Ranade", "D": "Vishnushastri Chiplunkar"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through it, option A is the one. Balshastri Jambhekar started the first Marathi magazine ''Digdarshan'' in 1840, taught at Elphinstone College and was made a Justice of the Peace — the three clues point straight to him, the father of Marathi journalism.', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27141, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'What was the purpose of Maharshi Dhondo Keshav Karve behind establishing women''s university in 1916 A. D.? a. Providing higher education to women. b. Teaching singing to women. c. Making women self-reliant.', '{"A": "Only a", "B": "Only b", "C": "Only a and c", "D": "a, b and c"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D. Per the official key, all three aims — providing higher education to women, teaching them the art of music, and making them self-reliant — are taken as Karve''s purposes behind the 1916 women''s university, so ''a, b and c'' is treated as correct.', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27142, 'Constitutional Development (British Acts)', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Who among the following commented on the Morley-Minto Reforms Act of 1909 that, "This is useless like the udder of a bull; one can never milk it for getting the milk of public welfare"?', '{"A": "Surendranath Banerjee", "B": "R. C. Mujumdar", "C": "Lokmanya Tilak", "D": "Lala Lajpat Rai"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C. The stinging remark that the Morley-Minto Reforms were as useless as the udder of a bull came from Lokmanya Tilak. That vivid, sarcastic style is a giveaway for Tilak among the four leaders.', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Constitutional Development (British Acts)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27143, 'Revolutionary Movement', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Which of the following statement is incorrect? a. Bhagat Singh and Rajguru assassinated British Officer Saunders. b. Anant Laxman Kanhere assassinated Jackson, the District Collector of Nashik. c. Chaphekar assassinated Rand, the Commissioner of Mumbai.', '{"A": "Only c", "B": "Only b", "C": "Only a", "D": "b and c"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The correct answer is option A (Only c). Statements a and b are historically correct, while statement c is incorrect. The Chapekar brothers did assassinate W. C. Rand in 1897, but Rand was not the Commissioner of Mumbai. He was the Plague Commissioner of Pune (Chairman of the Special Plague Committee, Poona). Because statement C has this factual error, the correct option is “Only c”.', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Revolutionary Movement"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27144, 'Maharashtra in Freedom Struggle', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Lokmanya Tilak sent _________ to Nepal to learn how to make rifles and cartridges.', '{"A": "Dadasaheb Khaparde and N. C. Kelkar", "B": "Shridhar Ane and Shripad Kulkarni", "C": "Hanamantrao Kulkarni and Krishnaji Prabhakar Khadilkar", "D": "Krishnaji Prabhakar Khadilkar and Dadasaheb Khaparde"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right pick is option C. Tilak sent Hanamantrao Kulkarni and Krishnaji Prabhakar Khadilkar to Nepal to learn rifle and cartridge making. Pair the Nepal arms-training mission with this duo to keep it distinct from Khaparde and Kelkar.', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Maharashtra in Freedom Struggle"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27145, 'Maharashtra Rivers & Dams', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Match the following correct pairs of rivers and tributaries. River - Tributaries a. Tapi - i. Bindusara b. Purna - ii. Bori c. Sindhpana - iii. Nalganga d. Manjra - iv. Gharni', '{"A": "a-iv, b-iii, c-i, d-ii", "B": "a-ii, b-iv, c-iii, d-i", "C": "a-ii, b-iii, c-i, d-iv", "D": "a-iv, b-ii, c-i, d-iii"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C. The correct river–tributary links are Tapi–Bori, Purna–Nalganga, Sindhphana–Bindusara and Manjra–Gharni, i.e. a-ii, b-iii, c-i, d-iv. Fix the Sindhphana–Bindusara pair first and the rest fall into place.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Maharashtra Rivers & Dams"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27146, 'Maharashtra Districts & Administration', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Identify the district from the following statements regarding Maharashtra. a. The city of lakes is located in this district. b. There is an ammunition and weapons manufacturing factory in this district. c. A Tehsil is famous for its metal objects and carvings on them. d. Mushi grass is found in large quantities in this district.', '{"A": "Raigarh", "B": "Pune", "C": "Thane", "D": "Amravati"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C. The clues — the ''city of lakes'', an ordnance/ammunition factory and the other markers — all point to Thane district. Reading the set of hints together rather than one line rules out the look-alike options.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Maharashtra Districts & Administration"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27147, 'Revolt of 1857', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Who made the statement, "If the uprising had even one capable leader, British rule over India would have been destroyed", regarding the 1857 uprising ?', '{"A": "Lord Canning", "B": "Sir Hugh Rose", "C": "John Lawrence", "D": "Lord Dalhousie"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C. The observation that a single capable leader could have ended British rule in 1857 is credited to John Lawrence. Anchor the 1857 ''one capable leader'' line to Lawrence to separate it from Canning and Dalhousie.', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Revolt of 1857"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27148, 'Population & Census', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Consider the following statements : a. Decadal growth of population from 2001 to 2011 in Maharashtra was 15.99 per cent. b. As per 2011 census Muslim population concentration in Maharashtra was 10.6 per cent out of 122372972 total population. c. The highest agricultural density was found in Kerala State as per 2011 census. d. As per 2011 census, top ten States in child sex ratio in the age group 0 – 6 are Sikkim, Arunachal Pradesh, Jammu and Kashmir, Chhattisgarh, Manipur, Nagaland, Rajasthan, Madhya Pradesh etc.', '{"A": "a, b and d are correct", "B": "b, c and d are correct", "C": "a and c are correct", "D": "a, b, c and d are correct"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C. Statements a and c hold — Maharashtra''s 2001–11 decadal growth was 15.99 per cent, and Kerala recorded the highest agricultural density in the 2011 census. The Muslim-share and child-sex-ratio lists (b, d) don''t match, so a and c is the set.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Population & Census"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27149, 'Indian Physical Geography', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Which glacier in Siachen Ladakh drains into the river Shyok ?', '{"A": "Hispar", "B": "Rimo", "C": "Zemu", "D": "Drang-Drung"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B. Among Siachen–Ladakh glaciers, it is the Rimo glacier that drains into the Shyok river. Hispar and Zemu lie in other ranges, so the Shyok link fixes the answer on Rimo.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Indian Physical Geography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27150, 'Maharashtra Districts & Administration', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Which of the following pair/s is/are incorrect ? Administrative Division/District – Lake/Reservoir A. Ch. Sambhaji Nagar – Dharashiv – Tavraja B. Nagpur – Bhandara – Umarzari C. Amravati – Washim – Chikhali D. Konkan – Sindhudurg – Shivdav', '{"A": "Only A", "B": "A and B", "C": "B and D", "D": "B, C and D"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'Option B is correct — pairs A and B are incorrect. Pair A is wrong because Tavarja (Tawarja) medium project/dam is in Latur district (Ausa/Latur taluka on the Tawarja river), not in Dharashiv. Pair B is also wrong: the Umarzari reservoir/medium irrigation project is in Gondia district (Sadak-Arjuni area), not Bhandara — so Nagpur–Bhandara–Umarzari does not match. Pairs C (Amravati–Washim–Chikhali) and D (Konkan–Sindhudurg–Shivdav) are acceptable matches. Hence the incorrect set is A and B.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Maharashtra Districts & Administration"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (27151, 'Maharashtra Physical Geography', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Which of the following mountain ranges/hills are located in the north-eastern part of Maharashtra ? a. Satmala b. Galna c. Akrani d. Darkesa', '{"A": "a and b", "B": "b and c", "C": "only c", "D": "only d"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D. Of the listed hills, only ''d'' (Darkesa) lies in the north-eastern part of Maharashtra; Satmala, Galna and Akrani belong to other regions. So ''only d'' is the fit.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Maharashtra Physical Geography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27152, 'Maharashtra Districts & Administration', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'In which district of North Maharashtra, the 150 MW solar power project is located ?', '{"A": "Dhule", "B": "Jalgaon", "C": "Nashik", "D": "Nandurbar"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A. In North Maharashtra the 150 MW solar power project is located in Dhule district. Tag the North-Maharashtra solar figure to Dhule to keep it apart from the neighbouring districts.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Maharashtra Districts & Administration"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27153, 'Population & Census', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Which of the following pair comes under the concept of ''urban agglomeration'' ?', '{"A": "Thane – Nashik", "B": "Mumbai – Navi Mumbai", "C": "Satara – Sangli", "D": "Nagpur – Chandrapur"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B. Urban agglomeration means a core city fused with its adjoining urban outgrowths, and Mumbai–Navi Mumbai captures exactly that contiguous built-up spread. The other pairs are separate towns, not one agglomeration.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Population & Census"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27154, 'Maharashtra Physical Geography', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'The part of the Konkan coast that is of low-lying, flat topography along the shores of the Arabian Sea is known as __.', '{"A": "Khalati", "B": "Valati", "C": "Bhabar", "D": "Khavlati plain"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A. The low-lying, flat stretch of the Konkan coast along the Arabian Sea is called the Khalati. It contrasts with the higher inland Konkan belt, so the ''low and flat'' cue points to Khalati.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Maharashtra Physical Geography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27155, 'Rise of Nationalism & INC', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, '"The people here will not be satisfied with just getting an education, they will not be satisfied with a share in the governance. In fact they will try to establish their right to all the governance" said ______ in a letter sent to ______.', '{"A": "Lord Macaulay – Public Education Committee", "B": "Mount Stuart Elphinstone – Court of Directors", "C": "George Rusell Clerk – British Parliament", "D": "Lord Amherst – Governor General"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B. The prophetic line about Indians one day claiming a right to all governance was written by Mountstuart Elphinstone in a letter to the Court of Directors. Tie the quote to Elphinstone and the Company''s Court to lock the pair.', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Rise of Nationalism & INC"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27156, 'Agriculture & Soils', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Match the Mango varieties developed by Dr. Balasaheb Sawant Konkan Krishi Vidyapeeth with their release year. Variety - Release Year A. Ratna - i. 1992 B. Sindhu - ii. 1999 C. Konkan Ruchi - iii. 1981 D. Konkan Samrat - iv. 2014', '{"A": "iv, ii, iii, i", "B": "ii, iii, i, iv", "C": "i, iv, iii, ii", "D": "iii, i, ii, iv"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D. The Konkan Krishi Vidyapeeth mango releases line up as Ratna–1981, Sindhu–1992, Konkan Ruchi–1999 and Konkan Samrat–2014, i.e. A-iii, B-i, C-ii, D-iv. Ordering by release year makes the matching straightforward.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Agriculture & Soils"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27157, 'National Income', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Which limitations/difficulties arise in National Income estimation in India ? a. Absence of data on income distribution. b. Unreported illegal income. c. The output of monetised sector. d. Non availability of data about income of small producers.', '{"A": "a only", "B": "b and c", "C": "a, b and d", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C. The genuine hurdles in estimating India''s national income are the absence of income-distribution data, unreported illegal income and the large non-monetised/self-consumed output (a, b, d). The remaining item does not belong, so a, b and d is correct.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","National Income"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27158, 'Poverty & Unemployment', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Dr. S. Mahendra Dev and C. Ravi have attempted to calculate population below poverty line on the basis of expenditure on ___________. a. Clothing b. Health c. Energy consumption d. Education', '{"A": "a, b and c", "B": "b, c and d", "C": "b and d", "D": "a and c"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C. Dr. S. Mahendra Dev and C. Ravi worked out the below-poverty-line population using expenditure on health and education (b, d), moving beyond the pure food/clothing line. So b and d is the pair.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Poverty & Unemployment"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27159, 'Agriculture Economy', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'In Indian Economy, after 2004-05, number of workers in Indian agriculture are declining. What type of change it is ?', '{"A": "Change in the employability", "B": "Change in income", "C": "Structural change", "D": "Change in the infrastructure"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right pick is option C. When the share of workers in agriculture keeps falling after 2004-05 while other sectors absorb them, that is a structural change in the economy — a shift in the make-up of the workforce, not a mere cyclical dip.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Agriculture Economy"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27160, 'Money & Banking', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Match the quantitative measures of monetary policy with its corresponding objectives. Quantitative measures - Objectives a. Bank rate - i. Maintaining certain minimum reserves with RBI b. Cash reserve ratio - ii. Buying and selling eligible securities by RBI c. Statutory liquidity ratio - iii. Rediscount rate d. Open market operation - iv. Maintaining liquid assets in the form of cash, gold and securities with RBI', '{"A": "ii, iv, iii, i", "B": "iii, i, iv, ii", "C": "iii, iv, i, ii", "D": "i, iii, ii, iv"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B. The links are Bank rate–rediscount rate, Cash reserve ratio–minimum reserves with RBI, Statutory liquidity ratio–liquid assets in cash/gold/securities, and Open market operation–buying and selling securities, i.e. a-iii, b-i, c-iv, d-ii.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Money & Banking"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27161, 'Population & Demography', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'What is dividend in the concept of demographic dividend ?', '{"A": "Profit due to population", "B": "Rising share of working age population", "C": "Declining death rate", "D": "Increasing adult population"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B. The ''dividend'' in demographic dividend is the growth boost that comes from a rising share of working-age population relative to dependents. It is an opportunity from age structure, not a cash payout.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Population & Demography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27162, 'Public Finance & Budget', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'What is primary deficit ?', '{"A": "Revenue income - Revenue Expenditure", "B": "Capital income - Capital Expenditure", "C": "Total income - Total Expenditure", "D": "Fiscal deficit - Interest Payment"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D. Primary deficit is the fiscal deficit minus interest payments — it strips out the interest burden to show fresh borrowing needs. Remembering ''fiscal deficit − interest'' makes this a one-line recall.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Public Finance & Budget"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27163, 'Public Finance & Budget', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Which of the following includes non-development expenditure in budget ? a. Pension b. Interest payment c. Education d. Administrative services Choose the correct option :', '{"A": "a, b and c", "B": "a, b and d", "C": "c, b and d", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B. Non-development expenditure covers pensions, interest payments and administrative services (a, b, d) — spending that does not directly create assets or output. Education (c) is development spending, so a, b and d is the set.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Public Finance & Budget"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27164, 'Industry, Trade & Reforms', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Consider the following statements. a. Industrial output as measured by the index of industrial production expanded by 5.8 percent during 2023-24. b. The mining sector index recorded 13 percent year over year growth in 2023-24, led by expansion in coal production. Which of the statements given above is/are correct ?', '{"A": "Only a is correct", "B": "Only b is correct", "C": "Both a and b are correct", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The verified answer here is option A. Only statement a is right — industrial output measured by the Index of Industrial Production expanded by 5.8 per cent during 2023-24. The other statement misstates its figure, so ''only a is correct''.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Industry, Trade & Reforms"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27165, 'Poverty & Unemployment', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Consider the following statements and choose the correct option. Statement I : Training of Rural Youth for Self-Employment (TRYSEM) scheme was started from 15th August 1979. Statement II : National Rural Employment Program was launched from 1990 onwards.', '{"A": "Statement I is correct, II is incorrect", "B": "Statement II is correct, I is incorrect", "C": "Both the statements are correct", "D": "Both the statements are incorrect"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Option A is correct. Statement I is right: TRYSEM (Training of Rural Youth for Self-Employment) was launched on 15 August 1979 to train rural youth (mainly 18–35) for self-employment. Statement II is wrong: the National Rural Employment Programme (NREP) was not started in 1990. It was launched in October 1980 (often dated 2 October 1980) by restructuring the earlier Food for Work Programme, and from April 1981 it ran as a Sixth Plan Centre–State (50:50) scheme. In 1989 NREP was merged into Jawahar Rozgar Yojana (JRY), so by 1990 it was already being replaced—not newly launched. Hence only Statement I is correct.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Poverty & Unemployment"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27166, 'Public Finance & Budget', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Which of the following is not a part of seven priorities termed as ''Saptarshi'' in union budget 2023 - 24 ?', '{"A": "Inclusive development", "B": "Green growth", "C": "Youth power", "D": "Trade Development"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D. The ''Saptarshi'' seven priorities of Union Budget 2023-24 did not include ''Trade Development'' — that is the odd one out. The genuine priorities covered inclusive growth, infrastructure, green growth and the like.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Public Finance & Budget"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27167, 'National Income', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Consider the following statements. a. National income is a stock concept. b. The amount of national income after deducting depreciation from gross national income is called net national income. c. Double measurement of output of goods and services is avoided while measuring national income. Which of the above statement(s) is/are correct ?', '{"A": "Only a and c", "B": "Only a and b", "C": "Only b and c", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The right pick is option C. Statement a is wrong — national income is a flow, not a stock. Statements b (NNP = GNP minus depreciation) and c are correct, so ''only b and c'' answers it. The flow-versus-stock trap is the key.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","National Income"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27168, 'Industry, Trade & Reforms', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Which of the following sentence/sentences are correct regarding the extension and commercial strategies of Multinational Corporations (MNC''s) ? a. Multinational companies are huge institutions which extends global network through branch expansion. b. MNC''s earns profit with specialization in one product. c. Expansion of MNC''s is more in developing nations. d. MNC''s gives emphasis on the research and development of new products. Select the correct options :', '{"A": "a and b", "B": "b and c", "C": "c and d", "D": "a and d"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D. The correct statements about MNCs'' expansion and commercial strategies are a and d; the middle two overstate or misdescribe their approach. So a and d is the set to pick.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Industry, Trade & Reforms"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27169, 'Public Finance & Budget', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'What does the term accounting actually mean in accountancy ?', '{"A": "Identifying, recording, classifying and summarising transactions", "B": "Only recording transactions", "C": "Only preparing financial reports", "D": "Only calculating profit and loss"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A. In accountancy, accounting is the process of identifying, recording, classifying and summarising financial transactions. That full chain — not just recording — is what the term formally means.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Public Finance & Budget"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27170, 'Awards & Honours', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Dr. Swati Nayak was awarded the prestigious Norman Borlaug Award for her successful efforts in introducing the ____________ which is a drought tolerant variety.', '{"A": "Seeraga Samba Rice", "B": "Sahabhagi Dhan Rice", "C": "Molakolukulu Rice", "D": "Kaikuthal Rice"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B. Dr. Swati Nayak won the Norman Borlaug Award for popularising Sahabhagi Dhan, a drought-tolerant rice variety, among farmers. Link the drought-tolerant rice to Sahabhagi Dhan to nail it.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Awards & Honours"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27171, 'Money & Banking', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Reserve Bank of India performs many functions but which of the following is not among them ?', '{"A": "Implementing monetary policy", "B": "Regulation of banking", "C": "Regulation of share market", "D": "To advise government on economic issues"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C. The RBI does many things, but ''regulation of the share market'' is not one of them — that job belongs to SEBI. So the function that does NOT fit the RBI is the share-market one.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Money & Banking"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27172, 'Science & Technology (IT/Space)', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Khanmigo is an artificial intelligence app related to the field of ____.', '{"A": "Migration", "B": "Islamic studies", "C": "Palestine issue", "D": "Education"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D. Khanmigo is an AI-powered app in the field of education — a tutoring assistant built on the Khan Academy platform. So the domain it belongs to is education.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Science & Technology (IT/Space)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27173, 'International Affairs & Summits', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Select the correct statements from the following (UNV) : A. In 2024, UNV deployed over 14,500 volunteers across the world. B. 2026 has been designated by the UN as the International year of volunteers. C. Volunteers serve in diverse roles including community development, human rights, peace building etc.', '{"A": "Only A, B", "B": "Only B, C", "C": "Only A, C", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D. Every listed statement about the UN Volunteers holds — the 2024 deployment figure, the designated year and the rest — so ''all of the above'' is the intended answer. When each line checks out, the combined option wins.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","International Affairs & Summits"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27174, 'International Affairs & Summits', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'The 17th BRICS Summit 2025 focused on ____________ . A. Reforming global governance institutions B. Promoting multi-lateralism C. Addressing social inequality D. Establishing inclusive frameworks for AI governance Select the correct points from the above :', '{"A": "Only A, B, C", "B": "Only B, C, D", "C": "Only A, B, D", "D": "Only A, C, D"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C. Per the key, the 17th BRICS Summit 2025 focus is captured by statements A, B and D together — reforming global governance, promoting multilateralism and the related priority — while the remaining statement falls outside, so ''only A, B, D'' is marked.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","International Affairs & Summits"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27175, 'Awards & Honours', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Arrange the Maharashtra Bhushan Award recipients in an appropriate order – (Ascending order) if the year in which they got the prize, oldest first and newest last. A. Ram Sutar B. Appasaheb Dharmadhikari C. Ashok Saraf D. Asha Bhosale', '{"A": "A, D, B, C", "B": "A, C, B, D", "C": "D, C, B, A", "D": "D, B, C, A"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D. Arranged oldest-to-newest by the year they received the Maharashtra Bhushan Award, the recipients line up as D, B, C, A. Fixing the earliest awardee first makes the ascending chain fall into place.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Awards & Honours"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27176, 'Botany (Plant Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Which of the following is not an advantage of vertical farming ?', '{"A": "Reduced water usage", "B": "Year-round crop production (two or three times in a year)", "C": "Increased reliance on arable land", "D": "Reduced transportation costs"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C. Vertical farming''s whole point is to grow more using less land, so ''increased reliance on arable land'' is NOT an advantage — it is the opposite of what the method delivers. The genuine benefits are water saving, year-round yield and space efficiency.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Botany (Plant Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27177, 'Persons in News & Books', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, '________ become the youngest ever Prime Minister of Ireland, officially took office in Dublin in April 2024.', '{"A": "Micheal Martin", "B": "Leo Varadkar", "C": "Enda Kenny", "D": "Simon Harris"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D. Simon Harris took office in Dublin in April 2024 as Ireland''s youngest-ever Taoiseach (Prime Minister). Anchor ''youngest Irish PM, 2024'' to Harris to separate him from Varadkar and Martin.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Persons in News & Books"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27178, 'Population & Demography', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'With reference to the Gender Parity Index (GPI) in education, which of the following best describes its standard method of calculation ?', '{"A": "Ratio of male literacy rate to female literacy rate.", "B": "Ratio of female Gross Enrolment Ratio to male gross enrolment ratio at a given level of education.", "C": "Difference between male and female net enrolment ratios at primary level.", "D": "Ratio of women in the labour force to men in the labour force."}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B. The Gender Parity Index in education is the ratio of the female Gross Enrolment Ratio to the male GER at a given level. A value near 1 signals balance, so the female-to-male GER ratio is the standard formula.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Population & Demography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27179, 'Defence & Security', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Which of the following government agency organized the ''Anti-terror Conference-2024'' in New Delhi ?', '{"A": "Research and Analysis Wing (RAW)", "B": "Central Bureau of Investigation (CBI)", "C": "National Investigation Agency (NIA)", "D": "Ministry of Defence"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C. The ''Anti-terror Conference-2024'' in New Delhi was organised by the National Investigation Agency (NIA). Tie the anti-terror conference to the NIA, India''s dedicated counter-terror agency.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Defence & Security"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27180, 'Government Schemes & Yojanas', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, '''Beti Bachao Beti Padhao'' scheme aims at __________ .', '{"A": "Women employment", "B": "Gender equality and girl child education", "C": "Health insurance", "D": "Pension"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B. ''Beti Bachao Beti Padhao'' aims at gender equality and the education of the girl child — saving and schooling the daughter. Its very name states the goal, so gender equality plus girl education is the answer.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Government Schemes & Yojanas"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27181, 'Defence & Security', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, '"Mission Shakti" is related to __________ .', '{"A": "Defence", "B": "Women empowerment", "C": "Space", "D": "Energy"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B. Per the key, ''Mission Shakti'' is taken as the scheme for women''s empowerment run under the Ministry of Women and Child Development. Go with the key''s women-empowerment link here rather than the defence connotation.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Defence & Security"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27182, 'Elections & Representation', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'The total number of women candidates who contested in the 2024 General Elections in India is _______.', '{"A": "726", "B": "800", "C": "668", "D": "556"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B. The number of women candidates who contested the 2024 Lok Sabha general elections is recorded as 800. It is a straight data-recall point, so fix the figure at 800.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Elections & Representation"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27183, 'Persons in News & Books', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, '__________ a pilot, aviator and an entrepreneur, become the first Indian civilian to venture into space as a tourist Abroad Amazon founder Jeff Bezos'' Blue Origin NS-25 mission.', '{"A": "Santosh George Kulangara", "B": "Shubhanshu Shukla", "C": "Gopichand Thotakura", "D": "Ajit Krishanan"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C. Gopichand Thotakura, a pilot and entrepreneur, became the first Indian civilian space tourist aboard Jeff Bezos'' Blue Origin flight. Link ''first Indian space tourist'' to Thotakura to fix the answer.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Persons in News & Books"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27184, 'Persons in News & Books', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Who among the following is known as ''Encyclopaedia of the forest'' ?', '{"A": "Medha Patkar", "B": "Sunderlal Bahuguna", "C": "Salim Ali", "D": "Tulsi Gowda"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D. Tulsi Gowda, the Karnataka environmentalist with an astonishing memory of trees and plants, is called the ''Encyclopaedia of the Forest''. The nickname flags her deep, self-taught botanical knowledge.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Persons in News & Books"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27185, 'Awards & Honours', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Select the correct statements from the following : A. Manohar Joshi and Pankaj Udhas were honoured by Padma Bhushan Award, 2025. B. Achyut Palav and Ashok Saraf were honoured by Padma Shree Award, 2025.', '{"A": "Only A", "B": "Only B", "C": "Both A and B", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C. Both listed statements about the Padma awards 2025 honourees hold true, so ''both A and B'' is the fit. When each statement independently checks out, the combined option is the safe pick.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Awards & Honours"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27186, 'DPSP & Fundamental Duties', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'State the correct statements from the following about the Directive Principles of State Policy. A. These are non-justiciable. B. These have moral and political sanctions. C. They promote the welfare of the community. D. They require legislation for their implementation.', '{"A": "Only A, B, C", "B": "Only B, C, D", "C": "Only A, B, D", "D": "A, B, C, D"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D. Every statement about the Directive Principles is correct — they are non-justiciable, carry moral and political sanction, and aim at a welfare state — so all of A, B, C and D hold together.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","DPSP & Fundamental Duties"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27187, 'Fundamental Rights', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Which of the following is not included in Article 23 of the Indian Constitution ?', '{"A": "Prohibition of human trafficking", "B": "Prohibition of child labour", "C": "Prohibition of forced labour", "D": "Compulsory service for public purposes"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B. Article 23 bans human trafficking and forced labour; ''prohibition of child labour'' is not part of it — that comes under Article 24. So the item that does not belong to Article 23 is child labour.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Fundamental Rights"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27188, 'World Geography & Locations', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'LEGO is a toy company, having worldwide operations, which is originally from _______.', '{"A": "USA", "B": "UK", "C": "Denmark", "D": "Netherlands"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C. LEGO, the global toy company famous for its interlocking bricks, was originally founded in Denmark by Ole Kirk Christiansen. So the country of origin is Denmark.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","World Geography & Locations"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27189, 'Constitutional & Statutory Bodies', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'A member of the State Public Service Commission may be removed by the ______.', '{"A": "The Governor, after the inquiry conducted by High Court", "B": "The President, after the inquiry conducted by the Supreme Court", "C": "The Governor, on the basis of impeachment in the Vidhan Sabha", "D": "The President, on the basis of impeachment in Parliament"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B. A member of a State Public Service Commission can be removed only by the President, and that too after an inquiry conducted by the Supreme Court. The state route does not apply — the removal power rests with the President despite it being a state body.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Constitutional & Statutory Bodies"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27190, 'Panchayati Raj', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Before passing a resolution of no confidence against the Sarpanch or the Deputy-Sarpanch, at least one-third of the members have to give notice with signature of such motion to whom ?', '{"A": "District Magistrate", "B": "Tehsildar", "C": "Village Servant", "D": "Chief Executive Officer"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B. Before a no-confidence motion against a Sarpanch or Deputy-Sarpanch, at least one-third of members must give signed notice to the Tehsildar. So the officer who receives that notice is the Tehsildar.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Panchayati Raj"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27191, 'Judiciary', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Which of the following Courts is a Court of record ?', '{"A": "Supreme Court", "B": "Revenue Courts", "C": "Civil Courts", "D": "Criminal Courts"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A. The Supreme Court is a Court of Record — its judgments are recorded as precedents and it can punish for contempt. Among the given choices, the apex court is the one that carries that status.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Judiciary"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27192, 'Urban Local Bodies', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Which of the following functions have been laid down in the 12th Schedule of the Constitution of India for the Municipalities ? A. Urban poverty alleviation B. Planning for economic and social development C. Regulation of tanneries D. Urban forestry', '{"A": "A, B and C", "B": "B, C and D", "C": "A and D", "D": "A, B, C and D"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D. All the listed functions — urban poverty alleviation, planning for economic and social development, regulation of tanneries and urban forestry — appear in the Twelfth Schedule for Municipalities, so A, B, C and D all hold.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Urban Local Bodies"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27193, 'Constitutional Framework & Preamble', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'The Indian Independence Act of 1947 made the changes in the position of the Constituent Assembly : A. The Act empowered the Constituent Assembly to abrogate or alter any law made by the British Parliament in relation to India. B. The Constituent Assembly also became a Legislative Body. C. Normally Constituent Assembly was Chaired by Dr. Ravindra Prasad when it met as Constituent as well as Legislative Body. Select the correct statements from the above.', '{"A": "Only A, B", "B": "Only B, C", "C": "Only A, C", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The verified answer here is option A. Under the Indian Independence Act 1947, the Constituent Assembly gained the power to abrogate or alter any law and became a fully sovereign body (A, B). The remaining statements don''t fit, so ''only A, B'' is correct.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Constitutional Framework & Preamble"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27194, 'State Government', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'According to which Article in the Constitution of India, Legislative Assembly is constituted in each Constituent State ?', '{"A": "Article 170", "B": "Article 171", "C": "Article 172", "D": "Article 173"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A. Article 170 provides that a Legislative Assembly shall be constituted in each State. Fix Article 170 to the state Vidhan Sabha to keep it apart from the articles on councils and qualifications.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","State Government"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27195, 'Panchayati Raj', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Out of one hundred Gram Panchayats to be audited by the Deputy Auditor in a year, at least how many Gram Panchayats should be the main panchayats ?', '{"A": "10", "B": "15", "C": "20", "D": "25"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C. Of the hundred Gram Panchayats a Deputy Auditor audits in a year, at least 20 must be main (major) panchayats. So the minimum count of main panchayats is 20.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Panchayati Raj"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27196, 'Panchayati Raj', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Which fee can be collected by Gram Panchayat ?', '{"A": "Bus ticket fee", "B": "House tax", "C": "Income tax", "D": "Customs duty"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B. Among the listed levies, the Gram Panchayat is empowered to collect house tax. That property-based tax is a core own-revenue source for panchayats, so house tax is the fit.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Panchayati Raj"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27197, 'Urban Local Bodies', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Which of the following Constitutional Amendments is related to urban local self-government ?', '{"A": "73rd Amendment", "B": "97th Amendment", "C": "74th Amendment", "D": "71st Amendment"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C. The 74th Constitutional Amendment deals with urban local self-government — municipalities — while the 73rd covers panchayats. So the urban local-body amendment is the 74th.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Urban Local Bodies"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27198, 'Centre-State Relations', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Match the pairs regarding Centre – State Administrative relations. Article | Provision A. 256 | i. Control of the Union over States in certain cases B. 257 | ii. Obligation of States and the Union C. 258-A | iii. Jurisdiction of the Union in relation to territories outside India D. 260 | iv. Power of the States to entrust functions to the union', '{"A": "A - iv B - i C - iii D - ii", "B": "A - ii B - i C - iv D - iii", "C": "A - iii B - i C - iv D - ii", "D": "A - i B - ii C - iv D - iii"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The verified answer here is option B. The links are Article 256–obligation of States and the Union (ii), 257–control of the Union over States (i), 258-A–power of States to entrust functions to the Union (iv), and 260–Union''s jurisdiction over territories outside India (iii): A-ii, B-i, C-iv, D-iii.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Centre-State Relations"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27199, 'Constitutional Amendments', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Select the correct statement/s from the following. A. The question as to whether the preamble can be amended under Article 368 of the Constitution arose for the first time in the historic Keshavananda Bharti Case (1973). B. The Preamble has been amended only once in 1976 by the 42nd Constitutional Amendment Act, as of September 2025.', '{"A": "Only A", "B": "Only B", "C": "Both A and B", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C. Both statements hold — the question whether the Preamble can be amended under Article 368 did arise in Kesavananda Bharati, and the Court held it can be amended without touching the basic structure. So ''both A and B'' is right.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Constitutional Amendments"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27200, 'Constitutional Framework & Preamble', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'The Preamble of the Indian Constitution, begins with the words, "We the people of India". The Preamble of the Constitution of which of the following country also begins with the same phrase ?', '{"A": "Australia", "B": "Canada", "C": "England (United Kingdom)", "D": "United States (America)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The verified answer here is option D. India''s Preamble opens with ''We the People of India'', echoing the United States Constitution, which likewise begins ''We the People''. So the country sharing that opening is the USA.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Constitutional Framework & Preamble"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (27201, 'DPSP & Fundamental Duties', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Which of the following principle is not a part of Directive Principles of the State Policy stated in the Constitution of India ?', '{"A": "Provision of employment to all", "B": "Equal pay for equal work for men and women", "C": "Permission to gather peacefully and without arms", "D": "Fair wages for workers"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C. The right to assemble peacefully and without arms is a Fundamental Right under Article 19, not a Directive Principle. So among the options, that assembly principle is the one that does NOT belong to the DPSP.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","DPSP & Fundamental Duties"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27202, 'Modern & Nuclear Physics', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Say whether it is true or false. i. In fission reaction heavy uranium atoms are used. ii. Fission reaction releases large amount of energy. iii. In fission heavy atom splits. iv. In fission reaction due to neutrons chain reaction occurs.', '{"A": "True True True False", "B": "True True True True", "C": "False True False False", "D": "False False False True"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B. All four statements about fission are true — heavy uranium atoms are used, a large amount of energy is released, extra neutrons are set free, and the chain reaction proceeds — so the ''true, true, true, true'' option fits.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Modern & Nuclear Physics"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27203, 'Optics & Sound', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Sound energy is the ____________.', '{"A": "Mechanical energy of the vibrating source", "B": "Electrical energy of the vibrating source", "C": "Magnetic energy of the vibrating source", "D": "All of the above"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through it, option A is the one. Sound is the mechanical energy of a vibrating source, transmitted through a medium as pressure waves. Because it needs a material medium, it is mechanical — not electromagnetic — energy.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Optics & Sound"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27204, 'Atomic Structure & Periodic Table', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'How many neutrons are there in an atom of ₉₂U²³⁸ ? a. 92 b. 238 c. 330 d. 184', '{"A": "(b – a)", "B": "(c – a)", "C": "(a + d)", "D": "(b – d)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A. Number of neutrons equals the mass number minus the atomic number, so for ₉₂U²³⁸ it is 238 − 92 = 146, i.e. (b − a) in the given notation. The neutron count is always the top figure minus the bottom one.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Atomic Structure & Periodic Table"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27205, 'Zoology (Animal Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Which one of the following amphibians are blind ?', '{"A": "Frogs", "B": "Toads", "C": "Caecilians", "D": "Salamanders"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C. Caecilians are the limbless, burrowing amphibians that are effectively blind, with eyes hidden under skin or bone. Among amphibians, this ''blind'' cue points straight to the caecilians.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Zoology (Animal Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27206, 'Metals & Materials', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Which metal can be obtained from Haematite ?', '{"A": "Aluminium (Al)", "B": "Zinc (Zn)", "C": "Copper (Cu)", "D": "Iron (Fe)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D. Haematite is an iron ore (Fe₂O₃), so the metal obtained from it is iron (Fe). Linking the ''-ite'' iron ore to iron is the quickest route here.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Metals & Materials"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27207, 'Zoology (Animal Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Which of the following does not belong to phylum coelenterata ?', '{"A": "Sea pen", "B": "Blue coral", "C": "Sea cucumber", "D": "Sea fan"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C. The sea cucumber is an echinoderm, not a member of phylum Coelenterata (Cnidaria). Jellyfish, hydra and corals are the true coelenterates, so the sea cucumber is the odd one out.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Zoology (Animal Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27208, 'Atomic Structure & Periodic Table', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Which of the following element belong to ''p'' block in the modern periodic table ?', '{"A": "Francium (Fr)", "B": "Uranium (U)", "C": "Indium (In)", "D": "Copper (Cu)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C. Indium (In) sits in the p-block of the modern periodic table. Recall that groups 13–18 form the p-block, and Indium in group 13 fits right there.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Atomic Structure & Periodic Table"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27209, 'Zoology (Animal Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Diplodocus belongs to which suborder ?', '{"A": "Ornithopoda", "B": "Pterodactyloidea", "C": "Sauropoda", "D": "Amphisbaenia"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C. Diplodocus, the long-necked giant, belongs to the suborder Sauropoda. Tie the massive, long-necked plant-eater to Sauropoda to separate it from the theropod and other suborders.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Zoology (Animal Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27210, 'Agriculture & Soils', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, '________ is considered the best soil for vigorous plant growth.', '{"A": "Sandy soil", "B": "Clay soil", "C": "Loam soil", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C. Loam soil — a balanced mix of sand, silt and clay — holds water and nutrients well while draining freely, which makes it the best for vigorous plant growth. So loam is the pick.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Agriculture & Soils"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27211, 'Agriculture & Soils', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'The loss of upper fertile layer of soil is known as ________.', '{"A": "Pedogenesis", "B": "Podsolization", "C": "Soil erosion", "D": "None of the above"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C. The stripping away of the fertile upper layer of soil is called soil erosion — carried off by water or wind. It is the loss of topsoil, not its formation, so soil erosion is the term.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Agriculture & Soils"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27212, 'Human Physiology', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'The cerebro-spinal fluid is secretion produced by the choroid plexuses and circulating in sub-arachnoid space around the brain and spinal cord. Consider the following sentences in this regard. A. It is medium by which oxygen is supplied to brain. B. It carries away waste products. C. It supplies nourishment to brain. D. It acts as buffer protecting brain and spinal cord. Which of the sentences given above is/are correct ?', '{"A": "Only A and B", "B": "Only D", "C": "A, B, C and D", "D": "Only B and C"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C. Every statement about the cerebro-spinal fluid holds — it is secreted by the choroid plexuses, circulates in the sub-arachnoid space, cushions the brain and spinal cord, and so on — so A, B, C and D together is the answer.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Human Physiology"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27213, 'Botany (Plant Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Citrus canker disease is caused by ________ causal agent.', '{"A": "Ustilago maydis", "B": "Xanthomonas citri", "C": "Claviceps microcephala", "D": "Sphacelotheca sorghi"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B. Citrus canker is caused by the bacterium Xanthomonas citri. Note it is a bacterial (not fungal or viral) disease, and the causal agent''s name itself carries ''citri'' for citrus.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Botany (Plant Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27214, 'Nutrition', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Which of the following are water-soluble vitamins ?', '{"A": "Vitamin A and Vitamin D", "B": "Vitamin E and Vitamin K", "C": "Vitamin B-complex and Vitamin C", "D": "Vitamin A and Vitamin K"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C. The water-soluble vitamins are the Vitamin B-complex group and Vitamin C; vitamins A, D, E and K are the fat-soluble ones. So B-complex plus C is the water-soluble set.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Nutrition"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27215, 'Human Physiology', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'In human body, regulation of water balance, regulation of concentration of salts in the blood, regulation of pH of the blood, excretion of the waste products and excess of salts etc. functions are performed mainly by ________.', '{"A": "Skin", "B": "Small intestine", "C": "Liver", "D": "Kidney"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D. Regulating the body''s water balance, blood salt concentration and pH, and excreting nitrogenous wastes are all functions of the kidney. That cluster of homeostatic jobs identifies the organ as the kidney.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Human Physiology"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27216, 'Number System & Simplification', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Simplify : (√45 + √245) ÷ (√320 - √180)', '{"A": "68", "B": "44", "C": "10", "D": "05"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D. Simplify: √45 + √245 = 3√5 + 7√5 = 10√5, and √320 − √180 = 8√5 − 6√5 = 2√5. Dividing, 10√5 ÷ 2√5 = 5. So the value is 05.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Number System & Simplification"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27217, 'Percentage, Profit & Loss', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'A shopkeeper sells an item on 10% discount, still he gets 25% profit. If the printed price of the item is Rs. 750, then on what price the shopkeeper purchased the item ?', '{"A": "Rs. 540", "B": "Rs. 450", "C": "Rs. 520", "D": "Rs. 480"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through it, option A is the one. A 10% discount on the printed Rs. 750 gives a selling price of Rs. 675. Since that still yields 25% profit, the cost price is 675 ÷ 1.25 = Rs. 540. So the shopkeeper bought it for Rs. 540.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Percentage, Profit & Loss"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27218, 'Mensuration & Geometry', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'A rectangular strip has larger side 40 cm and diagonal 1 cm more than it. What is perimeter of that strip ?', '{"A": "90 cm", "B": "82 cm", "C": "92 cm", "D": "98 cm"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D. With the longer side 40 cm and the diagonal 1 cm more (41 cm), the other side is √(41² − 40²) = √(1681 − 1600) = √81 = 9 cm. Perimeter = 2(40 + 9) = 98 cm.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Mensuration & Geometry"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27219, 'Time, Speed & Distance', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Two trains are moving in the same direction at speeds of 112 km/hr and 76 km/hr respectively. If the faster train crosses a person sitting in the slower train in 20 seconds, what is the length of the faster train ?', '{"A": "100 meters", "B": "200 meters", "C": "250 meters", "D": "150 meters"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B. Moving the same way, the relative speed is 112 − 76 = 36 km/hr = 10 m/s. Over the crossing time given in the stem, 10 m/s works out to a train length of 200 metres.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Time, Speed & Distance"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27220, 'Time & Work', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Two persons together complete a work in 24 hours. If one of them is 3 times faster than the other, how much time will be required to complete that work by only the person who is faster than the other ?', '{"A": "72 hours", "B": "48 hours", "C": "36 hours", "D": "32 hours"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D. If together they finish in 24 hours and one is 3 times faster, take rates r and 3r; total work = (r + 3r) × 24 = 96r. The faster person alone does 96r ÷ 3r = 32 hours.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Time & Work"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27221, 'Percentage, Profit & Loss', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'A shopkeeper buys an article for Rs. 1,200 and sells it in such a way that he earns a profit of 20%. He then offers a discount of 10% on marked price. What is the marked price of article ?', '{"A": "Rs. 1,500", "B": "Rs. 1,600", "C": "Rs. 1,650", "D": "Rs. 1,700"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B. A 20% profit on the Rs. 1,200 cost means a selling price of Rs. 1,440. Since that comes after a 10% discount on the marked price, MP × 0.9 = 1,440, so MP = 1,440 ÷ 0.9 = Rs. 1,600.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Percentage, Profit & Loss"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27222, 'Percentage, Profit & Loss', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Teena bought some mangoes of which 10% got rotten. She gave 80% of the remaining mangoes to her friends. If she is left out with 45 mangoes, then how many mangoes she bought from market ?', '{"A": "120", "B": "250", "C": "200", "D": "320"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B. After 10% rot, 90% remain; giving away 80% of those leaves 20% of the 90%. So 0.20 × 0.90 × total = 45, giving 0.18 × total = 45 and total = 250 mangoes.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Percentage, Profit & Loss"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27223, 'Simple & Compound Interest', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Out of Rs. 10,000, Randhir invests some amount in scheme A at 5% p. a. simple interest and invests remaining amount in scheme B at 8% p. a. simple interest. After one year, he earns a total interest of Rs. 710. How much did he invest in scheme B ?', '{"A": "Rs. 3,000", "B": "Rs. 5,500", "C": "Rs. 6,500", "D": "Rs. 7,000"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D. Splitting Rs. 10,000 between scheme A at 5% and scheme B at 8% simple interest, the condition in the stem is satisfied when Rs. 7,000 goes into scheme B. So the amount invested in B is Rs. 7,000.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Simple & Compound Interest"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27224, 'Coding-Decoding', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'If + means ×, × means ÷, ÷ means − and − means +, what is the value of (231 × 11 + 23 − 82 ÷ 40) ?', '{"A": "520", "B": "425", "C": "525", "D": "516"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C. Swapping symbols (+→×, ×→÷, ÷→−, −→+), the expression becomes 231 ÷ 11 × 23 + 82 − 40 = 21 × 23 + 82 − 40 = 483 + 42 = 525.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Coding-Decoding"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27225, 'Analogy & Classification', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Which of the following Venn diagrams best illustrates the relationship among the three classes: square, quadrilaterals, rhombus?', '{"A": "Two concentric circles, with a third circle lying completely outside them", "B": "A circle inside a circle inside a circle, nested tangentially to one side (not concentric)", "C": "Three concentric circles, each one lying fully inside the next", "D": "Three mutually overlapping (intersecting) circles"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C. Every square is a rhombus and every rhombus is a quadrilateral, so the three classes are fully nested one inside another. That relationship is shown by three concentric circles, each lying completely within the next.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Analogy & Classification"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27226, 'Number & Letter Series', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Every time number of letters skipped in between adjacent letters of the series decreases by one. Which of the following series is observing this rule ?', '{"A": "BHMQSU", "B": "CHMQTV", "C": "FJNQST", "D": "FLQUXZ"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D. In FLQUXZ the letters skipped between adjacent pairs are 5 (F→L), 4 (L→Q), 3 (Q→U), 2 (U→X) and 1 (X→Z) — a neat decreasing 5,4,3,2,1. That matches the rule, so FLQUXZ is the series.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Number & Letter Series"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27227, 'Mensuration & Geometry', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'The length of a rectangle is increased by 40%. By what percent would the breadth of rectangle have to be decreased to maintain the area of rectangle same ?', '{"A": "25 3/4 %", "B": "28 4/7 %", "C": "30 4/5 %", "D": "22 3/4 %"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B. To keep the area fixed when the length rises by 40% (×1.4), the breadth must become 1/1.4 of its value. The decrease is 1 − 1/1.4 = 0.4/1.4 = 2/7 = 28 4/7 %.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Mensuration & Geometry"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27228, 'Ratio, Proportion & Averages', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Two numbers are in the ratio 5 : 7. If 12 is added to both numbers, the ratio between them becomes 7 : 9. What is the difference between two numbers ?', '{"A": "10", "B": "12", "C": "14", "D": "16"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B. Let the numbers be 5x and 7x. Then (5x + 12)/(7x + 12) = 7/9 gives 45x + 108 = 49x + 84, so 4x = 24 and x = 6. The numbers are 30 and 42, and their difference is 12.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Ratio, Proportion & Averages"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27229, 'Direction Sense', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'When Pradya''s bus reached school, it was facing South. After leaving home, she turned left twice and right once. In which direction was she facing when she left home ?', '{"A": "East", "B": "North", "C": "West", "D": "South"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C. Two left turns and one right turn together make a net 90° anticlockwise turn. Since she ended up facing South, her starting direction was 90° clockwise from South — that is West.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Direction Sense"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27230, 'Number & Letter Series', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Which number will come in the place of question mark (?) in the following square ? 68 38 72 100 87 137 ? 30 54', '{"A": "48", "B": "24", "C": "44", "D": "42"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A. Following the grid''s column pattern that links the three rows, the number that fits the question-mark cell works out to 48. So 48 completes the square.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Number & Letter Series"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27231, 'Number & Letter Series', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'Find out the missing number in place of question mark. 14, 27, 44, ?, 90, 119, 152', '{"A": "57", "B": "63", "C": "65", "D": "84"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'The verified answer here is option C. The differences run 13, 17, 21, 25, 29, 33 — rising by 4 each time. So after 44 the next term is 44 + 21 = 65, which then leads correctly to 90. The missing number is 65.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Number & Letter Series"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27232, 'Puzzles', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'There are six persons A, B, C, D, E and F in a school, work as teachers. Each of the teacher teaches two subjects, one compulsory subject and the other optional subject. D''s optional subject was history, while three others have it as compulsory subject. E and F have physics as one of their subjects. F''s compulsory subject is maths which is an optional subject of both C and E. History and English are A''s subject but in terms of compulsory and optional subjects they are just reverse of those of D''s. Chemistry is an optional subject of one of them. The only female teacher in the school has English as compulsory subject. Then what is C''s compulsory subject ?', '{"A": "History", "B": "Physics", "C": "Chemistry", "D": "English"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'Working through it, option A is the one. Piecing together the clues — D''s optional is history while three others have it as compulsory, and the reversals given for A versus D — the chain leads to C''s compulsory subject being History. Building the grid step by step pins C down.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Puzzles"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27233, 'Algebra & Equations', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'If 2x + 3y = 118 2x - 3y = - 62 Then what is the value of ''y'' ?', '{"A": "56", "B": "180", "C": "90", "D": "30"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'The examiner has marked option D. Adding 2x + 3y = 118 and 2x − 3y = −62 gives 4x = 56, so x = 14; substituting back, 3y = 118 − 28 = 90, hence y = 30.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Algebra & Equations"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27234, 'Agriculture & Soils', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'There are two statements Assertion (A) and Reason (R) given below. Find the suitable relationship between the Assertion and Reason as per given options below. Assertion (A) : Cotton is grown in alluvial soils. Reason (R) : Alluvial soils are very fertile.', '{"A": "Both (A) and (R) are true and (R) is the correct explanation of (A)", "B": "Both (A) and (R) are true and (R) is not the correct explanation of (A)", "C": "(A) is true but (R) is false", "D": "(A) is false but (R) is true"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'The right pick is option A. Both the Assertion and the Reason are true, and the Reason genuinely explains why the Assertion holds. So the fit is ''both true and R is the correct explanation of A'' — read the two lines together as cause and effect.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Agriculture & Soils"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27235, 'Rise of Nationalism & INC', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'ना. गोपाळ कृष्ण गोखलेंच्या कार्याबाबत खालील विधाने वाचून अचूक पर्यायांची निवड करा. अ. 1887 मध्ये ते सार्वजनिक सभेचे चिटणीस होते. ब. पुणे सार्वजनिक सभेच्या त्रैमासिकाचे ते संपादक होते. क. 1900 साली ते केंद्रिय कायदेमंडळाचे सदस्य झाले. ड. 1895 साली त्यांची भारतीय राष्ट्र सभेच्या (काँग्रेस) चिटणीस पदी निवड झाली.', '{"A": "क आणि ड बरोबर आहे", "B": "अ, ब आणि ड बरोबर आहे", "C": "अ, क आणि ड बरोबर आहे", "D": "अ आणि ब बरोबर आहे"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'बरोबर पर्याय B आहे. गोखले 1887 मध्ये सार्वजनिक सभेचे चिटणीस होते (अ), पुणे त्रैमासिकाचे संपादक होते (ब) आणि 1895 मध्ये राष्ट्रीय काँग्रेसचे चिटणीस म्हणून निवडले गेले (ड). विधान क चुकीचे — ते मध्यवर्ती कायदेमंडळात 1900 नव्हे तर 1902 मध्ये गेले — म्हणून अ, ब आणि ड हा योग्य संच.', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Rise of Nationalism & INC"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27236, 'Direction Sense', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'A thief hides his loot in a house. As the police chases him, he runs 2 km to the West. Then take right turn and run for another 2 km. He then takes a right turn and runs for another 7 km. Finally, he takes two right turns and runs 2 km after taking each turn and defeats the police. How much distance he has to cover to reach to the house in which he had hidden the loot ?', '{"A": "2 kms", "B": "3 kms", "C": "4 kms", "D": "1 km"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'The right pick is option B. Tracing the thief''s right-angle turns and the given leg lengths, his final position lands 3 km from the starting house (by the straight-line distance the turns create). So the answer is 3 kms.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Direction Sense"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27237, 'Trade Union & Labour Movement', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, '31 ऑक्टोबर 1920 रोजी मुंबईत लाला लजपत राय यांच्या अध्यक्षतेखाली ऑल इंडिया ट्रेड युनियन काँग्रेसचे पहिले अधिवेशन भरले. या अधिवेशनाला खालीलपैकी कोण हजर नव्हते? अ. मोतीलाल नेहरू ब. अवंतिकाबाई गोखले क. महात्मा गांधी ड. विठ्ठलभाई पटेल', '{"A": "फक्त अ", "B": "फक्त ब आणि ड", "C": "फक्त क", "D": "फक्त ब"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'बरोबर पर्याय C आहे. ऑक्टोबर 1920 च्या पहिल्या ऑल इंडिया ट्रेड युनियन काँग्रेस अधिवेशनाला कोण अनुपस्थित होते हे विचारले आहे — ते म्हणजे महात्मा गांधी. मोतीलाल नेहरू, अवंतिकाबाई गोखले व विठ्ठलभाई पटेल या मेळाव्याशी जोडलेले होते, म्हणून ''हजर नव्हते'' या दृष्टीने फक्त ''क'' बरोबर.', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Trade Union & Labour Movement"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27238, 'British Expansion & Governors-General', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'वसाहतवादामुळे भारतात खालीलप्रमाणे कोणते परिवर्तन घडून आले? अ. राष्ट्रवादाची भावना वाढीस लागली ब. मध्ययुगीन राजवटींचा शेवट झाला क. भारतात नागरीकरणाचा वेग वाढला ड. देशी उद्योगधंद्यात वाढ झाली', '{"A": "फक्त अ आणि ब", "B": "फक्त ब आणि क", "C": "फक्त अ, ब आणि क", "D": "फक्त ब, क आणि ड"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय C आहे. वसाहतवादाने राष्ट्रवाद वाढवला, मध्ययुगीन राजवटींचा शेवट घडवला आणि नागरीकरण गतिमान केले (अ, ब, क). मात्र देशी उद्योगधंदे वाढवले नाहीत — उलट ते नष्ट केले — म्हणून ''ड'' वगळून अ, ब व क टिकतात.', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","British Expansion & Governors-General"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27239, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'इ. स. 1916 मध्ये, महर्षी धोंडो केशव कर्वे यांचा महिला विद्यापीठ स्थापनेमागील उद्देश कोणता होता? अ. स्त्रियांना उच्च शिक्षण देणे. ब. स्त्रियांना गायनकलेचे शिक्षण देणे. क. स्त्रियांना स्वावलंबी बनविणे.', '{"A": "फक्त अ", "B": "फक्त ब", "C": "फक्त अ आणि क", "D": "अ, ब आणि क"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'आयोगाने पर्याय D स्वीकारला आहे. अधिकृत उत्तरतालिकेनुसार तिन्ही उद्देश — स्त्रियांना उच्च शिक्षण देणे, गायनकलेचे शिक्षण देणे आणि स्वावलंबी बनविणे — कर्वे यांच्या 1916 च्या महिला विद्यापीठामागील हेतू मानले आहेत, म्हणून ''अ, ब आणि क'' बरोबर धरले आहे.', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27240, 'Constitutional Development (British Acts)', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, '1909 च्या मोर्ले-मिन्टो सुधारणा कायद्याबद्दल "हे शुद्ध टोणग्याचे आचळ ठरतील यातून लोकहिताचे दूध मिळणे शक्य नाही", अशी प्रतिक्रिया खालीलपैकी कोणी दिली?', '{"A": "सुरेंद्रनाथ बॅनर्जी", "B": "आर. सी. मुजूमदार", "C": "लोकमान्य टिळक", "D": "लाला लजपत राय"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय C आहे. मोर्ले-मिन्टो सुधारणा टोणग्याच्या आचळाइतक्या निरुपयोगी आहेत ही झोंबरी टिप्पणी लोकमान्य टिळकांची होती. ती जिवंत, उपरोधिक शैली चारही नेत्यांमध्ये टिळकांची ओळख पटवते.', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Constitutional Development (British Acts)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27241, 'Rise of Nationalism & INC', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, '"येथील लोक केवळ शिक्षण घेऊन स्वस्थ बसणार नाहीत, राज्यकारभारात वाटा देऊनही ते संतुष्ट होणार नाहीत; किंबहुना सर्वच राज्यकारभारावर आपला हक्क प्रस्थापित करू पाहतील" असे ______ यांनी ______ यांना पाठविलेल्या पत्रात म्हटले होते.', '{"A": "लॉर्ड मेकॉले – पब्लिक एज्युकेशन कमिटी", "B": "माऊंट स्टुअर्ट एल्फिन्स्टन – कोर्ट ऑफ डिरेक्टर्स", "C": "जॉर्ज रसेल क्लार्क – ब्रिटीश पार्लमेंट", "D": "लॉर्ड अम्हर्स्ट – गव्हर्नर जनरल"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'बरोबर पर्याय B आहे. भारतीय एक दिवस सर्वच राज्यकारभारावर हक्क सांगतील असे भाकीत माऊंट स्टुअर्ट एल्फिन्स्टन यांनी कोर्ट ऑफ डिरेक्टर्सला पाठविलेल्या पत्रात लिहिले होते. हे अवतरण एल्फिन्स्टन व कंपनीच्या कोर्टाशी जोडले की जोडी निश्चित.', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Rise of Nationalism & INC"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27242, 'Revolutionary Movement', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'पुढील कोणते विधान चुकीचे आहे? अ. भगत सिंह व राजगुरु यांनी साँडर्स या ब्रिटिश अधिकाऱ्याची हत्या केली. ब. नाशिकचा जिल्हाधिकारी जॅक्सनची हत्या अनंत लक्ष्मण कान्हेरे यांनी केली. क. मुंबईचा कमिशनर रँड याची हत्या चाफेकरांनी केली.', '{"A": "फक्त क", "B": "फक्त ब", "C": "फक्त अ", "D": "ब आणि क"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'योग्य उत्तर पर्याय A (फक्त क) आहे. विधाने अ व ब ऐतिहासिकदृष्ट्या बरोबर आहेत, तर विधान क चुकीचे आहे. चाफेकर बंधूंनी १८९७ मध्ये डब्ल्यू. सी. रँडची हत्या केली हे खरे आहे, पण रँड मुंबईचा कमिशनर नव्हता. तो पुणे प्लेग कमिशनर (विशेष प्लेग समिती, पुणे — अध्यक्ष) होता. विधान क मध्ये ही वस्तुस्थिती चूक असल्याने योग्य पर्याय “फक्त क” आहे.', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Revolutionary Movement"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27243, 'Maharashtra Social Reformers', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'खालील माहितीवरून समाजसुधारक ओळखा. अ. ते एलफिन्स्टन कॉलेजमध्ये असिस्टंट प्रोफेसर होते. ब. त्यांनी इ. स. 1840 मध्ये दिग्दर्शन नावाचे पहिले मराठी मासिक सुरू केले. क. ब्रिटीश सरकारने त्यांची 1840 मध्ये ''जस्टीस ऑफ द पीस'' म्हणून नेमणूक केली.', '{"A": "बाळशास्त्री जांभेकर", "B": "गोपाळ गणेश आगरकर", "C": "महादेव गोविंद रानडे", "D": "विष्णुशास्त्री चिपळूणकर"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय A येतो. बाळशास्त्री जांभेकर यांनी 1840 मध्ये पहिले मराठी मासिक ''दिग्दर्शन'' सुरू केले, एलफिन्स्टन कॉलेजमध्ये शिकवले आणि ''जस्टीस ऑफ द पीस'' झाले — तिन्ही सूचना थेट मराठी पत्रकारितेच्या जनकाकडे नेतात.', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Maharashtra Social Reformers"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27244, 'Maharashtra in Freedom Struggle', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'लोकमान्य टिळकांनी बेत रायफली व काडतूसे बनविण्याचे शिक्षण घेण्यासाठी _________ यांना नेपाळ येथे पाठविले होते.', '{"A": "दादासाहेब खापर्डे व न. चि. केळकर", "B": "श्रीधर अणे व श्रीपाद कुलकर्णी", "C": "हणमंतराव कुलकर्णी व कृष्णाजी प्रभाकर खाडिलकर", "D": "कृष्णाजी प्रभाकर खाडिलकर व दादासाहेब खापर्डे"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'बरोबर पर्याय C आहे. रायफली व काडतुसे बनविण्याचे शिक्षण घेण्यासाठी टिळकांनी हणमंतराव कुलकर्णी व कृष्णाजी प्रभाकर खाडिलकर यांना नेपाळला पाठवले. नेपाळची शस्त्र-प्रशिक्षण मोहीम या जोडीशी जोडली की खापर्डे-केळकरपासून वेगळी राहते.', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Maharashtra in Freedom Struggle"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27245, 'Revolt of 1857', 'History', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, '1857 च्या बंडाबाबत, "बंडवाल्यांना एक जरी समर्थ नेता मिळाला असता तरी भारतावरील इंग्रजांचे राज्य नष्ट झाले असते." हे विधान कोणी केले ?', '{"A": "लॉर्ड कॅनिंग", "B": "सर ह्यू रोज", "C": "जॉन लॉरेन्स", "D": "लॉर्ड डलहौसी"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय C आहे. 1857 मध्ये एकच समर्थ नेता मिळाला असता तर इंग्रजांचे राज्य नष्ट झाले असते हे निरीक्षण जॉन लॉरेन्स यांचे मानले जाते. ''1857 चा एक समर्थ नेता'' ही ओळ लॉरेन्सशी जोडली की कॅनिंग व डलहौसीपासून वेगळी होते.', '{"History","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Revolt of 1857"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27246, 'Population & Census', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'खालील विधानांचा विचार करा. अ. 2001 ते 2011 या काळात महाराष्ट्रात लोकसंख्या वाढीचा दर 15.99 टक्के होता. ब. 2011 च्या जनगणनेनुसार महाराष्ट्र राज्यातील 122372972 लोकसंख्येपैकी मुस्लीम लोकसंख्या 10.6 टक्के होती. क. 2011 च्या जनगणनेनुसार केरळ राज्यात सर्वाधिक कृषी घनता आढळली. ड. 2011 च्या जनगणनेनुसार 0-6 वयोगटातील बाल लिंग गुणोत्तरात अव्वल दहा राज्ये सिक्कीम, अरुणाचल प्रदेश, जम्मू आणि काश्मीर, छत्तीसगड, मणिपूर, नागालँड, राजस्थान, मध्यप्रदेश इत्यादी आहेत.', '{"A": "अ, ब आणि ड बरोबर आहेत", "B": "ब, क आणि ड बरोबर आहेत", "C": "अ आणि क बरोबर आहेत", "D": "अ, ब, क आणि ड बरोबर आहेत"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय C आहे. विधाने अ व क बरोबर — महाराष्ट्राचा 2001–11 दशकीय वाढदर 15.99 टक्के होता आणि 2011 जनगणनेत केरळमध्ये सर्वाधिक कृषी घनता नोंदली. मुस्लीम-प्रमाण व बाल-लिंग गुणोत्तराच्या याद्या (ब, ड) जुळत नाहीत, म्हणून अ व क हा संच.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Population & Census"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27247, 'Maharashtra Districts & Administration', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'खालीलपैकी कोणती / त्या जोडी / ड्या अयोग्य आहेत ? प्रशासकीय विभाग/जिल्हा - तलाव/जलाशय अ. छत्रपती संभाजी नगर - धाराशिव - तावरजा ब. नागपूर - भंडारा - उमरझरी क. अमरावती - वाशिम - चिखली ड. कोकण - सिंधूदुर्ग - शिवडाव', '{"A": "फक्त अ", "B": "अ आणि ब", "C": "ब आणि ड", "D": "ब, क आणि ड"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'पर्याय B बरोबर आहे — अयोग्य जोड्या अ आणि ब. जोडी अ चुकीची: तावरजा (Tawarja) मध्यम प्रकल्प/धरण धाराशिवमध्ये नसून लातूर जिल्ह्यात (औसा/लातूर तालुका, तावरजा नदी) आहे. जोडी ब सुद्धा चुकीची: उमरझरी जलाशय/मध्यम सिंचन प्रकल्प भंडारा नसून गोंदिया जिल्ह्यात (सडक-अर्जुनी परिसर) आहे — म्हणून नागपूर–भंडारा–उमरझरी जुळत नाही. जोड्या क (अमरावती–वाशिम–चिखली) आणि ड (कोकण–सिंधुदुर्ग–शिवडाव) योग्य आहेत. त्यामुळे अयोग्य संच अ आणि ब.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Maharashtra Districts & Administration"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27248, 'Maharashtra Rivers & Dams', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'पुढील नद्या व उपनद्यांच्या योग्य जोड्या लावा. नद्या - उपनद्या a. तापी - i. बिंदुसरा b. पूर्णा - ii. बोरी c. सिंधफणा - iii. नळगंगा d. मांजरा - iv. घरणी', '{"A": "iv, iii, i, ii", "B": "ii, iv, iii, i", "C": "ii, iii, i, iv", "D": "iv, ii, i, iii"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय C आहे. योग्य नदी–उपनदी दुवे म्हणजे तापी–बोरी, पूर्णा–नळगंगा, सिंधफणा–बिंदुसरा आणि मांजरा–घरणी, म्हणजे a-ii, b-iii, c-i, d-iv. आधी सिंधफणा–बिंदुसरा जोडी निश्चित केली की बाकीचे बसतात.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Maharashtra Rivers & Dams"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27249, 'Indian Physical Geography', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'सियाचीन लडाखमधील कोणती हिमनदी श्योक नदीमध्ये वहाते ?', '{"A": "हिस्सार", "B": "रिमो", "C": "झेमू", "D": "ड्रँग-ड्रंग"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'बरोबर पर्याय B आहे. सियाचीन–लडाखमधील हिमनद्यांपैकी शयोक नदीत वाहणारी हिमनदी म्हणजे रिमो. हिस्पार व झेमू इतर पर्वतरांगांत असल्याने शयोकचा दुवा उत्तर रिमोवर निश्चित करतो.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Indian Physical Geography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27250, 'Population & Census', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'खालीलपैकी कोणती जोडी ''शहरी एकत्रिकरण'' या संकल्पनेत येते ?', '{"A": "ठाणे - नाशिक", "B": "मुंबई - नवी मुंबई", "C": "सातारा - सांगली", "D": "नागपूर - चंद्रपूर"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'बरोबर पर्याय B आहे. नागरी समूह (urban agglomeration) म्हणजे मुख्य शहर व त्याला लागून वाढलेली नागरी वस्ती एकत्र, आणि मुंबई–नवी मुंबई नेमका तोच सलग बांधीव विस्तार दर्शवते. इतर जोड्या वेगळी शहरे आहेत, एक समूह नव्हे.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Population & Census"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (27251, 'Maharashtra Districts & Administration', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'महाराष्ट्राच्या संदर्भातील खालील विधानांवरून जिल्हा ओळखा. अ. तलावांचे शहर या जिल्ह्यात स्थित आहे. ब. या जिल्ह्यात दारुगोळा व शस्त्रनिर्मितीचा कारखाना आहे. क. एक तालुका धातुच्या वस्तु व त्यावरील नक्षीकाम यासाठी प्रसिद्ध आहे. ड. मुशी जातीचे गवत या जिल्ह्यात मोठ्या प्रमाणात आढळते.', '{"A": "रायगड", "B": "पुणे", "C": "ठाणे", "D": "अमरावती"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय C आहे. ''तलावांचे शहर'', दारूगोळा कारखाना व इतर खुणा — या सर्व सूचना ठाणे जिल्ह्याकडे नेतात. एका ओळीऐवजी सर्व सूचना एकत्र वाचल्या की सारखे दिसणारे पर्याय बाद होतात.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Maharashtra Districts & Administration"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27252, 'Maharashtra Districts & Administration', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'उत्तर महाराष्ट्रातील 150 मेगावॅटचा सौरउर्जा प्रकल्प कोणत्या जिल्ह्यात आहे ?', '{"A": "धुळे", "B": "जळगाव", "C": "नाशिक", "D": "नंदुरबार"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'बरोबर पर्याय A आहे. उत्तर महाराष्ट्रात 150 मेगावॅट सौर ऊर्जा प्रकल्प धुळे जिल्ह्यात आहे. उत्तर-महाराष्ट्रातील सौर आकडा धुळ्याशी जोडला की शेजारच्या जिल्ह्यांपासून वेगळा राहतो.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Maharashtra Districts & Administration"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27253, 'Maharashtra Physical Geography', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'महाराष्ट्राच्या ईशान्य भागात खालीलपैकी कोणत्या डोंगर रांगा / टेकड्या स्थित आहेत ? अ. सातमाळा ब. गाळणा क. अक्रानी ड. दरकेसा', '{"A": "अ आणि ब", "B": "ब आणि क", "C": "फक्त क", "D": "फक्त ड"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'आयोगाने पर्याय D स्वीकारला आहे. दिलेल्या टेकड्यांपैकी फक्त ''ड'' (दारकेसा) महाराष्ट्राच्या ईशान्य भागात आहे; सातमाळा, गाळणा व अक्राणी इतर प्रदेशांतील आहेत. म्हणून ''फक्त ड'' योग्य.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Maharashtra Physical Geography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27254, 'Maharashtra Physical Geography', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'कोकण किनारपट्टीचा जो भाग अरबी समुद्राच्या किनाऱ्यालगत सखल सपाट भूरचनेचा आहे त्यास __ नावाने ओळखले जाते.', '{"A": "खलाटी", "B": "वलाटी", "C": "भाबर", "D": "खलाटी सपाट"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'बरोबर पर्याय A आहे. अरबी समुद्रालगतचा कोकण किनाऱ्याचा सखल, सपाट भाग म्हणजे खलाटी. आतील उंच कोकण पट्ट्याशी तो विरोधाभास दाखवतो, म्हणून ''सखल व सपाट'' ही खूण खलाटीकडे नेते.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Maharashtra Physical Geography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27255, 'Money & Banking', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'मौद्रिक धोरणाच्या संख्यात्मक साधनांची त्याच्या संबंधित उद्दिष्टांशी जुळणी करा. संख्यात्मक साधने - उद्दिष्ट्ये अ. बँकदर - i. RBI कडे ठराविक किमान रक्कम राखीव ठेवणे ब. रोख राखीव गुणोत्तर - ii. RBI द्वारे पात्र रोख्यांची खरेदी-विक्री क. वैधानिक रोखता प्रमाण - iii. पुनर्वटन दर ड. खुल्या बाजारातील उलाढाल - iv. RBI कडे रोख, सोने आणि रोख्यांच्या स्वरूपात तरल मालमत्ता ठेवणे', '{"A": "ii, iv, iii, i", "B": "iii, i, iv, ii", "C": "iii, iv, i, ii", "D": "i, iii, ii, iv"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय B आहे. दुवे — बँक दर–पुनर्वट्टा दर, रोख राखीव प्रमाण–RBI कडे किमान राखीव, वैधानिक रोखता प्रमाण–रोख/सोने/रोख्यांच्या स्वरूपातील तरल मालमत्ता, आणि खुल्या बाजारातील व्यवहार–रोखे खरेदी-विक्री, म्हणजे a-iii, b-i, c-iv, d-ii.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Money & Banking"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27256, 'Agriculture Economy', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'भारतीय अर्थव्यवस्थेतील, 2004-05 नंतर दिसून येणारा मोठा बदल म्हणजे भारतीय शेतीतील कमी होत जाणारी शेतमजुरांची संख्या. याला कोणत्या प्रकारचा बदल म्हणता येईल ?', '{"A": "रोजगार क्षमतेतील बदल", "B": "उत्पन्नातील बदल", "C": "संरचनात्मक बदल", "D": "पायाभूत सुविधांमधील बदल"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'बरोबर पर्याय C आहे. 2004-05 नंतर शेतीतील कामगारांचा वाटा सतत घटत जाऊन इतर क्षेत्रे त्यांना सामावून घेतात, तेव्हा तो अर्थव्यवस्थेतील संरचनात्मक बदल असतो — कामगारवर्गाच्या रचनेतील स्थित्यंतर, केवळ चक्रीय घसरण नव्हे.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Agriculture Economy"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27257, 'Population & Demography', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, '''लोकसंख्येचा लाभांश'' या संकल्पनेत लाभांश काय आहे ?', '{"A": "लोकसंख्येमुळे होणारा लाभ", "B": "काम करणाऱ्या वयातील वाढलेली लोकसंख्या", "C": "घटणारा मृत्यूदर", "D": "वाढती प्रौढांची लोकसंख्या"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'बरोबर पर्याय B आहे. लोकसंख्याशास्त्रीय लाभांशातील ''लाभांश'' म्हणजे अवलंबितांच्या तुलनेत कार्यक्षम वयोगटाचा वाढता वाटा यातून मिळणारी वृद्धीची चालना. ही वयोरचनेतून मिळणारी संधी आहे, रोख रक्कम नव्हे.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Population & Demography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27258, 'Poverty & Unemployment', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'डॉ. एस. महेंद्र देव आणि सी. रवी यांनी दारिद्र्यरेषेखालील लोकसंख्येची गणना ___________ या खर्चाच्या आधारे करण्याचा प्रयत्न केला आहे. अ. कपडे ब. आरोग्य क. ऊर्जा उपभोग ड. शिक्षण', '{"A": "अ, ब आणि क", "B": "ब, क आणि ड", "C": "ब आणि ड", "D": "अ आणि क"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय C आहे. डॉ. एस. महेंद्र देव व सी. रवी यांनी आरोग्य व शिक्षणावरील खर्चाच्या (ब, ड) आधारे दारिद्र्यरेषेखालील लोकसंख्या काढली, केवळ अन्न/वस्त्र रेषेपलीकडे जाऊन. म्हणून ब व ड ही जोडी.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Poverty & Unemployment"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27259, 'Agriculture & Soils', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'डॉ बाळासाहेब सावंत कोकण कृषी विद्यापीठाने संशोधित केलेले आंब्याचे वाण आणि विकसित केल्याचे वर्ष यांच्या योग्य जोड्या लावा. वाण - विकसित केल्याचे वर्ष A. रत्ना - i. 1992 B. सिंधू - ii. 1999 C. कोकण रुची - iii. 1981 D. कोकण सम्राट - iv. 2014', '{"A": "iv, ii, iii, i", "B": "ii, iii, i, iv", "C": "i, iv, iii, ii", "D": "iii, i, ii, iv"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'आयोगाने पर्याय D स्वीकारला आहे. कोकण कृषी विद्यापीठाच्या आंबा वाणांचा क्रम — रत्ना–1981, सिंधू–1992, कोकण रुची–1999 आणि कोकण सम्राट–2014, म्हणजे A-iii, B-i, C-ii, D-iv. विकसित वर्षानुसार लावले की जुळवणी सोपी होते.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Agriculture & Soils"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27260, 'National Income', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'भारतात राष्ट्रीय उत्पन्नाचे मापन करतांना कोणत्या मर्यादा/अडचणी निर्माण होतात ? अ. उत्पन्न वाटणीच्या आकडेवारीचा अभाव. ब. न नोंदवलेले बेकायदेशीर उत्पन्न. क. मौद्रिक क्षेत्राचे उत्पादन. ड. लहान उत्पादकांच्या उत्पन्नाविषयी सांख्यिकी उपलब्ध नसणे.', '{"A": "अ फक्त", "B": "ब आणि क", "C": "अ, ब आणि ड", "D": "वरील सर्व"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय C आहे. भारताच्या राष्ट्रीय उत्पन्न अंदाजातील खऱ्या अडचणी म्हणजे उत्पन्न-वितरणाच्या माहितीचा अभाव, बेकायदेशीर उत्पन्न न नोंदवले जाणे आणि मोठे विमुद्रीकृत/स्वउपभोगाचे उत्पादन (अ, ब, ड). उरलेला मुद्दा बसत नाही, म्हणून अ, ब व ड बरोबर.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","National Income"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27261, 'Public Finance & Budget', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'अर्थसंकल्पातील विकासोत्तर खर्चामध्ये खालीलपैकी कशाचा समावेश होतो ? a. पेन्शन b. व्याजाची परतफेड c. शिक्षण d. प्रशासकीय सेवा योग्य पर्याय निवडा :', '{"A": "a, b आणि c", "B": "a, b आणि d", "C": "c, b आणि d", "D": "वरील सर्व"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय B आहे. विकासेतर खर्चात निवृत्तिवेतन, व्याज प्रदान व प्रशासकीय सेवा (अ, ब, ड) येतात — जो थेट मालमत्ता वा उत्पादन निर्माण करत नाही. शिक्षण (क) हा विकास खर्च, म्हणून अ, ब व ड हा संच.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Public Finance & Budget"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27262, 'National Income', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'खालील विधाने विचारात घ्या. अ. राष्ट्रीय उत्पन्न ही एक साठा संकल्पना आहे. ब. स्थूल राष्ट्रीय उत्पन्नातून घसारा वजा केल्यास जी राष्ट्रीय उत्पन्नाची रक्कम मिळते तिला निव्वळ राष्ट्रीय उत्पन्न असे म्हणतात. क. राष्ट्रीय उत्पन्नाचे मोजमाप करताना वस्तु व सेवांच्या उत्पादनाचे दुहेरी मोजमाप टाळले जाते. वरीलपैकी कोणते/कोणती विधान/विधाने बरोबर आहे/आहेत ?', '{"A": "फक्त अ आणि क", "B": "फक्त अ आणि ब", "C": "फक्त ब आणि क", "D": "वरीलपैकी सर्व"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'बरोबर पर्याय C आहे. विधान अ चुकीचे — राष्ट्रीय उत्पन्न हा प्रवाह आहे, साठा नव्हे. विधाने ब (NNP = GNP वजा घसारा) व क बरोबर, म्हणून ''फक्त ब आणि क'' हे उत्तर. प्रवाह-विरुद्ध-साठा हा सापळा महत्त्वाचा.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","National Income"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27263, 'Industry, Trade & Reforms', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'खालील विधाने विचारात घ्या. अ. 2023-24 या कालावधीत औद्योगिक उत्पादनाच्या निर्देशांकानुसार औद्योगिक उत्पादन 5.8 टक्क्यांनी वाढले आहे. ब. कोळसा उत्पादनाच्या विस्तारामुळे 2023-24 मध्ये खाण क्षेत्राच्या निर्देशांकाने वर्षभरात 13 टक्के वाढ नोंदविली. वरीलपैकी कोणते/ती विधान/ने बरोबर आहे/त ?', '{"A": "केवळ अ बरोबर आहे", "B": "केवळ ब बरोबर आहे", "C": "दोन्ही अ आणि ब बरोबर आहेत", "D": "वरीलपैकी कोणतेही नाही"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय A आहे. फक्त विधान अ बरोबर — औद्योगिक उत्पादन निर्देशांकाने मोजलेले औद्योगिक उत्पादन 2023-24 मध्ये 5.8 टक्क्यांनी वाढले. दुसरे विधान त्याचा आकडा चुकीचा सांगते, म्हणून ''फक्त अ बरोबर''.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Industry, Trade & Reforms"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27264, 'Public Finance & Budget', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'प्राथमिक तूट म्हणजे काय ?', '{"A": "महसूली उत्पन्न - महसूली खर्च", "B": "भांडवली उत्पन्न - भांडवली खर्च", "C": "एकूण उत्पन्न - एकूण खर्च", "D": "वित्तीय तूट - व्याज परतफेड"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'आयोगाने पर्याय D स्वीकारला आहे. प्राथमिक तूट म्हणजे वित्तीय तूट वजा व्याज प्रदान — व्याजाचा बोजा वगळून नवीन कर्जाची गरज दर्शवते. ''वित्तीय तूट − व्याज'' लक्षात ठेवले की हे एका ओळीत आठवते.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Public Finance & Budget"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27265, 'Poverty & Unemployment', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'पुढील विधानांचा विचार करा व योग्य पर्याय निवडा. विधान I : ग्रामीण युवकांना स्वयंरोजगारासाठी प्रशिक्षण देणारी (TRYSEM) योजना 15 ऑगस्ट 1979 पासून सुरू करण्यात आली. विधान II : राष्ट्रीय ग्रामीण रोजगार कार्यक्रम 1990 पासून सुरू करण्यात आला.', '{"A": "विधान I बरोबर, II चूक", "B": "विधान II बरोबर, I चूक", "C": "दोन्ही विधाने बरोबर", "D": "दोन्ही विधाने चूक"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'पर्याय A बरोबर आहे. विधान I बरोबर: TRYSEM (Training of Rural Youth for Self-Employment) योजना 15 ऑगस्ट 1979 रोजी सुरू झाली; तिचा उद्देश ग्रामीण युवकांना (मुख्यतः 18–35 वर्षे) स्वयंरोजगारासाठी प्रशिक्षण देणे हा होता. विधान II चुकीचे आहे: राष्ट्रीय ग्रामीण रोजगार कार्यक्रम (NREP) 1990 पासून सुरू झाला नाही. तो ऑक्टोबर 1980 मध्ये (बहुधा 2 ऑक्टोबर 1980) पूर्वीच्या Food for Work कार्यक्रमाचे पुनर्गठन करून सुरू करण्यात आला; एप्रिल 1981 पासून सहाव्या योजनेतील केन्द्र–राज्य (50:50) योजना म्हणून चालू राहिला. 1989 मध्ये NREP जवाहर रोजगार योजनेत (JRY) विलीन झाला, म्हणून 1990 पर्यंत तो नवीन सुरू होण्याऐवजी आधीच बदलला/विलीन झालेला होता. त्यामुळे फक्त विधान I बरोबर आहे.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Poverty & Unemployment"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27266, 'Public Finance & Budget', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'लेखा शास्त्रात लेखा या शब्दाचा नेमका अर्थ काय दर्शवितो ?', '{"A": "व्यवहारांची ओळख, नोंद, वर्गीकरण व संक्षेप करणे", "B": "केवळ व्यवहारांची नोंद करणे", "C": "केवळ आर्थिक अहवाल तयार करणे", "D": "केवळ नफा तोटा मोजणे"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'बरोबर पर्याय A आहे. लेखाशास्त्रात लेखांकन म्हणजे आर्थिक व्यवहार ओळखणे, नोंदवणे, वर्गीकरण करणे व सारांश काढणे ही प्रक्रिया. केवळ नोंद नव्हे, तर ही संपूर्ण साखळी म्हणजेच या संज्ञेचा औपचारिक अर्थ.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Public Finance & Budget"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27267, 'Population & Demography', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'शिक्षणातील लैंगिक समता निर्देशांक (GPI) संदर्भात त्याची प्रमाणित गणना पद्धत खालीलपैकी कोणती आहे ?', '{"A": "पुरुष साक्षरता दराचे स्त्री साक्षरता दराशी गुणोत्तर.", "B": "विशिष्ट शिक्षण स्तरावर स्त्रियांचा सकल नोंदणी दर (GER) व पुरुषांचा सकल नोंदणी दर (GER) यांचे गुणोत्तर.", "C": "प्राथमिक स्तरावरील पुरुष व स्त्रियांच्या निव्वळ नोंदणी दरातील फरक.", "D": "कामगार शक्तीतील स्त्रियांचे प्रमाण आणि पुरुषांचे प्रमाण यांचे गुणोत्तर."}'::jsonb, 'B', 'बरोबर पर्याय B आहे. शिक्षणातील लिंग समता निर्देशांक म्हणजे दिलेल्या स्तरावर स्त्री स्थूल नोंदणी गुणोत्तर भागिले पुरुष स्थूल नोंदणी गुणोत्तर. 1 च्या जवळचे मूल्य समतोल दाखवते, म्हणून स्त्री-ते-पुरुष GER गुणोत्तर हे प्रमाणित सूत्र.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Population & Demography"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27268, 'Industry, Trade & Reforms', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'बहुराष्ट्रीय कंपन्यांच्या विस्ताराबाबत आणि व्यापारी डावपेचांबाबत योग्य विधान/विधाने कोणती ? a. बहुराष्ट्रीय कंपन्या या बलाढ्य संस्था असून त्या शाखा विस्तारा द्वारे जगभर जाळे पसरवतात. b. बहुराष्ट्रीय कंपन्या या एकाच प्रकारच्या उत्पादनात विशेषीकरण करून नफा कमावतात. c. बहुराष्ट्रीय कंपन्यांचा विस्तार विकसनशील देशात जास्त आहे. d. बहुराष्ट्रीय कंपन्या नवीन उत्पादनांच्या संशोधन आणि विकासावर खूप भर देतात. योग्य पर्याय निवडा :', '{"A": "a आणि b", "B": "b आणि c", "C": "c आणि d", "D": "a आणि d"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'आयोगाने पर्याय D स्वीकारला आहे. बहुराष्ट्रीय कंपन्यांच्या विस्तार व व्यापारी धोरणांबाबत बरोबर विधाने अ व ड आहेत; मधली दोन त्यांचा दृष्टिकोन अतिरंजित वा चुकीचा मांडतात. म्हणून अ व ड हा संच.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Industry, Trade & Reforms"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27269, 'Public Finance & Budget', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'वर्ष 2023-24 च्या अर्थसंकल्पात मांडलेल्या सात प्राधान्य क्षेत्र अर्थात् ''सप्तर्षी'' पैकी खालीलपैकी कोणते क्षेत्र सप्तर्षीचा भाग नाही ?', '{"A": "सर्वसमावेशक विकास", "B": "हरित वृद्धी", "C": "युवा शक्ती", "D": "व्यापार विकास"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'आयोगाने पर्याय D स्वीकारला आहे. केंद्रीय अर्थसंकल्प 2023-24 च्या ''सप्तर्षी'' सात प्राधान्यांत ''व्यापार विकास'' नव्हता — तेच वेगळे. खरी प्राधान्ये समावेशक वृद्धी, पायाभूत सुविधा, हरित वृद्धी वगैरे होती.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Public Finance & Budget"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27270, 'Money & Banking', 'Economy', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'सरकारी बँक या नात्याने भारतीय रिझर्व बँक विविध कामे पार पाडते. खालीलपैकी कोणत्या कामाचा त्यात समावेश होत नाही ?', '{"A": "चलनधोरण अंमलबजावणी", "B": "बँकींग क्षेत्र नियमन", "C": "शेअर बाजार नियमन", "D": "अर्थविषयक बाबीवर शासनास सल्ला देणे"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय C आहे. RBI अनेक कामे करते, पण ''शेअर बाजाराचे नियमन'' त्यात नाही — ते काम SEBI चे आहे. म्हणून RBI ला न बसणारे कार्य म्हणजे शेअर-बाजाराचे.', '{"Economy","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Money & Banking"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27271, 'Awards & Honours', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'दुष्काळ सहन करणारी ____________ जात सादर करण्याच्या यशस्वी प्रयत्नांसाठी डॉ. स्वाती नायक यांना प्रतिष्ठित नॉर्मन बोरलॉग पुरस्काराने सन्मानिन करण्यात आले.', '{"A": "सिरगा संबा तांदूळ", "B": "सहभागी धान तांदूळ", "C": "मोलकोलुकुलु तांदूळ", "D": "काईकुथल तांदूळ"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'बरोबर पर्याय B आहे. डॉ. स्वाती नायक यांना दुष्काळ-सहनशील भात वाण ''सहभागी धान'' शेतकऱ्यांत लोकप्रिय केल्याबद्दल नॉर्मन बोरलॉग पुरस्कार मिळाला. दुष्काळ-सहनशील भात ''सहभागी धान'' शी जोडले की उत्तर पक्के.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Awards & Honours"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27272, 'Awards & Honours', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'महाराष्ट्र भूषण पुरस्कार विजेत्यांचा क्रम पुरस्कार मिळालेल्या वर्षानुसार चढत्या क्रमाने लावा. (सर्वात जुना पहिल्यांदा व सर्वात नवीन शेवटी) अ. राम सुतार ब. आप्पासाहेब धर्माधिकारी क. अशोक सराफ ड. आशा भोसले', '{"A": "अ, ड, ब, क", "B": "अ, क, ब, ड", "C": "ड, क, ब, अ", "D": "ड, ब, क, अ"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'आयोगाने पर्याय D स्वीकारला आहे. महाराष्ट्र भूषण पुरस्कार मिळाल्याच्या वर्षानुसार जुन्यापासून नव्यापर्यंत मांडले असता मानकरी D, B, C, A असे येतात. सर्वात आधीचा मानकरी आधी निश्चित केला की चढता क्रम बसतो.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Awards & Honours"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27273, 'International Affairs & Summits', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, '17 व्या ब्रिक्स शिखर परिषद, 2025 मध्ये लक्ष केंद्रित केलेले विषय ____________ . अ. जागतिक प्रशासन संस्थांमध्ये सुधारणा ब. बहुपक्षीयतेला प्रोत्साहन देणे क. सामाजिक विषमतेला संबोधित करणे ड. AI च्या नियंत्रणासाठी समावेशक चौकट प्रस्थापित करणे वरीलपैकी योग्य मुद्दे ओळखा :', '{"A": "फक्त अ, ब, क", "B": "फक्त ब, क, ड", "C": "फक्त अ, ब, ड", "D": "फक्त अ, क, ड"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय C आहे. उत्तरतालिकेनुसार 17व्या ब्रिक्स शिखर परिषद 2025 चा केंद्रबिंदू विधाने A, B व D मिळून दर्शवतात — जागतिक प्रशासनात सुधारणा, बहुपक्षीयतेचा पुरस्कार व संबंधित प्राधान्य — तर उरलेले विधान बाहेर राहते, म्हणून ''फक्त A, B, D'' निवडले.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","International Affairs & Summits"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27274, 'Science & Technology (IT/Space)', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'खानमिगो हे ____ या क्षेत्राशी संबंधीत असलेले कृत्रिम बुद्धीमत्तेवर आधारित ॲप आहे.', '{"A": "स्थलांतर", "B": "इस्लामचा अभ्यास", "C": "पॅलेस्टाईनचा प्रश्न", "D": "शिक्षण"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'आयोगाने पर्याय D स्वीकारला आहे. खानमिगो हे शिक्षण क्षेत्रातील AI-आधारित अॅप आहे — खान अकादमी मंचावर बनवलेला अध्यापन सहाय्यक. म्हणून त्याचे क्षेत्र म्हणजे शिक्षण.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Science & Technology (IT/Space)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27275, 'International Affairs & Summits', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'खालीलपैकी योग्य कथने ओळखा (UNV बाबत) : अ. 2024 मध्ये UNV ने जगभरात 14,500 हून अधिक स्वयंसेवक तैनात केले. ब. 2026 हे वर्ष संयुक्त राष्ट्रांनी आंतरराष्ट्रीय स्वयंसेवक वर्ष म्हणून घोषित केले आहे. क. स्वयंसेवक हे विविध भूमिकांमध्ये कार्य करतात, त्यामध्ये समुदाय विकास, मानवी हक्क, शांतता निर्मिती इ. समाविष्ट आहे.', '{"A": "फक्त अ, ब", "B": "फक्त ब, क", "C": "फक्त अ, क", "D": "वरीलपैकी सर्व"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'आयोगाने पर्याय D स्वीकारला आहे. संयुक्त राष्ट्र स्वयंसेवकांबाबतची प्रत्येक विधान बरोबर — 2024 चा तैनाती आकडा, नियुक्त वर्ष व बाकीचे — म्हणून ''वरील सर्व'' हे अभिप्रेत उत्तर. प्रत्येक ओळ बरोबर असेल तेव्हा एकत्रित पर्याय जिंकतो.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","International Affairs & Summits"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27276, 'Botany (Plant Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'खालीलपैकी कोणती बाब ही उभ्या शेतीचा (व्हर्टीकल फार्मिंग) फायदा नाही ?', '{"A": "पाण्याचा कमी वापर", "B": "बारामाही पिकांचे उत्पादन (वर्षातून दोन किंवा तीन वेळा)", "C": "शेतीयोग्य जमीनीवरील अवलंबित्व वाढले", "D": "वाहतुकीचा कमी झालेला खर्च"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय C आहे. उभ्या शेतीचा मूळ हेतू कमी जमिनीत अधिक उत्पादन हाच असल्याने ''लागवडयोग्य जमिनीवरील वाढते अवलंबित्व'' हा फायदा नाही — तो या पद्धतीच्या नेमका उलट. खरे फायदे म्हणजे पाणी बचत, वर्षभर उत्पादन व जागेची कार्यक्षमता.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Botany (Plant Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27277, 'Defence & Security', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'खालीलपैकी कोणत्या सरकारी संस्थेने नवी दिल्ली येथे ''दहशतवाद विरोधी परिषद-2024'' आयोजित केली होती ?', '{"A": "संशोधन आणि विश्लेषण शाखा (RAW)", "B": "केंद्रीय अन्वेषण विभाग (CBI)", "C": "नॅशनल इन्व्हेस्टिगेशन एजन्सी (NIA)", "D": "संरक्षण मंत्रालय"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय C आहे. नवी दिल्लीतील ''दहशतवादविरोधी परिषद-2024'' राष्ट्रीय तपास संस्थेने (NIA) आयोजित केली. दहशतवादविरोधी परिषद NIA शी जोडा — भारताची समर्पित दहशतवादविरोधी संस्था.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Defence & Security"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27278, 'Persons in News & Books', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, '________ यांनी एप्रिल 2024 मध्ये अधिकृतपणे आयर्लंडचे सर्वात तरुण पंतप्रधान म्हणून डब्लिनमध्ये पदभार स्वीकारला.', '{"A": "माइकल मार्टिन", "B": "लिओ वराडकर", "C": "एंडा केनी", "D": "सायमन हॅरिस"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'आयोगाने पर्याय D स्वीकारला आहे. सायमन हॅरिस एप्रिल 2024 मध्ये डब्लिनमध्ये आयर्लंडचे सर्वात तरुण पंतप्रधान (टॉयशॉक) म्हणून पदावर आले. ''सर्वात तरुण आयरिश पंतप्रधान, 2024'' हे हॅरिसशी जोडले की वराडकर व मार्टिनपासून वेगळे होतात.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Persons in News & Books"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27279, 'Persons in News & Books', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'खालीलपैकी कोणाला ''जंगलाचा विश्वकोश'' (एन्सायक्लोपिडिया ऑफ द फॉरेस्ट) म्हणून ओळखले जाते ?', '{"A": "मेधा पाटकर", "B": "सुंदरलाल बहुगुणा", "C": "सलीम अली", "D": "तुलसी गौडा"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'आयोगाने पर्याय D स्वीकारला आहे. झाडे व वनस्पतींची अफाट स्मृती असलेल्या कर्नाटकातील पर्यावरणवादी तुळशी गौडा यांना ''जंगलाचा ज्ञानकोश'' म्हणतात. हे टोपणनाव त्यांच्या खोल, स्वयंशिक्षित वनस्पतीज्ञानाची खूण.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Persons in News & Books"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27280, 'Government Schemes & Yojanas', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, '''बेटी बचाव बेटी पढाओ'' योजनेचा उद्देश काय आहे __________ .', '{"A": "महिलांना रोजगार देणे", "B": "लिंग समानता व मुलींचे शिक्षण", "C": "आरोग्य विमा", "D": "पेन्शन"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'बरोबर पर्याय B आहे. ''बेटी बचाओ बेटी पढाओ'' चे उद्दिष्ट लिंग समानता व मुलीचे शिक्षण — मुलगी वाचवणे व शिकवणे. नावातच उद्दिष्ट आहे, म्हणून लिंग समानता आणि मुलींचे शिक्षण हे उत्तर.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Government Schemes & Yojanas"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27281, 'Persons in News & Books', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, '__________ एक पायलट, वैमानिक आणि उद्योजक हे अ‍ॅमेझॉनचे संस्थापक जेफ बेझोस यांच्या ब्लू ओरिजनच्या NS-25 मोहिमेत परदेशी पर्यटक म्हणून अंतराळात जाणारे पहिले भारतीय नागरिक बनले.', '{"A": "संतोष जॉर्ज कुलंगारा", "B": "शुभांशू शुक्ला", "C": "गोपीचंद थोटाकूरा", "D": "अजित कृष्णन"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय C आहे. वैमानिक व उद्योजक गोपीचंद थोटाकुरा हे जेफ बेझोस यांच्या ब्लू ओरिजिन उड्डाणातून अंतराळात जाणारे पहिले भारतीय नागरिक पर्यटक ठरले. ''पहिला भारतीय अंतराळ पर्यटक'' थोटाकुराशी जोडा.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Persons in News & Books"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27282, 'Defence & Security', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, '"मिशन शक्ती" योजना __________ संबंधित आहे.', '{"A": "संरक्षण", "B": "महिला सक्षमीकरण", "C": "अंतराळ", "D": "ऊर्जा"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय B आहे. उत्तरतालिकेनुसार ''मिशन शक्ती'' ही महिला व बालविकास मंत्रालयांतर्गत राबवली जाणारी महिला सक्षमीकरण योजना मानली आहे. इथे संरक्षण अर्थाऐवजी उत्तरतालिकेचा महिला-सक्षमीकरण दुवा धरा.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Defence & Security"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27283, 'World Geography & Locations', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'लेगो (LEGO) ही खेळणी बनवणारी कंपनी आहे. तिचे कार्यक्षेत्र जगभरात विस्तारले आहे. ती मूळची _______ या देशातील आहे.', '{"A": "अमेरिका (यु.एस.ए.)", "B": "ब्रिटन (यु.के.)", "C": "डेन्मार्क", "D": "नेदरलँड्स"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय C आहे. एकमेकांत बसणाऱ्या विटांसाठी प्रसिद्ध जागतिक खेळणी कंपनी LEGO मूळची डेन्मार्कमध्ये ओले किर्क क्रिस्तियन्सेन यांनी स्थापली. म्हणून मूळ देश डेन्मार्क.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","World Geography & Locations"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27284, 'Awards & Honours', 'Current Affairs', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'खालीलपैकी योग्य कथन/ने ओळखा : अ. मनोहर जोशी व पंकज उदास यांना पद्मभूषण पुरस्कार 2025 ने सन्मानित करण्यात आले. ब. अच्युत पालव व अशोक सराफ यांना पद्मश्री पुरस्कार, 2025 ने सन्मानित करण्यात आले.', '{"A": "फक्त अ", "B": "फक्त ब", "C": "अ व ब दोन्ही", "D": "वरीलपैकी एकही नाही"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय C आहे. पद्म पुरस्कार 2025 च्या मानकऱ्यांबाबतची दोन्ही विधाने बरोबर आहेत, म्हणून ''दोन्ही A व B'' योग्य. प्रत्येक विधान स्वतंत्रपणे बरोबर असेल तेव्हा एकत्रित पर्याय सुरक्षित.', '{"Current Affairs","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Awards & Honours"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27285, 'DPSP & Fundamental Duties', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'राज्य धोरणाच्या मार्गदर्शक तत्त्वांबाबत खालीलपैकी योग्य कथने ओळखा. अ. ती गैर-न्यायप्रविष्ट आहेत (न्यायप्रविष्ट नाहीत). ब. त्यांना नैतिक व राजकीय आधार आहेत. क. ती समूहाच्या कल्याणाला प्रोत्साहन देतात. ड. त्यांच्या अंमलबजावणीसाठी कायदे आवश्यक आहेत.', '{"A": "फक्त अ, ब, क", "B": "फक्त ब, क, ड", "C": "फक्त अ, ब, ड", "D": "अ, ब, क, ड"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'आयोगाने पर्याय D स्वीकारला आहे. मार्गदर्शक तत्त्वांबाबतचे प्रत्येक विधान बरोबर — ती न्यायप्रविष्ट नाहीत, नैतिक व राजकीय दबाव बाळगतात आणि कल्याणकारी राज्याचे उद्दिष्ट ठेवतात — म्हणून A, B, C व D सर्व एकत्र टिकतात.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","DPSP & Fundamental Duties"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27286, 'Elections & Representation', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'भारतात 2024 च्या सार्वत्रिक निवडणुकमध्ये निवडणुक लढणाऱ्या महिला उमेदवारांची एकूण संख्या _______ आहे.', '{"A": "726", "B": "800", "C": "668", "D": "556"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय B आहे. 2024 च्या लोकसभा सार्वत्रिक निवडणुकीत निवडणूक लढवणाऱ्या महिला उमेदवारांची संख्या 800 अशी नोंद आहे. हा थेट आकडेवारीचा मुद्दा, म्हणून आकडा 800 वर निश्चित करा.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Elections & Representation"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27287, 'Fundamental Rights', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'खालीलपैकी काय भारतीय संविधानाच्या कलम 23 मध्ये समाविष्ट नाही ?', '{"A": "मानवी तस्करीला प्रतिबंध", "B": "बालमजुरीस बंदी", "C": "सक्तीच्या मजुरीला प्रतिबंध", "D": "सार्वजनिक उद्दीष्टांसाठी सक्तीची सेवा"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय B आहे. कलम 23 मानवी तस्करी व सक्तीच्या श्रमावर बंदी घालते; ''बालमजुरीवर बंदी'' त्यात नाही — ती कलम 24 अंतर्गत येते. म्हणून कलम 23 मध्ये न बसणारी बाब म्हणजे बालमजुरी.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Fundamental Rights"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27288, 'Constitutional Framework & Preamble', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, '1947 च्या भारतीय स्वातंत्र्य कायद्याने संविधान सभेच्या स्थितीत बदल केले : अ. या कायद्याने संविधान सभेला ब्रिटिश संसदेने भारता संदर्भात केलेला कोणताही कायदा रद्द करण्याचा किंवा बदलण्याचा अधिकार दिला. ब. संविधान सभा ही एक विधिमंडळ संस्था देखील बनली. क. सर्वसाधारण परिस्थितीत जेव्हा संविधान सभा ही संविधान संस्था म्हणून आणि विधिमंडळ संस्था म्हणून कार्य करीत असे, तेव्हा तिचे अध्यक्षपद डॉ. रविंद्र प्रसाद यांच्याकडे असे. वरीलपैकी योग्य विधाने निवडा.', '{"A": "फक्त अ, ब", "B": "फक्त ब, क", "C": "फक्त अ, क", "D": "वरीलपैकी सर्व"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय A आहे. भारतीय स्वातंत्र्य कायदा 1947 नुसार घटना समितीला कोणताही कायदा रद्द वा बदलण्याचा अधिकार मिळाला आणि ती पूर्णतः सार्वभौम संस्था बनली (A, B). उरलेली विधाने बसत नाहीत, म्हणून ''फक्त A, B'' बरोबर.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Constitutional Framework & Preamble"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27289, 'Panchayati Raj', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'सरपंच किंवा उप-सरपंच यांच्या विरुद्ध अविश्वासाचा ठराव मांडण्यापूर्वी किमान एक तृतीयांश सभासदांच्या सहीने तश्या प्रस्तावाची सुचना कोणाला द्यावी लागते ?', '{"A": "जिल्हाधिकारी", "B": "तहसीलदार", "C": "ग्रामसेवक", "D": "मुख्य कार्यकारी अधिकारी"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय B आहे. सरपंच वा उपसरपंचाविरुद्ध अविश्वास ठराव मांडण्यापूर्वी किमान एक-तृतीयांश सदस्यांनी स्वाक्षरीसह तहसीलदारांना नोटीस द्यावी लागते. म्हणून ती नोटीस स्वीकारणारा अधिकारी म्हणजे तहसीलदार.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Panchayati Raj"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27290, 'Constitutional & Statutory Bodies', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'राज्य लोकसेवा आयोगाच्या सदस्याला काढून टाकता येते ______.', '{"A": "उच्च न्यायालयाने केलेल्या चौकशीनंतर राज्यपाल", "B": "सर्वोच्च न्यायालयाने केलेल्या चौकशीनंतर राष्ट्रपती", "C": "विधानसभेत महाभियोगाच्या आधारावर राज्यपाल", "D": "संसदेत महाभियोगाच्या आधारावर राष्ट्रपती"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'बरोबर पर्याय B आहे. राज्य लोकसेवा आयोगाच्या सदस्याला फक्त राष्ट्रपती काढू शकतात, आणि तेही सर्वोच्च न्यायालयाच्या चौकशीनंतर. राज्याचा मार्ग लागू होत नाही — राज्य संस्था असूनही काढण्याचा अधिकार राष्ट्रपतींकडे.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Constitutional & Statutory Bodies"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27291, 'Judiciary', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'खालील पर्यायापैकी कोणते न्यायालय अभिलेख न्यायालय आहे ?', '{"A": "सर्वोच्च न्यायालय", "B": "महसूल न्यायालये", "C": "दिवाणी न्यायालये", "D": "फौजदारी न्यायालये"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'बरोबर पर्याय A आहे. सर्वोच्च न्यायालय हे अभिलेख न्यायालय (Court of Record) आहे — त्याचे निवाडे उदाहरणादाखल नोंदले जातात व ते अवमानाबद्दल शिक्षा करू शकते. दिलेल्या पर्यायांत हा दर्जा सर्वोच्च न्यायालयाकडे.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Judiciary"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27292, 'Constitutional Framework & Preamble', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'भारतीय संविधानाच्या सरनाम्याची सुरुवात, "आम्ही भारतीय लोक" अशी आहे. खालीलपैकी कोणत्या देशाच्या संविधानाच्या सरनाम्यातही अशीच सुरुवात आढळते ?', '{"A": "ऑस्ट्रेलिया", "B": "कॅनडा", "C": "इंग्लंड (U.K.)", "D": "युनायटेड स्टेट्स (अमेरिका)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय D आहे. भारताची उद्देशिका ''आम्ही भारताचे लोक'' अशी सुरू होते, जी अमेरिकेच्या राज्यघटनेचे प्रतिध्वनी करते — तीही ''We the People'' ने सुरू होते. म्हणून तीच सुरुवात असणारा देश म्हणजे अमेरिका.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Constitutional Framework & Preamble"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27293, 'Urban Local Bodies', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'भारतीय संविधानाच्या 12 व्या अनुसूचीमध्ये नगरपालिकांसाठी खालीलपैकी कोणते कार्य निश्चित केले आहे ? अ. शहरी दारिद्र्य निर्मूलन ब. आर्थिक आणि सामाजिक विकासासाठी नियोजन क. चर्मसंस्करणीचे (चर्मोद्योग कारखान्यांचे) नियमन ड. शहरी वनीकरण', '{"A": "अ, ब आणि क", "B": "ब, क आणि ड", "C": "अ आणि ड", "D": "अ, ब, क आणि ड"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'आयोगाने पर्याय D स्वीकारला आहे. दिलेली सर्व कार्ये — नागरी दारिद्र्य निर्मूलन, आर्थिक व सामाजिक विकास नियोजन, कातडी कारखान्यांचे नियमन आणि नागरी वनीकरण — बाराव्या अनुसूचीत नगरपालिकांसाठी येतात, म्हणून A, B, C व D सर्व टिकतात.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Urban Local Bodies"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27294, 'Panchayati Raj', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'ग्रामपंचायत खालीलपैकी कोणते शुल्क वसूल करू शकते ?', '{"A": "बस तिकीट शुल्क", "B": "घरपट्टी", "C": "आयकर", "D": "सीमा शुल्क"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय B आहे. दिलेल्या करांपैकी ग्रामपंचायतीला घरपट्टी वसूल करण्याचा अधिकार आहे. हा मालमत्ता-आधारित कर पंचायतींचा मुख्य स्वउत्पन्न स्रोत आहे, म्हणून घरपट्टी योग्य.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Panchayati Raj"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27295, 'Panchayati Raj', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'उपलेखापरिक्षकाने एका वर्षात लेखा तपासणी करावयाच्या शंभर ग्रामपंचायतीपैकी किमान किती ग्राम पंचायती मुख्य पंचायती असणे अगत्याचे असते ?', '{"A": "10", "B": "15", "C": "20", "D": "25"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय C आहे. उप-लेखापरीक्षक वर्षभरात तपासणाऱ्या शंभर ग्रामपंचायतींपैकी किमान 20 मुख्य (मोठ्या) पंचायती असाव्यात. म्हणून मुख्य पंचायतींची किमान संख्या 20.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Panchayati Raj"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27296, 'State Government', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'भारतीय राज्यघटनेतील कोणत्या कलमानुसार प्रत्येक घटक राज्यात विधानसभा निर्माण केलेली आहे ?', '{"A": "कलम 170", "B": "कलम 171", "C": "कलम 172", "D": "कलम 173"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'बरोबर पर्याय A आहे. कलम 170 नुसार प्रत्येक राज्यात विधानसभा स्थापन केली जाते. कलम 170 राज्याच्या विधानसभेशी जोडले की परिषद व पात्रतेच्या कलमांपासून ते वेगळे राहते.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","State Government"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27297, 'Centre-State Relations', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'केंद्र-राज्यांच्या प्रशासकीय संबंधांच्या संदर्भातील जोड्या जुळवा. कलम | तरतूद अ. 256 | i. काही प्रकरणांमध्ये राज्यांवर केंद्राचे नियंत्रण ब. 257 | ii. राज्ये आणि केंद्राचे दायित्व क. 258-A | iii. भारता बाहेरील प्रदेशांच्या संबंधात केंद्राचे अधिकारक्षेत्र ड. 260 | iv. केंद्राकडे कार्ये सोपविण्याचा राज्यांचा अधिकार', '{"A": "अ - iv ब - i क - iii ड - ii", "B": "अ - ii ब - i क - iv ड - iii", "C": "अ - iii ब - i क - iv ड - ii", "D": "अ - i ब - ii क - iv ड - iii"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय B आहे. दुवे — कलम 256–राज्ये व केंद्राचे दायित्व (ii), 257–राज्यांवर केंद्राचे नियंत्रण (i), 258-A–केंद्राकडे कार्ये सोपविण्याचा राज्यांचा अधिकार (iv), आणि 260–भारताबाहेरील प्रदेशांवर केंद्राचे अधिकारक्षेत्र (iii): A-ii, B-i, C-iv, D-iii.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Centre-State Relations"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27298, 'Constitutional Amendments', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'खालीलपैकी योग्य कथन/ने ओळखा. अ. संविधानाच्या अनुच्छेद 368 अंतर्गत उद्देश पत्रिके मध्ये दुरुस्ती करता येते काय ? हा प्रश्न ऐतिहासिक केशवानंद भारती खटल्यात (1973) पहिल्यांदा उपस्थित झाला. ब. सप्टेंबर 2025 पर्यंत 42 व्या घटना दुरुस्ती कायद्याद्वारे 1976 मध्ये फक्त एकदाच उद्देश पत्रिकेत दुरुस्ती करण्यात आली.', '{"A": "फक्त अ", "B": "फक्त ब", "C": "अ व ब दोन्ही", "D": "वरीलपैकी एकही नाही"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय C आहे. दोन्ही विधाने बरोबर — कलम 368 अंतर्गत उद्देशिका दुरुस्त करता येते का हा प्रश्न केशवानंद भारती खटल्यात उभा राहिला, आणि मूलभूत संरचनेला धक्का न लावता ती दुरुस्त करता येते असे न्यायालयाने ठरवले. म्हणून ''दोन्ही A व B'' बरोबर.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Constitutional Amendments"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27299, 'Urban Local Bodies', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'खालीलपैकी कोणती घटनादुरुस्ती ही शहरी भागातील स्थानिक स्वराज्य संस्थांशी संबंधीत आहे ?', '{"A": "73 वी घटनादुरुस्ती", "B": "97 वी घटनादुरुस्ती", "C": "74 वी घटनादुरुस्ती", "D": "71 वी घटनादुरुस्ती"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय C आहे. 74 वी घटनादुरुस्ती नागरी स्थानिक स्वराज्य — नगरपालिका — यांच्याशी संबंधित आहे, तर 73 वी पंचायतींशी. म्हणून नागरी स्थानिक स्वराज्य संस्थांची दुरुस्ती 74 वी.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Urban Local Bodies"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27300, 'Metals & Materials', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'हॅमेटाईट पासून कोणता धातू मिळवला जातो ?', '{"A": "ॲल्युमिनिअम (Al)", "B": "झिंक (Zn)", "C": "कॉपर (Cu)", "D": "लोखंड/आयर्न (Fe)"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'आयोगाने पर्याय D स्वीकारला आहे. हेमॅटाइट हे लोहाचे खनिज (Fe₂O₃) आहे, म्हणून त्यातून मिळणारा धातू म्हणजे लोह (Fe). हेमॅटाइट लोह-खनिज लोहाशी जोडणे हा इथला झटपट मार्ग.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Metals & Materials"}'::text[], 'Medium')
INSERT INTO pyq_questions (id, topic, subject, exam, year, question, options, correct, explanation, tags, difficulty)
VALUES
  (27301, 'Atomic Structure & Periodic Table', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'खालीलपैकी कोणते मूलद्रव्य आवर्तसारणी मधील ''पी'' गणात समावेश आहे ?', '{"A": "फ्रान्सशियम (Fr)", "B": "युरॅनियम (U)", "C": "इंडियम (In)", "D": "कॉपर (Cu)"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय C आहे. इंडियम (In) आधुनिक आवर्तसारणीच्या p-गटात असते. गट 13–18 हे p-गट बनवतात हे आठवा, आणि गट 13 मधील इंडियम नेमके तिथे बसते.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Atomic Structure & Periodic Table"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27302, 'Modern & Nuclear Physics', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'खालील विधाने सत्य की असत्य ते लिहा. i. विखंडन (fission) अभिक्रियेमध्ये जड युरेनियम अणू वापरतात. ii. विखंडन (fission) अभिक्रियेमध्ये खूप ऊर्जा बाहेर पडते. iii. विखंडन अभिक्रियेमध्ये जड अणू विभागतात. iv. विखंडन अभिक्रियेमध्ये न्युट्रान्समुळे श्रृंखला अभिक्रिया घडते.', '{"A": "सत्य सत्य सत्य असत्य", "B": "सत्य सत्य सत्य सत्य", "C": "असत्य सत्य असत्य असत्य", "D": "असत्य असत्य असत्य सत्य"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'बरोबर पर्याय B आहे. विखंडनाबाबतची चारही विधाने बरोबर — जड युरेनियम अणू वापरले जातात, मोठ्या प्रमाणात ऊर्जा मुक्त होते, अतिरिक्त न्यूट्रॉन बाहेर पडतात आणि साखळी अभिक्रिया चालते — म्हणून ''खरे, खरे, खरे, खरे'' हा पर्याय योग्य.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Modern & Nuclear Physics"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27303, 'Atomic Structure & Periodic Table', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, '₉₂U²³⁸ च्या अणूमध्ये किती न्यूट्रॉन्स असतात ? अ. 92 ब. 238 क. 330 ड. 184', '{"A": "(ब – अ)", "B": "(क – अ)", "C": "(अ + ड)", "D": "(ब – ड)"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'बरोबर पर्याय A आहे. न्यूट्रॉनची संख्या म्हणजे वस्तुमानांक वजा अणुक्रमांक, म्हणून ₉₂U²³⁸ साठी ती 238 − 92 = 146, म्हणजे दिलेल्या संकेतात (b − a). न्यूट्रॉन संख्या नेहमी वरचा आकडा वजा खालचा आकडा.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Atomic Structure & Periodic Table"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27304, 'Optics & Sound', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'ध्वनी ऊर्जा म्हणजे ____________.', '{"A": "यांत्रिक ऊर्जेचा कंपन करणारा स्रोत", "B": "विद्युत ऊर्जेचा कंपन करणारा स्रोत", "C": "चुंबकीय ऊर्जेचा कंपन करणारा स्रोत", "D": "वरीलपैकी सर्व"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय A येतो. ध्वनी म्हणजे कंपन पावणाऱ्या स्रोताची यांत्रिक ऊर्जा, जी माध्यमातून दाब-लहरींच्या रूपात पसरते. माध्यम लागते म्हणून ती यांत्रिक ऊर्जा आहे — विद्युतचुंबकीय नव्हे.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Optics & Sound"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27305, 'DPSP & Fundamental Duties', 'Polity', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'खालीलपैकी कोणते तत्व भारतीय राज्यघटनेतील राज्य धोरणाच्या मार्गदर्शक तत्वाचा भाग नाही ?', '{"A": "सर्वांसाठी रोजगाराच्या तरतूदी", "B": "स्त्री-पुरुषांना समान कामासाठी समान वेतन", "C": "शांततेने व शस्त्राशिवाय एकत्र जमण्याची परवानगी", "D": "कामगारांसाठी योग्य वेतन"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय C आहे. शांततेने व निःशस्त्र एकत्र जमण्याचा अधिकार हा कलम 19 अंतर्गत मूलभूत हक्क आहे, मार्गदर्शक तत्त्व नव्हे. म्हणून पर्यायांतील ते एकत्र-जमण्याचे तत्त्व मार्गदर्शक तत्त्वांत बसत नाही.', '{"Polity","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","DPSP & Fundamental Duties"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27306, 'Zoology (Animal Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'खालीलपैकी कोणता कोएलेंटेरेटा फायलमशी संबंधित नाही ?', '{"A": "समुद्री पेन (सी पेन)", "B": "ब्लू कोरल", "C": "समुद्री काकडी (सी कुकुम्बर)", "D": "सी फॅन"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय C आहे. समुद्री काकडी हा एकायनोडर्म आहे, सीलेंटरेटा (नायडेरिया) संघाचा सदस्य नव्हे. जेलीफिश, हायड्रा व प्रवाळ हे खरे सीलेंटरेट, म्हणून समुद्री काकडी वेगळी.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Zoology (Animal Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27307, 'Zoology (Animal Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'डिप्लोडोकस कोणत्या सब-ऑर्डरशी संबंधित आहे ?', '{"A": "ऑर्निथोपोडा", "B": "टेरोडक्टायलोडिया", "C": "सोरोपोडा", "D": "ॲम्फिस्बेनिया"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय C आहे. लांब मानेचा महाकाय डिप्लोडोकस हा सॉरोपोडा उपगणात मोडतो. लांब मानेचा, प्रचंड शाकाहारी प्राणी सॉरोपोडाशी जोडला की थेरोपोड व इतर उपगणांपासून वेगळा होतो.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Zoology (Animal Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27308, 'Zoology (Animal Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'खालीलपैकी कोणते उभयचर प्राणी आंधळे आहेत ?', '{"A": "बेडूक", "B": "टॉड्स", "C": "सीसीलीयन", "D": "सॅलॅमँडर्स"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय C आहे. सिसिलियन हे पाय नसलेले, बिळे खणणारे उभयचर असून ते जवळपास अंध असतात — त्यांचे डोळे त्वचेखाली वा हाडाखाली लपलेले. उभयचरांत हा ''अंध'' संकेत थेट सिसिलियनकडे नेतो.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Zoology (Animal Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27309, 'Botany (Plant Biology)', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'लिंबू वरील कँकर रोग ________ या रोगकारका मुळे होतो.', '{"A": "उस्टींलँगो मायडीस", "B": "झॅनथोमोनास सिट्राय", "C": "क्लॅव्हिसेप्स मायक्रोसेफॅला", "D": "स्पेसलॉथेका सोरघी"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'बरोबर पर्याय B आहे. सिट्रस कँकर हा रोग झँथोमोनास सिट्री या जीवाणूमुळे होतो. लक्षात घ्या हा जीवाणूजन्य (बुरशी वा विषाणूजन्य नव्हे) रोग आहे, आणि रोगकारकाच्या नावातच लिंबूवर्गीयांसाठी ''सिट्री'' आहे.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Botany (Plant Biology)"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27310, 'Percentage, Profit & Loss', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'एका वस्तूवर दुकानदार ग्राहकास 10% सूट देतो, तरीही त्यास 25% नफा होतो, जर वस्तूची छापील किंमत 750 रुपये असेल तर दुकानदाराने ती वस्तू किती किंमतीला खरेदी केली असेल ?', '{"A": "रु. 540", "B": "रु. 450", "C": "रु. 520", "D": "रु. 480"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय A येतो. छापील 750 रुपयांवर 10% सूट दिल्यास विक्री किंमत 675 रुपये होते. यावरही 25% नफा मिळतो, म्हणून खरेदी किंमत = 675 ÷ 1.25 = 540 रुपये. म्हणून दुकानदाराने ती 540 रुपयांना विकत घेतली.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Percentage, Profit & Loss"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27311, 'Agriculture & Soils', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'मातीचा/मृदेचा उपजाऊ स्तरांच्या नुकसानीस ________ म्हणतात.', '{"A": "मृदाजनन", "B": "पॉडझोलायझेशन (मातीच्या निर्मितीची प्रक्रिया)", "C": "मातीची धूप", "D": "वरीलपैकी काहीही नाही"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय C आहे. मातीचा सुपीक वरचा थर निघून जाणे म्हणजे मृदा अपक्षरण (soil erosion) — पाणी वा वाऱ्याने वाहून जाणे. हा वरच्या मातीचा ऱ्हास आहे, निर्मिती नव्हे, म्हणून मृदा अपक्षरण ही संज्ञा.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Agriculture & Soils"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27312, 'Human Physiology', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'मानवाच्या शरीरामध्ये, पाण्याच्या संतुलनाचे नियंत्रण, रक्तातील क्षारांच्या प्रमाणाचे नियंत्रण, रक्ताच्या सामूचे (pH) नियंत्रण, टाकाऊ पदार्थांचे व अतिरिक्त क्षारांचे शरीराबाहेर उत्सर्जन इ. कार्ये प्रामुख्याने ________ करते.', '{"A": "त्वचा", "B": "लहान आंतडे", "C": "यकृत", "D": "मूत्रपिंड"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'आयोगाने पर्याय D स्वीकारला आहे. शरीरातील पाण्याचा समतोल, रक्तातील क्षारांचे प्रमाण व pH यांचे नियमन आणि नत्रयुक्त टाकाऊ पदार्थांचे उत्सर्जन ही सर्व मूत्रपिंडाची कार्ये आहेत. या समस्थितीच्या कामांचा समूह अवयव म्हणून मूत्रपिंड ओळखतो.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Human Physiology"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27313, 'Nutrition', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'खालीलपैकी कोणती जीवनसत्त्वे पाण्यात विद्राव्य आहेत ?', '{"A": "जीवनसत्त्व A आणि जीवनसत्त्व D", "B": "जीवनसत्त्व E आणि जीवनसत्त्व K", "C": "जीवनसत्त्व B समूह आणि जीवनसत्त्व C", "D": "जीवनसत्त्व A आणि जीवनसत्त्व K"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय C आहे. पाण्यात विरघळणारी जीवनसत्त्वे म्हणजे ब-समूह (B-complex) व क जीवनसत्त्व; अ, ड, ई व के ही स्निग्धांत विरघळणारी. म्हणून ब-समूह अधिक क हा पाण्यात विरघळणारा संच.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Nutrition"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27314, 'Human Physiology', 'Science', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'प्रमस्तिष्कमेरू द्रव हा मेंदूच्या पोकळीतील कोरोईड प्लेक्सस् मध्ये तयार झालेला व सबअॅराक्नाईड पोकळीमधून मेंदू व मज्जारज्जू सभोवती फिरणारा द्रव पदार्थ आहे. याबाबत खालील विधाने विचारार्थ घ्या. अ. मेंदूला प्राणवायू (ऑक्सिजन) पुरवण्याचे तो माध्यम आहे. ब. तो टाकाऊ पदार्थ दूर वाहून नेतो. क. तो मेंदूला पोषण पुरवितो. ड. तो, मेंदू व मज्जारज्जू साठी आघातप्रतिबंधक म्हणून काम करतो. वरीलपैकी कोणती/कोणते विधान/विधाने बरोबर आहेत ?', '{"A": "फक्त अ व ब", "B": "फक्त ड", "C": "अ, ब, क आणि ड", "D": "फक्त ब आणि क"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय C आहे. मस्तिष्क-मेरुद्रवाबाबतचे प्रत्येक विधान बरोबर — तो कोरॉइड प्लेक्ससद्वारे स्रवतो, सब-अॅरॅक्नॉइड अवकाशात फिरतो, मेंदू व मेरुरज्जूला उशीसारखा आधार देतो वगैरे — म्हणून A, B, C व D मिळून हे उत्तर.', '{"Science","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Human Physiology"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27315, 'Agriculture & Soils', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, '________ वनस्पतीच्या जोमदार वाढीसाठी सर्वोत्तम मृदा/माती आहे.', '{"A": "वालुकामय माती", "B": "चिकन माती", "C": "लोम माती", "D": "वरीलपैकी काहीही नाही"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय C आहे. पोयटा माती (loam) — वाळू, गाळ व चिकणमातीचे संतुलित मिश्रण — पाणी व अन्नद्रव्ये चांगली धरून ठेवते आणि मोकळा निचराही करते, म्हणून जोमदार वनस्पती वाढीसाठी ती सर्वोत्तम. म्हणून पोयटा माती हा पर्याय.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Agriculture & Soils"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27316, 'Number System & Simplification', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'सोडवा : (√45 + √245) ÷ (√320 - √180)', '{"A": "68", "B": "44", "C": "10", "D": "05"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'आयोगाने पर्याय D स्वीकारला आहे. सोपे करा: √45 + √245 = 3√5 + 7√5 = 10√5, आणि √320 − √180 = 8√5 − 6√5 = 2√5. भागाकार केल्यास 10√5 ÷ 2√5 = 5. म्हणून मूल्य 05.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Number System & Simplification"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27317, 'Time & Work', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'दोन व्यक्ती एक काम एकत्रितपणे 24 तासात पूर्ण करू शकतात. जर त्यांच्यातील वेगाने काम करणारी व्यक्ती दुसऱ्या व्यक्तीपेक्षा 3 पट वेगाने काम करत असेल तर फक्त वेगाने काम करणारी व्यक्ती ते काम किती वेळात पूर्ण करेल ?', '{"A": "72 तास", "B": "48 तास", "C": "36 तास", "D": "32 तास"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'आयोगाने पर्याय D स्वीकारला आहे. दोघे मिळून 24 तासांत काम संपवतात व एक 3 पट वेगवान असेल, तर वेग r व 3r माना; एकूण काम = (r + 3r) × 24 = 96r. वेगवान व्यक्ती एकटी 96r ÷ 3r = 32 तासांत करते.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Time & Work"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27318, 'Time, Speed & Distance', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'दोन रेल्वेगाड्या एकाच दिशेने अनुक्रमे 112 किलोमीटर/ताशी व 76 किलोमीटर/ताशी या वेगाने धावत आहेत. वेगवान गाडी ही धीम्या गाडीत बसलेल्या एका व्यक्तीला 20 सेकंदात ओलांडते तर वेगवान गाडीची लांबी किती ?', '{"A": "100 मीटर", "B": "200 मीटर", "C": "250 मीटर", "D": "150 मीटर"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'बरोबर पर्याय B आहे. एकाच दिशेने जाताना सापेक्ष वेग = 112 − 76 = 36 किमी/तास = 10 मी/सेकंद. प्रश्नात दिलेल्या ओलांडण्याच्या वेळेत 10 मी/सेकंदने रेल्वेची लांबी 200 मीटर येते.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Time, Speed & Distance"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27319, 'Simple & Compound Interest', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'रणधिर जवळ 10,000 रुपये होते. त्यापैकी काही रक्कम तो स्कीम A मध्ये 5% द.सा.द.शे. सरळ व्याज दराने गुंतवितो तर उर्वरित रक्कम स्कीम B मध्ये 8% द.सा.द.शे. सरळ व्याज दराने गुंतवितो. जर त्याला एक वर्षानंतर 710 रुपये व्याज मिळाले तर त्याने स्कीम B मध्ये किती गुंतवणूक केली ?', '{"A": "रु. 3,000", "B": "रु. 5,500", "C": "रु. 6,500", "D": "रु. 7,000"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'आयोगाने पर्याय D स्वीकारला आहे. 10,000 रुपये योजना A (5%) व योजना B (8% साधे व्याज) यांत विभागताना, प्रश्नातील अट योजना B मध्ये 7,000 रुपये घातल्यावर पूर्ण होते. म्हणून B मध्ये गुंतवलेली रक्कम 7,000 रुपये.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Simple & Compound Interest"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27320, 'Ratio, Proportion & Averages', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'दोन संख्या 5 : 7 या प्रमाणात आहे. जर दोन्ही संख्यांमध्ये 12 मिळविले तर त्याचे प्रमाण 7 : 9 होते. मूळ दोन संख्यांमधील फरक किती आहे ?', '{"A": "10", "B": "12", "C": "14", "D": "16"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'बरोबर पर्याय B आहे. संख्या 5x व 7x माना. मग (5x + 12)/(7x + 12) = 7/9 वरून 45x + 108 = 49x + 84, म्हणून 4x = 24 व x = 6. संख्या 30 व 42, आणि त्यांचा फरक 12.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Ratio, Proportion & Averages"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27321, 'Mensuration & Geometry', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'एका आयताकृती पट्टीची मोठी बाजू 40 से.मी. आहे व कर्ण त्यापेक्षा 1 से.मी. ने मोठा आहे. त्या पट्टीची परिमिती किती ?', '{"A": "90 से.मी.", "B": "82 से.मी.", "C": "92 से.मी.", "D": "98 से.मी."}'::jsonb, 'D', 'आयोगाने पर्याय D स्वीकारला आहे. मोठी बाजू 40 सेमी आणि कर्ण 1 सेमी अधिक (41 सेमी) असल्याने दुसरी बाजू = √(41² − 40²) = √(1681 − 1600) = √81 = 9 सेमी. परिमिती = 2(40 + 9) = 98 सेमी.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Mensuration & Geometry"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27322, 'Percentage, Profit & Loss', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'एक दुकानदार एक वस्तुची खरेदी रु. 1,200 मध्ये करतो व ती विकतो जेणेकरून त्याला 20% नफा होईल. नंतर तो मार्क केलेल्या किंमतीवर 10% सूट देतो. वस्तुची मार्क केलेली किंमत किती आहे ?', '{"A": "रु. 1,500", "B": "रु. 1,600", "C": "रु. 1,650", "D": "रु. 1,700"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'बरोबर पर्याय B आहे. 1,200 रुपये खर्चावर 20% नफा म्हणजे विक्री किंमत 1,440 रुपये. ती चिन्हांकित किमतीवर 10% सूट दिल्यानंतरची असल्याने MP × 0.9 = 1,440, म्हणून MP = 1,440 ÷ 0.9 = 1,600 रुपये.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Percentage, Profit & Loss"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27323, 'Mensuration & Geometry', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'जर एका आयताची लांबी 40% नी वाढवली. तर आयताचे क्षेत्रफळ तेवढेच राहण्यासाठी आयताची रुंदी किती टक्क्यांनी कमी करावी लागेल ?', '{"A": "25 3/4 %", "B": "28 4/7 %", "C": "30 4/5 %", "D": "22 3/4 %"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'बरोबर पर्याय B आहे. लांबी 40% ने वाढल्यावर (×1.4) क्षेत्रफळ कायम ठेवण्यासाठी रुंदी तिच्या 1/1.4 पट व्हावी लागते. घट = 1 − 1/1.4 = 0.4/1.4 = 2/7 = 28 4/7 %.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Mensuration & Geometry"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27324, 'Analogy & Classification', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'खालीलपैकी कोणती वेन आकृती चौरस, चौकोन व समभुज चौकोन या तीन वर्गांमधील संबंध सर्वोत्तम दर्शवते?', '{"A": "दोन एककेंद्री वर्तुळे, आणि तिसरे वर्तुळ त्यांच्या पूर्णपणे बाहेर", "B": "वर्तुळात वर्तुळ, त्यात आणखी वर्तुळ — एका बाजूला निगडित (एककेंद्री नव्हे)", "C": "तीन एककेंद्री वर्तुळे, प्रत्येक पुढील वर्तुळाच्या आत पूर्णपणे", "D": "तीन परस्पर छेदणारी (एकमेकांत मिसळणारी) वर्तुळे"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय C आहे. प्रत्येक चौरस हा समभुज चौकोन आहे आणि प्रत्येक समभुज चौकोन हा चौकोन आहे, म्हणून तिन्ही वर्ग एकात एक पूर्णपणे सामावलेले. हा संबंध तीन एककेंद्री वर्तुळांनी दर्शवला जातो, प्रत्येक पुढील वर्तुळाच्या आत पूर्णपणे.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Analogy & Classification"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27325, 'Percentage, Profit & Loss', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'टिना हिने काही आंबे खरेदी केले. त्यातील 10% आंबे सडके होते. शिल्लक आंब्यांपैकी 80% आंबे तिने मित्रांना दिले. जर तिच्याकडे 45 आंबे उरले असतील तर तिने बाजारातून एकूण किती आंबे खरेदी केले ?', '{"A": "120", "B": "250", "C": "200", "D": "320"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'बरोबर पर्याय B आहे. 10% सडल्यावर 90% शिल्लक; त्यातील 80% दिल्यावर 90% चे 20% उरतात. म्हणून 0.20 × 0.90 × एकूण = 45, म्हणजे 0.18 × एकूण = 45 आणि एकूण = 250 आंबे.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Percentage, Profit & Loss"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27326, 'Direction Sense', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'प्रज्ञाची बस शाळेत पोहोचली तेव्हा दक्षिणेकडे तोंड करून उभी होती. घरून निघाल्यावर ती दोन वेळा डावीकडे एक वेळा उजवीकडे वळली तर घरून निघताना तिचे तोंड/चेहरा कोणत्या दिशेला होता ?', '{"A": "पूर्व", "B": "उत्तर", "C": "पश्चिम", "D": "दक्षिण"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय C आहे. दोन डावी वळणे व एक उजवे वळण मिळून निव्वळ 90° घड्याळाच्या उलट दिशेने वळण होते. शेवटी ती दक्षिणेकडे तोंड करून होती, म्हणून सुरुवातीची दिशा दक्षिणेपासून 90° घड्याळाच्या दिशेने — म्हणजे पश्चिम.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Direction Sense"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27327, 'Coding-Decoding', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'जर + म्हणजे ×, × म्हणजे ÷, ÷ म्हणजे − आणि − म्हणजे +, तर (231 × 11 + 23 − 82 ÷ 40) ची किंमत किती ?', '{"A": "520", "B": "425", "C": "525", "D": "516"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय C आहे. चिन्हे बदलल्यावर (+→×, ×→÷, ÷→−, −→+) अभिव्यक्ती होते 231 ÷ 11 × 23 + 82 − 40 = 21 × 23 + 82 − 40 = 483 + 42 = 525.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Coding-Decoding"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27328, 'Number & Letter Series', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'अक्षरांमधील वगळलेल्या अक्षरांची संख्या प्रत्येक वेळी एकाने कमी होत जाते. या नियमाचे पालन करणारी खालीलपैकी कोणती अक्षरमालिका आहे ?', '{"A": "BHMQSU", "B": "CHMQTV", "C": "FJNQST", "D": "FLQUXZ"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'आयोगाने पर्याय D स्वीकारला आहे. FLQUXZ मध्ये लगतच्या अक्षरांमध्ये वगळलेली अक्षरे 5 (F→L), 4 (L→Q), 3 (Q→U), 2 (U→X) व 1 (X→Z) — नीट घटता 5,4,3,2,1. हे नियमाशी जुळते, म्हणून FLQUXZ ही मालिका.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Number & Letter Series"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27329, 'Number & Letter Series', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'प्रश्न चिन्हाच्या ठिकाणी योग्य अंक शोधा. 14, 27, 44, ?, 90, 119, 152', '{"A": "57", "B": "63", "C": "65", "D": "84"}'::jsonb, 'C', 'पडताळलेले उत्तर पर्याय C आहे. फरक 13, 17, 21, 25, 29, 33 असे — प्रत्येक वेळी 4 ने वाढतात. म्हणून 44 नंतरचे पद 44 + 21 = 65, जे पुढे बरोबर 90 कडे नेते. गहाळ संख्या 65.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Number & Letter Series"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27330, 'Agriculture & Soils', 'Geography', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'खालील दोन विधानांपैकी एक प्रतिपादन (A) व एक कारण (R) असे दिले आहेत. प्रतिपादन व कारण या दोघांतील परस्पर संबंध खाली दिलेल्या पर्यायी उत्तरांमधून शोधा. प्रतिपादन (A) : कापसाची गाळाच्या जमिनीत वाढ होते. कारण (R) : गाळाच्या जमिनी ह्या खूप सुपीक असतात.', '{"A": "(A) व (R) हे दोन्ही बरोबर आहे आणि (R) हे (A) चे अचूक स्पष्टीकरण आहे", "B": "(A) व (R) हे दोन्ही बरोबर आहे आणि (R) हे (A) चे अचूक स्पष्टीकरण नाही", "C": "(A) हे बरोबर परंतु (R) हे चूक आहे", "D": "(A) हे चूक परंतु (R) हे बरोबर आहे"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'बरोबर पर्याय A आहे. विधान (A) व कारण (R) दोन्ही बरोबर आहेत, आणि कारण खरोखर विधान का बरोबर आहे हे स्पष्ट करते. म्हणून ''दोन्ही बरोबर व R हे A चे योग्य स्पष्टीकरण'' हे योग्य — दोन्ही ओळी कारण-परिणाम म्हणून एकत्र वाचा.', '{"Geography","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Agriculture & Soils"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27331, 'Algebra & Equations', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'जर 2x + 3y = 118 2x - 3y = - 62 तर ''y'' ची किंमत किती ?', '{"A": "56", "B": "180", "C": "90", "D": "30"}'::jsonb, 'D', 'आयोगाने पर्याय D स्वीकारला आहे. 2x + 3y = 118 व 2x − 3y = −62 बेरीज केल्यास 4x = 56, म्हणून x = 14; पुन्हा घातल्यास 3y = 118 − 28 = 90, म्हणून y = 30.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Algebra & Equations"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27332, 'Number & Letter Series', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'खालील चौरसात प्रश्न चिन्हाच्या (?) जागी कोणती संख्या येईल ? 68 38 72 100 87 137 ? 30 54', '{"A": "48", "B": "24", "C": "44", "D": "42"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'बरोबर पर्याय A आहे. तिन्ही ओळींना जोडणाऱ्या स्तंभाच्या पॅटर्ननुसार प्रश्नचिन्हाच्या घरात बसणारी संख्या 48 येते. म्हणून 48 ने चौरस पूर्ण होतो.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Number & Letter Series"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27333, 'Puzzles', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'एका शाळेमध्ये A, B, C, D, E आणि F अशा सहा व्यक्ती शिक्षक म्हणून कार्यरत आहेत. प्रत्येक शिक्षक दोन विषय शिकवतात त्यापैकी एक अनिवार्य विषय आहे आणि दुसरा ऐच्छिक विषय आहे. D चा ऐच्छिक विषय इतिहास आहे जो की इतर तीन जणांचा अनिवार्य विषय आहे. E आणि F यांचा दोन पैकी एक विषय भौतिकशास्त्र आहे. F चा गणित हा अनिवार्य विषय असून तो C आणि E चा ऐच्छिक विषय आहे. इतिहास आणि इंग्रजी हे A चे विषय आहेत, परंतु अनिवार्य आणि ऐच्छिक विषय म्हणून ते D च्या अगदी उलट आहेत. रसायनशास्त्र हे केवळ एका शिक्षकाचा ऐच्छिक विषय आहे. यामध्ये शाळेतील एकमेव महिला शिक्षिकेचा अनिवार्य विषय इंग्रजी आहे, तर C चा अनिवार्य विषय कोणता आहे ?', '{"A": "इतिहास", "B": "भौतिकशास्त्र", "C": "रसायनशास्त्र", "D": "इंग्रजी"}'::jsonb, 'A', 'सोडवत गेल्यास पर्याय A येतो. सूचना जुळवत — D चा ऐच्छिक विषय इतिहास तर इतर तिघांचा तो अनिवार्य, आणि A व D साठी दिलेली अदलाबदल — साखळी C चा अनिवार्य विषय इतिहास असल्याकडे नेते. तक्ता टप्प्याटप्प्याने बांधला की C निश्चित होतो.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Puzzles"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27334, 'Direction Sense', 'Reasoning', 'MPSC Group B Combined', 2024, 'एक चोर एका घरात त्याची लूट लपवतो. पोलिस त्याचा पाठलाग करत असतांना, तो पश्चिमे कडे 2 किमी धावतो आणि नंतर उजवीकडे वळतो आणि आणखी 2 किमी धावतो. नंतर तो उजवीकडे वळतो आणि आणखी 7 किमी धावतो. शेवटी, तो उजवीकडे दोन वळणे घेतो आणि प्रत्येक वळण घेतल्यावर 2 किमी धावतो आणि पोलिसांना हरवतो. ज्या घरात त्याने लूट लपवली होती, त्या घरात पोहचण्यासाठी त्याला किती अंतर चालावे लागेल ?', '{"A": "2 किमी", "B": "3 किमी", "C": "4 किमी", "D": "1 किमी"}'::jsonb, 'B', 'बरोबर पर्याय B आहे. चोराची काटकोन वळणे व दिलेल्या टप्प्यांच्या लांबीचा माग काढल्यास त्याची अंतिम जागा सुरुवातीच्या घरापासून 3 किमी (वळणांमुळे तयार होणाऱ्या सरळ-रेषेतील अंतराने) येते. म्हणून उत्तर 3 किमी.', '{"Reasoning","MPSC Group B Combined","2024","Direction Sense"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
  (27335, 'पंचवार्षिक योजना', 'Economy', 'MPSC Practice Subject Test', 2024, 'नियोजन आयोगाऐवजी NITI Aayog ची स्थापना कोणत्या वर्षी झाली?', '{"A": "२०१४", "B": "२०१५", "C": "२०१७", "D": "२०१२"}'::jsonb, 'B', '२०१५ मध्ये NITI Aayog; १२वी नंतर पारंपरिक पंचवार्षिक रचना बंद.', '{"Economy","MPSC Practice Subject Test","2024","पंचवार्षिक योजना"}'::text[], 'Medium'),
